\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 University of Idaho says staff can offer condoms for STDs \u8211\'20\'13 not birth control\b0\par\par\uc2 Gloria Oladipo \par \uc2 464 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 September 2022\par 18:37 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Memo warns employees they should not speak in support of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  following state ban on procedure\par \par \uc2 Condoms should only be provided to students to prevent sexually transmitted infections, not as birth control, according to a memo sent by the University of Idaho to staff last week.\par \par \uc2 The memo, first obtained by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.idahopress.com/news/local/u-of-i-memo-on-abortion-laws-draws-national-attention-1st-amendment-concerns/article_d7f3e458-3de8-11ed-8d34-173525bf7e95.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Idaho Press}}}\uc2  and issued to all employees on Friday, laid out the university\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive policies following the enactment of Idaho\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, which bans the procedure in nearly all cases.\par \par \uc2 The memo further warned employees that they could not speak in support of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and should \u8220\'20\'1Cproceed cautiously at any time that a discussion moves in the direction of reproductive health\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/3662295-university-of-idaho-warns-staff-not-to-offer-reproductive-health-services-following-states-near-total-abortion-ban/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported the Hill}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The advice on birth control was included because of the law\u8217\'20\'19s lack of clarity on \u8220\'20\'1Cprevention of conception\u8221\'20\'1D, the university said, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://idahocapitalsun.com/2022/09/26/university-of-idaho-releases-memo-warning-employees-that-promoting-abortion-is-against-state-law/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Idaho Capital Sun}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Staff have been prohibited from recommending or referring \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a student. Employees have also been told not to issue emergency contraception \u8211\'20\'13 the so-called morning after pill, also known as Plan B \u8211\'20\'13 except in cases of rape.\par \par \uc2 Standard birth control pills will reportedly still be distributed at student health centers, which are administered by Moscow Family Health, not the university itself. The university does not provide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services.\par \par \uc2 It warned that any staff recommending \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to students risked a felony conviction and could be banned from any future state employment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSince violation is considered a felony, we are advising a conservative approach here,\u8221\'20\'1D read the memo.\par \par \uc2 Idaho\u8217\'20\'19s near-total ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  only has exceptions for rape or when a person\u8217\'20\'19s life is in danger. It went into effect on 25 August and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/08/24/us/politics/idaho-abortion-ban.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 faced a lawsuit}}}\uc2  from the \uc2 US Department of Justice\uc2 , which argued it could prevent doctors from using the procedure in medical emergencies.\par \par \uc2 The university said it was issuing its recommendations that staff stay neutral on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to avoid punishment because of another law passed in 2021, the No Public Funds for \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Act, which bars state employees and officials from recommending abortions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a challenging law for many and has real ramifications for individuals in that it calls for individual criminal prosecution. This guidance was sent to help our employees understand the legal significance and possible actions of this new law passed by the Idaho legislature,\u8221\'20\'1D Jodi Walker, the executive director of communications at the university, told the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Not all universities in anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  states are following suit, however. \uc2 Vanderbilt University\uc2  in Tennessee, where a near-total ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  went into effect in August, has said it will continue providing birth control methods and emergency contraception to students, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/09/26/u-idaho-may-stop-providing-birth-control-under-new-abortion-law/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported the Post}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220927ei9r002e5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
