\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Former January 6 committee staffer says texts show evidence of \u8216\'20\'18attempted coup\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein \par \uc2 4,730 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 September 2022\par 20:07 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Denver Riggleman tells 60 Minutes that texts from \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  amounted to a \u8216\'20\'18roadmap to an attempted coup\u8217\'20\'19Sign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 A former staffer for the January 6 committee went public with a claim that someone at the White House called a Capitol rioter on the day of the attack, while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/26/jan-6-attack-denver-riggleman-biden-saving-money-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6331a1208f0877eea340583a#block-6331a1208f0877eea340583a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warning that evidence obtained}}}\uc2  from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff looked like an \u8220\'20\'1Cattempted coup\u8221\'20\'1D. The committee\u8217\'20\'19s lawmakers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/26/jan-6-attack-denver-riggleman-biden-saving-money-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6331adf48f08d07ba0ad64d6#block-6331adf48f08d07ba0ad64d6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 downplayed}}}\uc2  Denver Riggleman \u8217\'20\'19s interview with \uc2 CBS\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 60 Minutes program, and have been busy themselves, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/26/jan-6-attack-denver-riggleman-biden-saving-money-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6331b0eb8f0877eea34058e2#block-6331b0eb8f0877eea34058e2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sending a subpoena}}}\uc2  to the Republican speaker of Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s assembly.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2 , a Democratic senator known for bucking the party\u8217\'20\'19s priorities, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/26/jan-6-attack-denver-riggleman-biden-saving-money-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6331d7918f0877eea3405b56#block-6331d7918f0877eea3405b56"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 offered few reasons for her mysterious politics}}}\uc2  in a speech alongside the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s top Republican.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s student loan relief plan will cost $400 billion, if not more, the independent \uc2 Congressional Budget Office\uc2  said, prompting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/26/jan-6-attack-denver-riggleman-biden-saving-money-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6331fa3e8f08f9373688e5df#block-6331fa3e8f08f9373688e5df"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criticism from budget hawks}}}\uc2  as well as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/26/jan-6-attack-denver-riggleman-biden-saving-money-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-633200228f0877eea3405cc2#block-633200228f0877eea3405cc2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defense from Democrats}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2 , a Trump-backed 2020 election denier standing as the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s gubernatorial candidate in Pennsylvania, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/26/jan-6-attack-denver-riggleman-biden-saving-money-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6331d1168f08d07ba0ad672c#block-6331d1168f08d07ba0ad672c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appears to be lagging}}}\uc2  on the campaign trail.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former chief of staff Mark Meadows{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/26/jan-6-attack-denver-riggleman-biden-saving-money-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6331b64c8f08f9373688e2a6#block-6331b64c8f08f9373688e2a6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 exchanged texts}}}\uc2  with another conspiracy theorist and 2020 election denier.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democratic senators hit back at claims student debt relief too expensive\par \par \uc2 The Senate\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  along with Wall Street foe Elizabeth Warren have issued a joint statement underlining their support of president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s student debt relief plan, and drawing a contrast with Republican policies that slash taxes for the rich.\par \par \uc2 The statement came after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/26/jan-6-attack-denver-riggleman-biden-saving-money-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6331fa3e8f08f9373688e5df#block-6331fa3e8f08f9373688e5df"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the independent Congressional Budget Office (CBO) found}}}\uc2  the plan announced last month would cost a sizable $400 billion or more. The nonpartisan Committee for a Responsible Federal Budget seized on that estimate to say the plan was too expensive, and could push inflation higher.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday\u8217\'20\'19s CBO estimate makes clear that millions of middle class Americans have more breathing room thanks to President Biden\u8217\'20\'19s historic decision to cancel student debt,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer, who represents New York, and Warren, who represents Massachusetts, said in their statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn contrast to President Trump and Republicans who gave giant corporations $2 trillion in tax breaks, President Biden delivered transformative middle class relief by cancelling student debt for working people who need it most \u8212\'20\'14 nearly 90% of relief dollars will go to those earning less than $75,000 a year. We don\u8217\'20\'19t agree with all of CBO\u8217\'20\'19s assumptions that underlie this analysis, but it is clear the pandemic payment pause and student debt cancellation are policies that demonstrate how government can and should invest in working people, not the wealthy and billionaire corporations.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Idaho\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law is being challenged in federal court, but \uc2 The Washington Post\uc2  reports that the impact of the strict measure is already being felt by the state\u8217\'20\'19s universities.\par \par \uc2 The University of Idaho has advised employees that because the law is not written clearly, it may prohibit employees from offering birth control, and thus they should refrain from doing so:\par \par \uc2 enltrUniversity of Idaho employees were warned Friday that they could be charged with a felony for talking about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , because of the state\u8217\'20\'19s new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law.\par \par \uc2 They were also told *they could no longer provide birth control.*\par \par \uc2 Not just Plan B, but regular birth control. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/qHJoDRzMc2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/qHJoDRzMc2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Caroline Kitchener (@CAKitchener) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CAKitchener/status/1574468952687874080?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 26, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/25/idaho-judge-bars-state-enforcing-abortion-ban-medical-emergencies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Idaho judge bars state from enforcing \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban in medical emergencies}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 The fiscal hawks at the independent \uc2 Congressional Budget Office\uc2  have released their cost estimate for the student loan relief plan president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announced last month, and found it comes in at $400 billion, but could vary.\par \par \uc2 The plan partially satisfied Biden\u8217\'20\'19s campaign pledge to provide relief for Americans struggling with loans from higher education, but was criticized both for not being generous enough, and for adding on to the country\u8217\'20\'19s already mammoth federal budget deficit:\par \par \uc2 enltrCBO estimates that the cost of outstanding student loans to the federal government will increase by about $400 billion because of an executive action canceling some debt. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/FgEHBn2XP6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/FgEHBn2XP6}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 U.S. CBO (@USCBO) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/USCBO/status/1574459277292478464?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 26, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The Committee for a Responsible Federal Budget, which advocates for restraint in federal spending, criticized the plan as simply too expensive:\par \par \uc2 enltr". {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/USCBO?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @USCBO}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s new estimate confirms the outrageous cost of the White House plan to cancel large amounts of student debt, by executive order, to nearly all borrowers almost regardless of need." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/KFs9DQ8KYp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/KFs9DQ8KYp}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CRFB.org (@BudgetHawks) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BudgetHawks/status/1574471593245511701?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 26, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr"The debt cancellation and pause alone will cost $420 billion \u8211\'20\'13 a bit more than we previously thought \u8211\'20\'13 and costs could reach $510 to $610 billion with their IDR changes. The Biden Administration\u8217\'20\'19s failure to release their own cost estimate should have been a red flag."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CRFB.org (@BudgetHawks) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BudgetHawks/status/1574471595221028902?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 26, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr"As {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/USCBO?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @USCBO}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s estimates help confirm, the President\u8217\'20\'19s student debt plan would wipe out the ten-year savings from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/InflationReductionAct?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #InflationReductionAct}}}\uc2  twice over, worsen inflationary pressures, and deliver benefits to millions of Americans with advanced degrees in upper-income households."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CRFB.org (@BudgetHawks) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BudgetHawks/status/1574471596747755548?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 26, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr"This might be the most costly executive action in history. It\u8217\'20\'19s unacceptable that the President would implement it without offsets and without Congressional approval. Including these actions, the President has now added nearly $4.9 trillion to ten-year federal deficits..."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CRFB.org (@BudgetHawks) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BudgetHawks/status/1574471598316425246?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 26, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr"...through legislation and executive actions.\par \par \uc2 With {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/inflation?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #inflation}}}\uc2  at a 40-year high and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/nationaldebt?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #nationaldebt}}}\uc2  approaching record levels, we shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be adding to deficits \u8211\'20\'13 certainly not by executive fiat."\par \par \uc2 Full statement: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/KFs9DPR9zP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/KFs9DPR9zP}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CRFB.org (@BudgetHawks) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BudgetHawks/status/1574471600098791424?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 26, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/24/joe-biden-us-student-loan-debt-cancellation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden unveils plan to cancel $10,000 in student loan debt for millions}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration is generally keeping mum about Russia\u8217\'20\'19s decision to grant citizenship to Edward Snowden, who leaked \uc2 National Security Agency\uc2  documents and fled the United States.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the little state department spokesman \uc2 Ned Price\uc2  had to say about it:\par \par \uc2 enltrState Department Spokesperson \uc2 Ned Price\uc2  reacts to NSA whistleblower Edward Snowden being granted Russian citizenship:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPerhaps the only thing that has changed is \u8230\'20\'26 apparently now he may well be conscripted to fight in the reckless war in Ukraine.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ZemSN8CVur"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ZemSN8CVur}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1574466121482264576?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 26, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/26/putin-grants-russian-citizenship-to-us-whistleblower-edward-snowden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Putin grants Russian citizenship to US whistleblower Edward Snowden}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 January 6 committee member says DoJ investigation proceeding, but slowly\par \par \uc2 A Democratic member of the January 6 committee revealed details of the department of justice\u8217\'20\'19s investigation into the attack and its interaction with the congressional inquiry, describing the government\u8217\'20\'19s effort as plodding, thorough and bolstered by evidence the lawmakers had uncovered.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey have been very slow, though, on the much more comprehensive, and I believe, even more significant investigation of January 6," California congressman Adam Schiff said of the justice department during an interview at the Texas Tribune Festival, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/09/24/politics/january-6-doj-investigation-adam-schiff/index.html?utm_medium=social&utm_source=twCNNp&utm_content=2022-09-26T13%3A29%3A07&utm_term=link"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to CNN}}}\uc2 . However, he thought it was a mistake for the justice department to start their investigation with the individual rioters and proceed from there.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat works when you have one plot, one conspiracy. It doesn\u8217\'20\'19t work when there are multiple lines of effort to overturn an election, multiple plots, that may be all part of the same whole, but nonetheless each operating independently,\u8221\'20\'1D Schiff said.\par \par \uc2 The Democrat acknowledged federal investigators are matching the work of the January 6 committee, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CIt does appear now that they have interviewed many of the same significant witnesses that we have.\u8221\'20\'1D He did note that the justice department had requested much of the committee\u8217\'20\'19s materials, which he found \u8220\'20\'1Cbreathtaking\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy first reaction when we got the request \u8211\'20\'13 \u8216\'20\'18Turn over all your files to us\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 was: \u8216\'20\'18Why don\u8217\'20\'19t you have your own damn files? Why haven\u8217\'20\'19t you been conducting your own investigation? Why do you need us to do it?\u8221\'20\'1D Schiff said.\par \par \uc2 The lawmaker also found it strange that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/05/georgia-grand-jury-subpoenas-trump-legal-advisers-2020-election-effort"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a district attorney in Georgia had been left to singlehandedly investigate}}}\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his allies\u8217\'20\'19 involvement in trying to overturn the election there, but noted that situation might not last much longer. \u8220\'20\'1CThat may be changing too, but it\u8217\'20\'19s a long time coming,\u8221\'20\'1D Schiff said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 A former staffer for the January 6 committee went public with a claim that someone at the White House called a Capitol rioter on the day of the attack, while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/26/jan-6-attack-denver-riggleman-biden-saving-money-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6331a1208f0877eea340583a#block-6331a1208f0877eea340583a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warning that evidence obtained}}}\uc2  from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff looked like an \u8220\'20\'1Cattempted coup\u8221\'20\'1D. The committee\u8217\'20\'19s lawmakers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/26/jan-6-attack-denver-riggleman-biden-saving-money-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6331adf48f08d07ba0ad64d6#block-6331adf48f08d07ba0ad64d6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 downplayed}}}\uc2  Denver Riggleman \u8217\'20\'19s interview with \uc2 CBS\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 60 Minutes program, and have been busy themselves, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/26/jan-6-attack-denver-riggleman-biden-saving-money-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6331b0eb8f0877eea34058e2#block-6331b0eb8f0877eea34058e2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sending a subpoena}}}\uc2  to the Republican speaker of Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s assembly.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2 , a Democratic senator known for bucking the party\u8217\'20\'19s priorities, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/26/jan-6-attack-denver-riggleman-biden-saving-money-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6331d7918f0877eea3405b56#block-6331d7918f0877eea3405b56"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 offered few reasons for her mysterious politics}}}\uc2  in a speech alongside the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s top Republican.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2 , a Trump-backed 2020 election denier standing as the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s gubernatorial candidate in Pennsylvania, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/26/jan-6-attack-denver-riggleman-biden-saving-money-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6331d1168f08d07ba0ad672c#block-6331d1168f08d07ba0ad672c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appears to be trailing}}}\uc2  on the campaign trail.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former chief of staff Mark Meadows{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/26/jan-6-attack-denver-riggleman-biden-saving-money-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-6331b64c8f08f9373688e2a6#block-6331b64c8f08f9373688e2a6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 exchanged texts}}}\uc2  with another conspiracy theorist and 2020 election denier.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 There are few mysteries in Congress bigger than \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Once a member of the Green Party, the Democratic senator from Arizona has seized on the party\u8217\'20\'19s one-vote majority in the Senate to act a spoiler for progressive proposals, including changing the filibuster to get voting rights legislation passed, raising the national minimum wage to $15 per-hour and closing a tax loophole that benefited private equity firms. Unlike with \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2 , the fellow Democratic senator and frequent holdout vote who already had a reputation for conservatism and support for the fossil fuel industry, Sinema\u8217\'20\'19s reasons for acting this way aren\u8217\'20\'19t quite clear, and somewhat inexplicable given her left-wing activism earlier in her career. The tactic doesn\u8217\'20\'19t appear to have paid off, either. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aarp.org/content/dam/aarp/research/surveys_statistics/politics/2022/aarp-arizona-2022-elections-voter-survey-governor.doi.10.26419-2Fres.00550.011.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 An AARP poll released last week}}}\uc2  showed that independents, Republicans and, most of all, Democrats in Arizona viewed Sinema unfavorably.\par \par \uc2 The senator appeared today alongside the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s top Republican \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  for a speech in Kentucky, where she extolled the virtues of bipartisanship. While it certainly does not clear up the senator\u8217\'20\'19s mysterious approach to politics, her comments here may give some hints as to why she does what she does in Washington:\par \par \uc2 enltrSen. \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  (D-AZ), speaking at the McConnell Center, describes her "friendship" with Senate Minority Leader McConnell (R-KY):\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile we may not agree on every issue, we do share the same values.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2vz5ioNFeA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/2vz5ioNFeA}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1574416232174030850?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 26, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr"Not everyone likes me."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sen. \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  (D-AZ) jokes with the audience at the McConnell Center, after saying Democrats will "likely" lose some control of Congress after the midterms. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/naEjHhKO5D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/naEjHhKO5D}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1574430192680009734?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 26, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/04/democrats-kyrsten-sinema-agreement-climate-and-economic-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats secure breakthrough with Kyrsten Sinema on climate bill}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI signed a permission slip for a College and Career Day. What I got was indoctrination and trauma.\u8221\'20\'1D That sums up the experience of some of the more than 2,100 high school seniors bussed to a church in Louisiana last week on what was billed as a college fair but, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/maya-yang"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maya Yang}}}\uc2  reports, turned into something else:\par \par \uc2 More than 2,000 public school students in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/louisiana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Louisiana}}}\uc2  were told earlier this week that they were going to a college fair. They were then shuttled to what parents later deemed a sexist and transphobic church event which left many of the students traumatized.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, more than 2,100 high school seniors from the \uc2 East Baton Rouge Parish School System\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 which serves residents of Louisiana\u8217\'20\'19s capital \u8211\'20\'13 were taken to the local Living Faith Christian Center under the promise that they would receive college and career advice, as well as free food.\par \par \uc2 The Christian nonprofit organization 29:11 Mentoring Program organized the event, calling it \u8220\'20\'1CDay of Hope,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theadvocate.com/baton_rouge/news/education/article_97dc38c2-3a0d-11ed-a388-3f7b65892ceb.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Baton Rouge Advocate}}}\uc2  reported. The permission slips distributed to students promised \u8220\'20\'1Cfree food\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Cfun and games\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Ccollege fair\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cspecial guest\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/25/louisiana-school-college-fair-transphobic-church-event-students-say"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Louisiana school turned \u8216\'20\'18college fair\u8217\'20\'19 into transphobic church event, students say}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  sent a reporter to Pennsylvania to check on how the Republican candidate for governor is doing, and the verdict seems to be: not that well.\par \par \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2  is a \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  -endorsed, 2020 election denier who chartered busses to Washington on January 6 and has pledged to completely ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state if elected. However, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/governor/2022/pennsylvania/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he\u8217\'20\'19s well behind in the polls}}}\uc2 , and as the Times reports, has shunned much of what amounts to modern campaign tactics.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/09/26/us/politics/doug-mastriano-campaign-pennsylvania.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from their report}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 There is little indication that he has built a campaign infrastructure beyond the \uc2 Facebook\uc2  videos that propelled him to stardom in right-wing circles and to the vanguard of Christian nationalist politics.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI can\u8217\'20\'19t even assess things because I don\u8217\'20\'19t see a campaign,\u8221\'20\'1D said Matt Brouillette, the president of Commonwealth Partners Chamber of Entrepreneurs, an advocacy group that is a major player in Pennsylvania Republican politics. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve not seen anything that is even a semblance of a campaign.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mr. Brouillette, who backed one of Mr. Mastriano\u8217\'20\'19s rivals in the G.O.P. primary, added: \u8220\'20\'1CNow, maybe he knows something we don\u8217\'20\'19t on how you can win in the fifth-largest state without doing TV or mail. But I guess we\u8217\'20\'19re going to have to wait until Nov. 8 to see whether you can pull something like that off.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe New York from which Trump emerged was its own morass of corruption and dysfunction, stretching from seats of executive power to portions of the media to the real-estate industry in which his family found its wealth,\u8221\'20\'1D writes Maggie Haberman in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theatlantic.com/ideas/archive/2022/09/donald-trump-maggie-haberman-mar-a-lago/671510/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Atlantic}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CBut Trump nevertheless stood out to the journalists covering him as particularly brazen.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Haberman, a reporter for \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  and longtime watcher of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , is one of the best-known chroniclers of his presidency, and the Atlantic article is a good read for those who want to better understand what drives Trump. Adapted from her soon-to-be-released book \u8220\'20\'1CConfidence Man: The Making of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and the Breaking of America\u8221\'20\'1D, the piece touches on some of the drivers of his inexplicable behavior, such as his insistence that the election was stolen, and that he could even return to office in August 2021.\par \par \uc2 It also shows how Trump viewed the people around him, particularly his supporters, whose ardency appeared to take him by surprise. For more on that, take a look at how the piece starts:\par \par \uc2 Can you believe these are my customers?\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  once asked while surveying the crowd in the Taj Mahal casino\u8217\'20\'19s poker room. \u8220\'20\'1CLook at those losers,\u8221\'20\'1D he said to his consultant Tom O\u8217\'20\'19Neil, of people spending money on the floor of the Trump Plaza casino. Visiting the Iowa State Fair as a presidential candidate in 2015, he was astounded that locals fell in line to support him because of a few free rides in his branded helicopter. In the White House, he was sometimes stunned at his own backers\u8217\'20\'19 fervor, telling aides, \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re fucking crazy.\u8221\'20\'1D Yet they loved him and wanted to own a piece of him, and that was what mattered most.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 The supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s overturning of Roe v Wade allowed states to curtail \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights completely, potentially transformed the midterms and, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/maya-yang"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maya Yang}}}\uc2  reports, complicated access to other medicines in unexpected ways:\par \par \uc2 A few weeks after the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s 24 June decision to overturn the nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights established by Roe v Wade, the pharmacy chain \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  sent Annie England Noblin a message, informing her that her monthly prescription of methotrexate was held up.\par \par \uc2 Noblin, a 40-year-old college instructor in rural {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/missouri"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Missouri}}}\uc2 , never had trouble getting her monthly prescription of methotrexate for her rheumatoid arthritis. So she went to her local \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  to figure out why, standing in line with other customers as she waited for an explanation.\par \par \uc2 When it was finally her turn, a pharmacist informed Noblin \u8211\'20\'13 in front of the other customers behind her \u8211\'20\'13 that she could not release the medication until she received confirmation from Noblin\u8217\'20\'19s doctor that Noblin would not use it to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/sep/26/us-abortion-bans-restrict-access-essential-medications"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  bans restrict women\u8217\'20\'19s access to other essential medicine}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  on Riggleman\u8217\'20\'19s book and the revelations therein, including more mysterious calls from White House numbers to people connected with the assault on the Capitol:\par \par \uc2 The White House switchboard dialled a phone associated with a January 6 rioter after it was clear the deadly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-capitol-breach"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Capitol attack}}}\uc2  had failed to prevent the congressional certification of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the 2020 presidential election, according to a new book.\par \par \uc2 The book from former Republican congressman and House January 6 select committee adviser Denver Riggleman says the connection was an outgoing call routed through the switchboard at 4.34pm, and it was answered by an unnamed rioter who allegedly has since been charged by the justice department with a role in the storming of the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 Riggleman\u8217\'20\'19s book, titled The Breach, was reviewed by the Guardian in advance of its scheduled publication on Tuesday, and it has already become controversial after the select committee decried the work as an incomplete account that lacked information to which he was not privy once he left the panel\u8217\'20\'19s inquiry in April.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/26/white-house-call-january-6-rioter-denver-riggleman-book-the-breach"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 White House switchboard called phone linked to January 6 rioter after attack}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 January 6 committee deputy says expect more details o Secret Service in upcoming hearing\par \par \uc2 When the January 6 committee holds its Wednesday hearing, don\u8217\'20\'19t be surprised if lawmakers have more to say about the Secret Service\u8217\'20\'19s actions that day, particularly when it comes to agents\u8217\'20\'19 communications that were deleted following the insurrection.\par \par \uc2 What was on the Secret Service text messages that the agency erased following the insurrection and whether they could be recovered have emerged as two of the biggest outstanding questions of the investigation. Over the weekend, \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  said the committee had received a trove of evidence from the agency, but not as much cooperation as they would like:\par \par \uc2 enltr1/6 Committee Vice Chair \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  (R-WY) on Saturday said the committee received \u8220\'20\'1Cabout 800,000 pages at least\u8221\'20\'1D of Secret Service communications on and around Jan. 6:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are some [agents] who have not been forthcoming with the committee, and you will hear more about that.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/lqSrEkGD1f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/lqSrEkGD1f}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1574392197855715335?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 26, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/11/missing-secret-service-texts-congress-notified-april"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Secret Service watchdog suppressed memo on January 6 texts erasure}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s one of the quieter trends in Congress, but \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/chrismcgreal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chris McGreal}}}\uc2  reports on the slowly boiling outrage over the killing of Palestinian American journalist Shireen Abu Akleh, with a sizable number of Democratic lawmakers warning of consequences if Israel isn\u8217\'20\'19t more forthcoming about her death:\par \par \uc2 Israel has declared the case closed. The US state department has done its best to duck difficult questions. But leading members of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US Congress}}}\uc2  are refusing to drop demands for a proper accounting of the death of the Palestinian American journalist, Shireen Abu Akleh, four months ago.\par \par \uc2 The longest-serving member of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US Senate}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Patrick Leahy\uc2 , recently upped the ante by warning that Israel\u8217\'20\'19s failure to fully explain the \uc2 Al-Jazeera\uc2  reporter\u8217\'20\'19s killing could jeopardize America\u8217\'20\'19s huge military aid to the Jewish state under a law he sponsored 25 years ago cutting weapons supplies to countries that abuse human rights.\par \par \uc2 Nearly half of the Democratic members of the Senate have signed a letter calling into question Israel\u8217\'20\'19s claim that Abu Akleh was accidentally shot by a soldier. The letter suggests she may have been targeted because she was a journalist.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/sep/26/shireen-abu-akleh-us-senators-israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US senators refuse to let killing of Shireen Abu Akleh drop with Israel}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  was exchanging text messages with a lot of strange characters in the closing months of 2020. One of them was Phil Waldron, an election conspiracy theorist who texted the then-White House chief of staff about an effort to root out supposed voter fraud in Arizona.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/09/26/politics/meadows-texts-phil-waldron-seize-voting-machines-election-fraud/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN reports}}}\uc2  that the news Waldron brought was that a judge in the state had dismissed the lawsuit from GOP legislators allied with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to turn over voting equipment so they could be inspected for alleged election fraud. Waldron, an associate of \uc2 Michael Flynn\uc2 , the former Trump White House national security adviser {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/michael-flynn-christian-nationalism-investigation-50fa5dcff7f99cf93409fcd6c1357bee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who has lately been known for his Christian nationalist rhetoric}}}\uc2 , said the ruling meant Trump\u8217\'20\'19s opponents could delay his allies\u8217\'20\'19 efforts to get to voting machines and prove the supposed fraud.\par \par \uc2 Meadows responded with one word: \u8220\'20\'1Cpathetic\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 CNN\u8217\'20\'19s report gets further into Waldron\u8217\'20\'19s activities in both the closing weeks of the Trump administration and in recent months, where he has continued efforts to try to prove that the 2020 election was stolen, without success.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 The January 6 committee clearly did not take the weekend off ahead of its hearing this Wednesday. Politico reports that investigators have subpoenaed \uc2 Robin Vos\uc2 , Republican speaker of the Wisconsin state assembly.\par \par \uc2 They want to know about a phone call he had in July with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and are giving him a short deadline to speak to them \u8211\'20\'13 today. Vos is suing to stop the subpoena, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/minutes/congress/09-26-2022/wisconsin-house-speaker-subpoenaed/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to Politico}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 enltrNEWS: The Jan. 6 select committee subpoenaed Wisconsin House Speaker \uc2 Robin Vos\uc2  over the weekend and is seeking his testimony by *today* about a July phone call he had with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ZQD9X84SK4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/ZQD9X84SK4}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/gfOgHpdfgK"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/gfOgHpdfgK}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1574392573980020737?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 26, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrVos is suing to block the subpoena, saying the subpoena didn't give him enough notice and oversteps the select committee's authority. He's seeking an injunction from a federal judge. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ZQD9X84SK4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/ZQD9X84SK4}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1574395140948590593?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 26, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrVos suit drew Judge Pamela Pepper, who issued a scorcher of a ruling against one of the many lawsuits aimed at overturning the 2020 election. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/hK9XMTEztb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/hK9XMTEztb}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1574397689487302658?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 26, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 As eyebrow raising as Riggleman\u8217\'20\'19s interview is, January 6 committee members have also gone out of their way to downplay it, saying he stopped working with them months ago and is not aware of what the investigation uncovered since then.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe does not know what happened after April and a lot has happened in our investigation,\u8221\'20\'1D Democratic committee member \uc2 Zoe Lofgren{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/09/26/politics/mysterious-phone-call-white-house-rioter-jan-6/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told CNN}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CEverything that he was able to relay prior to his departure has been followed up on and in some cases didn\u8217\'20\'19t really peter out (sic), or there might have been a decision that suggested there was a connection between one number and one e-mail and a person that turned out not to pan out. So we follow up on everything, and, you know, I don\u8217\'20\'19t know what Mr. Riggleman is doing really.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s also worth noting the Riggleman has a book out tomorrow called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.amazon.com/Breach-Untold-Story-Investigation-January/dp/1250866766/ref=tmm_hrd_swatch_0?_encoding=UTF8&qid=1664200303&sr=8-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Breach: The Untold Story of the Investigation into January 6th\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 CNN has more details on the call from a White House number to the phone of one of the rioters who stormed the Capitol on January 6.\par \par \uc2 The nine-second phone call went to the phone of Anton Lunyk, a Brooklyn resident who had traveled to the city for the \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  -hosted rally that preceded the attack, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/09/26/politics/mysterious-phone-call-white-house-rioter-jan-6/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN reports}}}\uc2 . Lunyk, along with two friends who came with him from New York, pled guilty to charges of illegally protesting inside the Capitol, and earlier this month where sentenced to a few months of fines and probation.\par \par \uc2 Who was on the other end of the call remains a mystery. CNN was not able to identify which White House official may have placed it, only that it took place at 4:17 pm, shortly after Trump tweeted at rioters to \u8220\'20\'1Cgo home\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Denver Riggleman\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/video/denver-riggleman-60-minutes-video-2022-09-25/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interview with 60 Minutes}}}\uc2  is a rare breach in the carefully stage managed presentation the January 6 committee has given Americans over the past months about what happened during the insurrection at the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 A former Republican congressman who was ousted by a more conservative opponent in 2020 and now considers himself independent, Riggleman acted as a technical adviser for the committee, poring through evidence such as text messages and emails obtained from people thought to have knowledge of the attack. His interview provided a behind-the-scenes look at the investigation, most details about which have come from lawmakers\u8217\'20\'19 comments or the public hearings themselves.\par \par \uc2 Perhaps his most startling admission is his belief that text messages then-White House chief of staff \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  voluntarily turned over the committee amounted to a \u8220\'20\'1Croadmap to an attempted coup.\u8221\'20\'1D But Riggleman shared other disquieting details in the interview, such as that a White House number called one of the rioters who had stormed the Capitol as it was happening.\par \par \uc2 Then there were the text messages Meadows received containing an array of far-right conspiracy theories from Ginni Thomas, wife of rightwing supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat really shook me was the fact that if Clarence agreed with or was even aware of his wife\u8217\'20\'19s efforts, all three branches of government would be tied to the stop the steal movement,\u8221\'20\'1D Riggleman said on 60 Minutes.\par \par \uc2 Ginni Thomas\u8217\'20\'19s involvement in efforts to overturn the 2020 election results has been well documented in recent months, leading to calls for the January 6 committee to compel her testimony \u8211\'20\'13 efforts Riggleman said he supported. Last week, a deal was reached for Thomas to speak to investigators.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/21/virginia-thomas-january-6-panel-interview-clarence-thomas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Virginia Thomas agrees to interview with House January 6 panel}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former January 6 committee official sees evidence of 'attempted coup'\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. There was a rare look into the January 6 committee\u8217\'20\'19s investigative process yesterday evening when a former staff member {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/video/denver-riggleman-60-minutes-video-2022-09-25/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spoke to CBS\u8217\'20\'19 60 Minutes program}}}\uc2 , and what Denver Riggleman had to say will do little to soothe the nerves of those fearing for America\u8217\'20\'19s democracy. Among his revelations, Riggleman said text messages from \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff during the time of the insurrection, amounted to a \u8220\'20\'1Croadmap to an attempted coup\u8221\'20\'1D. Expect to hear more about Riggleman\u8217\'20\'19s interview today ahead of the January 6 committee\u8217\'20\'19s first public hearing in more than two months on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we can expect today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republicans still have a good chance of winning a majority in the House of Representatives, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/house-republican-majority-shrinks-opinion-poll-2022-09-25/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 but CBS News believes}}}\uc2  it won\u8217\'20\'19t be a very large one.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor, \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2 , will hold a re-election rally in Alpharetta at 3pm ET, where he will be joined by fellow GOP governor Glenn Youngkin of Virginia.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is in Delaware but will return to the White House this morning to greet 2021 World Series champions the \uc2 Atlanta Braves\uc2 , then preside over the third meeting of the White House Competition Council in the afternoon.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220926ei9q0020a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
