\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 US anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  extremists are already waging war on IVF\b0\par\par\uc2 Arwa Mahdawi \par \uc2 1,098 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 September 2022\par 13:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Republicans have made it very clear that they aren\u8217\'20\'19t going to stop at \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 : they\u8217\'20\'19re coming for birth control and fertility treatments\par \par \uc2 Are Republicans coming for IVF?\par \par \uc2 Going through fertility treatment isn\u8217\'20\'19t fun at the best of times: it\u8217\'20\'19s expensive, invasive and emotionally exhausting. Ever since Roe v Wade was overturned earlier this year, however, getting fertility treatments in the US has become exponentially more {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.webmd.com/infertility-and-reproduction/news/20220714/fertility-doctors-ivf-families-post-roe-were-anxious"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stressful}}}\uc2  ; the end of Roe triggered a spate of new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2022/jul/16/ivf-anti-abortion-states-embryos-personhood"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 personhood bills}}}\uc2  in Republican states which define a fertilized egg or embryo as a legal human entity. If you know anything about in vitro fertilization (IVF), which I\u8217\'20\'19m not sure any of the men drafting these personhood bills do, you\u8217\'20\'19ll immediately know that makes IVF hugely complex. Numerous embryos are usually created during the IVF process as not all will be genetically viable. Unviable embryos, along with embryos that aren\u8217\'20\'19t donated or frozen for later use, will be disposed. If these collections of cells are considered people then, according to the personhood laws, you\u8217\'20\'19ve committed a crime by disposing of them.\par \par \uc2 Hang on a second, you might say. If you have the gall to call yourself \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-life\u8221\'20\'1D then shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t you be making it easier for people who desperately want children to be able to have them? Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  extremists may be a bunch of raging {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2018/aug/25/a-republican-theme-on-abortions-its-ok-for-me-evil-for-thee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hypocrites}}}\uc2  who have demonstrated time and time again that they {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2019/apr/11/death-sentence-abortion-hypocrisy-pro-life"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 don\u8217\'20\'19t care about the sanctity of life}}}\uc2 , they just care about controlling women, but surely they\u8217\'20\'19re not going to wage war on IVF?\par \par \uc2 Sara Chambers, a 25-year-old from Tennessee who is currently going through IVF, had this very question. Tennessee is one of the most restrictive states when it comes to reproductive rights: the disingenuously named Human Life Protection Act {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tennesseelookout.com/briefs/tennessees-abortion-ban-to-be-codified-into-law-in-30-days/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 essentially outlaws}}}\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and declares that life begins at fertilization not implantation. Wondering what the law meant for her treatment, Chambers emailed her representative, Ryan Williams, asking whether she could discard her embryos without it being considered an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Williams\u8217\'20\'19s reply? Hell no. \u8220\'20\'1CLife does begin at conception either in the womb or in the IVF clinic,\u8221\'20\'1D Williams told her Chambers in an email she shared on a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tiktok.com/@sarammchambers/video/7143585565219294506"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 viral TikTok video}}}\uc2  ; if a doctor got rid of those embryos it would be a crime. Williams couldn\u8217\'20\'19t resist a little moralizing also. \u8220\'20\'1CI admit it is an unusual question for someone who struggled to have children and wants children to ask the question \u8216\'20\'18can I discard my embryos\u8217\'20\'19 but I hope this answers your questions,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 In her TikTok video Chambers said she felt judged by Williams\u8217\'20\'19s reply. She also felt scared about her options. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t want to transfer embryos that I know I have to miscarry, I want to save myself that heartache,\u8221\'20\'1D Chambers said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I don\u8217\'20\'19t want to have 20 children.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Williams may be just one politician but, make no mistake, he\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/12/ivf-treatment-us-anti-abortion-laws-bills"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 no outlier}}}\uc2  when it comes to this issue. Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  extremists aren\u8217\'20\'19t going to wage war on IVF, they\u8217\'20\'19re already doing so. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s hard for people to fathom that this is actually happening,\u8221\'20\'1D Chambers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jessica.substack.com/p/we-just-want-to-be-parents"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the feminist journalist Jessica Valenti}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThis is real, and it\u8217\'20\'19s happening right now.\u8221\'20\'1D Republicans have made it very clear that they aren\u8217\'20\'19t going to stop at just overturning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 : they\u8217\'20\'19re {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/may/25/banning-abortions-is-just-the-start-next-the-us-right-want-to-outlaw-contraception"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 coming for birth control}}}\uc2  and fertility treatments. They won\u8217\'20\'19t be happy until they\u8217\'20\'19ve taken away every aspect of women\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive autonomy.\par \par \uc2 Protests erupt in Iran after the death of Mahsa Amini\par \par \uc2 The 22-year-old\u8217\'20\'19s death in Iranian police custody has set off protests all over the country and could \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2022/sep/23/mahsa-amini-death-could-be-spark-broader-political-action-iran"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 be the spark that ignites Iran around women\u8217\'20\'19s rights}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D. Amini was allegedly arrested by the country\u8217\'20\'19s morality police for showing her hair and breaking the laws on wearing a hijab; her father has said she was beaten to death in custody. The backlash has been immense; British Iranian actor Omid Djalili has called it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/09/21/1124237272/mahsa-amini-iran-women-protest-hijab-morality-police"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIran\u8217\'20\'19s George Floyd\u8221\'20\'1D moment}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 CNN says Iran\u8217\'20\'19s president tried to make a hijab a condition for interview\par \par \uc2 An interview between CNN\u8217\'20\'19s chief international anchor, Christiane Amanpour, and the Iranian president, \uc2 Ebrahim Raisi\uc2 , was cancelled after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/09/22/1124559417/cnn-christiane-amanpour-raisi-iran-hijab"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amanpour refused to wear a hijab}}}\uc2 . It seems likely that Raisi wanted to capture an image of New York-based Amanpour wearing a hijab to use as propaganda \u8211\'20\'13 a signal to women protesting back in Iran. Good for Amanpour on refusing to let herself be used that way.\par \par \uc2 Josh Hawley thinks there\u8217\'20\'19s only one gender\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.huffpost.com/entry/josh-hawley-gender_n_632d5497e4b09d8701be4c6d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fundraising email}}}\uc2 , the conservative lawmaker and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/nov/06/josh-hawley-is-right-that-men-arent-doing-well-but-its-because-of-toxic-people-like-him"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 self-proclaimed expert on manliness}}}\uc2  said that teaching children that \u8220\'20\'1Cmore than one gender\u8221\'20\'1D exists is \u8220\'20\'1Ctransgender propaganda\u8221\'20\'1D. Bit of a Freudian slip there, Josh. Why not just come out and say directly that you don\u8217\'20\'19t think women are people?\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18How many women were abused to make that \uc2 Tesla\uc2 ?\u8217\'20\'19\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rollingstone.com/culture/culture-features/tesla-sexual-harassment-lawsuit-investigation-elon-musk-1234590697/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Seven women are suing}}}\uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s electric car company alleging sexual harassment.\par \par \uc2 How Russia\u8217\'20\'19s trolls undermined the US Women\u8217\'20\'19s March movement\par \par \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  has a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/09/18/us/womens-march-russia-trump.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 must-read report}}}\uc2  on how Russia\u8217\'20\'19s Internet Research Agency used online trolls to attack the Women\u8217\'20\'19s March and fracture alliances on the left. The trolls tested out different messages, but the best performing attacks were on Women\u8217\'20\'19s March co-chair \uc2 Linda Sarsour\uc2 , a Palestinian American activist who wears a hijab. One hundred and fifty-two different Russian accounts produced material on Sarsour, upending her life and damaging her reputation.\par \par \uc2 The week in poultryarchy\par \par \uc2 Last week, the \uc2 US Food and Drug Administration{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fda.gov/consumers/consumer-updates/recipe-danger-social-media-challenges-involving-medicines"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issued a warning}}}\uc2  : don\u8217\'20\'19t cook chicken in NyQuil or other cough and cold medicine. Why would anyone do that in the first place? Because of a TikTok food challenge, according to the \uc2 FDA\uc2 . Media outlets jumped all over the warning. Crazy kids are all eating poisonous chicken for TikTok Likes is a tempting narrative after all. But it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.eater.com/23365749/sleepy-nyquil-chicken-tiktok-stunt-food"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would appear that rumours of a NyQuil chicken challenge}}}\uc2  are grossly exaggerated. As Eater noted: \u8220\'20\'1CNyQuil chicken proves one of our worst collective tendencies online: to see something, take it at face value, and amplify it \u8230\'20\'26 What we ultimately do is bring a sense of legitimacy to that thing \u8211\'20\'13 if enough news sites tell you not to cook NyQuil chicken, it might start to seem like lots of people are actually cooking NyQuil chicken.\u8221\'20\'1D (OK, but, also, please don\u8217\'20\'19t cook NyQuil chicken.)\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220924ei9o001up\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
