\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US intelligence resumes national security review of Mar-a-Lago documents \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein in Washington \par \uc2 4,221 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 September 2022\par 12:35 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  says attacks Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 midterms agenda, saying real goal is to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwideSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 With an eye to reclaiming their majority, House Republicans have released their Commitment to America \u8211\'20\'13 which is not to be confused with 1994\u8217\'20\'19s Contract with America or 2010\u8217\'20\'19s Pledge to America unveiled before the party won the chamber in those years\u8217\'20\'19 midterms. \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/23/trump-biden-midterms-republicans-democrats-us-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-632de9718f0894f47d8a440f#block-632de9718f0894f47d8a440f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 responded to the plan}}}\uc2  by hammering the \u8220\'20\'1CMaga Republicans\u8221\'20\'1D he said want to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide and slash social security.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 Twitter\uc2  whistleblower whose anonymous testimony was made public by the January 6 committee warned of the peril facing America\u8217\'20\'19s democracy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/23/trump-biden-midterms-republicans-democrats-us-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-632de2988f0822acf24f568b#block-632de2988f0822acf24f568b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in an interview with The Washington Post}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 US intelligenceagencies{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/23/trump-biden-midterms-republicans-democrats-us-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-632e042b8f0894f47d8a4550#block-632e042b8f0894f47d8a4550"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have restarted their assessment}}}\uc2  of the risk to national security posed by the documents found at Mar-a-Lago.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 White House officials are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/23/trump-biden-midterms-republicans-democrats-us-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-632ddb378f0822acf24f5608#block-632ddb378f0822acf24f5608"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said to be mulling}}}\uc2  an effort to oust the Trump-installed \uc2 World Bank\uc2  president after he quibbled over whether humans caused climate change.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Former supreme court justice \uc2 Stephen Breyer{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/23/trump-biden-midterms-republicans-democrats-us-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-632dd1498f0822acf24f5552#block-632dd1498f0822acf24f5552"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expressed remorse}}}\uc2  over its decision ending Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Lawyers for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  are citing legal privilege to try to stop former White House officials from answering questions before a federal grand jury investigating his attempts to meddle with the 2020 election, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/09/23/politics/trump-grand-jury-court-fight/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The effort shows how attorneys for Trump hope to seize on both executive privilege conferred on presidents as well as attorney-client privilege to frustrate the investigation by the grand jury in Washington. His attorneys had made similar claims when they successfully petitioned a judge to appoint a special master to review documents seized from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago resort, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/21/donald-trump-mar-a-lago-records-hold-lifted"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a ruling that also temporarily halted}}}\uc2  the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s probe into the materials found there.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from CNN\u8217\'20\'19s story:\par \par \uc2 Former President Donald Trump\u8216\'20\'18s attorneys are fighting a secret court battle to block a federal grand jury from gathering information from an expanding circle of close Trump aides about his efforts to overturn the 2020 election, people briefed on the matter told CNN.\par \par \uc2 The high-stakes legal dispute -- which included the appearance of three attorneys representing Trump at the Washington, DC, federal courthouse on Thursday afternoon -- is the most aggressive step taken by the former President to assert executive and attorney-client privileges in order to prevent some witnesses from sharing information in the criminal investigation events surrounding January 6, 2021.\par \par \uc2 The court fight over privilege, which has not been previously reported and is under seal, is a turning point for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s post-presidency legal woes.\par \par \uc2 How the fight is resolved could determine whether prosecutors can tear down the firewall Trump has tried to keep around his conversations in the West Wing and with attorneys he spoke to as he sought to overturn the 2020 election and they worked to help him hold onto the presidency.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Michael Avenatti\uc2  was once a firebrand attorney and darling of those who loathed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Now he\u8217\'20\'19s been disgraced by a series of criminal convictions, and today was ordered to pay restitution to former client Stormy Daniels, who claimed to have had an affair with the former president.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/legal/michael-avenatti-ordered-pay-148750-restitution-stormy-daniels-2022-09-23/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Reuters reports}}}\uc2  that a Manhattan court ordered Avenatti to pay Daniels $148,750 after his conviction earlier this year on wire fraud and aggravated identity theft charges for embezzling her book proceeds.\par \par \uc2 He was sentenced to four years in prison in that case, and is also awaiting sentencing after pleading guilty to five federal charges in California.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/02/michael-avenatti-sentencing-stormy-daniels-book-deal-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michael Avenatti sentenced to four years for cheating Stormy Daniels}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 US intelligence resumes national security review of Mar-a-Lago documents after court ruling\par \par \uc2 American intelligence agencies have again begun their review of the national security risks of classified documents found at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago resort after an appeals court overturned a judge\u8217\'20\'19s order that had temporarily blocked it, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/09/23/national-security-risk-review-of-material-trump-kept-at-mar-a-lago-resumes-after-appeals-court-ruling-00058648"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The review is one of two that director of national intelligence \uc2 Avril Haines\uc2  said would be done of the documents the \uc2 FBI\uc2  found at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Florida resort last month: one focused on their classification levels, the other on what would happen if their contents were made public.\par \par \uc2 Trump-appointed federal judge Aileen Cannon had granted a request from the former president to halt the review of the seized material, but that was thrown out by an appeals court earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/21/donald-trump-mar-a-lago-records-hold-lifted"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Court lifts hold on classified records seized from Mar-a-Lago in Trump inquiry}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 More on Sinema: a recent poll on the senator found that she was viewed unfavorably by all political parties and across all demographic categories.\par \par \uc2 A poll conducted by AARP Arizona on the current political environment found that a majority of voters in both political parties did not view Sinema favorably, including across all age categories, genders, as well as racial and ethnic demographics.\par \par \uc2 The poll results can be viewed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aarp.org/content/dam/aarp/research/surveys_statistics/politics/2022/aarp-arizona-2022-elections-voter-survey-governor.doi.10.26419-2Fres.00550.011.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 In other news, Senator \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  of Arizona will be giving a talk on Monday at the McConnell Center, an institution named after Republican senator \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  that connects young people in Kentucky with political leaders.\par \par \uc2 The center advertised the talk on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , writing:\par \par \uc2 This Monday, Sept. 26, the McConnell Center is excited to welcome U.S. Senator \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  (D-AZ) to give a talk titled \u8220\'20\'1CThe Future of Political Discourse and the Importance of Bipartisanship.\u8221\'20\'1D Join via livestream at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/F7epAlno78"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://McConnellCenter.org}}}\uc2  at 10 AM.\par \par \uc2 enltrThis Monday, Sept. 26, the McConnell Center is excited to welcome U.S. Senator \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  (D-AZ) to give a talk titled "The Future of Political Discourse and the Importance of Bipartisanship." Join via livestream at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/F7epAlno78"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/F7epAlno78}}}\uc2  at 10 AM. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Leadership?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Leadership}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/t0LO0ZazOi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/t0LO0ZazOi}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 McConnell Center (@ULmCenter) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ULmCenter/status/1573357113627271171?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 23, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Reaction to Sinema\u8217\'20\'19s upcoming talk was somewhat negative, as users criticized the first-time senator for agreeing to give a talk at McConnell\u8217\'20\'19s namesake institution given McConnell\u8217\'20\'19s voting record.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 With an eye to reclaiming their majority, House Republicans have released their Commitment to America \u8211\'20\'13 which is not to be confused with 1994\u8217\'20\'19s Contract with America or 2010\u8217\'20\'19s Pledge to America unveiled before they reclaimed the chamber in those years\u8217\'20\'19 midterms. \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/23/trump-biden-midterms-republicans-democrats-us-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-632de9718f0894f47d8a440f#block-632de9718f0894f47d8a440f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 responded to the plan}}}\uc2  by hammering the \u8220\'20\'1CMaga Republicans\u8221\'20\'1D he said want to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide and slash social security.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 Twitter\uc2  whistleblower whose anonymous testimony was made public by the January 6 committee warned of the peril facing America\u8217\'20\'19s democracy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/23/trump-biden-midterms-republicans-democrats-us-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-632de2988f0822acf24f568b#block-632de2988f0822acf24f568b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in an interview with The Washington Post}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 White House officials are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/23/trump-biden-midterms-republicans-democrats-us-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-632ddb378f0822acf24f5608#block-632ddb378f0822acf24f5608"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said to be mulling}}}\uc2  an effort to oust the Trump-installed \uc2 World Bank\uc2  president after he quibbled over whether humans caused climate change.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Former supreme court justice \uc2 Stephen Breyer{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/23/trump-biden-midterms-republicans-democrats-us-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-632dd1498f0822acf24f5552#block-632dd1498f0822acf24f5552"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expressed remorse}}}\uc2  over its decision ending Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 This speech has amounted to a point-by-point rebuttal of House Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.republicanleader.gov/commitment/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Commitment to America}}}\uc2 , and as he wrapped up the speech, he turned to its call to \u8220\'20\'1Cincrease accountability in the election process\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd finally, with a straight face, Kevin McCarthy says that Maga Republicans will restore faith in our elections. As we say in my faith, bless me father for I have sinned,\u8221\'20\'1D said Biden, a practicing Catholic. \u8220\'20\'1CMaga Republicans refused to accept the results of the 2020 election and the will of the people.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou can\u8217\'20\'19t let the integrity of elections be undermined,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen one side believes there\u8217\'20\'19s only two outcomes in an election, either they win or they were cheated, that\u8217\'20\'19s not democracy. And that\u8217\'20\'19s where the mass majority of Maga Republicans are today. They don\u8217\'20\'19t understand what every patriotic American knows: you can\u8217\'20\'19t love your country only when you win.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden is hitting back at House Republicans and the Commitment to America plan they announced today, calling it \u8220\'20\'1Ca thin series of policy goals\u8221\'20\'1D and saying the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s true goal is banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide.\par \par \uc2 He cited the words of rightwing supreme court justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bridgemi.com/michigan-government/key-quotes-fridays-us-supreme-court-abortion-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who wrote in his opinion overturning Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  that the decision \u8220\'20\'1Callows women on both sides of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue to seek to affect the legislative process by influencing public opinion.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t believe Maga Republicans have a clue about the power American women,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said to applause in his speech stumping on behalf of the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Referring to the plan announced by top House Republican Kevin McCarthy, Biden said, \u8220\'20\'1CHere\u8217\'20\'19s a few of the things we didn\u8217\'20\'19t hear. We didn\u8217\'20\'19t hear mentioned the right to choose. We didn\u8217\'20\'19t hear mentioned Medicare. We didn\u8217\'20\'19t hear mentioned social security.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He went on to link the upcoming midterms to continuing availability of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in America, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CIn 46 days, America is going to choose. If Republicans win control of the Congress, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be banned. And by the way, it will be initially banned, but if they win Congress, I will veto it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This post was amended on 24 September 2022 to correct a mistranscription of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s remarks about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re about to hear from President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  at an event hosted by the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2 , where he\u8217\'20\'19ll no doubt stump for the party and potentially respond to House Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 Commitment to America plan announced today.\par \par \uc2 You can follow the event at the headquarters of the \uc2 National Education Association{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.c-span.org/video/?523136-1/president-biden-remarks-democratic-national-committee-event&live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWithout intervention we really are on this path to catastrophe.\u8221\'20\'1D Those are the chilling words of former \uc2 Twitter\uc2  employee Anika Collier Navaroli, whose anonymous testimony to the January 6 committee was shared last July, and who has now made her name public {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/technology/2022/09/22/jan6-committee-twitter-witness-navaroli/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in an interview with the Washington Post}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 She recounted how the platform relished the attention brought by Trump as he turned \uc2 Twitter\uc2  into a bully pulpit to rival all others, and downplayed her concerns that he was inciting violence:\par \par \uc2 After Trump told the Proud Boys, a far-right group with a history of violence, at a September 2020 presidential debate to \u8220\'20\'1Cstand back and stand by,\u8221\'20\'1D Navaroli pushed for the company to adopt a stricter policy around calls to incitement.\par \par \uc2 Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cwas speaking directly to extremist organizations and giving them directives,\u8221\'20\'1D she told the committee. \u8220\'20\'1CWe had not seen that sort of direct communication before, and that concerned me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She had also seen how his tweets were quickly sparking replies from other accounts calling for \u8220\'20\'1Ccivil war.\u8221\'20\'1D After Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cwill be wild\u8221\'20\'1D tweet in December, she said, \u8220\'20\'1Cit became clear not only were these individuals ready and willing, but the leader of their cause was asking them to join him in \u8230\'20\'26 fighting for this cause in D.C. on January 6th.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The company, however, declined to take action, she told the committee. She pleaded with managers, she said, to face the \u8220\'20\'1Creality that \u8230\'20\'26 if we made no intervention into what I saw occurring, people were going to die.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the interview with the Post, Navaroli called on other whistleblowers to come forward while warning that America\u8217\'20\'19s democracy may be irrevocably damaged:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy fear within the American context is that we have seen our last peaceful transition of power,\u8221\'20\'1D Navaroli said. But \u8220\'20\'1Cthe same playbook,\u8221\'20\'1D she added, is being used around the world, \u8220\'20\'1Cteeing up the idea that if an election is not in someone\u8217\'20\'19s favor, it\u8217\'20\'19s been rigged. Without intervention we really are on this path to catastrophe.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 World Bank\uc2  president \uc2 David Malpass\uc2  may be in the Biden Administration\u8217\'20\'19s crosshairs. Photograph: Issei Kato/Reuters\par \par \uc2 The Trump-appointed \uc2 World Bank\uc2  president \uc2 David Malpass\uc2  is under fire for deflecting on the question of humans causing climate change, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2022/09/23/world-bank-malpass-climate-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Axios reports}}}\uc2  the Biden administration is mulling an effort to remove him.\par \par \uc2 Appointed in 2019, Malpass, a Republican, worked in the Treasury under Trump and also at global financial crisis-casualty \uc2 Bear Stearns\uc2 . While Axios reports Biden officials have long been suspicious of him, the uproar began when Malpass replied, \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t even know -- I\u8217\'20\'19m not a scientist and that is not a question,\u8221\'20\'1D when asked at an event on Tuesday if he believed climate change is manmade.\par \par \uc2 While advocates for actions against climate change, including Democratic president \uc2 Al Gore\uc2 , have called for his ouster, it\u8217\'20\'19s not clear if the White House has the ability to boot him, since it does not control the executive directors board that appoints leader of the global development lender.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Malpass has tried to smooth over the situation, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/09/22/world/world-bank-david-malpass-climate-change-intl-hnk/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 telling CNN on Thursday}}}\uc2  he is \u8220\'20\'1Cnot a denier\u8221\'20\'1D of climate change.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ex-supreme court justice Breyer 'very sorry' about overturning of Roe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights\par \par \uc2 Recently retired \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  justice \uc2 Stephen Breyer\uc2  says he did \u8220\'20\'1Ceverything\u8221\'20\'1D he could to stop the highest bench in the land overturning {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  to strip US woman of their federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, and is \u8220\'20\'1Cvery very sorry\u8221\'20\'1D the decision was made.\par \par \uc2 In his first television interview since retiring earlier this year, Breyer told journalist Chris Wallace that he disagreed with the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mississippi Dobbs case}}}\uc2  that including the overthrowing of Roe, announced in June.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWas I happy about it? Not for an instant. Did I do everything I could to persuade people? Of course, of course. But there we are, and now we go on. We try to work together,\u8221\'20\'1D he said in the interview that aired on HBO Max today and airs on CNN on Sunday evening.\par \par \uc2 Breyer, 84, said: \u8220\'20\'1CDid I like this Dobbs decision? Of course I didn\u8217\'20\'19t. Of course I didn\u8217\'20\'19t.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He tells Wallace it was frustrating to be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/sep/11/john-roberts-defends-supreme-court-kamala-harris-abortion-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in the minority}}}\uc2  on the court, in terms of justices leaning liberal. The court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative majority was consolidated and then expanded by the Trump administration. The final addition under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  of ultra-conservative {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/amy-coney-barrett%27"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett}}}\uc2  in 2020, replacing the late liberal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ruth-bader-ginsburg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ruth Bader Ginsb}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ruth-bader-ginsburg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 urg}}}\uc2  , gave the nine-judge bench a six-three super majority in favor of judges leaning right.\par \par \uc2 Breyer announced in January that he would retire and he left the bench this summer, replaced by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s nominee, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ketanji-brown-jackson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ketanji Brown Jackson}}}\uc2  , who became the first Black woman on the court.\par \par \uc2 Breyer was one of the least high-profile justices. He lamented to Wallace the increasing rigidity of the conservatives on the bench.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou start writing too rigidly and you will see, the world will come around and bite you in the back. Because you will find something you see just doesn\u8217\'20\'19t work at all. And the supreme court, somewhat to the difference of others, has that kind of problem in spades.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLife is complex, life changes, and we want to maintain insofar as we can -- everybody does \u8211\'20\'13 certain key moral political values: democracy, human rights, equality, rule of law, etc. To try to do that in an ever-changing world. If you think you can do that by writing 16 computer programs \u8211\'20\'13 I just disagree.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Breyer concluded that he was \u8220\'20\'1Cvery, very sorry\u8221\'20\'1D about the overturning of Roe v Wade. He also said the unprecedented and still-mysterious {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/02/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-draft-opinion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leak in May}}}\uc2  of that draft decision, which was penned by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/may/06/samuel-alito-profile-abortion-supreme-court-justice"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ultra-conservative justice }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/may/06/samuel-alito-profile-abortion-supreme-court-justice"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Samuel Alito}}}\uc2  in the drafting and the final version, was \u8220\'20\'1Cvery damaging\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Stephen Breyer\uc2  in January, 2022. Photograph: Andrew Harnik/AP\par \par \uc2 Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  earlier this month criticized what she dubbed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/09/kamala-harris-activist-supreme-court-roe-v-wade-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an \u8220\'20\'1Cactivist\u8221\'20\'1D court}}}\uc2  and said the US was suffering as a nation since the court took away the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , leaving it up to individual states to decide on the law over the procedure.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republicans might be gunning for the House majority, but they have apparently thrown in the towel in one race.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2022/09/22/house-republicans-ohio-trump-majewski?utm_medium=social&utm_source=twitter&utm_campaign=editorial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Axios reports}}}\uc2  that the National Republican Congressional Committee tasked with winning House seats for the GOP has withdrawn $1m in television advertisements for J R Majewski, who is trying to unseat longtime Democratic incumbent \uc2 Marcy Kaptur\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It wasn\u8217\'20\'19t his embrace of the QAnon conspiracy theory that did him in. Nor his call for states that supported \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to secede from the union. Not even his participation in the January 6 insurrection.\par \par \uc2 No, it was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/2022-midterm-elections-afghanistan-ohio-campaigns-e75d2566635f11f49332bd1c46711999"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an Associated Press report}}}\uc2  that revealed Majewski did not see combat while deployed to Afghanistan following 9/11 attacks, as he had claimed, but rather loaded airplanes in Qatar for six months. Majewski remains in the race and is spending his time decrying \u8220\'20\'1Cfake news\u8221\'20\'1D, but it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear if he can recover from the news.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/13/jr-majewski-trump-ohio-republican-candidate-capitol-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Ultra-Maga\u8217\'20\'19: the Trump-backed Ohio Republican candidate who attacked the Capitol}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Much as today\u8217\'20\'19s high inflation may benefit Republicans, Democrats have their own advantage they are hoping to work as they woo voters ahead of the midterms: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 To be more specific, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and everything that happened during and since his presidency. While the Commitment to America top House Republican Kevin McCarthy rolled out today focuses on quality-of-life issues like fighting crime and lowering the cost of living, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s allies are eager to remind Americans that\u8217\'20\'19s not all Republicans stand for.\par \par \uc2 House majority leader \uc2 Steny Hoyer\uc2  has distributed a list of eight questions Democrats have for Republicans about their platform, which takes aim at many House members \u8211\'20\'13 including McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s \u8211\'20\'13 defense of Trump. \u8220\'20\'1CWho won the 2020 Presidential Election?\u8221\'20\'1D the list asks. \u8220\'20\'1CLike President Trump, do you believe that the January 6 insurrectionists were engaged in \u8216\'20\'18legitimate political discourse\u8217\'20\'19 and should not be prosecuted for their violent actions?\u8221\'20\'1D it continues. \u8220\'20\'1CDo you support defunding the \uc2 FBI\uc2  in retaliation for executing a search warrant at Mar-a-Lago?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It also seizes on the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and attempts to cut costs for Americans, particularly when it comes to health care. \u8220\'20\'1CWill Republicans pursue a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban?\u8221\'20\'1D Hoyer asks. \u8220\'20\'1CIf given the chance, will you try again to repeal the Affordable Care Act and strip health-care access away from millions of Americans?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Newt Gingrich, once a power player in Washington, today less so. Photograph: Shawn Thew/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 Are you a follower of American politics in your 30s or older? Do the words \u8220\'20\'1CCommitment to America\u8221\'20\'1D sound familiar to you, but you can\u8217\'20\'19t quite put your finger on it?\par \par \uc2 You are definitely on to something. In 1994, the top Republican in the House Newt Gingrich rolled out the Contract with America which contained pledges to, among other things, fight crime and strengthen the economy \u8211\'20\'13 as Kevin McCarthy promised today in his Commitment to America. There are, of course, differences germane to the times. Gingrich, for instance, promised to tighten down on American troops\u8217\'20\'19 ability to serve in \uc2 United Nations peacekeeping missions\uc2 , while McCarthy has the issue of inflation to campaign on, which today is at rates not seen since the 1980s.\par \par \uc2 McCarthy clearly hopes to pull off what Gingrich did in the midterms held 28 years ago: wipe out the Democrats and decisively take control of the House. Indeed, the GOP won 54 seats and pushed House Democrats into the minority for the first time since 1954, with Gingrich as speaker until his resignation in 1999.\par \par \uc2 The similarities aren\u8217\'20\'19t lost on opponents of today\u8217\'20\'19s Republican Party. The anti-Trump Lincoln Project has released an advertisement highlighting the connection:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Speaking in Pennsylvania, top House Republican Kevin McCarthy went through a laundry list of perceived Democratic failings to pitch his party as the right one to control Congress.\par \par \uc2 Among them were topics familiar to anyone who has heard a Republican speak over the last two years: inflation is too high and so is crime, the border isn\u8217\'20\'19t secure and fentanyl is killing too many. McCarthy also made mention of some specific Biden policies that have lately become targets for GOP attacks, saying he\u8217\'20\'19d {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/19/irs-republicans-target-misinformation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stop the hiring of new IRS agents}}}\uc2  and blaming the president\u8217\'20\'19s American Rescue Plan spending bill enacted last year {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/jun/07/janet-yellen-inflation-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for fueling inflation}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey control the House, the Senate, the White House, they control the committees they control the agencies. It\u8217\'20\'19s their plan, but they have no plan to fix all the problems they created,\u8221\'20\'1D McCarthy said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats have failed you, elect us instead. That\u8217\'20\'19s the message top House Republican Kevin McCarthy delivers in the video below, which was released ahead of the debut of the party\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bvv8ztUdBZw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Commitment to America platform}}}\uc2  happening right now in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 The California representative hones in on high inflation, rising crime and migrant and asylum seekers\u8217\'20\'19 arrival at the southern border. Considering the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/2022-election-forecast/house/?cid=rrpromo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 likelihood of Republicans again winning a majority}}}\uc2  in the House following the midterms, it\u8217\'20\'19s a message worth paying attention to:\par \par \uc2 The platform\u8217\'20\'19s debut {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bvv8ztUdBZw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 can be watched live here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump isn\u8217\'20\'19t alone in spending big to get Republicans who deny \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election win into power in November. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/peter-stone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Peter Stone}}}\uc2  reports that Pacs controlled by multibillionaire \uc2 Charles Koch\uc2  are spending big to support Republicans:\par \par \uc2 Fossil fuel giant \uc2 Koch Industries\uc2  has poured over $1m into backing \u8211\'20\'13 directly and indirectly \u8211\'20\'13 dozens of House and Senate candidates who voted against certifying \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s win on 6 January 2021.\par \par \uc2 Koch, which is controlled by multibillionaire \uc2 Charles Koch\uc2 , boasts a corporate Pac that has donated $607,000 to the campaigns or leadership Pacs of 52 election deniers since January 2021, making Koch\u8217\'20\'19s Pac the top corporate funder of members who opposed the election results, according to OpenSecrets, which tracks campaign spending.\par \par \uc2 In addition, the Super Pac \uc2 Americans for Prosperity\uc2  Action to which \uc2 Koch Industries\uc2  has given over $6m since January 2021, has backed some election deniers with advertising and other communications support, as well as a few candidates \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has endorsed who tried to help him overturn the 2020 election, or raised doubts about the final results.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/23/koch-bankrolls-election-denier-candidates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alarm as Koch bankrolls dozens of election denier candidates }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s no secret that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  would like to run for the White House again. The bigger question is when will he announce a 2024 campaign? Reports in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/07/14/trump-2024-announcement-fall/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/07/01/us/politics/trump-republicans-campaign-2024.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 weeks}}}\uc2  emphasize that Democrats would love if he did so before the midterms, so they can once again remind voters of the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s ties to the polarizing former president.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/09/23/trump-midterms-2024-pac-00058515?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=12069c7e-e346-405c-ad2c-71cb1a62e514&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The announcement of Maga, Inc}}}\uc2 , the new Super Pac run by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s allies, doesn\u8217\'20\'19t answer that question, but it does show that the former president is willing to work to get the lawmakers he wants elected in the Senate and elsewhere. That\u8217\'20\'19s welcome news for Kevin McCarthy and \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , the GOP leaders of the House and Senate, respectively, who hope voters will give them a majority following the 8 November midterms.\par \par \uc2 But it would also give Trump the chance to make sure candidates he favors win their elections \u8211\'20\'13 potentially putting politicians who support his baseless claims of fraud in the 2020 election in positions of power.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Embattled Trump aims funding firepower at loyal Republicans\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. It might be hard to believe, but the midterms are about to get even more Trumpier. The former president is poised to spend millions of dollars supporting candidates loyal to his wing of the Republican party through a new super PAC launched by his top allies, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/09/23/trump-midterms-2024-pac-00058515?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=12069c7e-e346-405c-ad2c-71cb1a62e514&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reports this morning}}}\uc2 . It isn\u8217\'20\'19t just an effort to bolster embattled GOP politicians nationwide \u8211\'20\'13 it may also be a prelude to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s widely expected announcement of a second run for the White House.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s not all that\u8217\'20\'19s going on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 House GOP leader Kevin McCarthy will debut the party\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CCommitment to America\u8221\'20\'1D platform as he hopes for a return to the majority in Congress\u8217\'20\'19s lower chamber.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump will hold a rally in North Carolina at 7 pm eastern time, where we could hear more about his plans for the midterms.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Elton John performs at the White House at 8 pm this evening, where president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will also give remarks.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220923ei9n0028o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
