\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Special master asks Trump team for proof of claims that \uc2 FBI\uc2  planted evidence \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein \par \uc2 5,230 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 September 2022\par 20:33 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Special master also gives series of deadlines after judges overturn ruling that temporarily blocked DoJ from the materialSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 The legal offensive against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  flared anew after a federal appeals court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/22/trump-mar-a-lago-records-justice-department-new-york-lawsuit-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-632c5abd8f08146227062153#block-632c5abd8f08146227062153"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cleared the justice department to continue reviewing documents}}}\uc2  seized from Mar-a-Lago as it probes his potentially unlawful retention of government secrets. Meanwhile, a senior federal judge demanded the former president\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/22/trump-mar-a-lago-records-justice-department-new-york-lawsuit-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-632ca7768f0891514fe7a225#block-632ca7768f0891514fe7a225"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 provide proof}}}\uc2  of claims that the \uc2 FBI\uc2  planted documents.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ginni Thomas, the wife of rightwing supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  and a supporter of efforts to keep \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  from getting into the White House, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/22/trump-mar-a-lago-records-justice-department-new-york-lawsuit-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-632c77bf8f0891514fe79eec#block-632c77bf8f0891514fe79eec"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will speak to the January 6 committee}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A slew of polls show tights races in battleground states like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/22/trump-mar-a-lago-records-justice-department-new-york-lawsuit-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-632c7c118f0891514fe79f3f#block-632c7c118f0891514fe79f3f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/22/trump-mar-a-lago-records-justice-department-new-york-lawsuit-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-632c889f8f0822acf24f47d0#block-632c889f8f0822acf24f47d0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona}}}\uc2 , Americans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/22/trump-mar-a-lago-records-justice-department-new-york-lawsuit-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-632c6b7c8f0814622706220b#block-632c6b7c8f0814622706220b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fired up to vote nationwide and Democrats with a slight lead on the generic congressional ballot}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 There appear to be enough votes for the Senate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/22/trump-mar-a-lago-records-justice-department-new-york-lawsuit-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-632c72d28f089a550b8aa85c#block-632c72d28f089a550b8aa85c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to pass a bill}}}\uc2  to prevent the type of legal schemes Trump\u8217\'20\'19s allies tried to execute on January 6 to stop the certification of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s election win.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Manhattan attorney general said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/22/trump-mar-a-lago-records-justice-department-new-york-lawsuit-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-632c60bc8f08f4c4bf5d80c6#block-632c60bc8f08f4c4bf5d80c6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his investigation into Trump}}}\uc2  and his organization is continuing.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Secretary of state Antony Blinken{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/22/trump-mar-a-lago-records-justice-department-new-york-lawsuit-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-632c8b438f0894f47d8a3507#block-632c8b438f0894f47d8a3507"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called on countries}}}\uc2  to speak out against Russia\u8217\'20\'19s nuclear threats in a speech at the United Nations.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Indiana\u8217\'20\'19sabortion ban was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/22/trump-mar-a-lago-records-justice-department-new-york-lawsuit-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-632c9e328f0891514fe7a198#block-632c9e328f0891514fe7a198"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked by a judge}}}\uc2  who found the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution likely protects access to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere on Capitol Hill, activists declared that America was in a \u8220\'20\'1Cmoral crisis\u8221\'20\'1D as they called for more help for the poor, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/joan-greve"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joan E Greve}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 A coalition of faith leaders gathered on Capitol Hill on Thursday to deliver an impassioned demand for more congressional action to combat poverty, telling lawmakers they have a moral obligation to improve life for low-income Americans.\par \par \uc2 The faith leaders called on the Democratic leaders of the House and Senate to take at least three votes on major progressive issues before midterm elections in November.\par \par \uc2 They emphasized the importance of putting lawmakers \u8220\'20\'1Con the record\u8221\'20\'1D about strengthening voting rights, raising wages and reinstating pandemic-era policies aimed at lifting families out of poverty.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2022/sep/22/us-faith-leaders-urge-lawmakers-combat-poverty"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We\u8217\'20\'19re in a moral crisis\u8217\'20\'19: US faith leaders urge lawmakers to combat poverty}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Environmental leaders protesting against new legislation which would scale back regulations to expedite major energy projects have been arrested in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 The sit-in was at the Hart building on Capitol Hill - where senate leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  and West Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s Joe Manchin both have their offices - to protest against their secret-deal to mandate fast track permits for energy and mining projects deemed to be of strategic national importance by limiting environmental and community review.\par \par \uc2 Eleven of the 13 national and community leaders who participated in the act of civil disobedience were arrested. It\u8217\'20\'19s not clear what charges - if any - will be brought. Among those was Tom BK Goldtooth, executive director of Indigenous Environmental Network, who said: \u8220\'20\'1C We must uplift and protect our Mother Earth, not repeal the minimal provisions that do exist. We must continue to fight against climate greenwashing and false solutions. We must take real action to keep fossil fuels in the ground.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 One of the most contested parts of the bill is pushing forward with construction of the Mountain Valley pipeline in central Appalachia, which has been suspended by the courts amid widespread community opposition and environmental violations.\par \par \uc2 Lauren Maunus, advocacy director for the youth-led environmental justice group, Sunrise Movement, said: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m angry and frustrated that this is how we have to spend our time after the Inflation Reduction Act - less than 50 days before the midterms - when we could and should be devoting our full attention to helping Democrats expand the majority and fight fascism. Stop the permitting deal now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Schumer wants to attach Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s Energy Independence and Security Act of 2022, released late on Wednesday, to a funding measure which must be passed by Congress by 1 October to avoid a government shutdown. It\u8217\'20\'19s opposed by dozens of Democrats in the House and Senate, as well as a broad range of environmentalists, scientists and health professionals.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/22/schumer-manchin-side-deal-pipelines-backlash"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Schumer and Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18dirty side deal\u8217\'20\'19 to fast-track pipelines faces backlash}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Several Senate Republicans don\u8217\'20\'19t appear comfortable with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s claims regarding classified documents, particularly his assertion yesterday that he could clear them for release just by thinking about it.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/09/22/politics/republican-reaction-trump-secret-records/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN has gotten several on the record}}}\uc2  saying that the former president should have followed procedures set out for handling government secrets.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think it ought to be adhered to and followed. And I think that should apply to anybody who has access to or deals with classified information,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 John Thune\uc2 , the Republican whip in the chamber, said. \u8220\'20\'1CI think the concern is about those being taken from the White House absent some way of declassifying them or the fact that there were classified documents removed \u8212\'20\'14 without sort of the appropriate safeguards.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI believe there\u8217\'20\'19s a formal process that needs to go through, that needs to be gone through and documented,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Thom Tillis\uc2  of North Carolina. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd to the extent they were declassified, gone through the process, that\u8217\'20\'19s fine... As I understand the Executive Branch requirements, there is a process that one must go through.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think anyone who takes the time to appropriately protect that information and who has taken the time to see what\u8217\'20\'19s in the information would have serious concerns about how items could be accessed if they\u8217\'20\'19re not stored properly,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Mike Rounds\uc2  of South Dakota.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Special master demands proof of tampering from Trump's lawyers in Mar-a-Lago case\par \par \uc2 The special master appointed to filter out privileged materials from the documents taken by the government from Mar-a-Lago has asked \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s lawyers to provide proof of their allegations that the \uc2 FBI\uc2  planted evidence.\par \par \uc2 In a new court filing, Raymond Dearie, the senior federal judge tasked with separating out documents covered under executive or attorney-client privilege from the trove taken by the \uc2 FBI\uc2  as part of its investigation into whether Trump unlawfully possessed government secrets, also laid out a series of deadlines in the case.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from Reuters:\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Mar-a-Lago special master is telling Trump's lawyers to say once and for all whether they really think the \uc2 FBI\uc2  planted evidence during its search, as the former president has publicly alleged. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/hVF7fCTjIj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/hVF7fCTjIj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Brad Heath (@bradheath) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/bradheath/status/1573010332146171908?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 22, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThis isn't the first time Judge Dearie has told Trump's lawyers to essentially put up or shut up about the things they've been saying in TV but not in court.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Brad Heath (@bradheath) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/bradheath/status/1573013231261679617?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 22, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrJudge Dearie is also setting some pretty short deadlines on the review of materials seized from Mar-a-Lago. He wants Trump's lawyers to decide by Monday whether to assert privilege over items singled as potentially privileged by the \uc2 FBI\uc2  filter team. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/8BX6IT310f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/8BX6IT310f}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Brad Heath (@bradheath) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/bradheath/status/1573013550834098177?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 22, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrAnd he says Trump's lawyers need to lay out all of their claims of privilege in about three weeks. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/rRCkwLjPuR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/rRCkwLjPuR}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Brad Heath (@bradheath) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/bradheath/status/1573013781927665665?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 22, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The demands regarding evidence planting appear to be a response to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/08/10/nyregion/trump-fbi-planting-evidence.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claims made without evidence by Trump}}}\uc2  and his allies after the August search of Mar-a-Lago.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/11/trump-mar-a-lago-witch-hunt-fbi-doj-safety"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s increasing tirade against FBI and DoJ endangering lives of officials}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 In August, Democratic senator Joe Manchin agreed to support the marquee Inflation Reduction Act \u8211\'20\'13 but only if party leaders would in turn put up for a vote a proposal to fast-track permitting for energy projects. The bill is here, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/nina-lakhani"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nina Lakhani}}}\uc2  reports on advocates\u8217\'20\'19 concerns it will gut environmental protections:\par \par \uc2 Scientists, health experts and environmental groups have condemned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/21/joe-manchin-energy-bill-fossil-fuels"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new legislation}}}\uc2  negotiated in secret by the fossil-fuel-friendly Democratic senator Joe Manchin and the Senate leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , which will fast-track major energy projects by gutting clean water and environmental protections.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.energy.senate.gov/services/files/EAB527DC-FA23-4BA9-B3C6-6AB108626F02"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 permitting bill }}}\uc2  published on Wednesday was the result of a deal between Manchin and Democratic leaders, which secured the West Virginia senator\u8217\'20\'19s vote for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s historic climate legislation, the Inflation Reduction Act, which Manchin held up for months.\par \par \uc2 The bill mandates all permits for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/26/joe-manchin-west-virginia-mountain-valley-pipeline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mountain Valley pipeline (MVP), }}}\uc2  a project long delayed by environmental violations and judicial rulings, be issued within 30 days of passage and strips away virtually any scope for judicial review.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/22/schumer-manchin-side-deal-pipelines-backlash"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Schumer and Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18dirty side deal\u8217\'20\'19 to fast-track pipelines faces backlash}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Judge blocks Indiana's hardline \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par \uc2 Indiana led the charge in tightening \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access after Roe v Wade was overturned in June, but a judge today blocked the new law on grounds that the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution protects access to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 The decision underscores the complications Republican-led states face as they move to take advantage of the conservative-led court\u8217\'20\'19s decision, which cleared the way for states to ban the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-health-indiana-legislature-9dda020bf811f19e6254915ca1324edc?utm_source=homepage&utm_medium=TopNews&utm_campaign=position_06"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Owen County Judge Kelsey Hanlon issued a preliminary injunction against the ban that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-health-indianapolis-legislature-lindsey-graham-4adefab532a14e548801a3980d43253e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 took effect one week ago.}}}\uc2  The injunction was sought by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic operators who argued in a lawsuit that the state constitution protects access to the medical procedure.\par \par \uc2 The ban was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-us-supreme-court-health-indianapolis-indiana-83fe300188fcf15d8a3b4a36ceee7443"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 approved by the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican-dominated Legislature}}}\uc2  on Aug. 5 and signed by GOP Gov. \uc2 Eric Holcomb\uc2 . That made Indiana the first state to enact tighter \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions since the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  eliminated federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-supreme-court-decision-854f60302f21c2c35129e58cf8d8a7b0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturning Roe v. Wade}}}\uc2  in June.\par \par \uc2 The judge wrote \u8220\'20\'1Cthere is reasonable likelihood that this significant restriction of personal autonomy offends the liberty guarantees of the Indiana Constitution\u8221\'20\'1D and that the clinics will prevail in the lawsuit. The order prevents the state from enforcing the ban pending a trial on the merits of the lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 Republican state Attorney General \uc2 Todd Rokita\uc2  said in a statement: \u8220\'20\'1CWe plan to appeal and continue to make the case for life in Indiana.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Since 1978 Ray Fair, ??professor of Economics at \uc2 Yale University\uc2 , has been using economic data to predict US election outcomes. His bare-boned, strictly by the numbers approach has a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fairmodel.econ.yale.edu/vote2020/indexne2.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fairly impressive}}}\uc2  record, usually coming within 3% of the final tally.\par \par \uc2 Sadly for Democrats \u8211\'20\'13 if Fair\u8217\'20\'19s on track again this time \u8211\'20\'13 the Biden administration will struggle to keep control of Congress in November\u8217\'20\'19s crucial midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 Elections are noisy events and this year\u8217\'20\'19s is no different. Recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/3650684-why-biden-is-seeing-a-rise-in-the-polls/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polling suggests}}}\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/now/video/president-biden-s-approval-numbers-on-the-rise-nbc-news-poll-shows-148840517702"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on a roll}}}\uc2 , reclaiming some of the ground he lost earlier in his presidency.\par \par \uc2 The Democrats have passed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/16/biden-signs-inflation-reduction-act-landmark-healthcare-climate-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 major legislation.}}}\uc2  There has been a surge in women registering to vote after the supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights drove voters to the polls in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/kansas-abortion-vote-state-constitution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deep-red Kansas}}}\uc2 . Gas prices, if not overall inflation, are falling. In the meantime, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and the candidates he has backed are dominating the headlines and helping Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 poll numbers.\par \par \uc2 But if Fair is right, we can largely set aside the personalities and the issues: the economy is the signal behind the noise and Biden is still in trouble.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/22/democrats-congress-midterms-biden-ray-fair"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats will struggle to keep control of Congress in midterms, expert says}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Greg Norman faced accusations of promoting Saudi \u8220\'20\'1Cpropaganda\u8221\'20\'1D following meetings with Washington lawmakers in which the Australian golfer sought to garner support for the Saudi-backed LIV Series in its bitter dispute with the PGA Tour.\par \par \uc2 Greg Norman. Photograph: Richard Cashin/USA Today Sports\par \par \uc2 Norman, who is LIV\u8217\'20\'19s CEO and the public face of the breakaway tour, ostensibly came to the capital this week to criticise what he has called the PGA\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Canti-competitive efforts\u8221\'20\'1D to stifle LIV.\par \par \uc2 But \u8211\'20\'13 apart from some lawmakers who allegedly sought to take their picture with Norman \u8211\'20\'13 the Saudi tour instead faced a considerable backlash from both Democrats and Republicans, who defended the PGA and accused LIV of being little more than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2022/jan/05/sportswashing-winter-olympics-world-cup"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a sportswashing vehicle}}}\uc2  for the kingdom.\par \par \uc2 Tim Burchett, a Republican congressman from Tennessee, left a meeting of the Republican Study Committee on Wednesday at which dozens of his party colleagues had met with Norman, expressing dismay that members of Congress were discussing a golf league backed by Saudi funds. He also called Norman\u8217\'20\'19s LIV pitch \u8220\'20\'1Cpropaganda\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to get out of bed with these people. They are bad actors. We need to keep them at arm\u8217\'20\'19s length,\u8221\'20\'1D Burchett told the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 He cited the September 11 attacks on the US, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2018/oct/21/death-of-dissident-jamal-khashoggi-mohammed-bin-salman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the murder of Saudi journalist Jamal Khashoggi}}}\uc2 , and the kingdom\u8217\'20\'19s treatment of gay people and women, which he called \u8220\'20\'1Cjust unacceptable\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2022/sep/22/greg-norman-liv-golf-series-saudi-arabia-us-congress-visit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US congressman accuses LIV CEO Greg Norman of pushing Saudi \u8216\'20\'18propaganda\u8217\'20\'19 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Blinken: \uc2 UN\uc2  must send 'clear message' to Russia on nuclear weapons\par \par \uc2 The US secretary of state, \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 , spoke at the United Nations in New York earlier, seeking to \u8220\'20\'1Csend a clear message\u8221\'20\'1D to Russia over its threats concerning the possible use of nuclear weapons during its war in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Tony Blinken\uc2 . Photograph: Lev Radin/Pacific Press/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery council member should send a clear message that these reckless nuclear threats must stop immediately,\u8221\'20\'1D Blinken said during a security council session, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CThe very international order we\u8217\'20\'19ve gathered here to uphold is being shredded before our eyes. We cannot \u8211\'20\'13 we will not \u8211\'20\'13 let President Putin get away with it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Blinken also said it was critical to show that \u8220\'20\'1Cno nation can redraw the borders of another by force\u8221\'20\'1D and said: \u8220\'20\'1CIf we fail to defend this principle when the Kremlin is so flagrantly violating it, we send the message to aggressors everywhere that they can ignore it, too.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As the Associated Press reports, the session on Thursday was \u8220\'20\'1Ccalled by France, the current council president, [and] focused on addressing accountability for alleged abuses and atrocities, and the US and other western members repeatedly accused Russia of committing them\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Sergey Lavrov\uc2 , the Russian foreign minister, was not in the room when Blinken and others spoke. In his own remarks, he claimed Ukraine was oppressing Russian speakers in the east of the country and western allies of the Ukrainian government \u8220\'20\'1Chave been covering up the crimes of the Kyiv regime\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Security council action against Russia is vastly unlikely, given Russia\u8217\'20\'19s veto power.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s some more Ukraine-based reading, from Oliver Milman :\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/sep/22/gas-industry-ukraine-war-biden-policy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How the gas industry capitalized on the Ukraine war to change Biden policy}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 The legal offensive against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  flared anew after a federal appeals court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/22/trump-mar-a-lago-records-justice-department-new-york-lawsuit-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-632c5abd8f08146227062153#block-632c5abd8f08146227062153"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cleared the justice department to continue reviewing documents}}}\uc2  seized from Mar-a-Lago as it probes his potentially unlawful retention of government secrets. Meanwhile, a slew of new polls show tights races in battleground states like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/22/trump-mar-a-lago-records-justice-department-new-york-lawsuit-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-632c7c118f0891514fe79f3f#block-632c7c118f0891514fe79f3f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/22/trump-mar-a-lago-records-justice-department-new-york-lawsuit-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-632c889f8f0822acf24f47d0#block-632c889f8f0822acf24f47d0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona}}}\uc2 , Americans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/22/trump-mar-a-lago-records-justice-department-new-york-lawsuit-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-632c6b7c8f0814622706220b#block-632c6b7c8f0814622706220b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fired up to vote nationwide and Democrats with a slight lead on the generic congressional ballot}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ginni Thomas, the wife of rightwing supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  and a supporter of efforts to keep \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  from getting into the White House, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/22/trump-mar-a-lago-records-justice-department-new-york-lawsuit-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-632c77bf8f0891514fe79eec#block-632c77bf8f0891514fe79eec"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will speak to the January 6 committee}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 There appear to be enough votes for the Senate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/22/trump-mar-a-lago-records-justice-department-new-york-lawsuit-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-632c72d28f089a550b8aa85c#block-632c72d28f089a550b8aa85c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to pass a bill}}}\uc2  to prevent the type of legal schemes Trump\u8217\'20\'19s allies tried to execute on January 6 to stop the certification of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s election win.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Manhattan attorney general said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/22/trump-mar-a-lago-records-justice-department-new-york-lawsuit-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-632c60bc8f08f4c4bf5d80c6#block-632c60bc8f08f4c4bf5d80c6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his investigation into Trump}}}\uc2  and his organization is continuing.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 The race to be the next governor of Arizona is shaping up to be a nailbiter, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aarp.org/content/dam/aarp/research/surveys_statistics/politics/2022/aarp-arizona-2022-elections-voter-survey-governor.doi.10.26419-2Fres.00550.011.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a new survey from AARP Arizona.}}}\par \par \uc2 The poll found Democrat \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2  and Republican Kari Lake in a statistical tie at 49% and 48% respectively, with just 3% of voters in the southwest battleground state undecided.\par \par \uc2 Among Arizonans aged 50 and over, who make up an estimated 60% of the state\u8217\'20\'19s electorate, Lake narrowly leads Hobbs, 50% to 48%, respectively. Among political independents, who comprise roughly one third of voters in the state, Hobbs holds a 4-point edge.\par \par \uc2 The picture is slightly brighter for Democrats in the state\u8217\'20\'19s competitive senate race, where incumbent Mark Kelly leads his Republican challenger, \uc2 Blake Masters\uc2 , by 8-points.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 A Republican senator wants to seize on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s recent statement that the \u8220\'20\'1Cpandemic is over\u8221\'20\'1D to pass a resolution ending the national emergency declared to combat Covid-19, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/republicans-to-force-vote-on-ending-covid-19-emergency-declaration-11663860630"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Wall Street Journal reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The resolution to be proposed by Roger Marshall of Kansas would end the state of emergency that the administration has used to justify suspending student loans repayments and some procedures at international borders, among other uses.\par \par \uc2 A previous attempt to end the declaration passed the Senate in March but went nowhere in the House. Both chambers are narrowly led by Democrats, but the White House promised then to veto the measure, if it made it to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s desk.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/19/biden-says-covid-pandemic-is-over-despite-us-daily-death-toll-in-the-hundreds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden says Covid \u8216\'20\'18pandemic is over\u8217\'20\'19, despite US daily death toll in the hundreds}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Back to the polls, \uc2 Monmouth University\uc2  has a new one on Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s governorship race that shows Democratic challenger Stacy Abrams with a narrower path to victory but more dedicated support base than the Republican incumbent \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2  as she again challenges him for the job.\par \par \uc2 The race is among the more high-profile gubernatorial contests to be decided in the 8 November midterms, and could make Abrams Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s first Black and first female governor if elected. Kemp, meanwhile, is known for resisting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn the results of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election win there in 2020, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/mar/25/georgia-voting-restrictions-law-passed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 though has backed a strict voting law}}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.monmouth.edu/polling-institute/reports/monmouthpoll_ga_092222/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to Monmouth}}}\uc2 , 34% will definitely and 15% will probably back Kemp, against Abrams\u8217\'20\'19 slightly worse 33% definite support and 12% probable support. Kemp is also viewed more favorably at 54%, versus Abrams\u8217\'20\'19s 48% favorability.\par \par \uc2 However, Democrats are more fired up for Abrams than Republicans are for Kemp. Monmouth finds that 83% of Democrats will definitely vote for Abrams versus 73% of GOP voters for Kemp \u8211\'20\'13 perhaps a consequence of his clashes with Trump.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSome election conspiracists may still hold a grudge against Kemp for not stepping in to overturn the 2020 result, but it\u8217\'20\'19s unlikely to cost him much support. They may not be enthusiastic, but they\u8217\'20\'19ll still vote for him over Abrams,\u8221\'20\'1D Patrick Murray, director of the independent Monmouth University Polling Institute, said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 The judge who had initially blocked the justice department from reviewing the documents seized from Mar-a-Lago and ordered a special master to weed out privileged materials has revised her ruling, Politico reports.\par \par \uc2 Federal judge Aileen Cannon \u8217\'20\'19s changes come after an appeals court overturned the part of her opinion that had halted the government\u8217\'20\'19s review of the documents taken from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s resort, hampering the investigation into whether the former president took government secrets with him when he left the White House.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from Politico:\par \par \uc2 enltrJUST IN: Judge Cannon has responded to the 11th Circuit Court of Appeals stay decision by striking aspects of her order appointing a special master. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/tttZG7qBz7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/tttZG7qBz7}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vROBSuypSu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/vROBSuypSu}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1572966868763430912?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 22, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThese are the two sections of Cannon's original order that she has now stricken: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/tttZG7qBz7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/tttZG7qBz7}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zoVpAzXDAW"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/zoVpAzXDAW}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1572967822086803457?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 22, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 On the topic of January 6, the committee investigating the attack has reached an agreement to hear the testimony of Virginia Thomas, the wife of supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  and a supporter of efforts to keep \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  from taking office despite his election win:\par \par \uc2 Conservative activist Virginia Thomas, the wife of supreme court justice {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/clarence-thomas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Clarence Thomas}}}\uc2 , has agreed to participate in a voluntary interview with the House panel investigating the January 6 insurrection, her lawyer said Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Attorney Mark Paoletta said Thomas is \u8220\'20\'1Ceager to answer the committee\u8217\'20\'19s questions to clear up any misconceptions about her work relating to the 2020 election\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The committee has sought an interview with Thomas in an effort to know more about her role in trying to help former president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  overturn his election defeat. She texted with White House chief of staff \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  and contacted lawmakers in Arizona and Wisconsin in the weeks after the election and before the insurrection.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/21/virginia-thomas-january-6-panel-interview-clarence-thomas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Virginia Thomas agrees to interview with House January 6 panel}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Bill to thwart another January 6 appears to have support to pass Senate\par \par \uc2 A Republican senator announced today he would support an effort to change the United States\u8217\'20\'19 electoral law and prevent the sort legal plot attempted on January 6 to stop \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  from taking office, potentially giving the measure enough votes to pass the Senate.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.inquirer.com/politics/nation/pat-toomey-electoral-count-reform-act-20220922.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Philadelphia Inquirer reports}}}\uc2  that Pennsylvania senator \uc2 Pat Toomey\uc2  will vote for the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s version of the legislation amending the 1887 Electoral Count Act, which allies of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  tried to use loopholes in to prevent Congress from certifying Biden\u8217\'20\'19s election win when it convened on 6 January, 2021.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe poor drafting of the 1887 Electoral Count Act endangered the transition of power from one administration to the next. Unfortunately, in the over 100 intervening years, individual Democratic and Republican members of Congress have occasionally attempted to exploit the ambiguities in this law to cast doubt on the validity of our elections, culminating in the debacle of January 6, 2021,\u8221\'20\'1D Toomey said in a statement to the Inquirer.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is past time Congress act.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 With the support of Toomey, who will retire from his post at the end of the year, the Inquirer reports that the bill appears to have enough support to pass the Senate and avoid a filibuster. Yesterday, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/19/liz-cheney-zoe-lofgren-electoral-count-act-bill-january-6-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House passed its own version of the legislation}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania was one of the states where Trump\u8217\'20\'19s allies attempted to orchestrate the overturning of its election results in favor of Biden. In August, Scott Perry, a congressman representing the state who had asked Trump for a preemptive pardon after January 6, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/09/scott-perry-says-phone-seized-fbi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had his cellphone seized by the FBI}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/20/bipartisan-senate-group-electoral-count-act"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bipartisan Senate group reaches deal to reform Electoral Count Act}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere in Congress, Republican senator Ted Cruz voted against a spending bill that paid for a new highway, but took credit for it anyway, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 The Texas Republican senator Ted Cruz {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenTedCruz/status/1569395926128631812?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1572677617668472834%7Ctwgr%5E4e9e953f4020c62dfa9423f5d8cf768f39f7be1b%7Ctwcon%5Es4_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fthehill.com%2Fhomenews%2Fadministration%2F3654555-white-house-slams-ted-cruz-for-touting-infrastructure-project-he-voted-against%2F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  a new highway project \u8220\'20\'1Ca great bipartisan victory\u8221\'20\'1D that will bring \u8220\'20\'1Cjobs to Texas and millions of dollars to the state\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The White House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WhiteHouse/status/1572673696904654848?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1572677617668472834%7Ctwgr%5E4e9e953f4020c62dfa9423f5d8cf768f39f7be1b%7Ctwcon%5Es2_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fthehill.com%2Fhomenews%2Fadministration%2F3654555-white-house-slams-ted-cruz-for-touting-infrastructure-project-he-voted-against%2F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 responded}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CSenator Cruz voted against this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for Cruz {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rollingstone.com/politics/politics-news/ted-cruz-touting-highway-expansion-project-voted-against-1234597428/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  the senator \u8220\'20\'1Cmade it possible\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 but did not contest that Cruz voted against the $1.5tn spending package which contained the highway project.\par \par \uc2 With \uc2 Ben Ray Luj\u225\'00\'E1n\uc2 , a New Mexico Democrat, Cruz co-sponsored an amendment adding the Ports to Plains highway project to the spending bill earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/22/white-house-ted-cruz-highway-spending-voted-against"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 White House says Ted Cruz voted against highway project he touted as \u8216\'20\'18victory\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Two new gauges of the national mood ahead of the 8 November midterm elections were released this morning. Let\u8217\'20\'19s take a look at them.\par \par \uc2 First, there\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1572917130265255937"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News}}}\uc2 , which crunched the numbers on voter enthusiasm from both this year and midterm and presidential elections past to conclude that Americans are particularly fired up to go to the polls. The network found in their most recent survey that 64% were respondents expressed high enthusiasm for the elections. That\u8217\'20\'19s up from the 58% two months before the 2018 midterms, when Democrats routed Republicans and took the House, or the 53% in 2010, when the GOP did the same to Democrats. Given those numbers, NBC predicts record turnout for this year\u8217\'20\'19s vote.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, CNN has done a poll of polls \u8211\'20\'13 an aggregation of the four most recent national polls \u8211\'20\'13 to find that Democrats have a three-point edge in the generic congressional ballot:\par \par \uc2 enltrCNN Poll of Polls (four most recent national polls)\par \par \uc2 August 29-September 14\par \par \uc2 REGISTERED VOTERS\par \par \uc2 Choice For Congress\par \par \uc2 Democrats 46%\par \par \uc2 Republicans 43%\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1572917130265255937?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 22, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  has a dive in the unique implications of the lawsuit filed by the New York attorney general against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his children yesterday, which, if successful, could take the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  out of his personal control:\par \par \uc2 Penalties being sought in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/21/trump-new-york-investigation-ivanka-donald-eric"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the civil fraud suit}}}\uc2  brought by the New York state attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s office against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and three of his adult children could potentially result in the end of the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2 , his real estate empire, in its current form.\par \par \uc2 The former US president, as well as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donald-trump-jr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump Jr}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Eric Trump\uc2 , were named as defendants in a sprawling 214-page complaint filed by New York attorney general Letitia James for allegedly falsely inflating his net worth by billions to enrich himself and secure favorable loans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor too long, powerful, wealthy people in this country have operated as if the rules do not apply to them. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  stands out as among the most egregious examples,\u8221\'20\'1D James said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CTrump thought he could get away with the art of the steal, but today that conduct ends.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/22/new-york-fraud-suit-trump-organization-letitia-james"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York civil fraud suit could bring down the Trump Organization}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 What does this all mean for Trump? Potentially the end of his hopes for running again in 2024, \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/davidsmith"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 David Smith}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/02/trump-mar-a-lago-search-doj-photos"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 legal perils}}}\uc2  have become insurmountable and could snuff out the former US president\u8217\'20\'19s hopes of an election-winning comeback, according to political analysts and legal experts.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Trump and three of his adult children were accused of lying to tax collectors, lenders and insurers in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/21/trump-new-york-investigation-ivanka-donald-eric"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cstaggering\u8221\'20\'1D fraud scheme}}}\uc2  that routinely misstated the value of his properties to enrich themselves.\par \par \uc2 The civil lawsuit, filed by New York\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general, came as the \uc2 FBI\uc2  investigates Trump\u8217\'20\'19s holding of sensitive government documents at his Mar-a-Lago estate in Florida and a special grand jury in Georgia considers whether he and others attempted to influence state election officials after his defeat there {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/nov/19/joe-biden-president-georgia-recount"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by Joe Biden}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The former US president has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/10/donald-trump-2024-election-big-tease-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repeatedly hinted}}}\uc2  that he intends to run for the White House again in 2024. But the cascade of criminal, civil and congressional investigations could yet derail that bid.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/21/donald-trump-lawsuit-new-york-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18He\u8217\'20\'19s done\u8217\'20\'19: how Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal woes have just gotten a lot worse}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Shortly after New York attorney general Letitia James finished announcing her lawsuit alleging fraud against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his children, Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  weighed in with a reminder:\par \par \uc2 enltrStatement from Manhattan D.A. \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 : {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/3b2Km2QaQU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/3b2Km2QaQU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2  (@ManhattanDA) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ManhattanDA/status/1572637408944091136?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Bragg\u8217\'20\'19s investigation is yet another source of legal peril for the former president. In August, the former chief financial officer of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s company pled guilty to tax charges and agreed to testify against the organization.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/18/allen-weisselberg-trump-organization-pleads-guilty-tax-fraud"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Allen Weisselberg, Trump Organization financial chief, pleads guilty to tax fraud}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 After the \uc2 FBI\uc2  searched Mar-a-Lago and carted away troves of documents containing government secrets, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  argued that he had declassified everything found during his time as president.\par \par \uc2 He doubled down on that argument last night in an interview with Fox News\u8217\'20\'19s conservative commentator \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2 , saying that when he was in the White House, he had the power to declassify something just \u8220\'20\'1Cby thinking about it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The three-judge panel that yesterday overturned a lower court judge\u8217\'20\'19s block and allowed the justice department to continue reviewing the Mar-a-Lago documents didn\u8217\'20\'19t have much time for the president\u8217\'20\'19s argument.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPlaintiff has not even attempted to show that he has a need to know the information contained in the classified documents. Nor has he established that the current administration has waived that requirement for these documents. And even if he had, that, in and of itself, would not explain why Plaintiff has an individual interest in the classified documents,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/f/?id=00000183-625b-da48-a3e3-e2ff83050000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the judges wrote}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It gets worse for Trump from there: \u8220\'20\'1CPlaintiff suggests that he may have declassified these documents when he was President. But the record contains no evidence that any of these records were declassified,\u8221\'20\'1D they wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CIn any event, at least for these purposes, the declassification argument is a red herring because declassifying an official document would not change its content or render it personal. So even if we assumed that Plaintiff did declassify some or all of the documents, that would not explain why he has a personal interest in them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s investigation will continue thanks to this ruling, don\u8217\'20\'19t expect the legal jousting over this case to be over.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Justice department can begin reviewing Mar-a-Lago records, jeopardizing Trump anew\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/21/donald-trump-mar-a-lago-records-hold-lifted"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Justice department investigators are cleared to resume}}}\uc2  going through documents taken from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago resort. Last night, a panel of judges overturned an earlier ruling that temporarily blocked them from reviewing the material as part of the government\u8217\'20\'19s inquiry into whether the former president took secrets with him when he left the White House. The judges\u8217\'20\'19 decision makes clear {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/21/donald-trump-lawsuit-new-york-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump remains in legal peril}}}\uc2 , both from that investigation, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/22/new-york-fraud-suit-trump-organization-letitia-james"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a New York lawsuit announced yesterday}}}\uc2  over his business practices and inquiries into his conduct during the 2020 election and January 6 uprising in Washington and Georgia.\par \par \uc2 That certainly is not all that\u8217\'20\'19s happening today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Nations General Assembly\uc2  continues in New York, with the US secretary of state, \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 ,{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/asia-pacific/blinken-chinese-counterpart-meet-friday-new-york-2022-09-22/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 set to meet his Chinese counterpart}}}\uc2 , Wang Yi, on its sidelines.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is still in New York City, where he is scheduled to meet with president \uc2 Ferdinand Marcos Jr\uc2  of the Philippines, visit a Fema office to assess its response to Hurricane Fiona in Puerto Rico, and attend a \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  fundraiser.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The House of Representatives will vote today {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepJoshG/status/1572652510829252609/photo/1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on bills to better fund police departments}}}\uc2 , answering the demands of vulnerable Democrats looking to improve their record on public safety.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220922ei9m001p9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
