\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I can\u8217\'20\'19t stay silent\u8217\'20\'19: Roe reversal powers new generation to sign up and vote\b0\par\par\uc2 Poppy Noor \par \uc2 1,603 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 September 2022\par 07:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Huge bloc of women expected to turn out in November midterms to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights \u8211\'20\'13 could it alter the election outcome?\par \par \uc2 Sonya Koenig is scared. A 19-year-old student from Kalamazoo, Michigan, Koenig often stays up until 2am thinking. Sometimes she paces up and down the hall, or speaks to her roommate about nightmare scenarios in which she ends up pregnant and in need of an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBeing in college, I hear stories all the time of women getting drugged at parties, or just walking down the street, and something unfortunate can happen,\u8221\'20\'1D says Koenig, a freshman at \uc2 Michigan State University\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CA guy can walk away, but [these \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans] mean the woman has to choose: \u8216\'20\'18Do I want to give this baby up \u8230\'20\'26 or raise this child with no help from anybody?\u8217\'20\'19 That\u8217\'20\'19s a really hard decision.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In August, a week after her 19th birthday, Koenig signed up to vote. She is one of many women registering in droves since the supreme court overturned the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on 24 June.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy brain is constantly on fire. I can\u8217\'20\'19t relax. I just want this election to be over with,\u8221\'20\'1D says Koenig, who plans to vote to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in a Michigan ballot as well as voting Democrat come November.\par \par \uc2 People such as Koenig threaten to be a hugely pivotal voting bloc as the midterms loom, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://supermajority.com/our-story/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 organizers focusing on women}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thecivicscenter.org/blog/2022/9/5/throughout-greater-philadelphia-dramatic-increase-in-voter-registration-for-youngest-voters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 young }}}\uc2  people in voter registration drives all over the country. The first hints of that bloc\u8217\'20\'19s voting power came in early August, when {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/kansas-abortion-rights-referendum-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 women in Kansas came out overwhelmingly to protect \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\uc2 . That election saw huge turnout, with women representing 70% of newly registered voters. They ultimately protected \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in a state where \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had a 15% lead in the 2020 presidential election that he lost to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That trend seems to be continuing in other states \u8211\'20\'13 a threat to Republican lawmakers, who in recent weeks have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/12/republicans-soften-staunch-anti-abortion-stance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 quietly removed \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 -related election pledges from their websites}}}\uc2  and softened their anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  messaging.\par \par \uc2 For instance, the Republican gubernatorial candidate for Minnesota, Scott Jensen, had previously said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mprnews.org/episode/2022/03/15/republican-gubernatorial-candidate-dr-scott-jensen"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he would ban \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  outright}}}\uc2 . But more recently, Jensen released a video saying he supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the cases of rape, incest, and threat to life of the pregnant person.\par \par \uc2 That pivot might not be enough to hide the party\u8217\'20\'19s hardline agenda: this week, Senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  of South Carolina proposed a nationwide ban on abortions after 15 weeks of pregnancy, despite months of Republican rhetoric about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/jun/24/us-attorneys-general-react-supreme-court-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 putting the question back to the states}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Perhaps women are unconvinced. Target Smart analyzed new voter registration from 45 states following the supreme court decision that reversed federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights \u8211\'20\'13 the group said female registration shot up 12%.\par \par \uc2 In Wisconsin, a battleground state that voted for Biden by a margin of just 30,000 votes in 2020, women are out-registering men by 16%. New registrants also skew hugely Democratic: 52% of newly registered voters in Wisconsin, compared to just 17% of new registrations by Republicans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn my 28 years of analyzing elections, I had never seen anything like what\u8217\'20\'19s happened in the past two months in American politics,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Tom Bonier\uc2 , chief executive of Target Smart, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/09/03/opinion/women-voters-roe-abortion-midterms.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  in the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWomen are registering to vote in numbers I never witnessed before. I\u8217\'20\'19ve run out of superlatives to describe how different this moment is.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This week, the Michigan supreme court agreed to put the question of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights directly to voters in November, after 730,000 Michiganders signed a petition requesting a vote. Initially, Republicans on the state\u8217\'20\'19s board of canvassers tried to block the call for a referendum, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/09/08/michigan-supreme-court-puts-abortion-on-november-ballot-00055774"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 complaining about spacing errors.}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI tend to do the bigger elections \u8230\'20\'26 I\u8217\'20\'19m disabled, and standing in line for a long time is not the best for me,\u8221\'20\'1D says Diamond Dor\u233\'00\'E9, 30, from Detroit. \u8220\'20\'1CBut seeing [the supreme court] decision, I was like, I have to vote. I\u8217\'20\'19m Black and queer, and I know this means a lot of Black women are gonna die. I couldn\u8217\'20\'19t stay silent.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A grassroots activist, Dor\u233\'00\'E9 phone canvasses, and says she has seen anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  voters suddenly wanting to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWhen this happened, a lot of people sat back and said, \u8216\'20\'18Oh, dang, this is for real. It\u8217\'20\'19s not just about me, this is about tons of other women and pregnant persons around America,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D says Dor\u233\'00\'E9.\par \par \uc2 News of a 10-year-old girl from Ohio traveling 200 miles to Indiana to get \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/14/man-charged-10-year-old-abortion-rightwing-media-indiana-ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 after being raped}}}\uc2  was one thing Dor\u233\'00\'E9 has seen sway voters. Add to that list people being forced to carry unsuccessful pregnancies to full term, at risk to their own lives, and the threat of criminalization.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of Black people feel like we are going back to what our ancestors went through,\u8221\'20\'1D says Dor\u233\'00\'E9.\par \par \uc2 William Wojciechowsk, 35, who hails from what he calls \u8220\'20\'1CTrump country, Michigan\u8221\'20\'1D (St Clair), says \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans across the country mean he will be voting Democrat in November for the first time.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll the way up until the last primary election, I voted very conservatively. But I\u8217\'20\'19m a transgender male, and abortions can affect me directly because I haven\u8217\'20\'19t had a hysterectomy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked if he felt abandoned by his party, Wojciechowsk responded: \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re too extreme. They\u8217\'20\'19re out of their minds. These bans are putting women and trans men back into the dark ages.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bonier says the gender gap in voter registration seems more pronounced in some states than others.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a general sense that even though Dobbs fell, that [some of the electorate still feels] \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is protected. In states like Oregon, where they\u8217\'20\'19ve been trying to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in their state constitution, you don\u8217\'20\'19t really see gender gaps [in those registering to vote] since the decision,\u8221\'20\'1D says Bonier. But in Republican-dominated states such as Alaska, Idaho, Kansas and Louisiana, and competitive midwestern swing states \u8211\'20\'13 such as Wisconsin, Pennsylvania, Ohio and Michigan \u8211\'20\'13 the gap is clearer, he says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[In those] races, governors and senators have certainly focused pretty extensively on [\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ]. And so I think voters generally have a sense of the stakes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Those stakes include control of Congress at a pivotal moment for American democracy \u8211\'20\'13 control that until recently looked like it could pass into Republican hands. The party in power has historically tended to struggle in the midterms.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJust a few months ago, if you were to watch any of the cable news shows or read any of the political columnists, there seemed to be a universal agreement that Republicans were on their way to an inevitable wave election, where they were going to take back the Senate and take back the House. Now that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t seem so sure,\u8221\'20\'1D Bonier says.\par \par \uc2 Now, surprise races are being won for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/24/democrat-who-campaigned-on-abortion-rights-wins-in-new-york-special-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 candidates putting \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  at the centre }}}\uc2  of their campaigns. Republicans lost Alaska\u8217\'20\'19s special House election at the end of August \u8211\'20\'13 a surprise victory for Mary Peltola, who was running against Alaska\u8217\'20\'19s former governor, \uc2 Sarah Palin\uc2 , and against Nicholas Begich, a Republican who comes from a lineage of Alaskan Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Younger people, in particular, are playing a key role in the surge in women voting. Usually, voter turnout is particularly low for young people in midterms and primaries. But in Kansas, voters under the age of 30 comprised over 14% of ballots cast, surpassing their vote share for each of the past three general elections in Kansas.\par \par \uc2 Katharine from Minnesota, who just turned 18 and did not give her surname for privacy, will vote for the first time in November. She remembers the moment she heard about the Dobbs decision: she was sitting in history class.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSomehow, in my mind, I still thought it wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t happen, that once [the draft opinion] was leaked, maybe the public would somehow sway the decision,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 She had written many school assignments about the importance of judicial precedent \u8211\'20\'13 and here she was seeing it all torn down.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s when I knew I had to vote,\u8221\'20\'1D she says. \u8220\'20\'1CTo see a lot of things I\u8217\'20\'19ve grown up viewing as basic rights being taken away was very jolting.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am ready to put these politicians in their place. We\u8217\'20\'19re tired of the older guys in office telling us what to do with our bodies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bonier cautions that young people usually surge in voter registration closer to midterms, and that first-time voters make up a tiny proportion of those who are registering to vote.\par \par \uc2 But, he says, past election cycles indicate that when a group shows a greater level of intensity at a particular point \u8211\'20\'13 registering to vote for the first time in increased numbers \u8211\'20\'13 those numbers translate to a higher level of turnout overall for that group.\par \par \uc2 In Michigan, Koenig recalls feeling stirred when she heard Ruth Bader Ginsberg, one of her idols, talk about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a human right, rather than simply an issue of gender.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CForcing a woman to have a child, it affects everything,\u8221\'20\'1D Koenig says. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not just an issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It\u8217\'20\'19s a racial issue. It\u8217\'20\'19s a women\u8217\'20\'19s rights issue. And I feel like a lot of these politicians are so concerned with their power, they don\u8217\'20\'19t think about how we going to support babies that are going to be born.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf something terrible happens to me, I want to have a choice in the matter.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220918ei9i000ma\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
