\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 January 6 panel could release report on Trump and Capitol attack before midterms \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein \par \uc2 4,959 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 September 2022\par 20:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Judge appoints special master to weed out documents seized from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago residence under legal privilege rulesSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 The run-up to the 8 November midterms will be even more eventful than usual, after the January 6 committee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/16/trump-special-master-documents-biden-south-africa-latest?page=with:block-63249c258f083f878e70edbb#block-63249c258f083f878e70edbb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made clear its plans}}}\uc2  to release more details of the attack on the Capitol in the weeks ahead. Meanwhile, a federal judge has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/16/trump-special-master-documents-biden-south-africa-latest?page=with:block-632471018f08ee6e81d2b0fc#block-632471018f08ee6e81d2b0fc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 approved the appointment}}}\uc2  of a special master to review documents seized by the government from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago resort, while stopping the justice department from further examining them until the master has finished his work.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/16/trump-special-master-documents-biden-south-africa-latest?page=with:block-632479f08f08ee6e81d2b14e#block-632479f08f08ee6e81d2b14e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 meet with the families}}}\uc2  of two Americans detained in Russia, while Moscow has yet to act on a reported prisoner-swap offer made to secure their freedom.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The White House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/16/trump-special-master-documents-biden-south-africa-latest?page=with:block-6324b4678f083f878e70ef0f#block-6324b4678f083f878e70ef0f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 condemned}}}\uc2  GOP governors\u8217\'20\'19 transportation of migrants to Washington, DC and Martha\u8217\'20\'19s Vineyard, Massachusetts.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/16/trump-special-master-documents-biden-south-africa-latest?page=with:block-632498788f08ee6e81d2b355#block-632498788f08ee6e81d2b355"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 apparently embraced}}}\uc2  the QAnon conspiracy theory to shore up his support base amid mounting legal problems.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers faced rancor and strife of all kinds, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/16/trump-special-master-documents-biden-south-africa-latest?page=with:block-6324c13e8f08ee6e81d2b585#block-6324c13e8f08ee6e81d2b585"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a condemnation at a committee hearing}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/16/trump-special-master-documents-biden-south-africa-latest?page=with:block-6324cb828f083f878e70efe0#block-6324cb828f083f878e70efe0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a feud on a flight}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/16/trump-special-master-documents-biden-south-africa-latest?page=with:block-6324c7258f083f878e70efbb#block-6324c7258f083f878e70efbb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a kicking outside the Capitol}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 No, the White House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/16/trump-special-master-documents-biden-south-africa-latest?page=with:block-632485f38f0836766296d71c#block-632485f38f0836766296d71c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 did not hire a satanist}}}\uc2  as the deputy coordinator of its monkeypox response.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 West Virginia's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban goes into effect with governor's signature\par \par \uc2 West Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor \uc2 Jim Justice\uc2  has signed a recently passed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban into law, making it the latest state to crack down on the procedure after the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade last June.\par \par \uc2 enltrToday I signed HB 302 - a bill that protects life.\par \par \uc2 I said from the beginning that if WV legislators brought me a bill that protected life and included reasonable and logical exceptions I would sign it, and that's what I did today.\par \par \uc2 Read the bill ?? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/G7i9DTirSN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/G7i9DTirSN}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Governor \uc2 Jim Justice\uc2  (@WVGovernor) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WVGovernor/status/1570816789952577537?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 16, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The legislation approved by the GOP-controlled state legislature is intended to shut down the state\u8217\'20\'19s only \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic, but contains some exceptions for minors and victims of rape and incest.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/14/west-virginia-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 West Virginia passes sweeping \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban with few exceptions}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere on Thursday, the partisan venom went airborne, when Senator Ted Cruz encountered a supporter of Democrat \uc2 Beto O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke\uc2  on a flight.\par \par \uc2 The Texas senator\u8217\'20\'19s camera-wielding foe, whose identity remains unclear, captured their encounter on video, in which he challenged Cruz\u8217\'20\'19s stance on gun control and asked him to name a victim of the May shooting in the town of Uvalde:\par \par \uc2 enltrSenator Cruz was on my flight, and I asked him to name any of the Uvalde victims.\par \par \uc2 He couldn\u8217\'20\'19t. Texas deserves better than spineless hacks like this. Right the wrongs of 2018, and make {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BetoORourke?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @betoorourke}}}\uc2  our next Governor. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/betoforgovernor?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #betoforgovernor}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/cancuncrus?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #cancuncrus}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/uvaldestrong?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #uvaldestrong}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/AW34oxuUNv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/AW34oxuUNv}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Beto For Everyone (@Nathan_VBB) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Nathan_VBB/status/1570487154425348098?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 15, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Cruz defeated O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke when he stood against him for Senate in 2020. O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke is currently trying to unseat Texas governor Greg Abbott, who is running for a third term.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 The congressional tumult extended beyond committee chambers on Thursday, when video appeared to show rightwing Republican House representative \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  kicking an activist as they argued about gun control.\par \par \uc2 The Georgia lawmaker herself posted a lengthy video of the encounter. The alleged kicking happens at about the 1:15 mark:\par \par \uc2 enltrThese foolish cowards want the government to take away guns & the rights of parents to defend their children in schools.\par \par \uc2 You have to be an idiot to think gun control will create a utopian society where criminals disarm themselves and obey the law.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGun-free\u8221\'20\'1D zones kill people. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/1T37HH8jEO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/1T37HH8jEO}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2 ???? (@RepMTG) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepMTG/status/1570530379550916609?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 15, 2022}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/09/15/video-appears-show-marjorie-taylor-greene-kicking-gen-z-activist/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Washington Post}}}\uc2  has a write-up about the encounter between Voters of Tomorrow, a group representing Gen Z, and Greene, whom Democratic leadership booted from her committee assignments for a series of offensive remarks last year.\par \par \uc2 The entire encounter is reminiscent of what Greene used to do before being elected to Congress in 2020. She appeared in Washington the year prior to follow for several blocks and heckle gun control activist David Hogg, a survivor of the 2018 shooting in Parkland, Florida.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile in the House of Representatives, rancor was the order of the day in a Thursday committee hearing when one Republican lawmaker\u8217\'20\'19s comments to a witness prompted a rebuke from his Democratic colleague.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m trying to give you the floor, boo,\u8221\'20\'1D Republican \uc2 Clay Higgins\uc2  said as Raya Salter, a clean energy advocate, spoke before the House oversight committee.\par \par \uc2 New York Democrat \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  was not pleased by how her colleague from Louisiana treated Salter, who was talking about how the fossil fuel industry affected Black people and other racial minorities.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the four years that I\u8217\'20\'19ve sat on this committee, I have never seen members of Congress, Republican or Democrat, disrespect a witness in the way that I have seen them disrespect you today,\u8221\'20\'1D Ocasio-Cortez told Salter. \u8220\'20\'1CFrankly, men who treat women like that in public \u8211\'20\'13 I fear how they treat them in private.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/house/3645202-ocasio-cortez-blasts-gop-lawmakers-treatment-of-female-witness-im-trying-to-give-you-the-floor-boo/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In a statement to the Hill}}}\uc2 , Higgins said, \u8220\'20\'1CWhen radicals show up in front of my committee with an attitude talking anti-American trash, they can expect to get handled. I really don\u8217\'20\'19t care if I hurt anybody\u8217\'20\'19s feelings while I\u8217\'20\'19m fighting to preserve our Republic.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a video of the exchange:\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  said bringing migrants to Democratic-led areas of the country was necessary to draw attention to the government\u8217\'20\'19s failures at the southern border, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/richardluscombe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Richard Luscombe}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has accused \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  of \u8220\'20\'1Cplaying politics with people\u8217\'20\'19s lives\u8221\'20\'1D for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/15/ron-desantis-migrants-marthas-vineyard"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 flying Venezuelan migrants}}}\uc2  to the wealthy liberal island community of Martha\u8217\'20\'19s Vineyard without warning, while the legality of the Florida governor\u8217\'20\'19s move is also under scrutiny.\par \par \uc2 In what immigration activists and Democratic politicians have decried as a \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitical stunt\u8221\'20\'1D, DeSantis, who is expected to run for the Republican party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nomination in 2024, arranged for two charter planes of about 50 migrant adults and children to fly from Texas to Martha\u8217\'20\'19s Vineyard on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Claiming that \u8220\'20\'1Cevery community in America should be sharing in the burdens,\u8221\'20\'1D DeSantis told a press briefing he wanted to draw attention to what he claimed was a failure by the Biden administration to secure the US-Mexico border.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/16/migrants-marthas-vineyard-desantis-biden-democrats-criticism"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DeSantis criticized for sending migrants to Martha\u8217\'20\'19s Vineyard: \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s un-American\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 One migrant had to be taken to urgent care upon arriving in Washington. Another wasn\u8217\'20\'19t aware that he was arriving on the Massachusetts island of Martha\u8217\'20\'19s Vineyard until his plane began its descent.\par \par \uc2 Those were some of the anecdotes White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  relayed as she continued her condemnation of Republicans governors sending migrants from the southern border to Democratic-run communities.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis should not be happening,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CRepublican officials should not be using human beings as political pawns.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Florida governor 'misled' migrant children and mothers by flying them to Martha's Vineyard \u8211\'20\'13 White House\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  is echoing \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  last night {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/16/migrants-marthas-vineyard-desantis-biden-democrats-criticism"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in slamming}}}\uc2  Florida\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , after he arranged for a group of migrants from Venezuela to be flown to the small Massachusetts island, without warning to the state or a true explanation to the people being transported.\par \par \uc2 She said DeSantis did not notify Massachusetts that \u8220\'20\'1Cmigrant children, in need of food and shelter, were about to land on their doorstep.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre added: \u8220\'20\'1CThese vulnerable migrants were misled about where they were headed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She said they were told they were going to Boston and misled about what benefits they would be provided when they arrived, \u8220\'20\'1Cpromised shelter, refuge benefits and more\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She accused the Florida leader, and Greg Abbott, the governor of Texas, who has unilaterally been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/11/new-york-asylum-seeker-attacked-officer-shelter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bussing thousands of migrants}}}\uc2  awaiting the processing of their immigration applications in the US to Democratic-led cities New York, Washington and Chicago, of \u8220\'20\'1Cthe tactics of smugglers in places like Mexico and Guatemala\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd for what? A photo op? Because these governors care about creating political theater, not creating actual solutions,\u8221\'20\'1D Jean-Pierre fumed.\par \par \uc2 She accused Republicans of treating humans like \u8220\'20\'1Cchattel in a cruel, pre-meditated political stunt\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrFrom the White House Press Secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/kKrEtpMa1q"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/kKrEtpMa1q}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Danny Usher (@dsurte66) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/dsurte66/status/1570832474179268609?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 16, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  is due to brief the media shortly, in Washington DC. The session has been put back slightly from its original 1pm ET scheduling.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is due to meet South African president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/cyril-ramaphosa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cyril Ramaphosa}}}\uc2  at the White House early afternoon.\par \par \uc2 The US president plans to fly to the UK tomorrow, ahead of Queen Elizabeth \u8217\'20\'19s state funeral on Monday.\par \par \uc2 But on Sunday he plans to have his first meeting with the brand new British prime minister, \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2 . She met the Queen as incoming prime minister just two days before the monarch\u8217\'20\'19s death last Thursday, providing the world with the last official photographs of the Queen, at Balmoral, smiling and wearing a tartan skirt.\par \par \uc2 And as the campaigns rev up for the US midterm elections in early November, the White House has just said that Biden will hit the trail, traveling to Orlando, Florida, on Tuesday to attend a \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  rally.\par \par \uc2 Then next Wednesday, Biden plans a major speech in New York at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/unitednations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 United Nations}}}\uc2  general assembly, where he will expand on the theme he is hammering on this autumn \u8211\'20\'13 the battle between the forces of democracy and autocracy, including within the US.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian president \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  has also now been confirmed as a speaker at \uc2 UNGA\uc2  and will address world leaders via a video-link from is country, embattled since the invasion by Russia six months ago.\par \par \uc2 If readers want to dive into live news of all the developments in the war, do follow our global blog on the topic, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/sep/16/russia-ukraine-war-zelenskiy-compares-scenes-in-izium-to-bucha-massacre-live-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And for news on Queen Elizabeth and the British royal family, as thousands queue to see the casket of the monarch as she lies in state in London, follow developments in our blog out of London, as they happen, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/live/2022/sep/16/queen-elizabeth-ii-lying-in-state-westminster-hall-king-charles-iii-mourners-queue-london-live-news-latest-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 The run-up to the 8 November midterms will be even more eventful than usual, after the January 6 committee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/16/trump-special-master-documents-biden-south-africa-latest?page=with:block-63249c258f083f878e70edbb#block-63249c258f083f878e70edbb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made clear its plans}}}\uc2  to release more details of the attack on the Capitol in the weeks ahead. Meanwhile, a federal judge has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/16/trump-special-master-documents-biden-south-africa-latest?page=with:block-632471018f08ee6e81d2b0fc#block-632471018f08ee6e81d2b0fc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 approved the appointment}}}\uc2  of a special master to review documents seized by the government from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago resort, while stopping the justice department from further examining them until the master has finished his work.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/16/trump-special-master-documents-biden-south-africa-latest?page=with:block-632479f08f08ee6e81d2b14e#block-632479f08f08ee6e81d2b14e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 meet with the families}}}\uc2  of two Americans detained in Russia, while Moscow has yet to act on a reported prisoner-swap offer made to secure their freedom.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/16/trump-special-master-documents-biden-south-africa-latest?page=with:block-632498788f08ee6e81d2b355#block-632498788f08ee6e81d2b355"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 apparently embraced}}}\uc2  the QAnon conspiracy theory to shore up his support base amid mounting legal problems.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 No, the White House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/16/trump-special-master-documents-biden-south-africa-latest?page=with:block-632485f38f0836766296d71c#block-632485f38f0836766296d71c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 did not hire a satanist}}}\uc2  as the deputy coordinator of its monkeypox response.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 One of the biggest outstanding questions the January 6 committee is trying to answer is what the Secret Service knew about the attack, and why agents acted the way they did as the Capitol was being stormed.\par \par \uc2 Questions have swirled around the Secret Service as its actions were brought to light, particularly after it was revealed that it deleted much of agents\u8217\'20\'19 communications from around the time of the insurrection. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2022-09-14/house-panel-gets-more-secret-service-records-in-jan-6-probe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloomberg reports}}}\uc2  that the committee has obtained documents, text messages and other materials from the Secret Service that could answer some of those questions. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a combination of a number of text messages, radio traffic, that kind of thing. Thousands of exhibits,\u8221\'20\'1D the committee\u8217\'20\'19s chair \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2  said earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 It was unclear if any of what had been turned over were the communications from January 5 and 6 that were reported as erased. Another committee member, \uc2 Zoe Lofgren\uc2 , said some of what had been obtained was \u8220\'20\'1Crelevant\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/11/missing-secret-service-texts-congress-notified-april"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Secret Service watchdog suppressed memo on January 6 texts erasure}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 January 6 committee could release interim report before midterms\par \par \uc2 The House committee investigating January 6 plans to release preliminary findings into the attack on the Capitol sometime in October, meaning voters may be digesting new details of the insurrection as the midterms approach, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2022/09/16/jan-6-committee-report-midterm-elections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Axios reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The committee has tentative plans to hold its first public hearing since July on 28 September, and Axios reports that its members are meeting today to flesh out the rest of their schedule. The Democratic chair \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2  said an early version of its report into the attack will come out in October. \u8220\'20\'1CThe goal is to have \u8230\'20\'26 some information pushed out, obviously, before the November election,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, adding that the time between the late-September hearing and the 8 November election \u8220\'20\'1Cwon\u8217\'20\'19t be a quiet period.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The committee\u8217\'20\'19s public hearings held in June and July {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/20/january-6-hearings-key-players"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dredged up highly publicized details}}}\uc2  of the attack and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s actions before, during and after that put the former president and his Republican allies on the defensive. That dynamic may repeat in the two months ahead, assuming the committee is able to match its earlier revelations.\par \par \uc2 For a sense of how the committee is thinking in relation to its impact on the midterms, here are the thoughts of one of its Democratic members, \uc2 Jamie Raskin\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThere are those partisans of former President Trump that will denounce anything we do, so we\u8217\'20\'19re not going to jump through hoops to please people who will call anything we do partisan.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 If there\u8217\'20\'19s one thing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  likes, it\u8217\'20\'19s people who like him. The Associated Press reports that the former president has reached out to a new group of friends: QAnon supporters.\par \par \uc2 While saying as recently as 2020 that he didn\u8217\'20\'19t know much about the convoluted conspiracy theory-turned-movement, he has lately made several social media posts embracing some of its ideas. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/technology-donald-trump-conspiracy-theories-government-and-politics-db50c6f709b1706886a876ae6ac298e2?utm_source=homepage&utm_medium=TopNews&utm_campaign=position_3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The AP reports}}}\uc2  that it may be a way to shore up his support base as he deals with an array of legal troubles, like the Mar-a-Lago investigation:\par \par \uc2 The former president may be seeking solidarity with his most loyal supporters at a time when he faces escalating investigations and potential challengers within his own party, according to Mia Bloom, a professor at \uc2 Georgia State University\uc2  who has studied QAnon and recently wrote a book about the group.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese are people who have elevated Trump to messiah-like status, where only he can stop this cabal,\u8221\'20\'1D Bloom told the AP on Thursday. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s why you see so many images (in online QAnon spaces) of Trump as Jesus.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On Truth Social, QAnon-affiliated accounts hail Trump as a hero and savior and vilify President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  by comparing him to Adolf Hitler or the devil. When Trump shares the content, they congratulate each other. Some accounts proudly display how many times Trump has \u8220\'20\'1Cre-truthed\u8221\'20\'1D them in their bios.\par \par \uc2 By using their own language to directly address QAnon supporters, Trump is telling them that they\u8217\'20\'19ve been right all along and that he shares their secret mission, according to Janet McIntosh, an anthropologist at \uc2 Brandeis University\uc2  who has studied QAnon\u8217\'20\'19s use of language and symbols.\par \par \uc2 It also allows Trump to endorse their beliefs and their hope for a violent uprising without expressly saying so, she said, citing his recent post about \u8220\'20\'1Cthe storm\u8221\'20\'1D as a particularly frightening example.\par \par \uc2 A survey published earlier this year found that belief in QAnon has surged ever since Trump left the White House.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/feb/23/qanon-believers-increased-america-study-finds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Belief in QAnon has strengthened in US since Trump was voted out, study finds}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats are growing increasingly engaged and cheery about the country\u8217\'20\'19s direction, though \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  remains is still unpopular and many Americans have a gloomy outlook for the country, according to a poll from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/09/16/us/politics/biden-democrats-abortion-trump-poll.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times released today}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The findings bolster the case that Biden\u8217\'20\'19s recent legislative successes, coupled with the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision overturning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and the mounting legal troubles of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , could make a meaningful difference for Democrats in the midterms.\par \par \uc2 The survey indicates an increase in enthusiasm among Democrats, 50% of which view the country as going in the right direction, up from 27% in July. Biden\u8217\'20\'19s approval rating among his party\u8217\'20\'19s voters has also climbed to 83% from 70% two months ago. But overall, the president\u8217\'20\'19s approval rating among all voters is still underwater at 42%, and while the poll does find Democrats with a two percentage point lead over the GOP on congressional ballots, that\u8217\'20\'19s within the survey\u8217\'20\'19s margin of error.\par \par \uc2 If there\u8217\'20\'19s one takeaway from the data, it could be this: Democratic voters are getting fired up to fight for Biden and their congressional majorities, but whether it will be enough to keep the House and Senate in the party\u8217\'20\'19s hands is another question. There\u8217\'20\'19s more to unpack from the poll, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2022/09/16/upshot/september-2022-times-siena-poll-crosstabs.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here\u8217\'20\'19s a link}}}\uc2  to the full data.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  is going to have a busy weekend. She\u8217\'20\'19s currently in Berlin representing the United States at a meeting of assembly speakers from the G7 group of wealthiest nations, but will this weekend head to Armenia, where fighting has flared with its neighbor and arch-rival Azerbaijan.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/russia-ukraine-azerbaijan-baku-armenia-719a56510651d0ac74d97722a9761d92"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more from the Associated Press}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Pelosi told reporters in Berlin she would to travel to Armenia on Saturday with a delegation that includes Rep. Jackie Speier, D-Calif., who is of Armenian descent. Pelosi declined to give further details about the trip, saying that traveling members of the Congress \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t like to be a target.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn any case, it is all about human rights and the respecting the dignity and worth of every person,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Armenian Defense Ministry\uc2  said the situation on the border with Azerbaijan has remained quiet since the cease-fire took effect at 8 p.m. Wednesday, and no violations were reported.\par \par \uc2 The cease-fire declaration followed two days of heavy fighting that marked the largest outbreak of hostilities in nearly two years.\par \par \uc2 Armenia and Azerbaijan traded blame for the shelling, with Armenian authorities accusing Baku of unprovoked aggression and Azerbaijani officials saying their country was responding to Armenian attacks.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Speaking of conservative media, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/ramon-antonio-vargas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ramon Antonio Vargas}}}\uc2  tuned into conservative stalwart Fox News to see what their political coverage looks like ahead of the midterms:\par \par \uc2 With most US voters indicating that the preservation of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights is their chief focus as midterm elections loom, the face of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/fox-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fox News}}}\uc2  and Republican politicians appear to be trying to shift attention to crime, a progressive media watchdog has warned.\par \par \uc2 As Democrats seek to maintain razor-thin advantages in both congressional chambers, an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mediamatters.org/fox-news/tucker-carlson-told-republicans-focus-crime-theyre-listening"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 analysis}}}\uc2  from \uc2 Media Matters for America\uc2  notes that on 19 August, the highest-rated Fox News host, \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 , implored \u8220\'20\'1Cevery Republican candidate in the United States\u8221\'20\'1D to pitch themselves as favoring \u8220\'20\'1Claw and order and equality under the law\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Since then, the word \u8220\'20\'1Ccrime\u8221\'20\'1D has appeared in 29% of Republican political ads, up from 12% in July, Media Matters said, citing reporting from the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/16/midterms-crime-fox-news-tucker-carlson-republicans-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fox News and Republicans try to shift attention to crime as midterms loom}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House has hired a satanist! Or at least that\u8217\'20\'19s what some conservative media outlets would like you to be believe.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/09/15/demetre-daskalakis-monkeypox-adviser-biden-00057021"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico has published a fascinating interview}}}\uc2  with Demetre Daskalakis, the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s deputy monkeypox coordinator, which gets into his passion for fighting HIV, his path to the White House and the thirst trap photos on his \uc2 Instagram\uc2  that led to some rather outrageous allegations of satanism. First, a bit about his career:\par \par \uc2 As a kid, he always knew he wanted to be a doctor (\u8220\'20\'1CFisher Price play kit,\u8221\'20\'1D he muses). But it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t until he was an undergraduate at \uc2 Columbia University\uc2  that he experienced an epiphany.\par \par \uc2 He was working on a big display of the AIDS memorial quilt, he says, and was tasked with flying to San Francisco to bring back a \u8220\'20\'1Croll of carpet that looked like a body in a shroud.\u8221\'20\'1D On the day the exhibit opened for the finished quilt, he watched as men his age \u8212\'20\'14 people who should have been enjoying their 20s \u8212\'20\'14 walked in, coughing and raging with a disease very likely to kill them.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy job is going to be to never let anyone get HIV or if people have HIV, make sure that they don\u8217\'20\'19t get sick and die. It hit me like that,\u8221\'20\'1D he recalls with a snap of his fingers.\par \par \uc2 Daskalakas\u8217\'20\'19s appearances at the White House briefing room have put him in the public eye, but much of the hubbub around him stems from photos on his \uc2 Instagram\uc2  account {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.poz.com/article/4-ways-bare-talks-doctor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 and elsewhere}}}\uc2  that show off his substantial tattoos, including one of a pentagram that led to allegations of satanism \u8211\'20\'13 which he denies. \u8220\'20\'1CI wish I were that interesting,\u8221\'20\'1D he told Politico, noting that he also has a large but less noticed tattoo of Jesus on his stomach.\par \par \uc2 As for the intent behind the photos, Daskalakas said he posted them for the same reason many people use \uc2 Instagram\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI spent a lot of money on my tattoos and a lot of time at the gym. I\u8217\'20\'19m showing it off.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s detention of Americans has been a thorn in the side of the White House for months, despite the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to win their release. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the Associated Press about the saga:\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  plans to meet at the White House on Friday with family members of \uc2 WNBA\uc2  star {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/brittney-griner"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Brittney Griner}}}\uc2  and Michigan corporate security executive Paul Whelan, both of whom remain jailed in Russia, senior administration officials told the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 The separate meetings are to be the first in-person encounter between Biden and the families and are taking place amid sustained but so far unsuccessful efforts by the administration {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2022/aug/05/russia-ready-to-discuss-prisoner-swap-but-will-resist-pressure-to-free-brittney-griner"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to secure the Americans\u8217\'20\'19 release}}}\uc2 . The administration said in July that it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2022/jul/27/brittney-griner-prisoner-swap-biden-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had made a \u8220\'20\'1Csubstantial proposal\u8221\'20\'1D to get them home}}}\uc2 , but despite plans for the White House meetings, there is no sign that a breakthrough is imminent.\par \par \uc2 Biden plans to speak at the White House with Griner\u8217\'20\'19s wife, Cherelle, and with the player\u8217\'20\'19s agent in one meeting and with Whelan\u8217\'20\'19s sister, Elizabeth, in the other.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2022/sep/15/joe-biden-to-meet-families-of-brittney-griner-and-paul-whelan-over-release-efforts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden to meet families of Brittney Griner and Paul Whelan over release efforts}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to meet today with families of Americans detained in Russia\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will meet today with the relatives of \uc2 WNBA\uc2  star Brittney Griner and executive Paul Whelan as his administration seeks their release from detention in Russia, the White House announced.\par \par \uc2 At the meeting with Griner\u8217\'20\'19s wife Cherelle Griner and Whelan\u8217\'20\'19s sister Elizabeth Whelan, Biden will \u8220\'20\'1Cdiscuss his continuing commitment to bringing their family members home safely,\u8221\'20\'1D press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said yesterday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs we have said before, we believe that Russia is wrongfully detaining Brittney and Paul under intolerable circumstances. And as you know, we have been directly engaged with the Russian government through appropriate channels,\u8221\'20\'1D Jean-Pierre said, noting that Washington had recently made a \u8220\'20\'1Csignificant offer\u8221\'20\'1D to secure their release. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have followed up on that offer repeatedly, and we\u8217\'20\'19ll continue to pursue every avenue to bring them home safely.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/09/16/politics/joe-biden-brittney-griner-and-paul-whelan-families-meeting/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to CNN}}}\uc2 , that offer includes a prisoner swap that would release Viktor Bout, an arms dealer jailed in the United States.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mobsters, corruption and now Trump: Raymond Dearie, the senior federal judge selected yesterday as special master in the Mar-a-Lago case, certainly has had an interesting career.\par \par \uc2 Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/09/15/brooklyn-judge-raymond-dearie-mar-a-lago-00057085"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published a profile}}}\uc2  of the 78-year-old juror who will be tasked with figuring out which documents taken by the \uc2 FBI\uc2  from the south Florida resort are privileged:\par \par \uc2 Lawyers and litigants who have appeared before Dearie describe him as independent, thorough and even-handed jurist who is fit to wrangle the dueling sides. As much as any judge put in this difficult position, they say he\u8217\'20\'19s up to the task.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s one of the few judges who both sides want to appear in front of. He is held in the highest regard by attorneys. He\u8217\'20\'19s someone who actually listens to the lawyers and considers what they have to say before he makes a decision,\u8221\'20\'1D said Lindsay Gerdes, a former Brooklyn federal prosecutor.\par \par \uc2 Sean Hecker, an attorney at Kaplan Hecker & Fink LLP who has had several cases before Dearie (including one pending) said much the same. \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s independent-minded, extremely smart and wise. Hard to imagine a more qualified person for this challenging assignment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump may be getting his way \u8211\'20\'13 for now - in the Mar-a-Lago case, but the former president could face legal peril from several other investigations nationwide.\par \par \uc2 A reminder of what\u8217\'20\'19s at stake came yesterday, when \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , the Georgia district attorney who empaneled a special grand jury to investigate the campaign of meddling aimed at overturning the state\u8217\'20\'19s election results in 2020, said her investigation could lead to people facing charges.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe allegations are very serious. If indicted and convicted, people are facing prison sentences,\u8221\'20\'1D Willis told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2022/09/15/fani-willis-georgia-prison/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Washington Post in an interview}}}\uc2 . She said her office has credible evidence that the law had been broken in the course of the effort by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s allies, which drew in well-known figures like his attorney \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  and senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But, this is the legal world, where matters play out over long timelines. Willis couldn\u8217\'20\'19t say when indictments are to be expected, and would not discuss who she may be targeting.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s a special master, and why has \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  asked for one in the Mar-a-Lago case?\par \par \uc2 As the Guardian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/15/judge-raymond-drearie-trump-special-master-records-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported yesterday}}}\uc2 , a special master can best be described as \u8220\'20\'1Can independent arbiter to vet records\u8221\'20\'1D, specifically for the two types of privilege Trump is worried about: \u8220\'20\'1Cattorney-client confidentiality or \u8230\'20\'26 a legal principle called executive privilege\u8221\'20\'1D. The winning candidate is Raymond Dearie, a veteran federal judge with long experience handling sensitive matters, including terrorism and other national security cases.\par \par \uc2 But the biggest impact of the ruling from judge Aileen Cannon is that the justice department can\u8217\'20\'19t continue reviewing documents taken from Mar-a-Lago while the special master does his work, greatly complicating their investigation into what was going on at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Florida resort. That ruling sets the stage for the government to take the matter to a higher court. Don\u8217\'20\'19t be surprised if we hear more about that today.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Judge continues to block DoJ from reviewing Trump documents as legal fight goes on\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. It was good news for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and bad news for the justice department yesterday, when the judge assigned to referee the legal wrangling over the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s search of Mar-a-Lago extended her block on the government reviewing the documents it had seized. Instead, she appointed a special master to go through them and weed out any that are under legal privilege rules. This is certainly not the last word on the matter, legally speaking \u8211\'20\'13 the justice department is expected to appeal the decision to a higher court.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a busy day otherwise:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is meeting with the South African president, \uc2 Cyril Ramaphosa\uc2 , at the White House at 2.15pm ET.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Fury is growing over Republican governors\u8217\'20\'19 campaign to bring migrants from the souther border to Democratic-run areas, which has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/09/15/desantis-migrants-marthas-vineyard-immigration-florida-00056870?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=12069c7e-e346-405c-ad2c-71cb1a62e514&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attracted the attention of the justice department}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Thedeputy secretary of state, \uc2 Wendy Sherman\uc2 , will discuss the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to free Americans held hostage abroad in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/washington-post-live/2022/09/16/deputy-secretary-state-wendy-sherman-americans-held-hostage-abroad/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Washington Post event}}}\uc2  at 10.30 am ET.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220916ei9g0020b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
