\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden vows to tackle \u8216\'20\'18venom and violence of white supremacy\u8217\'20\'19 and decries Trump over Charlottesville \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh (now) and Chris Stein (earlier) \par \uc2 5,943 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 September 2022\par 22:20 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President host \u8216\'20\'18United We Stand Summit\u8217\'20\'19 against hate crimeSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/15/biden-rail-strike-deal-united-summit-hate-violence-latest?page=with:block-632346138f0836766296cbad#block-632346138f0836766296cbad"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 took a victory lap this morning}}}\uc2  after his administration helped rail companies and unions reach a deal to head off a strike that could have worsened America\u8217\'20\'19s inflation issues, though the agreement still needs to win approval from workers. Elsewhere, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  took to the airwaves {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/15/biden-rail-strike-deal-united-summit-hate-violence-latest?page=with:block-63234d5c8f083f878e70e121#block-63234d5c8f083f878e70e121"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to warn of \u8220\'20\'1Cbig problems\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  if he was indicted, and saying it wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t stop him from running for office, should he decide to do so.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden delivered an address {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/09/15/fact-sheet-the-united-we-stand-summit-taking-action-to-prevent-and-address-hate-motivated-violence-and-foster-unity/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about hate crimes}}}\uc2 , highlighting the threat f white supremacists and efforts by the federal government to bolster community resources against hate-fueled violence.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Indiana\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/15/biden-rail-strike-deal-united-summit-hate-violence-latest?page=with:block-63232ddb8f0836766296ca80#block-63232ddb8f0836766296ca80"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 went into effect}}}\uc2 , outlawing the procedure with a few narrow exceptions.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s governor\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  had two planeloads of migrants {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/mexico-donald-trump-kamala-harris-immigration-ron-desantis-f9dcae99bdca91c1c874d68453a5960c?utm_source=homepage&utm_medium=TopNews&utm_campaign=position_4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 flown to the upscale island of Martha\u8217\'20\'19s Vineyard}}}\uc2  in Massachusetts, creating what authorities have called a \u8220\'20\'1Chumanitarian crisis\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former chief of staff \uc2 Mark Meadows\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/15/biden-rail-strike-deal-united-summit-hate-violence-latest?page=with:block-632351f68f0836766296cc29#block-632351f68f0836766296cc29"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has responded to a subpoena}}}\uc2  from federal investigators looking into the January 6 attack. He is the highest ranking former administration official to do so.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Reality Winner, the intelligence contractor who served more than four years in prison for leaking a report on Russian interference in the 2016 US election, has said she finds accusations that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  mishandled sensitive documents \u8220\'20\'1Cincredibly ironic\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/reality-winner"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 given her prosecution }}}\uc2  under his administration.\par \par \uc2 An \uc2 FBI\uc2  search of the former president\u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago home in Florida last month found {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/08/22/us/politics/trump-mar-a-lago-documents.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 300 classified documents}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Speaking to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/donald-trump/reality-winner-imprisoned-leaking-classified-report-calls-case-trump-i-rcna46683"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News}}}\uc2 , Winner, 30, said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt is incredibly ironic, and I would just let the justice department sort it out.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Winner added that it \u8220\'20\'1Cwasn\u8217\'20\'19t hard to believe\u8221\'20\'1D Trump held on to classified documents.\par \par \uc2 Reflecting on her own prison sentence, she said: \u8220\'20\'1CWhat I did when I broke the law was a political act at a very politically charged time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Winner also said she did not believe Trump should go to prison. She did not comment further on whether the former president should face charges under the Espionage Act, as she did in 2017.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not a case where I expect to see any prison time,\u8221\'20\'1D Winner said, \u8220\'20\'1Cand I\u8217\'20\'19m just fine with that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Winner was released early, on good behavior, in June 2021.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 The US is expected to announce a new $600m arms package to help the Ukrainian military, Reuters reports:\par \par \uc2 Two of the people familiar with the deliberations said the package could be announced later this evening\par \par \uc2 Several sources said it was expected the package would contain munitions, including more High Mobility Artillery Rocket Systems (HIMARS). Two of the sources said the package would include ammunition for howitzers\par \par \uc2 The White House declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 Washington has sent about $15.1bn\par \par \uc2 in security assistance to the Kyiv government since Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a 2017 interview by my colleague Lois Beckett with Susan Bro:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2017/oct/01/heather-heyers-mother-on-hate-in-the-us-were-not-going-to-hug-it-out-but-we-can-listen-to-each-other"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 'A white girl had to die for people to pay attention': Heather Heyer's mother on hate in the US}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s a damn shame that a white girl had to die for people to have to pay attention,\u8221\'20\'1D Bro said at the time. \u8220\'20\'1CI think if a black girl had died, or a black man, [the reaction would have been] \u8216\'20\'18Oh well, another person lost to violent protest.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden has honed in on right wing and white supremacist violence as a theme in the last few weeks.\par \par \uc2 In Philadelphia earlier this month, he a delivered rare primetime address on threats to democracy, taking a far more direct tone than he has in the past in condemning \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for his role in provoking violence, and Trump supporters\u8217\'20\'19 embrace of white supremacist ideologies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to confront the ways in which our toxic division fuel this crisis,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said tonight. In the last few years, he said, there has been \u8220\'20\'1CToo much hate \u8211\'20\'13 all for power and profit\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Among the new initiatives Biden announced tonight was what he called \u8220\'20\'1Ca new era\u8221\'20\'1D of national service to \u8220\'20\'1Cfoster stronger communities\u8221\'20\'1D. He is asking Congress to raise the compensation for national service through programs like \uc2 AmeriCorps\uc2  to go to $15 an hour.\par \par \uc2 AmeriCorps\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cwill develop new training opportunities for members in skills like bridge building, promoting civic engagement, and fostering social cohesion, and will develop new mechanisms to evaluate the impact and cost-effectiveness of national service and volunteerism interventions,\u8221\'20\'1D the White House said in a fact-sheet recapping the new initiatives.\par \par \uc2 The president also mentioned trainings on identifying and reporting hate fueled violence for local law enforcement groups, workplaces and houses of worship.\par \par \uc2 The Department of Education and the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2  will work with schools on programs to deter bullying, the White House said. And the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  will $20m in grants for state, local and Tribal governments, nonprofits, and universities to prevent hate-fueled violence.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden condemns 'the last guy' for defending white supremacists\par \par \uc2 Biden did not mention \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  by name, but while discussing the Charlottesville white supremacist rally, he did mention that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe last guy\u8221\'20\'1D defended the white supremacists in the aftermath of the attack.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen the last guy was asked, \u8216\'20\'18What do you think?\u8217\'20\'19 he said he thought there were some fine people on both sides,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe remain in a battle for the soul of our nation,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said, reviving a central theme of his 2020 campaign.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden vows to stop 'venom and violence' of white supremacy\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhite supremacist will not have the last word and this venom and violence cannot be the story of our time,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 Biden listed off a series of attacks against Jewish people, trans people, Asian Americans\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 He specifically mentioned the 2018 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2018/oct/27/pittsburgh-synagogue-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shooting}}}\uc2  at the Tree of Life synagogue in Pittsburgh, and violence against Asian Americans amid the pandemic, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/feb/05/hbcu-bomb-threats-fear-education-hate-crimes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bomb threats}}}\uc2  at HBCUs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll forms of hate fueled violence have no place in America,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, adding that we must \u8220\'20\'1Csilence it, rather than remain silent.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden speaks on countering hate crimes\par \par \uc2 The president was introduced by Susan Bro, the mother of Heather Heyer \u8211\'20\'13 who was killed in 2017 while protesting a white supremacist rally in Charlottesville, Virginia.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAcross the country, hate crimes are on the rise,\u8221\'20\'1D Bro said. And while her daughter\u8217\'20\'19s death received national and international attention, \u8220\'20\'1Call too often these hateful attacks are committed against people of color with unacceptably little public attention,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Biden has said that attack in Charlottesville spurred him to run in 2020, and he specifically asked Bro to introduce him tonight.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will soon make his appearance at a White House summit about countering hate crimes, where he\u8217\'20\'19s expected to unveil steps to bolster the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s response to violence motivated by antisemitism, xenophobia and racism.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/joan-greve"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joan E Greve}}}\uc2  has a preview of what we can expect from the president\u8217\'20\'19s address at the \u8220\'20\'1CUnited We Stand Summit\u8221\'20\'1D, which you can watch {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FZhhyxM1frY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The summit came four months after a white supremacist gunman attacked a supermarket in a predominantly Black area of Buffalo, New York, killing 10. Similar attacks in recent years have included the 2019 shooting at a \uc2 Walmart\uc2  in El Paso and the 2018 shooting at the Tree of Life synagogue in Pittsburgh.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe vast majority of Americans agree there\u8217\'20\'19s no place for hate-fueled violence in our country,\u8221\'20\'1D a senior administration official said, previewing Biden\u8217\'20\'19s remarks. \u8220\'20\'1C[The summit] is going to be a packed day of very rich conversation and an opportunity to demonstrate that we\u8217\'20\'19re more united than we are divided.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ahead of the summit, the Biden administration announced it would take several steps at the executive level to bolster the federal response to hate-fueled violence.\par \par \uc2 Among other policies, the White House said federal agencies would strengthen coordination to address such violence and more resources would be made available to schools, libraries and other community institutions to prevent hate-fueled attacks.\par \par \uc2 A bipartisan group of former White House officials will also launch a citizens\u8217\'20\'19 initiative meant to help foster community dialogue and develop solutions.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/15/biden-united-we-stand-summit-innitiatives"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden set to unveil initiatives to combat hate-fueled violence}}}\par \par \uc2 On that note, reporter {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/maanvi-singh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maanvi Singh}}}\uc2  is taking over the blog to cover Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech and the political developments in the final hours of the day.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has condemned Republican governors who brought migrants from the southern US border to Democratic-run areas further north.\par \par \uc2 Texas\u8217\'20\'19s Greg Abbott and other GOP governors have for months been sending migrants to Democratic-run cities including Washington, DC, but controversy over the practice flared anew today when {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/mexico-donald-trump-kamala-harris-immigration-ron-desantis-f9dcae99bdca91c1c874d68453a5960c?utm_source=homepage&utm_medium=TopNews&utm_campaign=position_4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two buses dropped migrants off}}}\uc2  in front of vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s residence in the capital, according to the Associated Press. Separately, Florida\u8217\'20\'19s governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  had two planeloads of migrants {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/mexico-donald-trump-kamala-harris-immigration-ron-desantis-f9dcae99bdca91c1c874d68453a5960c?utm_source=homepage&utm_medium=TopNews&utm_campaign=position_4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 flown to the upscale island of Martha\u8217\'20\'19s Vineyard}}}\uc2  in Massachusetts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is a legal way of doing this, for managing migrants. Republican governors interfering in this and using migrants as political pawns is shameful, is reckless,\u8221\'20\'1D White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PhGHiLyCnzs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said at her briefing to reporters today}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The American Civil Liberties Union\uc2  joined in condemning the practice, describing it as dehumanizing:\par \par \uc2 enltrAsylum-seekers are people\u8212\'20\'14period.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s cruel that some governors are involuntarily flying and busing people to other states, based on perceived immigration status.\par \par \uc2 Martha's Vineyard's response shows what MA looks like at its best: a place that values the lives of all people. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/WNaNI8OBOz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/WNaNI8OBOz}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ACLU Massachusetts (@ACLU_Mass) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ACLU_Mass/status/1570408524441845761?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 15, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Also on the list of things Democrats will punt until after the midterms: a ban on stock trading by congress members, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businessinsider.com/senate-bill-ban-congress-trading-stocks-after-midterms-merkley-2022-9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Insider reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Calls to bar lawmakers from holding or trading securities while in office have risen in recent months, fueled by repeated instances of congress members or their relatives buying or selling shares in companies that intersect with their work in the Capitol. Earlier this week, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2022/09/13/us/politics/congress-members-stock-trading-list.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The New York Times published an analysis}}}\uc2  that showed 97 lawmakers from both parties had carried out such transactions.\par \par \uc2 Democratic senator \uc2 Jeff Merkley\uc2  told Insider the upper chamber\u8217\'20\'19s effort to restrict trading wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t come up for consideration until after the November 8 midterms. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m looking forward to getting this across the finish line, but it\u8217\'20\'19s not going to happen before the election,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, citing his colleagues\u8217\'20\'19 busy schedule. \u8220\'20\'1CThere are a whole lot of other bills and judicial nominations lined up for the balance of the few days we have left here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The announcement came despite House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  saying yesterday that such a ban would be ready to come to the floor of that chamber this month. Some of Merkley\u8217\'20\'19s colleagues were openly disappointed with his comments, with senator Elizabeth Warren saying, \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no reason that we should not have a stock trading bill on the floor and vote on it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 On the subject of the (hopefully) averted rail strike, the president is throwing a little shade at the Wall Street Journal, thus:\par \par \uc2 enltrThanks for your concern, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WSJ?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @wsj}}}\uc2 . To answer your question: yes, the trains are running on time. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ZpJIyFZJvL"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ZpJIyFZJvL}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1570440907710930944?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 15, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 More:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/sep/15/biden-tentative-agreement-freight-rail-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden hails \u8216\'20\'18tentative agreement\u8217\'20\'19 to avoid looming US rail strike}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Politico reports that the Senate bill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/24/pete-buttigieg-same-sex-bill-republicans-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to protect same-sex marriage}}}\uc2  under federal law will be with us after the midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 Such a bill is needed, the thinking goes, because the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  removed the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June and noises have also emanated from that chamber which suggest other privacy based rights, including same-sex marriage, same-sex sex, interracial marriage and access to contraception, could next be targeted.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://judiciary.house.gov/news/documentsingle.aspx?DocumentID=5027#:~:text=Washington%2C%20July%2019%2C%202022&text=This%20is%20the%20first%20time,Act%20over%20a%20decade%20ago."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Respect for Marriage Act}}}\uc2  passed the House with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/interactive/2022/republican-marriage-equality-vote-count/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 only 47 Republicans}}}\uc2  in support. Senators are more hopeful that 10 Republicans will back it, thereby beating the filibuster.\par \par \uc2 Today, Burgess Everett of Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/burgessev/status/1570465497375801344?s=46&t=2FOTPEjYknoNYavAyOZmlw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  that \uc2 Tammy Baldwin\uc2 , a Democratic senator from Wisconsin, \u8220\'20\'1Csays the same sex marriage vote will be AFTER the election. Group will put out a statement soon\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He adds that \uc2 Thom Tillis\uc2 , a Republican from North Carolina, \u8220\'20\'1Csays the bipartisan group recommended to [majority leader Chuck] Schumer that the bill should be delayed until after the election and has a much better chance of passing then.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Since the death of the Queen on 8 September, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk/prince-andrew"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Prince Andrew}}}\uc2  has returned to the public sphere.\par \par \uc2 Prince Andrew. Photograph: Danny Lawson/AP\par \par \uc2 The Duke of York\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/video/2022/sep/12/royal-family-walk-behind-queen-coffin-edinburgh-procession-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prominence}}}\uc2  at events marking the death of his mother, such as the progress of her coffin through Edinburgh and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2022/sep/14/prince-andrew-queen-coffin-procession-counsellor-of-state-jeffrey-epstein-scandal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 London this week}}}\uc2 , is to be expected. Andrew is grieving personal loss during a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/the-demise-of-her-majesty-queen-elizabeth-ii-national-mourning-guidance/the-demise-of-her-majesty-queen-elizabeth-ii-national-mourning-guidance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 national period of mourning}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But just months ago, amid fallout from his long and controversial association with the convicted sex traffickers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jeffrey-epstein"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ghislaine-maxwell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ghislaine Maxwell}}}\uc2  , any public appearance at all would have seemed entirely unlikely.\par \par \uc2 The royal, now eighth in line to the throne, was stripped of his military patronages and use of the HRH title after he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2022/feb/15/prince-andrew-and-virginia-giuffre-reach-settlement-in-principle"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 paid a financial settlement to }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2022/feb/15/prince-andrew-and-virginia-giuffre-reach-settlement-in-principle"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Virginia Giuffre}}}\uc2  , who had accused him of sexual assault, a claim he denied.\par \par \uc2 For attorneys who represented Epstein victims, and for other advocates for sex-crimes victims, Andrew\u8217\'20\'19s sudden reappearance has seemed jarring. Some have said it could prove triggering for Epstein survivors, even if they never encountered Andrew.\par \par \uc2 Mariann Wang, who represented more than a dozen Epstein survivors, said it was \u8220\'20\'1Cbeyond shameful to see Andrew being granted any form of state-sponsored honor or privilege, given his past affiliation with Jeffrey Epstein\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Epstein pleaded guilty to solicitation of a minor for prostitution in 2008.\par \par \uc2 Andrew, who continued to associate with the New York financier long after his guilty plea, vehemently denies a claim that he had sex with an Epstein accuser when the girl was a teen.\par \par \uc2 Wang continued: \u8220\'20\'1CThe brave women who came forward to hold Epstein, Maxwell and others to account deserve better. His past conduct and judgment make clear that he is not worthy of any state-sponsored privileges, including reaping the benefits of being a royal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/15/jeffrey-epstein-prince-andrew-queen-death"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein victims condemn Prince Andrew\u8217\'20\'19s return to public life}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s White House chief of staff secretly bought a book in which 27 mental health professionals warned that the president was psychologically unfit for the job, then used it as a guide in his attempts to cope with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s irrational behavior.\par \par \uc2 News of \uc2 John Kelly\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s surreptitious purchase comes in a new book from Peter Baker of the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  and Susan Glasser of the New Yorker. The Divider: Trump in the White House, 2017-2021, will be published next week. \uc2 The Guardian{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2022/sep/14/trump-iran-assassination-fear-suleimani-drone-strike-divider-book-baker-glasser"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 obtained}}}\uc2  a copy.\par \par \uc2 The book Kelly bought, The Dangerous Case of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , was a bestseller in 2017. In January 2018 its editor, then Yale psychiatrist Bandy Lee, described its aims {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2018/jan/07/donald-trump-dangerous-psychiatrist"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a Guardian column}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 She wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CWhile we keep within the letter of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/head-quarters/2017/jul/28/the-goldwater-rule-why-commenting-on-mental-health-from-a-distance-is-unhelpful"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Goldwater rule}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 which prohibits psychiatrists from diagnosing public figures without a personal examination and without consent \u8211\'20\'13 there is still a lot that mental health professionals can tell before the public reaches awareness.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese come from observations of a person\u8217\'20\'19s patterns of responses, of media appearances over time, and from reports of those close to him. Indeed, we know far more about Trump in this regard than many, if not most, of our patients.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNevertheless, the personal health of a public figure is her private affair \u8211\'20\'13 until, that is, it becomes a threat to public health.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2022/sep/15/john-kelly-dangerous-case-donald-trump-peter-baker-susan-glasser-divider"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump chief of staff used book on president\u8217\'20\'19s mental health as guide}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats in Congress are trying to make the most of the next few weeks before the midterms, where voters may well eject them from the majority in the House, Senate or perhaps both. One of their priorities has been a bill codifying into law same-sex marriage rights \u8211\'20\'13 which are currently guaranteed by a supreme court ruling.\par \par \uc2 The effort came after conservative judge \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  suggested reconsidering the case granting the rights in an opinion released as the court overturned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights guaranteed by Roe v Wade. While the bill, known as the Respect for Marriage Act, passed the House with some Republican support, its fate in the Senate has been mysterious. It will need at least 10 GOP votes to overcome the inevitable filibuster, but the opposition party hasn\u8217\'20\'19t made clear whether they\u8217\'20\'19ll organize for or against it.\par \par \uc2 Punchbowl News reports that Democrats in the chamber and the Republicans who do support the bill are making a renewed push to get it up for a vote:\par \par \uc2 enltrBaldwin, collins, Sinema and Tillis are huddled around a desk on the senate floor. They are the key players on the same sex marriage bill.\par \par \uc2 Theres buzz Schumer could file cloture today. Very fluid situation.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Sherman (@JakeSherman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1570447055218438144?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 15, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Its fortunes however remain shrouded in mystery. Republican senator \uc2 John Thune\uc2 , for instance, isn\u8217\'20\'19t sure how the bill will fare:\par \par \uc2 enltrJust caught up with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenJohnThune?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SenJohnThune}}}\uc2 , who told us this about the same sex marriage bill: \u8220\'20\'1CI don't think we will know [whether it will pass] until we have the vote\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Sherman (@JakeSherman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1570433467959349248?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 15, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Looks like we may get more clarity later today on when exactly it will come up for a vote:\par \par \uc2 enltrLawmakers negotiating the same sex marriage bill said they\u8217\'20\'19ll have a statement later today on the path forward.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jake Sherman (@JakeSherman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1570452416184848386?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 15, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/15/biden-rail-strike-deal-united-summit-hate-violence-latest?page=with:block-632346138f0836766296cbad#block-632346138f0836766296cbad"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 took a victory lap this morning}}}\uc2  after his administration helped rail companies and unions reach a deal to head off a strike that could have worsened America\u8217\'20\'19s inflation issues, though the agreement still needs to win approval from workers. Elsewhere, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  took to the airwaves {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/15/biden-rail-strike-deal-united-summit-hate-violence-latest?page=with:block-63234d5c8f083f878e70e121#block-63234d5c8f083f878e70e121"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to warn of \u8220\'20\'1Cbig problems\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  if he was indicted, and saying it wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t stop him from running for office, should he decide to do so.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden plans to make an address {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/09/15/fact-sheet-the-united-we-stand-summit-taking-action-to-prevent-and-address-hate-motivated-violence-and-foster-unity/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about hate crimes}}}\uc2  this afternoon at 3:30 pm, which the White House is calling the \u8220\'20\'1CUnited We Stand Summit\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Indiana\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/15/biden-rail-strike-deal-united-summit-hate-violence-latest?page=with:block-63232ddb8f0836766296ca80#block-63232ddb8f0836766296ca80"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has gone into effect}}}\uc2 , outlawing the procedure with a few narrow exceptions.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former chief of staff Mark Meadows{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/15/biden-rail-strike-deal-united-summit-hate-violence-latest?page=with:block-632351f68f0836766296cc29#block-632351f68f0836766296cc29"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has responded to a subpoena}}}\uc2  from federal investigators looking into the January 6 attack. He is the highest ranking former administration official to do so.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s an example of the type of legal trouble Trump could face beyond the Mar-a-Lago investigation. The federal inquiry into the January 6 attack is ongoing, and Reuters reports citing CNN that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former chief of staff \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  has responded to a subpoena from investigators:\par \par \uc2 The former White House chief of staff \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , who served under {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 , has complied with a subpoena from the justice department investigation into the events surrounding the January 6 attack on the Capitol, CNN reported on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 That makes him the highest-ranking Trump official known to have responded to a subpoena in the federal investigation, CNN said.\par \par \uc2 The attack on the Capitol by Trump supporters led to several deaths, injured police officers and delayed certification of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory over Trump in the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 Meadows provided the same materials he gave to the House January 6 committee, satisfying the obligations of the subpoena, CNN reported, citing an unnamed source.\par \par \uc2 Meadows initially cooperated with the January 6 committee in 2021 but later sued over the subpoenas.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US House of Representatives\uc2  earlier this year voted to refer Meadows to the justice department for contempt of Congress. The department declined to charge him.\par \par \uc2 Reuters could not immediately contact Meadows for comment. George Terwilliger, a lawyer who represents Meadows, did not immediately respond to an e-mailed request for comment.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/15/trumps-ex-chief-of-staff-mark-meadows-complies-with-january-6-subpoena"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s ex-chief of staff Mark Meadows complies with January 6 subpoena}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump warns of 'big problems' if indicted\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who is at the center of an array of state and federal investigations over various events before, during and after his presidency, warned in an interview today that \u8220\'20\'1Cbig problems\u8221\'20\'1D would ensue if he was indicted.\par \par \uc2 Trump also said such a development wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t stop him from running for the White House again, as he is widely believed to do in the 2024 election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think the people of the United States would stand for it. And as you know, if a thing like that happened, I would have no prohibition against running,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hughhewitt.com/donald-trump-returns-to-talks-election-2022-indictments/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an interview with conservative radio host Hugh Hewitt}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think they\u8217\'20\'19d have big problems, big problems. I just don\u8217\'20\'19t think they\u8217\'20\'19d stand for it. They will not, they will not sit still and stand for this ultimate of hoaxes,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said as he discussed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/02/trump-mar-a-lago-search-doj-photos"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the investigation into government secrets found by the FBI at his Mar-a-Lago resort}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Hewitt seemed to understand how the former president\u8217\'20\'19 comments would sound, and asked, \u8220\'20\'1CYou know that the legacy media will say you\u8217\'20\'19re attempting to incite violence with that statement. How do you respond to what will inevitably,\u8221\'20\'1D before Trump cut him off.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s not, that\u8217\'20\'19s not inciting. I\u8217\'20\'19m just saying what my opinion is. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think the people of this country would stand for it,\u8221\'20\'1D he replied.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrat representatives \uc2 Cori Bush\uc2 , \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2  and \uc2 Jamaal Bowman\uc2  will today introduce a resolution in the House recognizing access to utilities - water, sanitation, electricity, heating, cooling, public transit, and broadband communications - as basic human rights which should be safe, reliable, affordable, sustainable, and climate resilient.\par \par \uc2 Millions of Americans are struggling to afford utility bills, and as many as one in three households are forced to choose between paying rent, medicine, food or their water, power and broadband services.\par \par \uc2 The resolution includes a commitment to providing affordable utilities based on households\u8217\'20\'19 ability to pay and ending shutoffs, tax sale foreclosures, and the selling of debt to collection agencies. It also calls for a ban on water privatisation as investors increasingly view struggling utilities like those in Jackson, Mississippi and Baltimore, Maryland as opportunities.\par \par \uc2 Resolutions have no binding authority but are a way to push Congress to commit to further action such as hearings and future legislation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA person should never be forced to choose between electricity or heat during the winter. A person should never have their only option for water be water that is not properly sanitized. A person should never have to wait in a restaurant parking lot to get Wi-Fi to finish their homework or pay their bills,\u8221\'20\'1D said Bush, who represents Missouri.\par \par \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s war in Ukraine, the climate breakdown and corporate greed have driven up fossil fuel prices for consumers, while rising water and sanitation costs are linked to aging and neglected infrastructure, federal disinvestment and climate shocks. Utilities can use punitive measures to collect unpaid bills, forcing people to lose their homes or cutting off essential services - which disproportionately impacts households of color, Indigenous Americans and low-income communities.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the richest country the world has ever known, it is an outrage that millions of Americans struggle with utility insecurity, substandard and dangerous services, and inhumane shutoffs. It\u8217\'20\'19s time to change the conversation around what we all deserve, take the profit motive out of providing the basics of a good life, and give every American the opportunity to thrive,\u8221\'20\'1D said Tlaib of Michigan.\par \par \uc2 Bowman of New York said: \u8220\'20\'1CFrom Jackson, Mississippi to New York\u8217\'20\'19s 16th Congressional District, Black people do not have access to clean water, are disproportionately energy burdened, and are bearing the brunt of the climate crisis. This resolution will recognize utilities as a basic human right, ban the destructive practice of privatizing our utilities, and promote public power. We cannot thrive as a nation and as a people until all have safe, accessible, reliable and climate conscious utility rights.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The resolution is endorsed by more than 200 environmental, racial justice and faith organizations, and co-sponsored by \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2 , Barbara Lee, \uc2 Ilhan Omar\uc2 , and Jan Schakowsky, among others.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 The message from Biden\u8217\'20\'19s just-concluded event at the White House with labor union and railway company representatives could be summed up with two words: \u8220\'20\'1Cthank you\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The president was undoubtedly sincere, for a strike that took freight rail out of commission could have driven inflation higher and further soured voters on his administration.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur nation\u8217\'20\'19s rail system is the backbone of our supply chain,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said, listing all the goods it carries, from natural gas to food.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis agreement allows us to continue to rebuild a better America with an economy that truly works for working people and their families. Today is a win, I mean it sincerely, a win for America. I want to thank you all for getting this done, both business and labor, thank you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As he was leaving the Rose Garden, a reporter asked whether the celebration wasn\u8217\'20\'19t premature, given that the labor unions still need to approve the deal. The president did not respond.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden has begun speaking at the White House about the agreement reached to head off a rail workers strike.\par \par \uc2 You can watch it below:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 As we wait for Biden to speak, consider reading Adam Lowenstein\u8217\'20\'19s report on Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 plans to challenge new rules requiring publicly trade companies to disclose the impacts of their business on the climate:\par \par \uc2 Republican officials and corporate lobby groups are teeing up a multi-pronged legal assault on the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s effort to help investors hold public corporations accountable for their carbon emissions and other climate change risks.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  (SEC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sec.gov/rules/proposed/2022/33-11042.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposed}}}\uc2  new climate disclosure rules in March that would require public companies to report the climate-related impact and risks to their businesses.\par \par \uc2 The regulator has since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sec.gov/news/speech/gensler-statement-financial-stability-oversight-council-meeting-072822"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 received}}}\uc2  more than 14,500 comments. Submissions from 24 Republican state attorneys general and some of the country\u8217\'20\'19s most powerful industry associations suggest that these groups are preparing a series of legal challenges after the regulation is finalized, which could {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.bloomberglaw.com/securities-law/gm-goldman-press-secs-gensler-on-indirect-emissions-in-10-ks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 happen}}}\uc2  as soon as next month.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/sep/15/republicans-climate-rules-legal-challenge-allow-emissions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans plan legal assault on climate disclosure rules for public companies}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt might not make sense for us to poke the bear.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t want to see a dustup over anything.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Those are two of the quotes from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/09/15/democrats-congress-midterms-legislation-00056804"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this Politico piece}}}\uc2  that captures the vibe among Democrats in Congress worried about their control of the House and Senate less than two months before the midterms. According to the piece, lawmakers are looking to avoid any disputes or crises in the weeks ahead and instead concentrate voters\u8217\'20\'19 attention on the bills they\u8217\'20\'19ve passed over the last two years. \u8220\'20\'1CJust brag about everything we\u8217\'20\'19ve gotten done,\u8221\'20\'1D is how Rhode Island representative \uc2 David Cicilline\uc2  put it.\par \par \uc2 The vibes are similar at the White House, where \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has taken time out of his day to personally fete the deal his administration brokered to keep rail worker unions from striking. It\u8217\'20\'19s a crisis that\u8217\'20\'19s been averted, and he intends to remind voters of that.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to speak on rail labor agreement after strike narrowly averted\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will meet the negotiators who reached an agreement that headed off a strike by railway worker\u8217\'20\'19s unions, and deliver remarks on the deal at 11 am eastern time, the White House announced. This was scheduled with short notice so it\u8217\'20\'19s not listed yet, but the White House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/c/WhiteHouse"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 YouTube channel}}}\uc2  typically broadcasts such events live.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Now that a strike has been averted, \uc2 Amtrak\uc2  announced that it is trying to reschedule the long-distance trains it cancelled yesterday in anticipation of a work stoppage:\par \par \uc2 enltrAmtrak is working to quickly restore canceled trains and reaching out directly to impacted customers to accommodate on first available departures. Visit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Bdp20oXtFZ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Bdp20oXtFZ}}}\uc2  for the latest updates.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Amtrak Alerts (@AmtrakAlerts) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AmtrakAlerts/status/1570397115783733249?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 15, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Indiana has joined the ranks of states banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , outlawing the procedure except in narrow circumstances with a law that went into effect today, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/poppy-noor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Poppy Noor}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 A sweeping \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban went into effect in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/indiana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Indiana}}}\uc2  on Thursday, containing only extremely narrow exceptions for medical emergencies, rape and incest and making it the latest state to largely outlaw the procedure in the US.\par \par \uc2 The ban is being challenged in court by the \uc2 ACLU\uc2  and several \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care providers, with hearings set to start on 19 September.\par \par \uc2 Indiana lawmakers passed the legislation during a special legislative session in early August, with a six-week pause before it came into effect. Then, Indiana was the first in the nation to bring in a new law banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after Roe fell. Before that, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists had relied on so-called \u8220\'20\'1Ctrigger laws\u8221\'20\'1D, written pre-Roe, to ban the procedure once the supreme court decision came down.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/15/indiana-abortion-ban-trigger-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Near-total \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban takes effect in Indiana}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 As part of the agreement to avert a potential strike, freight rail companies conceded to a more flexible attendance policy that will allow workers to call out for medical emergencies without being punished, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2022/09/15/rail-strike-deal-agreement-biden/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Washington Post reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It also includes a pay increase of 24 percent over the next two years, annual bonuses and changes in how health care costs are managed, the Post reports. Had the impasse not been resolved, a strike could have begun after midnight on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Democratic political leaders are cheering the agreement. Here\u8217\'20\'19s House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The report of a tentative agreement between railroads represented by labor unions and the National Carriers\u8217\'20\'19 Conference Committee is good news for our nation\u8217\'20\'19s economy, our security and the well-being of the American people. I commend President Biden for his personal involvement and insistence on resolution and especially Labor Secretary \uc2 Marty Walsh\uc2  for leading the negotiations.\par \par \uc2 Had a deal not been reached, Pelosi said Congress may have stepped in, she said:\par \par \uc2 Congress under the Commerce Clause of the Constitution has the authority and responsibility to ensure the uninterrupted operation of essential transportation services and has in the past enacted legislation for such purposes. Led by the Transportation and Infrastructure Committee, the House prepared and had reviewed legislation, so that we would be ready to act, pursuant to Section 10 of the Railway Labor Act. Thankfully this action may not be necessary.\par \par \uc2 The deal must still be approved by the rail workers\u8217\'20\'19 unions.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  on the narrowly averted rail strike:\par \par \uc2 A tentative agreement has been reached to avert {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/sep/14/us-railroad-strike-union-pacific-bnsf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a freight rail strike}}}\uc2  that could have disrupted commuter rail services across the US, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 A strike would also have dealt a major blow to Democrats two months before midterm elections in which they will try to keep control of the Senate and the House.\par \par \uc2 A rail shutdown could have hit food and fuel supplies \u8211\'20\'13 freezing almost 30% of US cargo shipments by weight, stoking inflation, costing the US economy as much as $2bn a day and affecting the energy, agriculture, manufacturing and retail sectors.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/sep/15/biden-tentative-agreement-freight-rail-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden hails \u8216\'20\'18tentative agreement\u8217\'20\'19 to avoid looming US rail strike}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 How disruptive would a freight rail strike be to the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest economy? Here are a few numbers, from industry group {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aar.org/economic-impact-of-railroad-shutdown#!"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Association of America Railroads}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A work stoppage would have cost $2 billion per-day, and required 467,000 trucks to pick up the slack from idled railroads, which moved approximately 75,000 cars, containers and trailers daily. But the shipping industry doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have that capacity \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s struggling with shortages of manpower and trucks.\par \par \uc2 Amtrak\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s announcement yesterday that it would cancel long-distance service in anticipation of the strike that could have started Friday was a taste of the consequences that could have come. More worrying would have been the economic ripple effects from tens of thousands of shipping containers being idled or delayed. Supply chain snarls such as these are one reason why consumer prices have risen so quickly in the United States since the start of 2021, and sent Biden\u8217\'20\'19s approval rating steadily lower. And {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/sep/13/us-inflation-rate-august-2022-gas-prices"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as data released earlier this week indicated}}}\uc2 , the inflation wave isn\u8217\'20\'19t abating as quickly as many economists hoped.\par \par \uc2 All of this would have most likely been worsened by the narrowly averted rail strike.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden administration breathes sigh of relief as rail strike averted\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s US politics blog is wishing you a good morning and hoping you got a restful night of sleep, because a bunch of people in Washington did not. After 20 hours of talks that stretched into the wee hours of Thursday, rail companies and unions representing their employees agreed to a tentative deal that would avert a strike, which could have snarled commerce across the country and likely made America\u8217\'20\'19s inflation problem worse.\par \par \uc2 Consider it a crisis averted for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , who is looking to avoid economic disruptions as he fights to rebuild his popularity ahead of the November midterms.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden is hosting the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/09/15/fact-sheet-the-united-we-stand-summit-taking-action-to-prevent-and-address-hate-motivated-violence-and-foster-unity/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnited We Stand Summit\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  at the White House today at 3.30pm eastern time, where he\u8217\'20\'19ll highlight communities\u8217\'20\'19 efforts to recover from hate crimes, including mass shootings.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The House of Representatives will consider legislation to prevent attempts to make it easier to fire federal employees, something \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2022/07/22/trump-2025-radical-plan-second-term"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has mulled doing}}}\uc2  if he returns to the White House.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Top Senate Democrat \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  thinks the party will lose its majority in the House in the upcoming midterms, according to comments he loudly made at a Washington restaurant {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://punchbowl.news/archive/91522-punchbowl-news-am/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that were reported by Punchbowl News}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220915ei9f001uq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
