\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Democrats call Indiana\u8217\'20\'19s near-total  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban a \u8216\'20\'18death sentence\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Poppy Noor \par \uc2 937 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 September 2022\par 18:52 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Law, which takes effect today, contains narrow exceptions and effectively wipes out \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access for 1.5m people in the state\par \par \uc2 As Indiana\u8217\'20\'19s near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban went into effect on Thursday, Democratic lawmakers announced their dismay, referring to the ban as a \u8220\'20\'1Cdeath sentence\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The bill, SB 1, contains only extremely narrow exceptions in which abortions may now be performed \u8211\'20\'13 with abortions for rape and incest capped at 10 weeks; only to be delivered in hospitals; and limiting the procedure to medical emergencies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHoosier women have lost a fundamental right to privacy in medical decisions with this near total ban, which is extremely cruel,\u8221\'20\'1D said Representative Sue Errington of the 34th district in Indiana. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m old enough to remember before Roe v Wade. And I know that laws like this only ban safe legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Women are going to suffer, and some will die from this,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Errington, who tried to bring a referendum on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Indiana this year, said the bill was hugely out of step with what Hoosiers want. The Republican party\u8217\'20\'19s own polling from late June, before they signed the bill into law, showed most people in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://indianacapitalchronicle.com/2022/07/19/abortion-gop-poll-shows-little-hoosier-support-for-total-ban/?eType=EmailBlastContent&eId=1587f191-0e3c-4603-bcb4-ca657ad41bb6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Indiana do not support a total ban}}}\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The ban is being challenged in court by the \uc2 ACLU\uc2  and several \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care providers, with hearings set to start on 19 September.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe basic right we all believe we possess is to be able to control our bodies and make decisions for ourselves surrounding reproductive issues, without interference from the state,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ken Falk, of the \uc2 ACLU\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CBut what the state is saying here, is, \u8216\'20\'18we don\u8217\'20\'19t care that your pregnancy is going to cause you severe mental harms or physical problems, you just can\u8217\'20\'19t have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Indiana lawmakers passed the legislation during a special legislative session in early August, with a six-week pause before it came into effect.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/14/west-virginia-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 West Virginia followed}}}\uc2  and also passed a sweeping ban.\par \par \uc2 The law effectively wipes out \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access for 1.5 million Hoosiers of reproductive age, and will have far-reaching consequences as Indiana had become a safe haven for those seeking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in other nearby states.\par \par \uc2 Now, residents in places like Wisconsin and Kentucky, which have total or near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in place, will have to travel hundreds of miles for the procedure. Meanwhile, other midwestern states, like Michigan, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2022/09/08/michigan-supreme-court-abortion/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will put \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights directly to the public in a ballot in November}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe impact is going to be felt suddenly. But its true force is going to be felt over the years to come,\u8221\'20\'1D said the Indiana state senator Shelli Yoder. \u8220\'20\'1CWe continue to hear from healthcare providers that they are second-guessing whether or not they should practice in Indiana because the way the law is written, it puts their profession and their license at severe risk.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Indiana law is an all-encompassing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban with some extreme restrictions. It limits abortions to cases where there is serious risk to the health or life of the pregnant person, and in the case of a lethal fetal anomaly up to 20 weeks post-fertilization.\par \par \uc2 Similar \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions in other states have already {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2022/08/03/texas-abortion-law-pregnancy/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  putlivesat risk}}}\uc2 , which is of huge concern in Indiana, which has some of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wthr.com/article/news/investigations/13-investigates/indiana-has-one-worst-rates-childbirth-related-death/531-c9366a08-be9a-41fe-b8ce-18f1d8e37492"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 worst maternal and infant mortality rates in the US}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Because of those restrictions, Yoder said she believed the bill was anything but pro-life. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s totally hypocritical,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CYou would think that if a state is going to pronounce they are a pro-life, that we would have a support network in place to actually help those living there.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Furthermore, she said exceptions allowing abortions in the case of rape or incest will cause more grief \u8211\'20\'13 because of a clause that caps them after 10 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis bill says, we are only going to give full constitutional rights to women if their very life is threatened, or they are a victim of rape. Then those women and girls have just 10 weeks to come to terms with the assault, being pregnant by their assaulter, and sorting through that trauma,\u8221\'20\'1D Yoder said.\par \par \uc2 Other experts have said parts of that stipulate abortions must be performed in hospitals or surgical centers owned by hospitals are going to have huge knock on effects.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHistorically, in recent years, almost all abortions have taken place in clinics. It\u8217\'20\'19s not clear how many hospitals in Indiana will even choose to make abortions available,\u8221\'20\'1D says Mary Ziegler, a US \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law expert from the \uc2 University of California, Davis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMany hospitals have religious policies that are opposed to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . So requiring all abortions to be performed in this handful of facilities will make it more likely there\u8217\'20\'19ll be fewer abortions altogether,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Ziegler says the law is just the latest in a set of attempts by lawmakers to change the national conversation around \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CStates that are criminalizing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  are trying to create a new framework. It\u8217\'20\'19s a conscious effort to say, \u8216\'20\'18we shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be thinking of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as healthcare, we should be thinking of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a crime,\u8217\'20\'19 she said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe more people in states hear that kind of argument and see things framed that way by people in power, the more some of them will come to believe it,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ziegler.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 This story was updated on 15 September 2022 to remove Ohio from the list of states with current near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, following a state court suspension of the measure.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220915ei9f000um\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
