\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Republicans won\u8217\'20\'19t stop until  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  is banned across America. And it could be\b0\par\par\uc2 Moira Donegan \par \uc2 1,093 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 September 2022\par 16:41 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 It is time for liberal Americans, and all American women, to face this reality: there will soon be no safe states\par \par \uc2 Republicans want to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide, and they have the nerve to claim that this is a compromise. This week, Senator Lindsay Graham, of South Carolina, introduced a bill to ban all abortions everywhere in the United States at 15 weeks. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is already banned before 15 weeks in 15 states.\par \par \uc2 It is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2022/us/abortion-laws-roe-v-wade.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banned outright}}}\uc2  in Alabama, Arkansas, Idaho, Kentucky, Louisiana, Mississippi, Missouri, Oklahoma, South Dakota, Tennessee, Texas and Wisconsin. Indiana\u8217\'20\'19s ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  went into effect {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/09/14/1122835073/indiana-abortion-ban-thursday-roe-dobbs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 just this Wednesday}}}\uc2 . It is banned at six weeks \u8211\'20\'13 in practice a total ban \u8211\'20\'13 in Georgia and Ohio. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/09/13/politics/west-virginia-state-legislature-abortion-ban/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 West Virginia}}}\uc2  passed an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, too. It won\u8217\'20\'19t be the last.\par \par \uc2 The Republican national 15-week ban that Graham has introduced will do nothing to help the women in these states, who will not have their rights restored. It\u8217\'20\'19s not a floor for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legality: it is a ceiling. The goal is to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in blue states. Currently, 58% of American women of childbearing age live in states that are \u8220\'20\'1Chostile or extremely hostile\u8221\'20\'1D to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/united-states/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Guttmacher Institute}}}\uc2 . Republicans want to raise that to 100%.\par \par \uc2 One way that we know that the Republicans will ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationally as soon as they get the chance is because they keep saying that they want to. This is the sixth time Graham has introduced a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban bill. The previous five were, by his standards, less extreme: they all banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 20 weeks. That Graham has pushed his ban back earlier in pregnancy is a sign of the rapidly lowering standards for American women.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re now told that 15 weeks is a compromise. But 15 weeks is not a compromise. It is the very beginning of the second trimester \u8211\'20\'13 before fetal abnormalities and other health risks are detected, before many women in red states, burdened by poverty and travel and the medically needless burdens imposed by their states, can get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at all. And there is no stage of pregnancy where a woman deserves the indignity of a ban. There is no point at which she becomes unworthy of controlling her own life and health; there is no point at which a legislator knows more about what\u8217\'20\'19s best for her than she does. Any ban is unacceptable; a national ban, like the kind that the Republicans are now pursuing, is abhorrent.\par \par \uc2 This was always their plan. The anti-choice movement, and their servants in the Republican party, have long understood the overturning of Roe v Wade \u8211\'20\'13 the long-desired goal that they achieved this summer, on 24 June, when the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  issued its decision in Dobbs v Jackson \u8211\'20\'13 as just the opening salvo in their assault on women\u8217\'20\'19s rights.\par \par \uc2 Their real goal is a national ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , beginning with the kind of legislation introduced this week by Graham. They have made no secret of this: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2022/05/02/abortion-ban-roe-supreme-court-mississippi/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anti-choice groups announced}}}\uc2  their plan for a national ban even before the Dobbs decision was officially released. They don\u8217\'20\'19t have the votes for it now, but they could get the votes in the future. And when they do, a combination of factors, including pressure from fundraisers and their base and what seems to be a genuine hatred for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the freedom that it provides to women, combine to make a political certainty: the next time Republicans hold both houses of \uc2 US Congress\uc2  and the White House, they will ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide.\par \par \uc2 It is time for liberal Americans, and all American women, to face this reality: there will soon be no safe states, no place in America where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal. In the future, we will come to see this horrible era \u8211\'20\'13 the time after Roe fell, but before \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was banned nationally \u8211\'20\'13 as an interregnum, when the suffering and loss enforced on women by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans was only confined to red states.\par \par \uc2 As horrible as this state of affairs is, one day we will look back on it fondly. As women bleed for days, and little girls are pushed out of school, and thousands of dreams are abandoned to forced birth \u8211\'20\'13 even these, eventually, might come to seem like the good old days.\par \par \uc2 Because though the Republicans will certainly ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationally at their first opportunity, they may not even need to wait for an electoral victory to do so. A group calling itself Catholics for Life has already asked the supreme court to declare fetuses and embryos to be persons under the 14th amendment, a move that would grant them constitutional rights. From there, \u8220\'20\'1Cit\u8217\'20\'19s a short step to saying that laws allowing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  are unconstitutional because they deny equal protection to those persons that are unborn human beings,\u8221\'20\'1D the Berkeley Law School dean, Erwin Chemerinsky, told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://msmagazine.com/2022/09/14/catholic-pro-life-supreme-court-abortion-ban-constitutional-rights-fetus-person-dobbs/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ms magazine}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI believe that there may be a majority on the Court to take that position.\u8221\'20\'1D The unelected, lifetime-appointed judges on the court could extend their assertion in Dobbs that it\u8217\'20\'19s legal to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and instead say that it\u8217\'20\'19s actually illegal to allow it. To get that outcome, the Republicans don\u8217\'20\'19t need to win even one more vote.\par \par \uc2 These are the stakes of every election now, for the rest of our lives. A national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban will be on the ballot every time Americans vote for congressmen and senators; it will be on the ballot every time they vote for president. In previous years, while Roe was still in place, voting for a governor or state legislatures could affect practical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access within a state quite substantially. Red states were able to cut funding, impose labyrinthine requirements, up the cost for patients and impose uniquely onerous burdens on providers. But Roe preserved a bare-bones floor for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights: no state could ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before viability.\par \par \uc2 Now, any state \u8211\'20\'13 or the United States at the federal level \u8211\'20\'13 can ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as early as they want. There is no bottom, and Republicans are determined to keep pushing further and further back, dragging the rights and dignity of American women further and further down into the dirt. This is the possibility that we have to resist every time we vote. It\u8217\'20\'19s also the possibility that Democrats accept \u8211\'20\'13 every day that they do not expand the court.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Moira Donegan is a Guardian US columnist\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220915ei9f001xi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
