\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: Near-total  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban takes effect in Indiana\b0\par\par\uc2 Nicola Slawson \par \uc2 1,515 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 September 2022\par 09:20 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Law in effect wipes out \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access for 1.5 million people in the state, which was a safe haven for those seeking the procedure. Plus, how house music changed the world\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/15/indiana-abortion-ban-trigger-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sweeping \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban went into effect in Indiana}}}\uc2  today, containing only extremely narrow exceptions for medical emergencies, rape and incest \u8211\'20\'13 making it the latest state to largely outlaw the procedure in the US.\par \par \uc2 The ban is being challenged in court by the \uc2 ACLU\uc2  and several \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care providers, with hearings set to start on 19 September.\par \par \uc2 Indiana lawmakers passed the legislation during a special legislative session in early August, with a six-week pause before it came into effect. Then, Indiana was the first state in the nation to bring in a new law banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after Roe fell.\par \par \uc2 The law in effect wipes out \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access for 1.5 million Indianans of reproductive age, and will have far-reaching consequences as Indiana had become a safe haven for those seeking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in other nearby states.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will always have more work to do because we need to make it unimaginable to end an unborn baby\u8217\'20\'19s life,\u8221\'20\'1D the Republican state senator Liz Brown said when she backed the bill six weeks ago.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What are the exceptions? The Indiana law \u8211\'20\'13 known as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://iga.in.gov/legislative/2022ss1/bills/senate/1#digest-heading"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SB 1}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 is an all-encompassing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban with some extreme restrictions. It limits abortions to cases where there is serious risk to the health or life of the pregnant person, and in the case of a lethal fetal anomaly up to 20 weeks post-fertilization.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18People disappeared\u8217\'20\'19: Izium\u8217\'20\'19s residents on Russia\u8217\'20\'19s occupation\par \par \uc2 The horror slowly unfolds from the burnt-out rubble in Izium, one of the most strategically vital towns for the Russians before {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/sep/10/ukrainian-forces-kupiansk-advances-north-east-russia-izyum"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 its recapture last weekend}}}\uc2  by Ukrainian forces.\par \par \uc2 Tank carcasses with Moscow\u8217\'20\'19s signature Z symbol are dotted along the crater-covered streets. Dozens of bombed-out apartment buildings in the city centre lie derelict along roads covered with the debris of what has been one of this war\u8217\'20\'19s most fierce battles, resulting in the deaths of at least 1,000 people, according to Ukrainian officials. On Wednesday, the city, described as a second Mariupol because of the heavy bombardments it has suffered, was visited by the outside world for the first time after its recapture.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is impossible to explain what we have been through if you have not lived it,\u8221\'20\'1D says Olga, 44. \u8220\'20\'1CWe lay down on the floor and remained inside our house, for so long that we learned to recognise bombs. If the Russian plane we heard from outside wasn\u8217\'20\'19t that loud, then we knew it was going to drop two bombs. If, on the other hand, the plane was very loud, it would drop six. We counted every single explosion before we could breathe a sigh of relief.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s happening now in the city? Regarded for centuries as the gateway to the Donbas region of eastern {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2  and, from there, to the Black Sea, today Izium is a giant crime scene where Ukrainian prosecutors are moving fast to gather evidence on war crimes allegedly perpetrated by the Russians.\par \par \uc2 R Kelly found guilty on child pornography and sex abuse charges\par \par \uc2 A federal jury has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/14/r-kelly-found-guilty-on-child-pornography-and-sex-abuse-charges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 convicted R Kelly of several child pornography and sex abuse charges}}}\uc2  in his home town of Chicago, delivering another legal blow to a singer who used to be one of the biggest R&B stars in the world.\par \par \uc2 Kelly, 55, was found guilty on three counts of child pornography and three counts of child enticement.\par \par \uc2 But the jury acquitted him on a fourth pornography count as well as a conspiracy to obstruct justice charge accusing him of fixing his state child pornography trial in 2008. He was found not guilty on all three counts of conspiring to receive child pornography and for two further enticement charges.\par \par \uc2 His two co-defendants were found not guilty on all charges.\par \par \uc2 The verdict comes months after a federal judge in New York sentenced Kelly to 30 years in prison in June for racketeering and sex trafficking. Based on that sentence, the 55-year-old won\u8217\'20\'19t be eligible for release until he is around 80.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Is this the last of the trials against him? No. Kelly\u8217\'20\'19s legal troubles continue. Two sexual misconduct trials still await him \u8212\'20\'14 one in Minnesota and one in state court in Chicago. Kelly maintains his innocence.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A Catholic nun from New Orleans who was kidnapped while working in western Africa, contracted malaria as she was held for nearly five months and was ultimately freed, said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/sep/15/kidnapped-new-orleans-nun-details-harrowing-ordeal-prayer-sustained-me"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reciting prayers helped her survive}}}\uc2  her ordeal. \u8220\'20\'1CPrayer sustained me,\u8221\'20\'1D Suellen Tennyson, 83 said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donors to a \uc2 GoFundMe\uc2  appeal have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/14/girl-who-killed-accused-rapist-must-pay-his-family-150000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raised enough money}}}\uc2  to pay the $150,000 restitution an Iowa court ruled a teenage human trafficking victim must pay to the family of her accused rapist, whom she stabbed to death. The judge in the case said he had \u8220\'20\'1Cno other option\u8221\'20\'1D but to impose restitution on Pieper Lewis, 17 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors have filed a motion to vacate the murder conviction of 42-year old\par \par \uc2 Adnan Syed\par \par \uc2 , a case that previously gained international attention after it was featured on the podcast Serial. Baltimore City state\u8217\'20\'19s attorney has requested the new trial after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/14/prosecutors-baltimore-murder-conviction-serial-adnan-syed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an investigation pointed to alternative suspects}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Lebanese and Syrians firefighters have joined forces to fight wildfires after more than 1,500 hectares (3,700 acres) were destroyed by fire last year. The volunteer firefighting service is bringing refugees and local people together to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2022/sep/15/volunteer-firefighters-lebanon-wildfires-akkar-province"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 save Akkar province\u8217\'20\'19s ancient woodlands}}}\uc2 , where some trees are more than a 100 years old.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s White House chief of staff secretly bought a book in which 27 mental health professionals warned that the president was psychologically unfit for the job, then used it as a guide in his attempts {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2022/sep/15/john-kelly-dangerous-case-donald-trump-peter-baker-susan-glasser-divider"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to cope with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s irrational behavior}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: Mourners wait in 3 mile\par \par \uc2 line to pay last respects to Queen Elizabeth II\par \par \uc2 In a country famous for perfecting the orderly queue, those lining up for a few seconds alongside the Queen\u8217\'20\'19s coffin proved no exception. By 5pm, when the first members of the public filed into Westminster Hall, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2022/sep/14/queen-elizabeth-ii-westminster-hall-london"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the line snaked back through the capital for about 3 miles (5km)}}}\uc2 , crossing the Thames and stretching all the way to London Bridge. After the long wait, it took little more than three minutes to file past the coffin. A few crossed themselves. Most bowed or curtsied. Some wiped away tears, but most were stoic. The queue outside continued to grow as night fell and will be open 24 hours a day until 6.30am on Monday, before the funeral later that day.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: How house music changed the world\par \par \uc2 When house first broke, nearly 40 years ago, the genre seemed to offer a temporary release, rather than longer-term liberation. Yet today it\u8217\'20\'19s clear that the music, which used affordable technology to rework disco, provided a much longer lasting voice to queer, Black and marginalised musicians, DJs and club goers, first in the big cities of the American midwest, then across the world. From Chicago to New York, Manchester, London, Tokyo, Paris and Berlin, house seeded local scenes and reshaped pop. As Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 and Drake take on the genre, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2022/sep/15/house-music-robin-s-marshall-jefferson-jesse-saunders"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 legends from Robin S to Jesse Saunders reflect on its resurgence}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Climate check: Healthy teenagers at risk of irregular heartbeats from air pollution, says study\par \par \uc2 Healthy teenagers are more prone to irregular heartbeats after breathing in fine particulate air pollution, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/sep/14/healthy-teenagers-risk-irregular-heartbeats-air-pollution-study"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the first major study}}}\uc2  of its impact on otherwise healthy young individuals. Doctors monitored heart activity and the air breathed by more than 300 healthy US teenagers over 24-hour periods. The findings have raised concern among researchers because heart arrhythmias, which can increase the risk of heart disease and sudden cardiac death, appear to be triggered even when air pollution is within common air quality limits.\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: \u8216\'20\'18Wobbly\u8217\'20\'19 moon probable cause of mass tree deaths in Australia, scientists say\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/sep/14/wobbly-moon-probable-cause-of-mass-tree-deaths-in-australia-scientists-say"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wobble in the moon\u8217\'20\'19s orbit}}}\uc2  around Earth affects mangrove cover across Australia and most likely contributed to mass tree deaths in the Gulf of Carpentaria, new research suggests. A study has found that an 18.61-year cycle known as the lunar nodal cycle shapes the condition of tidal wetlands. The moon\u8217\'20\'19s orbit around Earth does not occur in a flat plane. \u8220\'20\'1CSince the 1720s, people have known that it moves up and down by a few degrees,\u8221\'20\'1D said the study\u8217\'20\'19s author, Prof Neil Saintilan. He likened the motion to \u8220\'20\'1Cwhen you\u8217\'20\'19re spinning a coin \u8211\'20\'13 as it loses momentum, it kind of wobbles\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220915ei9f001bg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
