\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden touts efforts to boost electric vehicles at Detroit auto show \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein \par \uc2 5,247 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 September 2022\par 20:20 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President is in Detroit to promote the Inflation Reduction Act, which includes incentives for buying electric carsSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  struck a triumphant note in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/14/trump-special-master-jan-6-committee-next-hearing-biden-detroit-politics-latest?page=with:block-632221b68f0894b39b47f19f#block-632221b68f0894b39b47f19f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Detroit speech}}}\uc2  where he promoted his administration\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to revitalize manufacturing and get Americans behind the wheel of electric vehicles. Meanwhile, the January 6 committee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/14/trump-special-master-jan-6-committee-next-hearing-biden-detroit-politics-latest?page=with:block-6321d3c38f081d6324a73538#block-6321d3c38f081d6324a73538"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has signaled}}}\uc2  it will resume public hearings later this month, and potentially share more of its evidence with justice department investigators looking into the attack on the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 House Speaker Nancy Pelosi{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/14/trump-special-master-jan-6-committee-next-hearing-biden-detroit-politics-latest?page=with:block-63222a858f0892ec9e8ce005#block-63222a858f0892ec9e8ce005"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expressed optimism}}}\uc2  that Democrats would gain, not lose, seats in the chamber in the November midterms, despite widespread expectations that voters will elevate the Republicans into the majority.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  disavowed his former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , saying he would not choose him as a running mate again, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/14/trump-special-master-jan-6-committee-next-hearing-biden-detroit-politics-latest?page=with:block-6321f6e38f08d0ddb28304c2#block-6321f6e38f08d0ddb28304c2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a soon-to-be-published book obtained by The Guardian}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 FBI\uc2  agents{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/14/trump-special-master-jan-6-committee-next-hearing-biden-detroit-politics-latest?page=with:block-6321de768f08565ccb58e5a9#block-6321de768f08565ccb58e5a9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 paid a visit}}}\uc2  to prominent Trump ally and pillow mogul Mike Lindell, seizing his cellphone and questioning him in a fast food restaurant\u8217\'20\'19s drive-thru lane.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden called Britain\u8217\'20\'19s King Charles III and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/14/trump-special-master-jan-6-committee-next-hearing-biden-detroit-politics-latest?page=with:block-6321e1fb8f083917350c6afe#block-6321e1fb8f083917350c6afe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expressed condolences}}}\uc2  over the death of the queen. It remains unclear if the president will meet Charles III or new prime minister \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2  when he heads to London for the queen\u8217\'20\'19s funeral.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Republican senator \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  co-sponsored a bill to ban abortions nationwide after 15 weeks, in what could help his Democratic challenger Val Demings as she looks to energize pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment among voters.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Amtrak\uc2  has begun canceling long-distance routes ahead of a possible rail strike that could begin within days, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2022/09/14/amtrak-cancels-long-distance-trains-labor-dispute"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Axios reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Unions and freight rail companies are negotiating furiously to prevent the strike, which would be the first in three decades and worsen supply chains that have been plagued by delays and manpower and equipment shortages over the past two years as the United States has bounced back from the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile we are hopeful that parties will reach a resolution, \uc2 Amtrak\uc2  has now begun phased adjustments to our service in preparation for a possible freight rail service interruption later this week,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Amtrak\uc2  said, according to Axios.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSuch an interruption could significantly impact intercity passenger rail service, as \uc2 Amtrak\uc2  operates almost all of our 21,000 route miles outside the Northeast Corridor (NEC) on track owned, maintained, and dispatched by freight railroads. These initial adjustments include canceling all Long Distance trains and could be followed by impacts to most State-Supported routes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The negotiations between the railroad companies and 12 unions are complex and have drawn in the Biden administration. Here\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/health-covid-government-and-politics-87bc3c3e0120b8258557767576262d89?utm_source=homepage&utm_medium=TopNews&utm_campaign=position_4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the latest from the Associated Press}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Members of one union rejected a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/government-and-politics-497a373594515a27e7435cdf97df7a41"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tentative deal}}}\uc2  with the largest U.S. freight railroads Wednesday while three other unions remained at the bargaining table just days ahead of a strike deadline, threatening to intensify snarls in the nation\u8217\'20\'19s supply chain that have contributed to rising prices.\par \par \uc2 About 4,900 members of the International Association of Machinists and Aerospace Workers District 19 voted to reject the tentative agreement negotiated by \uc2 IAM\uc2  leadership with the railroads, the union said Wednesday. But the \uc2 IAM\uc2  agreed to delay any strike by its members until Sept. 29 to allow more time for negotiations and to allow other unions to vote.\par \par \uc2 Railroads are trying to reach an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/biden-technology-economy-congress-eb70df8309880dfea8cbe36aaae3fc47"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 agreement}}}\uc2  with all their other unions to avert a strike before Friday\u8217\'20\'19s deadline. The unions aren\u8217\'20\'19t allowed to strike before Friday under the federal law that governs railroad contract talks.\par \par \uc2 Government officials and a variety of businesses are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/norfolk-kansas-city-southern-government-and-politics-8773238e61d632b59ddbba22175d0df2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bracing}}}\uc2  for the possibility of a nationwide rail strike that would paralyze shipments of everything from crude and clothing to cars, a potential calamity for businesses that have struggled for more than two years due to COVID-19 related supply chain breakdowns.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s inclination for optimism was on full display in Detroit, but he was outdone today by his Democratic colleague House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , who insisted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://punchbowl.news/archive/91422-punchbowl-news-am/?utm_source=Sailthru&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=9/14/22%20%20Punchbowl%20News%20AM&utm_term=Punchbowl%20AM%20and%20Active%20Subscribers%20from%20Memberful%20Combined"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in an interview with Punchbowl News}}}\uc2  that the party was poised to gain \u8211\'20\'13 not lose \u8211\'20\'13 seats in the chamber in the midterms.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYes, indeed,\u8221\'20\'1D she told Punchbowl when they asked if she thought the party\u8217\'20\'19s majority would grow in the November 8 election.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s unpack the many reasons that statement appears improbably. First of all, it\u8217\'20\'19s a reflection of how much the political climate is thought to have shifted in the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 favor over the past few months. Declining gas prices, the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s overturning of national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and Biden\u8217\'20\'19s legislative wins are all believed to have energized Democratic voters, while on their part, Republicans have chosen some weaker nominees for key races.\par \par \uc2 But history is against Pelosi. As {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/09/biden-motivate-voters-maga-republicans-midterm-elections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Joan E Greve has reported}}}\uc2 , the party holding the White House has only gained seats in the House in two midterms, and Pelosi personally experienced the ruinous 2010 election that saw Democrats lose 63 seats in the lower chamber and end her speakership for eight years. She may well be poised to endure that again \u8211\'20\'13 poll aggregator FiveThirtyEight gives the GOP {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/2022-election-forecast/house/?cid=rrpromo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a very good shot}}}\uc2  at returning to the majority next year in the House, though the Senate may be harder to conquer. Nonetheless, analysts generally believe that the political developments over the past few months are meaningful for Democrats, and while Republicans may win the House, their gains won\u8217\'20\'19t be enormous, and certainly not comparable to 2010.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2  chairwoman \uc2 Ronna McDaniel\uc2  had to say about Biden\u8217\'20\'19s visit to Detroit, which she described as a stop on his \u8220\'20\'1Cfailure tour\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhether it\u8217\'20\'19s handing out tax credits for luxury electric vehicles or bailing out the wealthy\u8217\'20\'19s debts, Biden and Democrats are leaving hardworking Americans behind. Democrats will be driven out of office in November because they put their left-wing special interests ahead of Americans struggling to fill grocery carts and gas tanks.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica is back,\u8221\'20\'1D declared president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  at the Detroit Auto Show. Photograph: Mandel Ngan/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmerican manufacturing is back, Detroit is back, America is back,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden declared at the conclusion of his speech in Detroit, where he touted the benefits of legislation passed to repair infrastructure and promote electric vehicles.\par \par \uc2 The speech at the Detroit Auto Show hit familiar talking points for the president as he attempts to convince voters to re-elect Democrats in the upcoming midterm elections and preserve their majorities in Congress. Among these were his recent legislative successes, including the $1 trillion measure Democrats and some Republicans in Congress approved last year to overhaul the nation\u8217\'20\'19s infrastructure. In his speech, he announced that he had authorized funding from that law for 35 states to build electric vehicle charging stations.\par \par \uc2 Beyond being the center of the auto industry, Michigan is among the more crucial states to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s political fortunes. It\u8217\'20\'19s a perennial swing state that Biden narrowly won in the 2020 election, and its Democratic governor \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  will also be on the ballot in November as she stands for second term against Republican challenger Tudor Dixon.\par \par \uc2 Biden appeared at the show along with the governor, and spent much of his speech shouting out other Michigan Democrats, while closing on a note of triumph. \u8220\'20\'1CFolks, we\u8217\'20\'19re proving it\u8217\'20\'19s never, ever, ever a good bet to bet against the American people, never never, never. You just gotta remember who we are.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 In the ongoing legal wrangling over documents seized by the government from Mar-a-Lago, \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/richardluscombe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Richard Luscombe}}}\uc2  reports that the justice department is sounding the alarm over an order preventing them from reviewing the materials.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lawyers are causing \u8220\'20\'1Cirreparable harm\u8221\'20\'1D to the government and public by delaying the investigation into his hoarding of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/23/trump-classified-documents-records-mar-a-lago-fbi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 highly classified documents}}}\uc2  at his Florida mansion, the \uc2 US Department of Justice\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 The claim came in a strongly worded court filing urging a district judge, Aileen Cannon, to reconsider her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/05/donald-trump-special-master-fbi-mar-a-lago"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruling last week}}}\uc2  granting Trump\u8217\'20\'19s request for an independent \u8220\'20\'1Cspecial master\u8221\'20\'1D in the case.\par \par \uc2 The Department of Justice argued that the order stops it continuing its review of thousands of documents, some reportedly containing details of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/06/donald-trump-mar-a-lago-documents-nuclear-weapons-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 foreign power\u8217\'20\'19s nuclear secrets}}}\uc2 , seized during an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/08/trump-says-fbi-raided-his-mar-a-lago-home"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FBI search}}}\uc2  of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago resort in Palm Beach last month.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/14/trump-documents-justice-department-irreparable-harm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mar-a-Lago documents: Trump delaying tactics causing \u8216\'20\'18irreparable harm\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 DoJ}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Self-confessed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dmarge.com/joe-biden-classic-corvette"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Ccar guy\u8221\'20\'1D Joe Biden}}}\uc2  is about to take the podium at the Detroit motor show to tell Americans why they should be buying electric vehicles.\par \par \uc2 The president, who owns a vintage Corvette, has set what the White House calls \u8220\'20\'1Ca bold goal\u8221\'20\'1D for electric vehicles to make up 50% of all vehicles sold in the US by 2030.\par \par \uc2 Biden is in Detroit touting the Inflation Reduction Act, the marquee spending bill he signed last month that includes incentives for buying electric vehicles, as part of a larger strategy to lower America\u8217\'20\'19s carbon emissions.\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden\u8217\'20\'19s Inflation Reduction Act makes it easier and cheaper to purchase an electric or fuel-cell vehicle \u8211\'20\'13 new or used \u8211\'20\'13 through tax credits for consumers.\par \par \uc2 Learn more at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/KTCwt5Tmue"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/KTCwt5Tmue}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The White House (@WhiteHouse) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WhiteHouse/status/1569823239735492609?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 13, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 While we await Biden\u8217\'20\'19s words, here\u8217\'20\'19s the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/09/14/fact-sheet-president-bidens-economic-plan-drives-americas-electric-vehicle-manufacturing-boom/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 White House factsheet}}}\uc2 , which says that since Biden took office last year, companies have invested nearly $85bn in manufacturing electric vehicles, batteries, and EV chargers in the US.\par \par \uc2 The number of electric vehicles sold in that time has almost tripled, the handout claims.\par \par \uc2 But there are concerns that his plans to build a nationwide network of charging stations will leave behind disadvantaged and lower income areas and communities of color.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/aug/31/joe-biden-electric-cars-charging-stations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Is Biden\u8217\'20\'19s goal to build charging stations for electric cars leaving low-income areas behind?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Call it a magical mystery tour\u8230\'20\'26 migrants being {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/08/08/1116285340/new-york-migrant-bus-texas-abbott"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sent on buses from Texas to New York}}}\uc2  by the lone star state\u8217\'20\'19s governor Greg Abbott in protest at \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s immigration policies are being moved on to Florida.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s according to Fox 5 New York, which interviewed the city\u8217\'20\'19s commissioner of immigration \uc2 Manuel Castro\uc2  on its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fox5ny.com/news/nyc-helping-migrants-who-were-bused-from-texas-relocate-to-other-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Good Day New York show}}}\uc2  on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 enltrNew York City officials claim that many of the migrants who are being bused from Texas did not want to go to New York so they are helping them get to other states. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/KFbzJyMs4N"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/KFbzJyMs4N}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Fox5NY (@fox5ny) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/fox5ny/status/1570061105812180992?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Castro says many of those arriving from Texas don\u8217\'20\'19t want to be there, and have ties elsewhere:\par \par \uc2 Many want to go to places like Florida, where the largest community of Venezuelans live.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re helping them get to their actual final destination. We\u8217\'20\'19re doing our best.\par \par \uc2 The move probably isn\u8217\'20\'19t going to go down too well with Florida\u8217\'20\'19s hardline Republican governor and frequent Biden critic \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , who likes what he sees coming out of Texas and has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tallahassee.com/story/news/2022/08/26/ron-desantis-plan-relocate-undocumented-immigrants-florida-worries-advocates/7895029001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mulling his own plan to bus undocumented Cuban migrants }}}\uc2  from Florida to Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll states and all cities have a role to play here, not just New York and Chicago and other places,\u8221\'20\'1D Castro told Fox 5.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to nominate first woman US ambassador to Russia\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  plans to nominate career diplomat Lynne Tracy, who is currently serving in Armenia, as the next US ambassador to Russia, CNN says.\par \par \uc2 Tracy has experience of Moscow, having served there as deputy ambassador from 2014 to 2017. She would be the first woman in the role, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/09/14/politics/lynne-tracy-ambassador-russia-nomination/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the network said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Lynne Tracy. Photograph: Department of State handout/AP\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration hopes to get her in place swiftly to replace \uc2 John Sullivan\uc2 , who stepped down earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 But the timing of her arrival and official nomination will depend on Russia agreeing to accept her as ambassador at a time of huge tension between Washington and Moscow as the war in Ukraine continues.\par \par \uc2 Typically, the host country will approve the name of an ambassador pick before they are officially nominated through a process called agr\u233\'00\'E9ment. The US has already given Tracy\u8217\'20\'19s name to the Russians to begin that process, two sources told CNN.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 While we\u8217\'20\'19re on the subject of November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections, Martin Pengelly has this look at how Democrats got the matchup they wanted \u8211\'20\'13 an extremist, Trump-supporting election denier \u8211\'20\'13 as their Republican opponent for a New Hampshire Senate seat:\par \par \uc2 A far-right Republican who backs \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election fraud lie and has vowed to decertify results in 2024 will be the GOP candidate for \uc2 US Senate\uc2  in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-hampshire"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New Hampshire}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Don Bolduc, a retired special forces general {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/08/world/africa/donald-bolduc-ptsd.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who has said}}}\uc2  he suffered from PTSD and a traumatic brain injury, edged out Chuck Morse, the state senate president, to face the incumbent Democrat, \uc2 Maggie Hassan\uc2 , in November.\par \par \uc2 Don Bolduc. Photograph: Reba Saldanha/AP\par \par \uc2 Most if not all forecasters called the race for Bolduc before Morse conceded.\par \par \uc2 The primary was the last in a series that have seen Republicans select candidates aligned with Trump, causing some to fear damage to their chances of winning the Senate in November.\par \par \uc2 Bolduc, 61, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/meet-the-press/meetthepressblog/new-hampshire-republican-senate-hopefuls-trash-fbi-2020-election-resul-rcna43133"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 echoed Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lie}}}\uc2  about election fraud in his defeat by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . He has also questioned whether the \uc2 FBI\uc2  should be abolished following its search of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Florida estate, which turned up {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/14/trump-documents-justice-department-irreparable-harm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a cache of classified documents}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Though Bolduc has courted Trump, he has not won an endorsement. Trump did call Bolduc a \u8220\'20\'1Cstrong guy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Last October, Bolduc {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newyorker.com/news/q-and-a/the-republicans-running-to-support-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spoke to the New Yorker}}}\uc2 . He said he thought his \u8220\'20\'1Cvalues and principles as an American, and the constitution, which I served for 33-plus years in the military, was safe with President Trump\u8221\'20\'1D, and that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s appeal stemmed from the ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2022/aug/25/trump-reading-kushner-book-breaking-history"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 notoriously reading-averse}}}\uc2  ) former president\u8217\'20\'19s reading and understanding of the constitution.\par \par \uc2 He also said \u8220\'20\'1Cthere was a tremendous amount of fraud\u8221\'20\'1D in 2020, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CI very much believe it and I think it exists, and I think it happens and it\u8217\'20\'19s been happening for a long time in this country. When you try to steal the presidency, a lot of people are going to go, \u8216\'20\'18OK, wait a minute. What the hell\u8217\'20\'19s going on here?\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/14/republican-trump-don-bolduc-new-hampshire-senate-primary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican backer of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s big lie wins New Hampshire Senate primary}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Florida Republican \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  has emerged as a co-sponsor of \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s nationwide {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/13/republican-national-abortion-ban-lindsey-graham"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 15-week \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban bill}}}\uc2 , providing Democratic hopeful Val Demings new ammunition as she challenges for his Senate seat in November.\par \par \uc2 Rubio\u8217\'20\'19s campaign has not said why he\u8217\'20\'19s signed on to the controversial and extreme bill, which has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/09/13/grahams-abortion-ban-senate-gop-00056423"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 confused and angered many congressional Republicans}}}\uc2 . Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  says he\u8217\'20\'19s sure his members would prefer to leave the issue to the states.\par \par \uc2 Val Demings. Photograph: Marco Bello/Reuters\par \par \uc2 But Rubio\u8217\'20\'19s overall position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is clear. Talking to a Christian group in south Florida earlier this month, he said an unborn child\u8217\'20\'19s rights outweighed those of the mother and that, in an apparent contradiction to his position on the Graham bill, \u8220\'20\'1CThe state legislatures will decide [the] law.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI would rather be right and lose an election than [be] wrong,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.local10.com/vote-2022/2022/09/01/in-abortion-remarks-rubio-says-unborn-childs-rights-should-prevail-over-mothers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to ABC10 Miami}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He may get his wish, at least the losing the election part, if Demings has her way. The former Orlando police chief and US congresswoman is a vocal pro-choice advocate and has slammed Rubio\u8217\'20\'19s position.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s outrageous to mandate what a woman can and can\u8217\'20\'19t do with their bodies,\u8221\'20\'1D she says in a televised {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rBHoxrfONfo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 campaign message}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI know something about fighting crime, Senator Rubio. Rape is a crime. Incest is a crime. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Polling by RealClearPolitics gives Rubio, a former candidate for the Republican presidential nomination, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.realclearpolitics.com/epolls/2022/senate/fl/florida-senate-rubio-vs-demings-7382.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a narrow lead over Demings}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is set to proclaim his administration\u8217\'20\'19s efforts {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/14/trump-special-master-jan-6-committee-next-hearing-biden-detroit-politics-latest?page=with:block-6321f9a48f08d0ddb28304e7#block-6321f9a48f08d0ddb28304e7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to boost the electric car business}}}\uc2  with a speech at the Detroit Auto Show set for 1:45 pm eastern time. Meanwhile, the January 6 committee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/14/trump-special-master-jan-6-committee-next-hearing-biden-detroit-politics-latest?page=with:block-6321d3c38f081d6324a73538#block-6321d3c38f081d6324a73538"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has signaled}}}\uc2  it will resume public hearings later this month, and potentially share more of its evidence with justice department investigators looking into the attack on the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  disavowed his former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , saying he would not choose him as a running mate again, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/14/trump-special-master-jan-6-committee-next-hearing-biden-detroit-politics-latest?page=with:block-6321f6e38f08d0ddb28304c2#block-6321f6e38f08d0ddb28304c2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a soon-to-be-published book obtained by The Guardian}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 FBI\uc2  agents{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/14/trump-special-master-jan-6-committee-next-hearing-biden-detroit-politics-latest?page=with:block-6321de768f08565ccb58e5a9#block-6321de768f08565ccb58e5a9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 paid a visit}}}\uc2  to prominent Trump ally and pillow mogul Mike Lindell, seizing his cellphone and questioning him in a fast food restaurant\u8217\'20\'19s drive-thru lane.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden called Britain\u8217\'20\'19s King Charles III and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/14/trump-special-master-jan-6-committee-next-hearing-biden-detroit-politics-latest?page=with:block-6321e1fb8f083917350c6afe#block-6321e1fb8f083917350c6afe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expressed condolences}}}\uc2  over the death of the queen. It remains unclear if the president will meet Charles III or new prime minister \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2  when he heads to London for the queen\u8217\'20\'19s funeral.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s check in with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , who has arrived at the Detroit Auto Show.\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s set to deliver \u8220\'20\'1Cremarks highlighting the electric vehicle manufacturing boom in America" at 1:45 pm eastern time according to the White House, but is first getting a look at the latest models from America\u8217\'20\'19s automakers.\par \par \uc2 Biden is a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dmarge.com/joe-biden-classic-corvette"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vintage Chevrolet Corvette owner}}}\uc2 , and CNN caught him behind the wheel of the latest model:\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden at the Detroit Auto Show {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/54IMxuUnfO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/54IMxuUnfO}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kate Sullivan (@KateSullivanDC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KateSullivanDC/status/1570077709048455170?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Here he is checking out \uc2 Ford\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s new electric offerings:\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Mustang Mach-E.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C0 to 60 in three seconds,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C3.5, but who\u8217\'20\'19s counting?\u8221\'20\'1D Bill Ford replied. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/yctQP3c9LX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/yctQP3c9LX}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Josh Wingrove (@josh_wingrove) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/josh_wingrove/status/1570078959995613185?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Why does Biden care so much about electric cars? In part because the Inflation Reduction Act, as the marquee spending bill he signed last month is known, includes incentives to try to get more Americans to buy the vehicles, as part of a larger strategy to lower America\u8217\'20\'19s carbon emissions. The other reason is that Biden is a \u8220\'20\'1Ccar guy\u8221\'20\'1D, as he likes to describe himself.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/17/biden-climate-law-savings-rebate-electric-car-solar-panel-appliance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Electric cars to solar panels: tax breaks in Biden\u8217\'20\'19s climate law for Americans}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 A presidential run may be \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s best hope of getting back into the White House. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  reports that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has thoroughly disavowed his former vice president:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will not pick \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  as his running mate if he runs for the presidency again, according to an interview with the authors of a new book on his time in the White House.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt would be totally inappropriate,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump told Peter Baker and Susan Glasser. \u8220\'20\'1CMike committed political suicide\u8221\'20\'1D by refusing to reject electoral college votes in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 defeat by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , Trump said.\par \par \uc2 Baker, of the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 , and Glasser, of the New Yorker, are the husband-and-wife team behind The Divider: Trump in the White House, 2017-2021, which will be published next Tuesday. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  obtained a copy.\par \par \uc2 The authors interviewed Trump twice for their book, in April and November last year.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2022/sep/14/trump-pence-running-mate-2024-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump tells authors of \u8216\'20\'18The Divider\u8217\'20\'19 book he won\u8217\'20\'19t pick Pence for 2024 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 While many Republicans attempted to distance themselves from senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s proposal for national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions yesterday, former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , a longtime opponent of the procedure who is considering running for president in 2024, wholeheartedly embraced it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI welcome any and all efforts to advance the cause of life in state capitals or in the nation\u8217\'20\'19s capital,\u8221\'20\'1D Pence said in an interview {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.realclearpolitics.com/articles/2022/09/14/mike_pence_abortion_bans_more_important_than_short-term_politics_148191.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with RealClearPolitics}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I have every confidence that the next Republican president, whoever that may be, will stand for the right to life.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He also downplayed fears that after its decision to overturn Roe v Wade, the conservative-dominated supreme court could reverse rulings guaranteeing other rights, such as same-sex marriage. \u8220\'20\'1CI have enormous respect for Justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  but the majority on the Supreme Court in the Dobbs case made it clear that their decision was about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Pence said. Thomas was the author of an opinion that mulled revisiting cases the court had previously decided.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s proposal to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks nationwide was excoriated by Democrats and downplayed by Republicans after it was introduced yesterday.\par \par \uc2 But pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment isn\u8217\'20\'19t unanimous among Democrats in the chamber. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nationalreview.com/corner/manchin-absolutely-backs-20-week-abortion-limit-and-is-very-interested-in-15-week-bill/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 National Review reports}}}\uc2  that \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2 , the conservative Democratic senator representing West Virginia, reiterated his support for banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 20 weeks, noting he\u8217\'20\'19d voted for such a measure in the past. As for Graham\u8217\'20\'19s more stringent proposal, Manchin said he was \u8220\'20\'1Cvery interested\u8221\'20\'1D in it.\par \par \uc2 As long as Democrats control the Senate, Graham\u8217\'20\'19s measure probably won\u8217\'20\'19t even be put up for a vote. And even if Republicans did gain control, they\u8217\'20\'19d need to find 60 votes to overcome an inevitable filibuster from Democrats before the bill could pass.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Yesterday should have been a rough day for the Biden administration. It started off with the government releasing new inflation data that was worse than expected, and ended with a massive sell-off on Wall Street.\par \par \uc2 Both developments should have been potent fodder for Republicans aiming to convince voters that inflation was the fault of Biden and the Democrats ahead of the November midterms. Instead, much of yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s news cycle was dominated by Republican senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s proposal for federal restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which are controversial with many voters, including in the GOP.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/09/13/lindsey-graham-joe-biden-abortion-00056505"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico has published}}}\uc2  a rundown of the own goal scored by the senator and the unexpected reprieve it won for Democrats from the disquieting economic news:\par \par \uc2 So obvious was the apparent ill-timing of the bill\u8217\'20\'19s introduction that one White House aide said a Republican lobbyist friend joked that Graham appeared to be working for the Biden administration. Other aides suggested that the comments continued a Democratic winning streak that started mid-summer and began to imagine holding onto both houses of Congress.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDems might need to send gift baskets and champagne to Graham and other Republicans for their selfless act of service today,\u8221\'20\'1D another Democratic official told POLITICO.\par \par \uc2 The immediate response to Graham\u8217\'20\'19s legislation, which would not just establish a ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks of pregnancy but also allow states to keep and pass more restrictive laws, was a microcosm of the way \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  politics has wholly upended the midterm sprint.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not as if the images out of the White House were pristine. Live TV coverage of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech was bracketed by large red arrows signifying the stock market\u8217\'20\'19s downward trajectory. The more Biden talked about how the legislation would help the economy, the more the markets tumbled. By the closing bell, Wall Street had suffered its worst day since June 2020, with the Dow dropping more than 1,250 points.\par \par \uc2 But Democrats, who have been on the defensive for months over stubbornly high inflation, felt once again revitalized in trying to fend off GOP-led initiatives to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Virtually every Senate candidate quickly issued statements excoriating Graham\u8217\'20\'19s bill and asking their Republican opponents whether they would sign off on it.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden has said he will attend the funeral of Elizabeth II, but it remains unclear if he will meet with new prime minister \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2  or \uc2 King Charles III\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  did not shed much light on the matter today, \uc2 The Washington Post\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrAsked if Biden will be meeting with new \uc2 King Charles III\uc2  or new British prime minister \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2  while he's in London, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PressSec?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @PressSec}}}\uc2  says: "I don't have an update on who he's going to be meeting or anything like that." She notes this morning's call between the president and the king.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Matt Viser (@mviser) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mviser/status/1570055234550136832?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  called Britain\u8217\'20\'19s King Charles III today and offered his condolences on the death of Queen Elizabeth II, the White House announced.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the full readout from the Biden administration:\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joseph R. Biden\uc2 , Jr. spoke today with \uc2 King Charles III\uc2  to offer his condolences on the passing of Queen Elizabeth II. The President recalled fondly the Queen\u8217\'20\'19s kindness and hospitality, including when she hosted him and the First Lady at Windsor Castle last June. He also conveyed the great admiration of the American people for the Queen, whose dignity and constancy deepened the enduring friendship and special relationship between the United States and the United Kingdom. President Biden conveyed his wish to continue a close relationship with the King.\par \par \uc2 Elizabeth II passed away last week, and her coffin has just arrived in the Palace of Westminster in London to lie in state. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  is running a live blog with the latest events, which you can read below.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/live/2022/sep/14/king-charles-iii-prince-william-harry-accompany-queen-elizabeth-ii-coffin-casket-westminster-hall-lie-lying-in-state-live-updates-latest-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Queen Elizabeth\u8217\'20\'19s coffin arrives at Palace of Westminster to lie in state \u8211\'20\'13 latest updates}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Busy times for the feds, it seems. \uc2 FBI\uc2  agents reported to the drive-thru lane of a Minnesota Hardee\u8217\'20\'19s to question and seize the cellphone of Mike Lindell, a prominent Trump ally and 2020 election denier who is also known for his company MyPillow, which makes\u8230\'20\'26 pillows. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/richardluscombe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Richard Luscombe}}}\uc2  explains what they were looking for:\par \par \uc2 Mike Lindell, the pillow salesman who became an enthusiastic mouthpiece for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lie about a stolen election, has said he was forced to hand his phone to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/fbi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FBI}}}\uc2  agents who surrounded him at a fast-food drive-through.\par \par \uc2 The incident happened on Tuesday as Lindell, chief executive of My Pillow, was in line at a branch of Hardee\u8217\'20\'19s in Mankato, Minnesota, his home town, following a hunting trip.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCars pulled up in front of us, to the side of us, and behind us and I said those are either bad guys or the \uc2 FBI\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D the conspiracy theorist said on his internet show, the Lindell Report. \u8220\'20\'1CWell, it turns out they were the \uc2 FBI\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Lindell said the agents questioned him about Tina Peters, a fellow election denier {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cpr.org/2022/09/07/mesa-clerk-tina-peters-pleads-not-guilty-in-election-security-breach-case/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 facing criminal charges in Colorado}}}\uc2  for tampering with voting machinery as a county clerk, and who in June {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/29/colorado-primary-result-tina-peters-republican"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lost a Republican primary}}}\uc2  to become the state\u8217\'20\'19s top election official.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/14/my-pillow-ceo-mike-lindell-phone-fbi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 My Pillow CEO Mike Lindell has phone seized by FBI at fast-food outlet}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 In June, federal investigators issued a subpoena for surveillance footage from inside Mar-a-Lago and obtained a hard drive in response, according to a newly revealed portion of the warrant authorizing last month\u8217\'20\'19s search of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s resort by the \uc2 FBI\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The detail was redacted from the warrant released by a federal judge last month, but the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/donald-trump-mar-a-lago-subpoenas-government-and-politics-7996b97001d36fba1088c66599bb7f08"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Associated Press reports}}}\uc2  that the justice department asked for it to be released after Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers publicly revealed the subpoena\u8217\'20\'19s existence.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the AP about the possible significance of the subpoena for surveillance footage:\par \par \uc2 The newly visible portions of the \uc2 FBI\uc2  agent\u8217\'20\'19s affidavit show that the \uc2 FBI\uc2  on June 24 subpoenaed for the footage after a visit weeks earlier to Mar-a-Lago in which agents observed 50 to 55 boxes of records in the storage room at the property. \uc2 The Trump Organization\uc2  provided a hard drive on July 6 in response to the subpoena, the affidavit says.\par \par \uc2 The footage could be an important piece of the investigation, including as agents evaluate whether anyone has sought to obstruct the probe. The Justice Department has said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/mar-a-lago-government-and-politics-1fef158c3a66bfc0ba6224570753ba47"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 separate filing}}}\uc2  that it has \u8220\'20\'1Cdeveloped evidence that government records were likely concealed and removed from the Storage Room and that efforts were likely taken to obstruct the government\u8217\'20\'19s investigation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 The January 6 committee has accumulated reams of evidence and testimonies in its investigation into the attack on the Capitol, but one outstanding question has been what will happen to it all. Will the evidence be shared with federal prosecutors? What about the lawyers of people facing charges over the attack?\par \par \uc2 The lawmakers in the committee gathered behind closed doors yesterday for their first meeting in more than a month, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/09/13/jan-6-panel-testimony-transcripts-justice-department-00056459"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico has reported}}}\uc2  a few details about where they were on these questions. \u8220\'20\'1CI think now that the department of justice is being proactive in issuing subpoenas and other things, I think it\u8217\'20\'19s time for the committee to determine whether or not the information we\u8217\'20\'19ve gathered can be beneficial to their investigation,\u8221\'20\'1D the committee\u8217\'20\'19s chair \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Indeed, the justice department has recently issued a flurry of subpoenas to associates of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as part of its investigation into the attack on the Capitol, and the January 6 committee seems to be aware that some of what it has found in its own, separate investigation could be useful to them. However, that could also open the door for attorneys of people defending charges over the attack to get access to the committee\u8217\'20\'19s evidence as well.\par \par \uc2 Either way, expect to be hearing a lot more from the committee later this month. Thompson said the lawmakers are eyeing September 28 as the date to resume their hearings, according to Politico.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 January 6 committee eyes September hearing, sharing evidence with justice department\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. After weeks of quiet, congress members investigating the January 6 attack have reconvened with plans to hold a new public hearing later this month, and potentially share evidence with the justice department. That would set the stage for the insurrection at the Capitol to remain in the public eye in the lead up to the November midterms, where a slew of Trump-supporting Republicans are on the ballot.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is traveling to Michigan for an appearance promoting electric vehicles at the Detroit auto show.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Federal health officials including CDC director \uc2 Rochelle Walensky\uc2  will testify about the response to Monkeypox before the Senate health committee.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has ruled out picking his former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  as his running mate, a soon-to-be published book obtained by \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  reveals.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220914ei9e001xj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
