\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  proposes nationwide 15-week  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban\b0\par\par\uc2 Nicola Slawson \par \uc2 1,464 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 September 2022\par 10:51 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 White House says South Carolina senator\u8217\'20\'19s proposed bill \u8216\'20\'18wildly out of step with what Americans believe\u8217\'20\'19. Plus, how \uc2 YouTube\uc2  got swamped with creepy content for kidsDon\u8217\'20\'19t already get First Thing in your inbox? Sign up here\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  proposed legislation on Tuesday for a nationwide 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, a politically risky strategy as a backlash grows to the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  ruling earlier this summer overturning federal protections for the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Polling shows that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/fact-tank/2022/07/15/key-facts-about-the-abortion-debate-in-america/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 57% of Americans disapproved}}}\uc2  of the court\u8217\'20\'19s June {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reversal of the 1973 Roe v Wade ruling}}}\uc2  guaranteeing access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and 62% say the procedure should be legal in all or most cases.\par \par \uc2 The proposal by Graham, a hardline South Carolina Republican, will be called the \u8220\'20\'1CProtecting Pain-capable Unborn Children from Late-term Abortions Act\u8221\'20\'1D. It stands almost no chance of becoming law, but is seen by analysts as an attempt to frame the discussion around \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with fewer than 60 days until the midterms.\par \par \uc2 The White House and top Democrats promptly decried Graham\u8217\'20\'19s efforts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday, Senator Graham introduced a national ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  which would strip away women\u8217\'20\'19s rights in all 50 states. This bill is wildly out of step with what Americans believe,\u8221\'20\'1D White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Could Graham\u8217\'20\'19s legislation pass? Even if Republicans seize control of the Senate chamber in November, Graham\u8217\'20\'19s bill is unlikely to pass because the current Senate minority leader, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , has indicated he would be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/11/mitch-mcconnell-senate-republicans-could-not-pass-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unwilling to lift the filibuster}}}\uc2  - a procedure that requires a bill to win the support of 60 senators \u8211\'20\'13 for the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue.\par \par \uc2 Louisiana woman carrying skull-less fetus forced to travel to New York for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 A Louisiana woman who was carrying a skull-less fetus that would die within a short time after birth, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/14/louisiana-woman-skull-less-fetus-new-york-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 traveled about 1,400 miles to New York City to terminate her pregnancy}}}\uc2  after her local hospital denied her an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid uncertainty over the procedure\u8217\'20\'19s legality.\par \par \uc2 Davis\u8217\'20\'19s trek was necessary because Louisiana has outlawed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  with very few exceptions after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision in June to eliminate federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights that which were established by its 1973 Roe v Wade ruling. New York is among the states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains legal.\par \par \uc2 Nancy Davis, 36, told the Guardian that she was about 10 weeks pregnant in late July when an ultrasound at Woman\u8217\'20\'19s hospital in Baton Rouge \u8211\'20\'13 Louisiana\u8217\'20\'19s capital \u8211\'20\'13 showed that her fetus was missing the top of its skull, a rare but fatal condition known as acrania that kills babies within days \u8211\'20\'13 and sometimes minutes \u8211\'20\'13 of birth.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Doesn\u8217\'20\'19t Louisiana\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban contain a general exception for fetuses that cannot survive outside their mothers\u8217\'20\'19 wombs? Yes and the law\u8217\'20\'19s author \u8211\'20\'13 state senator Katrina Jackson \u8211\'20\'13 has insisted that Davis could have legally obtained an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  without having to go across the country.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 So why wasn\u8217\'20\'19t Davis allowed one? Acrania is not explicitly included in the list of conditions for exemption so officials at the hospital where Davis had her ultrasound refused to provide an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for her, apparently fearing that they could be exposed to prison time, fines and forfeiture of their licenses to practice if they performed the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Ken Starr\par \par \uc2 , who investigated\par \par \uc2 Bill Clinton\par \par \uc2 over\par \par \uc2 Monica Lewinsky\par \par \uc2 affair, dies at 76\par \par \uc2 Ken Starr\uc2 , the lawyer who relentlessly pursued \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2  over his affair with \uc2 Monica Lewinsky\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/13/ken-starr-dead-clinton-lewinsky"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has died at the age of 76}}}\uc2 , according to a statement issued by his family.\par \par \uc2 Starr was a prosecutor whose Whitewater investigation led to the impeachment of Clinton in 1998. He died yesterday, at Baylor St Luke\u8217\'20\'19s Medical Center in Houston, of complications from surgery, the statement said.\par \par \uc2 A Reagan judicial appointee and US solicitor general under George HW Bush, Starr presented many arguments before the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Starr also served as independent counsel, president and chancellor of \uc2 Baylor University\uc2  and dean of the Pepperdine Caruso School of Law, the family statement said, and described their loved one as having had \u8220\'20\'1Ca distinguished career in academia, the law and public service\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What had Starr done more recently? In January 2020, Starr served as a member of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s legal team in the then-president\u8217\'20\'19s first impeachment trial over dealings with Ukraine. Last year it was also reported that Starr had waged a \u8220\'20\'1Cscorched-earth\u8221\'20\'1D legal campaign to persuade federal prosecutors to drop a sex-trafficking case against the late sex offender and billionaire financier Jeffrey Epstein.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A teenage human trafficking victim who was initially charged with first-degree murder after she stabbed her accused rapist to death was sentenced yesterday in an Iowa court to five years of closely supervised probation. Pieper Lewis, 17, was also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/14/girl-who-killed-accused-rapist-must-pay-his-family-150000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ordered to pay $150,000 restitution to the man\u8217\'20\'19s family}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 British\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2022/sep/13/prince-andrew-epstein-sexual-abuse-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 authorities protected Prince Andrew}}}\par \par \uc2 from US prosecutors investigating his relationship with\par \par \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein\par \par \uc2 , according to a new book by a US attorney who led the investigation in New York. \uc2 Geoffrey Berman\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s claims may cause consternation in a royal family dealing with the death of the Queen.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 More than 50 winners of the world\u8217\'20\'19s most prestigious environmental prize are calling on the \uc2 UN\uc2  to reject a bid by Vietnam to join the international organization\u8217\'20\'19s human rights council (\uc2 UNHRC\uc2 )\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/sep/14/vietnam-climate-activists-united-nations-human-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 amid a crackdown on the country\u8217\'20\'19s climate activists}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ontario, California, was once at the center of the dairy industry. Now it\u8217\'20\'19s home to Amazon\u8217\'20\'19s largest warehouse and hundreds of others \u8211\'20\'13 with\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/13/ontario-california-amazon-warehouses"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dangerous consequences}}}\uc2 . More than 600 warehouses are clumped into Ontario\u8217\'20\'19s 50 square miles (129.5 sq km), feeding the country\u8217\'20\'19s ever-growing hunger for online shopping.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: My father\u8217\'20\'19s family kept slaves \u8211\'20\'13 and he defended it. Acknowledging it matters\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJust a little more than three of my lifetimes ago \u8211\'20\'13 I\u8217\'20\'19m 51 \u8211\'20\'13 my ancestors were holding people in bondage,\u8221\'20\'1D writes Maud Newton. \u8220\'20\'1C\u8216\'20\'18Those who don\u8217\'20\'19t know history are doomed to repeat it\u8217\'20\'19 was a frequent warning in the schoolrooms of my childhood, one typically given in connection with major events like the fall of Rome or the American revolution. But there is no more intimate connection to history than through our individual families. And with the rise of laws forbidding discussions of racist histories, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/sep/14/slavery-family-racist-history-ancestors-wrongdoing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sharing our own ancestors\u8217\'20\'19 shameful wrongdoings has never been more urgent}}}\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26 or this: I was angry about being left out of my father\u8217\'20\'19s will. Then I found peace in the woods\par \par \uc2 Moniek Kramer always wanted a little house in the countryside. At the age of 65, struggling with the fallout from her father\u8217\'20\'19s death, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2022/sep/12/a-new-start-after-60-i-was-angry-about-being-left-out-of-my-fathers-will-then-i-found-peace-in-the-woods#comments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 she finally got it}}}\uc2 . She had been reading an article about Henry David Thoreau, the 19th-century American philosopher whose book Walden is based on his experience of living in a woodland cabin. An advert caught her eye: \u8220\'20\'1C\u8216\'20\'18Are you looking for your own Walden hut?\u8221\'20\'1D The next day she was on a train out of Amsterdam, and an hour later the sellers met her at the station. She plundered her pension \u8211\'20\'13 and moved in.\par \par \uc2 Climate check: World heading into \u8216\'20\'18uncharted territory of destruction\u8217\'20\'19, says climate report\par \par \uc2 The world\u8217\'20\'19s chances of avoiding the worst ravages of climate breakdown are diminishing rapidly, as we enter \u8220\'20\'1Cuncharted territory of destruction\u8221\'20\'1D through our failure to cut greenhouse gas emissions and take the actions needed to stave off catastrophe, leading scientists have said. Despite intensifying warnings in recent years, governments and businesses have not been changing fast enough, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/sep/13/world-heading-into-uncharted-territory-of-destruction-says-climate-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the United in Science report published yesterday}}}\uc2 . We are in danger of provoking \u8220\'20\'1Ctipping points\u8221\'20\'1D in the climate system that will mean more rapid and in some cases irreversible shifts.\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: Unboxing, bad baby and evil Santa \u8211\'20\'13 how \uc2 YouTube\uc2  got swamped with creepy content for kids\par \par \uc2 In 2015, with kids\u8217\'20\'19 material ballooning on \uc2 YouTube\uc2 , the company introduced \uc2 YouTube\uc2  Kids, an app with bigger, bubblier buttons for smaller fingers and settings for parents including a built-in timer. The company unveiled it as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe first \uc2 Google\uc2  product built from the ground up with little ones in mind\u8221\'20\'1D. \uc2 YouTube\uc2  hoped that children would only watch on the app, not its main site. But that didn\u8217\'20\'19t happen. And soon, kids\u8217\'20\'19 content mutated and as the company tried to promote its wholesome content, it was blindsided by a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/sep/13/unboxing-bad-baby-evil-santa-youtube-swamped-creepy-kids-content"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strange beast born within its walls}}}\uc2 , charging hard in another direction.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220914ei9e001ea\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
