\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Democrats condemn \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s nationwide  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban proposal \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein in Washington \par \uc2 5,094 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 September 2022\par 20:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Senator\u8217\'20\'19s bill would outlaw procedure after 15 weeksSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Republican senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  caused quite the stir {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/13/republicans-abortion-ban-trump-special-master-graham-biden-latest?page=with:block-6320aba98f084fa8528cf211#block-6320aba98f084fa8528cf211"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by proposing}}}\uc2  a nationwide ban on abortions past the 15-week mark, which even {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/13/republicans-abortion-ban-trump-special-master-graham-biden-latest?page=with:block-6320c9778f08581537027df1#block-6320c9778f08581537027df1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 many fellow GOP lawmakers don\u8217\'20\'19t support}}}\uc2 , at least not right now. The legislation could mark the start of a campaign to seek federal restrictions on the procedure after the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade in June. Meanwhile, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/13/republicans-abortion-ban-trump-special-master-graham-biden-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-632084a08f0879cd6b7f1610#block-632084a08f0879cd6b7f1610"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new inflation data}}}\uc2  showed prices continuing to rise \u8211\'20\'13 albeit at a slower rate \u8211\'20\'13 across the economy, dampening hopes that the wave of cost increases had faded for good.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Senate Republican leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  was among those downplaying Graham\u8217\'20\'19s proposal, but the Kentucky lawmakers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/13/republicans-abortion-ban-trump-special-master-graham-biden-latest?page=with:block-6320d7608f084fa8528cf3d6#block-6320d7608f084fa8528cf3d6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has previously said}}}\uc2  the chamber could consider a federal ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the GOP wins a majority.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Criminal referrals from the January 6 committee to the justice department are \u8220\'20\'1Clikely\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/13/republicans-abortion-ban-trump-special-master-graham-biden-latest?page=with:block-63208aa18f08acdcb33f90b8#block-63208aa18f08acdcb33f90b8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a lawmaker on the panel said}}}\uc2 . More public hearings by the committee are also expected to be announced soon.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democrat and Republican lawmakers love trading stocks, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/13/republicans-abortion-ban-trump-special-master-graham-biden-latest?page=with:block-6320941d8f0879cd6b7f16ef#block-6320941d8f0879cd6b7f16ef"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to an analysis from The New York Times}}}\uc2  that will likely add pressure on party leaders to ban congress members from owning or trading securities.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A jury in Connecticut is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/13/republicans-abortion-ban-trump-special-master-graham-biden-latest?page=with:block-6320a4d18f0818891db88bdb#block-6320a4d18f0818891db88bdb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 considering how much to order}}}\uc2  conspiracy theorist Alex Jones to pay relatives of the victims of the Sandy Hook massacre for spreading lies that the killings were a hoax.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s proposal to outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks isn\u8217\'20\'19t just unpopular with many of his fellow Senate Republicans - it would also appear to be unpopular with the \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  of just a month ago, who said the question of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access should be left up to the states.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a reminder from The Recount of what Graham had to say about the issue just this past August:\par \par \uc2 enltrSen. \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  (R-SC) in August: States should regulate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Sen. \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  in September: The federal government should regulate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/VvMDZd9fsp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/VvMDZd9fsp}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1569726692402364417?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 13, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 The discomfort over the Republican \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban proposal extends beyond the Senate to the campaign trail, where several of the party\u8217\'20\'19s nominees to the chamber are trying to distance themselves from it.\par \par \uc2 Tiffany Smiley, the GOP Senate nominee in Washington state, says she wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t get behind such a bill, Politico reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrA spokesperson for WA GOP nominee Tiffany Smiley also said she doesn't support the Graham bill and that it should be left up to the states to decide their \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Marianne LeVine (@marianne_levine) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/marianne_levine/status/1569770620858298368?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 13, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Joe O\u8217\'20\'19Dea, a Republican vying for Colorado\u8217\'20\'19s Senate seat, also opposed it, according to Politico. However \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , who\u8217\'20\'19s in a tight race for the senate seat occupied by Georgia Democrat Raphael Warnock, appeared to support it:\par \par \uc2 enltrHerschel Walker: "I believe the issue should be decided at the state level, but I WOULD support this policy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Joe O'Dea of Colorado: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t support Senator Graham\u8217\'20\'19s bill. A Republican ban is as reckless and tone deaf as is \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s hostility to" compromise\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Burgess Everett (@burgessev) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/burgessev/status/1569744633663463424?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 13, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senate Republican leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  may have downplayed the idea of a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban today, but don\u8217\'20\'19t be surprised if he one day changes his mind.\par \par \uc2 Consider {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/2022/05/06/gop-avoids-abortion-ahead-potential-scotus-ruling-overturn-roe/9631996002/?gnt-cfr=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his comments to USA Today}}}\uc2  in May, after a draft opinion leaked showing the supreme court was poised to overturn Roe v Wade, but before they officially did so later the following month.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf the leaked opinion became the final opinion, legislative bodies \u8211\'20\'13 not only at the state level, but at the federal level \u8211\'20\'13 certainly could legislate in that area,\u8221\'20\'1D the Kentucky lawmaker said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd if this were the final decision, that was the point that it should be resolved one way or another in the legislative process. So yeah, it\u8217\'20\'19s possible. It would depend on where the votes were.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That means Graham\u8217\'20\'19s proposal, or one like it, could be put up for a vote if Republicans reclaim control of the Senate \u8211\'20\'13 which they\u8217\'20\'19ll have a chance of doing in the November midterms.\par \par \uc2 However, Democrats could use the filibuster to block any such legislation, and even the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s most optimistic forecasts don\u8217\'20\'19t have the party winning the 60 seats needed to overcome that. In the USA Today interview, McConnell also made clear he was not in favor of changing the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s rules to make legislation easier to pass. \u8220\'20\'1CNo carve out of the filibuster \u8211\'20\'13 period. For any subject,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats, meanwhile, are trying to make the most of Graham\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban proposal as they make their case to maintain control of Congress.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s top Senate Democrat \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  at a press conference today:\par \par \uc2 enltrSenate Majority Leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  (D-NY) slams Sen. \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 's (R-SC) proposed 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban:\par \par \uc2 "What Senator Graham is introducing is a MAGA Republican nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. If it walks like a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and talks like a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban..." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/CofXO5SUB4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/CofXO5SUB4}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1569756979928698882?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 13, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 So much for that. Republican Senate leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  has poured cold water on the party making any concerted effort to get a vote on \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s proposed 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what CNN reports that McConnell, who would become Senate majority leader if the GOP wins a majority in the upper chamber in the midterm elections, had to say about the idea:\par \par \uc2 enltrMcConnell on Graham\u8217\'20\'19s bill: \u8220\'20\'1Cyou\u8217\'20\'19ll have to ask him about it.\u8221\'20\'1D Says most Republicans want to leave it to the states\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Burgess Everett (@burgessev) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/burgessev/status/1569756408270258176?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 13, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 A more immediate obstacle for Graham is the Democratic majorities in both the House and Senate, which are sure to oppose his bill.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Politico has more on the cool reception \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban has received in the Senate, particularly among his fellow Republicans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat wasn\u8217\'20\'19t a conference decision. It was an individual senator\u8217\'20\'19s decision,\u8221\'20\'1D Texas\u8217\'20\'19s Republican senator \uc2 John Cornyn{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/09/13/grahams-abortion-ban-senate-gop-00056423"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in the piece}}}\uc2 , echoing the sentiment of several lawmakers from Republican-dominated states that are moving to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but wary of pursuing such bans nationwide.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy state, today, is working on this. I\u8217\'20\'19m not sure what he\u8217\'20\'19s thinking here. But I don\u8217\'20\'19t think there will be a rallying around that concept,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Shelley Moore Capito\uc2 , a Republican senator from West Virginia, said.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, Democrats have seized on the proposal to attack Republicans. The Democratic Party of Virginia {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://vademocrats.org/news/while-jen-kiggans-claims-its-not-her-job-to-focus-on-abortion-in-congress-republicans-introduce-national-abortion-banin-congress/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 put out a statement}}}\uc2  accusing Jen Kiggans, a state senator vying for a US House seat against Democratic incumbent \uc2 Elaine Luria\uc2 , of changing her stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe reason why Jen Kiggans is trying to walk back her stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is that she knows her extreme anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  agenda is out of touch with Coastal Virginians and will cost her the election,\u8221\'20\'1D the Democrats wrote.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 The full text of the 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban proposed by Republican senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  can be read {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.lgraham.senate.gov/public/_cache/files/3065785d-86b8-4d36-986a-72aa1c8f100c/protecting-pain-capable-unborn-children-from-late-term-abortions-act-.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 , and contains an important detail about exactly what would be outlawed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe term \u8216\'20\'18perform\u8217\'20\'19, with respect to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , includes inducing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  through a medical or chemical intervention, including writing a prescription for a drug or device intended to result in an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D according to the text of the bill.\par \par \uc2 That likely means it would outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills that are seen as one of the best options for women to receive care in states where the procedure has been outlawed or restricted.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/07/us-mail-order-abortions-oklahoma"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mail-order \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pills become next US reproductive rights battleground}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Republican proposal to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks is only hours old, but it\u8217\'20\'19s already become an issue on the campaign trail in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 According to Insider, \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 , the Democratic nominee to represent the state in the Senate, has used the proposal to attack his Republican opponent, Mehmet Oz.\par \par \uc2 enltrFetterman already using the Graham bill against Oz {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/gBkSslVOI4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/gBkSslVOI4}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 bryan metzger (@metzgov) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/metzgov/status/1569735635803701248?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 13, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Republican senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/13/republicans-abortion-ban-trump-special-master-graham-biden-latest#top-of-blog"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposed legislation}}}\uc2  to ban abortions nationally after 15 weeks, in what is likely the start of a campaign to seek federal restrictions on the procedure after the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade in June. Meanwhile, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/13/republicans-abortion-ban-trump-special-master-graham-biden-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-632084a08f0879cd6b7f1610#block-632084a08f0879cd6b7f1610"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new inflation data}}}\uc2  showed prices continuing to rise \u8211\'20\'13 albeit at a slower rate \u8211\'20\'13 across the economy, dampening hopes that the wave of cost increases had faded for good.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Criminal referrals from the January 6 committee to the justice department are \u8220\'20\'1Clikely\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/13/republicans-abortion-ban-trump-special-master-graham-biden-latest?page=with:block-63208aa18f08acdcb33f90b8#block-63208aa18f08acdcb33f90b8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a lawmaker on the panel said}}}\uc2 . More public hearings by the committee are also expected to be announced soon.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democrat and Republican lawmakers love trading stocks, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/13/republicans-abortion-ban-trump-special-master-graham-biden-latest?page=with:block-6320941d8f0879cd6b7f16ef#block-6320941d8f0879cd6b7f16ef"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to an analysis from The New York Times}}}\uc2  that will likely add pressure on party leaders to ban congress members from owning or trading securities.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A jury in Connecticut is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/13/republicans-abortion-ban-trump-special-master-graham-biden-latest?page=with:block-6320a4d18f0818891db88bdb#block-6320a4d18f0818891db88bdb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 considering how much to order}}}\uc2  conspiracy theorist Alex Jones to pay relatives of the victims of the Sandy Hook massacre for spreading lies that the killings were a hoax.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Further cracks have appeared in Graham\u8217\'20\'19s insistence that his proposed 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban has wide political support.\par \par \uc2 CNN reports that not all Senate Republicans are onboard with the measure:\par \par \uc2 enltrSenate GOP not on same page on Graham\u8217\'20\'19s 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Thune supports it. \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2  said he\u8217\'20\'19d \u8220\'20\'1Clook at it.\u8221\'20\'1D Cornyn and Ron Johnson said it should be left to the states. Asked if he backs Graham bill, Johnson said it should be decided by \u8220\'20\'1Cwe the people\u8221\'20\'1D in the 50 states.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1569729902928166915?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 13, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think there will be a couple of Democrats who will be with us, maybe, hope, pray,\u8221\'20\'1D Republican senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  replied when asked about whether his proposed nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban after 15 weeks will win enough votes to pass the closely divided Congress.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think the public\u8217\'20\'19s with us,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s unclear whether any Democratic votes would materialize for the proposal, but that party controls the House and Senate, and it\u8217\'20\'19s unlikely they\u8217\'20\'19ll even let the measure come up for a vote as long as that\u8217\'20\'19s the case.\par \par \uc2 As for public support for Graham\u8217\'20\'19s proposal, a recent poll doesn\u8217\'20\'19t bear that out. Earlier this month, a poll by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/support-for-legalized-abortion-grows-since-dobbs-ruling-wsj-poll-shows-11662210020"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Wall Street Journal found}}}\uc2  57% of respondents opposed an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban at 15 weeks with exceptions for the health of a mother \u8211\'20\'13 exactly the kind of measure Graham proposed.\par \par \uc2 In fact, the survey found voter support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  increasing overall since the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade in June. While in March, 55% of voters said the procedure should be legal in all or most cases, that had risen to 60% in the phone survey conducted in mid-August.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democratic leaders condemn proposed nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par \uc2 Top Democrats have decried a nationwide ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks proposed today by Republican senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday, Senator Graham introduced a national ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  which would strip away women\u8217\'20\'19s rights in all 50 states. This bill is wildly out of step with what Americans believe,\u8221\'20\'1D White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/09/13/statement-by-press-secretary-karine-jean-pierre-on-proposed-national-abortion-ban/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in a statement}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile President Biden and Vice President Harris are focused on the historic passage of the Inflation Reduction Act to reduce the cost of prescription drugs, health care, and energy \u8211\'20\'13 and to take unprecedented action to address climate change \u8211\'20\'13 Republicans in Congress are focused on taking rights away from millions of women,\u8221\'20\'1D Jean-Pierre continued, adding that the Biden administration and Democrats in Congress \u8220\'20\'1Care committed to restoring the protections of Roe v. Wade.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democratic house speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  joined in, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CThe nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban proposal put forth today is the latest, clearest signal of extreme MAGA Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 intent to criminalize women\u8217\'20\'19s health freedom in all 50 states and arrest doctors for providing basic care. Make no mistake: if Republicans get the chance, they will work to pass laws even more draconian than this bill \u8211\'20\'13 just like the bans they have enacted in states like Texas, Mississippi and Oklahoma.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  has unveiled his proposed nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, which would outlaw the procedure after 15 weeks, with certain exceptions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think we should have a law on the books that says after 15 weeks, no \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on demand except in cases of rape, incest, to save the life of the mother, and that should be where America\u8217\'20\'19s at,\u8221\'20\'1D Graham said as he unveiled the legislation in the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 Graham said the proposal, dubbed the \u8220\'20\'1CProtecting Pain-Capable Unborn Children from Late-Term Abortions Act\u8221\'20\'1D, would match similar laws in European countries. He said the 15-week threshold is when fetuses will feel pain, however that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t quite match the science. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/06/health/late-term-abortion-trump.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Many scientists say}}}\uc2  fetuses can\u8217\'20\'19t feel pain before 24 weeks, although the subject is complicated and continuing to be researched.\par \par \uc2 Graham acknowledged the political realities of his proposal. \u8220\'20\'1CIf the Democrats are in charge, I don\u8217\'20\'19t know if we\u8217\'20\'19ll ever have a vote on our bill.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As The \uc2 Guardian\uc2  has reported previously, late-term abortions are very rare in the United States.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/news/datablog/2019/mar/07/abortion-late-term-what-pregnancy-stage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The truth about late-term abortions in the US: they\u8217\'20\'19re very rare}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  will soon introduce his legislation to ban abortions nationally. While it has no chance in the Senate as long as Democrats are in control, it will likely attract considerable support from Republican lawmakers, and could mark the start of the party\u8217\'20\'19s effort to restrict the procedure nationwide thanks to the supreme court ruling overturning Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  reports that Graham has said the ban will apply after 15 weeks of pregnancy \u8211\'20\'13 five weeks less than in previous versions of the legislation the South Carolina lawmaker has introduced:\par \par \uc2 enltrBreaking: Graham just told Fox News that his "late-term \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  act" is indeed a 15-week ban.\par \par \uc2 This is pretty extraordinary language to be using for 15 weeks. When antiabortion groups use "late term abortions" (not a medical phrase), it's usually understood to mean 21-24 weeks +\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Caroline Kitchener (@CAKitchener) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CAKitchener/status/1569714687327244288?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 13, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 You can watch the senator\u8217\'20\'19s press conference {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.c-span.org/video/?522830-1/senator-graham-holds-news-conference-abortion-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 A Connecticut jury began hearing arguments Tuesday in a trial to decide how much money conspiracy theorist and right-winger Alex Jones should pay relatives of victims of the Sandy Hook tragedy, for spreading a lie that the massacre was a hoax, \uc2 The Associated Press\uc2  reports.\par \par \uc2 Alex Jones talks to media during break in his trial in Texas in July.\par \par \uc2 Photograph: Briana Sanchez/AP\par \par \uc2 A settlement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/05/alex-jones-punitive-damages-sandy-hook-family"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was ordered}}}\uc2  at trial against Jones last month in a civil case in Texas brought by parents of a child killed in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/newtown-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2012 Sandy Hook school shooting}}}\uc2  with the current case in Connecticut pending.\par \par \uc2 Critics have said many things of Jones and his platform Infowars, among them the \uc2 Southern Poverty Law Center\uc2 , which tracks hate and extremist groups in the US, whose spokesman {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/aug/08/he-has-done-more-to-further-the-cause-of-hate-in-the-us-than-almost-anyone-the-rise-and-fall-of-alex-jones"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in August}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CHe has probably done more to further the cause of hate in this country than almost anyone outside of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  himself.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The AP writes today of this trial in Waterbury, Connecticut, not far from Sandy Hook:\par \par \uc2 More than a dozen family members, including parents of some victims, filed into the courtroom to listen to the opening statements and first day of evidence.\par \par \uc2 A jury of three men and three women along with several alternates will decide how much the conspiracy theorist should pay relatives of eight victims and an \uc2 FBI\uc2  agent who responded to the school.\par \par \uc2 Judge Barbara Bellis found Jones liable without a trial last year after he failed to turn over documents to the families\u8217\'20\'19 lawyers.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, she sanctioned Jones for failing to turn over analytic data related to his website and the popularity of his show.\par \par \uc2 She told his lawyers that because of that failure, they will not be allowed to argue he didn\u8217\'20\'19t profit from his Sandy Hook remarks.\par \par \uc2 Jones did not attend the opening of the trial Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 He said on his show Monday that he would be traveling to Connecticut next week.\par \par \uc2 The trial is expected to last about a month and feature testimony from both Jones and the families.\par \par \uc2 Alex Jones faces second defamation trial over Sandy Hook claims. In Connecticut, family members of victims of the Sandy Hook Elementary School shooting arrive at the court house today. Photograph: Michelle McLoughlin/Reuters\par \par \uc2 More of the Guardian piece that contains that \uc2 SPLC\uc2  quote, above, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/aug/08/he-has-done-more-to-further-the-cause-of-hate-in-the-us-than-almost-anyone-the-rise-and-fall-of-alex-jones"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/aug/08/he-has-done-more-to-further-the-cause-of-hate-in-the-us-than-almost-anyone-the-rise-and-fall-of-alex-jones"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18He has done more to further the cause of hate in the US than almost anyone\u8217\'20\'19: the rise and fall of Alex Jones}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Indiana to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday\par \par \uc2 As the news cycle today has focused on senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s proposals for a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban from 15 weeks, its worth remembering that Republican-controlled Indiana will bring in its almost total ban {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abc7chicago.com/is-abortion-legal-in-indiana-law-2022-laws-ban/12226533/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on Thursday}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As ABC {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abc7chicago.com/is-abortion-legal-in-indiana-law-2022-laws-ban/12226533/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 , there is a challenge to the extreme law in the state\u8217\'20\'19s courts, but that won\u8217\'20\'19t be heard until next week \u8211\'20\'13 after it comes into effect.\par \par \uc2 ABC says: An Indiana judge won\u8217\'20\'19t hear arguments until next week on a lawsuit seeking to block the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, leaving that new law set to take effect on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The special judge overseeing the case issued an order Monday setting a court hearing for Sept. 19, which is four days after the ban\u8217\'20\'19s effective date.\par \par \uc2 Indiana\u8217\'20\'19s Republican-dominated Legislature approved the tighter \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions during a two-week special legislative session that ended Aug. 5, making it the first state to do so since the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  eliminated federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections by overturning Roe v. Wade in June.\par \par \uc2 Indiana \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic operators filed the lawsuit Aug. 31, saying the ban, which includes limited exceptions, \u8220\'20\'1Cstrips away the fundamental rights of people seeking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care\u8221\'20\'1D in violation of the Indiana Constitution.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 The stock trading activities of lawmakers have become increasingly controversial this year.\par \par \uc2 House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  has come under scrutiny for the trading activities of her husband, Paul Pelosi, a venture capitalist {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/house/3579634-mccarthy-swipes-at-pelosi-over-ban-on-lawmaker-stock-trading/https://thehill.com/homenews/house/3579634-mccarthy-swipes-at-pelosi-over-ban-on-lawmaker-stock-trading/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 whose stock transactions Republicans have}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/house/3579634-mccarthy-swipes-at-pelosi-over-ban-on-lawmaker-stock-trading/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  raised their eyebrows at}}}\uc2 . However, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2022/09/13/us/politics/congress-members-stock-trading-list.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as The New York Times investigation}}}\uc2  released today makes clear, Pelosi is far from the only lawmaker whose family members engage in trading.\par \par \uc2 There seems to be an awareness in some corners of Congress that these trades are too problematic to continue. In February, a bipartisan group of senators and House representatives {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jayapal.house.gov/2022/02/09/jayapal-rosendale-warren-daines-introduce-new-bipartisan-bill-to-ban-members-of-congress-from-owning-and-trading-stocks/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 introduced legislation}}}\uc2  to ban owning and trading stocks. Punchbowl News {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://punchbowl.news/archive/7-28-22-punchbowl-news-am/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported in July}}}\uc2  that House Democrats would propose their own ban on trading in August.\par \par \uc2 That month has come and gone with no proposal made public, but lawmakers are now back in Washington, meaning that could change in the coming weeks.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/feb/22/us-politicians-trading-stocks-bipartisan-idea"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Money unites: Republicans and Democrats find rare bipartisanship over trading stocks}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Be they Democrat or Republican, House or Senate, a \uc2 New York Times\uc2  investigation published today has found dozens of Congress members trading stocks in companies that their committees are involved with.\par \par \uc2 Here are a few examples, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2022/09/13/us/politics/congress-stock-trading-investigation.html?partner=slack&smid=sl-share"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from the Times\u8217\'20\'19 report}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Senator Tommy Tuberville, Republican of Alabama and a member of the agriculture committee, regularly reported buying and selling contracts tied to cattle prices starting last year, even as the panel, by Mr. Tuberville\u8217\'20\'19s own account, had \u8220\'20\'1Cbeen talking about the cattle markets.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Representative Bob Gibbs, an Ohio Republican on the House Oversight Committee, reported buying shares of the pharmaceutical company \uc2 AbbVie\uc2  in 2020 and 2021, while the committee was investigating \uc2 AbbVie\uc2  and five rivals over high drug prices.\par \par \uc2 The timing of one trade by the wife of Representative Alan Lowenthal, Democrat of California, was especially striking: His disclosure statement said she had sold \uc2 Boeing\uc2  shares on March 5, 2020 \u8212\'20\'14 one day before a House committee on which he sits released {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://transportation.house.gov/news/press-releases/nearly-one-year-after-launching-its-boeing-737-max-investigation-house-transportation-committee-issues-preliminary-investigative-findings-"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 damaging findings}}}\uc2  on the company\u8217\'20\'19s handling of its 737 Max jet, which was involved in two fatal crashes.\par \par \uc2 All told, 97 lawmakers or their family members traded securities in companies that were affected by their congressional work, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2022/09/13/us/politics/congress-members-stock-trading-list.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Times\u8217\'20\'19 investigation found}}}\uc2 , in what will surely add to calls to ban lawmakers from trading stocks, bonds and other investments.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 An advocacy group linked to the Biden administration has joined in on attacking Republicans for their upcoming proposal to ban abortions nationwide after 15 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRepublicans in Congress have shown yet again that they will impose a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban if given the opportunity,\u8221\'20\'1D Danielle Melfi, executive director of Building Back Together, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis bill underscores just how out of touch they are with the vast majority of the American people, who overwhelmingly oppose proposals to take away our rights and freedoms. While today President Biden will highlight the Inflation Reduction Act and his work to lower costs for working families, Republicans in Congress are continuing their fight to take personal freedoms away from millions of Americans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe decision to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a deeply personal one that should only ever be between a woman and her doctor \u8212\'20\'14 not politicians. It\u8217\'20\'19s essential that we have more allies in Congress who will stand up for the right of all people to make decisions about their own health for themselves.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 , the Republican senator backing the legislation, will unveil it at a 12 noon eastern time event with anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Speaking of the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s January 6 investigation, Reuters yesterday reported new details of the inquiry into the attack on the Capitol, which appears to be widening:\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Justice Department\uc2  has issued about 40 subpoenas over the past week seeking information about efforts by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his allies to overturn the 2020 election, the \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/09/12/us/politics/trump-aides-jan-6-doj.html?partner=slack&smid=sl-share"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Boris Epshteyn, a longtime Trump adviser, and Mike Roman, a campaign strategist for Trump, had their phones seized last week as evidence, the Times said, citing people familiar with the situation.\par \par \uc2 Dan Scavino, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former social media director, was also among those who were subpoenaed, according to the paper, which said the group included low-level aides as well as senior advisers.\par \par \uc2 An attorney for Scavino did not immediately respond to a request for comment from Reuters, while Reuters was unable to contact Roman and Epshteyn.\par \par \uc2 The subpoenas seek information on a failed bid by the former president and his allies to overturn the results of the 2020 election by submitting alternative slates of fake electors.\par \par \uc2 The inquiry is also looking at the assault on the US Capitol on 6 January 2021 by Trump supporters.\par \par \uc2 Some of the subpoenas also seek information on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Save America political fundraising group, which the Times said was a new line of inquiry by the justice department.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/12/us-subpoenas-donald-trump-2020-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US issues 40 subpoenas about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s failed bid to overturn the 2020 election}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 January 6 committee member says criminal referral 'likely' over attack\par \par \uc2 A criminal referral from the January 6 committee to the justice department is \u8220\'20\'1Clikely", \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2 , one of the committee\u8217\'20\'19s two Republican members, said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen it comes to criminality, that\u8217\'20\'19s not our role,\u8221\'20\'1D Kinzinger said in an interview on MSNBC, describing the justice department as in the midst of a \u8220\'20\'1Cpretty fulsome investigation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd that\u8217\'20\'19s going to be where this baton, so to speak, is handed to. Not by us, we may have a criminal referral, I think that\u8217\'20\'19s likely, but with their investigation from here on out.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrRep. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AdamKinzinger?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @AdamKinzinger}}}\uc2  (R-IL) says a criminal referral from the 1/6 committee to the Department of Justice is \u8220\'20\'1Clikely\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf the rule of law says, \u8216\'20\'18You can attempt a coup as long as you fail,\u8217\'20\'19... that is way more dangerous for this country than fear of short-term violence.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/YGK6JLTZad"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/YGK6JLTZad}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1569677388820127747?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 13, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The January 6 committee has publicly aired a trove of evidence about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to disrupt the 2020 election and his actions before and during the attack on the US Capitol. It\u8217\'20\'19s been unclear what the end result of the bipartisan House panel\u8217\'20\'19s investigation will be, but Kinzinger\u8217\'20\'19s comments make it clear he thinks the justice department may act on their findings.\par \par \uc2 The January 6 committee is expected to resume its hearings later this month, which Kinzinger described as \u8220\'20\'1Cmust-watch TV\u8221\'20\'1D for those who care about the fate of the \uc2 US government\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s gonna be \u8230\'20\'26 must-watch TV, not from an entertainment perspective, but from a if you care about the United States of American government perspective.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2  (R-IL), who says there will be "a lot more evidence" against Trump at the next 1/6 committee hearing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/HRrMA9Xsvn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/HRrMA9Xsvn}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1569679560823771138?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 13, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Inflation wave not over for US yet as prices rise against expectations in August\par \par \uc2 New data released by the \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2  today showed prices continuing to rise across the country in August, defying expectations for a decrease in the most potent inflation wave since the 1980s. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a look at the numbers from \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/dominic-rushe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dominic Rushe}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Prices in the US surged again in August but the pace of inflation slowed for the second consecutive month as energy costs fell.\par \par \uc2 The Consumer Price Index (CPI), the \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 monthly cost of living survey, found prices were 8.3% higher last month compared with August last year. The figure was down from an annual rate of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/10/us-inflation-rate-july-2022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 8.5% recorded in July}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/jul/13/high-us-gas-food-prices-june-led-to-largest-annual-increase-inflation-40-years"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 9.1% in June}}}\uc2 , the highest rate in four decades.\par \par \uc2 Falling gas prices were the major contributor to the drop. Gas prices have fallen for 13 weeks in a row. Nationally, a gallon of gas currently costs an average of $3.71, according to AAA, down from a high of over $5 in June.\par \par \uc2 Used and new car prices \u8211\'20\'13 once a major driver of inflation \u8211\'20\'13 fell, as did airfares.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/sep/13/us-inflation-rate-august-2022-gas-prices"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US inflation slows to 8.3% in August but prices still rising}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 The chair of the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2 Jaime Harrison\uc2  has put out a statement condemning the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s proposed ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is expected to be introduced today.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf Republicans gain control, they will try to pass a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, following extreme bans Republicans have implemented across the country with no exceptions for rape or incest. That\u8217\'20\'19s the Republican agenda,\u8221\'20\'1D Harrison said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 This will be the sixth time Republican senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  has introduced his national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in Congress, only now, the South Carolina lawmaker has made it even more strict.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.lgraham.senate.gov/public/index.cfm/2021/1/graham-reintroduces-20-week-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Previous versions of the bill}}}\uc2  have outlawed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 20 weeks of pregnancy, but Graham is now expected to propose a ban that takes effect after 15 weeks. That would align federal law with Florida, which outlaws the procedure after the same period of time, with some medical exceptions.\par \par \uc2 The GOP is in an uncertain spot when it comes to such legislation. Data has shown an increase in women registering to vote after the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade in June and allowed states to outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while in Republican-dominated Kansas, voters there resoundingly rejected an attempt to lay the groundwork for a statewide ban. It\u8217\'20\'19s also worth remembering that Graham proposed his national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban during a period when Republicans controlled both Congress and the White House, and it didn\u8217\'20\'19t pass then.\par \par \uc2 Yet outlawing the procedure retains a strong constituency within the Republican party. After Roe was overturned, former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.breitbart.com/politics/2022/06/24/exclusive-mike-pence-on-scotus-overturning-roe-today-life-won/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called for}}}\uc2  a national ban, while Graham\u8217\'20\'19s measure we co-sponsored by most Republican senators when it was last introduced.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican senator set to propose national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. Republicans will give the country a preview of what they\u8217\'20\'19d like to see happen to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights today, when senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  proposes a national ban on the procedure after 15 weeks of pregnancy, according to \uc2 The Washington Post\uc2 . Democrats control the Senate and there is no chance of the bill going anywhere as long as that is the case, so instead, the proposal will serve as a reminder to both \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  supporters and opponents alike of what they can expect should the GOP return to the majority in Congress.\par \par \uc2 Besides that, there\u8217\'20\'19s a lot going on:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 By the time you read this, the labor department will have released its August inflation data, which is expected to show consumer price growth moderating, though by how much remains to be seen.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Speaking of inflation, president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will hold a White House event to celebrate his Inflation Reduction Act spending bill at 3 pm eastern time. Vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will speak as well .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Delaware, New Hampshire and Rhode Island are holding the final primary elections in the nation today, setting the stage for the November 8 midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Nations General Assembly\uc2  begins today in New York City.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220913ei9d001xk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
