\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Guess what, women can vote! Is that why even hardline anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  Republicans are backtracking?\b0\par\par\uc2 Arwa Mahdawi \par \uc2 770 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 September 2022\par 13:58 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 In the weeks after Roe v Wade was overturned, there was a huge rush to register to vote. Now rightwing candidates are toning down their rhetoric but history tells us they can\u8217\'20\'19t be trusted\par \par \uc2 Want to know a fun fact about women in the US? They comprise half the population and they\u8217\'20\'19ve got the right to vote. Pissing them off en masse is a risky political move \u8211\'20\'13as Republicans are quickly finding out. A few months ago it looked like Republicans would decimate the Democrats in the midterm elections in November; now they are on much shakier ground. A recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jezebel.com/abortion-top-motivating-factor-2022-elections-poll-1849484518"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wall Street Journal}}}\uc2  poll found that 60% of voters support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in most or all cases, and that the supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/jun/26/the-guardian-view-on-overturning-roe-v-wade-anti-abortionists-reign-supreme"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturning Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  earlier this year is \u8220\'20\'1Cthe single issue most likely to make them vote this November\u8221\'20\'1D. In the two weeks after Roe was overturned, the number of people registering to vote {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.economist.com/graphic-detail/2022/08/30/americas-fight-over-abortions-has-fired-up-women-voters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increased by 10%}}}\uc2 , new women voters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/09/03/opinion/women-voters-roe-abortion-midterms.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 far outnumbering}}}\uc2  men.\par \par \uc2 Cue {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/12/republicans-soften-staunch-anti-abortion-stance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 furious back-pedalling}}}\uc2  from the right on women\u8217\'20\'19s rights. Numerous Republican congressional candidates have removed or amended references to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from their online profiles in recent months, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/08/30/republicans-abortion-trump-online/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post reports}}}\uc2 . Colorado state senator Barbara Kirkmeyer, for example, no longer refers to the \u8220\'20\'1Csanctity of life\u8221\'20\'1D on her campaign website. Arizona senate candidate \uc2 Blake Masters\uc2  has also been hitting the delete button. In an interview this year with a Catholic news outlet, Masters compared \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \u8220\'20\'1Cchild sacrifice\u8221\'20\'1D, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CIt needs to stop.\u8221\'20\'1D Last month he toned down his language and clarified he simply supports \u8220\'20\'1Ca ban on very late-term and partial-birth \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D. He also amended his website so it no longer proclaims he is \u8220\'20\'1C100% pro-life\u8221\'20\'1D and instead says: \u8220\'20\'1CProtect babies, don\u8217\'20\'19t let them be killed,\u8221\'20\'1D followed with: \u8220\'20\'1CDemocrats lie about my views on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Minnesota Republican gubernatorial nominee Scott Jensen has similarly moved away from publicly espousing hardline views on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In March, Jensen said in a radio interview that he would \u8220\'20\'1Ctry to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8230\'20\'26 There is no reason for us to be having abortions going out.\u8221\'20\'1D In a video released in July, Jensen said his previous comments were clumsy, and announced he supports abortions in cases of rape or incest or if the life of the woman is in danger. (Thank you, sir, very nice of you to suggest it\u8217\'20\'19s OK for a woman not to be forced to give birth if she will almost certainly die doing so!)\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s nothing wrong with politicians changing their minds; on the contrary, politicians should be commended for thoughtfully evolving their positions based on feedback from the people they represent. Sadly, I don\u8217\'20\'19t think that\u8217\'20\'19s what is happening here. What\u8217\'20\'19s happening here is that a lot of Republicans are morally bankrupt idiots who are happy to tone down their rhetoric to win elections and are likely to rapidly revert to their extremist agenda as soon as they get into power. That\u8217\'20\'19s what supreme court justice {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/25/gorsuch-kavanaugh-misled-senators-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh }}}\uc2  appeared to do, after all. Senator \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2 , one of the few Republicans to support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, said she would nominate Kavanaugh because he had reassured her that he was a big fan of judicial precedent and wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t overturn Roe. Though others have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/may/05/trump-justices-abortion-roe-v-wade-gorsuch-kavanaugh-coney-barrett"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 challenged Collins\u8217\'20\'19 account}}}\uc2  of what Kavanaugh said.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re often told \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a divisive issue. The thing is, it\u8217\'20\'19s not. Poll after poll shows {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/06/03/1102872199/gallup-poll-pro-choice-roe-v-wade-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most Americans}}}\uc2  support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  being {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/religion/2022/05/06/americas-abortion-quandary/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 broadly legal}}}\uc2 . Just look at Kansas. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/aug/05/the-guardian-view-on-the-kansas-abortion-vote-voice-of-america"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Last month}}}\uc2  the conservative state decisively voted to reject a ballot measure that would restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. (A \u8220\'20\'1Cballot measure\u8221\'20\'1D is a form of direct democracy where proposed legislation is approved or rejected by voters rather than legislators.) Instead of reflecting on what happened in Kansas, Republicans across the US are now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/09/10/the-lefts-best-chance-for-restoring-abortion-rights-in-red-states-is-in-jeopardy-00055901"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 working overtime to try to make it harder}}}\uc2  to pass ballot measures.\par \par \uc2 Republicans may be doing their best to suppress democracy but it\u8217\'20\'19s not dead yet. \u8220\'20\'1CTo those of you who feel that women are inferior, remember you were warned,\u8221\'20\'1D Republican South Carolina state senator Sandy Senn recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fivethirtyeight.com/features/why-republicans-keep-failing-to-pass-abortion-bans/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told colleagues}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be interesting to see what happens in the November elections. Because this issue is huge. You don\u8217\'20\'19t think that women will vote single-issue on something like this? Because they will.\u8221\'20\'1D The problem is, where there\u8217\'20\'19s a will, there\u8217\'20\'19s often a Republican way to subvert it.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Arwa Mahdawi is a Guardian columnist\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220913ei9d0025w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
