\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18A wakeup call\u8217\'20\'19: more Republicans are softening staunch anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  stance\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang \par \uc2 1,492 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 September 2022\par 17:14 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Moves come amid a ferocious backlash to the fall of Roe that has seen Democrat hopes in the midterm elections revived\par \par \uc2 A growing number of Republicans are changing their positions on abortions since the fall of Roe v Wade as midterm elections approach in the US, signaling a softened shift from their previously staunch anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  stances.\par \par \uc2 Since the supreme court overturned the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June, many Republicans are adopting more compromised positions in attempts to win votes in key states through a slew of changes in messaging on websites, advertisements and public statements.\par \par \uc2 The moves come amid a ferocious backlash to the decision that has revived Democratic hopes in the midterm elections, as a solidly red state like Kansas voted in a referendum to keep some \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 With midterm elections approaching, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also served as a prime motivator for female voters across the country, especially among Democrats, and driving {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/03/mary-peltola-alaska-congress-interview-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 striking special-election successes }}}\uc2  for the party seeking to hold both houses of Congress.\par \par \uc2 According to a new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/24/democrats-midterms-abortion-pat-ryan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 survey}}}\uc2  by the \uc2 Pew Research Center\uc2 , 56% of voters say that the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be \u8220\'20\'1Cvery important\u8221\'20\'1D to them at the polls this fall, marking a significant increase from 43% in March.\par \par \uc2 Additionally, an increasing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/tbonier/status/1559897880042868736"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 number}}}\uc2  of states, including Pennsylvania and Wisconsin, are seeing growing gender gaps among new registrants since the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s Dobbs decision, according to the Democratic data services firm TargetSmart.\par \par \uc2 As a result, Republicans are increasingly recognizing that the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  could cost them dearly at the polls as they attempt to gain control of the House and Senate.\par \par \uc2 The difficulty of shifting from gung-ho anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rhetoric to a more complicated reality for a lot of Republicans was starkly illustrated by Kansas\u8217\'20\'19s referendum. The usually reliably Republican state voted to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections in its state constitution, thus providing an unprecedented boost in red state America to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights movement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe vote earlier this summer in Kansas is a wakeup call to Republicans that not only are the most extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions non-starters with voters but the whole issue has flipped as a Democratic motivation to head to the polls,\u8221\'20\'1D Republican strategist Barrett Marson told the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COver the years, it\u8217\'20\'19s been OK to advocate for the strictest \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulations in a Republican primary because \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  generally was protected by Roe v Wade. Now it\u8217\'20\'19s no longer theoretical. So now the most restrictive policies have real-life consequences. And suburban women are giving a candidate\u8217\'20\'19s position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  greater weight as they consider who to vote for,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, a Republican Senate nominee in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/washington-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington state}}}\uc2  said that she was against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 but supported a state law that guarantees the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  until fetal viability.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI respect the voters of Washington state,\u8221\'20\'1D said Tiffany Smiley, who previously said she was \u8220\'20\'1C100% pro-life\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CThey long decided where they stand on the issue,\u8221\'20\'1D she added, referring to the state law that was passed in 1991.\par \par \uc2 In an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=t5lAs4l-Sr8&ab_channel=SmileyforWashington"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  ad}}}\uc2  released last week, Smiley told viewers she was \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-life but I opposed a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\u8221\'20\'1D. The ad came in response to an ad from \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2 , Smiley\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic incumbent opponent, which called Smiley \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s hand-picked candidate\u8221\'20\'1D, referring to the Senate Republican leader known for his anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  views and push to stack the supreme court with conservative justices opposed to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Murray\u8217\'20\'19s ad claimed that if elected, Smiley would support federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMurray is trying to scare you, I am trying to serve you.\u8221\'20\'1D Smiley said, \u8220\'20\'1CI made it clear in my ad that \u8230\'20\'26 I am not for a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. You know, the extreme in this race is \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2 . She is for federalizing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, earlier this year, Smiley\u8217\'20\'19s campaign accepted the endorsement of Tennessee Republican senator \uc2 Marsha Blackburn\uc2 , a staunch anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activist who previously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/marshablackburn/status/1083499955686440960"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 introduced}}}\uc2  a bill to the Senate that sought to strip all \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers, including Planned Parenthood, of federal funding.\par \par \uc2 Another Republican whose position shift was more apparent than Smiley\u8217\'20\'19s is Arizona Senate candidate \uc2 Blake Masters\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In an interview in March with Catholic news outlet EWTN, Masters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/09/01/1120599968/as-the-midterms-approach-some-republicans-are-changing-how-they-talk-about-abort"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CEvery society has had child sacrifice or has had human sacrifice in some form, and this is our form. And it needs to stop,\u8221\'20\'1D referring to abortions.\par \par \uc2 Since then, Masters has appeared to soften his \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  views. In August, the Donald Trump-endorsed candidate released an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/09/01/1120599968/as-the-midterms-approach-some-republicans-are-changing-how-they-talk-about-abort"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ad}}}\uc2  that said, \u8220\'20\'1CLook, I support a ban on very late-term and partial birth \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . And most Americans agree with that. That would just put us on par with other civilized nations.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Moreover, Masters has made {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2022-election/arizona-blake-masters-backtracks-abortion-scrubs-campaign-website-rcna44808"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 changes}}}\uc2  to his campaign website which once stated that he supported a \u8220\'20\'1Cfederal personhood law\u8221\'20\'1D and that he was \u8220\'20\'1C100% pro-life\u8221\'20\'1D. His website now says, \u8220\'20\'1CProtect babies, don\u8217\'20\'19t let them be killed,\u8221\'20\'1D followed with, \u8220\'20\'1CDemocrats lie about my views on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 According to his current campaign website, Masters would support a third trimester federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. Previously, his website {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/08/29/politics/republicans-shift-abortion-positions-general-election/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  that he supported a constitutional amendment that \u8220\'20\'1Crecognizes unborn babies are human being[s] that may not be killed\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group Susan B Anthony Pro-Life America has come to the defense of Masters\u8217\'20\'19 shifting position. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Blake Masters\uc2  has rightfully centered his position on what is achievable now at the federal level: a limit on abortions at a point by which the unborn child can feel excruciating pain,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://sbaprolife.org/newsroom/press-releases/natl-pro-life-group-blake-masters-has-rightfully-centered-his-position-on-what-is-achievable-at-the-federal-level"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  the organization\u8217\'20\'19s president, Marjorie Dannenfelser.\par \par \uc2 Minnesota Republican gubernatorial nominee Scott Jensen has signaled a similar softening in his \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  position. In an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mprnews.org/episode/2022/03/15/republican-gubernatorial-candidate-dr-scott-jensen"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interview}}}\uc2  with Minnesota Public Radio in March, Jensen said, \u8220\'20\'1CI would try to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . I think that we\u8217\'20\'19re basically in a situation where we should be governed by \u8230\'20\'26 there is no reason for us to be having abortions going out.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 However, Jensen backtracked on his words a few months later. In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ePWrUIKS3Bs&t=852s&ab_channel=Dr.ScottJensenforGovernor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 video}}}\uc2  released in July, Jensen said that he supports abortions in cases of rape or incest or if the life of the woman is in danger.\par \par \uc2 Jensen described his previous comments as clumsy, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CI never thought it necessary to try and identify what those exceptions might be in regards to legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or not, because I always thought when I uphold the pregnant woman\u8217\'20\'19s life, and if her mental and physical health is in danger or jeopardized, that\u8217\'20\'19s all that needs to be said.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Despite Jensen\u8217\'20\'19s amended comments, not everyone is convinced that he is genuine about his position. Minnesota Democratic party chairman Ken Martin said that if Jensen is elected, he will still try to pass an all-out \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law that would not make exceptions for rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no reason to assume that Governor Scott Jensen would not attempt to pass the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban \u8211\'20\'13 without exceptions for rape and incest \u8211\'20\'13 that he has repeatedly supported,\u8221\'20\'1D he said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.startribune.com/minnesota-gop-governor-candidate-scott-jensen-shifts-abortion-position-announces-new-plan/600194181/?refresh=true"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement.}}}\par \par \uc2 In May, Iowa Republican candidate Zach Nunn raised his hand during a primary debate when asked if \u8220\'20\'1Call abortions, no exceptions\u8221\'20\'1D should be illegal.\par \par \uc2 Nunn also previously voted for a measure that required women seeking an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to wait 72 hours. The measure included an exception to protect the mother\u8217\'20\'19s life but did not mention cases of rape and incest.\par \par \uc2 Nunn\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic opponent, Representative \uc2 Cindy Axne\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kcci.com/article/nunn-pushes-back-on-new-axne-ad-targeting-his-no-exceptions-abortion-stance/40874901#"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released}}}\uc2  a political ad against him that used footage of him raising his hand at the primary. \u8220\'20\'1CEven in the case of rape, even in the case of incest, even if a woman\u8217\'20\'19s life is in danger \u8211\'20\'13 who will take away a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to make her own decisions, regardless of the circumstances? Zach Nunn,\u8221\'20\'1D the video said.\par \par \uc2 In response to the video, Nunn changed his tune in an op-ed he published last month, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.desmoinesregister.com/story/opinion/columnists/iowa-view/2022/08/19/zach-nunn-protect-life-mother-and-baby/10312721002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m pro-life, and I support protecting the life of the mother and the baby.\u8221\'20\'1D He accused Axne of taking his comments out of context and went on to say, \u8220\'20\'1CThis issue is too important: Iowans deserve to have their voices heard.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the op-ed, Nunn said that he supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \u8220\'20\'1Cexceptions for horrific circumstances like rape, incest and fetal abnormalities, and to save the life of the mother\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 With many Republicans looking to secure votes from moderate and independent voters, some political strategists worry that all this effort spent on reconfiguring their \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions could negatively affect their political momentum, especially as Democrats are making the issue a cornerstone in their own campaigns.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile the economy and inflation should be the most important issue this cycle, Republican candidates are now having to defend their stances on eliminating all or most \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  options,\u8221\'20\'1D said Marson.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAny time they aren\u8217\'20\'19t talking [about the] economy and inflation, they are losing opportunities.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220912ei9c000xg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
