\par\par \uc2 Law\par \b \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  defends supreme court as \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  lashes out at Roe ruling\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang in New York \par \uc2 596 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 September 2022\par 17:19 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Chief justice warns against linking contentious decisions with court legitimacy as vice-president attacks \u8216\'20\'18activist court\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  chief justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  has defended his conservative-leaning bench from attacks over its decision in June to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturn federal \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\uc2 , as US vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  launched a fierce attack on what {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/09/kamala-harris-activist-supreme-court-roe-v-wade-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 she called}}}\uc2  today\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cactivist court\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Roberts, in his first public appearance since the bombshell ruling to overturn the landmark 1973 Roe v Wade decision, warned against linking contentious decisions with court legitimacy, saying at an event on Friday night: \u8220\'20\'1CThe court has always decided controversial cases and decisions have always been subject to intense criticism, and that is entirely appropriate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But in her first sit-down interview with a TV network since becoming vice-president, Harris told NBC News that she now believes the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supreme court}}}\uc2  is an \u8220\'20\'1Cactivist court\u8221\'20\'1D after the institution took away nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe had an established right for almost half a century, which is the right of women to make decisions about their own body as an extension of\u8230\'20\'26 the privacy rights to which all people are entitled,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said during the interview with Chuck Todd for Meet the Press, aired in full on Sunday after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/09/kamala-harris-activist-supreme-court-roe-v-wade-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 being trailed}}}\uc2  on Friday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd this court took that constitutional right away, and we are suffering as a nation because of it,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 Harris said: \u8220\'20\'1CI believe government should not be telling women what to do with their bodies. I believe government should not be telling women how to plan their families\u8230\'20\'26 should not be criminalizing healthcare providers... should not be saying \u8216\'20\'18no exception for rape or incest\u8217\'20\'19.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Before becoming a US Senator and then the first female US vice-president, Harris was attorney general of California and, before that, district attorney of San Francisco.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs a prosecutor, former prosecutor, who specialized in child sexual assault cases, understanding the violence that occurs against women and children, and then to further subject them to those kind of inhumane conditions \u8211\'20\'13 that\u8217\'20\'19s what I believe,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president also remarked that she has \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat concern about the integrity of the court overall\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Since the Trump administration achieved three appointments to the nine-member bench, the court has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/sep/06/supreme-court-trump-texas-abortion-law-democracy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 swung sharply}}}\uc2  to the right with a six-three conservative supermajority. It voted in June to dismantle Roe, returning the power over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to the states and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/abortion-rights-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leaving}}}\uc2  58% of US women of reproductive age, or 40 million women, in states hostile to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 And Roberts defended the court.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe added, at the Friday event: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t understand the connection between the opinions people disagree with and the legitimacy of the supreme court,\u8221\'20\'1D while being interviewed by two judges from the Denver-based 10th US circuit court of appeals at its conference in Colorado Springs, the Gazette {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gazette.com/news/courts/chief-justice-roberts-deems-it-mistake-to-question-supreme-courts-legitimacy-based-on-decisions/article_892aed50-d6c7-56a8-b1e5-aebe88bea8c9.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newspaper reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf the court doesn\u8217\'20\'19t retain its legitimate function of interpreting the constitution, I\u8217\'20\'19m not sure who would take up that mantle. You don\u8217\'20\'19t want the political branches telling you what the law is, and you don\u8217\'20\'19t want public opinion to be the guide about what the appropriate decision is,\u8221\'20\'1D Roberts said.\par \par \uc2 Roberts said that fencing around the court building in Washington DC, installed amid fierce protests over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, has come down. And that when the next supreme court term begins in October, arguments will be open to the public in person again, after the building was shut in the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220911ei9b002jr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
