\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 New \u8216\'20\'18objective\u8217\'20\'19 CNN appears to be making itself objectively rightwing\b0\par\par\uc2 Arwa Mahdawi \par \uc2 1,200 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 September 2022\par 15:35 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The cable network\u8217\'20\'19s CEO dramatic hiring and firing of on-air talent seems designed to woo the Fox News crowd\par \par \uc2 CNN has a very odd definition of \u8216\'20\'18objectivity\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 CNN wants to be the new Fox News and it\u8217\'20\'19s not even trying to hide it. Earlier this year Chris Licht became the new CEO of the cable network and immediately made it clear that he was going to change the network\u8217\'20\'19s direction. One of Licht\u8217\'20\'19s first moves was to embark on what {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2022/07/21/cnn-boss-licht-capitol-hill-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Axios}}}\uc2  described as a \u8220\'20\'1CCapitol Hill diplomacy tour\u8221\'20\'1D and others described as a Republican boot-licking tour. Licht met with lawmakers who had become wary of cable news and promised them that CNN was moving away from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2022/06/02/cnn-breaking-news-guidelines"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Calarmist\u8221\'20\'1D programming}}}\uc2  towards more neutral, objective reporting.\par \par \uc2 What does that mean in practice? Well, it appears to mean firing anyone who is critical of Donald Trump or Republicans. Last month CNN suddenly axed Brian Stelter\u8217\'20\'19s Sunday show in a move many commentators considered {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/aug/24/the-changes-at-cnn-look-politically-motivated-that-should-concern-us-all"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 politically motivated}}}\uc2  ; Stelter had been an outspoken critic of Trump and was reviled by many on the right. Earlier this month White House correspondent John Harwood was fired shortly after calling Trump \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2022/sep/02/john-harwood-cnn-correspondent-leaves-trump-demagogue"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a dishonest demagogue}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D on the air.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not just who was fired that is alarming \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s the abrupt manner in which they were fired. As the media analyst {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://talkingpointsmemo.com/edblog/lets-see-ya-dance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Josh Marshall}}}\uc2  noted, \u8220\'20\'1CThe most striking thing about Licht\u8217\'20\'19s firings to date is how they are choreographed for \u8230\'20\'26 right-wing media consumption and designed to generate mass schadenfreude on the right: the b\u234\'00\'EAte noires Fox has been harping on for years suddenly marched to the top of the pyramid and hurled to the ground.\u8221\'20\'1D Licht says he\u8217\'20\'19s moving away from sensational news, but he appears to be putting on his own little drama for the right.\par \par \uc2 After purging progressive voices, Licht has just made his first big hire: announcing on Tuesday that John Miller would be joining CNN as the network\u8217\'20\'19s chief law enforcement and intelligence analyst. Miller isn\u8217\'20\'19t exactly an obvious hire if you\u8217\'20\'19re looking to brandish your new \u8220\'20\'1Cneutrality\u8221\'20\'1D credentials. The former New York police department (\uc2 NYPD\uc2 ) deputy commissioner of intelligence and counter-terrorism is an extremely polarizing figure who made headlines in March when he testified to the New \uc2 York city council\uc2  that the \uc2 NYPD\uc2  did not, in his opinion, inappropriately spy on Muslims after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.huffpost.com/entry/cnn-john-miller-muslims-nypd_n_6318f6f3e4b027aa40575e18"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 11 attacks}}}\uc2 . Which is a weird thing to say because Pulitzer Prize-winning reporting has clearly shown that the \uc2 NYPD\uc2  used census data to spy on Muslims following September 11 and the department has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2018/apr/05/nypd-muslim-surveillance-settlement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 settled a number of lawsuits }}}\uc2  related to the illegal spying.\par \par \uc2 A number of Muslims and civil rights activists are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.huffpost.com/entry/cnn-john-miller-muslims-nypd_n_6318f6f3e4b027aa40575e18"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 alarmed}}}\uc2  about Miller taking on his new role at CNN. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have no faith that as chief law enforcement and intelligence analyst at CNN, Miller won\u8217\'20\'19t continue to propagandize on behalf of law enforcement and dismiss clear discrimination against Muslims and other marginalized communities,\u8221\'20\'1D Muslim Advocates, a group involved in one of the lawsuits against the \uc2 NYPD\uc2 , said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Licht doesn\u8217\'20\'19t seem to mind that his new hire may alienate Muslims or anyone who cares about illegal police surveillance programs. He doesn\u8217\'20\'19t seem to find it alarming that his new analyst has been accused of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/03/23/muslim-leaders-want-nypd-official-censured-00019450"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lying}}}\uc2  about the \uc2 NYPD\uc2  surveillance of Muslims. He doesn\u8217\'20\'19t seem to find it awkward that even \uc2 Eric Adams\uc2 , the mayor of New York City and a former police officer, said Miller was \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nydailynews.com/news/politics/new-york-elections-government/ny-nypd-john-miller-muslim-new-yorkers-outrage-20220321-ldxukd7fhngotp5hlzxxz4yiki-story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrong}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D to deny the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://popular.info/p/what-corporate-media-executives-mean?utm_source=email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 existence of the program}}}\uc2 . Instead, the CNN CEO announced, with a seemingly straight face, that Miller \u8220\'20\'1Cwill help deliver on CNN\u8217\'20\'19s commitment to tackle complex issues while presenting audiences with independent, objective news\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s funny whose views are considered objective and whose aren\u8217\'20\'19t. While Miller\u8217\'20\'19s experiences with the \uc2 NYPD\uc2  apparently make him a paragon of neutrality, people from marginalized backgrounds are constantly told that their life experiences make them biased. The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t let its former reporter, Felicia Sonmez, a sexual assault survivor, cover stories on sexual misconduct because of her history and public statements {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/mar/30/washington-post-felicia-sonmez-sexual-assault-sexism"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 she\u8217\'20\'19d made about it}}}\uc2 . A Black Pittsburgh Post-Gazette reporter was barred from covering the George Floyd protests over a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2020/06/08/872234014/editors-barred-a-black-reporter-from-covering-protests-then-her-newsroom-rebelle"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 flippant tweet comparing looters}}}\uc2  to country music fans. Last year, the Associated Press fired a news associate called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2021/may/21/associated-press-emily-wilder-fired-pro-palestinian-views"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Emily Wilder}}}\uc2 , who is Jewish, for past pro-Palestinian activism and accused her of showing \u8220\'20\'1Cclear bias\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 So who is CNN going to hire next in order to demonstrate its objectivity? Trump seems to be angling for a job. On Sunday Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mediaite.com/trump/trump-throws-temper-tantrum-over-fox-news-pushing-democrat-agenda-before-suggesting-cnn-go-conservative/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posted}}}\uc2  on Truth Social that \u8220\'20\'1Cif \u8216\'20\'18low ratings\u8217\'20\'19 CNN ever went Conservative, they would be an absolute gold mine, and I would help them to do so\u8221\'20\'1D. The way CNN is going I wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be surprised if they make Trump their new election integrity analyst next week.\par \par \uc2 Ginni Thomas has links to anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups who lobbied to overturn Roe\par \par \uc2 Speaking of bias \u8230\'20\'26 a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/09/ginni-thomas-abortion-roe-v-wade-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new analysis}}}\uc2  has found 51% of the parties who filed amicus briefs (legal arguments used to lobby justices) calling for an end to a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  right have political connections to Ginni Thomas, who is the wife of the supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThe Thomases are normalizing the prospect of too close an association between the supreme court and those who litigate before it,\u8221\'20\'1D a law professor told the Guardian. \u8220\'20\'1CThis isn\u8217\'20\'19t the first time that Mrs Thomas has had dealings with those who come before the court and seek her husband\u8217\'20\'19s vote.\u8221\'20\'1D A very healthy democracy!\par \par \uc2 Five Republicans help Democrats block near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in South Carolina\par \par \uc2 One of the most vocal Republican dissenters was Tom Davis, who said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/09/south-carolina-republicans-democrats-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he\u8217\'20\'19d promised his daughters}}}\uc2  he wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t vote to further restrict access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Opposition by the five Republicans means that the restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill will head back to the state house. Some good news for once.\par \par \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  says he has \u8216\'20\'18never met anyone who hates women\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Misogyny simply doesn\u8217\'20\'19t exist, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.yahoo.com/entertainment/tucker-carlson-mocks-aoc-experiences-234402094.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said the Fox News host}}}\uc2 , during an incredibly misogynistic segment about Congresswoman \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Rishi Sunak says he\u8217\'20\'19s been an awful father and husband\par \par \uc2 Sunak, who recently lost the contest to become the UK\u8217\'20\'19s new prime minister to \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2 , was recently asked about the greatest sacrifice he\u8217\'20\'19d made during his political career. His answer was that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thewire.in/world/rishi-sunak-final-hustings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he\u8217\'20\'19d been}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Can absolutely appalling husband and father\u8221\'20\'1D for the last couple of years \u8211\'20\'13 which was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mikeysmith/status/1565065228609544192?s=20&t=1qM-V0eGplgwq0ZLbdfUyw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 greeted with applause}}}\uc2 . Imagine, for a second, a female politician saying something like that. She wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t get applause in response \u8211\'20\'13 she\u8217\'20\'19d get a thousand think-pieces chiding her for not being a good mum and calling her selfish for putting her career first.\par \par \uc2 The week in pawtriarchy\par \par \uc2 The world is going to the dogs and Dolly Parton has taken note. The singer recently announced the launch of \u8220\'20\'1CDoggy Parton\u8221\'20\'1D, a line of dog apparel for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/08/31/entertainment/dolly-parton-doggy-parton-line/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pampered pooch}}}\uc2 . It apparently includes rhinestoned harnesses, cowgirl dresses and blond wigs. Pawfect.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220910ei9a001p6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
