\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Women are the reason we can win,\u8217\'20\'19 \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  says at Pennsylvania rally\b0\par\par\uc2 Richard Luscombe \par \uc2 530 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 September 2022\par 14:24 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Democrat Senate candidate puts \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights at top of his agenda as he targets Republican opponent Mehmet Oz\par \par \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  has placed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights at the top of his agenda to capture Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s Senate seat in November, telling supporters at a raucous rally on Sunday: \u8220\'20\'1CWomen are the reason we can win. Don\u8217\'20\'19t piss off women.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Democrat was targeting comments made by his Republican opponent Mehmet Oz in May that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thedailybeast.com/dr-oz-says-abortion-is-still-murder-at-any-stage-of-pregnancy?ref=home"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  at any stage of pregnancy was \u8220\'20\'1Cmurder\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Oz, in keeping with a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/12/republicans-soften-staunch-anti-abortion-stance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent trend among Republican candidates}}}\uc2 , has attempted to soften his extremist position as the fall\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections draw closer, insisting that he now believes in exceptions for rape, incest and the health of the woman.\par \par \uc2 But Oz\u8217\'20\'19s rival was uncompromising in his criticism during Sunday\u8217\'20\'19s rally at a community college in rural Pennsylvania attended by several thousand supporters, including a large number of women in pink \u8220\'20\'1CFetterwoman\u8221\'20\'1D T-shirts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis decision is between a woman and a real doctor,\u8221\'20\'1D Fetterman said of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , alluding to Oz\u8217\'20\'19s status as a celebrity television doctor who has been branded by medical ethicists as a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/01/dr-oz-dropped-by-columbia-amid-pro-trump-republican-senate-run-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 huge danger to public health}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COz believes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is murder,\u8221\'20\'1D Fetterman continued. \u8220\'20\'1CIf every \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is murder, that means Oz thinks every woman who had to choose an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a killer. Think about that.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWomen are the reason we can win. Let me say that again. Women are the reason we win. Don\u8217\'20\'19t piss women off.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 According to research by TargetSmart, a polling analysis company, Pennsylvania ranks fifth in states showing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/tbonier/status/1559897880042868736"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 large gaps in registration numbers between men and women}}}\uc2  since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  in June overturned the 1973 Roe v Wade decision that established federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania joins Arkansas with 12% more women than men registering, while Kansas \u8211\'20\'13 a staunchly Republican state where pro-choice advocates won a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/democrats-abortion-rights-victory-kansas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 massive victory last month}}}\uc2  retaining constitutional protection for the procedure \u8211\'20\'13 leads the country with a 40% gap.\par \par \uc2 Democrats are attempting to channel nationwide anger at the reversal of Roe, and the escalation in anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation by Republicans in several states, into success in November\u8217\'20\'19s elections.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic party faces an uphill battle to retain control of both congressional chambers, but it is encouraged by research showing that voters are outraged at the ending of nearly half a century of federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/politics/2022/08/23/abortion-rises-in-importance-as-a-voting-issue-driven-by-democrats/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pew Research poll}}}\uc2  last month showed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was an important factor for 56% of registered voters, up from 43% in March. Among Democratic voters the figure rises to 71%.\par \par \uc2 In Pennsylvania, the candidates are locked in a tight race.\par \par \uc2 Fetterman has painted Oz as a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/25/john-fetterman-dr-oz-pennsylvania-social-media-snooki"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cvisitor\u8221\'20\'1D from New Jersey}}}\uc2  who knows little about the state he wishes to represent. Oz\u8217\'20\'19s campaign, meanwhile, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/31/john-fetterman-dr-oz-health-stroke"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mocked the health of Fetterman}}}\uc2 , who is recovering from a stroke.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.inquirer.com/politics/election/fetterman-abortion-senate-pennsylvania-oz-20220911.html#loaded"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to the Philadelphia Inquirer}}}\uc2 , Fetterman \u8211\'20\'13 who has said he is struggling with auditory processing issues since his stroke \u8211\'20\'13 spoke for about 10 minutes Sunday, and he did not appear to stumble over as many words as in other recent appearances.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220912ei9c002gy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
