\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  says \u8216\'20\'18everything on the line\u8217\'20\'19 in midterm elections\b0\par\par\uc2 Nicola Slawson \par \uc2 1,298 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 September 2022\par 10:46 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Vice-president says elections will determine whether \u8216\'20\'18age-old sanctity\u8217\'20\'19 of right to vote would be protected. Plus, how the movies covered Queen Elizabeth IIDon\u8217\'20\'19t already get First Thing in your inbox? Sign up here\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said yesterday that the midterm elections in November would determine whether the \u8220\'20\'1Cage-old sanctity\u8221\'20\'1D of the right to vote would be protected in the US or whether \u8220\'20\'1Cso-called extremist leaders around the country\u8221\'20\'1D would continue to restrict access to the ballot box.\par \par \uc2 With 56 days to go until the elections, and with a paper-thin Democratic majority in both chambers of Congress, the vice-president said: \u8220\'20\'1CEverything is on the line in these elections.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In an interview with NBC News\u8217\'20\'19 Meet the Press, she said the country was facing a rising domestic extremism threat. \u8220\'20\'1CI think it is very dangerous and I think it is very harmful, and it makes us weaker,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Harris pointed to the plethora of extreme election deniers, many endorsed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who have embraced Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lie that the 2020 election \u8211\'20\'13 won by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 was \u8220\'20\'1Cstolen\u8221\'20\'1D from him.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What else did she say? \u8220\'20\'1CThere are 11 people right now running for secretary of state, the keepers of the integrity of the voting system of their state, who are election deniers,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1CCouple that with people who hold some of the highest elected office in our country who refuse to condemn an insurrection on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/09/us-capitol-insurrection-white-supremacist-terror"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 6}}}\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Russian strikes knock out power and water in Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s Kharkiv region\par \par \uc2 Russian strikes have knocked out power and water to much of the Kharkiv region, plunging its cities into darkness and cutting power in hospitals in what Ukraine {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/sep/11/russian-strikes-knock-out-power-and-water-in-ukraines-kharkiv-region"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 described as an act of \u8220\'20\'1Crevenge\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  by Russia for its recent battlefield successes.\par \par \uc2 Over the last few days, Ukrainian forces have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/sep/11/zelenskiy-ukraine-kharkiv-territorial-gains-surprise-north-east-counteroffensive"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recaptured the majority of Russian-occupied territory in the region}}}\uc2  in a lightning counteroffensive.\par \par \uc2 Ihor Terekhov\uc2 , the mayor of Kharkiv city, said work was under way to restore power and some areas reported that the electricity was back on at about 1am on Monday local time.\par \par \uc2 However, Ukrainian presidential advisers said earlier that a fire was raging at Kharkiv\u8217\'20\'19s number 5 power station.\par \par \uc2 There were also initial reports of blackouts in neighbouring Sumy and Poltava regions, as well as in Dnipropetrovsk, potentially affecting millions of civilians. \uc2 Kyrylo Tymoshenko\uc2 , the deputy head of Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s presidential office, said power had now been restored.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What has Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s president said? \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/sep/11/zelenskiy-says-next-three-months-critical-as-ukrainian-advance-continues"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blamed \u8220\'20\'1CRussian terrorists\u8221\'20\'1D for the blackouts}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CNo military facilities [were attacked],\u8221\'20\'1D the Ukrainian president said in a statement on social media. \u8220\'20\'1CThe goal is to deprive people of light and heat.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18A wakeup call\u8217\'20\'19: more Republicans are softening staunch anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance\par \par \uc2 A growing number of Republicans are changing their positions on abortions since the fall of Roe v Wade as midterm elections approach in the US, signaling a softened shift from their previously staunch anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  stances.\par \par \uc2 Since the supreme court overturned the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June, many Republicans are adopting more compromised positions in attempts to win votes in key states through a slew of changes in messaging on websites, advertisements and public statements.\par \par \uc2 The moves come amid a ferocious backlash to the decision that has revived Democrat hopes in the midterm elections and even had a solidly red state like Kansas vote in a referendum to keep certain \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 With midterm elections approaching, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also served as a prime motivator for female voters across the country, especially among Democrats, fueling {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/03/mary-peltola-alaska-congress-interview-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 striking special-election successes}}}\uc2  for the party seeking to hold both houses of Congress.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What else is happening with regards to the\par \par \uc2 supreme\par \par \uc2 court\u8217\'20\'19s decision? \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  chief justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  has defended his conservative-leaning bench from attacks over its decision in June to overturn federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, as Harris launched a fierce attack on what {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/09/kamala-harris-activist-supreme-court-roe-v-wade-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 she called}}}\uc2  today\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cactivist court\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 There were loud cheers and generous applause as Queen Elizabeth II\u8217\'20\'19s\par \par \uc2 cortege made its way down the cobblestoned Royal Mile in Edinburgh, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2022/sep/11/applause-affection-and-dissent-edinburgh-greets-queens-cortege-and-proclamation-of-new-king"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 watched by tens of thousands of people}}}\uc2 . It capped a day in which the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2022/sep/11/proclamations-of-king-charles-iii-read-in-edinburgh-cardiff-and-belfast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new King was proclaimed in Scotland}}}\uc2  as a minority of republicans also made themselves heard.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Democratic chair of the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  intelligence committee has demanded that a federal judge allows the committee to be briefed on the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s search of Mar-a-Lago and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/11/senate-intelligence-committee-trump-mar-a-lago-search"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the potential damage caused by Donald Trump}}}\uc2  hoarding top secret documents at his private club.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The far-right Sweden Democrats party was\par \par \uc2 a big winner in the country\u8217\'20\'19s election yesterday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/sep/11/swedish-election-exit-polls-far-right"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increasing its share of the vote}}}\uc2  by two to three percentage points and becoming the second-largest party, but the overall result was too close to call as counting continued.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Two women who allegedly lured a driver to death may be part of a growing religious sect, the University of Cosmic Intelligence, whose leader is currently awaiting trial for child abuse in Georgia. The off-grid bandits {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/11/alabama-women-lured-driver-death-university-of-cosmic-intelligence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accused of killing Adam Simjee}}}\uc2  have been charged with murder, kidnapping and robbery.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A novel by the punk feminist writer\par \par \uc2 Virginie Despentes\par \par \uc2 has pushed the #MeToo movement back into spotlight in France. The irreverently titled Cher Connard \u8211\'20\'13 which roughly translates as Dear Asshole \u8211\'20\'13 has become a bestseller, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/sep/12/france-metoo-movement-virginie-despentes-bestselling-novel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prompting a debate about sexual harassment}}}\uc2  and equality in the social media age.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: Lights, camera, corgis! How movies tackled the enigma that was Elizabeth II\par \par \uc2 Wise, witty, patient, crisp, faintly martyred or skydiving with James Bond \u8230\'20\'26 our film critic looks at how cinema portrayed the monarch \u8211\'20\'13 and recalls the night she put him on the spot at Windsor Castle.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Queen asked me crisply, her eyes boring into mine: \u8216\'20\'18What\u8217\'20\'19s the name of that horror film that begins with a G?\u8217\'20\'19 Various courtiers and functionaries turned expectantly to me, looking like the giant playing cards from Alice\u8217\'20\'19s Adventures in Wonderland. The silence extended. The room was melting. I couldn\u8217\'20\'19t think of a single word beginning with a G. Eventually I said: \u8216\'20\'18Is it The Grinch, Your Majesty?\u8217\'20\'19 \u8216\'20\'18Yes!\u8217\'20\'19 said the Queen, beaming. \u8216\'20\'18The Grinch,\u8217\'20\'19 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2022/sep/12/lights-camera-corgis-how-movies-tackled-the-enigma-that-was-elizabeth-ii"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Peter Bradshaw writes}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Climate check: Tourism is sucking Utah dry. Now it faces a choice \u8211\'20\'13 growth or survival?\par \par \uc2 It was a typically hot summer day in Utah\u8217\'20\'19s Zion national park, where early-afternoon heat hovered near 100F. But the extreme conditions did little to dissuade the throngs of tourists, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/sep/11/tourism-utah-drought-zion-economy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes Gabrielle Canon}}}\uc2 . Thousands descend on this waterway year after year, even as the region falls deeper into drought. Fueled by the climate crisis and the overuse of dwindling water resources, the drought threatens the safety and sustainability of the spectacular sights; at the same time, tourists and the industries that cater to them contribute to an unfolding crisis in the cherished lands that brought them there.\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: Meaty, cheesy, coconutty: a chef\u8217\'20\'19s quest to prove insects taste delicious\par \par \uc2 Insect consumption has been highlighted by the UN\u8217\'20\'19s Food and Agriculture Organization as an important tool in addressing food insecurity for a growing global population. Insect-eating presents a compelling climate solution, too \u8211\'20\'13 crickets, for example, can provide the same amount of protein as cows for less than 0.1% of the emissions. Some people might shy away from eating bugs off their plates, but chef Joseph {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/sep/09/insects-food-menu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Yoon is popularizing the age-old practice of entomophagy}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 with mouthwatering results\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220912ei9c001rz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
