\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: Queen Elizabeth II\u8217\'20\'19s death marks end of an era\b0\par\par\uc2 Nicola Slawson \par \uc2 1,391 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 September 2022\par 10:20 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Death brings end to Britain\u8217\'20\'19s second Elizabethan era and heralds reign of \uc2 King Charles III\uc2 . Plus, rural Virginia pivots from coal to green jobs\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 Queen Elizabeth II, the longest-serving monarch in British history, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2022/sep/08/queen-elizabeth-ii-britains-longest-reigning-monarch-dies-aged-96"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has died aged 96}}}\uc2 , drawing to a close the country\u8217\'20\'19s second Elizabethan era and heralding the reign of her son, \uc2 King Charles III\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The monarch, for whom abdication was never an option, died peacefully at Balmoral on Thursday afternoon, two days after her final public constitutional duty: the appointment of the 15th prime minister of her 70-year reign.\par \par \uc2 Her death means Charles becomes king, and the Duchess of Cornwall becomes Queen Consort.\par \par \uc2 In a statement on Thursday evening, the King said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe death of my beloved mother, Her Majesty the Queen, is a moment of the greatest sadness for me and all members of my family.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe mourn profoundly the passing of a cherished sovereign and a much-loved mother. I know her loss will be deeply felt throughout the country, the realms and the Commonwealth, and by countless people around the world.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 How did \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  pay tribute? In a statement issued jointly with the first lady, Jill Biden, the president said: \u8220\'20\'1CHer Majesty, Queen Elizabeth II, was more than a monarch. She defined an era.\u8221\'20\'1D Tributes have also poured in from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/08/queen-elizabeth-tributes-biden-clinton-us-presidents"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 former leaders}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 How have people reacted to the news? From the UK to the Commonwealth and beyond, admirers of the Queen have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2022/sep/09/tears-candles-and-a-farewell-to-boss-lady-the-world-mourns-queen-elizabeth-ii"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 paid their respects}}}\uc2  to the longest reigning monarch in British history while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2022/sep/08/she-has-been-so-strong-mourners-gather-at-buckingham-palace"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crowds gathered}}}\uc2  at royal residences.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What happens now? The UK now enters a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2022/sep/08/the-queens-funeral-what-we-can-expect-over-the-next-10-days"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 period of official mourning}}}\uc2  which will last for 10 days. Elizabeth II will be accorded a state funeral at Westminster Abbey, expected to be held on Monday 19 September though that has not yet been confirmed.\par \par \uc2 Justice department appeals special master ruling for Trump documents\par \par \uc2 The US justice department has demanded that a federal judge restore its access to documents seized from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago resort that carried classification markings, adding that if it would not, the department {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/08/justice-department-appeals-special-master-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would appeal to a higher court}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The demands came in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.flsd.618763/gov.uscourts.flsd.618763.68.0_1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 three-page notice of appeal}}}\uc2  filed by the justice department on Thursday in the case involving Trump\u8217\'20\'19s request for a so-called special master. They pave the way for the government to submit a detailed appeals brief to the US court of appeals for the 11th circuit.\par \par \uc2 But the justice department indicated that it would not appeal if the order for a special master to review classified materials that stopped the investigation into Trump\u8217\'20\'19s unauthorised retention of government secrets was reversed.\par \par \uc2 The filings amounted to a forceful, if clever, response against the decision by the judge \u8211\'20\'13 a Trump appointee \u8211\'20\'13 to give unusually deferential treatment to Trump on account of his status as a former president.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What else is happening? Top former Trump strategist \uc2 Steve Bannon{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/08/steve-bannon-border-wall-charges-surrender"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has been charged in New York}}}\uc2  with money laundering, conspiracy and scheme to defraud. The former Trump adviser surrendered to authorities in Manhattan on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Revealed: Ginni Thomas\u8217\'20\'19s links to anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups\par \par \uc2 that lobbied to overturn Roe\par \par \uc2 Ginni Thomas, the self-styled \u8220\'20\'1Cculture warrior\u8221\'20\'1D and extreme rightwing activist, has links to more than half the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups and individuals who lobbied her husband, \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , and his fellow \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  justices before their decision to eradicate a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to terminate a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Analysis of written legal arguments, or \u8220\'20\'1Camicus briefs\u8221\'20\'1D, used to lobby the justices as they deliberated over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights underlines the extent to which \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s wife was intertwined with the pressure campaign.\par \par \uc2 The survey found 51% of parties that filed amicus briefs calling for an end to a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  right have political connections to Ginni Thomas, raising concerns about a possible conflict of interest at the highest levels of the US judiciary.\par \par \uc2 The six-to-three rightwing majority of the court, supercharged by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s three appointed conservative justices, overthrew the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June. \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  was one of the six who voted for the hotly contested ruling, Dobbs v Jackson.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What have legal experts said? \u8220\'20\'1CThis isn\u8217\'20\'19t the first time that Mrs Thomas has had dealings with those who come before the court and seek her husband\u8217\'20\'19s vote,\u8221\'20\'1D Melissa Murray, a law professor, said.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Los Angeles has\par \par \uc2 had a 4% increase in its homeless population during the pandemic, with 69,144 unhoused people counted across the county this year, according to government data released on Thursday. The figures are a rough estimate from a single day and are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/08/los-angeles-homelessness-unhoused-people-number"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 believed to be an undercount}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A former paratrooper who allegedly enlisted in the army to become more proficient at killing Black people was given top security clearance despite ties to white supremacist organizations and Nazi ideology. Killian Ryan was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/08/us-military-killian-ryan-racism-social-media"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arrested on 26 August}}}\uc2  and charged with making a false statement on his army application.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A collision of extreme weather events is bearing down on California as wildfires threaten communities, a record-setting heatwave adds stress to the electrical grid, and moisture from a hurricane is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/08/california-wildfires-fairview-fire-heatwave"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expected to bring thunderstorms and flash floods}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 North Korea has passed a law enshrining the right to \u8220\'20\'1Cautomatically\u8221\'20\'1D use preemptive nuclear strikes to protect itself, a move leader Kim Jong-un said makes its nuclear status \u8220\'20\'1Cirreversible\u8221\'20\'1D and bars any de-nuclearisation talks, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/sep/09/kim-jong-un-says-new-law-guarantees-north-korea-will-never-give-up-nuclear-weapons"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 state media has reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: Poorest areas have 26% greater air pollution than wealthy areas, US study shows\par \par \uc2 It has long been known that the poorest and those from minority ethnic communities shoulder the greatest burden from air pollution, and now a study {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/sep/09/poorest-areas-bear-brunt-air-pollution-us-study-finds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has provided compelling evidence}}}\uc2 . Researchers used sensors mounted on satellites and aircraft to map nitrogen dioxide across 11 major US cities. Researchers were able to map the pollution exposure well enough to compare with census data. The poorest areas in New York and Newark \u8211\'20\'13 defined as those with more than one-fifth of households below the poverty level \u8211\'20\'13 had air pollution about 26% greater than wealthier areas.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: Whispers, hours of uncertainty \u8211\'20\'13 then news of the death of the Queen\par \par \uc2 It was immediately obvious that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2022/sep/08/whispers-hours-of-uncertainty-then-news-of-the-death-of-the-queen"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 something grave was occurring}}}\uc2 , writes Dan Sabbagh. At Westminster, it was said that \u8220\'20\'1Cpeople with constitutional roles\u8221\'20\'1D had been told to prepare for the worst. An aide to one said they were engaged in a string of \u8220\'20\'1Cemergency calls\u8221\'20\'1D as official bodies went over their preparedness for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2017/mar/16/what-happens-when-queen-elizabeth-dies-london-bridge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Operation London Bridge}}}\uc2 , the plans for the death of Queen Elizabeth II. There were whispers and hours of uncertainty then the statement everybody had hoped not to hear: a 70-year reign was over.\par \par \uc2 Climate check: Rural Virginia pivots from coal to green jobs\par \par \uc2 In the past decade or so, unemployment and poverty have forced many to leave south-west Virginia as the coal industry\u8217\'20\'19s decline ricocheted across central Appalachia. It has torn many families apart and any talk of renewable energy was considered anti-coal, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/08/rural-virginia-pivots-from-coal-solar-green-jobs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attitudes are starting to change}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to get away from fossil fuels that are killing our planet. Technology has come a long way and will keep getting better. This is the future,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jimmy Rogers, 49, whose family worked on the coal trains in Tennessee.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/sep/08/world-on-brink-five-climate-tipping-points-study-finds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 World on brink of five \u8216\'20\'18disastrous\u8217\'20\'19 climate tipping points, study finds}}}\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: Queen\u8217\'20\'19s corgis tested palace loyalties\par \par \uc2 They were as emblematic of British royalty as the crown: Queen Elizabeth II\u8217\'20\'19s corgis, preceding her like a \u8220\'20\'1Cmoving carpet\u8221\'20\'1D wherever she was living, were the other royal dynasty to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2022/sep/09/queens-elizabeth-corgis-tested-palace-loyalties"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 inspire worldwide fascination}}}\uc2 . They featured in portraits, official photographs, on a golden jubilee Isle of Man crown, and were even immortalised in china. The Queen owned more than 30 corgis and dorgis (a corgi dachshund cross) but not everyone was so enamoured. Courtiers feared for their ankles while Prince Philip, heard often to exclaim: \u8220\'20\'1CBloody dogs. Why do you have so many?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220909ei99001h5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
