\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Revealed: Ginni Thomas\u8217\'20\'19s links to anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  groups who lobbied to overturn Roe\b0\par\par\uc2 Ed Pilkington in New York \par \uc2 1,683 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 September 2022\par 07:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Analysis of \u8216\'20\'18amicus briefs\u8217\'20\'19 shows how closely \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s wife was entwined with rightwing effort to reverse 1973 ruling\par \par \uc2 Ginni Thomas, the self-styled \u8220\'20\'1Cculture warrior\u8221\'20\'1D and extreme rightwing activist, has links to more than half of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups and individuals who lobbied her husband \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  and his fellow \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  justices ahead of their historic decision to eradicate a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to terminate a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 A new analysis of the written legal arguments, or \u8220\'20\'1Camicus briefs\u8221\'20\'1D, used to lobby the justices as they deliberated over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  underlines the extent to which \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s wife was intertwined with this vast pressure campaign.\par \par \uc2 The survey found that 51% of the parties who filed amicus briefs calling for an end to a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  right have political connections to Ginni Thomas, raising concerns about a possible conflict of interest at the highest levels of the US judiciary.\par \par \uc2 The six-to-three rightwing majority of the court, supercharged by Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s three appointed conservative justices, in June overthrew the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  was among the six who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted for the hotly contested ruling}}}\uc2 , Dobbs v Jackson.\par \par \uc2 The ruling was one of the most consequential in the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s 233-year history. It has triggered the lightning spread of partial or total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans across Republican-controlled states, affecting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/25/us-abortion-trigger-bans-laws-tennessee-texas-idaho"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 almost one in three women}}}\uc2  aged 15 to 44.\par \par \uc2 The Dobbs case, brought by Mississippi which sought to ban abortions after 15 weeks of pregnancy, attracted an almost unprecedented 130 amicus briefs from both sides of the legal argument. Of those, 74 were filed in favour of overturning the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , enshrined in 1973 in Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 In turn, the new analysis shows that 38 of the 74 anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  amicus briefs \u8211\'20\'13 51% \u8211\'20\'13 were produced by entities and individuals with links to Ginni Thomas. They included rightwing groups, religious interests, prominent conservative individuals and lawyers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Thomases are normalizing the prospect of too close an association between the supreme court and those who litigate before it,\u8221\'20\'1D said Melissa Murray, a law professor at \uc2 New York University\uc2  and co-host of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://strict-scrutiny.simplecast.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Strict Scrutiny podcast}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThis isn\u8217\'20\'19t the first time that Mrs Thomas has had dealings with those who come before the court and seek her husband\u8217\'20\'19s vote.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The revelation that there is substantial overlap between Ginni Thomas and the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lobbying effort focused on her husband and the other conservative justices will intensify the growing sense of unease surrounding her hyper-energetic conservative activism. In recent years she has placed herself in the thick of some of the most bitterly contested political controversies that have come \u8211\'20\'13 or could come \u8211\'20\'13 before the court.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, the New Yorker published an investigation into the mounting evidence of possible conflicts of interest under {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newyorker.com/magazine/2022/01/31/is-ginni-thomas-a-threat-to-the-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the headline}}}\uc2  : \u8216\'20\'18Is Ginni Thomas a threat to the supreme court?\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Thomas has been dubbed a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NormOrnstein/status/1507130939381583877"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 radical insurrectionist}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D for her role in backing Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attempt to subvert the 2020 presidential election. Yet her husband has refused to recuse himself from cases relating to the insurrection, including one in January in which he became the only justice to dissent in an 8-1 decision over allowing hundreds of documents held by the National Archives to be reviewed by the House committee investigating the January 6 storming of the US Capitol.\par \par \uc2 Five weeks after that decision, it was revealed that leading up to January 6 Ginni Thomas exchanged {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/mar/25/ginni-thomas-texts-clarence-ethics-supreme-court-conflict-of-interest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 29 text messages}}}\uc2  with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s White House chief of staff, \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , urging him to block Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s victory. It is very possible that those text messages were among the documents that the committee had been seeking, with \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  the sole justice opposing disclosure.\par \par \uc2 The January 6 committee has said it wants to interview Ginni Thomas over her anti-democratic antics around the 2020 election. Last week the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/investigations/2022/09/01/ginni-thomas-wisconsin-bernier-tauchen/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post revealed}}}\uc2  that she applied pressure on lawmakers in Wisconsin to block Biden\u8217\'20\'19s win, having previously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/investigations/2022/06/10/ginni-thomas-election-arizona-lawmakers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 done the same in Arizona}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The analysis of the amicus briefs was carried out by Advance Democracy Inc, a non-partisan organization specializing in public-interest research and investigations. It shared its findings with the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 They show an intricate web of connections between many of the most influential groups and figures on the conservative hard right, with Ginni Thomas at the centre of it. Several of the links run through {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2022/04/05/inside-the-consulting-firm-run-by-ginni-thomas-wife-of-supreme-court-justice-clarence-thomas.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 her consultancy}}}\uc2 , Liberty Consulting, which she set up in 2010 and which brags that it can \u8220\'20\'1Cgive access to any door in Washington\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Another {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/02/22/magazine/clarence-thomas-ginni-thomas.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 major route}}}\uc2  is through the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cfnp.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Council for National Policy}}}\uc2  (CNP), a secretive Christian conservative networking group that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2004/08/28/us/2004-campaign-conservatives-club-most-powerful-gathers-strictest-privacy.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times}}}\uc2  described as a \u8220\'20\'1Clittle-known club of a few hundred of the most powerful conservatives in the country\u8221\'20\'1D. The binding mission of the members is \u8220\'20\'1Climited government, strong national defense, and support for traditional western values\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Ginni Thomas is listed as a board director of the lobbying arm of the group, CNP Action, in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://documented.net/media/2020-cnp-action-990"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2020 tax filing}}}\uc2  obtained by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://documented.net/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 investigative watchdog Documented}}}\uc2 . In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://vimeo.com/470515080"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a speech to a CNP event}}}\uc2  in 2019 she described her role within the conservative movement as that of \u8220\'20\'1Ca convenor \u8211\'20\'13 I find the talent and I put them in the room and have them talk to one another\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A leaked {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/21409776-council-for-national-policy-meeting-program-february-24-26-%202022#document/p13/a2091417"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNP directory}}}\uc2  from this year lists as Thomas\u8217\'20\'19s fellow members several prominent conservatives involved in filing amicus briefs to the supreme court in the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case. They include Marjorie Dannenfelser, president of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group Susan B Anthony List, who led a discussion at a CNP conference in February titled: After Roe, Then What?\par \par \uc2 Leonard Leo\uc2 , the founder of the rightwing \uc2 Federalist Society\uc2 , with which \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  is intimately associated, sits on the board of the Ethics and Public Policy Center, which filed an amicus brief. Leo was arguably the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/04/leonard-leo-federalist-society-conservative-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 key strategist}}}\uc2  behind Trump\u8217\'20\'19s packing of the supreme court to obtain its current supermajority; he shares CNP membership with Ginni Thomas and is a close collaborator of hers.\par \par \uc2 Other CNP members who have been involved in filing amicus briefs in the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case include: Jay Sekulow, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former lawyer at his first impeachment trial, who is chief counsel for the American Center for Law & Justice; David Nammo of the Christian Legal Society; \uc2 Tony Perkins\uc2 , president of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 Family Research Council\uc2 ; Margaret Hartshorn, chair of Heartbeat International; and many more.\par \par \uc2 There are several other overlapping connections to the amicus briefs through separate networks such as Groundswell, a conservative advocacy group of which Ginni Thomas {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/5703586-Letter-to-Tim-Scott-defending-Thomas-Farr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 described herself as chairman}}}\uc2  in 2019. Groundswell was formed in 2013 to foment \u8220\'20\'1Ca 30-front war seeking to fundamentally transform the nation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 John Eastman, the conservative lawyer who is heavily implicated in the effort to block certification of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s presidential victory, filed an amicus brief in the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case on behalf of the Claremont Institute\u8217\'20\'19s center for constitutional jurisprudence, of which he was founding director. Eastman acted as law clerk to Justice Thomas in 1996 and has been described by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/02/22/magazine/clarence-thomas-ginni-thomas.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times}}}\uc2  as a \u8220\'20\'1Cclose friend\u8221\'20\'1D of Clarence and Ginni.\par \par \uc2 Thomas herself has denied any conflict of interest between her activism and her husband\u8217\'20\'19s jurisprudence. She told the Washington Free Beacon earlier this year: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have our own separate careers, and our own ideas and opinions too. Clarence doesn\u8217\'20\'19t discuss his work with me, and I don\u8217\'20\'19t involve him in my work.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Whether that is true is perhaps a moot point, given that the mere appearance of conflict of interest can in itself damage an institution\u8217\'20\'19s reputation. Already, the supreme court is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://mazon.com/Pioneer-SP-SB23W-Andrew-Soundbar-System/dp/B00EHBPF6W/ref=sr_1_1?ie=UTF8&qid=1482794563&sr=8-1&keywords=Pioneer+SP-SB23W"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 viewed unfavourably}}}\uc2  by 44% of the American people according to a \uc2 Pew Research Center\uc2  poll, with only 16% thinking they do an excellent or good job keeping their personal political views out of their decisions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe supreme court is unlike any other branch because it only has its legitimacy to make the public adhere to what it does. Lose that and the court loses the kind of institutional pull that makes the law come together and bind us,\u8221\'20\'1D Murray said.\par \par \uc2 Unlike all other federal judges in lower appeals and district courts who are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.uscourts.gov/judges-judgeships/code-conduct-united-states-judges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 obliged to recuse themselves}}}\uc2  in cases of potential conflict of interest involving their spouses, the nine justices of the supreme court are entirely unfettered by any code of judicial ethics. They in effect police themselves.\par \par \uc2 Every year \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  has to file a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fixthecourt.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Thomas-C-J3.-SC_SR_20.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 financial disclosure,}}}\uc2  but the detail given is minimal. He lists under his spouse\u8217\'20\'19s income \u8220\'20\'1CLiberty Consulting, Inc \u8211\'20\'13 salary and benefits\u8221\'20\'1D, but does not reveal her clients or her board positions on groups such as CNP or Groundswell.\par \par \uc2 The lack of controls have led to a rising chorus {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fixthecourt.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/Scholars-letter-to-CJ-Roberts-2.3.22.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calling for reform}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CAt the very least the justices need to adopt a formal code of conduct that they commit to following,\u8221\'20\'1D said Gabe Roth, executive director of the non-partisan group {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fixthecourt.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fix the Court}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThat code would take on board potential conflicts of interests involving their spouses.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ginni Thomas\u8217\'20\'19s ties with groups responsible for the whirlwind lobbying campaign over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  could have serious ramifications in future cases that come before the court. \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  made it clear in his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/22067323-dobbs-v-jackson-womens-health-organization-clarence-thomas-concurrence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 concurring opinion}}}\uc2  in Dobbs that he intends to use exactly the same arguments that were deployed in overthrowing Roe v Wade to challenge the constitutional right to same-sex marriage, same-sex relations and contraception.\par \par \uc2 Many of the interests to which Ginni Thomas was connected who filed anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  amicus briefs have a parallel track record of anti-LGBT agitating. The founder of CNP, Tim LaHaye, was an evangelical Christian minister and a virulent homophobe.\par \par \uc2 His 1978 book The Unhappy Gays depicted gay people as \u8220\'20\'1Cmilitant, organized\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cvile\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CHomosexuality is a blight on humanity,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CMany parents would prefer the death of their child to his adopting the unhappy wretchedness of homosexuality.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220909ei9900132\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
