\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Nuclear secrets reportedly found at Mar-a-Lago are \u8216\'20\'18gamechanger\u8217\'20\'19, experts say \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Sam Levin (now) and Richard Luscombe (earlier) \par \uc2 7,415 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 September 2022\par 23:45 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Report appears to confirm security officials\u8217\'20\'19 worst fears about the nature of the material Trump refused to hand backSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.16am BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s all for today, thanks for following along. Some key links and developments from the day:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  reported that a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2022/09/06/trump-nuclear-documents/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 foreign power\u8217\'20\'19s nuclear secrets}}}\uc2  were among classified documents found by the \uc2 FBI\uc2  at former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s Florida residence.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Former \uc2 FBI\uc2  deputy director \uc2 Andrew McCabe\uc2  said the revelation showed federal agents \u8220\'20\'1Cabsolutely had to go in\u8221\'20\'1D to retrieve the intelligence, while Shawn Turner, former director of communications for US national intelligence, said knowledge Trump was hoarding classified nuclear documents was a \u8220\'20\'1Cgamechanger with regard to the risk it poses to our national security\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago resort and residence in Palm Beach, Florida, is a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/07/mar-a-lago-trump-nuclear-documents-spies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 magnet for foreign spies}}}\uc2 , former intelligence officials have warned.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Barack and \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  returned to the White House for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/07/barack-michelle-obama-white-house-unveiling-portraits"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unveiling of their official portraits}}}\uc2 . The former president paid tribute to his successor \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , while the former first lady said the unveiling showed \u8220\'20\'1Cthere\u8217\'20\'19s a place for everyone in this country\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Former Trump administration defense secretaries \uc2 Jim Mattis\uc2  and \uc2 Mark Esper{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/07/trump-nuclear-document-special-master-biden-obama-bannon-latest?page=with:block-6318c4038f08d2b5fa6d9903#block-6318c4038f08d2b5fa6d9903"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have joined}}}\uc2  a group of retired military officers who have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://warontherocks.com/2022/09/to-support-and-defend-principles-of-civilian-control-and-best-practices-of-civil-military-relations/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 written an open letter}}}\uc2  warning of an \u8220\'20\'1Cextremely adverse environment\u8221\'20\'1D for the military \u8211\'20\'13 a thinly-veiled attack on the former president\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to use servicemen and women to advance his political goals.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Massachusetts is on course to elect its first woman and first gay governor after Maura Healey{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/09/06/us/politics/maura-healey-massachusetts-governor.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won}}}\uc2  the Democratic primary on Tuesday and a Trump-backed candidate, \uc2 Geoff Diehl\uc2 , won the Republican contest to face her.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A federal judge in Texas {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/07/texas-employers-hiv-prevention-prep-drugs-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled today}}}\uc2  that employers can refuse to cover HIV infection prevention drugs.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/07/michigan-1931-anti-abortion-law-judge-strikes-down"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struck down Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s 1931 anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  law}}}\uc2 , months after suspending it.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.39am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 A US senator has dismissed an Israeli army report that claims a soldier accidentally killed the Palestinian American journalist Shireen Abu Aqleh in the midst of a gun battle, saying it is unsupported by the evidence, my colleague Chris McGreal reports:\par \par \uc2 Chris Van Hollen\uc2 , a Democratic senator for Maryland, repeated his call for an independent US investigation into Abu Aqleh\u8217\'20\'19s killing in the West Bank in May, saying that the United Nations and reconstructions by major news outlets found that the Al Jazeera television journalist was not in the immediate vicinity of fighting with Palestinian militants and could not have been caught in the crossfire.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, more than four months after her killing, Israel finally admitted it was \u8220\'20\'1Chighly probable\u8221\'20\'1D that an Israeli soldier shot Abu Aqleh while she was reporting on a military raid on the occupied West Bank city of Jenin.\par \par \uc2 The report said Abu Aqleh was probably shot by an Israeli soldier who was under fire from a group of Palestinian gunmen. It claimed the soldier was using a telescopic sight and misidentified her as one from his armed opponents. The army said no crime was committed so no one will be prosecuted.\par \par \uc2 However, eyewitness accounts and videos of Abu Aqleh and the area around her at the time of her killing do not show a gun battle. She was also wearing body armour and a helmet clearly labelled as \u8220\'20\'1Cpress\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-briefing-notes/2022/06/killing-journalist-occupied-palestinian-territory"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 United Nations investigation}}}\uc2  said that Israeli soldiers fired \u8220\'20\'1Cseveral single, seemingly well-aimed bullets\u8221\'20\'1D at Abu Aqleh and other journalists.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe crux of the \u8220\'20\'1Cdefense\u8221\'20\'1D in this \uc2 IDF\uc2  report is that a soldier was \u8220\'20\'1Creturning fire\u8221\'20\'1D from militants. But investigations {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nytimes?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @NYTimes}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AP?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @AP}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CNN?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @CNN}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/washingtonpost?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @washingtonpost}}}\uc2  & {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UN?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @UN}}}\uc2  found no such firing at the time. This underscores need for independent US inquiry into this American journalist\u8217\'20\'19s death. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vblvL5Euha"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/vblvL5Euha}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senator \uc2 Chris Van Hollen\uc2  (@ChrisVanHollen) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChrisVanHollen/status/1566943549924458496?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 6, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/07/shireen-abu-aqleh-us-senator-rejects-israeli-army-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US senator rejects Israeli army report on killing of Palestinian American reporter}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.31am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 A federal judge in Texas ruled today that employers can refuse to cover HIV infection prevention drugs if they claim that it violates their religious beliefs. My colleague {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/07/texas-employers-hiv-prevention-prep-drugs-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maya Yang reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 US district judge \uc2 Reed O\u8217\'20\'19Connor\uc2  on Wednesday ruled in favor of Braidwood Management, a Christian-owned company based in Texas, saying it was not required to cover the cost of Truvada and Descovy, two pre-exposure prophylactic drugs also known as PrEP.\par \par \uc2 The drugs, which are taken every day by hundreds of thousands of Americans, are used to prevent HIV transmission and are made available through company health insurance via provisions for preventive healthcare in the Affordable Care Act (ACA).\par \par \uc2 A lawsuit filed by the conservative former Texas solicitor general Jonathan Mitchell on behalf of Braidwood Management against the US Department of Health and Human Services argued that the ACA provision \u8220\'20\'1Cviolated [the plaintiffs\u8217\'20\'19] religious beliefs by making them complicit in facilitating homosexual behavior, drug use, and sexual activity outside of marriage between one man and woman\u8221\'20\'1D, in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.txnd.330381/gov.uscourts.txnd.330381.92.0_2.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 words of the judge}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mitchell is also known for designing Texas\u8217\'20\'19s highly restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law.\par \par \uc2 O\u8217\'20\'19Connor ruled in favor of the company.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDefendants outline a generalized policy to combat the spread of HIV, but they provide no evidence connecting that policy to employers such as Braidwood, nor do they provide evidence distinguishing potential religious exemptions from existing secular exemptions,\u8221\'20\'1D O\u8217\'20\'19Connor said in his ruling.\par \par \uc2 Some additional context here:\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: US District Judge \uc2 Reed O\u8217\'20\'19Connor\uc2  in Texas rules that requiring employers to provide coverage for PrEP drugs (preventing the transmission of HIV) violates the religious rights of employers under federal law (RFRA). {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/d85C3izqSF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/d85C3izqSF}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chris \u8220\'20\'1CSubscribe to Law Dork!\u8221\'20\'1D Geidner (@chrisgeidner) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/chrisgeidner/status/1567523876451614720?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 7, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 And the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/07/texas-employers-hiv-prevention-prep-drugs-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas judge rules employers not required to cover HIV prevention drugs}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Judge strikes down Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s 1931 anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law\par \par \uc2 A judge today struck down a 1931 anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law in Michigan, months after suspending it, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CA law denying safe, routine medical care not only denies women of their ability to control their bodies and their lives \u8211\'20\'13 it denies them of their dignity. Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s Constitution forbids this violation of due process.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The law had long been inactive prior to the overturning of Roe v Wade and made it illegal to perform abortions unless there was a life-threatening emergency.\par \par \uc2 Judge Elizabeth Gleicher said the law \u8220\'20\'1Ccompels motherhood\u8221\'20\'1D, prevents a woman from determining the \u8220\'20\'1Cshape of her present and future life\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cforces a pregnant woman to forgo her reproductive choices and to instead serve as \u8216\'20\'18an involuntary vessel entitled to no more respect than other forms of collectively owned property\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor praised the ruling, but warned it was likely to be challenged and said there were \u8220\'20\'1Cextremists who will stop at nothing to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  even in cases of rape and incest\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrToday, the courts ruled once again Michigan women have the right to make medical decisions for themselves.\par \par \uc2 However, this decision is likely to be challenged, and we know that there are extremists who will stop at nothing to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  even in cases of rape and incest.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Governor \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  (@GovWhitmer) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GovWhitmer/status/1567621981868101635?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 7, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The decision comes amid an ongoing court battle that will determine whether another {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/sep/01/michigan-abortion-elections-panel-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  measure}}}\uc2  is on the ballot before voters in Michigan this year.\par \par \uc2 The full story on Gleicher\u8217\'20\'19s decision:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/07/michigan-1931-anti-abortion-law-judge-strikes-down"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Judge strikes down Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s strict 1931 anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  law}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hi all, Sam Levin here in Los Angeles taking over our live coverage for the rest of the day.\par \par \uc2 A new report suggests that hundreds of US law enforcement officers, elected officials and military personnel were listed on leaked documents as members of the Oath Keepers, a far-right extremist group {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/01/oath-keepers-lawyer-charged-with-conspiracy-january-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 linked}}}\uc2  to the January 6 insurrection.\par \par \uc2 The Anti-Defamation League Center on Extremism reviewed 38,000 leaked names on a membership list of the group and said it identified more than 370 people believed to be active members of police agencies, in addition to more than 100 people currently in the military, the AP reports. The review also identified more than 80 people running for office or currently serving as elected officials as of this summer. The list included sheriffs and police chiefs, the AP said.\par \par \uc2 Some of the officials contacted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/oath-keepers-leaked-membership-rolls-2ca4195ed3a10e45dd189bf98f3e5a26"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by the AP}}}\uc2  responded they were members years ago but were no longer active.\par \par \uc2 In recent years, there has been escalating concerns about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/16/us-capitol-riot-police-neo-nazis-far-right"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 links between police departments and far-right extremist groups}}}\uc2  in the US, a problem that was widely scrutinized after the insurrection, where off-duty officers were present.\par \par \uc2 Last week, a retired New York police officer received the longest sentence yet for his involvement in the attack on the Capitol, during which he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/01/retired-nypd-officer-capitol-attack-longest-sentence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 assaulted an officer with a flagpole}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The full story on the Oath Keepers leak:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/07/oath-keepers-membership-rolls-police-military-elected-officials"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oath Keepers membership rolls feature police, military and elected officials}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Certain prominent legal experts aren\u8217\'20\'19t pulling their punches this afternoon, already skeptical of the ruling by the federal judge in Florida granting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s request to have a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/07/why-did-judge-grant-special-master-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 special master}}}\uc2  interrupt and oversee the Department of Justice\u8217\'20\'19s review of documents seized by the \uc2 FBI\uc2  from the former president\u8217\'20\'19s residence at Mar-a-Lago.\par \par \uc2 Harvard\u8217\'20\'19s Laurence Tribe, as pithy as usual, has quote tweeted former federal prosecutor Andrew Weissmann over what needs to happen next in the court case \u8211\'20\'13 and not long after.\par \par \uc2 enltrA good list. I'd offer a friendly amendment to item 2:\par \par \uc2 2. Indict Trump before this December. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Zl4GiT3v2B"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Zl4GiT3v2B}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Laurence Tribe (@tribelaw) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/tribelaw/status/1567560906317381633?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 7, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Tribe wrote for the Guardian today that the ruling two days ago on the special master by Aileen Cannon, the federal judge in West Palm Beach, \u8220\'20\'1Chas to rank high in the annals of the worst reasoned judicial decisions in American history\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He warns: \u8220\'20\'1CIf it signals that judicial Trumpism has spread more broadly than we thought, there may be danger ahead to our entire system of equal justice.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Tribe wrote the piece with former federal prosecutor Dennis Aftergut and you can read the rest of it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/sep/07/the-trump-special-master-ruling-violates-the-principle-that-no-one-is-above-the-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Tribe also notes that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general Bill Barr has called Cannon\u8217\'20\'19s ruling \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mediaite.com/tv/bill-barr-rips-deeply-flawed-ruling-by-trump-appointed-judge-says-the-law-is-pretty-clear/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deeply flawed}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D. (Barr also called it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/07/why-did-judge-grant-special-master-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Ca crock of shit\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .)\par \par \uc2 But he adds in a tweet: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m glad Bill Barr is making the rounds on his \u8220\'20\'1Cdismantle Trump\u8221\'20\'1D tour, but if it\u8217\'20\'19s a \u8220\'20\'1Crehabilitate Barr\u8221\'20\'1D tour, count me out.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrI'm glad Bill Barr is making the rounds on his "dismantle Trump" tour, but if it's a "rehabilitate Barr" tour, count me out... {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ELnloUmIn2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/ELnloUmIn2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Laurence Tribe (@tribelaw) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/tribelaw/status/1567559715713949699?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 7, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The rehab tour started in earnest with the main round of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jan-6-hearings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 6 hearings}}}\uc2 , and no matter what it does or doesn\u8217\'20\'19t do for Barr, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/13/jan-6-house-committee-second-hearing-conspiracy-theories"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his testimony}}}\uc2  to that House committee\u8217\'20\'19s inquiry did a lot for the congressional investigation itself (as well as for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/09/ivanka-trump-election-not-stolen-testimony"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ivanka Trump\u8217\'20\'19s view}}}\uc2  of who won the 2020 election, apparently).\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House: 'no calls to foreign governments to read out' over Trump nuclear discovery\par \par \uc2 Reporters at the White House press briefing are wondering if the US has had contact with any other countries over the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2022/09/06/trump-nuclear-documents/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported discovery}}}\uc2  of a foreign power\u8217\'20\'19s nuclear secrets among classified documents hoarded by ex-president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  speaks to reporters on Wednesday. Photograph: Patrick Semansky/AP\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  is sticking closely to her previous position of flat-out refusing to comment on the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s investigation into Trump\u8217\'20\'19s handling of secret material, but does say this:\par \par \uc2 We don\u8217\'20\'19t have any calls to foreign governments to read out at this time on this particular issue as known.\par \par \uc2 When it comes to this specific issue, the ODNI [office of the director of national intelligence] is in the middle of an assessment, and DoJ [justice department] is in the middle of an ongoing criminal investigation. So I\u8217\'20\'19m not going to comment.\par \par \uc2 It should be noted that Jean-Pierre is not saying no such calls have taken place, nor is she saying they have. She\u8217\'20\'19s just saying that she has nothing that she can share.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ve hopped across the White House from the East Room to the briefing room, to join press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Monkeypox is first on the agenda. Robert Fenton, White House national monkeypox response coordinator, says the country has ample supplies of vaccines to supply the most at-risk.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur focus is to reach the remainder of the eligible population where they are,\u8221\'20\'1D he says, citing the success of thousands of doses being administered over the weekend at pride events in Louisiana, Georgia and elsewhere.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese events demonstrate our strategy is working.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Dr Demetre Daskalakis, deputy response coordinator, says the population at highest risk is largely men who have sex with other men.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s important people know a safe and effective vaccine is available for those who need it,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s important we speak to the community in a way that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t stigmatize them. [The virus] doesn\u8217\'20\'19t distinguish between people based on their sexual orientation or gender.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2 : 'There\u8217\'20\'19s a place for everyone in this country'\par \par \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s speech from her portrait unveiling at the White House is worth a read. The day, the former first lady said, belongs not to her or \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , and it\u8217\'20\'19s not even about the paintings:\par \par \uc2 Too often in this country, people feel like they have to look a certain way or act a certain way to fit in. They have to make a lot of money, or come from a certain group or class or faith in order to matter.\par \par \uc2 But what we\u8217\'20\'19re looking at today, a portrait of a biracial kid with an unusual name and the daughter of a water pump operator and a stay at home mom, what we are seeing is a reminder that there\u8217\'20\'19s a place for everyone in this country.\par \par \uc2 Because, as Barack said, if the two of us can end up on the walls of the most famous address in the world, it is so important for every young kid who is doubting themselves to believe that they can too.\par \par \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  speaks at the White House on Wednesday. Photograph: Andrew Harnik/AP\par \par \uc2 That is what this country is about. It\u8217\'20\'19s not about blood or pedigree or wealth. It\u8217\'20\'19s a place where everyone should have a fair shot. Whether you\u8217\'20\'19re a kid taking two buses and a train just to get to school, or a single mother who\u8217\'20\'19s working two jobs to put some food on the table.\par \par \uc2 Or an immigrant, just arriving, getting your first apartment, forging a future for yourself in a place you dreamed of.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s why for me this day isn\u8217\'20\'19t about me or Barack. It\u8217\'20\'19s not even about these beautiful paintings. It\u8217\'20\'19s about telling that fuller story, a story that includes every single American in every single corner of the country so that our kids and grandkids can see something more for themselves.\par \par \uc2 And as much as some folks might want us to believe that that story has lost some of its shine, that division, and discrimination and everything else might have dimmed its light, I still know deep in my heart, that what we share, as my husband continues to say, is so much bigger than what we don\u8217\'20\'19t.\par \par \uc2 Our democracy is so much stronger than our differences.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has tweeted about his \u8220\'20\'1Cold pals act\u8221\'20\'1D at the White House on Wednesday, the vice-president turned president greeting his former boss \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  and former first lady \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  for the unveiling of their portraits.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSomeone once said that if you\u8217\'20\'19re looking for a friend in Washington get a dog,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Obama\uc2  said during his speech in the East Room.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur family was lucky enough to have two wonderful dogs. But I was even luckier to have a chance to spend eight years working day and night with a man who became a true partner and a true friend.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJoe, it is now America\u8217\'20\'19s good fortune to have you as president\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrBarack and Michelle, welcome back. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/wcdBvfMcGg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/wcdBvfMcGg}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1567586398504370179?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 7, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Intelligence officials: Trump residence 'a magnet for spies'\par \par \uc2 Mar-a-Lago \u8211\'20\'13 the Palm Beach resort and residence where \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/26/redacted-trump-mar-a-lago-affidavit-fbi-takeaways"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly stored nuclear secrets}}}\uc2  among a trove of highly classified documents for 18 months since leaving the White House \u8211\'20\'13 is a magnet for foreign spies, former intelligence officials have warned.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2022/09/06/trump-nuclear-documents/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post}}}\uc2  reported that a document describing an unspecified foreign government\u8217\'20\'19s defences, including its nuclear capabilities, was one of the many highly secret papers Trump took away from the White House when he left office in January 2021.\par \par \uc2 n aerial view of former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's Mar-a-Lago club in Palm Beach, Florida. Photograph: Steve Helber/AP\par \par \uc2 There were also documents marked SAP, for Special-Access Programmes, which are often about US intelligence operations and whose circulation is severely restricted, even among administration officials with top security clearance.\par \par \uc2 Potentially most disturbing of all, there were papers stamped HCS, Humint Control Systems, involving human intelligence gathered from agents in enemy countries, whose lives would be in danger if their identities were compromised.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/national-security/intel-officials-will-assess-risk-national-security-documents-found-tru-rcna45112"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Office of the Director of National Intelligence}}}\uc2  is conducting a damage assessment review which is focused on the sensitivity of the documents, but US officials said it is the job of \uc2 FBI\uc2  counter-intelligence to assess who may have gained access to them.\par \par \uc2 That is a wide field. The home of a former president with a history of being enthralled by foreign autocrats, distrustful of US security services, and boastful about his knowledge of secrets, is an obvious foreign intelligence target.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI know that national security professionals inside government, my former colleagues, [they] are shaking their heads at what damage might have been done,\u8221\'20\'1D John Brennan, former CIA director, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=L5zJF2YgIz4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told MSNBC.}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m sure {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/mar-a-lago"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mar-a-Lago}}}\uc2  was being targeted by Russian intelligence and other intelligence services over the course of the last 18 or 20 months, and if they were able to get individuals into that facility, and access those rooms where those documents were and made copies of those documents, that\u8217\'20\'19s what they would do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  also thanked artists Robert McCurdy and Sharon Sprung for their respective portraits of himself and \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe captures every wrinkle of your face, every crease of your shirt, [and] you\u8217\'20\'19ll note he refused all of my requests to make my ears smaller,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe also talked me out of wearing a tan suit, by the way,\u8221\'20\'1D he added to laughter and applause, a nod to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/gallery/2014/aug/29/yes-we-tan-barack-obama-suit-in-pictures"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 social media firestorm he created back in 2014}}}\uc2  when he wore one.\par \par \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  unveils his and former first lady \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2 's official White House portraits. Photograph: Evelyn Hockstein/Reuters\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat you realize when you\u8217\'20\'19re sitting behind that desk, and what I want people to remember about Michelle and me, is that presidents and first ladies are human beings.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve always described the presidency as a relay race. You take the baton from someone, you run your leg as hard and as well as you can, and then you hand it off to someone else, knowing that your work will be incomplete.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe portraits hanging in the White House chronicle the runners in that race.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Obama\uc2 : America's 'good fortune' to have Biden as president\par \par \uc2 Having unveiled his portrait, \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  is now paying tribute to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , saying it is \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica\u8217\'20\'19s good fortune\u8221\'20\'1D to have him as president:\par \par \uc2 You have guided us through some perilous times, you have built on and gone beyond the work we all did together to expand healthcare, to fight climate change, to advance social justice and to promote economic fairness.\par \par \uc2 Thanks to you our faith in our democracy and the American people, the country is better off than when you took office.\par \par \uc2 He also acknowledged his aides, staffers and colleagues from his time in the White House. Many are in the audience in the East Room:\par \par \uc2 For eight years, even longer for some of you, I drew on your energy and dedication and your goodness. You inspired me and I never wanted to disappoint you.\par \par \uc2 Even during the toughest times it was all of you that kept me going. It\u8217\'20\'19s good to be back and see all of you\u8230\'20\'26what\u8217\'20\'19s been a special joy to see what\u8217\'20\'19s happened since.\par \par \uc2 [But] I am a little disappointed I haven\u8217\'20\'19t heard anyone naming a kid Barack yet.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COr Michelle\u8230\'20\'26\u8221\'20\'1D the former first lady interjected from beside him.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is acknowledging \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  as his inspiration for everything he does as president.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at the official unveiling of the former president and first lady, \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2 , at the White House, Biden said:\par \par \uc2 With Barack as our president we got up every day and went to work full of hope, for real, full of purpose, and excited about the possibility before us.\par \par \uc2 Few people I\u8217\'20\'19ve ever known have more integrity, decency, and moral courage than \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mr President, nothing could have prepared me better, and more, to become president of the United States than to be your side for eight years. I mean it from the bottom of my heart.\par \par \uc2 No matter what the issue was, no matter how difficult, no matter what it was about, you never did what it was the easy way, the easy way out. It was never about doing it that way, it was always about doing what was right.\par \par \uc2 To that end, Biden cited \uc2 Obama\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s signature achievement, passage of the Affordable Care Act, nicknamed Obamacare, which survived a bumpy passage and overcame Republican opposition in the Senate to become law:\par \par \uc2 He never gave up on the simple truth that health care was a right for all Americans when so many were telling him, including me at one point, take the compromise, take the compromise\u8230\'20\'26 we weren\u8217\'20\'19t sure we get anything done.\par \par \uc2 You refused. You went big. And now the Affordable Care Act is there permanently and it\u8217\'20\'19s even being improved.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here are the portraits:\par \par \uc2 enltrJUST UNVEILED: The official {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WhiteHouse?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @WhiteHouse}}}\uc2  portraits of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BarackObama?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @BarackObama}}}\uc2  & {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MichelleObama?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @MichelleObama}}}\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dDTxblOe5e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/dDTxblOe5e}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Peter Alexander (@PeterAlexander) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PeterAlexander/status/1567569680268673025?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 7, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden unveils White House portraits of Barack and \uc2 Michelle Obama\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is speaking at the White House, where he is unveiling the official portraits of former first lady \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2 , and 44th president \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , whom he served as vice-president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBarack and Michelle, welcome home,\u8221\'20\'1D the president began.\par \par \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , followed by former first lady \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  and first lady Jill Biden, arrive for a ceremony to unveil the Obamas\u8217\'20\'19 official White House portraits. Photograph: Mandel Ngan/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://youtu.be/PCnEBtru3dU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a video interview}}}\uc2  with the portraits\u8217\'20\'19 artists, Robert McCurdy and Sharon Sprung.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 New York state is ending a 28-month-old Covid-19 mandate requiring masks on trains, buses and other modes of public transit, governor \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  said at a news conference today, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Starting today masks will be optional. We have to restore some normalcy to our lives...Masks are encouraged but optional,\u8221\'20\'1D Hochul said, citing recent revised guidance from the \uc2 US Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC)\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 New York first adopted the mandate in April 2020 as Covid-19 was rampaging in the New York City area.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s always been a visible reminder that something is not normal here, and it was there for the right reason. It protected health and now we\u8217\'20\'19re in a far different place,\u8221\'20\'1D Hochul said.\par \par \uc2 In April, the Biden administration decided to no longer enforce a US mask mandate on public transportation after a federal judge in Florida ruled the directive was unlawful. New York declined to adopt the Biden policy in April.\par \par \uc2 In recent months, many riders in New York had stopped observing the mask policy.\par \par \uc2 Hochul said masks will still be required in some places like adult care facilities and some other medical facilities.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Justice Department\uc2  appealed the Florida judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling invalidating the transportation mask mandate, but a federal appeals court has not yet set the case for oral arguments.\par \par \uc2 Passengers riding the New York City subway in mid-April. Photograph: Spencer Platt/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been a lively morning in US political news and there\u8217\'20\'19s more to come. The unveiling at the White House of the official portraits of Barack and \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  is just ahead, with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in attendance, and the White House press briefing with \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  follows not long after that. We\u8217\'20\'19ll be watching for any other significant breaking news and will bring it to you as it happens.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Former Trump administration defense secretaries \uc2 Jim Mattis\uc2  and \uc2 Mark Esper{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/07/trump-nuclear-document-special-master-biden-obama-bannon-latest?page=with:block-6318c4038f08d2b5fa6d9903#block-6318c4038f08d2b5fa6d9903"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have joined}}}\uc2  a group of retired military officers who have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://warontherocks.com/2022/09/to-support-and-defend-principles-of-civilian-control-and-best-practices-of-civil-military-relations/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 written an open letter}}}\uc2  warning of an \u8220\'20\'1Cextremely adverse environment\u8221\'20\'1D for the military \u8211\'20\'13 a thinly-veiled attack on the former president\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to use servicemen and women to advance his political goals.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Andrew McCabe\uc2 , former deputy director of the FBI{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/07/trump-nuclear-document-special-master-biden-obama-bannon-latest?page=with:block-6318b5038f082daedc5f5c6c#block-6318b5038f082daedc5f5c6c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 says federal agents}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cabsolutely had to go in\u8221\'20\'1D to retrieve highly classified documents from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s private residence relating to the nuclear secrets of a foreign power.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s legal jeopardy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/07/trump-nuclear-document-special-master-biden-obama-bannon-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-6318ac038f08d2b5fa6d979b#block-6318ac038f08d2b5fa6d979b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could be heightened}}}\uc2  by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/06/donald-trump-mar-a-lago-documents-nuclear-weapons-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported discovery}}}\uc2  of a foreign nation\u8217\'20\'19s nuclear secrets among his hoard of improperly retained classified materials, some experts believe.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The reported discovery of information about a foreign nation\u8217\'20\'19s nuclear secrets in materials found at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s private residence in the \uc2 FBI\uc2  search last month is horrifying intelligence experts. The legal and security situation was already extremely serious and the further revelation has been called \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/sep/07/trump-nuclear-document-special-master-biden-obama-bannon-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-63189e088f082daedc5f5b13#block-63189e088f082daedc5f5b13"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a gamechanger}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Massachusetts is on course to elect its first woman and first gay governor after \uc2 Maura Healey{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/09/06/us/politics/maura-healey-massachusetts-governor.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won}}}\uc2  the Democratic primary on Tuesday and a Trump-backed candidate, \uc2 Geoff Diehl\uc2 , won the Republican contest to face her.\par \par \uc2 Maura Healey\uc2 . Photograph: Chris Christo/AP\par \par \uc2 Healey, the state attorney general, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/maura_healey?lang=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CI am honored to receive the Democratic nomination \u8230\'20\'26 Together, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to win in November and build a Massachusetts that works for everyone.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Massachusetts has a long record of electing moderate Republicans. Only one Democrat \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Deval Patrick\uc2 , from 2007 to 2015 \u8211\'20\'13 has been governor since 1991.\par \par \uc2 Healey, a former college and professional basketball player, has been attorney general since 2015. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/governor/2022/massachusetts/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Polls}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fivethirtyeight.com/features/massachusetts-governor-2022/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 give}}}\uc2  her huge leads over Diehl.\par \par \uc2 The Republican {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=k22n1CiMbbU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 backs}}}\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lie that his defeat by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in the 2020 election was the result of electoral fraud, opposed the extension of mail-in voting, opposed public health mandates in the Covid pandemic and supports the supreme court decision overturning Roe v Wade, the 1973 ruling that guaranteed the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue alone has driven electoral successes that have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  hoping they can prosper in the midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, Trump \u8211\'20\'13 the de facto leader of a party dominated by supporters Biden has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/26/biden-trump-republicans-fascism-speech-maryland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Csemi-fascist\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/09/06/massachusetts-primary-governor-attorney-general/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  Massachusetts Republicans that Diehl would push back against \u8220\'20\'1Cultra-liberal extremists\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Crule your state with an iron fist\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Full-story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/07/maura-healey-woman-gay-massachusetts-governor-geoff-diehl-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Massachusetts set to elect first female, gay governor over Trumpist opponent}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former Trump administration defense secretaries \uc2 Jim Mattis\uc2  and \uc2 Mark Esper\uc2  have joined a group of retired military officers who have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://warontherocks.com/2022/09/to-support-and-defend-principles-of-civilian-control-and-best-practices-of-civil-military-relations/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 written an open letter}}}\uc2  warning of an \u8220\'20\'1Cextremely adverse environment\u8221\'20\'1D for the military \u8211\'20\'13 a thinly-veiled attack on the former president\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to use servicemen and women to advance his political goals.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMilitary officers swear an oath to support and defend the Constitution, not an oath of fealty to an individual or to an office,\u8221\'20\'1D the letter, published by the online security analysis website War on the Rocks, states.\par \par \uc2 Former defense secretary \uc2 Jim Mattis\uc2  with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Photograph: Jim Young/Reuters\par \par \uc2 It is signed by eight former secretaries of defense, serving both Republican and Democratic administrations, and five retired generals or admirals who are former chairs of the Joint Chiefs of Staff, including Martin Dempsey, who served in the \uc2 Obama\uc2  administration from 2011 to 2015.\par \par \uc2 The letter does not mention Trump by name, but refers to a \u8220\'20\'1Cdisruption\u8221\'20\'1D in the transfer of power from one administration to the other. Trump is the only president in modern history to fail to acknowledge his successor\u8217\'20\'19s victory and commit to handing over his administration peacefully.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPolitically, military professionals confront an extremely adverse environment characterized by the divisiveness of affective polarization that culminated in the first election in over a century when the peaceful transfer of political power was disrupted and in doubt,\u8221\'20\'1D the letter says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLooking ahead, all of these factors could well get worse before they get better.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Polling oracle FiveThirtyEight has calculated that more than 50% of US voters will have an election denier somewhere on the ballot during November\u8217\'20\'19s midterms.\par \par \uc2 Researchers drew on \u8220\'20\'1Cnews reports, debate footage, campaign materials and social media and reached out to every single Republican nominee for the House, Senate, governor, secretary of state and attorney general to determine their position on the 2020 election\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrCandidates who support former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s false claims that the 2020 election was stolen will appear on ballots in nearly every state this fall. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/huF3dyvfcK"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/huF3dyvfcK}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 FiveThirtyEight (@FiveThirtyEight) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FiveThirtyEight/status/1567332336311615488?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 7, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Of 529 total Republican nominees running for office, FiveThirtyEight found 195 it says fully denied the legitimacy of the 2020 election by either stating the election was stolen from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , or taking legal action to overturn the results including voting not to certify election results or joining lawsuits that sought to overturn the election.\par \par \uc2 You can {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/republicans-trump-election-fraud/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 find their research here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  will reunite with his former vice-president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  at the White House at lunchtime when the 44th US president and his wife Michelle return for the unveiling of their official portraits.\par \par \uc2 Large, formal portraits of presidents and first ladies adorn walls, hallways and rooms throughout the White House and, customarily, a former president returns for the unveiling during his successor\u8217\'20\'19s tenure.\par \par \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  at the White House in April. Photograph: Carolyn Kaster/AP\par \par \uc2 But the Obamas, who have remained popular since leaving the political limelight, did not have their ceremony while \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  held power, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/07/barack-michelle-obama-white-house-unveiling-portraits"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this Reuters report states}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Before winning election in 2016 and succeeding \uc2 Obama\uc2  in 2017, Trump was a longtime proponent of the \u8220\'20\'1Cbirther\u8221\'20\'1D movement that falsely suggested \uc2 Obama\uc2  was not born in the US.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for \uc2 Obama\uc2  declined to comment on the timing of the Obamas\u8217\'20\'19 portrait unveilings.\par \par \uc2 The White House Historical Association president, Stewart McLaurin, said there was no prescribed process for presidential portraits.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s really up to the current president in the White House and the former president that is portrayed in the portrait to determine the right moment, but there is no set timeline,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Obama\uc2  hosted former president \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  and his wife, Laura, for their portrait unveilings in 2012, during \uc2 Obama\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s first term.\par \par \uc2 The Obamas and Bidens became close during \uc2 Obama\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidency, going through the ups and downs of their political and personal lives, including the death of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s son, Beau, from cancer.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 McCabe: \uc2 FBI\uc2  'absolutely had to go in' to recover nuclear document\par \par \uc2 The former deputy director of the \uc2 FBI\uc2  says federal agents \u8220\'20\'1Cabsolutely had to go in\u8221\'20\'1D to retrieve highly classified documents from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s private residence relating to the nuclear secrets of a foreign power.\par \par \uc2 Andrew McCabe\uc2 , whom {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2018/mar/16/andrew-mccabe-former-fbi-director-fired-russia-inquiry"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump fired}}}\uc2  in 2018 before the justice department {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2021/10/14/1039690679/andrew-mccabe-lawsuit-trump-fbi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reversed the decision}}}\uc2  last year, also said the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/06/donald-trump-mar-a-lago-documents-nuclear-weapons-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported discovery}}}\uc2  dispelled claims from the former president\u8217\'20\'19s legal team that it had been openly negotiating the return of hoarded documents to the National Archives.\par \par \uc2 Andrew McCabe\uc2 . Photograph: Alex Brandon/AP\par \par \uc2 McCabe told CNN on Wednesday:\par \par \uc2 The seriousness of the documents eliminates any question about whether or not the department and the \uc2 FBI\uc2  actually had to go in with a search, which at the time was perceived as this overly aggressive move taken out of the blue, without any sort of appropriate wind up.\par \par \uc2 Of course, we now know that that\u8217\'20\'19s not true. We know that the parties were not negotiating in good faith. We know that the folks on the Trump team were misleading the government\u8230\'20\'26 [and] resisted the return of these documents for basically a year and a half.\par \par \uc2 Knowing what was in there, they absolutely have to go in and recover this material. It\u8217\'20\'19s essential to national security.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Top former Trump strategist {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/steve-bannon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Steve Bannon}}}\uc2  is expected to be indicted on Thursday on state fraud charges connected to his role in a fundraising scheme to build a border wall, according to two sources familiar with the matter, years after he received a presidential pardon in the federal case.\par \par \uc2 The expected move by the Manhattan district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office was quietly communicated to Bannon in recent days, the sources said of the sealed indictment, and indicated the state charges will likely mirror the federal case in which he was pardoned.\par \par \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 . Photograph: Alex Brandon/AP\par \par \uc2 Bannon and three others were charged in that case by federal prosecutors in Manhattan with falsely claiming that they would not take compensation in the private \u8220\'20\'1CWe Build the Wall\u8221\'20\'1D fundraising effort to underwrite part of the construction of the wall on the US-Mexico border.\par \par \uc2 The architect of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  2016 election campaign and later White House adviser was accused of personally taking more than $1m from what people had donated to the fundraising push that promised to secure funding in order to ensure the completion of the border wall.\par \par \uc2 Bannon \u8211\'20\'13 alongside disabled veteran Brian Kolfage, Andrew Badolato and Timothy Shea \u8211\'20\'13 raised more than $25m in the online crowdfunding effort, which also promised donors that all of the proceeds would go towards constructing the wall.\par \par \uc2 Though Bannon pleaded not guilty to the federal charges in August 2020, two others, Kolfage and Badolato, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/22/two-plead-guilty-fraud-we-build-the-wall-project-trump-bannon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pleaded guilty to siphoning off money}}}\uc2  from the scheme and defrauding others for their own gain.\par \par \uc2 Bannon received a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/20/donald-trump-pardons-steve-bannon-amid-last-acts-of-presidency-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 last-minute pardon}}}\uc2  in the final days of the Trump administration that expunged the federal indictment. But presidential pardons do not apply to state-level charges.\par \par \uc2 The Manhattan district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office started examining whether to pursue a case against Bannon almost immediately after he received the pardon, one source with knowledge of the matter said, and several close Bannon allies were subpoenaed to testify before a grand jury in recent months.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/07/steve-bannon-to-be-indicted-on-fresh-charges-over-border-wall-sources"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Steve Bannon to be indicted on fresh fraud charges over border wall \u8211\'20\'13 sources}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Experts: 'No good way' for Trump to spin nuclear revelations\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s legal jeopardy could be heightened by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/06/donald-trump-mar-a-lago-documents-nuclear-weapons-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported discovery}}}\uc2  of a foreign nation\u8217\'20\'19s nuclear secrets among his hoard of improperly retained classified materials, some experts believe.\par \par \uc2 Michael Moore, former US attorney for Georgia, was asked on CNN if the finding could provide the justice department \u8211\'20\'13 which is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/15/donald-trump-mar-a-lago-search-justice-department"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conducting a criminal investigation}}}\uc2  into the former president\u8217\'20\'19s handling of secret documents \u8211\'20\'13 with more evidence to bring charges:\par \par \uc2 I really think that\u8217\'20\'19s probably the case. The documents that they had dealing with national defense may have been enough as it was under the Espionage Act, [which] doesn\u8217\'20\'19t really require classified materials to be held and stolen. It [only] required defense information.\par \par \uc2 This information about nuclear capabilities and defense is particularly troubling to me, and there\u8217\'20\'19s no good way to spin it for the [ex]-president. The three blind mice would say that he\u8217\'20\'19s in trouble with this at this point.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, Moore added, the apparent leaking to the media about the content of the papers seized by the \uc2 FBI\uc2  in their search of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago residence in Florida last month had \u8220\'20\'1Cjustified\u8221\'20\'1D one aspect of his legal defense:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m worried about is how the news is getting information about what the documents are. It seems to me that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/07/why-did-judge-grant-special-master-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s request for a special master}}}\uc2  is justified, because somebody somewhere is leaking information about the specifics of these highly classified, highly sensitive documents.\par \par \uc2 That may change the dynamics, not just on the criminal side, but also the legal side.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senior Democrats, intelligence experts and retired senior military officers are among those offering thoughts this morning on the alleged {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2022/09/06/trump-nuclear-documents/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 discovery of a foreign power\u8217\'20\'19s nuclear secrets}}}\uc2  at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Florida residence.\par \par \uc2 Adam Schiff, representative for California and chair of the House intelligence committee:\par \par \uc2 enltrNew reporting that Trump had highly classified information, including on foreign nuclear programs.\par \par \uc2 If true, it raises yet more questions.\par \par \uc2 Why would Trump take them to Mar-a-Lago?\par \par \uc2 Why did he refuse to return them?\par \par \uc2 The investigation must continue uninterrupted and unimpeded.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Adam Schiff (@RepAdamSchiff) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepAdamSchiff/status/1567326054431485954?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 7, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Mark Hertling, retired \uc2 US Army\uc2  lieutenant general and national security analyst:\par \par \uc2 enltrNB (note bene): this is just the beginning\u8230\'20\'26and it\u8217\'20\'19s gonna get much, much worse.\par \par \uc2 Special Access Programs (SAP), TS/SCI, NOFORN\u8230\'20\'26some of our most closely guarded secrets.\par \par \uc2 Yeah, this is more than a \u8220\'20\'1Cstorage problem,\u8221\'20\'1D ? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/marcorubio?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @marcorubio}}}\uc2  ? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/NtCzAY3L8I"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/NtCzAY3L8I}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Mark Hertling (@MarkHertling) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MarkHertling/status/1567320428397355008?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 7, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Democratic congressman for California, \uc2 Ted Lieu\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 enltrDonald Trump was, and remains, a U.S. national security disaster.\par \par \uc2 Anyone else in America holding highly classified nuclear information at their residence would have been arrested and indicted. And Trump as ex-President doesn\u8217\'20\'19t even have a security clearance. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/HtfX27ro9x"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/HtfX27ro9x}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Ted Lieu\uc2  (@tedlieu) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/tedlieu/status/1567344556240404480?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 7, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 John W Dean, White House counsel for \uc2 Richard Nixon\uc2  during Watergate crisis:\par \par \uc2 enltrDonald Trump is a serious threat to the national security of the United States...\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 John W. Dean (@JohnWDean) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JohnWDean/status/1567326729093652480?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 7, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Key event\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  doesn\u8217\'20\'19t seem too concerned that information about a foreign nation\u8217\'20\'19s nuclear capabilities was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2022/09/06/trump-nuclear-documents/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly found}}}\uc2  at his Florida mansion.\par \par \uc2 The former president, according to a post on his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/108957155977977709"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 troubled Truth Social network}}}\uc2  this morning, would seem to indicate he\u8217\'20\'19s more worried by federal agents having sight of his medical records.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt least they\u8217\'20\'19ll see that I\u8217\'20\'19m very healthy, an absolutely perfect physical specimen!\u8221\'20\'1D wrote Trump, who has a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/oct/03/trump-covid-flip-flop-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 questionable history}}}\uc2  at best over claims about his weight and overall health.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Photograph: Justin Lane/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNot only did the \uc2 FBI\uc2  steal my Passports in the \uc2 FBI\uc2  Raid and Break-In of my home, Mar-a-Lago, but it has just been learned through court filings that they also improperly took my complete and highly confidential medical file and history, with all the bells and whistles.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPlus personal Tax Records (Illegal to take), and lawyer/client/privileged information, a definite NO, NO. Days of the Soviet Union!\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Nuclear secrets at Trump residence 'a gamechanger'\par \par \uc2 The reported discovery of information about a foreign nation\u8217\'20\'19s nuclear secrets in materials found at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s private residence is horrifying intelligence experts.\par \par \uc2 Federal agents seized the document during their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/02/trump-fbi-search-materials-list-fbi-latest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 search of Mar-a-Lago}}}\uc2 , the former president\u8217\'20\'19s Palm Beach mansion in Florida, last month, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2022/09/06/trump-nuclear-documents/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Washington Post reported}}}\uc2 . It appears to confirm officials\u8217\'20\'19 worst fears about the nature of the intelligence he should have returned to the National Archives.\par \par \uc2 Shawn Turner, former director of communications for US national intelligence, was searing in his criticism during an interview Wednesday on CNN\u8217\'20\'19s New Day:\par \par \uc2 The fact we now know there were highly classified, restricted access documents about another country\u8217\'20\'19s nuclear defense capabilities stored at Mar-a-Lago is a gamechanger with regard to the risk it poses to our national security.\par \par \uc2 That these documents may have been seen by unauthorized personnel \u8230\'20\'26 tells individuals what our capabilities are with regard to intelligence collection related to nuclear programs.\par \par \uc2 More important is it identifies or exposes our gaps with regard to intelligence collection.\par \par \uc2 The bottom line is others are going to look at this information and determine what we know and don\u8217\'20\'19t know, and they\u8217\'20\'19re going to make decisions about their nuclear programs based on that information. And that is an extremely dangerous thing.\par \par \uc2 The Post\u8217\'20\'19s reporting is only the latest twist in a weeks-long saga over the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s investigation into his handling of classified materials after he left office in January 2021.\par \par \uc2 Trump, who is mulling another run for the presidency in 2024, attacked the department {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/04/trump-rally-fbi-doj-vicious-monsters-mar-a-lago-search"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at a weekend rally}}}\uc2  where he called the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and DoJ \u8220\'20\'1Cvicious monsters\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Many others, including Trump\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/03/william-barr-trump-mar-a-lago-fbi-justice-department"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 former attorney general, William Barr}}}\uc2 , have defended the investigation into his retention of government records, saying that it posed a major national security risk.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/06/donald-trump-mar-a-lago-documents-nuclear-weapons-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FBI found document on foreign nuclear defenses at Mar-a-Lago \u8211\'20\'13 report}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Good morning US politics blog readers! Wednesday begins with another extraordinary development in the saga of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s hoarding of classified documents at his Florida residence.\par \par \uc2 Among the papers found by the \uc2 FBI\uc2  during a search last month was one describing a foreign government\u8217\'20\'19s nuclear capabilities, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2022/09/06/trump-nuclear-documents/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post}}}\uc2  reported. It would appear to confirm security officials\u8217\'20\'19 worst fears about the nature of the material the former president refused to hand back to the National Archives.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll be watching for reaction.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s also increasing scrutiny and growing criticism of the judge in the case, Trump appointee Aileen Cannon, who made the decision to appoint an independent special master to review the evidence in the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s inquiry.\par \par \uc2 Some legal scholars question the legitimacy of the unprecedented decision, saying it places Trump above the law. Bill Barr, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former attorney general, was more succinct, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/09/02/us/politics/barr-trump-special-master.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 telling the New York Times}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a crock of shit.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re watching today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former senior strategist who is already awaiting sentencing for contempt of Congress after refusing to cooperate with the January 6 trial, is expected to be indicted on fraud charges relating to a fundraising scheme.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Barack and \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  return to the White House at 1.30pm for the unveiling of their official portraits, hosted by Joe and Jill Biden.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Victory by \uc2 Geoff Diehl\uc2 , a Trump-supporting election denier, in Massachusetts\u8217\'20\'19 Republican primary could pave the way for an openly gay Democrat Maura Healy to become state governor in November\u8217\'20\'19s midterms.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , is scheduled to deliver her daily briefing at 2.45pm.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220907ei970020c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
