\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Republican Senate candidate says she\u8217\'20\'19s anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  but against federal ban\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang \par \uc2 580 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 September 2022\par 19:04 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Tiffany Smiley, a trained nurse, wants to win in Washington state, where a 1991 law protects \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access\par \par \uc2 A Republican Senate nominee in Washington state said on Sunday she was against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 but supported a state law that guarantees the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  until fetal liability.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to CNN\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union, Tiffany Smiley said she supported the law despite the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  decision earlier this summer, in Dobbs v Jackson, which overturned the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a right previously guaranteed for almost 50 years.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI respect the voters of Washington state,\u8221\'20\'1D Smiley said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey long decided where they stand on the issue.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The state law was passed in 1991. Across the US, polls consistently show that nearly two-thirds of Americans support the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in some form.\par \par \uc2 As the midterm elections approach, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has served as a prime motivator for women voters across the US, especially among Democrats and fueling {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/03/mary-peltola-alaska-congress-interview-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 striking special-election successes}}}\uc2  for the party seeking to hold both houses of Congress.\par \par \uc2 Smiley\u8217\'20\'19s remarks reflected a growing recognition among Republicans that the fall of Roe v Wade, the 1973 ruling which protected the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  until June this year, may have been a longed-for supreme court success but could cost them dearly at the polls as they seek to take the House and Senate.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to CNN, Smiley also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/videos/politics/2022/09/04/tiffany-smiley-washington-gop-candidate-sotu-vpx.cnn/video/playlists/this-week-in-politics/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  backed off}}}\uc2  her previous statement that she would welcome an endorsement from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am laser-focused on the endorsement of the voters of Washington state,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, twice, as she sought to deflect the question.\par \par \uc2 Smiley, a trained nurse, is challenging the incumbent Democratic senator, \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2 , who has criticized Smiley for her \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://host2.adimpact.com/admo/viewer/aa751805-2913-4ad3-8622-fb44bead19a6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 100% pro-life\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  views.\par \par \uc2 In an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=t5lAs4l-Sr8&ab_channel=SmileyforWashington"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  ad}}}\uc2  released last week, Smiley told viewers she was \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-life but I opposed a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\u8221\'20\'1D. The ad came in response to a Murray {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://host2.adimpact.com/admo/viewer/aa751805-2913-4ad3-8622-fb44bead19a6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ad}}}\uc2  which called Smiley \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s hand-picked candidate\u8221\'20\'1D, referring to the Senate Republican leader known for his anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  views and push to stack the supreme court with conservative justices opposed to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Murray\u8217\'20\'19s ad claimed that if elected, Smiley would support federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. Smiley said: \u8220\'20\'1CMurray is trying to scare you, I am trying to serve you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On Sunday, Smiley said: \u8220\'20\'1CI made it clear in my ad that \u8230\'20\'26 I am not for a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. You know, the extreme in this race is \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2 . She is for federalizing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Smiley previously expressed support for a Texas law that implements a near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, the Hill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/573524-texas-abortion-law-creates-2022-headache-for-the-gop/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  last year. On Sunday, Smiley said \u8220\'20\'1Cthere\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of parts of [the Texas ban] that make it very hard for me in Washington state\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She added: \u8220\'20\'1CBut at the end of the day, I\u8217\'20\'19m pro-woman first and then always pro-life.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In response, Murray told CNN: \u8220\'20\'1CWhat I believe is that we have a constitutional right in this country under Roe by the supreme court that allowed women and their families and their faith and their doctor to make a decision for them about whether or not they should carry their pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat is what the law and constitutional right of this land was, until this supreme court overturned that.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI do not believe that politicians should be making these decisions for women. That is what I support.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220904ei940020a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
