\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden speech: \u8216\'20\'18Democracy is under assault\u8217\'20\'19 from election deniers and political violence, president warns - as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh \par \uc2 2,866 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 September 2022\par 02:59 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The president called out Maga forces as a threat \u8216\'20\'18to our personal rights, to the pursuit of justice, to the very soul of this country\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.34am BST\par \par \uc2 Key takeaways\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s all from us tonight.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  spoke for just over 20 minutes tonight, offering a rare primetime address that forecasted the midterm elections as a battle for the nation\u8217\'20\'19s soul. In what very much came across as a campaign speech, the president stuck a dark, stern tone \u8211\'20\'13 building on a new, more direct approach he\u8217\'20\'19s recently taken in attacking \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his allies.\par \par \uc2 Here are some key takeaways:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Speaking in front of Philadelphia\u8217\'20\'19s Independence Hall \u8211\'20\'13 where the Declaration of Independence and the US constitution were signed \u8211\'20\'13 back lit in red, white and blue, and played on and off by the Marine band playing anthems from the 1800s \u8211\'20\'13 the night really played up patriotism. \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica is an idea,\u8221\'20\'1D he said at one point, flanked by Marines at parade rest. \u8220\'20\'1CThe most powerful idea in the history of the world.\u8221\'20\'1D Throughout his address, Biden evoked the founding ideals of the country, and aligned himself with them \u8211\'20\'13 casting Trump and extremist Republicans as an existential threat to the nation. \u8220\'20\'1CI know your hearts. And I know our history,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, addressing the \u8220\'20\'1CAmerican people\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a nation that honors our constitution,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The president issued stern warnings that the integrity of American elections was vulnerable. Condemning Trump and other Republicans who have denied the legitimacy of the 2020 elections \u8211\'20\'13 and have threatened to do so in the midterms, Biden asked Americans to join him in resisting election misinformation and the rollback of voting rights. \u8220\'20\'1CWe can\u8217\'20\'19t let the integrity of our elections be undermined,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe can\u8217\'20\'19t allow violence to be normalized in this country,\u8221\'20\'1D he added, referencing the January 6 insurrection.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden \u8211\'20\'13 who usually makes couched references to \u8220\'20\'1Cthe former guy\u8221\'20\'1D and his \u8220\'20\'1Cpredecessor\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 explicitly named and called out \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  tonight. Trump and the \u8220\'20\'1CMaga (Make America great again)\u8221\'20\'1D Republicans \u8220\'20\'1Crepresent an extremism that threatens the very foundation of our republic\u8221\'20\'1D, Biden said. Hedging that \u8220\'20\'1Cnot every Republican\u8221\'20\'1D is an extremist, he added: \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s no question that the Republican party today is dominated, driven and intimidated by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D The president even made reference to the commotion surrounding the Justice Department\u8217\'20\'19s discovery that Trump was holding on to classified documents \u8211\'20\'13 something he\u8217\'20\'19s largely avoided discussing. Biden\u8217\'20\'19s directness tonight was a culmination of a new, aggressive approach he\u8217\'20\'19s taken recently in aiming to marginalize Trump\u8217\'20\'19s agenda.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden also touted his and Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 policy goals, urging Americans to \u8220\'20\'1Cvote, vote, vote\u8221\'20\'1D. The speech tonight was presented as an official address \u8211\'20\'13 but it also very much came off as a campaign appeal. During a jarringly optimistic segment in an otherwise dark speech, Biden touted reforming healthcare, combatting climate change and addressing the Covid-19 pandemic. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve never been more optimistic about America\u8217\'20\'19s future,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to end cancer as we know it. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to create millions of new jobs in the clean energy economy. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to think big, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to make the 21st century another American century.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden may have missed an opportunity to highlight outrage over the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to revoke the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The issue energized Democrats ahead of the midterm, and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates have expressed frustration at Biden and other Democrats for not speaking more directly and forcefully about it. Biden did mention that \u8220\'20\'1CMaga Republicans\u8221\'20\'1D want to take the country \u8220\'20\'1Cbackwards to an America where there is no right to choose. No right to privacy. No right to contraception.\u8221\'20\'1D But he lost a chance to play the issue up as an urgent example of rights at stake.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.43am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.58am BST\par \par \uc2 The scenes from tonight\u8217\'20\'19s speech\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  delivered his primetime speech at Independence National Historical Park in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania. Photograph: Alex Wong/Getty Images \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and the first lady Jill Biden walk out as military members stand by. Photograph: Jonathan Ernst/Reuters Biden spoke on \u8216\'20\'18the continued battle for the soul of the nation\u8217\'20\'19. Photograph: Alex Wong/\uc2 Getty Images\uc2  Earlier in the day, the presidential helicopter Marine One lifted off from the White House bound for Philadelphia. Photograph: Susan Walsh/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.20am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.04am BST\par \par \uc2 One quick note just for my UK readers \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 You may have been confused as to why God Save the Queen was playing as Biden walked off the stage. Some of my British colleagues certainly were.\par \par \uc2 What you actually heard was the American patriotic song My Country, Tis of Thee. It was written by Samuel Francis Smith in 1831 \u8211\'20\'13 and is sung to the same melody as God Save the Queen.\par \par \uc2 As an American editor said, \u8220\'20\'1CGuess we\u8217\'20\'19re united in more ways than one!\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.17am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.53am BST\par \par \uc2 One thing that was conspicuously missing from the speech tonight: the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In recent weeks, public backlash against the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to revoke the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has energized Democrats ahead of the midterm. Biden did mention that \u8220\'20\'1CMaga Republicans\u8221\'20\'1D want to take the country \u8220\'20\'1Cbackwards to an America where there is no right to choose. No right to privacy. No right to contraception.\u8221\'20\'1D He also mentioned that the right to marriage equality was under threat.\par \par \uc2 (In concurring opinion in the case that resulted in the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  being overturned, Justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  wrote that the rights to same-sex marriage and the right for couples to use contraception should be reconsidered.)\par \par \uc2 But \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates have expressed frustration at Biden and other Democrats for not speaking about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  more directly and forcefully, given that the majority of Americans support the right \u8211\'20\'13 and the issue has proved to be energizing in the primaries so far.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.21am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.40am BST\par \par \uc2 This sort of prime time address from the president is rare. But it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear what its impact will be.\par \par \uc2 Several major networks did not cary the broadcast. NBC showed Law and Order, \uc2 CBS\uc2  aired Young Sheldon, and ABC had Press Your Luck on.\par \par \uc2 And then there was Fox News, which seemed to jump the gun a bit:\par \par \uc2 enltrit... hasn't happened yet? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zCPIQ1X30w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/zCPIQ1X30w}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1565490080780779521?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 2, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.43am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.36am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech has concluded.\par \par \uc2 Stay tuned for more analysis and reflections from me and the Guardian politics team.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.44am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.35am BST\par \par \uc2 Thee second half of the speech struck an entirely different tone, evoking Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 successes and goals in reforming healthcare, combatting climate change and addressing the Covid-19 pandemic:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ve never been more optimistic about America\u8217\'20\'19s future\u8230\'20\'26 We\u8217\'20\'19re going to end cancer as we know it. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to create millions of new jobs in the clean energy economy. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to think big we\u8217\'20\'19re going to make 21st century another American Century.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.49am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.32am BST\par \par \uc2 Protesters outside Independence Hall were shouting \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s go, Brandon,\u8221\'20\'1D which Biden was able to brush off.\par \par \uc2 Biden addressed them, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re entitled to be outrageous. This is a democracy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 And followed with a quip that such protestors have never suffered from \u8220\'20\'1Cgood manners\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.44am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.27am BST\par \par \uc2 And there it is: \u8220\'20\'1CI ran for president because I believe we\u8217\'20\'19re in a battle for the soul of this nation. I still believe that to be true,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said , in a speech that is seeming very much like a campaign speech.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica is defined by the sacred proposition that all are created equal in the image of God, that all are entitled to be treated with decency, dignity and respect that all deserve justice in a shot at lives are a consequence,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CDemocracy makes all these things possible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo matter what the white supremacists and extremists say,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden continued, \u8220\'20\'1CI made a bet on you, the American people, and that bet is paying off.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The president also evoked the \u8220\'20\'1Cdarkness\u8221\'20\'1D of the Charlottesville white nationalist rally that he has said upset him so much, it compelled him to run for president.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.46am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.21am BST\par \par \uc2 Raising his voice, Biden warns that \u8220\'20\'1Cwe can\u8217\'20\'19t let the integrity of our elections be undermined\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 adding that doing so leads down a \u8220\'20\'1Cpath to chaos\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDemocracy endures only if we the people respect the guardrails of the Republic,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 The tone has so far been stern, and dark. \u8220\'20\'1CThroughout our history, Americans often made the greatest progress coming out of some of our darkest moments,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said \u8211\'20\'13 transitioning.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.21am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.14am BST\par \par \uc2 Invoking his \u8220\'20\'1Csoul of the nation\u8221\'20\'1D theme from his presidential campaign, Biden says that Maga forces \u8220\'20\'1Care determined to take this country backwards. Backwards to an America where there is no right to choose. No right to privacy. No right to contraception, no right to marry.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 These forces \u8220\'20\'1Cpromote authoritarian leaders and they fan the flames of political violence\u8221\'20\'1D are a threat \u8220\'20\'1Cto our personal rights, to the pursuit of justice, to the rule of law, to the very soul of this country\u8221\'20\'1D, he continues.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.15am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.10am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs I stand here tonight, equality and democracy are under assault,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden dives in. \u8220\'20\'1CWe do ourselves no favor to pretend otherwise. So tonight, I\u8217\'20\'19ve come to this place where it all began to speak as plainly as I can to the nation, about the threats we face, about the power we have in our own hands to meet these threats, and about the incredible future that lies in front of us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Hedging that \u8220\'20\'1Cnot every Republican\u8221\'20\'1D is an extremist, he singles out \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Maga Republicans\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The president has historically avoided calling out Trump by name \u8211\'20\'13 often couching references to his \u8220\'20\'1Cpredecessor\u8221\'20\'1D. But in recent appearances, he has struck a more aggressive tone, and willingness to more directly attack Trump and Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Trump and his supporters represents an \u8220\'20\'1Cextremism that threatens the foundations of our Republic\u8221\'20\'1D, he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.13am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.05am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden begins primetime address\par \par \uc2 Biden has begun his address from outside Philadelphia\u8217\'20\'19s Independence Hall, where the Declaration of Independence and Constitution were signed.\par \par \uc2 Walking out to the tune of Hail to the Chief, Biden began: \u8220\'20\'1CI speak to you tonight from sacred ground in America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.10am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.48am BST\par \par \uc2 And just in: the January 6 committee is requesting testimony from Newt Gingrich, a Trump ally and former House speaker.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://january6th.house.gov/sites/democrats.january6th.house.gov/files/2022-9-1.BGT%20letter%20to%20Gingrich%20Final.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In a letter sent today,}}}\uc2  the committee said it is interested in emails between Gingrich and former Trump senior advisers, including Trump\u8217\'20\'19s son-in-law \uc2 Jared Kushner\uc2 , that the committee said provided input on advertisements repeating election lies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese advertising efforts were not designed to encourage voting for a particular candidate. Instead, these efforts attempted to cast doubt on the outcome of the election after voting had already taken place,\u8221\'20\'1D committee chairman \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2 ,wrote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey encouraged members of the public to contact their state officials and pressure them to challenge and overturn the results of the election. To that end, these advertisements were intentionally aired in the days leading up to December 14, 2020, the day electors from each state met to cast their votes for president and vice-president.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.59am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.33am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech on threats to democracy comes as investigations into \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and the January 6 insurrection intensify.\par \par \uc2 Two former Trump White House lawyers \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Pat Cipollone\uc2  and Patrick Philbin, will be testifying this week before a grand just investigating the insurrection. The House January 6 select committee is continuing its digging, interviewing senior Trump officials. Once its investigation concludes, the decision over whether to file criminal charges against Trump will be made by the \uc2 US Department of Justice\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile the South Carolina Republican senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  will also have to testify before the special grand jury in Georgia in a criminal case related to allegations that Trump illegally attempted to overturn the state\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 presidential election results.\par \par \uc2 Moreover, my colleague {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levine}}}\uc2  reported earlier today:\par \par \uc2 Trump said he would pardon and apologize to those who participated in the deadly attack on the US Capitol on January 6 if he were elected to the White House again.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI mean full pardons with an apology to many,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2022/09/01/trump-jan-6-rioters-pardon/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  he told Wendy Bell}}}\uc2 , a conservative radio host on Thursday. \u8220\'20\'1CI will be looking very, very strongly about pardons, full pardons.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Five people died in connection with the attack and more than 140 law enforcement officers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/US/numbers-jan-investigation-shaping-year/story?id=82057743"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 were injured}}}\uc2 . More than 875 people have been charged with crimes related to January 6, according to an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2021/02/09/965472049/the-capitol-siege-the-arrested-and-their-stories#database"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NPR tracker.}}}\uc2  370 people have pleaded guilty to crimes so far.\par \par \uc2 Trump also said he was offering financial support to some of those involved in the attack. \u8220\'20\'1CI am financially supporting people that are incredible and they were in my office actually two days ago, so they\u8217\'20\'19re very much in my mind,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a disgrace what they\u8217\'20\'19ve done to them. What they\u8217\'20\'19ve done to these people is disgraceful.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It was not immediately clear what the extent of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s financial assistance was.\par \par \uc2 The former president has indicated he plans to run again in 2024.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.40am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.04am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden will be delivering his speech from Philadelphia, Pennsylvania \u8211\'20\'13 where American democracy was born.\par \par \uc2 Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s primetime speech is the second of three visits by the president in less than a week to battleground Pennsylvania, home to several consequential races this election season.\par \par \uc2 In the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  race, Mehmet Oz, the Trump-backed heart surgeon turned celebrity doctor, is squaring off against the state\u8217\'20\'19s lieutenant governor, Democrat \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 , in a contest that could determine which party controls the chamber, evenly divided at present.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Democrats have warned about the risks of \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2 , the far-right Republican nominee for governor, a leading figure in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn the results of the 2020 election in Pennsylvania who helped shuttle people on 6 January to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Washington DC rally that preceded the attack on the US capitol.\par \par \uc2 In Pennsylvania, the governor appoints the secretary of state, giving the next governor enormous sway over how the 2024 presidential election is conducted in the state. Mastriano faces Democrat \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2 , Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general.\par \par \uc2 In a speech not far from Biden\u8217\'20\'19s birthplace of Scranton, Pennsylvania, on Tuesday, the US president lashed out at \u8220\'20\'1CMaga Republicans in Congress\u8221\'20\'1D over their attacks on the \uc2 FBI\uc2  after agents seized boxes of classified documents from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago estate last month. The remarks were designed to counter Republican attacks on Democrats as \u8220\'20\'1Csoft on crime\u8221\'20\'1D, with Biden casting his opponents\u8217\'20\'19 rhetoric as a threat to law enforcement and the rule of law.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe idea you turn on a television and see senior senators and congressmen saying, \u8216\'20\'18If such and such happens there\u8217\'20\'19ll be blood on the street\u8217\'20\'19?\u8221\'20\'1D he said in Wilkes-Barre. \u8220\'20\'1CWhere the hell are we?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.04am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden will deliver a rare primetime address on threats to American democracy\par \par \uc2 Good evening, and welcome to the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s US politics liveblog, primetime edition.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll be bringing you live updates and analysis tonight, as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  addresses the country. The president is expected to speak about threats to American democracy, and \u8220\'20\'1Cthe power we have in our own hands to meet those threats\u8221\'20\'1D, according to excerpts of his speech that the White House has shared with the media.\par \par \uc2 In recent weeks, Biden has unleashed an uncharacteristically energetic, aggressive line of attack against Republicans allied with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and the party\u8217\'20\'19s willingness to erode democratic rights and personal freedoms.\par \par \uc2 As my colleague Lauren Gambino {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/01/biden-speech-philadelphia-extremist-republicans-threaten-democracy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 , Biden is expected to evoke a battle for the \u8220\'20\'1Csoul of the nation\u8221\'20\'1D, reviving a theme from his presidential campaign, and build on public backlash against the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to end the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s our main report on the night ahead:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/01/biden-speech-philadelphia-extremist-republicans-threaten-democracy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden to warn \u8216\'20\'18extremist\u8217\'20\'19 Republicans loyal to Trump threaten US democracy }}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220901ei910035z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
