\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump search affidavit reveals potential for \u8216\'20\'18evidence of obstruction\u8217\'20\'19 at Mar-a-Lago \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang and Martin Pengelly in New York and Chris Stein in Washington \par \uc2 6,072 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 August 2022\par 11:43 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Heavily redacted document also says several documents contained what appear to be Trump\u8217\'20\'19s handwritten notesSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 It has been a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/26/doj-redacted-trump-affidavit-mar-a-lago-search"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 day of drama}}}\uc2  as the redacted affidavit explaining why the \uc2 FBI\uc2  chose to raid \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago residence was finally published to an eagerly awaiting world. It wasn\u8217\'20\'19t exactly a damp squib. The document \u8211\'20\'13 much of which was blanked out \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/26/doj-redacted-trump-affidavit-mar-a-lago-search"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 detailed }}}\uc2  the huge numbers of secret documents squirreled away and security risks they posed.\par \par \uc2 But due to the large numbers of redactions there was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/26/doj-redacted-trump-affidavit-mar-a-lago-search"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 no explosive new line}}}\uc2 , though one thing does seem certain: this \uc2 FBI\uc2  investigation is just getting started and has a long long way to go.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett\uc2  was in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/26/amy-coney-barrett-faith-group-people-of-praise"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the news via a Guardian US scoop }}}\uc2  showing that a faith group she has been closely associated with places huge emphasis on female obedience.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and his administration {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/26/biden-trump-republicans-fascism-speech-maryland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stood by}}}\uc2  his calling out of the Republican politicians as behaving like semi-fascists. The move drew ire from the rightwing party.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Washington is to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/26/washington-gas-car-ban-sales"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 follow the path}}}\uc2  of its fellow west coast state California and pursue the eventual ban of sales of new gasoline-powered cars.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A Jim Crow-era provision of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/mississippi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mississippi}}}\uc2  constitution designed to disfranchise Black voters is constitutional, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/26/mississippi-jim-crow-era-felony-voting-law-constitutional-federal-court-rules"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a federal appellate court ruled}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Dow drops 1,000 points\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Dominic Rushe writes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/aug/26/fed-inflation-jerome-powell-job-losses-jackson-hole"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here }}}\uc2  that there has been a steep drop on Wall Street in response to the latest forecasts on the economy from \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  chief \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A 1,000 plus point {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/aug/26/fed-inflation-jerome-powell-job-losses-jackson-hole"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drop}}}\uc2  is hardly a catastrophe but it is definitely a nasty fall.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/aug/26/fed-inflation-jerome-powell-job-losses-jackson-hole"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dominic writes}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 US stock markets nosedived on Friday after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/federal-reserve"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Federal Reserve}}}\uc2  chair, \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2 , warned of \u8220\'20\'1Cpain\u8221\'20\'1D ahead as the central bank struggles to bring down inflation from a 40-year high.\par \par \uc2 Powell\u8217\'20\'19s highly anticipated speech was more hawkish than had been expected, with the Fed chair pledging to do all he could to end rising prices. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/dowjones"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dow Jones}}}\uc2  Industrial Average lost just over 1,000 points, 3%, the S&P fell 3.3% and the Nasdaq dropped almost 4%.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at the \uc2 Kansas City Fed\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s annual meeting of the world\u8217\'20\'19s central bankers in Jackson Hole, Wyoming, Powell said the Fed\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Coverarching focus right now is to bring inflation back down\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/aug/26/fed-inflation-jerome-powell-job-losses-jackson-hole"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dow plunges 1,000 points after Fed chief Powell warns of inflation \u8216\'20\'18pain\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley for 2024?\par \par \uc2 The former \uc2 UN\uc2  ambassador under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is often mentioned as a potential 2024 candidate and someone who could \u8211\'20\'13 potentially \u8211\'20\'13 straddle the two disparate and often bitterly feuding worlds of Trump and non-Trump Republicans.\par \par \uc2 That sees Haley frequently seek to a perform a difficult dance between courting her old bosses\u8217\'20\'19 favor, but also trying not to seem too close to him.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/08/26/donors-secretly-funded-nikki-haleys-nonprofit-00053963"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico}}}\uc2  has the details of some of the people donating to her political future and it makes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/08/26/donors-secretly-funded-nikki-haleys-nonprofit-00053963"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interesting reading}}}\uc2  of a long list of Republican stalwarts.\par \par \uc2 The report says: \u8220\'20\'1CMany of the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s biggest donors are among those who funneled anonymous contributions to former U.N ambassador Nikki Haley\u8217\'20\'19s nonprofit as she lays the groundwork for a prospective 2024 presidential bid, according to previously unreported tax documents obtained by Politico.\par \par \uc2 Haley\u8217\'20\'19s nonprofit policy advocacy group, Stand For America, Inc, has received major donations from people including New York hedge fund manager \uc2 Paul Singer\uc2 , investor \uc2 Stanley Druckenmiller\uc2 , and Miriam Adelson and her late husband, casino mogul \uc2 Sheldon Adelson\uc2 , the \uc2 Internal Revenue Service\uc2  filings reveal.\par \par \uc2 The roster of supporters who gave undisclosed donations in 2019 also includes Suzanne Youngkin, the wife of Virginia Governor Glenn Youngkin, himself a possible presidential contender; former Pennsylvania Senate candidate and hedge fund executive David McCormick; and Vivek and Lakshmi Garipalli, members of a New Jersey family that has donated large sums to Democrats \u8211\'20\'13 but which gave Haley\u8217\'20\'19s organization $1 million.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Fascist or not?\par \par \uc2 It might have seemed an odd question even just a few years ago, but \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s speech on Thursday night has put the word \u8220\'20\'1Cfascism\u8221\'20\'1D squarely into mainstream American political discourse.\par \par \uc2 His accusations that modern Republicans were behaving like semi-fascists certainty triggered questions to his top press spokesperson. The Biden administration \u8211\'20\'13 understandably \u8211\'20\'13 is standing behind the phrase.\par \par \uc2 Reuters captures the scene:\par \par \uc2 The actions of some Republicans allied to former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  fit the definition of fascism, White House spokeswoman \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  told reporters on Friday, a day after President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said they edged toward \u8220\'20\'1Csemi-fascism.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was very clear when laying out and defining what MAGA Republicans have done and you look at the definition of fascism and you think about what they\u8217\'20\'19re doing in attacking our democracy. \u8230\'20\'26 That is what that is. It is very clear,\u8221\'20\'1D Jean-Pierre told a press briefing.\par \par \uc2 MAGA refers to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CMake America Great Again\u8221\'20\'1D slogan. Fascism is a political philosophy that exalts nation and often race above the individual and supports an autocratic government led by a dictatorial leader involving the forced suppression of opposition, U.S. dictionary Merriam-Webster says.\par \par \uc2 In response to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s Thursday evening comments that Trump-allied Republicans embraced violence and hatred, and edged toward \u8220\'20\'1Csemi-fascism,\u8221\'20\'1D the \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2  called the remarks \u8220\'20\'1Cdespicable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 A key question\par \par \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  columnist Helaine Olen seems to have hit the nail on the head with a very simple {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/helaineolen/status/1563245254781726722"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweet}}}\uc2 . Answers on a postcard please\u8230\'20\'26 no redactions.\par \par \uc2 enltrWhat\u8217\'20\'19s the innocent explanation for Trump keeping all these classified documents?\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Helaine Olen (@helaineolen) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/helaineolen/status/1563245254781726722?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 26, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Arizona judge strikes blow against election fairness skeptics\par \par \uc2 In just one of many such scenes playing out in courts across the US, Republicans who believe \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s unfounded claims of a stolen election and a fraudulent US voting process have suffered a set back.\par \par \uc2 An Arizona judge has refused to require that Arizona officials count ballots by hand in November, dismissing a lawsuit filed by Republican nominees for governor and secretary of state based on false claims of problems with vote-counting machines.\par \par \uc2 AP has more:\par \par \uc2 Kari Lake, who is running for governor, and Mark Finchem, a secretary of state candidate, won their GOP primaries after aggressively promoting the narrative that the 2020 election was marred by fraud or widespread irregularities.\par \par \uc2 Their lawsuit repeated unfounded allegations about the security of machines that count votes. They relied in part on testimony from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  supporters who led a discredited review of the election in Maricopa County, including Doug Logan, the CEO of Cyber Ninjas, who oversaw the effort described by supporters as a \u8220\'20\'1Cforensic audit.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 U.S. District Judge John Tuchi ruled that Lake and Finchem failed to show any realistic likelihood of harm and that their lawsuit must be brought in state, not federal, court. He also ruled that it is too close to the election to upend the process.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe 2022 Midterm Elections are set to take place on November 8,\u8221\'20\'1D Tuchi wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CIn the meantime, Plaintiffs request a complete overhaul of Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s election procedures.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Various reactions have been pouring out online over the affidavit.\par \par \uc2 Virginia Democratic senator Mark Warner, who chairs the Senate Intelligence Committee said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt appears, based on the affidavit unsealed this morning, that among the improperly handled documents at Mar-a-Lago were some of our most sensitive intelligence * which is one reason the Senate Intelligence Committee has requested, on a bipartisan basis, a damage assessment of any national security threat posed by the mishandling of this information. The Department of Justice investigation must be allowed to proceed without interference.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, North Carolina Republican Representative \uc2 Dan Bishop\uc2  said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo much for transparency,\u8221\'20\'1D tweeting alongside a photo of redacted sections of the affidavit. Bishop is a member of the House of Representatives Homeland Security and Government Affairs Committee.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s son \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2 . echoed similar sentiments online, tweeting a photo of the redacted affidavit with the caption, \u8220\'20\'1CWell this really clears things up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrWell this really clears things up. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6S2FxIQtSi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/6S2FxIQtSi}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2 . (@DonaldJTrumpJr) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DonaldJTrumpJr/status/1563217956552601601?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 26, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18A deal with the devil\u8217\'20\'19: outrage in Appalachia over Manchin pipeline plan\par \par \uc2 Nina Lakhani and Oliver Milman report\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Taking on the fossil fuel industry in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/west-virginia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 West Virginia}}}\uc2  was always going to be a David v Goliath type battle, but after years of protests, lobbying and lawsuits, 68-year-old Becky Crabtree thought the community-led resistance had beaten the Mountain Valley pipeline (MVP) in a fair fight.\par \par \uc2 So when news broke earlier in August that the state\u8217\'20\'19s fossil-fuel friendly senator {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joe-manchin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Manchin}}}\uc2  had resurrected the pipeline, Crabtree, a high school science teacher who teaches students about the climate crisis, felt \u8220\'20\'1Cnumb\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Manchin, a conservative Democrat who receives more campaign financing from the fossil fuel industry \u8211\'20\'13 including pipeline companies \u8211\'20\'13 than any other lawmaker in Congress, had agreed to back his party\u8217\'20\'19s historic climate legislation before the crucial midterm elections. But only after he negotiated a side-deal to fast-track the MVP.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s the unfairness that makes me so angry. It\u8217\'20\'19s a deal with the devil,\u8221\'20\'1D said Crabtree, 68, who owns a 30-acre sheep farm in Lindside, Monroe county.\par \par \uc2 Full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/26/joe-manchin-west-virginia-mountain-valley-pipeline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s a deal with the devil\u8217\'20\'19: outrage in Appalachia over Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18vile\u8217\'20\'19 pipeline plan }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 'They are attacking democracy' \u8211\'20\'13 White House defends Biden's remarks on Trumpism as "semi-fascism"\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  has just finished briefing the media and taking questions and she was asked about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s remarks at a fundraiser last night where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/26/biden-trump-republicans-fascism-speech-maryland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he referred}}}\uc2  to the \u8220\'20\'1CMAGA Republican philosophy\u8221\'20\'1D as akin to \u8220\'20\'1Csemi-fascism\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Asked to explain what the US president meant by that remark, Jean-Pierre said of right-wing Republicans: \u8220\'20\'1CHe was very powerful last night. When it comes to \u8216\'20\'18MAGA Republicans\u8217\'20\'19, when it comes to the extreme, ultra wing of the Republicans, they are attacking democracy, they are taking away rights and freedoms, they are using threats of violence, taking away voting rights, and he [Biden] called it what it is \u8230\'20\'26 and what many would argue, historians would agree with us on.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe believes that presidents should be the strongest voice for democracy,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre also strove to differentiate between what she referred to as \u8220\'20\'1Ctraditional, conservative\u8221\'20\'1D Republicans and the [Trumpist] \u8220\'20\'1CMake America Great Again\u8221\'20\'1D rightwing loyalists to the former president.\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , speaks to the press. Photograph: Michael Reynolds/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 A quick recap, blog readers, it\u8217\'20\'19s been a dramatic morning and there will be plenty more news over the coming few hours. But for now, here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/26/trump-affidavit-fbi-biden-abortion-student-loan-latest-updates?page=with:block-630904908f0876e20fe151ef#block-630904908f0876e20fe151ef"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released a statement}}}\uc2  about the release of the government affidavit that underpinned the search of his Mar-a-Lago club and residence in Florida earlier this month. He posted it on Truth Social, his struggling social media platform that he created after being banned by \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Department of Justice\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/26/trump-affidavit-fbi-biden-abortion-student-loan-latest-updates?page=with:block-6308f7858f08237696474fc1#block-6308f7858f08237696474fc1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the FBI had}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cprobable cause to believe that evidence of obstruction\u8221\'20\'1D would be found at Mar-a-Lago when it sought a warrant to search the property, the affidavit notes.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The affidavit is replete {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/26/trump-affidavit-fbi-biden-abortion-student-loan-latest-updates?page=with:block-6308f40a8f08237696474f7a#block-6308f40a8f08237696474f7a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with details}}}\uc2  that would provide \u8220\'20\'1Ca roadmap\u8221\'20\'1D for anyone intent on obstructing the investigation.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The affidavit reminds us ofthe context of the \uc2 FBI\uc2  raid on Mar-a-Lago, thus: \u8220\'20\'1CThe government is conducting a criminal investigation concerning the improper removal and storage of classified information in unauthorized spaces, as well as the unlawful concealment or removal of government records.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 While the public waited for the affidavit to be released, we also noted that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/26/trump-affidavit-fbi-biden-abortion-student-loan-latest-updates?page=with:block-6308b6448f0876e20fe14d3c#block-6308b6448f0876e20fe14d3c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden called}}}\uc2  the \u8220\'20\'1CMAGA Republican\u8221\'20\'1D philosophy \u8220\'20\'1Csemi-fascism\u8221\'20\'1D last night, based on the anti-democratic efforts of the more extreme wing of the GOP that hews unfailingly to Trump.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump statement released\par \par \uc2 We have \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s reaction, on Truth Social, the social media platform he set up after being kicked off \uc2 Twitter\uc2  over the Capitol attack\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Affidavit heavily redacted!!! Nothing mentioned on \u8220\'20\'1CNuclear,\u8221\'20\'1D a total public relations subterfuge by the FBI & DOJ, or our close working relationship regarding document turnover - WE GAVE THEM MUCH. Judge Bruce Reinhart should NEVER have allowed the Break-In of my home. He recused himself two months ago from one of my cases based on his animosity and hatred of your favorite President, me. What changed? Why hasn\u8217\'20\'19t he recused himself on this case? Obama must be very proud of him right now!\par \par \uc2 To unpick:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNuclear\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 it has been reported that some of the materials kept at Mar-a-Lago concerned nuclear weapons. And some concerned \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2 , which, by the by, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/aug/26/serious-problem-if-france-and-uk-cant-tell-if-they-are-friends-or-enemies-says-macron-liz-truss"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 might interest Liz Truss}}}\uc2 . But anyway\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBreak-in\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 nope. Warrant duly served, etc, which is why we\u8217\'20\'19re here.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CObama must be very proud\u8221\'20\'1D of the judge \u8230\'20\'26 we may all remember \uc2 John Roberts\uc2 , the chief justice of the supreme court, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2018/nov/21/john-roberts-chief-justice-trump-obama-judge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rebuking Trump}}}\uc2  for referring to \u8220\'20\'1CObama judges\u8221\'20\'1D, etc. We may also all remember Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pride at having installed a huge number of judges himself, including three on Roberts\u8217\'20\'19 court. In short \u8211\'20\'13 judges are not meant to act politically but they are politically appointed. And so on.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Of Judge Reinhart:{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/08/18/us/politics/judge-bruce-reinhart-trump-mar-a-lago.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he made a donation to }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/08/18/us/politics/judge-bruce-reinhart-trump-mar-a-lago.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Barack Obama}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/08/18/us/politics/judge-bruce-reinhart-trump-mar-a-lago.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  in 2008}}}\uc2 . He also donated to Republicans, if not \uc2 Donald J Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Attached to the affidavit is a letter from lawyers for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , complaining of unfair treatment and asserting a president\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cabsolute authority to declassify documents\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 both features of his response to the search and the claims of his supporters in Republican ranks and on the right of the US media.\par \par \uc2 The letter, signed by M Evan Corcoran of Silverman Thompson Slutkin White, begins:\par \par \uc2 Public trust in the government is low. At such times, adherence to the rules and long-standing policies is essential. President \uc2 Donald J Trump\uc2  is a leader of the Republican Party. The Department of Justice (DOJ), as part of the Executive Branch, is under the control of a President from the opposite party. It is critical, given that dynamic, that every effort is made to ensure that actions by DOJ that may touch upon the former President, or his close associates, do not involve politics.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 I refer you back to President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s comment to reporters before the affidavit was filed today, when asked if he thought national security might have been compromised at Mar-a-Lago while Trump was storing classified documents there:\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll let the justice department determine that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The lawyers\u8217\'20\'19 letter conforms to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s worldview, that attorneys general and the Department of Justice exist to serve presidents politically. Biden\u8217\'20\'19s answer speaks for generally accepted wisdom, which is that the DoJ does not exist for that purpose and is in fact independent of any White House or administration.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 The affidavit contain reference to and quotes from a back-and-forth between the DoJ and counsel for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  (referred to as FPOTUS, or Former President of the United States) over storage of materials at Mar-a-Lago.\par \par \uc2 After a lot of redactions, the agent writes: \u8220\'20\'1CBased upon this investigation, I believe that the STORAGE ROOM, FPOTUS\u8217\'20\'19s residential suite, Pine Hall, the \u8216\'20\'1845 Office\u8217\'20\'19 and other spaces within the PREMISES are not currently authorized locations for the storage of classified information or [national defense information, or NDI].\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSimilarly, based upon this investigation, I do not believe that any spaces within the PREMISES have been authorized for the storage of classified information at least since the end of FPOTUS\u8217\'20\'19s Presidential Administration on January 20, 2021.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After more redactions, the affidavit concludes:\par \par \uc2 Based on the foregoing facts and circumstances, I submit that probable cause exists to believe that evidence, contraband, fruits of crime, or other items illegally possessed \u8230\'20\'26 will be found at the PREMISES.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFurther, I submit that this affidavit supports probable cause for a warrant to search the PREMISES described in Attachment A and seize the items described in Attachment B.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Affidavit details probable cause\par \par \uc2 The affidavit as released is of course full of redactions, across its 38 pages. But it reveals some interesting nuggets about the search, including that the Department of Justice and \uc2 FBI\uc2  had \u8220\'20\'1C probable cause to believe that evidence of obstruction\u8221\'20\'1D would be found at Mar-a-Lago.\par \par \uc2 In another interesting section \u8230\'20\'26 the affidavit says that on 9 February 2022, the DoJ leaned that a preliminary review of 15 boxes taken to Mar-a-Lago \u8220\'20\'1Cindicated that they contained \u8216\'20\'18newspapers, magazines, printed news articles, photos, miscellaneous print-outs, notes, presidential correspondence, personal and post-presidential records, and \u8216\'20\'18 a lot of classified records \u8217\'20\'19.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COf most significant concern was that highly classified records were unfoldered, intermixed with other records, and otherwise unproperly [sic] identified.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The affidavit reproduces a Trump statement after the issue became public, and then \u8230\'20\'26 is extensively redacted. The redacted passage is a chronological retelling of how the issue developed.\par \par \uc2 The next significant un-redacted passage contains the news that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s own notes were included in the materials in question. It reads as follows:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFrom May 16-18, 2022, \uc2 FBI\uc2  agents conducted a preliminary review of the FIFTEEN BOXES provided to NARA and identified documents with classification markings in fourteen of the FIFTEEN BOXES. A preliminary triage of the documents with classification markings revealed the following approximate numbers: 184 unique documents bearing classification markings, including 67 documents marked as CONFIDENTIAL, 92 documents marked as SECRET, and 25 documents marked as TOP SECRET. Further, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  agents observed markings reflecting the following compartments/dissemination controls: HCS, FISA, ORCON, NOFORN, and SI.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBased on my training and experience, I know that documents classified at these levels typically contain NDI. Several of the documents also contained what appears to be FPOTUS\u8217\'20\'19s [Trump\u8217\'20\'19s] handwritten notes.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 The identity of the \uc2 FBI\uc2  agent who filed the affidavit for the Mar-a-Lago search is of course redacted. He or she describes himself or herself as \u8220\'20\'1Ca Special Agent with the \uc2 FBI\uc2  assigned to the Washington Field Office\u8221\'20\'1D, trained \u8220\'20\'1Cat the FBI Academy located at Quantico, Virginia, specific to counterintelligence and espionage investigations\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBased on my experience and training,\u8221\'20\'1D the agent writes, \u8220\'20\'1CI am familiar with efforts used to unlawfully collect, retain, and disseminate sensitive government information, including classified\u8221\'20\'1D information.\par \par \uc2 The agent details the origins of the investigation and the documents sought, which we know much about, and writes: \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s investigation has established that documents bearing classification markings, which appear to contain National Defense Information (NDI), were among the materials contained in the FIFTEEN BOXES and were stored at the PREMISES in an unauthorized location.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFurther, there is probable cause to believe that additional documents that contain classified NDI or that are Presidential records subject to record retention requirements currently remain at the PREMISES. There is also probable cause to believe that evidence of obstruction will be found at the PREMISES.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The agent adds: \u8220\'20\'1CBased upon the following facts, there is probable cause to believe that the locations to be searched at the PREMISES contain evidence, contraband, fruits of crime, or other items illegally possessed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.31pm BST\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uploads.guim.co.uk/2022/08/31/gov.uscourts.flsd.617854.102.1_1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uploads.guim.co.uk/2022/08/31/gov.uscourts.flsd.617854.102.1_1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 affidavit}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uploads.guim.co.uk/2022/08/31/gov.uscourts.flsd.617854.102.1_1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  is now out}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 DoJ: Affidavit would be 'roadmap for obstruction'\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1563197210807873539"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Speaking}}}\uc2  of proposed redactions to the affidavit concerning the Mar-a-Lago search \u8230\'20\'26 here\u8217\'20\'19s a screengrab of what has been filed today, and quoted in my previous post.\par \par \uc2 A shot of the DoJ paperwork quoting from the affidavit. Photograph: Court Listener\par \par \uc2 The document as filed and released continues:\par \par \uc2 Although the public is now aware that the government executed a search warrant at the premises owned by the former President and seized documents marked as classified, the affidavit is replete with further details that would provide a roadmap for anyone intent on obstructing the investigation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMaximizing the Government\u8217\'20\'19s access to untainted facts \u183\'00\'B7 increases its ability to make a fully-informed prosecutive decision\u8221\'20\'1D \u8230\'20\'26 For example \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26 and then we have many more black lines.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 The paperwork just released, containing portions of the affidavit, is as predicted heavily redacted.\par \par \uc2 The document says: \u8220\'20\'1CInformation in the affidavit could be used to identify many, if not all, of these witnesses. For example\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 which is followed by a long redacted passage.\par \par \uc2 The document then adds: \u8220\'20\'1CIf witnesses\u8217\'20\'19 identities are exposed, they could be subjected to harms including retaliation, intimidation, or harassment, and even threats to their physical safety. As the court has already noted, \u8216\'20\'18these concerns are not hypothetical in this case\u8217\'20\'19.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Another redacted passage follows, then the following text appears:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMeanwhile, \uc2 FBI\uc2  agents who have been publicly identified in connection with this investigation have received repeated threats of violence from members of the public. Exposure of witnesses\u8217\'20\'19 identities would likely erode their trust in the government\u8217\'20\'19s investigation, and it would almost certainly chill other potential witnesses from coming forward in this investigation and others.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Justice department files redacted Mar-a-Lago search affidavit\par \par \uc2 The justice department has filed the affidavit justifying the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s search of Mar-a-Lago, a day after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/26/doj-redacted-trump-affidavit-mar-a-lago-search"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a federal magistrate judge ordered its release}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The document has been redacted, but could offer details of the alleged crimes that brought the \uc2 FBI\uc2  to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s Florida resort {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/08/trump-says-fbi-raided-his-mar-a-lago-home"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 earlier this month}}}\uc2  and opened up {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/22/trump-sues-us-government-fbi-mar-a-lago"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 yet another legal front}}}\uc2  for the embattled former president.\par \par \uc2 You can read documents concerning the affidavit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/64872441/102/1/united-states-v-sealed-search-warrant/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 We have the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/64872441/99/united-states-v-sealed-search-warrant/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 order}}}\uc2  to unseal the affidavit used in the \uc2 FBI\uc2  search of Mar-a-Lago, but not the redacted affidavit itself, yet.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 An expectant Louisiana woman who is carrying a skull-less fetus that would die almost immediately after birth has cemented plans to travel to North Carolina to terminate her pregnancy after her local medical provider dithered on performing the procedure, citing fear that the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban outlawed it.\par \par \uc2 Standing on the steps of Louisiana\u8217\'20\'19s Capitol building in her hometown of Baton Rouge, Nancy Davis, 36, announced this morning that her grim trip would be next week, financed by more than $30,000 in donations raised by an online {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gofundme.com/f/zk8p5r-nancy-davis-louisiana-woman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 GoFundMe campaign}}}\uc2  launched after she went public with her plight earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 Her lawyer, the prominent civil rights attorney \uc2 Ben Crump\uc2 , called on Louisiana\u8217\'20\'19s lawmakers to at least clarify the wording of their \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban \u8211\'20\'13 if not repeal it altogether \u8211\'20\'13 to prevent anyone else from enduring what Davis and her family had during the last several weeks.\par \par \uc2 The state\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 John Bel Edwards\uc2 , should call a special legislative session in advance of the regular one scheduled to begin in April of next year to do that if necessary, Crump said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLouisiana lawmakers inflicted unspeakable pain, emotional damage and physical risk upon this beautiful mother,\u8221\'20\'1D Crump said, gesturing at Davis, who was accompanied by her partner Shedric Cole, their young daughter and her two stepchildren.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey replaced care with confusion, privacy with politics and options with ideology.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMs Davis was among the first women to be caught in this crosshairs of confusion due to Louisiana\u8217\'20\'19s rush to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But she will hardly be the last.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/aug/20/louisiana-abortion-woman-nancy-davis-benjamin-crump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Louisiana woman faces \u8216\'20\'18horrifically cruel\u8217\'20\'19 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  choice over fetus missing skull}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has just been asked if he thinks national security might have been compromised at Mar-a-Lago while \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was storing classified documents there.\par \par \uc2 The president\u8217\'20\'19s answer, per the wire services and the pool reporter: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ll let the justice department determine that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Still waiting for the release of the redacted affidavit behind the \uc2 FBI\uc2  search of Mar-a-Lago, which is due by noon.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Three new sealed filings have appeared online in the federal court system related to the Mar-a-Lago case, Politico reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrFor those following along at home or elsewhere, 3 sealed filings have been docketed in last 10 minutes in the Trump Mar-a-Lago search warrant case. Not clear whether that's what we're eventually supposed to get or whether DOJ is asking for last-minute changes.... {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/qYapvHYFL3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/qYapvHYFL3}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Josh Gerstein (@joshgerstein) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/joshgerstein/status/1563186407106981888?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 26, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Since they are not public, it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear what they are, but a federal magistrate judge gave the justice department until noon eastern time today to make the redacted affidavit justifying the search public.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Why might the \uc2 FBI\uc2  have been so worried about the potential that government secrets were stored at Mar-a-Lago?\par \par \uc2 As we await the release of the redacted affidavit from federal agents\u8217\'20\'19 search of the property, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://newsinteractive.post-gazette.com/anna-de-rothschild-trump-mar-a-lago-security-fbi-investigation/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an investigation}}}\uc2  by The Pittsburgh Post-Gazette and the Organized Crime and Corruption Reporting Project appears to indicate that an imposter repeatedly entered the resort last year, and mingled with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The outlets found that a woman named Inna Yashchyshyn posed as a member of a famous European banking family and managed to get into the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s Florida club, playing a round of golf at a nearby course with Trump and his ally senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  in May 2021.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the story:\par \par \uc2 The ability of Ms. Yashchyshyn \u8212\'20\'14 the daughter of an Illinois truck driver \u8212\'20\'14 to bypass the security at Mr. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s club demonstrates the ease with which someone with a fake identity and shadowy background can get into a facility that\u8217\'20\'19s one of America\u8217\'20\'19s power centers and the epicenter of Republican Party politics.\par \par \uc2 Those issues have become even more critical after \uc2 FBI\uc2  agents seized boxes of classified and top-secret materials two weeks ago from Mar-a-Lago after executing a search warrant on Mr. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s home.\par \par \uc2 Her entry \u8212\'20\'14 multiple trips in and out of the club grounds \u8212\'20\'14 lays bare the vulnerabilities of a facility that serves as both the former president\u8217\'20\'19s residence and a private club, and highlights the gaps in security that can take place.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s his residence,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ed Martin, a former \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  special agent who spent more than two decades in criminal intelligence. \u8220\'20\'1CShe shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have been in there.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Relax, Californian fans of \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 : the governor says he will not be running for president in 2024.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with ABC News, he was rather vehement in his answer:\par \par \uc2 enltrCalifornia Gov. Newsom tells {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mattgutmanABC?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @mattgutmanabc}}}\uc2  he has no plans to run for president in 2024 and that Pres. Biden \u8220\'20\'1Ccan sleep better than any modern American president with what he\u8217\'20\'19s accomplished in the last two years.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/a7aUoFIWST"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/a7aUoFIWST}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/IrhtgB7BZo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/IrhtgB7BZo}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ABC News (@ABC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ABC/status/1562991410592489473?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 26, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The Democrat is standing for re-election to a second term as California\u8217\'20\'19s governor, and if he wins, will keep the post until January 2027.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 However, not all pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Republicans appear to be equally vulnerable.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.slu.edu/research/research-institute/big-ideas/slu-poll/data-archive/august-2022-poll/slu-poll-august-2022-toplineresults.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll released today}}}\uc2  of voters in Missouri by \uc2 Saint Louis University\uc2  and \uc2 YouGov\uc2  found Republican candidate \uc2 Eric Schmitt\uc2  with a strong lead in the race for the open Senate seat. He was up 49% against his Democratic challenger Trudy Busch Valentine, who polled at 38%.\par \par \uc2 Schmitt is the state\u8217\'20\'19s current attorney general, and made a point of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ago.mo.gov/home/news/2022/06/24/missouri-attorney-general-eric-schmitt-becomes-first-to-issue-opinion-following-scotus-opinion-in-dobbs-effectively-ending-abortion-in-missouri"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 quickly implementing}}}\uc2  Missouri\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban after the supreme court overturned Roe v. Wade. And unlike Arizona, Missouri is these days solidly Republican, having not voted for a Democratic president since 1996.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 The states that have newly banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  are all Republican led, but not all in the party appear ready to embrace such rhetoric, particularly if they are running for election. Consider the case of Blake Masters.\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s the GOP nominee for Senate in Arizona, and is up against Democratic incumbent Mark Kelly, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/senate/2022/arizona/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appears to be leading}}}\uc2  among voters. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2022-election/arizona-blake-masters-backtracks-abortion-scrubs-campaign-website-rcna44808"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News reports}}}\uc2  that, for whatever reason, Masters has removed the most strident anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rhetoric from his campaign website on Thursday. Five of his six positions have been deleted or rewritten, according to the story, among them, \u8220\'20\'1CI am 100% pro-life,\u8221\'20\'1D which is now gone entirely.\par \par \uc2 Also removed is a mention of Masters\u8217\'20\'19 support for \u8220\'20\'1Ca federal personhood law (ideally a Constitutional amendment) that recognizes that unborn babies are human beings that may not be killed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from their story:\par \par \uc2 Masters previously expressed support for \u8220\'20\'1Cthe Pain-Capable Unborn Child Protection Act, the Born Alive \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Survivors Protection Act, the SAVE Moms and Babies Act, and other pro-life legislation.\u8221\'20\'1D The Pain-Capable Unborn Child Protection Act would make it a criminal offense to perform or attempt to perform an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  20 weeks after conception.\par \par \uc2 Now the website states he backs \u8220\'20\'1Ca law or a Constitutional amendment that bans late term (third trimester) \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and partial-birth \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the federal level\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-life legislation, pregnancy centers, and programs that make it easier for pregnant women to support a family and decide to choose life.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Among the potential reasons why Masters may have opted to soften his rhetoric: Kansas voters\u8217\'20\'19 rejection earlier this month of an effort to change the state constitution to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House has condemned a slew of new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions that recently went into effect in four states.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday marks the latest attack against the fundamental rights of Americans as new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans go into effect in Idaho, Oklahoma, Tennessee, and Texas,\u8221\'20\'1D press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 She continued:\par \par \uc2 These extreme bans will criminalize \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in some cases without exceptions for rape or incest. These near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans are part of a growing effort by Republican legislators to roll back the freedoms Americans have relied on for nearly half a century. Today\u8217\'20\'19s radical steps take away women\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive rights and put personal health care decisions in the hands of politicians instead of women and their doctors, threatening women\u8217\'20\'19s health and lives. Americans need to know that these and other fundamental rights, including the right to contraception and marriage equality, are at risk. Congress should act immediately to pass a law restoring the protections of Roe\u8211\'20\'13and people across the country to should make their voices heard.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/25/us-abortion-trigger-bans-laws-tennessee-texas-idaho"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Slew of trigger laws kick in as three more US states ban abortions}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Biden Administration\u8217\'20\'19s renewed feistiness was in full effect last night when the normally staid White House twitter account began calling out Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Whoever was behind the official account took issue with GOP lawmakers who objected to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s student loan relief plan announced earlier this week, and highlighted the politicians\u8217\'20\'19 own history of benefiting from debt forgiveness.\par \par \uc2 enltrCongresswoman \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  had $183,504 in PPP loans forgiven. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4FoCymt8TB"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/4FoCymt8TB}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The White House (@WhiteHouse) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WhiteHouse/status/1562916200866267138?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrCongressman Vern Buchanan had over $2.3 million in PPP loans forgiven. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/bXpwJlWRm4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/bXpwJlWRm4}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The White House (@WhiteHouse) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WhiteHouse/status/1562916204011995136?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrCongressman \uc2 Markwayne Mullin\uc2  had over $1.4 million in PPP loans forgiven. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Vc7mLQa2RS"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Vc7mLQa2RS}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The White House (@WhiteHouse) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WhiteHouse/status/1562916206419509248?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrCongressman \uc2 Kevin Hern\uc2  had over $1 million in PPP loans forgiven. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/XsBaqxNZN4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/XsBaqxNZN4}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The White House (@WhiteHouse) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WhiteHouse/status/1562916208441180161?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrCongressman Mike Kelly had $987,237 in PPP loans forgiven. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Syb5Oe8gDG"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Syb5Oe8gDG}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The White House (@WhiteHouse) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WhiteHouse/status/1562916210819436544?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrCongressman \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  had $482,321 in PPP loans forgiven. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/XPgC0pETkp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/XPgC0pETkp}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The White House (@WhiteHouse) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WhiteHouse/status/1562916212841103360?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 As he courted voters in Democrat-friendly Maryland last night, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  sought to cast the Republican party as extreme and play up his own recent legislative accomplishments. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/joan-greve"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joan E Greve}}}\uc2  was there, and filed this report on the renewed optimism in the Democratic party:\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has transformed his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/18/joe-biden-age-approval-rating-2024-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rough July}}}\uc2  into a jubilant August. Last month, the US president was drowning in negative headlines about his handling of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/09/biden-democrats-jimmy-carter-crisis-white-house"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 numerous crises}}}\uc2 , from the war in Ukraine to record-high gas prices and the apparent demise of his signature legislative proposal.\par \par \uc2 Now, as the summer draws to a close, Biden is riding high, powered by the passage of Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 climate and healthcare package and glimmers of hope for his party\u8217\'20\'19s prospects in the midterm elections. That optimism was on vivid display on Thursday, as Biden took the stage for a rally held by the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  in Rockville, Maryland.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve come a long way in 18 months. Covid no longer controls our lives. A record number of Americans are working,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden told the cheering crowd. \u8220\'20\'1CWe never gave up. We never gave in. We\u8217\'20\'19re delivering for the American people now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Get ready to learn more about the investigation that sparked the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s search of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago resort earlier this month \u8211\'20\'13 but don\u8217\'20\'19t get your hopes up too high.\par \par \uc2 In response to a lawsuit from media organizations and other groups, a federal magistrate judge yesterday ordered the release of the affidavit from the search, which should contain details like the probable cause that justified the warrant. But Bruce Reinhart also allowed the justice department to redact \u8220\'20\'1Cthe identities of witnesses, law enforcement agents, and uncharged parties\u8230\'20\'26 the investigation\u8217\'20\'19s strategy, direction, scope, sources, and methods, and\u8230\'20\'26 grand jury information.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The document could therefore potentially contain lots of blacked out lines rather than new information. But as \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/26/doj-redacted-trump-affidavit-mar-a-lago-search"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported yesterday}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cdepending on how the affidavit was produced, several former US attorneys said, it could also contain elements that are not directly related to the investigation, such as descriptions of potential crimes that the justice department suspected were being committed at Mar-a-Lago.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Deadline looms for release of Mar-a-Lago affidavit as Biden decries Republicans' 'semi-fascism'\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. The justice department has a noon eastern time deadline to make public the affidavit used to justify the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s search of Mar-a-Lago, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/26/doj-redacted-trump-affidavit-mar-a-lago-search"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 after a judge ordered its release yesterday}}}\uc2 . While the document could provide new details of the investigation, it will also be redacted \u8211\'20\'13 perhaps heavily. Meanwhile, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  last night accused Republicans who aligned with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  of veering into \u8220\'20\'1Csemi-fascism\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/26/democrats-have-their-mojo-has-the-tide-shifted-for-biden-and-his-party"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as he sought to rally}}}\uc2  Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 enthusiasm ahead of the November midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 And in case that isn\u8217\'20\'19t enough, here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we can expect today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Today is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/presidential-actions/2022/08/25/a-proclamation-on-womens-equality-day-2022/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Women\u8217\'20\'19s Equality Day}}}\uc2 , and Biden is set to make an appearance at a White House meeting on protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access at 11 am eastern time.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Federal Reserve chair \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  is making a major speech on the central bank\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to lower inflation without causing a recession at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/calendar.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 10am eastern time}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220826ei8q001ur\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
