\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden \u8216\'20\'18determined to ban assault weapons\u8217\'20\'19 as he lays out crime prevention plans \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Richard Luscombe in Miami \par \uc2 5,589 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 August 2022\par 21:53 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President details his Safer America Plan in Pennsylvania speech and says funding police provides \u8216\'20\'18peace of mind\u8217\'20\'19Sign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 The US politics blog is closing now and will resume tomorrow. It\u8217\'20\'19s been a busy day in news from Washington, DC, and beyond of a political nature, finishing with US president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s speech in Pennsylvania on gun safety and law enforcement.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s how the day went:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/30/biden-gun-control-trump-republicans-democrats-fbi-latest-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-630e6ce18f08fb7d69ffe300#block-630e6ce18f08fb7d69ffe300"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  he is \u8220\'20\'1Cdetermined\u8221\'20\'1D to achieve an assault weapons ban in the US. The push to reenact such a ban formed a centerpiece of the Safer America Plan that the president laid out in an address this afternoon in Wilkes-Barre, Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US president made {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/30/biden-gun-control-trump-republicans-democrats-fbi-latest-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-630e61858f08fb7d69ffe2ad#block-630e61858f08fb7d69ffe2ad"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a case}}}\uc2  for how funding the police \u8211\'20\'13 a deliberate rebuffing of the progressive cause of defunding the police (switching funds from policing to a spectrum of social services) \u8211\'20\'13 provides \u8220\'20\'1Cpeace of mind\u8221\'20\'1D to the American public.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/30/biden-gun-control-trump-republicans-democrats-fbi-latest-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-630e5e228f08fa7e6340c714#block-630e5e228f08fa7e6340c714"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  it is sending more {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/monkeypox"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 monkeypox}}}\uc2  vaccines to certain states and cities in an effort to combat further spread of the disease.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Victor Madrigal-Borloz, United Nations independent expert on sexual orientation and gender identity, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/30/biden-gun-control-trump-republicans-democrats-fbi-latest-updates?page=with:block-630e50ff8f08fb7d69ffe230#block-630e50ff8f08fb7d69ffe230"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2  that LGBTQ+ equality in the US \u8216\'20\'18not yet within reach\u8217\'20\'19 because of states that have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/28/lgbtq-rights-us-dont-say-gay"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed legislation restricting LGBTQ+ rights}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The DoJ {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/30/biden-gun-control-trump-republicans-democrats-fbi-latest-updates?page=with:block-630e4f318f08fa7e6340c69b#block-630e4f318f08fa7e6340c69b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tightened rules}}}\uc2  around some staff attending election events when attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  issued a memo saying that political appointees at the \uc2 US Department of Justice\uc2  will be barred from attending election campaign events or fundraisers.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 And the public still awaits the DoJ\u8217\'20\'19s legal response to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/20/trump-mar-a-lago-search-fbi-legal-motion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 request for a \u8220\'20\'1Cspecial master\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  to oversee its review of classified documents seized by the \uc2 FBI\uc2  in a raid on his Florida home. The deadline for the latest filing in federal court in West Palm Beach is today.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll be closing this US politics blog shortly. By now you will probably have heard or read that former Soviet leader \uc2 Mikhail Gorbachev\uc2  has died. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  has launched a separate live blog to cover details and reaction, which you can follow {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/aug/30/mikhail-gorbachev-former-soviet-leader-dies-moscow-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 And here is the current main {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/aug/30/mikhail-gorbachev-dies-soviet-leader-92"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 news story}}}\uc2 . There will be a lot more coverage on this huge event from the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  closed his remarks with a vociferous attack on Republicans who defended the January 6 insurrection incited by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at the US Capitol, and called the deadly riot that claimed several lives, including police officers, \u8220\'20\'1Csickening\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 What I find even more incredible is the defense. Cops attacked, assaulted. Speared with flag poles. Sprayed with mace. Stomped on. Dragged. Brutalized. Police lost their lives as a result of that day.\par \par \uc2 Let me say this to my Maga Republican friends in Congress. Don\u8217\'20\'19t tell me you support law enforcement if you won\u8217\'20\'19t condemn what happened on January 6. Don\u8217\'20\'19t tell me. For God\u8217\'20\'19s sake, whose side are you on?\par \par \uc2 You can\u8217\'20\'19t be pro law enforcement and pro insurrection. You can\u8217\'20\'19t be a party of law and order and call the people who attacked the police on January 6 patriots. You can\u8217\'20\'19t do it.\par \par \uc2 Biden also condemned Republicans who have called for the \uc2 FBI\uc2  to be defunded after the raid on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago residence in Florida that resulted in the seizure of classified documents the former president was hoarding:\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s sickening to see the new attacks on the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , threatening the lives of law enforcement agents and their families for simply carrying out the law and doing their job.\par \par \uc2 I want to set it out as clear as I can. There is no place in this country, no place, for endangering the lives of law enforcement. No place, no, never, period.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden recalls a long list of mass shootings in the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMore children in America die from guns than active duty police and active duty military in the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to act for those families of Buffalo, Uvalde, Newtown, El Paso, Parkland, Charleston, Las Vegas, Orlando \u8230\'20\'26 I\u8217\'20\'19ve been to every one of those. Sat down with those parents. I spent four hours last time with every single one of the parents and families who have lost someone, and seen the looks in their faces.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThink about it. Think about the devastation that\u8217\'20\'19s occurred. We have to act for all those kids gunned down on our streets every single day that never make the news. There\u8217\'20\'19s a mass shooting every single day in this country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden 'determined' to enact assault weapons ban\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  says he is \u8220\'20\'1Cdetermined\u8221\'20\'1D to achieve an assault weapons ban in the US.\par \par \uc2 The push to reenact such a ban forms a centerpiece of the Safer America Plan that the president is laying out in an address Tuesday afternoon in Wilkes-Barre, Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 He is reminding the crowd that in 1994, as chair of the Senate judiciary committee, he helped engineer the original assault weapons ban that later lapsed:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m determined to ban assault weapons in this country. Determined.\par \par \uc2 I did it once before. And I\u8217\'20\'19ll do it again. For many of you at home, I want to be clear. It\u8217\'20\'19s not about taking away anybody\u8217\'20\'19s guns. In fact, we should be treating responsible gun owners as examples, how every gun owner should be.\par \par \uc2 Over 48,000 people died from gunshot wounds in 2021 in the United States of America. Over 26,000 by suicide.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden also attacked the \uc2 National Rifle Association\uc2 , touring the success of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/24/bipartisan-gun-control-law-house-vote-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bipartisan gun control law}}}\uc2  he signed into law this year.\par \par \uc2 We beat the \uc2 NRA\uc2 . We took them on and we beat \u8216\'20\'18em straight up.\par \par \uc2 You have no idea how intimidating they are to elected officials. The \uc2 NRA\uc2  was against it, which means a vast majority. The vast majority of Republicans in Congress couldn\u8217\'20\'19t even stand up and vote for it.\par \par \uc2 Law enforcement supported it. Faith leaders, teachers supported it. Victims of gun violence and their families supported it. Young people in this country, like the students of this great university, supported it.\par \par \uc2 And the \uc2 NRA\uc2 , the vast majority of congressional Republicans, voted against it, saving lives and keeping America safe. But guess what? We took on \uc2 NRA\uc2  we\u8217\'20\'19re gonna take them on again. And we won and we will win again. We\u8217\'20\'19re not stopping here. I\u8217\'20\'19m determined to ban assault weapons in this country.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is laying into Republicans who refused to back the American Rescue Plan in congress last year, which he says provided $350bn to states to help make their communities safer.\par \par \uc2 Guess what? Every single Republican member of Congress, every single one voted against us support law enforcement. They talk about how much they love it. They voted against the funding. Flat out. Flat out. Every Republican in the House. Every Republican in the Senate. Every single one.\par \par \uc2 And know we expect so much of our law enforcement officers, so we need to support them. That\u8217\'20\'19s why my crime plan to help communities recruit, hire and train nationwide more than 100,000 additional officers for community policing\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden: Funding police provides 'peace of mind'\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is talking up his crime prevention plans during a speech in Pennsylvania, and says funding the police is the pathway to providing American families with peace of mind.\par \par \uc2 During an address at which he is also expected to call for an assault weapons ban, the president is laying out his Safer America Plan. A series of deadly mass shootings have destroyed Americans\u8217\'20\'19 sense of security, he says:\par \par \uc2 Peace of mind [is] knowing your kids can go to school, or the playground, or movies, at a high school game, and come home safely. Not have to think about it for too long. So many families haven\u8217\'20\'19t had that peace of mind.\par \par \uc2 They watch the news and they see kids being gunned down in schools and on the streets. Almost every single night you turn the news on that\u8217\'20\'19s what you see. They see their neighbors lose their loved ones to drugs like fentanyl, which is a flat killer.\par \par \uc2 They see hate and anger and violence. Just walking the streets of America and they just want to feel safe again. They want to feel a sense of security. That\u8217\'20\'19s what my crime plan is all about.\par \par \uc2 Turning to funding law enforcement funding, which some Republicans accuse Democrats of wanting to scrap, Biden was clear:\par \par \uc2 When it comes to public safety in this nation, the answer is not defund the police. It\u8217\'20\'19s to fund to the police. We expect them to do everything. We expect them to be protect us, to be psychologist to be sociologists. I mean, we expect you to do everything. We ask so much of you.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House announces vaccine 'surge' to combat monkeypox\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has announced it is sending more {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/monkeypox"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 monkeypox}}}\uc2  vaccines to certain states and cities in an effort to combat further spread of the disease.\par \par \uc2 The White House national monkeypox response team said at a press briefing on Tuesday afternoon that the aim was to \u8220\'20\'1Cprotect individuals most at risk of contracting the virus.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Monkeypox vaccines. Photograph: Pascal Guyot/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Additional vaccines and support will be sent to states and cities holding events that convene large groups of LGBTQI+ individuals, specifically gay, bisexual, and other men who have sex with men, officials said.\par \par \uc2 They also announced a pilot to \u8220\'20\'1Csurge\u8221\'20\'1D vaccine availability and other prevention resources to communities of color in light of recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/poxvirus/monkeypox/response/2022/demographics.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CDC data}}}\uc2  showing the disproportionate reach of the virus among Black and Latino gay, bisexual, and other men.\par \par \uc2 New Orleans, Louisiana; Atlanta, Georgia; and Oakland, California are among the first cities benefiting from the additional vaccines.\par \par \uc2 The White House released a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/08/30/fact-sheet-white-house-monkeypox-response-team-announces-new-plans-to-support-large-lgbtqi-events-and-equity-interventions-to-reach-communities-at-highest-risk-of-contracting-the-virus/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 monkeypox fact sheet}}}\uc2  to accompany the briefing.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Three Arizona Republicans, including secretary of state nominee Mark Finchem and congressman \uc2 Paul Gosar\uc2 , must pay $75,000 in attorney fees for filing a defamation suit against a former Democratic lawmaker \u8220\'20\'1Cprimarily for purposes of harassment\u8221\'20\'1D, a judge has ruled.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press reports that the Republicans filed the lawsuit last year against former state representative Charlene Fernandez after she and other Democrats called for an investigation of their roles in the 6 January insurrection at the US Capitol.\par \par \uc2 Paul Gosar\uc2 . Photograph: Ross D Franklin/AP\par \par \uc2 The judge, Levi Gunderson, dismissed the lawsuit in April, saying Fernandez\u8217\'20\'19s request was protected by the first amendment\u8217\'20\'19s rights to free speech and to petition the government.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, Gunderson ruled that the lawsuit appeared to have been \u8220\'20\'1Cwritten for an audience other than the assigned trial court judge\u8221\'20\'1D as it made irrelevant references to open borders and Democrats \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  and \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit \u8220\'20\'1Cwas brought for an improper purpose, having been filed against a political opponent primarily for purposes of harassment,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 Fernandez and 41 other Democratic lawmakers signed a letter in January 2021 urging the justice department to investigate Finchem, Gosar and then state representative Anthony Kern, allies of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  who were in or around the US Capitol at the time of the riot. All deny wrongdoing.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 UN\uc2  expert: LGBTQ+ equality in US 'not within reach'\par \par \uc2 States that have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/28/lgbtq-rights-us-dont-say-gay"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed legislation restricting LGBTQ+ rights}}}\uc2  have come under attack from an independent United Nations expert on protection against violence and discrimination based on sexual orientation and gender identity.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at a \uc2 UN\uc2  briefing on discrimination against LGBTQ+ communities in New York on Tuesday, Victor Madrigal-Borloz said he looked at a cross-section of key indicators from housing to health care access:\par \par \uc2 Equality is not yet within reach, and in many cases not within sight of LGBT communities and populations in the US. All outcomes in the sectors I mentioned are inferior, and in many cases significantly inferior, for the LGBT population.\par \par \uc2 I am extremely concerned about a series, and I would say a concerted series, of actions at state level, both legislative and administrative, that tend to base on prejudice and stigma, to attack and to rollback the rights of LGBT persons.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/11/republican-states-mimic-florida-dont-say-gay-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Numerous US states}}}\uc2  have passed, or have been contemplating restrictive anti-LGBTQ+ legislation in recent months, none more so than Florida.\par \par \uc2 Republican governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  signed into law a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/04/florida-dont-say-gay-bill-children-mental-health"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t say gay\u8221\'20\'1D bill}}}\uc2  that outlaws most classroom discussion of gender identity and sexual orientation topics, as well as a law {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2021/apr/29/florida-bill-transgender-school-sports-ban-women-girls"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banning transgender athletes}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 DoJ tightens rules around some staff attending election events\par \par \uc2 Political appointees at the \uc2 US Department of Justice\uc2  (DoJ) will be barred from attending campaign events or fundraisers, according to new guidance issued by attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  today, ahead of November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 I know you agree it is critical that we hold ourselves to the highest ethical standards to avoid even the appearance of political influence as we carry out the department\u8217\'20\'19s mission. It is in that spirit that I have added these new restrictions on political activities by non-career employees,\u8221\'20\'1D Garland wrote in a memo.\par \par \uc2 While it is common for the justice department to remind its staff to tread carefully about political activities ahead of election seasons, Garland\u8217\'20\'19s memo contains among the most restrictive policies in recent times.\par \par \uc2 Federal employees in general are subject to the Hatch Act, a law which limits some of their political activities to ensure the government is free from partisan influence.\par \par \uc2 Previously, political appointees at the department were permitted to attend partisan events in their personal capacity, as long as they sought prior approval.\par \par \uc2 Under the new guidance, however, there will be no exceptions \u8211\'20\'13 including on the evening of election day itself.\par \par \uc2 The change comes at a time when the justice department is under a national microscope over its extraordinary decision to search the Florida estate of former Republican president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 This was part of an ongoing criminal investigation into whether he illegally retained government records, including some marked as top secret.\par \par \uc2 In addition to the pressure the department has faced over its investigation into Trump, some of its political appointees have also faced criticism for attending political functions.\par \par \uc2 Republican Senator Tom Cotton of Arkansas in July called for an investigation after Rachael Rollins, an outspoken progressive prosecutor who serves as the US attorney for Massachusetts, attended a Democratic fundraiser that month that was also attended by first lady Jill Biden.\par \par \uc2 Rollins in a tweet following news reports on her attendance said she had \u8220\'20\'1Capproval to meet Dr. Biden & left early to speak at 2 community events\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for Rollins did not immediately respond to a request for comment on today.\par \par \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 . Photograph: Brendan Smialowski/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  is holding a gaggle aboard Air Force One, as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  heads to Wilkes-Barre, Pennsylvania, to talk about gun safety.\par \par \uc2 The first topic in the gaggle is the flooding in Mississippi and the failure of the Jackson area water treatment services, which has caused a crisis over clean drinking water.\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre indicated the federal government is standing by in the event of a request from the state for federal supplies of water. Meanwhile, she said the \uc2 Federal Emergency Management Agency\uc2  (Fema) is liaising.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe state has created an incident command center to step in and restore water at the city\u8217\'20\'19s plant. We are sending a request for a federally-declared disaster to support state and city emergencies. Clear communication between locals/state/feds. Please keep Jackson in your prayers! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/fmTPpqNu10"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/fmTPpqNu10}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Governor \uc2 Tate Reeves\uc2  (@tatereeves) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/tatereeves/status/1564661750355697667?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 30, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is on his way to Pennsylvania, where he will give an address this afternoon promoting an assault weapons ban, while attacking Republicans over crime, and calls by some in the party to defund the \uc2 FBI\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The president is scheduled to speak at 3.15pm in Wilkes-Barre, one of three upcoming appearances in the key swing state where a \uc2 US Senate\uc2  seat and governorship are at stake in the November\u8217\'20\'19s election, now just 10 weeks away.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you his speech when it begins, and news from White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s lunchtime \u8220\'20\'1Cgaggle\u8221\'20\'1D with reporters onboard Air Force One.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19ve been following:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/secret-service"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Secret Service}}}\uc2  official Tony Ornato, a figure of intense interest to the congressional committee investigating the January 6 Capitol attack, has retired from the agency. He was an eyewitness to some of the most critical incidents involving {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  in the hours leading up to the deadly assault on the US Capitol.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 NBC News reported that Trump has hired a criminal attorney who was once Florida\u8217\'20\'19s solicitor to his legal team. Chris Kise is expected to make his first appearance in federal court in West Palm Beach on Thursday when district judge Aileen Cannon mulls Trump\u8217\'20\'19s request for a special master to oversee the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s review of classified materials seized by the \uc2 FBI\uc2  at his home.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re awaiting at any moment the justice department \u8217\'20\'19s legal response to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s request, which will be a lengthy filing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.flsd.618763/gov.uscourts.flsd.618763.33.0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 running up to 40 pages}}}\uc2  after Cannon waived a 20-page limit imposed by the court.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Incumbent Democratic Arizona senator Mark Kelly leads Republican challenger \uc2 Blake Masters\uc2  by more than three points in a poll released today, appearing to confirm a growing belief within the party that pro-choice messaging on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be vote-winner in November\u8217\'20\'19s midterms.\par \par \uc2 Stay with us for what will surely be a busy afternoon.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Up the workers! A poll has found increased approval among US citizens for labor unions to its highest point in more than half a century.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/398303/approval-labor-unions-highest-point-1965.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gallup survey}}}\uc2  reveals that 71% have a favorable view of unions and union activity, up three points from a year ago and matching the figure from 1965. Peak public approval came in 1953 at 75%.\par \par \uc2 enltr71% of Americans now approve of labor unions. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ATbdyzrVyc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/ATbdyzrVyc}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6OiARAHt7j"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/6OiARAHt7j}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 GallupNews (@GallupNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GallupNews/status/1564583282100305921?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 30, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The Covid-19 pandemic is, the study says, at least partly responsible for this renewed enthusiasm, which reflects a steady rise from only 48% approval just over a decade ago:\par \par \uc2 The low unemployment rate that developed during the pandemic altered the balance of power between employers and employees, creating an environment fostering union membership that has resulted in the formation of unions at several high-profile companies.\par \par \uc2 While already on an upswing, public approval of unions has only increased further during the pandemic and is now at a level not seen in nearly six decades.\par \par \uc2 Several large companies, including \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  and \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , have led a backlash against unionization in their workforces, the Guardian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/25/starbucks-union-employees-fired"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reporting this week}}}\uc2  that the coffee giant had created a \u8220\'20\'1Cculture of fear\u8221\'20\'1D and fired dozens of workers involved in union activism.\par \par \uc2 Workers for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/aug/03/delta-flights-attendants-union-push"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 airlines}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/08/ups-drivers-union-heat-temperatures-climate-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 delivery companies}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/aug/16/mcdonalds-sexual-harassment-retaliation-firings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fast food restaurants}}}\uc2 , in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/23/minnesota-nurses-strike-vote-safety-conditions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 medical profession}}}\uc2  and even {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/18/los-angeles-strip-club-dancers-unionize-actors-equity-association"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strippers }}}\uc2  have all been featured in the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-unions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent coverage}}}\uc2  of labor unions.\par \par \uc2 Read the views of Bernie Sanders, Vermont senator and a former candidate for the Democratic party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nomination, on the importance of unions:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/30/people-are-tired-of-being-ignored-while-the-rich-get-richer-bernie-sanders-on-anger-and-hope-in-the-us-and-uk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18People are tired of being ignored while the rich get richer\u8217\'20\'19: Bernie Sanders on anger and hope in the US and UK}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 There are exactly 10 weeks until November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections, and Democrats are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/11/democrats-midterms-win-projections-biden-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 daring to believe}}}\uc2  that what was once expected to be a Republican rout might not yet come to pass.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thetrafalgargroup.org/news/az-sen-0829/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 only one poll}}}\uc2 , but some good news for the party comes from Arizona, where incumbent Democrat Mark Kelly leads Republican challenger \uc2 Blake Masters\uc2  by more than three points.\par \par \uc2 Mark Kelly. Photograph: \uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Kelly is among Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 top targets as they seek to win back control of the Senate, but Arizona appears to be one of a number of states where the Supreme Court\u8217\'20\'19s reversal of federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections this summer appears to be resonating.\par \par \uc2 Masters, who believes in a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/newsletters/weekly-score/2022/08/29/a-battle-of-the-extremes-00054025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 federal personhood law}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D recognizing unborn babies as human beings, has been attempting to promote the argument that his approach is common sense, and it\u8217\'20\'19s Kelly\u8217\'20\'19s support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/newsletters/weekly-score/2022/08/29/a-battle-of-the-extremes-00054025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 represents the \u8220\'20\'1Cextreme\u8221\'20\'1D position}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 NBC reported that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2022-election/arizona-blake-masters-backtracks-abortion-scrubs-campaign-website-rcna44808"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Masters has backtracked}}}\uc2 , and replaced pro-life statements on his campaign website with softer messaging.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s a long way to go of course, in Arizona and elsewhere, but there are signs the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate could prove a clear vote-winner for Democrats in November. Last week in New York, pro-choice Democrat Pat Ryan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/24/democrat-who-campaigned-on-abortion-rights-wins-in-new-york-special-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defeated his opponent }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/24/democrat-who-campaigned-on-abortion-rights-wins-in-new-york-special-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Marc Molinaro}}}\uc2  in a swing House seat expected to fall to the Republican.\par \par \uc2 Masters is not the only Republican candidate appearing to realize that presenting a strong anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  message could be harmful in the fall election. CNN has details of a number of GOP hopefuls {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/08/29/politics/republicans-shift-abortion-positions-general-election/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Ctrying to shift or paper over\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  their more conservative positions.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Top US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/secret-service"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Secret Service}}}\uc2  official Tony Ornato, who has become a figure of intense interest to the congressional committee investigating the January 6 Capitol attack, has retired from the agency.\par \par \uc2 Ornato was thrust into the center of the January 6 furor as an eyewitness to some of the most critical incidents involving {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  in the hours leading up to the deadly assault on the US Capitol.\par \par \uc2 He began as head of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Secret Service detail but in an unprecedented move in December 2019 became deputy chief of staff in the White House.\par \par \uc2 In that capacity, he was drawn into the sights of the January 6 committee in its investigation of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s role in inciting the Capitol insurrection. A former White House aide, Cassidy Hutchinson, in June {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/28/january-6-committee-session-new-evidence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 testified publicly}}}\uc2  to the committee that Ornato had told her Trump had become \u8220\'20\'1Cirate\u8221\'20\'1D when his security detail refused to drive him to the Capitol as the assault on Congress was beginning.\par \par \uc2 Cassidy Hutchinson testifies to the 6 January committee in June. Photograph: Jacquelyn Martin/AP\par \par \uc2 The attack aimed to prevent the congressional certification of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s defeat to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in the 2020 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 When his Secret Service driver insisted it was not safe to go, Trump lunged for the steering wheel and then grabbed the agent\u8217\'20\'19s throat, Hutchinson testified Ornato had told her. Ornato {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ShimonPro/status/1541938642918178819"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly denied}}}\uc2  the account through unnamed sources.\par \par \uc2 Hutchinson also revealed to the committee that Ornato had briefed top White House aides on January 6 itself that weapons were being carried among the crowd at the Capitol, including guns, knives and spears. Ornato has not denied that allegation.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, he confirmed that he had retired from the Secret Service, saying in a statement that he wanted to work in the private sector. He has already been interviewed twice by the January 6 committee, though the contents of his testimony have not been made public.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/30/secret-service-tony-ornato-january-6-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Top Secret Service official at heart of January 6 Trump row steps down}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Talking of the \uc2 FBI\uc2  raid on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Florida mansion, NBC News is reporting that the former president has hired a criminal attorney who was once the state\u8217\'20\'19s solicitor general.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/donald-trump/trump-hires-former-florida-solicitor-general-criminal-probe-mar-lago-d-rcna45383"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to the network}}}\uc2 , Chris Kise, who has close ties to both \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , Florida\u8217\'20\'19s ultra-conservative Republican governor, and DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s predecessor and current US Senator \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2 , joined Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team after the 8 August raid.\par \par \uc2 Kise, NBC says, has a reputation as a \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitical knife fighter\u8221\'20\'1D and has \u8220\'20\'1Ca winning record\u8221\'20\'1D in the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Sources have confirmed the hiring to the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEWS: Trump signed \u8220\'20\'1C360 degree lawyer\u8221\'20\'1D to rep him in the Mar-a-Lago documents case: former Florida Solicitor General Chris Kise, who has notched 4 wins before {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Scotus?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SCOTUS}}}\uc2  and has a reputation as a political knife fighter {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/cWuLw966mA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/cWuLw966mA}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Marc Caputo (@MarcACaputo) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MarcACaputo/status/1564610286761480202?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 30, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Trump has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vanityfair.com/news/2022/08/donald-trump-lawyer-problems-classified-documents-raid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struggled to find and retain experienced lawyers}}}\uc2  as he fights criminal and civil proceedings and investigations on multiple fronts, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/13/nuclear-or-not-classified-or-not-mar-a-lago-files-spell-out-jeopardy-for-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 none placing him in more legal jeopardy}}}\uc2  than the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s investigation into his alleged retention of highly classified documents after he left office last year\par \par \uc2 The hiring of Kise would appear to buck that trend. He is expected to make his first appearance as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attorney in federal court in West Palm Beach on Thursday, NBC says.\par \par \uc2 At that hearing, district judge Aileen Cannon will mull whether to grant the former president\u8217\'20\'19s request for a special master to oversee the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s review of materials seized by the \uc2 FBI\uc2  at his home.\par \par \uc2 Boris Epshteyn is staying on as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s in-house legal adviser, the \uc2 Guardian\uc2  understands. Others on his legal team for the documents case are Evan Corcoran, Jim Trusty and Lindsey Halligan.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Justice department to file 'special master' response\par \par \uc2 A little later this morning we\u8217\'20\'19re expecting to see the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s legal response to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/20/trump-mar-a-lago-search-fbi-legal-motion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 request for a \u8220\'20\'1Cspecial master\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  to oversee its review of classified documents seized by the \uc2 FBI\uc2  in a raid on his Florida home.\par \par \uc2 It will be a lengthy filing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.flsd.618763/gov.uscourts.flsd.618763.33.0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 running up to 40 pages}}}\uc2  after Florida district judge Aileen Cannon waived a 20-page limit imposed by the court.\par \par \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 . Photograph: Brendan Smialowski/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 The justice department argued the lower limit wasn\u8217\'20\'19t sufficient to \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1564378464345546753"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 adequately address the legal and factual issues}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D raised by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s demand.\par \par \uc2 Many observers see the former president\u8217\'20\'19s move as a delaying tactic to the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s investigation, given that any special master \u8211\'20\'13 usually a retired lawyer or judge \u8211\'20\'13 would require time to review all the materials.\par \par \uc2 As the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/26/doj-redacted-trump-affidavit-mar-a-lago-search"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Guardian has previously reported}}}\uc2 , \uc2 FBI\uc2  agents confiscated about 30 boxes containing highly sensitive documents from his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/mar-a-lago"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mar-a-Lago}}}\uc2  resort in an investigation into the unauthorized retention of government secrets. Attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  approved the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s request for a warrant to carry out the raid.\par \par \uc2 Cannon\u8217\'20\'19s order said the justice department had to file its response to the Trump request \u8220\'20\'1Con or before Tuesday\u8221\'20\'1D. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team will have until 8pm Wednesday to give a reply, and Cannon has scheduled a hearing for Thursday at which she is expected to make a decision.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you details of the justice department filing as we get them.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 More than two-fifths of Americans believe civil war is at least somewhat likely in the next 10 years, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://today.yougov.com/topics/politics/articles-reports/2022/08/26/two-in-five-americans-civil-war-somewhat-likely"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a new survey}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a figure that increases to more than half among self-identified \u8220\'20\'1Cstrong Republicans\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Amid heated rhetoric from supporters of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the findings, in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://today.yougov.com/topics/politics/articles-reports/2022/08/26/two-in-five-americans-civil-war-somewhat-likely"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 research}}}\uc2  by \uc2 YouGov\uc2  and the Economist, follow {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.science.org/content/article/half-of-americans-anticipate-a-us-civil-war-soon-survey-finds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 similar results}}}\uc2  in other polls.\par \par \uc2 On Sunday night, the South Carolina senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/29/lindsey-graham-riots-trump-prosecuted-records"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 predicted}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Criots in the streets\u8221\'20\'1D if Trump is indicted over his retention of classified documents after leaving the White House, materials recovered by the \uc2 FBI\uc2  at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s home this month.\par \par \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 . Photograph: Sarah Silbiger/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Graham earned widespread {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/29/lindsey-graham-riots-trump-prosecuted-records"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rebuke}}}\uc2 . On Monday, Mary McCord, a former acting deputy attorney general, told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/brikeilarcnn/status/1564238823122509824?s=20&t=yGU9qFfhmkgQfiZ617TYBA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN}}}\uc2  it was \u8220\'20\'1Cincredibly irresponsible for an elected official to basically make veiled threats of violence, just if law enforcement and the Department of Justice \u8230\'20\'26 does their job\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Saying \u8220\'20\'1Cpeople are angry, they may be violent\u8221\'20\'1D, McCord said, showed that \u8220\'20\'1Cwhat [Trump] knows and what {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/people/lindsey-graham/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lindsey Graham }}}\uc2  also knows \u8230\'20\'26 is that people listen to that and people actually mobilise and do things.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJanuary 6 was the result of this same kind of tactic by President Trump and his allies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/01/05/us/politics/jan-6-capitol-deaths.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nine deaths}}}\uc2  including suicides among police officers have been linked to the Capitol attack on 6 January 2021, when supporters Trump told to \u8220\'20\'1Cfight like hell\u8221\'20\'1D to overturn his defeat by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  attempted to stop the certification of electoral results.\par \par \uc2 Since then, fears of political violence have grown.\par \par \uc2 Most experts believe a full-scale armed conflict, like the American civil war of 1861-65, remains unlikely.\par \par \uc2 But many fear an increase of jagged political division and explicitly political violence, particularly as Republican politicians who support Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lie about electoral fraud run for Congress, governor\u8217\'20\'19s mansions and key state elections posts.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/29/us-civil-war-fears-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 More than 40% of Americans think civil war likely within a decade}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 An assault weapons ban is back on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s agenda today as he heads to Pennsylvania to deliver a speech on guns, crime and Republican attacks on the \uc2 FBI\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The push for a ban is a centerpiece of the president\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/08/01/fact-sheet-president-bidens-safer-america-plan-2/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Safer America Plan}}}\uc2  unveiled earlier his month, and Biden will use his afternoon address in Wilkes-Barre to hammer Republicans for their opposition to it.\par \par \uc2 A series of deadly mass shootings has propelled {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/gun-crime"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gun violence}}}\uc2  back into prominence, and the White House says, during his remarks in Pennsylvania, Biden will continue to press for a reinstatement of the ban, believing it will resonate with voters ahead of the November midterms, 10 weeks ahead today.\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  addresses reporters on Monday. Photograph: Oliver Contreras/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  told reporters at her briefing Monday:\par \par \uc2 The president is going to talk about how he brought the Democrats and Republicans together earlier this month to pass the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/25/joe-biden-signs-gun-control-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most significant safety law in 30 years}}}\uc2 . He\u8217\'20\'19ll talk about how we have built on that momentum and how we must act on banning assault weapons.\par \par \uc2 A majority of Americans support\u8230\'20\'26 banning assault weapons; the \uc2 National Rifle Association\uc2  opposes it. We are going to hear from the president about the importance of making sure that we protect our communities.\par \par \uc2 [He] has been really clear that congressional Republicans, that extreme MAGA [Make America Great Again] agenda that you heard him talk about last week is a threat to the rule of law.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s the first of three visits Biden will make to the key battleground state of Pennsylvania in six days. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://discuss/%20how%20America’s%20standing%20in%20the%20world%20and%20its%20own%20democracy%20are%20at%20stake"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 On Thursday he will give a primetime address}}}\uc2  from Philadelphia on \u8220\'20\'1Cthe continued battle for the soul of the nation,\u8221\'20\'1D covering America\u8217\'20\'19s standing in the world and how its democracy is at stake.\par \par \uc2 On Labor Day, next Monday, he will be in Pittsburgh celebrating {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/administration/3619550-biden-to-visit-wisconsin-pennsylvania-for-labor-day/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cthe dignity of American workers.\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s administration, while carefully avoiding commentary on the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s investigation into former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and the \uc2 FBI\uc2  raid on his Florida resort that netted hidden classified documents, nevertheless sees opportunity in the moment.\par \par \uc2 Some extreme Republicans have called for defunding the \uc2 FBI\uc2  in protest at the raid. Biden will use today\u8217\'20\'19s speech to promote Democrats as the party of law and order and tough on crime, reiterating that fully funding law enforcement is another key tenet of the Safer America plan.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Good morning, and welcome to Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s US politics blog.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has a busy day ahead, and will use a visit to Pennsylvania to hammer Republicans on guns, crime, and calls by some in the party to defund the \uc2 FBI\uc2  after the agency\u8217\'20\'19s raid on former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s Florida resort.\par \par \uc2 Biden is expected to renew calls for an assault weapons ban, something Republicans in Congress remain resolutely opposed to despite a recent series of deadly mass shootings.\par \par \uc2 The president is scheduled to give remarks in Wilkes-Barre at 3.15pm. We\u8217\'20\'19ll have more details about that coming up.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re watching today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The fallout from the seizure of classified documents from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Palm Beach residence continues. We\u8217\'20\'19re expecting a legal response from the justice department to the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s demand for a \u8220\'20\'1Cspecial master\u8221\'20\'1D to be appointed to oversee the review of what was found.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s renewed hope among Democrats for their prospects in November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections. A poll in Arizona shows Democratic senator Mark Kelly, a top Republican target, leading his opponent by more than three points.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  will address reporters on board Air Force One en route to Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Congress is on summer recess, so we\u8217\'20\'19re not anticipating much excitement in Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220830ei8u001xi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
