\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Are Latino voters really moving right? The end of Roe may muddy the picture\b0\par\par\uc2 Salom\u233\'00\'E9 G\u243\'00\'F3mez-Upegui \par \uc2 1,121 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 August 2022\par 14:32 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Latinos support reproductive rights by large margins \u8211\'20\'13 and that could prove a powerful mobilizing tool in the midterms\par \par \uc2 After the Republican party made some inroads among Latino voters in the 2020 presidential election, when Latino support for Trump went up by 3% {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/article/usa-election-exitpoll-idUKL1N2HP2VN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 compared with 2016}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2021/07/11/1014967344/latino-voters-are-leaving-the-democratic-party"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 many commentators}}}\uc2  declared this group was decisively moving away from the Democratic party.\par \par \uc2 As November\u8217\'20\'19s midterms approach, the GOP is aiming to capitalize on these gains. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/15/mayra-flores-texas-house-republican-special-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent victory}}}\uc2  of the Latina Republican Mayra Flores, who won a congressional seat representing southern Texas, is one they are hoping to replicate across the country.\par \par \uc2 Yet, with increased support largely limited to Florida and Texas, the political landscape is more complicated than it seems heading into this year\u8217\'20\'19s midterms, and experts say the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn Roe v Wade may play a role in halting the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s gains.\par \par \uc2 Christine Sierra, professor emerita of political science at the \uc2 University of New Mexico\uc2  and a specialist in Latino politics, says that any Republican gains in the 2020 presidential election did not mark a definitive trend. \u8220\'20\'1CWhile Republicans managed to make a few inroads in very specific counties in Florida and Texas, for example, Democrats maintain a majority of the Latino vote,\u8221\'20\'1D she recently told the Guardian. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://catalist.us/wh-national/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 More than 60%}}}\uc2  of Latinos voted for Joe Biden.\par \par \uc2 Historically, Latinos have focused on issues such as economics, jobs, education and immigration to determine their vote \u8211\'20\'13 areas in which the GOP believes it has an upper hand among more moderate voters. However, the quickly changing landscape of sexual and reproductive rights in the United States might influence what matters most to Latino voters. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans are expected to have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reproductiverights.org/supreme-court-case-mississippi-abortion-ban-disproportionate-harm/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a greater effect on women of color}}}\uc2 , and Latina women {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/infographic/2016/us-abortion-patients"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 account for about 25%}}}\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients in the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow, given the controversy and salience of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as an issue, it may go to the top one, two, or three issues [that matter to Latinos],\u8221\'20\'1D Sierra said.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://medium.com/@votolatino/latinos-in-battleground-states-support-gun-control-abortion-rights-692e59ea2170"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll}}}\uc2  conducted in June by Change Research on behalf of the political organization Voto Latino found that 64% of Latinos in battleground states \u8220\'20\'1Care more motivated to vote in November\u8221\'20\'1D due to the fall of Roe, and 52% are \u8220\'20\'1Cmuch more motivated\u8221\'20\'1D. The poll surveyed Latino voters in Texas, Arizona, Nevada, Florida, Georgia, North Carolina and Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 Another poll by the same organization conducted in May found that across the battleground states of Arizona, Pennsylvania, Nevada and Georgia, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://medium.com/@votolatino/latino-battleground-poll-results-a-strong-majority-support-protecting-abortion-access-democrats-486f4da086b7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 70% of Latino voters}}}\uc2  are in favor of protecting the right to choose. At least 30% of Latino Republicans in these states believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal \u8220\'20\'1Cin all or most cases\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Moreover, a recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ipsos.com/en-us/news-polls/axios-latino-views-on-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Axios-Ipsos Latino poll}}}\uc2  in partnership with Noticias Telemundo revealed at least 50% of Latino voters in the US say \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal while another 21% don\u8217\'20\'19t have a view. One-fourth believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be illegal \u8220\'20\'1Cat any time under any circumstances\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Lina-Maria Murillo, assistant professor of gender, women\u8217\'20\'19s and sexuality studies as well as history and Latinx studies at the \uc2 University of Iowa\uc2 , believes this extreme conservative stance among a minority of Latino voters can be traced back to the influence of the evangelical Christian church, where Latinos {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2022/06/23/latino-evangelical-leader-latino-voters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have been }}}\uc2  considered \u8220\'20\'1Cone of the fastest growing segments\u8217\'20\'19\u8217\'20\'19, and of which Flores is a member. Bucking what Murillo says is a common stereotype that Latinos oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to their Catholicism, the May {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://medium.com/@votolatino/latino-battleground-poll-results-a-strong-majority-support-protecting-abortion-access-democrats-486f4da086b7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Voto Latino poll}}}\uc2  shows Catholic Latinos support a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose at about the same rate as Latinos in general.\par \par \uc2 Still, Ameer Patel, vice-president of programs at Voto Latino, says the belief that Latinos are generally conservative is more anecdotal than anything else. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re actually really in favor of reproductive rights. And that number obviously increases when we look at younger Latinos,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. In the May Voto Latino poll, 75% of respondents between the ages of 18 through 39 said they support a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose.\par \par \uc2 Every year, about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.unidosus.org/issues/voting-and-political-empowerment/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 1 million Latinos}}}\uc2  turn 18 and become eligible to vote in the US. Patel says their stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  represents a unique mobilization opportunity for Democrats. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you\u8217\'20\'19re able to use this as a mobilization issue for young Latino voters in places like Arizona, Georgia and Nevada, this is an extremely powerful tool,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 In Arizona, where the end of Roe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/25/arizona-planned-parenthood-abortion-state-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could revive a civil war-era law}}}\uc2  banning abortions, Latinos account for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://newsroom.ucla.edu/releases/latino-vote-analysis-2020-presidential-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about 25% of voters and played a critical role }}}\uc2  in flipping the state in the 2020 presidential election. Moreover, 64% of respondents to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://medium.com/@votolatino/latino-battleground-poll-results-a-strong-majority-support-protecting-abortion-access-democrats-486f4da086b7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Voto Latino poll in Arizona}}}\uc2  said they would not support a candidate who stands for a complete \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, stating \u8220\'20\'1Cit would be a deal breaker.\u8221\'20\'1D This picture could affect contests like the attorney general race, where the Republican candidate Abraham Hamadeh has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://knst.iheart.com/featured/garret-lewis/content/2022-07-01-garret-talks-to-abraham-hamadeh-about-scotus-rulings-az-abortion-law/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 campaigned on the promise}}}\uc2  of upholding Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws.\par \par \uc2 Patel says Republicans are taking note of this trend and choosing not to focus on reproductive rights as an issue to sway Latino voters, \u8220\'20\'1Cbecause [they know] this is not a message they can win them on\u8221\'20\'1D. While Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic candidate for governor, \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2 , has been outspoken about her stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , for instance, the Republican candidate, Kari Lake, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.azcentral.com/story/opinion/op-ed/ej-montini/2022/08/04/abortion-katie-hobbs-stance-solid-and-kari-lake-squishy/10236018002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has recently shied away}}}\uc2  from discussing the issue. In Texas, the Democratic candidate \uc2 Beto O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke\uc2  has repeatedly vowed to repeal the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban if elected governor. In Florida, the Republican governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.msnbc.com/opinion/msnbc-opinion/why-ron-desantis-avoiding-talking-about-abortion-n1296843"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 avoiding the subject.}}}\par \par \uc2 Murillo believes the role of Latinas working for reproductive justice is often overlooked. \u8220\'20\'1CIf we look at some of the major \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds in Texas, like West Fund and Frontera Fund, they have been established and are run by Latinx folks,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 If O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke can \u8220\'20\'1Cgalvanize the youth in Texas, especially around issues of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D, said Murillo, \u8220\'20\'1Cthen I think he has a chance and I think that Latinx people in Texas have a major role to play in that\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 According to a \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/08/14/us/politics/abortion-midterms-2022-ads-democrats.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 analysis}}}\uc2 , Democrats are vastly outspending Republicans on midterm ads talking about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Still, Murillo believes Democrats are not fully seizing the opportunity to sway Latino voters. \u8220\'20\'1CDemocrats are stuck in these old pandering ways; they\u8217\'20\'19re not seeing the changes that are coming and the ways that Latinx people are not a monolith and that the youth component of this community is overwhelmingly progressive,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 If Democrats don\u8217\'20\'19t act, she says, while Latino voters \u8220\'20\'1Care not necessarily going to be turning to Republicans, they may just not vote at all\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220830ei8u002xm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
