\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US judge orders Trump Mar-a-Lago affidavit to be unsealed with redactions \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein in Washington \par \uc2 4,877 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 August 2022\par 20:31 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bruce Reinhart gives \uc2 US government\uc2  until noon ET Friday to make the redacted document publicSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Tomorrow may bring more details of just what the \uc2 FBI\uc2  was looking for when it searched \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago resort earlier this month, after a federal judge ordered the affidavit for the search made public by Friday at noon eastern time. However, the justice department will redact the document first and could appeal the decision entirely, meaning it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear how many new details will be released, if any.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/25/trump-fbi-documents-mar-a-lago-biden-student-debt-campaign-latest-updates?page=with:block-6307a04f8f08b9ef100e15fa#block-6307a04f8f08b9ef100e15fa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 set to appear}}}\uc2  at Democratic fundraisers ahead of the midterm elections, as the party aims to maintain its majority in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former attorney general Bill Barr said the ex-president controls the Republican party {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/25/trump-fbi-documents-mar-a-lago-biden-student-debt-campaign-latest-updates?page=with:block-6307c91f8f088e8ce8eb0908#block-6307c91f8f088e8ce8eb0908"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 through \u8220\'20\'1Cextortion\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A brass band{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/25/trump-fbi-documents-mar-a-lago-biden-student-debt-campaign-latest-updates?page=with:block-6307873f8f08b9ef100e145d#block-6307873f8f08b9ef100e145d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeared}}}\uc2  before the White House to thank \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  for relieving student debt, though some {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/25/trump-fbi-documents-mar-a-lago-biden-student-debt-campaign-latest-updates?page=with:block-63078f698f08b9ef100e14f9#block-63078f698f08b9ef100e14f9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats aren\u8217\'20\'19t comfortable with }}}\uc2  the plan.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/25/trump-fbi-documents-mar-a-lago-biden-student-debt-campaign-latest-updates?page=with:block-6307836f8f08b9ef100e1411#block-6307836f8f08b9ef100e1411"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plans to unveil}}}\uc2  a federal rule to protect \u8220\'20\'1Cdreamers\u8221\'20\'1D, as undocumented immigrants who came to the United States as children are known, but it could still face a court challenge.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Texas, Tennessee and Idaho became the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/25/trump-fbi-documents-mar-a-lago-biden-student-debt-campaign-latest-updates?page=with:block-6307aea28f088e8ce8eb0826#block-6307aea28f088e8ce8eb0826"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 latest US states to ban \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden pledged{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/25/trump-fbi-documents-mar-a-lago-biden-student-debt-campaign-latest-updates?page=with:block-6307beab8f08b9ef100e1785#block-6307beab8f08b9ef100e1785"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 continued support}}}\uc2  for Ukraine in a phone call with its president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Federal judge orders Mar-a-Lago search affidavit unsealed, with redactions\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  reports that a federal judge has ordered a redacted version of the affidavit for the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s search of Mar-a-Lago unsealed:\par \par \uc2 enltrJust in: Federal Judge orders the Trump Mar-a-Lago affidavit to be unsealed in part with redactions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zzd7gNASgf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/zzd7gNASgf}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1562887333955108865?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Bruce Reinhart, the magistrate judge handling the case, gave the government until noon eastern time tomorrow to make the redacted document public.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI find that the Government has met its burden of showing a compelling reason/good cause to seal portions of the Affidavit,\u8221\'20\'1D Reinhart wrote in the filing. The portions that will be excluded include identifying information of witnesses, grand jury material and details of the investigation\u8217\'20\'19s strategy and direction, he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI further find that the Government has met its burden of showing that its proposed redactions are narrowly tailored to serve the Government\u8217\'20\'19s legitimate interest in the integrity of the ongoing investigation and are the least onerous alternative to sealing the entire Affidavit.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 In Alabama, \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levine}}}\uc2  has the story of how one resident\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuit opened the door for a majority Black city to finally have a city council representative of its racial makeup:\par \par \uc2 A few years ago, Eric Calhoun felt out of touch with his city council in Pleasant Grove, a small {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/alabama"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alabama}}}\uc2  city of just under 10,000 people outside of Birmingham.\par \par \uc2 Calhoun, who is 71 and has lived in the city for nearly three decades, couldn\u8217\'20\'19t find contact information for any of the five council members online. During the 2016 election, none of the white candidates running asked him for his vote. Voters in the city had never elected a Black person to the city council. Calhoun, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.census.gov/quickfacts/fact/table/pleasantgrovecityalabama,US/PST045221"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  like 61% of the city}}}\uc2 , is Black.\par \par \uc2 In 2018, Calhoun became a plaintiff in a federal lawsuit that argued the racial makeup of the city council in Pleasant Grove was not an accident. The way the city was choosing its city council candidates made {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/feb/28/alabama-pleasant-grove-fight-to-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nearly impossible}}}\uc2  for a Black candidate to get elected. Essentially, the city allowed city council candidates to run citywide, instead of in districts, allowing blocs of white voters in the city to come together and defeat candidates preferred by Black voters.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/25/alabama-pleasant-grove-city-council-black-majority"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 He challenged his all-white city council in Alabama. Now he\u8217\'20\'19s on it}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 In yet another sign that the two men are no longer friends, Bill Barr, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attorney general from 2019 until just before the end of his time in the White House, accused the former president of using \u8220\'20\'1Cextortion\u8221\'20\'1D to control Republicans.\par \par \uc2 The comments came during an interview with Barr on podcast Honestly with Bari Weiss:\par \par \uc2 enltrFormer Attorney General Bill Barr accuses \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  of using "extortion" to "exert control over the Republican Party":\par \par \uc2 "That shows what he's all about. He's all about himself." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/EgPVwXUghQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/EgPVwXUghQ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1562874976772014080?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press reports that guilty pleas have been entered in the bizarre case of two people in Florida who tried to sell possessions belonging to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s daughter to conservative activists:\par \par \uc2 Two Florida residents have pleaded guilty in a scheme to sell a diary and other items belonging to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s daughter to the conservative group Project Veritas for $40,000, prosecutors said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Aimee Harris and Robert Kurlander pleaded guilty to conspiracy to commit interstate transportation of stolen property, the office of the Manhattan US attorney \uc2 Damian Williams\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHarris and Kurlander sought to profit from their theft of another person\u8217\'20\'19s personal property, and they now stand convicted of a federal felony as a result,\u8221\'20\'1D Williams said.\par \par \uc2 Requests for comment were sent to lawyers for Harris, 40, of Palm Beach, and Kurlander, 58, and to Project Veritas.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/25/ashley-biden-steal-diary-project-veritas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Duo plead guilty to plot to sell Biden daughter\u8217\'20\'19s stolen diary to Project Veritas}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden reaffirms support for Ukraine in phone call with Zelenskiy\par \par \uc2 US president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  called Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s president \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  today, and reaffirmed his support for the country against Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the full readout from the White House:\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joseph R. Biden\uc2 , Jr. spoke today with President \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskyy\uc2  of Ukraine. He congratulated Ukraine on its Independence Day and expressed his admiration for the people of Ukraine, who have inspired the world as they defended their country\u8217\'20\'19s sovereignty over the past six months. He reaffirmed the United States\u8217\'20\'19 continued support for Ukraine and provided an update on the ongoing provision of security assistance, including yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s announcement of nearly $3 billion to support Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s defense capabilities for the long term. The two leaders also called for Russia to return full control of the Zaporizhzhya Nuclear Power Plant to Ukraine and for \uc2 International Atomic Energy Agency\uc2  (IAEA) access to the plant.\par \par \uc2 And here\u8217\'20\'19s Zelenskiy\u8217\'20\'19s take:\par \par \uc2 enltrHad a great conversation with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2 . Thanked for the unwavering U.S. support for Ukrainian people \u8211\'20\'13 security and financial. We discussed Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s further steps on our path to the victory over the aggressor and importance of holding Russia accountable for war crimes. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4edng8vkvn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/4edng8vkvn}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ????????? ?????????? (@ZelenskyyUa) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ZelenskyyUa/status/1562842303936741377?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/aug/24/joe-biden-ukraine-military-aid-zelenskiy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden announces $3bn in fresh Ukraine military aid}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 A federal grand jury found a Florida man guilty on hate crime charges for a \u8220\'20\'1Cracially motivated\u8221\'20\'1D attack on a Black man traveling with his family in Seminole, 24 miles west of Tampa, the US justice department {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/opa/pr/florida-man-found-guilty-hate-crime-racially-motivated-attack-against-black-man-driving-his"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The Black man, identified only by as \u8220\'20\'1C JT \u8221\'20\'1D, was driving with his daughter and girlfriend last August when Jordan Patrick Leahy, 29, spewed racial slurs and attempted to run him off the road for nearly a mile.\par \par \uc2 The two drivers then encountered each other at a light, where Leahy got out of his car and \u8220\'20\'1Ctried to assault\u8221\'20\'1D the Black man as he continued to yell racist invective, prosecutors said.\par \par \uc2 Hate crimes, especially against Black, Asian and Jewish Americans, climbed across the US throughout the coronavirus pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/25/florida-man-hate-crime-charges-jordan-patrick-leahy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida man found guilty on hate crime charges for attacking Black man}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Committee for a Responsible Federal Budget is in touch about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s student debt cancellation plan, and unsurprisingly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.crfb.org/blogs/new-student-debt-changes-will-cost-half-trillion-dollars"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 it is not happy}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The nonpartisan Washington think tank says: \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Biden yesterday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://avanan.url-protection.com/v1/url?o=https%3A//r20.rs6.net/tn.jsp%3Ff%3D001RVMwVqxvRqwaUUW-dpr886INiCNMmesaOZcMlbhf4jMiXJMhVShtqd7ZuJKR4UZN3wu21OUHiJLWNdkdL8xCrCgu4YVFz6pkJgM95628So7kkUUJUlOfXwNtsPD-y4a3gpTrQfr7zSsUD-YPVTh1X2BHqJIsFQkfXO4PdtaEjYKvlTb_pArU9dwby92k7HpOems4zwLkQ0UfD8xaWHT6fQn-1oUpReBrNkk6gaCRdeWBILo1y1DuOWC005Zn--XPtYam_Tf7S7MP_LFwykTwn4xHIoU-C5rMeOgVF2Cixxmuz8fGrmYXzUdE6Ximuknymo-WTV1G9INH367msIymAA%3D%3D%26c%3DB1gFhH2PwQ3KP47T4IDjnXc8a0xY_7E87rAZR9rrkcxRumVVam6s4w%3D%3D%26ch%3DIW8aZl7IwLNUqdSDD3NnWrTYlQMonmlenGqmbsKqpr2XLtJ8Eij-mA%3D%3D&g=YWQwZmE5YmI3ZGNhNTViZg==&h=Yjk0NThlNGM0MTRjYjA4YTc5MmI2OWE2ZWQyYTEyNGQxZjU4YmRlY2JiZDFhNTM3Y2U1YmI0NDE4YTE4ZjIzMg==&p=YXAzOmNyZmI6YTpvOmE2YzI5MzhmNmIwYWUzMzY1ZGQ0NWI2YTA0NWFkMGUwOnYxOmg6VA=="}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  a set of changes to student loans \u8211\'20\'13 including cancellation of up to $20,000 for some borrowers \u8211\'20\'13 that will cost between $440bn and $600bn over the next ten years, with a central estimate of roughly $500bn.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCombined with today\u8217\'20\'19s announcement, the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s actions on student loans since the start of the Covid-19 pandemic have cost roughly $800bn. Of that amount, roughly $750bn is due to executive action and regulatory changes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The CRFB adds: \u8220\'20\'1CIt is extremely troubling to see the administration reverse the legislative progress made on deficit reduction.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is long past time that student debt repayments resume, and now it is even more important for policymakers to enact changes that reduce deficits through spending reductions and revenue increases in order to put the national debt on a downward sustainable path.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on Biden\u8217\'20\'19s plan, from Edwin Rios :\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/money/2022/aug/25/biden-student-loan-debt-forgiveness"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden says his student loan relief is \u8216\'20\'18life-changing\u8217\'20\'19. Will it fix the system\u8217\'20\'19s inequities?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Democratic candidate for governor in Texas, \uc2 Beto O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke\uc2 , has released his first general election ads targeting his opponent, the incumbent Republican, Greg Abbott \u8211\'20\'13 and the subject is \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Beto O'Rourke\uc2 . Photograph: Suzanne Cordeiro/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 The ads on an issue proving electorally productive for Democrats across the US as the midterm elections approach, come on the day Texas\u8217\'20\'19s stringent post- Roe v Wade \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban goes into effect.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HADmasoNpyQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 One says}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CFrom this day forward, 25 August, women all across Texas are no longer free to make decisions about our own body, no longer free to choose if a pregnancy is right for us or our families, not even in cases of rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd women will die because of it. Because of Greg Abbott\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law. It\u8217\'20\'19s too extreme. So I\u8217\'20\'19m voting for Beto, who will give women are freedom back.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3O30qRPnIHs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Another}}}\uc2  features a couple, the woman described as a \u8220\'20\'1Clifelong Democrat\u8221\'20\'1D, the man a \u8220\'20\'1Clifelong Republican\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COf course people are going to disagree on the big issues,\u8221\'20\'1D the woman says. \u8220\'20\'1CBut Greg Abbott signed the most extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in the United States.\par \par \uc2 The man says: \u8220\'20\'1CNo exception for rape? No exception for incest? $100,000 fines and jail time?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The woman: \u8220\'20\'1COnly 11% of Texans agree with it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The man: \u8220\'20\'1CI mean, this is a free country. We need a governor that gets that. That\u8217\'20\'19s Beto.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Polling gives Abbott {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/governor/2022/texas/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nearly nine points up}}}\uc2  on O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke. But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/24/democrats-midterms-abortion-pat-ryan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  Lauren Gambino with a look about how focusing on the supreme court ruling which removed the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has paid off so far for Democrats:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/24/democrats-midterms-abortion-pat-ryan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 hopes rise for midterms amid backlash over \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Three US states saw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  trigger bans kick-in on Thursday, Tennessee, Texas and Idaho joining eight other states that have formally outlawed the procedure since the supreme court overturned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  in June.\par \par \uc2 Depending on the state, trigger laws are designed to take effect either immediately following the overturn of Roe or 30 days after the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s transmission of its judgement, which happened on 26 July.\par \par \uc2 Nearly one in three women between the ages of 15 to 44 live in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been banned or mostly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2022/08/22/more-trigger-bans-loom-1-3-women-lose-most-abortion-access-post-roe/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banned.}}}\uc2  According to US census data, that is nearly 21 million women.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMore people will lose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access across the nation as bans take effect in Texas, Tennessee and Idaho. Vast swaths of the nation, especially in the south and midwest, will become \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  deserts that, for many, will be impossible to escape,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Nancy Northup\uc2 , chief executive of the Center of Reproductive Rights, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reproductiverights.org/abortion-trigger-bans-take-effect-in-three-states-tomorrow/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvidence is already mounting of women being turned away despite needing urgent, and in some cases life-saving, medical care. This unfolding public health crisis will only continue to get worse. We will see more and more of these harrowing situations, and once state legislatures reconvene in January, we will see even more states implement \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans and novel laws criminalizing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers, pregnant people, and those who help them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 More:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/25/us-abortion-trigger-bans-laws-tennessee-texas-idaho"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Slew of trigger laws kick in as three more US states ban abortions}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Taiwan has a new American visitor: Republican senator \uc2 Marsha Blackburn\uc2  of Tennessee.\par \par \uc2 enltrI just landed in Taiwan to send a message to Beijing \u8212\'20\'14 we will not be bullied.\par \par \uc2 The United States remains steadfast in preserving freedom around the globe, and will not tolerate efforts to undermine our nation and our allies. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/yVcaYN7yIA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/yVcaYN7yIA}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sen. \uc2 Marsha Blackburn\uc2  (@MarshaBlackburn) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MarshaBlackburn/status/1562841112674328577?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 She elaborated on her reasons for visiting the island {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.blackburn.senate.gov/2022/8/senator-blackburn-lands-in-taiwan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a statement}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Taiwan is our strongest partner in the Indo-Pacific Region. Regular high-level visits to Taipei are long-standing U.S. policy. I will not be bullied by Communist China into turning my back on the island. During my visit to Taiwan, I look forward to hearing directly from the nation\u8217\'20\'19s leadership about their needs and how we can support freedom for the Taiwanese people. I look forward to meeting with leaders in Taipei to advance and strengthen our partnerships.\par \par \uc2 Democratic House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s visit to the island enraged China, which launched military exercises in response. But since then, more American lawmakers have visited what Beijing considers to be a breakaway province.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/aug/14/us-congressional-delegation-visits-taiwan-on-heels-of-pelosi-trip"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US congressional delegation visits Taiwan on heels of Pelosi trip}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 The wheels of justice have ground forward ever so slowly in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s various court battles today. The justice department {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/25/trump-fbi-documents-mar-a-lago-biden-student-debt-campaign-latest-updates?page=with:block-6307a04f8f08b9ef100e15fa#block-6307a04f8f08b9ef100e15fa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appears to have submitted}}}\uc2  the redactions it proposes should a judge decide to release the affidavit for the Mar-a-Lago search. Meanwhile, the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers are due to respond to another judge\u8217\'20\'19s questions about their own lawsuit over the case.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/25/trump-fbi-documents-mar-a-lago-biden-student-debt-campaign-latest-updates?page=with:block-6307a04f8f08b9ef100e15fa#block-6307a04f8f08b9ef100e15fa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 set to appear}}}\uc2  at Democratic fundraisers ahead of the midterm elections, as the party aims to maintain its majority in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A brass band{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/25/trump-fbi-documents-mar-a-lago-biden-student-debt-campaign-latest-updates?page=with:block-6307873f8f08b9ef100e145d#block-6307873f8f08b9ef100e145d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeared}}}\uc2  before the White House to thanks \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  for relieving some student debt, though some {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/25/trump-fbi-documents-mar-a-lago-biden-student-debt-campaign-latest-updates?page=with:block-63078f698f08b9ef100e14f9#block-63078f698f08b9ef100e14f9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats aren\u8217\'20\'19t comfortable with }}}\uc2  the plan.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/25/trump-fbi-documents-mar-a-lago-biden-student-debt-campaign-latest-updates?page=with:block-6307836f8f08b9ef100e1411#block-6307836f8f08b9ef100e1411"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plans to unveil}}}\uc2  a federal rule to protect \u8220\'20\'1Cdreamers\u8221\'20\'1D, as undocumented immigrants who came to the United States as children are known, but it could still face a court challenge.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 It appears the justice department has filed its proposed redactions to the affidavit in the Mar-a-Lago search, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrJust in: New entry on the Trump Mar-a-Lago docket \u8212\'20\'14 under seal \u8212\'20\'14 appears to indicate the Justice Dept has now filed proposed redactions for the \uc2 FBI\uc2  affidavit\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1562832522785894403?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Another lawyer for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  who assisted in his attempt to overturn the result of the 2020 election has filed a court motion resisting a subpoena for his appearance before a special grand jury in Georgia, Politico reports.\par \par \uc2 The panel in Fulton county is looking into election meddling in the state two years ago, and has already heard from testimony \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 , who was informed he is a target of its investigation.\par \par \uc2 enltrJUST IN: Kenneth Chesebro, one of the architects of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's plan to remain in power, is suing to block a Fulton County Grand Jury subpoena, claiming he's bound by attorney-client privilege to the Trump campaign. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/r0RWoRI0y0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/r0RWoRI0y0}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ypvHxXbd22"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ypvHxXbd22}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1562830886885765120?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Republican senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  has also been subpoenaed by the grand jury, but is currently fighting it in court.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 As midterm election campaigns hit the home stretch over the next two months, voters may start seeing a familiar Democratic face: \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2022/08/25/scoop-obama-enters-the-chat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Axios reports}}}\uc2  that the former president is scheduled to appear at two upcoming fundraisers for the party, one of which is focused on Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 campaign to maintain their majority in the Senate, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/2022-election-forecast/senate/?cid=rrpromo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 they seem slightly favored to do}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Justice department expected to submit redactions to Mar-a-Lago search affidavit today\par \par \uc2 The justice department will probably submit today their proposed redactions to the affidavit that justified the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s search of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago resort, US media report.\par \par \uc2 The redactions are likely to be filed under seal, meaning they won\u8217\'20\'19t be available to the public, and come after news organizations and others sought the release of the affidavit that outlines the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s reasons in asking for the warrant authorizing the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s search, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/08/25/us/politics/trump-justice-dept-affidavit.html?smid=tw-nytimes&smtyp=cur"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/justice-department-to-file-redacted-mar-a-lago-affidavit-to-judge-11661433643?mod=e2tw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Wall Street Journal}}}\uc2 . The justice department has until noon eastern time to submit its proposal.\par \par \uc2 A federal judge is weighing how much, if anything, of the affidavit can be made public, which could offer further details into what the justice department is looking into, and how involved the former president might be.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the Times on what the document\u8217\'20\'19s release could mean:\par \par \uc2 The submission by the Justice Department is a significant legal milepost in an investigation that has swiftly emerged as a major threat to Mr. Trump, whose lawyers have offered a confused and at times stumbling response. But it is also an inflection point for Attorney General \uc2 Merrick B. Garland\uc2 , who is trying to balance protecting the prosecutorial process by keeping secret details of the investigation, and providing enough information to defend his decision to request a search unlike any other in history.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are clearly opposed poles here,\u8221\'20\'1D said Daniel C. Richman, a former federal prosecutor and a law professor at \uc2 Columbia University\uc2 , who said it might be difficult, even impossible, for Mr. Garland to strike the right balance.\par \par \uc2 Last week, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/08/18/us/politics/judge-bruce-reinhart-trump-mar-a-lago.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bruce E. Reinhart}}}\uc2 , a federal magistrate judge in Florida, surprised prosecutors by saying he was inclined to release portions of the affidavit at the request of news organizations, including \uc2 The New York Times\uc2 , after the government proposed redactions.\par \par \uc2 Disclosing even a partial version of the affidavit would be highly unusual: Such documents, which typically include evidence gathered to justify the search, like information provided by witnesses, are almost never unsealed before the government files criminal charges. There is no indication the Justice Department plans to file charges anytime soon.\par \par \uc2 Judge Reinhart reiterated this week that he might {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/08/22/us/politics/trump-warrant-affidavit-reinhart.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 agree to extensive redactions}}}\uc2 , acknowledging that they could be severe enough to render release of the final document \u8220\'20\'1Cmeaningless.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI cannot say at this point that partial redactions will be so extensive that they will result in a meaningless disclosure, but I may ultimately reach that conclusion after hearing further from the government,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote in an order issued on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/18/trump-redacted-affidavit-release-mar-a-lago-fbi-search"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Judge orders DoJ to prepare redacted Trump search affidavit for possible release}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 While many in the party cheered Biden\u8217\'20\'19s student debt relief plan, some lawmakers who are in tough re-election fights expressed hesitancy towards it.\par \par \uc2 Colorado senator Michael Benne t argued that it should have been more narrowly targeted:\par \par \uc2 enltrMy statement on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2  's student loan relief plan: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/NAJnYMhTvS"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/NAJnYMhTvS}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Michael Bennet (@SenatorBennet) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenatorBennet/status/1562527164737544193?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Nevada\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2 , who is among the most vulnerable Democratic senators, said she opposed it, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thenevadaindependent.com/article/cortez-masto-pushes-back-against-biden-student-loan-forgiveness-as-other-dems-cheer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Nevada Independent}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t agree with today\u8217\'20\'19s executive action because it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t address the root problems that make college unaffordable,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe should be focusing on passing my legislation to expand Pell Grants for lower income students, target loan forgiveness to those in need, and actually make college more affordable for working families.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 House Democrat Tim Ryan, who is vying for the open Senate seat in Ohio, was also critical:\par \par \uc2 enltrTim Ryan, running for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/OHSEN?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #OHSEN}}}\uc2  puts out a statement critical of Biden's student loan plan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/L85ZpReR5T"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/L85ZpReR5T}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Zaid Jilani (@ZaidJilani) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ZaidJilani/status/1562523156908503040?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s measures announced yesterday provide a reprieve for student borrowers, but may not be enough to address racial inequities when it comes to college debt, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edwin-rios"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Edwin Rios}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 As \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announced the details of his plan to help those with student loan debt, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://protectborrowers.org/who-we-are/our-team/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kat Welbeck}}}\uc2  wrestled with the idea. For millions of Americans, the unprecedented relief would be \u8220\'20\'1Clife-changing\u8221\'20\'1D, especially for low-income and Black and Latino Americans, who are disproportionately saddled with decades-long debt, she said.\par \par \uc2 But the plans\u8217\'20\'19 income cap on who can receive cancellation, and its unclear bureaucratic process for Americans seeking debt relief could perpetuate the inequities that underpin the nation\u8217\'20\'19s student loan system, Welbeck, director of advocacy and civil rights counsel for the Student Borrower Protection Center, said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile a $10,000 cancellation is so meaningful for millions of student loan borrowers, there\u8217\'20\'19s a lot that\u8217\'20\'19s still to be done to fix this student debt crisis,\u8221\'20\'1D Welbeck says.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/money/2022/aug/25/biden-student-loan-debt-forgiveness"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden says his student loan relief is \u8216\'20\'18life-changing\u8217\'20\'19. Will it fix the system\u8217\'20\'19s inequities?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile outside the White House, a brass band has appeared at a rally to thank \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  for his student debt relief measures announced yesterday.\par \par \uc2 enltrSome celebrating happening outside the White House today thanking POTUS for cancelling student debt. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/z2Pi1DhimP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/z2Pi1DhimP}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kellan Howell (@kellanhowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kellanhowell/status/1562797078753214470?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House plans to issue immigration regulation to protect 'dreamers'\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration will soon issue a federal rule to protect from deportation \u8220\'20\'1Cdreamers\u8221\'20\'1D, the undocumented immigrants who arrived in the United States as children, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/immigration-daca-biden-federal-regulation-dreamers/?ftag=CNM-00-10aab7e&linkId=178569871"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CBS News reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The proposal would formalize Deferred Action for Childhood Arrivals (Daca), in an attempt to protect it from court challenges, which it has already faced from Republican officials. According to \uc2 CBS\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CThe regulation will maintain the longstanding eligibility rules for DACA, which include requirements that applicants prove they arrived in the U.S. by age 16 and before June 2007; studied in a U.S. school or served in the military; and lack any serious criminal record.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The new regulation would satisfy a judge\u8217\'20\'19s opinion that Daca should have been created via the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s official rule-making process, rather than by the 2012 memo under which it currently operates, \uc2 CBS\uc2  reports. Last year, a judge in Texas {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/23/dreamers-ruling-blocks-new-daca-applications"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  blocked the program}}}\uc2  from taking on more applicants.\par \par \uc2 However, the new regulation is not immune from being sued over, according to \uc2 CBS\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 U.S. District Court Judge \uc2 Andrew Hanen\uc2 , who closed DACA to first-time applicants in July 2021, ruled that the policy itself violates federal immigration law, as Texas and other Republican-led states have argued in a lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 The 5th Circuit Court of Appeals, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/immigration-daca-dreamers-appeals-court-biden-administration/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 held a hearing}}}\uc2  in July on the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s appeal of Hanen\u8217\'20\'19s ruling, is expected to issue an opinion on DACA\u8217\'20\'19s legality later this year. The conservative-leaning appeals court is expected to side with Republican state officials who argue that DACA is unlawful. The Biden administration could appeal such a ruling to the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 The ongoing litigation could keep DACA closed to new applicants and even lead to its complete termination, a scenario that would bar the program\u8217\'20\'19s beneficiaries from working in the U.S. legally and render them eligible for deportation, though they would likely not be prioritized for arrest under the Biden administration.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Last week, Florida governor and potential aspirant for the Republican presidential nomination in 2024 \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  announced charges against 19 people over election fraud. But as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levine}}}\uc2  reports, there may be less to the cases than it initially appeared:\par \par \uc2 Several Floridians facing criminal voter fraud charges, loudly trumpeted by Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  last week, believed they were eligible to vote, and in some cases said they were advised by government officials that they could cast ballots.\par \par \uc2 Court and election documents reviewed by the Guardian raise questions about whether the 19 people charged last week knowingly committed fraud or whether they were confused about their eligibility. All those charged have prior murder or sexual offense convictions, which means they cannot vote in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida}}}\uc2  unless they receive clemency. All of the defendants also submitted voter registration applications, which were approved by local election officials, ahead of the 2020 election, and several said they had received voter registration cards in the mail, which they took as a signal that they were eligible to vote.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/25/florida-voting-fraud-charges-eligibility"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Floridians charged over voting believed they were eligible, documents show}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jared Kushner\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s memoir of his time in the White House was critically panned but has one famous reader: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theatlantic.com/politics/archive/2018/01/americas-first-post-text-president/549794/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 notoriously averse}}}\uc2  to reading his briefing papers as president but according to \uc2 Jared Kushner\uc2  he has started reading {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2022/aug/14/breaking-history-review-jared-kushner-trump-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Breaking History}}}\uc2 , his son-in-law and former adviser\u8217\'20\'19s 500-page White House memoir.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to the Fox News host Brian Kilmeade on Wednesday, Kushner {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/media/jared-kushner-trump-acted-normal-person-probably-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CWhen I gave it to him, he said, \u8216\'20\'18Look, this is a very important book. I\u8217\'20\'19m glad somebody wrote a book that\u8217\'20\'19s really going to talk about what actually happened in the room.\u8217\'20\'19 And he says, \u8216\'20\'18I\u8217\'20\'19m going to read it.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo he started reading and he\u8217\'20\'19s given me some compliments on it so far. And again, I hope he\u8217\'20\'19s proud of it. I don\u8217\'20\'19t know if he\u8217\'20\'19ll like anything [in it].\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Critics have not liked much in Kushner\u8217\'20\'19s book. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2022/aug/14/breaking-history-review-jared-kushner-trump-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 For the Guardian}}}\uc2 , Lloyd Green called it \u8220\'20\'1Ca mixture of news and cringe\u8221\'20\'1D which \u8220\'20\'1Cselectively parcels out dirt\u8221\'20\'1D. In the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 , Dwight Garner {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/08/17/books/review-breaking-history-jared-kushner.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  the book \u8220\'20\'1Cearnest and soulless\u8221\'20\'1D, saying \u8220\'20\'1CKushner looks like a mannequin, and he writes like one. \u8220\'20\'1CKushner\u8217\'20\'19s fealty to Trump remains absolute. Reading this book reminded me of watching a cat lick a dog\u8217\'20\'19s eye goo,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2022/aug/25/trump-reading-kushner-book-breaking-history"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump is reading my memoir, Kushner claims of famously book-shy boss}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s latest legal salvo following the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s search of his Mar-a-Lago resort may have inadvertently tipped his hand.\par \par \uc2 As the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/23/trump-illegal-documents-fbi-mar-a-lago"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported earlier this week}}}\uc2 , the former president appeared to concede in a court filing that some of the documents agents found at Mar-a-Lago could be subject to executive privilege \u8211\'20\'13 meaning they should have been turned over to the National Archives when he left the White House, rather than kept.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf he\u8217\'20\'19s acknowledging that he\u8217\'20\'19s in possession of documents that would have any colorable claim of executive privilege, those are by definition presidential records and belong at the National Archives,\u8221\'20\'1D Asha Rangappa, a former {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/fbi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FBI}}}\uc2  agent and former associate dean at Yale Law School, said of the matter.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd so it\u8217\'20\'19s not clear that executive privilege would even be relevant to the particular crime he\u8217\'20\'19s being investigated for and yet in this filing, he basically admits that he is in possession of them, which is what the government is trying to establish.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Whether a federal judge agrees could be made apparent in the days and weeks to come. But the government secrets investigation isn\u8217\'20\'19t the only one the former president faces - indeed, he\u8217\'20\'19s caught up in array of lawsuits and inquiries. Fortunately, Reuters has a good explainer that briefly summarizes each one.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/08/donald-trump-fbi-raid-explainer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What lawsuits and investigations is Donald Trump facing?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump to answer judge's questions over Mar-a-Lago lawsuit\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. Answers could come today from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , after a federal judge he appointed during his time in office {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2022/08/23/judge-orders-trump-to-give-details-about-mar-a-lago-warrant-lawsuit.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 asked him to explain}}}\uc2  a recently filed lawsuit that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/22/trump-sues-us-government-fbi-mar-a-lago"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seeks to block the FBI from reviewing documents taken from Mar-a-Lago}}}\uc2 . The response from the former president\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers could give a sense of his legal strategy against the investigation into whether he took government secrets with him when he left the White House.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will hold a rally in suburban Maryland at 7pm eastern time, where he\u8217\'20\'19ll no doubt promote his recent legislative accomplishments as well as yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s move to cancel some student debt.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The White House cheered a court ruling blocking Idaho\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in cases of medical emergencies.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tennessee\u8217\'20\'19s strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, which has no exceptions for rape or incest, comes into effect today.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220825ei8p001ux\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
