\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Student loan forgiveness: Biden hails plan for \u8216\'20\'18generation saddled with unsustainable debt\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein in Washington \par \uc2 5,501 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 August 2022\par 03:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President had campaigned on promise of loan forgiveness of up to $10,000 for those struggling with student debt \u8226\'20\'22 Biden set to cancel $10,000 in student loan debt for millions of Americans\u8226\'20\'22 Trump appears to concede he illegally retained official documents in filing\u8226\'20\'22 Sign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announced his long-awaited {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/24/biden-student-loan-debt-ukraine-democrats-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-630645078f08b9ef100e09bb#block-630645078f08b9ef100e09bb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plan to provide student loan relief}}}\uc2 , which he said would allow tens of millions of Americans to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/24/biden-student-loan-debt-ukraine-democrats-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-630673f78f082fadccfc89ae#block-630673f78f082fadccfc89ae"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cfinally crawl out from under that mountain of debt\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 . Meanwhile, Democrats are celebrating after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/24/biden-student-loan-debt-ukraine-democrats-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-63061e158f088e8ce8eaf870#block-63061e158f088e8ce8eaf870"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 their candidate prevailed}}}\uc2  in a politically finicky House district\u8217\'20\'19s special election last night, a sign that the party may be more popular than expected.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more about what happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A Republican lawmaker who had his phone seized as part of the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s probe into 2020 election meddling by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s allies {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/24/biden-student-loan-debt-ukraine-democrats-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-63062ef68f082fadccfc85fd#block-63062ef68f082fadccfc85fd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is suing to stop them from accessing its data}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The White House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/24/biden-student-loan-debt-ukraine-democrats-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-6306699d8f08b9ef100e0bd0#block-6306699d8f08b9ef100e0bd0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decried}}}\uc2  a Texas court ruling that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/24/biden-student-loan-debt-ukraine-democrats-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-630661bc8f08b9ef100e0b89#block-630661bc8f08b9ef100e0b89"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked a requirement}}}\uc2  hospitals carry out abortions in emergencies.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump appeared to concede that he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/24/biden-student-loan-debt-ukraine-democrats-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-630635d98f08b9ef100e08d7#block-630635d98f08b9ef100e08d7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 illegally kept official documents at Mar-a-Lago}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden said that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/24/biden-student-loan-debt-ukraine-democrats-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-6306775d8f082fadccfc89b7#block-6306775d8f082fadccfc89b7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he was not told}}}\uc2  in advance about the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s search of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s resort.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Florida Democrats in a very conservative district{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/24/biden-student-loan-debt-ukraine-democrats-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-63062c0b8f082fadccfc85c1#block-63062c0b8f082fadccfc85c1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have chosen a former health worker}}}\uc2  who was a fierce critic of governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s response to the Covid-19 pandemic as their House candidate, but her chances of victory appear slim.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Opponents of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s student debt plan have claimed it is unfair to Americans who already paid off their loans. The president was asked about this as he wrapped up his speech at the White House.\par \par \uc2 In his response, he draws a comparison to the business-friendly cuts that exist across America\u8217\'20\'19s tax code:\par \par \uc2 enltrREPORTER: Is this unfair to people who paid their student loans or chose not to take out loans?\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: Is it fair to people who, in fact, do not own multi-billion-dollar businesses if they see one of these guys getting all the tax breaks? Is that fair? What do you think? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/HA9LzLBMSC"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/HA9LzLBMSC}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 JM Rieger (@RiegerReport) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RiegerReport/status/1562520081342406658?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 As he spoke at the White House, Biden made special mention of how his plan would give racial minorities some relief from their heavy debt loads.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAbout a third of the borrowers have debt but no degree, the worst of both worlds, debt and no degree. The burden is especially heavy on Black and Hispanic borrowers, who on average have less family wealth to pay for it\u8230\'20\'26 they don\u8217\'20\'19t own their homes to borrow against to be able to pay for college. And the pandemic only made things worse,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 The National \uc2 Association for the Advancement of Colored People (NAACP) \uc2 civil rights group has been vocal in encouraging Biden\u8217\'20\'19s student debt relief efforts. NAACP president \uc2 Derrick Johnson\uc2  expressed some support for the White House plan, but added it didn\u8217\'20\'19t go as far as the group hoped.\par \par \uc2 enltrA notably supportive statement from the \uc2 NAACP\uc2 , which had been extremely critical of Biden on student debt in recent months: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/LlrF21Xj3N"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/LlrF21Xj3N}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Andrew Restuccia (@AndrewRestuccia) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewRestuccia/status/1562509628319023105?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden has concluded his White House address on student loan relief, but as the president was heading out the door, a reporter asked whether he had any advance knowledge of the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s search of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago resort.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI didn\u8217\'20\'19t have any advance notice,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden answered. \u8220\'20\'1CNone, zero, not one single bit.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The White House has previously said the president was not told ahead of time of the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s plans to search the south Florida property as part of its investigation into the former president\u8217\'20\'19s alleged retention of government secrets.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden has compared his measure relieving some student debt to his administration\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to revive the economy following the Covid-19 pandemic.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur approach is why America\u8217\'20\'19s economic recovery \u8230\'20\'26 was faster and stronger than any other advanced nation in the world. And now it\u8217\'20\'19s time to address the burden of student debt the same way,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said. His administration\u8217\'20\'19s goal is \u8220\'20\'1Cto provide more breathing room for people so they have less burdened by student debt.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden predicted his plan would provide relief to 43 million people, comprised of two groups: those who received a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://studentaid.gov/understand-aid/types/grants/pell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pell Grant}}}\uc2  and will be eligible for $20,000 in relief, and those who received other federal student loans and will be eligible for $10,000 in relief. Both groups will need to make under $125,000 a year to qualify, or $250,000 for families. \u8220\'20\'1CAll this means people can start finally crawl out from under that mountain of debt,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said, predicting the relief would completely cancel the debts of 20 million people.\par \par \uc2 Among his measures, Biden extended the pause on student debt repayments to the end of the year, but has made clear he won\u8217\'20\'19t do that again. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m extending to December 31, 2022. And it\u8217\'20\'19s going to end at that time,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Declaring \u8220\'20\'1Ceducation is a ticket to a better life\u8221\'20\'1D, Biden is outlining his plan to relieve student debt in a speech at the White House.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COver time, that ticket has become too expensive for too many Americans. All this means is the entire an entire generation is now saddled with unsustainable debt,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said, speaking alongside education secretary \uc2 Miguel Cardona\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThe burden is so heavy that even if you graduate you may not have access to middle-class life that the college degree was\u8221\'20\'1D meant to provide.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is over 15 minutes late to his planned speech on student loan relief, but the White House just released the below video, in which he explains the plan.\par \par \uc2 Perhaps this is what\u8217\'20\'19s been keeping him:\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2  breaks down our student debt relief announcement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/D1yrpii2Hu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/D1yrpii2Hu}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Herbie Ziskend (@HerbieZiskend46) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HerbieZiskend46/status/1562507652017815557?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will soon make an address from the White House, where he\u8217\'20\'19ll detail his plan to relieve student loan debt.\par \par \uc2 You can follow along at the live stream at the top of this page. For those just tuning in, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://studentaid.gov/debt-relief-announcement/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here\u8217\'20\'19s a link}}}\uc2  to the department of education page explaining how the program will work.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Earlier today, White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  condemned the Texas court decision that blocked hospitals from being required to carry out emergency abortions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday\u8217\'20\'19s decision is a blow to Texans,\u8221\'20\'1D Jean-Pierre said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/08/24/statement-from-press-secretary-karine-jean-pierre-on-the-u-s-district-court-for-the-northern-district-of-texas-emergency-medical-treatment-and-labor-act-decision/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a statement}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CTexas filed this suit to ensure that it can block medical providers from providing life-saving and health-preserving care. Because of this decision, women in Texas may now be denied this vital care \u8211\'20\'13 even for conditions like severe hemorrhaging or life-threatening hypertension. It\u8217\'20\'19s wrong, it\u8217\'20\'19s backwards, and women may die as a result. The fight is not over. The President will continue to push to require hospitals to provide life-saving and health-preserving reproductive care.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s attempt to preserve \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in states with governments hostile to the procedure faced a setback in Texas, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edwin-rios"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Edwin Rios}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 A federal judge in Texas has blocked a Biden administration guidance that required hospitals to provide emergency abortions, even in states like Texas, which prohibits the practice following the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s overturning of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The legal effort by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2  attorney general, \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , a stalwart Republican, represents the latest attempt to stop the federal government from influencing the reproductive access landscape in the aftermath of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s Dobbs decision, which overturned longstanding constitutional protections on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Such preventions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access could have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/02/cost-banning-abortion-financial-emotional-comic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 devastating }}}\uc2  financial and health consequences on women, especially {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/19/black-mothers-birth-maternal-mortality"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Black}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/27/roe-v-wade-overturned-maternal-mortality-rate-will-rise"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Latino and Indigenous women}}}\uc2  who already disproportionately suffer from deaths during childbirth.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/24/texas-judge-blocks-emergency-abortion-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas judge blocks Biden order requiring hospitals to provide emergency abortions}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here are a few more details about who the student loan relief plan will affect, from a briefing White House officials held with the press.\par \par \uc2 From CBS News:\par \par \uc2 enltrWH says most student loan borrowers -- roughly 27 million -- will be able to receive up to $20,000 in debt forgiveness, as Pell Grant recipients make up more than 60% of borrowers.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Steven Portnoy (@stevenportnoy) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/stevenportnoy/status/1562472844377726984?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrWH says Biden's plan will cancel the entire remaining federal student loan balance for roughly 20 million borrowers.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Steven Portnoy (@stevenportnoy) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/stevenportnoy/status/1562473758849347585?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 And some of the mechanics of how it will work, from the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 enltrImplementation: Borrowers will submit application showing they meet income caps, according to senior admin official. Official notes some borrowers already have submitted income information to Ed Dep and could receive debt relief soon. Ed Dep will release more details\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Zolan Kanno-Youngs (@KannoYoungs) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KannoYoungs/status/1562473230241529856?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrSeeing questions about the income cap.\par \par \uc2 Senior official: For the purposes of the immediate debt relief, a borrower's income in EITHER 2020 or 2021 tax year is assessed. If their income was below the cap in either year, they would be eligible.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Zolan Kanno-Youngs (@KannoYoungs) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KannoYoungs/status/1562491672436453378?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrIncome cap is UNDER 125K. Those making 125K would not be eligible, per official.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Zolan Kanno-Youngs (@KannoYoungs) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KannoYoungs/status/1562493031164456961?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jill Biden is positive for Covid-19 again with rebound case\par \par \uc2 This just in: First lady Jill Biden has tested positive for Covid-19 again with a rebound case, announced the White House today.\par \par \uc2 enltrTHIS JUST IN: First Lady Jill Biden has tested positive for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/COVID19?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #COVID19}}}\uc2  AGAIN with a rebound case, like her husband weeks before her.\par \par \uc2 She's now gone back into isolation in Delaware, while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2  has returned to the White House. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/C7A6ikyqnU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/C7A6ikyqnU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Eric Martin (@EMPosts) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/EMPosts/status/1562489154033790976?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The first lady had tested negative on Sunday and was with Biden at their beach house in Delaware.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will wear his mask for the next 10 days following Jill\u8217\'20\'19s rebound case, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Jill Biden is not experiencing any reemergence of symptoms, said the White House, and is currently following isolation procedures in Delaware.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe First Lady has experienced no reemergence of symptoms, and will remain in Delaware where she has reinitiated isolation procedures,\u8221\'20\'1D her deputy communications director, Kelsey Donohue, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Previously, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  tested positive for Covid-19 on 31 July, testing positive again due to a rebound case.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more information on the impact of student debt on Black college students and how it reinforces the racial wealth gap from Andre M. Perry, Marshall Steinbaum, and Carl Romer of the Brookings Institute:\par \par \uc2 No matter what you want to do with your life, I guarantee that you\u8217\'20\'19ll need an education to do it,\u8221\'20\'1D President \uc2 Barack Obama{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?app=desktop&v=3iqsxCWjCvI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  in a 2009 national address to students. Such guidance is regularly told to Black people: The way to get out of poverty and achieve middle class status is to get a college degree.\par \par \uc2 But a college degree does not eliminate the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/publication/black-white-wage-gaps-expand-with-rising-wage-inequality/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 income gaps}}}\uc2  between white and Black workers. Black students finance their education through debt, and thus college degrees actually further contribute to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/abs/10.1177/2332649218790989"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fragility}}}\uc2  of the upwardly mobile Black middle class. And because education does not achieve income parity for Black workers, the disproportionate debt Black students are taking to finance their education is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brookings.edu/essay/student-debt-cancellation-should-consider-wealth-not-income/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reinforcing the racial wealth gap}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Today, the average white family has roughly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://contexts.org/articles/disrupting-the-racial-wealth-gap/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 10 times}}}\uc2  the amount of wealth as the average Black family, while white college graduates have over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://contexts.org/articles/disrupting-the-racial-wealth-gap/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seven times}}}\uc2  more wealth than Black college graduates.\par \par \uc2 Read the full article {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brookings.edu/research/student-loans-the-racial-wealth-divide-and-why-we-need-full-student-debt-cancellation/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Experts and politicians are also emphasizing how student debt forgiveness is a racial equity issue considering the disproportionate impact that student debt has on racial minorities.\par \par \uc2 A majority of Black and Latinx students take out student loans to attend college.\par \par \uc2 On average, Black college graduates also owe tens of thousands of dollars more in debt than white college grads, a heightened financial burden.\par \par \uc2 From \uc2 Princeton University\uc2  professor Eddie S. Glaude Jr:\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CBlack and African American bachelor\u8217\'20\'19s degree holders have an average $52,000 in student loan debt.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Eddie S. Glaude Jr. (@esglaude) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/esglaude/status/1562483952492761088?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CBlack and African American college graduates owe an average of $25,000 more in student loan debt than White college graduates.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Eddie S. Glaude Jr. (@esglaude) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/esglaude/status/1562483337540673536?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 From Washington congresswoman \uc2 Pramila Jayapal\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 enltr? 90% of Black students have loans\par \par \uc2 ? 72% of Latino students have loans\par \par \uc2 ? 40% of borrowers never finished their degree\par \par \uc2 Canceling student debt is a racial justice issue and will help to close the racial wealth gap. This is a major step forward.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. \uc2 Pramila Jayapal\uc2  (@RepJayapal) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepJayapal/status/1562484889173229568?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 More reactions across both sides of the political aisle are coming in following \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s announcement of his administration\u8217\'20\'19s plan to alleviate student debt.\par \par \uc2 Washington senator \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2  called the the announcement \u8220\'20\'1Chuge\u8221\'20\'1D, tweeting:\par \par \uc2 enltrAfter months of pushing, real student debt relief is here. This is huge.\par \par \uc2 And we can\u8217\'20\'19t stop here. I'll keep fighting to lower the cost of college and pushing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2  to fix our broken student loan system. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/e6HcwvvotK"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/e6HcwvvotK}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senator \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2  (@PattyMurray) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PattyMurray/status/1562479012911665159?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Massachusetts senator Elizabeth Warren, who previously praised the plan, tweeted that the initiative is \u8220\'20\'1Ca big deal\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 enltrI\u8217\'20\'19ll continue working with the Biden administration to reform our higher education system and create a stronger economy for all Americans. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2  ' action to cancel student debt is a big deal.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Elizabeth Warren (@SenWarren) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenWarren/status/1562464769176915968?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, very in line with Republican sentiment, House minority leader Kevin McCarthy shared his contempt for the measure, writing:\par \par \uc2 enltrWho will be forced to pay for Biden's debt transfer scam? Hard-working Americans who already paid off their debts or never took on student loan debt in the first place.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kevin McCarthy (@GOPLeader) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GOPLeader/status/1562474995116175360?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The specific measures will be further detailed during a later speech at 2:15 pm eastern time.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announced his long-awaited {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/24/biden-student-loan-debt-ukraine-democrats-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-630645078f08b9ef100e09bb#block-630645078f08b9ef100e09bb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plan to relieve student debt}}}\uc2 , which he will detail in a White House address scheduled for 2:15 pm eastern time. Meanwhile, Democrats are celebrating, after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/24/biden-student-loan-debt-ukraine-democrats-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-63061e158f088e8ce8eaf870#block-63061e158f088e8ce8eaf870"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 their candidate prevailed}}}\uc2  in a politically finicky house district\u8217\'20\'19s special election last night in a sign that the party may be more popular than polls indicate.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more of what has happened so far today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A Republican lawmaker who had his phone seized as part of the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s probe into 2020 election meddling by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s allies {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/24/biden-student-loan-debt-ukraine-democrats-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-63062ef68f082fadccfc85fd#block-63062ef68f082fadccfc85fd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is suing to stop them from accessing its data}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump appeared to concede that he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/24/biden-student-loan-debt-ukraine-democrats-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-630635d98f08b9ef100e08d7#block-630635d98f08b9ef100e08d7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 illegally kept official documents at Mar-a-Lago}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Florida Democrats in a very conservative district{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/24/biden-student-loan-debt-ukraine-democrats-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-63062c0b8f082fadccfc85c1#block-63062c0b8f082fadccfc85c1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have chosen a former health worker}}}\uc2  who was a fierce critic of governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s response to the Covid-19 pandemic as their House candidate, but her chances of victory appear slim.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Calling it \u8220\'20\'1Cstudent loan socialism\u8221\'20\'1D, the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s top Republican \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  has blasted the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s debt relief proposal.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s an excerpt from his statement:\par \par \uc2 Washington Democrats have found yet another way to make inflation even worse, reward far-left activists, and achieve nothing for millions of working American families who can barely tread water.\par \par \uc2 President Biden\u8217\'20\'19s student loan socialism is a slap in the face to every family who sacrificed to save for college, every graduate who paid their debt, and every American who chose a certain career path or volunteered to serve in our Armed Forces in order to avoid taking on debt. This policy is astonishingly unfair.\par \par \uc2 The median American with student loans already has a significantly higher income than the median American overall. Experts who studied similar past proposals found that the overwhelming benefit of student loan socialism flows to higher-earning Americans. Democrats specifically wrote this policy to make sure that people earning six figures would benefit.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s allies are cheering his student debt relief announcement, with the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s top Democrat \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  and Elizabeth Warren, a longtime advocate of the policy in the chamber, issuing a joint statement.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what the senators had to say:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith the flick of a pen, President Biden has taken a giant step forward in addressing the student debt crisis by cancelling significant amounts of student debt for millions of borrowers. The positive impacts of this move will be felt by families across the country, particularly in minority communities, and is the single most effective action that the President can take on his own to help working families and the economy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis action, along with the pause on federal student loan payments, interest, and collections will improve borrowers\u8217\'20\'19 economic security, allowing them to invest in their families, save for emergencies, and pay down other debt. In addition, we are pleased to see the President\u8217\'20\'19s proposed work towards greatly simplifying and expanding access to student loan relief programs, including the Public Service Loan Forgiveness program, and look forward to additional improvements to other programs like Income Driven Repayment, which will also allow millions more student loan borrowers to better access existing programs to reduce their student loan debts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo president or Congress has done more to relieve the burden of student debt and help millions of Americans make ends meet. Make no mistake, the work - our work - will continue as we pursue every available path to address the student debt crisis, help close the racial wealth gap for borrowers, and keep our economy growing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 For those curious about the finer points of the White House\u8217\'20\'19s student debt relief plan, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has just tweeted out a link to a website with further details:\par \par \uc2 enltrI\u8217\'20\'19ll be delivering remarks on my Administration's student loan debt relief plan at 2:15 PM ET.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, go to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/80wXPTae6V"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/80wXPTae6V}}}\uc2  for more information.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1562464809471266816?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden plans afternoon speech to detail student debt relief\par \par \uc2 The White House has just announced president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will make a speech at 2.15pm eastern time to outline his student debt relief measures. He has also tweeted the basics of his proposal:\par \par \uc2 enltrIn keeping with my campaign promise, my Administration is announcing a plan to give working and middle class families breathing room as they prepare to resume federal student loan payments in January 2023.\par \par \uc2 I'll have more details this afternoon. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/kuZNqoMe4I"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/kuZNqoMe4I}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1562462774969581570?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 The GOP is teeing up their counter-attack to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s impending announcement on student debt relief, decrying it as a \u8220\'20\'1Cbribe\u8221\'20\'1D that will be paid for by American taxpayers.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what the Senate Republicans said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 enltrOnce again, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is passing the buck to working class Americans.\par \par \uc2 Over half of student loans are held by people who went to grad school but \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  wants you to pay for it.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senate Republicans (@SenateGOP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenateGOP/status/1562163098953424896?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 23, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Arkansas senator Tom Cotton:\par \par \uc2 enltrAmericans who paid off student loans or never borrowed for school just took on $300 billion in new debt, thanks to Biden's shameless bribe.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tom Cotton (@TomCottonAR) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TomCottonAR/status/1562450885271523329?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden owes Americans an explanation on why a truck driver who didn't go to college is now responsible for the student loans of a rich lawyer.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tom Cotton (@TomCottonAR) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TomCottonAR/status/1562452098448379904?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Texas senator Ted Cruz cast it as worsening the ongoing inflation:\par \par \uc2 enltrThe average cost per taxpayer is\u8230\'20\'26$2100.\par \par \uc2 Wow. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Bidenflation?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Bidenflation}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/q0VyCJ2vAA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/q0VyCJ2vAA}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ted Cruz (@tedcruz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/tedcruz/status/1562291769106173952?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lauren-aratani"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauren Aratani}}}\uc2  has more on American students\u8217\'20\'19 mammoth debt load, how it became a political issue for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and whether his proposed relief will make much of a difference:\par \par \uc2 America\u8217\'20\'19s students have a debt problem. A big one. More than 45 million Americans \u8211\'20\'13 more than the population of California \u8211\'20\'13 now owe a collective $1.7tn in student debt.\par \par \uc2 The vast majority of the money is owed to the federal government, which has been backing or directly offering student loans for higher education since 1958. While student loans are not new in the United States, the amount of student debt has more than tripled over the last 16 years.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is expected to announce on Wednesday a cancellation of a large swath of student debt to address the crisis, the first large cancellation in US history. Borrowers making under $125,000 could see $10,000 shaved off their debt. Most borrowers will qualify for some cancellation. For at least {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.americanprogress.org/article/5-things-to-know-about-debt-cancellation/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 15 million}}}\uc2 , that means complete erasure of their debt.\par \par \uc2 Student debt will remain a hot political issue. Understanding the impact of such a dramatic policy requires unpacking the student debt crisis, beginning with its origins.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/money/2022/may/26/us-student-loan-debt-forgiveness-cost"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How the US student loan debt crisis started \u8212\'20\'14 and how it could end}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to announce $10,000 in student debt relief: media reports\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will today announce as much as $10,000 in student debt relief for millions of American borrowers, as well as up to $20,000 in relief for borrowers who received a Pell Grant, according US media reports.\par \par \uc2 The White House has been debating how much student debt relief to offer for months, after Biden made the issue part of his pitch to voters on the 2020 campaign trail. The announcement of the aid is expected later today, once Biden returns to the White House from vacation.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/08/23/biden-student-loan-forgiveness-repayment-pause-00053299"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to Politico}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CThe loan relief will be limited to borrowers who earn less than $125,000 a year or families earning less than $250,000. In addition, the White House plans to extend the moratorium on monthly payments and interest for a \u8216\'20\'18final time\u8217\'20\'19 through Dec. 31.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Politico reports Biden\u8217\'20\'19s fellow Democrats were lobbying him as recently as last night to aggressively cancel debt, while some groups say the amounts proposed won\u8217\'20\'19t be enough:\par \par \uc2 Progressives, civil rights organizations and labor unions have all urged the Biden administration to provide large amounts \u8212\'20\'14 as much as $50,000 per borrower \u8212\'20\'14 of loan forgiveness to people across-the-board. And they signaled on Tuesday their disappointment with any policy that stops short of sweeping relief.\par \par \uc2 Derrick Johnson\uc2 , president of the \uc2 NAACP\uc2 , made clear that $10,000 of debt relief per borrower would be insufficient for addressing the racial inequities in student loan debt. \u8220\'20\'1CIf the rumors are true, we\u8217\'20\'19ve got a problem,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Biden\u8217\'20\'19s decision on student debt cannot become the latest example of a policy that has left Black people \u8212\'20\'14 especially Black women \u8212\'20\'14 behind,\u8221\'20\'1D he added. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not how you treat Black voters who turned out in record numbers and provided 90 percent of their vote to once again save democracy in 2020.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  reports on the latest in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s response to the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s search of Mar-a-Lago, in which the former president has apparently admitted to having documents he should not have at his Florida resort:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  appeared to concede in his court filing surrounding the seizure of materials from his Florida resort that he unlawfully retained official government documents, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the former president}}}\uc2  argued that some of the documents collected by the \uc2 FBI\uc2  could be subject to executive privilege.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/22/trump-sues-us-government-fbi-mar-a-lago"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 motion submitted on Monday}}}\uc2  by the former president\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers argued that a court should appoint a so-called special master to separate out and determine what materials the justice department can review as evidence due to privilege issues.\par \par \uc2 But the argument from Trump that some of the documents are subject to executive privilege protections indicates that those documents are official records that he is not authorized to keep and should have turned over to the National Archives at the end of the administration.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/23/trump-illegal-documents-fbi-mar-a-lago"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump appears to concede he illegally retained official documents}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 A Republican lawmaker who had his phone seized as part of an investigation into attempts to meddle with the 2020 election filed a lawsuit to stop the justice department from reviewing its data, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/08/24/rep-scott-perry-suing-to-block-doj-access-to-his-cell-phone-00053486"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Federal agents took Pennsylvania House representative and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  ally Scott Perry\u8217\'20\'19s phone earlier this month. The lawmaker has been mentioned as involved in the attempt by Trump to install a loyalist at the top of the justice department in order to interfere with the results of the 2020 election. He also is among the Republicans who asked Trump for a pardon.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[F]ederal agents should not be given carte blanche to root around in Rep. Perry\u8217\'20\'19s phone data looking for evidence that they hope might further their investigation,\u8221\'20\'1D the lawmaker\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys wrote in the lawsuit, Politico reports.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/09/scott-perry-says-phone-seized-fbi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Congressman and Trump ally Scott Perry says FBI seized his cellphone}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats in a deeply conservative Florida district have chosen as their congressional candidate Rebekah Jones, a former health department employee who was a fierce critic of governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s response to the Covid-19 pandemic, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/08/23/us/politics/rebekah-jones-matt-gaetz-florida.html?smtyp=cur&smid=tw-nytimes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Jones will go up against Republican congressman \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  in a district viewed as a safe for the GOP, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/22/matt-gaetz-republican-sex-trafficking-investigation-marries-california"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 despite the lawmaker\u8217\'20\'19s scandals}}}\uc2 . Jones burst into the public spotlight during the pandemic\u8217\'20\'19s early months after being fired from her job and accusing DeSantis of mishandling Covid-19 cases, though she is under investigation herself. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a brief recap from the Times:\par \par \uc2 That clash put a spotlight on Ms. Jones in 2020, when she claimed that she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/19/us/coronavirus-usa-live.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had been fired}}}\uc2  from her government job for refusing to suppress virus data from the public. In what became a monthslong saga, Ms. Jones filed a whistle-blower complaint, turned into a vocal critic of Mr. DeSantis and was eventually {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2020/12/11/us/florida-coronavirus-data-rebekah-jones.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criminally charged}}}\uc2  with accessing a state computer and downloading a file without authorization.\par \par \uc2 The criminal case against Ms. Jones is pending. In May, an inspector general for the Department of Health {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/live/2022/05/26/world/covid-19-mandates-vaccine-cases/an-inspector-general-in-florida-dismissed-a-former-government-employees-complaints-about-coronavirus-data-manipulation?smid=url-share"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found}}}\uc2  that three allegations that Ms. Jones had made against several health officials were \u8220\'20\'1Cunsubstantiated.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 In Florida, Democrats picked \uc2 Charlie Crist\uc2  as their candidate to stand against governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  in November, in what will be a test of whether voters are on board with the Republican\u8217\'20\'19s culture war offensive:\par \par \uc2 Charlie Crist\uc2  will challenge Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis}}}\uc2 , in November after trouncing \uc2 Nikki Fried\uc2 , the state agriculture commissioner, in Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic primary.\par \par \uc2 Crist, a former Republican governor of Florida who switched parties and became a Democratic congressman, fought a campaign touting his experience in office and opposition to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/09/florida-abortion-ban-ron-desantis-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 15-week \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2  signed by DeSantis.\par \par \uc2 In his victory speech in St Petersburg, Crist promised that if elected he will on his first day in office sign an executive order overturing the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law.\par \par \uc2 And he pledged to end the White House hopes of \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/23/florida-election-candidates-desantis-charlie-crist-primary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wannabe dictator}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D DeSantis, who is tipped as a likely contender for the Republican presidential nomination in 2024. DeSantis has signed a raft of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/3590127-desantis-stokes-culture-wars-as-2024-profile-grows/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 culture war legislation}}}\uc2  in Florida, attacking LBGTQ+ rights and \u8220\'20\'1Cwoke\u8221\'20\'1D corporations.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/23/florida-charlie-crist-wins-ron-desantis-democratic-primary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida: Charlie Crist wins Democratic primary to challenge Ron DeSantis}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from Reuters on the Democratic victory in upstate New York last night:\par \par \uc2 A New York Democrat who campaigned on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and the future of US democracy has won a special congressional election in a swing district, a victory that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  hope could signal a fundamental shift in national voter sentiment ahead of the November midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 Democrat Pat Ryan defeated Republican \uc2 Marc Molinaro\uc2  51.3% to 48.7%, with 99% of the vote counted, Edison Research said, after a hard-fought contest for an open seat in New York\u8217\'20\'19s 19th congressional District, which spans part of the Hudson Valley and Catskill Mountains region and is known as a bellwether.\par \par \uc2 The election took on outsized national importance and became a testing ground for both parties\u8217\'20\'19 campaign strategies. Ryan made the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\uc2  a centrepiece of his campaign, mobilising Democrats outraged by the ruling. Molinaro focused on crime and soaring inflation that voters say is their most pressing concern.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/24/democrat-who-campaigned-on-abortion-rights-wins-in-new-york-special-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrat who campaigned on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights wins in New York special election}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats have the slimmest of majorities in Congress, and thus it\u8217\'20\'19s not hard to see how they could lose the House and potentially the Senate in the November midterms.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s unpopularity is one thing working against them, and then there\u8217\'20\'19s the historic tendency for the party in power to lose big in their first midterm \u8211\'20\'13 as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  found out in 2018, and \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  eight years before that.\par \par \uc2 The lesson Democrats are drawing from Pat Ryan \u8217\'20\'19s victory over Republican \uc2 Marc Molinaro\uc2  in a closely divided upstate New York House district is that this will be no ordinary year. Ryan won by capitalizing on the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s Dobbs decision ending nearly a half-century of nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, and Democrats are no doubt hoping the dynamic repeats in races across the country.\par \par \uc2 Dave Wasserman of the Cook Political Report largely agreed that Ryan\u8217\'20\'19s victory indicated Democratic voters were unusually fired up, but warned that may not translate to a continued majority in the House:\par \par \uc2 enltrLots of focus on Dems being more engaged/energetic post-Dobbs, which is undeniably true. But to me, the GOP/Trump base appears less engaged than it was last November, which is just as big a part of the story.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Dave Wasserman (@Redistrict) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Redistrict/status/1562289784520851457?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrIf not for a devastating string of legal defeats towards the end of redistricting (esp. FL, NY, OH), Dems might have a good shot to hold the House. As it stands, still believe Rs are clear favorites in a higher-turnout scenario, which November will be.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Dave Wasserman (@Redistrict) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Redistrict/status/1562295564557066240?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Surprise election win signals Democrats may be stronger than they appear\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. Democrats scored a victory in upstate New York last night, when a candidate who had campaigned on protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights triumphed over his Republican challenger for a vacant seat in the House of Representatives. The victory has given the party hope that they have a shot at keeping their majorities in Congress in November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm election, despite President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s low approval ratings and voters\u8217\'20\'19 historical tendency to punish the party holding the White House. Expect to hear plenty more about what this result portends today.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is on the agenda:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden is heading back to the White House from vacation in Delaware, and is expected to make public his long-anticipated decision on student debt relief.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Washington has announced $3bn more in military aid for Ukraine on the country\u8217\'20\'19s independence day, which will go towards long-term improvements to its defenses.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ballot counting continues in the special election for Alaska\u8217\'20\'19s vacant House seat, with the Democratic candidate maintaining her lead.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220825ei8p000b5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
