\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Republicans thought they had midterms in the bag. Voters just rejected them again\b0\par\par\uc2 Lloyd Green \par \uc2 822 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 August 2022\par 15:49 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s special election in New York state was more evidence that voters are furious about Republican attacks on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights \u8211\'20\'13 and going to the polls to boost Democrats\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will both appear on November\u8217\'20\'19s ballot. On Tuesday, Pat Ryan, a Democrat and a decorated Iraq war veteran, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/24/democrat-who-campaigned-on-abortion-rights-wins-in-new-york-special-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 upset}}}\uc2  Republican \uc2 Marc Molinaro\uc2  in a special congressional election in New York\u8217\'20\'19s Upper Hudson Valley. Ryan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/08/24/pat-ryan-molinaro-new-york-special-00053458"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won 52-48}}}\uc2  after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DataProgress/status/1562083045645197312"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pre-election polls}}}\uc2  had painted him as the clear underdog.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a huge victory for Dems in a bellwether, Biden +1.5 district,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Redistrict/status/1562283492171472896?s=20&t=ByHgIEuDQBxiLYK7ApGw_g"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according}}}\uc2  to Dave Wasserman, the doyen of congressional-race watchers, with the key words being \u8220\'20\'1Chuge\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cbellwether\u8221\'20\'1D. Said differently, Republican efforts to convert the contest into a referendum on the Democrats and inflation failed.\par \par \uc2 On the campaign trail Ryan made \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a central issue. \u8220\'20\'1CChoice is [on] the ballot, but we won\u8217\'20\'19t go back,\u8221\'20\'1D he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/PatRyanUC"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posted}}}\uc2  to \uc2 Facebook\uc2  hours before the polls opened. \u8220\'20\'1CFreedom is under attack, but it\u8217\'20\'19s ours to defend.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Usually, midterms spell disaster for the \u8220\'20\'1Cin\u8221\'20\'1D party that controls the White House. From the looks of things, 2022 may be different.\par \par \uc2 There is a clear backlash against the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s evisceration of the rights to privacy and personal autonomy. At the same time, nonstop reports of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s mishandling of top-secret documents, and possible obstruction of justice charges against the 45th president, cloud his party\u8217\'20\'19s future.\par \par \uc2 The end of Roe v Wade is not the blessing Republicans had assumed it would be. Looking back, the defeat of Kansas\u8217\'20\'19s anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  referendum was not a one-off event.\par \par \uc2 For the court\u8217\'20\'19s majority, it appears that being \u8220\'20\'1Cright\u8221\'20\'1D was more important than being smart. Ginni Thomas\u8217\'20\'19s husband and four of his colleagues could have upheld Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law without demolishing a half-century of precedent.\par \par \uc2 Chief Justice Robert\u8217\'20\'19s concurrence made that reality crystal clear. Yet around the country, Republican candidates still appear hellbent on doubling-down.\par \par \uc2 Tudor Dixon, Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s Republican candidate for governor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businessinsider.com/michigan-gop-governor-candidate-said-having-baby-healing-rape-victims-2022-8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spoke of}}}\uc2  the upside of a 14-year-old rape victim carrying the child to term. \u8220\'20\'1CThe bond that those two people made and the fact that out of that tragedy there was healing through that baby, it\u8217\'20\'19s something that we don\u8217\'20\'19t think about,\u8221\'20\'1D Dixon told an interviewer.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mjs_DC/status/1559541026695544833?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1559541026695544833%7Ctwgr%5Eb9a19079d0013eaa7172a0818751dbe4a499d994%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.thedailybeast.com%2Fflorida-court-will-force-teen-to-give-birth-as-shes-not-sufficiently-mature-for-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in Florida}}}\uc2 , an appellate court affirmed a lower court\u8217\'20\'19s order that barred a parentless 16-year-old from ending her pregnancy. The unnamed mother-to-be had failed to demonstrate that she was \u8220\'20\'1Csufficiently mature to decide whether to terminate her pregnancy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, the learned judges and the Republican state legislature believed her to be sufficiently adult to deliver and raise a child.\par \par \uc2 And then there is Texas. Later this week, physicians who perform abortions stand to face life in prison and fines of at least $100,000. Under Texas\u8217\'20\'19s current law, abortions are banned after six weeks, and the state\u8217\'20\'19s statute contains no exceptions for rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 Heading into the fall, Democrats will also be bolstered by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s slowly rising approval numbers, tamer inflation figures, and the emergence of democracy\u8217\'20\'19s precarity as a campaign issue. According to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/meet-the-press/first-read/nbc-news-poll-57-voters-say-investigations-trump-continue-rcna43989"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent NBC poll}}}\uc2 , the threat to US democracy has overtaken the cost of living as the No 1 issue for voters.\par \par \uc2 Or, in the words of Congressman-elect Ryan, \u8220\'20\'1COur democracy is fragile, but we will fight for it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Adding to Republican woes is the poor performance of Trump-endorsed Senate candidates in pre-election trial heats. In Arizona, Pennsylvania and Georgia, they all lag.\par \par \uc2 By {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/2022-election-forecast/senate/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the numbers}}}\uc2 , forecasters give the Democrats better than a three-in-five chance of continuing to control the upper chamber and leaving their imprimatur on Biden judicial nominations. These days, even Senator \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  concedes that the odds of him again becoming majority leader are iffy: \u8220\'20\'1CFlipping the Senate \u8230\'20\'26 It\u8217\'20\'19s a 50/50 proposition \u8230\'20\'26 I think the outcome is likely to be very, very close either way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He also reminded Republicans that running for Senate is not the same thing as running for a House seat albeit with a louder and larger microphone. \u8220\'20\'1CSenate races are statewide,\u8221\'20\'1D McConnell observed. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re just different in nature from individual congressional districts.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Apparently, Senator \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2 , the chairman of the Republican National Senatorial Committee, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2022/08/23/rick-scott-senate-republicans-vacation-italy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not yet noticed}}}\uc2 . First, he burned-through a pile of campaign cash. Now, he has been spotted vacationing on a luxury yacht off the coast of Italy while Americans struggle.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, Scott {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenRickScott/status/1561818208142823424?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1561818208142823424%7Ctwgr%5Eda927318299ee4e0f185d856bce540b4353c1b94%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.axios.com%2F2022%2F08%2F23%2Frick-scott-senate-republicans-vacation-italy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CAnother week of President Biden vacationing in Delaware vs. working at the White House.\u8221\'20\'1D Cluelessness is not just the province of Justices Alito, Thomas and Kavanaugh.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Lloyd Green served in the Department of Justice from 1990 to 1992\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220824ei8o002h2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
