\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18The world flipped upside down\u8217\'20\'19: will end of Roe galvanize Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 base in midterms?\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Gambino in Washington \par \uc2 1,457 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 August 2022\par 14:07 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Democrats believe a brewing backlash after June ruling will reshape the battle for control of Congress and statehouses this fall\par \par \uc2 For years, Democrats warned that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights were under grave threat. Across the US, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists in red states chipped away at access and pushed for conservative judges to secure their gains. Yet for many Americans, the prospect of losing the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that had existed since 1973 remained worrying but remote.\par \par \uc2 That all changed in June, when in Dobbs v Jackson, the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade, the 49-year-old ruling which had established the right.\par \par \uc2 Since then, bans have taken effect in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2022/jun/28/tracking-where-abortion-laws-stand-in-every-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at least 10 states}}}\uc2 . Republicans are rushing ahead with new restrictions and stirring fears that other rights, including same-sex marriage and access to contraception, could be vulnerable too.\par \par \uc2 And yet, from rural Minnesota to ruby red Kansas and a conservative corner of Nebraska, there are signs of a brewing backlash that Democrats believe will reshape the battle for control of Congress and statehouses this fall.\par \par \uc2 Republicans are \u8220\'20\'1Cthe dog that caught the bus\u8221\'20\'1D, said Cecile Richards, a former head of \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThis is what they\u8217\'20\'19ve been wanting for years. Now they own it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 White House officials, Democratic candidates and party strategists say the loss of reproductive choice has not only galvanized their once- {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/meet-the-press/democrats-face-double-digit-enthusiasm-deficit-ahead-midterms-n1287910"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 disillusioned}}}\uc2  base but is strengthening Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 appeal among independent and Republican-leaning women in suburbs who were key to the party\u8217\'20\'19s recent victories.\par \par \uc2 The landslide vote to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in conservative Kansas earlier this month further emboldened Democrats \u8211\'20\'13 and emphasized that Republicans risk overreaching on one of the most emotionally charged issues in American life.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe world just completely flipped upside down after the Dobbs decision,\u8221\'20\'1D said Richards, now co-chair at American Bridge 21st Century, a liberal Super Pac. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re no longer defending a right. We now actually have to fight to get a right back.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18A top-tier issue\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Republicans doubt \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be a decisive factor in a midterm election shaped by anxiety over high gas prices and inflation and an unpopular Democratic president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery public and private poll shows inflation and the economy are the top issues headed into the midterms,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mike Berg, a spokesman for the Republican National Congressional Committee. \u8220\'20\'1CDemocrats are desperate to talk about anything else because they have a disastrous record on both of those issues.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But Democrats are forging ahead, lashing Republicans over their uncompromising stances and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/01/utah-republican-women-control-intake-of-semen-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sometimes bizarre}}}\uc2  rhetoric on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Underscoring their confidence in the salience of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  this election cycle, Democrats are spending heavily on television ads on the subject. One particularly searing ad from \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2 , the nominee for governor in Georgia, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/staceyabrams/status/1554830008350216196"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 features a somber montage of women}}}\uc2  warning that women could be \u8220\'20\'1Ccriminalized\u8221\'20\'1D for seeking abortions if \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2 , the Republican governor, is re-elected.\par \par \uc2 Many ads aim to use Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 words against them, as part of an effort by Democrats to cast the GOP as too extreme\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe only way to stop this attack on the women of Georgia,\u8221\'20\'1D the women say, \u8220\'20\'1Cis to stop \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Many of their ads aim to use Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 words against them, as part of a broader effort by Democrats to cast the GOP as too extreme.\par \par \uc2 In Michigan, where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2022/us/politics/midterms-abortion-access.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voters may decide}}}\uc2  to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections in the state constitution in November, the \uc2 Democratic Governors Association\uc2  launched an ad attacking the Republican nominee, Tudor Dixon, over her opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , without exception for rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 In a similar vein, an ad from the the Democratic nominee for governor in Pennsylvania, \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2 , features his far-right opponent, \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2 , saying \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KzkexwZMmoE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 I don\u8217\'20\'19t give a way for exceptions}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, including when the life of the mother is at risk.\par \par \uc2 Polling has shown that most Americans support at least some \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. According to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/religion/2022/05/06/americas-abortion-quandary/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pew Research Center}}}\uc2 , about 60% say \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in all or most cases while just 8% say it should be illegal with no exceptions.\par \par \uc2 The aggressive messaging from Democrats is a reminder of how rapidly the politics of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  have shifted.\par \par \uc2 Molly Murphy, a Democratic pollster and strategist who has studied public opinion on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said: \u8220\'20\'1CSix months ago, if you asked voters, \u8216\'20\'18What\u8217\'20\'19s the top priority that you want elected leaders to focus on,\u8217\'20\'19 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  might get 3%, 4%, 5% at most. Now it really is a top-tier issue, only behind inflation and the economy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Murphy said anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s resounding defeat in the Kansas referendum showed voters were motivated by the opportunity \u8220\'20\'1Cto stop something bad from happening\u8221\'20\'1D. To channel that fury, she said, Democrats must convince voters Republicans are not just opposed to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  but a threat to it.\par \par \uc2 Some Democrats are adopting Republican language about government overreach on issues like masking to accuse their opponents of infringing on individual rights and freedoms when it comes to women\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive health. It is all part of a broader strategy to cast Republicans as extremists determined to strip Americans of a right they have come to rely on.\par \par \uc2 The pitch is similar to Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 messaging in 2018, when they stormed to victory in the House after lashing Republicans over attempts to repeal the Affordable Care Act, said Camille Rivera, a Democratic strategist.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs we learned with Obamacare, once you have a right, you don\u8217\'20\'19t want, really don\u8217\'20\'19t want, that right taken away,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Another key question for this November is just how much \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights will resonate among independent women in battleground suburbs who have deep concerns about the economy. Sarah Longwell, a moderate Republican strategist, said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was usually not the first issue raised in focus groups with swing voters. But when prompted, the discussion around \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  often became personal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe thing that happens when you start talking to a group of women about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is they immediately start telling stories about complications and the things that can go wrong during a pregnancy,\u8221\'20\'1D she said in a recent interview.\par \par \uc2 What is clear, Longwell said, is that women, even those who call themselves \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-life\u8221\'20\'1D, are \u8220\'20\'1Cdeeply uncomfortable with the idea of getting between women and their doctors on decisions that could put their lives at risk\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We are living it\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Republicans are largely shying away from the issue on the campaign trail. With total bans proving deeply unpopular, some candidates are softening their rhetoric, emphasizing support for exceptions and for the health and wellbeing of women. In Nevada, a battleground state, the Republican candidate for Senate, \uc2 Adam Laxalt\uc2 , has argued that his personal opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not change protections already in place.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy views have not shifted the policy in Nevada, nor has the ruling in the Dobbs case,\u8221\'20\'1D Laxalt {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rgj.com/story/opinion/voices/2022/08/02/setting-record-straight-adam-laxalt/10187587002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  earlier this month. \u8220\'20\'1CVoters in 1990 determined that Nevada is and will remain a pro-choice state.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But the issue is hard to ignore. Harrowing stories have spread. A 10-year-old girl who was raped {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/27/indiana-investigates-abortion-doctor-10-year-old-rape-victim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had to travel from Ohio}}}\uc2  to Indiana to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Weeks later, Indiana became the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/aug/06/indiana-assembly-passes-anti-abortion-bill-sends-it-to-governor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first state in the post-Roe era}}}\uc2  to adopt a near-total ban. This week, a judge in Florida told a 16-year-old she was not {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/17/florida-pregnant-teenager-abortion-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cnot sufficiently mature\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  to decide whether to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are no longer speaking about this as a hypothetical,\u8221\'20\'1D Murphy said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are living it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Among Kansans who registered to vote in the wake of the Dobbs ruling, Democrats held an eight-point advantage, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://insights.targetsmart.com/how-abortion-changed-the-kansas-electorate.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 data}}}\uc2  from TargetSmart. Among those newly registered voters, 70% were women.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, in a pair of post-Roe special House elections, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/08/10/democrats-minnesota-nebraska-special-elections/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats outperformed expectations}}}\uc2 , boosted by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/08/10/democrats-special-election-minnesota-roe/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strong turnout}}}\uc2  in suburban areas.\par \par \uc2 In Minnesota\u8217\'20\'19s first district, the Democrat lost by just four points. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won there by more than 10 in 2020. The trend was more pronounced in a June election in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/07/05/trailer-nationalize-this-race-democrats-run-abortion-special-elections/?itid=lk_inline_manual_5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nebraska\u8217\'20\'19s first district}}}\uc2 . Two years ago, Trump won there by nearly 15 points. This year, the Republican won by six.\par \par \uc2 Analysts caution against drawing firm conclusions from such a small sampling. Republicans only need to win a handful of seats to gain control of the House, as they are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/2022-election-forecast/house/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 favored}}}\uc2  to do, while the 50-50 Senate remains a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cookpolitical.com/analysis/senate/senate-overview/three-senate-rating-changes-pennsylvania-colorado-and-utah"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 genuine toss-up.}}}\par \par \uc2 A special election in New York on Tuesday may offer more clues. In the most competitive House race since Roe fell, the Democrat, Pat Ryan, has made \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  central to his campaign. The Republican, \uc2 Marc Molinaro\uc2 , has focused on the economy and inflation.\par \par \uc2 Urging New Yorkers to vote, Ryan said \u8220\'20\'1Cchoice\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cfreedom\u8221\'20\'1D were both \u8220\'20\'1Con the ballot\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220822ei8m000p5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
