\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Americans should focus on Biden\u8217\'20\'19s accomplishments, says chief of staff \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein \par \uc2 5,129 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 August 2022\par 20:07 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Ron Klain\uc2  argues president has made a historic impact and that focus shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be on inflation or Afghanistan withdrawalSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/biden-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden administration}}}\uc2  took advantage of a quiet week in Washington to lay the groundwork for the roughly two months of campaigning before the November midterm elections, when Democrats will have to fight for control of Congress.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 White House chief of staff \uc2 Ron Klain{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/19/biden-midterms-inflation-violence-trump-pence-latest-updates?page=with:block-62ff874e8f081780606cb6e9#block-62ff874e8f081780606cb6e9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gave an interview to Politico}}}\uc2 , where he promoted Biden\u8217\'20\'19s legislative accomplishments and previewed Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 message to voters.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A Georgia judge blocked senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/19/biden-midterms-inflation-violence-trump-pence-latest-updates?page=with:block-62ffd8dd8f08f8ea5d3a0c26#block-62ffd8dd8f08f8ea5d3a0c26"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attempt to quash a subpoena}}}\uc2  compelling his appearance before the special grand jury investigating election meddling in the state.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democrats attackedMike Pence \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/19/biden-midterms-inflation-violence-trump-pence-latest-updates?page=with:block-62ffb2978f081780606cb95b#block-62ffb2978f081780606cb95b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 trip to Iowa}}}\uc2 , as the former vice president continues exploring whether to run for the Republican presidential nomination in 2024.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 An Ohio House Democrat{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/19/biden-midterms-inflation-violence-trump-pence-latest-updates?page=with:block-62ffe6158f08f8ea5d3a0c90#block-62ffe6158f08f8ea5d3a0c90"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criticized Biden in a television advertisement}}}\uc2 . She is fighting to keep her seat representing a district whose boundaries have been redrawn to include more Republican voters.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 More LGBTQ politicians are holding elected office in America than ever before, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/19/biden-midterms-inflation-violence-trump-pence-latest-updates?page=with:block-62ffad0a8f081780606cb911#block-62ffad0a8f081780606cb911"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a new survey}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn Roe v. Wade may be causing a surge in women registering to vote, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/19/biden-midterms-inflation-violence-trump-pence-latest-updates?page=with:block-62ffad0a8f081780606cb911#block-62ffad0a8f081780606cb911"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a political data firm has found}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s letting Ohio solar manufacturers be undercut by China.\u8221\'20\'1D Sounds like a Republican campaign advertisement. It\u8217\'20\'19s not \u8211\'20\'13 instead, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://host2.adimpact.com/admo/viewer/070cefa1-834d-4ae1-b377-769e639813c4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 it\u8217\'20\'19s a television spot}}}\uc2  from an Ohio House Democrat fighting for her seat in a newly redrawn district that\u8217\'20\'19s become much more friendly to the GOP.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/08/19/us/politics/marcy-kaptur-biden-ad.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The New York Times reports }}}\uc2  that \uc2 Marcy Kaptur\uc2  has become the latest and most prominent Democratic lawmakers to publicly break with Biden with an ad that also highlights her collaboration with Rob Portman, Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s retiring Republican senator. It\u8217\'20\'19s a reversal from just last month, when she greeted the president at the airport in Cleveland during his visit to the city. However, such conduct is not unheard of for Democrats this election cycle. Maine representative Jared Golden aired an ad where he described himself as an \u8220\'20\'1Cindependent voice\u8221\'20\'1D that voted against \u8220\'20\'1Ctrillions of dollars of President Biden\u8217\'20\'19s agenda because I knew it would make inflation worse,\u8221\'20\'1D according to the Times.\par \par \uc2 Then there are the somewhat bizarre actions of \uc2 Carolyn Maloney\uc2  of New York, who is fighting to keep her House seat against a challenge from \uc2 Jerry Nadler\uc2 , a fellow Democrat. She had to apologize after saying Biden wasn\u8217\'20\'19t planning to stand for reelection in 2024, only to make the same comment again.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/04/carolyn-maloney-biden-2024-election-apology"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Democrat apologises for saying Biden won\u8217\'20\'19t run in 2024 \u8211\'20\'13 then says it again}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican House candidates who are facing close races are being advised not to talk too much about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , but rather try to concentrate voters\u8217\'20\'19 attention on the issues where they see an advantage over Democrats, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/08/19/politics/trump-vulnerable-repulicans-midterm-elections/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t say his name, ever. I just avoid saying his name generally,\u8221\'20\'1D a Republican lawmaker in a tight race told the network. \u8220\'20\'1CI talk about the policies of his that I like.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The advice comes from \uc2 Tom Emmer\uc2 , a GOP House representative and chairman of the National Republican Congressional Committee, which is tasked with reclaiming Congress\u8217\'20\'19 lower chamber in the November elections. While a spokesman for Emmer didn\u8217\'20\'19t address the report about Trump, he told CNN, \u8220\'20\'1CCandidates know their districts best,\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cpublic and private polls show the midterms will be a referendum on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 failed agenda that\u8217\'20\'19s left voters paying record prices, dealing with soaring violent crime and facing billions in middle-class tax hikes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As the report notes, this strategy could become complicated if Trump opts to announce another campaign for the presidency before the November midterms. Earlier this week, \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  reported he was being counseled to do so to avoid an indictment by the justice department over his handling of classified material.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/15/donald-trump-2024-election-indictment-mar-a-lago"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump should announce run for 2024 soon to avoid indictment, source says}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 The investigation into \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s ties to Russia was one of the earliest and most intense scandals of his presidency, and the legal wrangling over it still hasn\u8217\'20\'19t finished.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/russia-ukraine-donald-trump-william-barr-obstruction-of-justice-992952614b7619681df0e1109548a27f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Associated Press reports}}}\uc2  that a federal court of appeals panel has found that \uc2 William Barr\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general in 2019, wrongly withheld a memo that he cited to say that Trump did not obstruct justice during in the investigation into his ties with Moscow.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the AP:\par \par \uc2 At issue in the case is a March 24, 2019, memorandum from the head of the \uc2 Justice Department\u8217\'20\'19s Office of Legal Counsel\uc2 , or OLC, and another senior department official that was prepared for Barr to evaluate whether evidence in special counsel \uc2 Robert Mueller\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s investigation could support prosecution of the president for obstruction of justice.\par \par \uc2 Barr has said he looked to that opinion in concluding that Trump did not illegally obstruct the Russia probe, which was an investigation of whether his campaign had colluded with Russia to tip the 2016 election.\par \par \uc2 The Justice Department turned over other documents to Citizens for Responsibility and Ethics in Washington as part of the group\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuit, but declined to give it the memo. Government lawyers said they were entitled under public records law to withhold the memo because it reflected internal deliberations among lawyers before any formal decision had been reached on what Mueller\u8217\'20\'19s evidence showed.\par \par \uc2 But U.S. District Judge Amy Berman Jackson said last year that those arguments were disingenuous because the memo was prepared for Barr at about the same time as a separate Justice Department letter informing Congress and the public that Barr and other senior department leaders concluded that Trump had not obstructed justice.\par \par \uc2 The memo noted that \u8220\'20\'1CMueller had declined to accuse President Trump of obstructing justice but also had declined to exonerate him\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Crecommended that Barr \u8216\'20\'18reach a judgment\u8217\'20\'19 on whether the evidence constituted obstruction of justice,\u8221\'20\'1D the panel wrote Friday. The memo also noted that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe Report\u8217\'20\'19s failure to take a definitive position could be read to imply an accusation against President Trump\u8221\'20\'1D if the confidential report were released to the public, the court wrote.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Busy day for courts in Georgia. A federal judge in the state has just rejected another bid by Republican senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  to quash a subpoena compelling his appearance before a special grand jury probing attempts to meddle in the 2020 elections by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s allies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSenator Graham raises a number of arguments as to why he is likely to succeed on the merits, but they are all unpersuasive, not least because they largely misconstrue the Court\u8217\'20\'19s holdings,\u8221\'20\'1D judge Leigh Martin May {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.gand.305825/gov.uscourts.gand.305825.37.0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  in denying the senator\u8217\'20\'19s motion.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA stay is not justified even assuming for the sake of argument that Senator Graham has shown \u8216\'20\'18a substantial case on the merits.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attorney \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  appeared before the panel, which has informed him he is a target of their investigation.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/15/rudy-giuliani-target-criminal-investigation-georgia-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rudy Giuliani informed he is target of criminal investigation in Georgia}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 However in Georgia, a judge will allow a state law provision that bans giving food and water to voters standing in line to go into effect for the November midterm elections, though it is still subject to further legal challenges, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/2022-midterm-elections-voting-rights-georgia-stacey-abrams-general-c1c7c7103c4757c46f266afde514fd59"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The law, passed last year, was part of a Republican-backed effort to reform the state\u8217\'20\'19s election system, which Democrats attacked as an attempt to make it harder for the poor and racial minorities to vote.\par \par \uc2 But as the AP notes, the legal battle isn\u8217\'20\'19t over:\par \par \uc2 U.S. District Judge J.P. Boulee said the voting rights groups may ultimately prevail on part of their challenge, but he agreed with the state that it\u8217\'20\'19s too close to the election to block any part of the provision. He noted that requiring different rules for the general election than those in place for the primaries earlier this year could cause confusion for election workers.\par \par \uc2 Boulee said that voting rights groups had failed to show that prohibiting the distribution of food and drinks within 150 feet (45 meters) of a polling place violates their constitutional rights. But he said that another part of the provision that bars people from offering food and drink within 25 feet (7.6 meters) of any person in line is probably unconstitutional because that zone is tied to the location of voters and could stretch thousands of feet from the polling place.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/mar/25/georgia-voting-restrictions-law-passed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia's Republican-led legislature passes sweeping voting restrictions}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile in Florida, a federal judge has blocked a provision of the \u8220\'20\'1CStop WOKE\u8221\'20\'1D Act that banned private employers from discussing \u8220\'20\'1Cwhite man\u8217\'20\'19s privilege\u8221\'20\'1D and other biases during diversity training.\par \par \uc2 Judge \uc2 Mark Walker\uc2  compared the law to the popular TV show Stranger Things in ordering the injunction, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/08/19/business/dealbook/florida-desantis-stop-woke-act.html?smtyp=cur&smid=tw-nytimes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The New York Times reports}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIn the popular television series \u8216\'20\'18Stranger Things,\u8217\'20\'19 the \u8216\'20\'18upside down\u8217\'20\'19 describes a parallel dimension containing a distorted version of our world. Now, like the heroine in \u8216\'20\'18Stranger Things,\u8217\'20\'19 this court is once again asked to pull Florida back from the upside down.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The law bans Florida employers from forcing its workers to attend diversity trainings that would make them feel guilty or uncomfortable, and also regulates what can be said at such trainings. According to the Times, businesses have chafed at its restrictions, with Bill George, a professor of management at Harvard, describing it to the Times as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe No. 1 issue I hear about from C.E.O.s these days.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Conservatives\u8217\'20\'19 judicial losing streak continued today, when a Michigan judge blocked the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban from taking effect.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s video of Jacob James Cunningham \u8217\'20\'19s ruling:\par \par \uc2 enltrJudge Jacob James Cunningham sides with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates and grants an injunction to block enforcement of Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s 1931 law banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe harm to the body of women \u8230\'20\'26 in not issuing the injunction could not be more real, clear, present, and dangerous.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/lnt59yEdoA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/lnt59yEdoA}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1560661639875203073?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 19, 2022}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-health-michigan-gretchen-whitmer-state-courts-52cdc0f365267808fb0832987a662309"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to the Associated Press}}}\uc2 , the injunction will keep \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legal in the state until this fall, when voters will decide whether to keep the ban on the books. It is also possible that the state supreme court will weigh in on the law around that time.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Details are out about what\u8217\'20\'19s in the next package of military aid for Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a taste from the Associated Press:\par \par \uc2 The United States is poised to announce it will provide Ukraine with nearly $800m in new military aid Friday, including at least a dozen Scan Eagle surveillance drones, according to several US officials.\par \par \uc2 Officials said the bulk of the aid package will be additional howitzers and ammunition, including Javelin missiles that the Ukrainian military has been using effectively to try and hold off Russian forces and take back territory Moscow has gained.\par \par \uc2 Two officials confirmed the new inclusion of the portable, long-endurance drones which are launched by a catapult and can be retrieved. The officials spoke on condition of anonymity to discuss the aid ahead of its public release.\par \par \uc2 And here\u8217\'20\'19s our latest reporting on the war in Ukraine:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/aug/19/russia-ukraine-war-putin-is-losing-information-war-in-ukraine-uk-spy-chief-says-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia-Ukraine war: UN urges Moscow not to take nuclear power plant off grid; Putin and Macron hold talks \u8211\'20\'13 live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Transgender children in Utah will be not be subjected to sports participation limits at the start of the new school year, after a judge delayed the implementation of a statewide ban.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press has more:\par \par \uc2 Judge Keith Kelly\u8217\'20\'19s decision Friday to put the law on hold until a legal challenges is resolved came after he recently rejected a request by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/utah"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Utah}}}\uc2  state attorneys to dismiss the case. Most Utah schools students head back to classes this month.\par \par \uc2 Attorneys representing the families of three transgender student-athletes filed the lawsuit challenging the ban last May, contending it violates the Utah constitution\u8217\'20\'19s guarantees of equal rights and due process.\par \par \uc2 Similar cases are underway in states such as Idaho, West Virginia and Indiana.\par \par \uc2 The issue of whether transgender girls should be allowed to participate in female sports has become flashpoint across the US with Republican lawmakers passing legislation to block them based on the premise it gives them an unfair competitive advantage.\par \par \uc2 Transgender rights advocates counter that the rules aren\u8217\'20\'19t just about sports, but another way to demean and attack transgender youth.\par \par \uc2 More:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2022/aug/19/utah-transgender-sports-law-put-on-hold"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trans kids in Utah free to compete after judge grants injunction on ban }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 A Republican candidate for Congress in New York said he was \u8220\'20\'1Cbeing facetious\u8221\'20\'1D when, in the same interview, he said the US attorney general, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/merrick-garland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Merrick Garland}}}\uc2  , should be executed for authorising the \uc2 FBI\uc2  search at Mar-a-Lago, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Florida home.\par \par \uc2 The candidate, Carl Paladino, recently caused controversy when he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.yahoo.com/gop-candidate-carl-paladino-calls-161513014.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 praised Adolf Hitler}}}\uc2 , as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe kind of leader we need today\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Paladino made his remark about the attorney general in an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.breitbart.com/radio/2022/08/13/republican-ny-congressional-candidate-carl-paladino-mar-a-lago-raid-susan-rice-likely-behind-gestapo-tactics/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interview}}}\uc2  with the far-right site {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.breitbart.com/news/paladino-saying-hitler-kind-of-leader-we-need-was-mistake/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Breitbart}}}\uc2 . Paladino said: \u8220\'20\'1CSo we have a couple of unelected people who are running our government, in an administration of people like Garland, who should be not only impeached, he probably should be executed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe guy is just lost. He\u8217\'20\'19s a lost soul. He\u8217\'20\'19s trying to get an image, and his image, his methodology is just terrible. To raid the home of a former president is just \u8211\'20\'13 people are scratching their heads and they\u8217\'20\'19re saying, \u8216\'20\'18What is wrong with this guy?\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked to explain his \u8220\'20\'1Cexecuted\u8221\'20\'1D remark, Paladino said: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m just being facetious. The man should be removed from office.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 More:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/19/republican-carl-paladino-comment-garland-should-be-executed-facetious-hitler"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican says comment Garland should be executed was \u8216\'20\'18facetious\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration is taking advantage of a quiet week in Washington to lay the groundwork for the roughly two months of campaigning before the November midterm elections, when Democrats will have to fight for control of Congress.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 White House chief of staff \uc2 Ron Klain{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/19/biden-midterms-inflation-violence-trump-pence-latest-updates?page=with:block-62ff874e8f081780606cb6e9#block-62ff874e8f081780606cb6e9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gave an interview to Politico}}}\uc2 , where he promoted Biden\u8217\'20\'19s legislative accomplishments and previewed Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 message to voters.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democrats attackedMike Pence \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/19/biden-midterms-inflation-violence-trump-pence-latest-updates?page=with:block-62ffb2978f081780606cb95b#block-62ffb2978f081780606cb95b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 trip to Iowa}}}\uc2  as the former vice president continues exploring whether to run for the Republican presidential nomination in 2024.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 More LGBTQ politicians are holding elected office in America than ever, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/19/biden-midterms-inflation-violence-trump-pence-latest-updates?page=with:block-62ffad0a8f081780606cb911#block-62ffad0a8f081780606cb911"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a new survey}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn Roe v. Wade may be causing a surge in women registering to vote, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/19/biden-midterms-inflation-violence-trump-pence-latest-updates?page=with:block-62ffad0a8f081780606cb911#block-62ffad0a8f081780606cb911"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a political data firm has found}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s visit to Iowa, which marks his fourth trip to the Hawkeye State since leaving office last year, has intensified speculation that he plans to run for president next year.\par \par \uc2 As the first caucus state on the presidential primary calendar, Iowa is a top destination for potential candidates, and Pence has also made recent appearances in other early voting states like New Hampshire and South Carolina.\par \par \uc2 While in New Hampshire on Wednesday, Pence made headlines by suggesting he was open to speaking to the House select committee investigating the January 6 insurrection. Pence was on Capitol Hill as the insurrection started, and he had to be escorted out of the Senate chamber due to concerns for his safety.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf there was an invitation to participate, I would consider it,\u8221\'20\'1D Pence said Wednesday. \u8220\'20\'1CI would have to reflect on the unique role that I was serving as vice-president.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters on Friday, \uc2 Jaime Harrison\uc2 , the chair of the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2 , did not address Pence\u8217\'20\'19s potential appearance before the January 6 committee.\par \par \uc2 Harrison also deflected questions about whether Iowa would continue to serve as the first caucus state, after the disastrous handling of the Democratic results in 2020.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe rules and bylaws committee will revisit the calendar in the coming days after the midterms,\u8221\'20\'1D Harrison said. \u8220\'20\'1COur focus is primarily on winning these midterm elections, and then we\u8217\'20\'19ll revisit where we are on the presidential calendar right after the midterms.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats attack Pence as the former VP heads to Iowa\par \par \uc2 Democratic leaders went on the attack against \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , as the former vice-president under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  heads to Iowa today amid increased speculation of a potential 2024 campaign.\par \par \uc2 Jaime Harrison\uc2 , the chairman of the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2 , sharply criticized Pence\u8217\'20\'19s repeated calls for a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/06/24/abortion-supreme-court-trump-pence-republicans-roe/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 national \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2  in the wake of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPence wants to criminalize \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and further restrict access to reproductive health care for thousands of Iowans,\u8221\'20\'1D Harrison said on a press call today. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  has been dreaming of the day \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is outlawed. He\u8217\'20\'19s been dreaming about it for years.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While in Iowa, Pence is expected to appear alongside Republican Senator \uc2 Chuck Grassley\uc2 , who is up for reelection in November, and Republican congressional candidate Zach Nunn.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese candidates also support the most extreme anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies that the Republican party is pushing,\u8221\'20\'1D Harrison said. \u8220\'20\'1CRepublicans are more focused on taking us backwards on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  than making progress on the issues that Iowans care about.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 More LGBTQ politicians than ever are holding public office in the United States, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://victoryinstitute.org/out-for-america-2022/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a new report}}}\uc2  that underscores the growing diversity of leaders nationwide.\par \par \uc2 As of June 2022, there are 1,043 known officials across the country who identify as LGBTQ, equal to about 0.2 percent of elected offices, the LGBTQ Victory Institute said in its annual data. That\u8217\'20\'19s an increase of 5.8 percent overall from 2021, though the ranks of out politicians of color rose 12.3 percent compared to 1.3 percent for white politicians over the same period.\par \par \uc2 However, the proportion of elected officials that identify as gay, lesbian, bisexual, transgender or queer is far from representative of the share of the overall population, which about 7.1 percent.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDespite the fact the LGBTQ community has never had equitable representation in government \u8211\'20\'13 and we still have a long way to go \u8211\'20\'13 there are clear signs of progress. LGBTQ elected officials represent the strength and diversity of not only who we are as a society now, but also the America we aspire to build for future generations,\u8221\'20\'1D the institute\u8217\'20\'19s president and CEO Annise Parker said in a statement accompanying the report.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 The supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s June decision to overturn Roe v. Wade and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights nationally may be driving a surge of women registering to vote, according to a political data firm.\par \par \uc2 Tom Bonier\uc2 , CEO of TargetSmart, has tweeted a few thoughts on what he has observed among voter registration data:\par \par \uc2 enltrWow. I've been sharing data showing a huge surge in women registering to vote since the 6/24 Dobbs decision. I just started to look at some age and party breakdowns of those new registrants, and the numbers are jaw-dropping.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Tom Bonier\uc2  (@tbonier) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/tbonier/status/1560597119009955841?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 19, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrStarting in PA, where women have accounted for >56% of new registrants in that time period. Those women new registrants are 62%D to 15% R and 54% are under the age of 25. Compare that to men new registrants at 41% <25 and 43% D, 28% R.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Tom Bonier\uc2  (@tbonier) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/tbonier/status/1560598465448742912?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 19, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrI've seen some noting that the number of new regs we've seen since Dobbs is small relative to the number of existing regs (presumably to minimize what we're seeing). That's accurate, but variations in new registrant patterns are indicative of changes in intensity overall.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Tom Bonier\uc2  (@tbonier) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/tbonier/status/1560638295218049024?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 19, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The firm has published {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://insights.targetsmart.com/not-just-kansas-women-motivated-to-vote-in-states-with-repro-rights-at-risk.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a deeper dive into the data}}}\uc2 , with a focus on Michigan and Wisconsin, where the November elections could make a big difference on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care accessibility.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Remember Covid-19? The pandemic caused the United States\u8217\'20\'19 biggest health and economic crisis in nearly a century and upended the 2020 election, but now appears forgotten in the public discourse \u8211\'20\'13 to many Americans\u8217\'20\'19 chagrin, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/maya-yang"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maya Yang}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 Despite signs that indicate the latest Covid-19 surge is slowing down, an average of 400 deaths in the US is still reported on a daily basis.\par \par \uc2 Various mask and social distancing mandates across the country are becoming anything but strictly enforced.\par \par \uc2 But as Americans and many of their elected officials go about their daily lives, many healthcare professionals still on the frontlines of the pandemic and severely affected Covid-19 patients are left wondering whether the rest of us are moving too quickly from the worst days of the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Have we simply forgotten about Covid-19?\par \par \uc2 Data {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://covid.cdc.gov/covid-data-tracker/#trends_dailycases_select_00"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 obtained}}}\uc2  earlier this month by the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  (CDC) reveals that the rate of new infections has been decreasing, with the country reporting an average of 107,000 new cases a day. This marks a 12% decrease compared to infection rates two weeks ago.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/19/us-covid-cases-mandates-deaths"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Most have thrown their hands up\u8217\'20\'19: has the US forgotten about Covid?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 A major corporate lobbying group has tried to convince Americans that it cares about the environment and climate change. But as Adam Lowenstein reports, its actions are not matching its words:\par \par \uc2 Three years ago today, in a statement that would be described as \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fortune.com/2020/08/19/business-roundtable-statement-purpose-responsibility/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 historic}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fastcompany.com/90391743/top-ceo-group-business-roundtable-drops-shareholder-primacy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 monumental}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.forbes.com/sites/forbesagencycouncil/2019/10/17/are-companies-rising-to-the-occasion-why-181-ceos-signed-a-revolutionary-corporate-governance-pact/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 revolutionary}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, America\u8217\'20\'19s most powerful and politically connected corporations {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businessroundtable.org/business-roundtable-redefines-the-purpose-of-a-corporation-to-promote-an-economy-that-serves-all-americans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 promised}}}\uc2  to \u8220\'20\'1Cprotect the environment by embracing sustainable practices across our businesses\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The \u8220\'20\'1CStatement on the Purpose of a Corporation\u8221\'20\'1D came from the Business Roundtable, an influential Washington DC lobbying group whose 200-plus members include the chief executives of some of the world\u8217\'20\'19s biggest companies, including \uc2 Apple\uc2 , Pepsi, \uc2 Walmart\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/google"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Google}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Today, on the statement\u8217\'20\'19s third anniversary, the Business Roundtable and its member CEOs continue to issue earnest statements about the climate crisis. But the organization is also working diligently \u8211\'20\'13 and spending liberally \u8211\'20\'13 to weaken efforts that would enable investors to hold companies accountable for their climate promises.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/aug/19/top-us-business-lobby-group-climate-action-business-roundtable"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How a top US business lobby promised climate action \u8211\'20\'13 but worked to block efforts}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Back on the topic of whether voters are beginning to drift towards Democrats despite Biden\u8217\'20\'19s poor approval ratings, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cookpolitical.com/analysis/national/national-politics/vibe-shift"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Cook Political Report with Amy Walter}}}\uc2  has today published a piece that looks at just that question.\par \par \uc2 It confirms that there are signs of a shift in voters\u8217\'20\'19 perceptions, but that has less to do with Democrats than Republicans. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not that voters think Democrats are doing better; it\u8217\'20\'19s that they think Republicans are as out-of-touch as as Democrats,\u8221\'20\'1D according to the report.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the story:\par \par \uc2 For the last six weeks or so, the media spotlight has been off of Biden and focused instead on issues that put Republicans on the defensive, like \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , January 6th and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . That has helped to erode Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 previous advantage as the party that is more in tune with voters\u8217\'20\'19 day-to-day concerns.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEach week that goes by, more and more people see the GOP as increasingly focused on the wrong things,\u8221\'20\'1D veteran Democratic strategist \uc2 Jesse Ferguson\uc2  told me. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re focused on what ignites right-wing social media and what pleases the former President, not on what matters to the American people. It\u8217\'20\'19s like a CEO promising to rehab a company by focusing on renovating the executives\u8217\'20\'19 parking spaces.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean the potent forces working against Biden have gone anywhere, or that voters are necessarily getting over the inflation wave that\u8217\'20\'19s pushed costs up across the economy. It concludes with an anecdote:\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, I was able to see how this match-up of messages might play out with voters this fall. At a focus group of white male swing voters, the moderator presented a list of Democratic accomplishments, including things like the infrastructure bill, the Recovery Act, and, of course, the newly passed Inflation Reduction Act. Also noted were low unemployment and strong job growth. When asked to respond, a man from Georgia replied, \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t disagree with anything here. But, I am paying double for lumber and groceries than I was three years ago.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press reports that Biden plans a summit next month to address gun violence and racism:\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will host a White House summit next month aimed at combating hate-fueled violence.\par \par \uc2 The White House announced on Friday that Biden will host the United We Stand Summit on 15 September, seeking to highlight the \u8220\'20\'1Ccorrosive effects\u8221\'20\'1D of violence on public safety and democracy.\par \par \uc2 Advocates pushed Biden to hold the event after 10 Black people were killed at a supermarket in Buffalo, New York, in May, aiming as well to address hate-driven violence in cities including El Paso, Texas, Pittsburgh and Oak Creek, Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs President Biden said in Buffalo after the horrific mass shooting earlier this year, in the battle for the soul of our nation \u8216\'20\'18We must all enlist in this great cause of America,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/19/biden-host-united-we-stand-summit-hate-fueled-us-gun-violence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden to host \u8216\'20\'18United We Stand\u8217\'20\'19 summit to address hate-fueled US gun violence}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Democratic spending bill Biden signed into law last week to fight climate change and lower health care costs also reversed years of underfunding at the \uc2 Internal Revenue Service\uc2 . \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/joan-greve"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joan E Greve}}}\uc2  reports on the Republican counterattack to the money, which relies on claims that are more or less false:\par \par \uc2 The picture that the top Republican painted was both vivid and terrifying. He warned that additional funding for the \uc2 Internal Revenue Service\uc2  would lead to armed auditors banging down front doors to squeeze hard-earned dollars from working Americans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAre they going to have a strike force that goes in with AK-15s already loaded, ready to shoot some small-business person in Iowa with these?\u8221\'20\'1D Senator \uc2 Chuck Grassley\uc2  said on Fox News last week.\par \par \uc2 The Orwellian image conjured up by Grassley bears little resemblance to reality. Democrats have indeed directed nearly $80bn to the \uc2 IRS\uc2  over the next 10 years as part of their climate and healthcare spending package, the Inflation Reduction Act, which \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  signed into law on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/19/irs-republicans-target-misinformation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Armed... auditors? The IRS becomes the latest target of GOP misinformation}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the meat of White House chief of staff \uc2 Ron Klain\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s argument to American voters, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/newsletters/playbook/2022/08/19/ron-klain-says-season-of-substance-could-save-dems-00052839?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=12069c7e-e346-405c-ad2c-71cb1a62e514&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as he put it to Politico}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CElections are choices, and the choice just couldn\u8217\'20\'19t be any clearer right now. Democrats have stood up to the big special interests. They stood up to the big corporations and insisted that all corporations pay minimum taxes, stood up to the big oil companies and passed climate change legislation. They stood up to Big Pharma and passed prescription drug legislation. They stood up to the gun industry and passed gun control legislation. Things that this city [was] unable to deliver on for decades because the special interests had things locked down, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and his allies in Congress have been able to deliver on.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The point of interviews like these is to get the administration\u8217\'20\'19s message out ahead of November\u8217\'20\'19s midterms, when voters will get a chance to decide which lawmakers they want representing them, and ultimately which party controls Congress. Considering Biden\u8217\'20\'19s low approval ratings, the base case now is that Republicans have a good shot at taking the House, while Democrats seem favored to narrowly keep the Senate, though anything could happen.\par \par \uc2 The White House would, of course, prefer Democrats hold onto both chambers. If one falls into the hands of the GOP, the prospects for any major legislation getting through Congress become dramatically slimmer for the next two years. Klain and others seem to be hoping that two things will happen: either enough voters change their minds about Biden, or they divorce their dislike of the president from their opinions of Democrats on the ballot. It may be premature to say whether the latter is happening, but when it comes to the former, polling aggregator FiveThirtyEight {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/biden-approval-rating/?cid=rrpromo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 does show the president\u8217\'20\'19s approval rating recovering from something of a nadir reached in mid-July}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In closing, Klain offered this comment on Biden\u8217\'20\'19s public profile, as compared to the previous White House occupant:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think it\u8217\'20\'19s true he\u8217\'20\'19s out there less than his predecessors. I just think \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  created an expectation of a president creating a shitstorm every single day.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House sees Biden accomplishments as historic. Will Americans agree?\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. Over the past year and a half of his presidency, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has signed legislation to intended to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/24/bipartisan-gun-control-law-house-vote-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 curb gun violence}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/16/biden-signs-inflation-reduction-act-landmark-healthcare-climate-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fight climate change, lower health care costs}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/31/bernie-sanders-conservative-thinktanks-semiconductor-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 promote semiconductor production}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/06/joe-biden-infrastructure-bill-democrats-monumental-step-forward"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 revamp the nation\u8217\'20\'19s infrastructure}}}\uc2 . He\u8217\'20\'19s also presided over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/jul/13/high-us-gas-food-prices-june-led-to-largest-annual-increase-inflation-40-years"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the highest inflation rate since the 1980s}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/30/pentagon-kabul-drone-strike-islamic-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the chaotic withdrawal from Afghanistan}}}\uc2 , cratering his approval ratings. But to White House chief of staff \uc2 Ron Klain\uc2 , the focus should be on the former, not the latter. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/newsletters/playbook/2022/08/19/ron-klain-says-season-of-substance-could-save-dems-00052839?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=12069c7e-e346-405c-ad2c-71cb1a62e514&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In an interview with Politico}}}\uc2  published this morning, he argues that Biden has made a historic impact comparable to Democratic predecessors like Franklin D Roosevelt and Lyndon B Johnson. Come November, we\u8217\'20\'19ll see if voters believe him.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a look at what to expect today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden remains on vacation, and is currently in Delaware.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , the Republican former vice-president, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kcci.com/article/former-vice-president-mike-pence-to-visit-iowa-republicans-politics/40883752"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is visiting Iowa}}}\uc2 , an early kingmaker for presidential contenders.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 If you\u8217\'20\'19re wondering why it\u8217\'20\'19s so quiet, Washington DC is usually this way in August. Not only is the president on vacation, but Congress is in recess and most lawmakers are back in their districts. They should return around the first week of September.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220819ei8j0028v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
