\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  lays groundwork for potential 2024 run with Iowa and New Hampshire visits \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein \par \uc2 4,863 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 August 2022\par 20:06 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Former vice-president will visit Iowa and New Hampshire, both early voting states in the Republican presidential primarySign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s visit to New Hampshire has added to speculation that he may be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/17/cheney-trump-republicans-primary-results-giuliani-biden-latest-updates?page=with:block-62fd3a7b8f0892f840b89134#block-62fd3a7b8f0892f840b89134"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mulling a presidential run in 2024}}}\uc2 . Meanwhile, \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  announced she was considering her own bid for the White House as a defiantly anti-Trump Republican, hours after GOP voters in Wyoming {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/17/cheney-trump-republicans-primary-results-giuliani-biden-latest-updates?page=with:block-62fd03938f080eafb891776e#block-62fd03938f080eafb891776e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected her bid}}}\uc2  to continue as the state\u8217\'20\'19s House representative.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a rundown of today\u8217\'20\'19s news:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/17/cheney-trump-republicans-primary-results-giuliani-biden-latest-updates?page=with:block-62fd431e8f083ef020e6f905#block-62fd431e8f083ef020e6f905"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sure seems to like}}}\uc2  a Wall Street Journal column suggesting a Republican-led Congress or White House could retaliate against Democrats over the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s search of Mar-a-Lago.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A poll from Wisconsin{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/17/cheney-trump-republicans-primary-results-giuliani-biden-latest-updates?page=with:block-62fd343a8f0892f840b890f8#block-62fd343a8f0892f840b890f8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 indicates}}}\uc2  Democrats may have momentum in the state\u8217\'20\'19s Senate race, though the contest for the governorship appears to be tightening.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/17/cheney-trump-republicans-primary-results-giuliani-biden-latest-updates?page=with:block-62fced358f08595b289dfd87#block-62fced358f08595b289dfd87"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has appeared}}}\uc2  before a special grand jury in Atlanta that is investigating attempts to meddle with the state\u8217\'20\'19s election results in 2020. He has been told he is a target of the investigation.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The memoir of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s son-in-law and former White House adviser \uc2 Jared Kushner\uc2  was torn apart by \uc2 The New York Times\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/17/cheney-trump-republicans-primary-results-giuliani-biden-latest-updates?page=with:block-62fd0a358f080eafb89177b1#block-62fd0a358f080eafb89177b1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 book reviewer}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A court ruling allowed the Biden administration to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/17/cheney-trump-republicans-primary-results-giuliani-biden-latest-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62fcf56b8f083ef020e6f5a0#block-62fcf56b8f083ef020e6f5a0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 again pause}}}\uc2  new oil and gas drilling leases on federal land.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his political action committee have promoted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/the-payback-for-mar-a-lago-will-be-brutal-trump-raid-fbi-justice-department-president-investigation-11660255311?mod=opinion_featst_pos2&utm_medium=email_hf&utm_source=ncl__&utm_campaign=20220817___sa&utm_content=__4921&_nlid=5EWDU8XCxp&_nhids=DdJ1F6b7BN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Wall Street Journal column}}}\uc2  suggesting that Republicans could seek revenge against Democratic politicians for the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s search of Mar-a-Lago.\par \par \uc2 Attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Craid has made even the highest political figures fair prosecutorial game, and the media\u8217\'20\'19s new standard is that the department can\u8217\'20\'19t be questioned as it goes about ensuring \u8216\'20\'18no one is above the law.\u8217\'20\'19 Let\u8217\'20\'19s see how that holds when a future Republican Justice Department starts raiding the homes of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , \uc2 Eric Holder\uc2 , \uc2 James Comey\uc2  and John Brennan,\u8221\'20\'1D writes Kimberley A. Strassel, a member of the Journal\u8217\'20\'19s editorial board.\par \par \uc2 She also posits that a GOP-controlled House, which could come as soon as next year, might create their own select committees similar to the one investigating the January 6 attack, and perhaps subpoena Democratic lawmakers. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat goes around always comes around. What went around this week will come around hard,\u8221\'20\'1D Strassel wrote in the piece published August 11.\par \par \uc2 Trump was apparently a fan of the column:\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump reposts an op-ed describing the likelihood of payback \u8212\'20\'14 such as raiding homes of Biden, Clinton, Comey etc \u8212\'20\'14 if he retakes the White House. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/v067yHOK69"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/v067yHOK69}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1559948057457958912?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 As was the Trump War Room, managed by his Save America PAC:\par \par \uc2 enltrICYMI: "The Payback for Mar-a-Lago Will Be Brutal" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/58YugoDe8m"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/58YugoDe8m}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Trump War Room (@TrumpWarRoom) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TrumpWarRoom/status/1559984053339693057?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  lays groundwork for potential 2024 run\par \par \uc2 Today, he\u8217\'20\'19s in New Hampshire, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Mike_Pence/status/1559921559669821441"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 promoting conservative policies}}}\uc2  while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/17/cheney-trump-republicans-primary-results-giuliani-biden-latest-updates?page=with:block-62fd20088f080eafb8917913#block-62fd20088f080eafb8917913"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calling on fellow Republicans to hold off on attacking the FBI}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/17/cheney-trump-republicans-primary-results-giuliani-biden-latest-updates?page=with:block-62fcfe728f083ef020e6f613#block-62fcfe728f083ef020e6f613"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signaling a willingness}}}\uc2  to talk to the January 6 committee. Next, he\u8217\'20\'19ll be in Iowa, where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kcci.com/article/former-vice-president-mike-pence-to-visit-iowa-republicans-politics/40883752#"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he is to attend the state fair and meet with the state\u8217\'20\'19s GOP honchos}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Just what is \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  doing? Laying the groundwork for a potential presidential run in 2024, that\u8217\'20\'19s what. Iowa and New Hampshire are both early voting states in the Republican presidential primary, and stops by prospective candidates such as Pence are not out of the ordinary.\par \par \uc2 Where Pence would fit into the 2024 Republican field is unclear. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is seen as champing at the bit to return to the campaign trail, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/25/trump-hang-mike-pence-chant-jan-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly has}}}\uc2  little love for his former number two. If Pence hopes to capture the support of Republicans who have tired of Trump, he may have to vie against Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , who could tailor his campaign to the same voters. Then there\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , a conservative Republican who was last night ousted from the House by the Wyoming GOP in favor of a Trump-backed attorney. If Pence opts to run as a defiantly anti-Trump Republican, she would be his chief opponent, assuming she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/17/liz-cheney-president-2024-trump-republican-primary-defeat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decides to aim for the presidency}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But that\u8217\'20\'19s not all. Pence could find himself up against Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former United Nations ambassador Nikki Haley, or his former secretary of state \uc2 Mike Pompeo\uc2 , or even South Dakota\u8217\'20\'19s governor \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2 , not to mention conservative senators like \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2 , Ted Cruz, or Tom Cotton. In a field with this much potential for crowding, one can see why Pence may want an early start.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood plans to spend a record $50 million ahead of November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections, pouring money into contests where access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be on the ballot.\par \par \uc2 The effort, which breaks the group\u8217\'20\'19s previous $45 million spending record set in 2020, comes about two months after the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade. It will be waged by the organization\u8217\'20\'19s political and advocacy arms and will focus on governor\u8217\'20\'19s offices, \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2  seats and legislative races in nine states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights could be restricted or expanded, depending on the outcome at the ballot.\par \par \uc2 The historic proportions of the midterm campaign, when less money is usually spent than in presidential races, were made possible by a torrent of money raised after the decision by the high court\u8217\'20\'19s new conservative majority, touching off a tectonic shift in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  politics. For the first time, Republicans who have long campaigned against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will face voters on an issue that is no longer hypothetical and carries real life consequences.\par \par \uc2 ??As {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  move towards an election season rife with internal disagreements and mixed public opinions on exceptions in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans such as instances of rape and incest, many rightwing lawmakers are finding it increasingly difficult to implement cohesive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies.\par \par \uc2 The phenomenon has been starkly illustrated by Kansas\u8217\'20\'19s referendum a few weeks ago, where the usually Republican state voted to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections in its constitution, providing an unexpected boost from red state America to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights movement.\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood says its spending will help remind voters in Arizona, Georgia, Michigan, Minnesota, Nevada, New Hampshire, North Carolina, Pennsylvania and Wisconsin what\u8217\'20\'19s at stake in a bid to drive turnout by Democratic and independent voters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWho wins in these midterm elections will determine whether a state has access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and potentially determine whether we will face a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jenny Lawson, the executive director of Planned Parenthood Votes. \u8220\'20\'1CWe will be clear about who is on which side.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood says it intends to contact 6 million voters through door knocking, phone calls, digital advertising, mailers and radio ads.\par \par \uc2 It also is launching a website, takecontrol2022.com.\par \par \uc2 According to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/fact-tank/2022/07/15/key-facts-about-the-abortion-debate-in-america/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 survey}}}\uc2  conducted between 27 June and 4 July by the \uc2 Pew Research\uc2  center, a majority of the American public disapproves of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn Roe: 57% of adults disapprove of the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision, including 43% who strongly disapprove, and 41% of American adults approve while 25% strongly approve of the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision.\par \par \uc2 The survey also found that 62% of Americans say that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in all or most cases, and 36% of Americans say that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be illegal in all or most cases. Only 38% of Republicans say that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in all or most cases, marking a 1-point decrease from poll results obtained in 2007.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 A poll from Wisconsin is adding credence to the idea that Democrats are gaining strength in congressional races.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://law.marquette.edu/poll/2022/08/17/mlsp71-press-release/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The survey from Marquette University Law School}}}\uc2  shows the Democratic nominee for Senate, Mandela Barnes, up by 51 percent against Republican incumbent Ron Johnson \u8217\'20\'19s 44 percent. The race for governor is much closer, with Democratic incumbent \uc2 Tony Evers\uc2  coming in with 45 percent of support against \uc2 Tim Michels\uc2 , the Republican challenging him, whose preference was at 43 percent.\par \par \uc2 The data confirms increased momentum for Barnes, who was polling at 46 percent against Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s 44 percent in a mid-June survey. In the governor\u8217\'20\'19s race, it suggest tightening, as Evers was up by 48 percent against Michels\u8217\'20\'19 41 percent in the earlier poll.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 It appears Harriet Hageman, the attorney who ousted \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  from the House of Representatives in the Wyoming Republican party primary, has no interest in talking to her predecessor.\par \par \uc2 Politico reports that Cheney attempted to concede in a phone call to Hageman, but ended up leaving a voice message:\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: Rep. \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  tells me her concession call to Harriet Hageman ended up being a "clear and direct" voicemail that she left before she went on stage last night, after trying multiple times to get in touch w/ her.\par \par \uc2 Cheney says she still has not heard anything back.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Olivia Beavers (@Olivia_Beavers) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Olivia_Beavers/status/1559935659673980929?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr"I left her a message before I went on stage -- again, after we tried three different times to reach her," Cheney told me in an interview today. "And that was that was that."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Olivia Beavers (@Olivia_Beavers) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Olivia_Beavers/status/1559936180963004417?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 As afternoon turned to evening on January 6, 2021, the \uc2 US Capitol Police\uc2  received the following message from the \uc2 US Secret Service\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CGood afternoon, The \uc2 US Secret Service\uc2  is passing notification to the \uc2 US Capitol Police\uc2  regarding discovery of a social media threat directed toward Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Secret Service sent along a social media post containing threats to lawmakers, including Pelosi. But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.citizensforethics.org/reports-investigations/crew-investigations/secret-service-held-onto-pelosi-threat-until-after-insurrection/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to Citizens for Responsibility and Ethics in Washington}}}\uc2 , which obtained Secret Service emails containing the warning, the agency had first learned about it two days before the insurrection at the Capitol, during which many of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s supporters made no secret of their desire for revenge against lawmakers who were a thorn in his side.\par \par \uc2 The investigation adds to the questions swirling around the Secret Service. The agency is embroiled in a scandal after it was revealed it allowed agents\u8217\'20\'19 text messages from around the time of the attack to be deleted, prompting calls in Congress for accountability.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/11/missing-secret-service-texts-congress-notified-april"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Secret Service watchdog suppressed memo on January 6 texts erasure}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  is facing a federal lawsuit from a state attorney he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/04/ron-desantis-suspends-andrew-warren-prosector-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suspended earlier this month}}}\uc2  for \u8220\'20\'1Cwokeness\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In a \uc2 Twitter\uc2  post, Andrew Warren said he filed papers in Tallahassee this morning, calling his removal as state attorney for Hillsborough county \u8220\'20\'1Ca blatant abuse of power\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrToday we took action against \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 ' abuse of power and unlawful suspension. Please join us in this fight at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/mebZt8It8i"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/mebZt8It8i}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/DefendDemocracyNow?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #DefendDemocracyNow}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ekluzexc2H"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ekluzexc2H}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Andrew Warren (@AndrewWarrenFL) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewWarrenFL/status/1559911172756934657?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 DeSantis suspended Warren on 4 August for \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.flgov.com/2022/08/04/governor-ron-desantis-suspends-state-attorney-andrew-warren-for-refusing-to-enforce-florida-law/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 neglect of duty}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D after the twice-elected official said he would not enforce the state\u8217\'20\'19s new 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. The governor said Warren was following a \u8220\'20\'1Cwoke agenda,\u8221\'20\'1D although some analysts question the legality of the move based on an action that hasn\u8217\'20\'19t taken place yet.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe governor has broken two laws. He\u8217\'20\'19s violated my first amendment rights by retaliating against me for speaking out on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and transgender rights, and he\u8217\'20\'19s violated the Florida constitution by removing me from office without any legal justification,\u8221\'20\'1D Warren said in the post.\par \par \uc2 There was no immediate reaction from DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s office.\par \par \uc2 The Orlando Sentinel noted that DeSantis, seen as a likely candidate for the Republican party\u8217\'20\'19s 2024 presidential nomination, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.orlandosentinel.com/news/os-ne-florida-sheriffs-gun-control-desantis-20220808-olkcvjqfkfcm7b2pb6unzh2hsi-story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has taken no action}}}\uc2  against so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cconstitutional\u8221\'20\'1D sheriffs who say they won\u8217\'20\'19t enforce certain Florida gun laws.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  asked fellow Republicans to stop lashing out at the \uc2 FBI\uc2  over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/10/fbi-searched-trumps-home-seeking-classified-presidential-records-sources"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 their recent search of Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s house}}}\uc2 , reports the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 During an event in New Hampshire, Pence called demands from Republicans to defund the \uc2 FBI\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cjust as wrong\u8221\'20\'1D as previous calls from activists to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/feb/03/joe-biden-new-york-crime-us-politics-democrats-republicans-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 divest funding from the police}}}\uc2  for other needs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Republican Party is the party of law and order,\u8221\'20\'1D said Pence.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur party stands with the men and women who stand on the thin blue line at the federal and state and local level, and these attacks on the \uc2 FBI\uc2  must stop. Calls to defund the \uc2 FBI\uc2  are just as wrong as calls to defund the police.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Pence added Republicans can criticize attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  and ask for more transparency around the search without condemning the \uc2 FBI\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 FBI\uc2  officials have said that law enforcement have encountered a number of Trump supporters who seem ready to attack the \uc2 FBI\uc2  or those they believe are investigating Trump too much, following the search.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 The director of the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  (CDC) announced today that the agency will undergo a massive restructuring following failures during the Covid-19 pandemic.\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  sign stands at the entrance of their offices in Atlanta on Tuesday, April 19, 2022. Photograph: Ron Harris/AP\par \par \uc2 CDC director \uc2 Rochelle P. Walensky\uc2  announced the planned changes during a meeting with senior staff today, acknowledging the CDC\u8217\'20\'19s botched response to Covid-19, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/08/17/us/politics/cdc-rochelle-walensky-covid.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported the New York Times}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor 75 years, \uc2 C.D.C\uc2 . and public health have been preparing for Covid-19, and in our big moment, our performance did not reliably meet expectations,\u8221\'20\'1D said Walensky on the agency\u8217\'20\'19s shortcomings.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy goal is a new, public health, action-oriented culture at \uc2 C.D.C\uc2 . that emphasizes accountability, collaboration, communication and timeliness.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Changes will be aimed at increasing the CDC\u8217\'20\'19s ability to faster respond to major health crises and restoring public trust.\par \par \uc2 Critics of the CDC say that during the Covid-19 pandemic, the agency failed to scale up testing, vaccination efforts, and data collection.\par \par \uc2 The CDC has also been accused of publishing ineffective and contradictory health advice on Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 Similar issues have been raised about the CDC\u8217\'20\'19s response to the spread of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/07/monkeypox-vaccine-appointments-new-york-san-francisco"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 monkey pox}}}\uc2  in the US.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s elections in Wyoming and Alaska have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/17/cheney-trump-republicans-primary-results-giuliani-biden-latest-updates?page=with:block-62fd03938f080eafb891776e#block-62fd03938f080eafb891776e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ousted}}}\uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  from her House seat while giving \uc2 Sarah Palin{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/17/cheney-trump-republicans-primary-results-giuliani-biden-latest-updates?page=with:block-62fd104b8f080eafb891781e#block-62fd104b8f080eafb891781e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a shot at}}}\uc2  getting her own spot in the chamber. But Cheney has vowed to keep fighting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his allies, a task at which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/17/cheney-trump-republicans-primary-results-giuliani-biden-latest-updates?page=with:block-62fce44f8f08b9fd3e4e05fe#block-62fce44f8f08b9fd3e4e05fe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 many before her have failed}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a rundown of what has happened so far today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/17/cheney-trump-republicans-primary-results-giuliani-biden-latest-updates?page=with:block-62fcfe728f083ef020e6f613#block-62fcfe728f083ef020e6f613"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signaled a degree of openness}}}\uc2  to talking to the January 6 committee, though with several caveats.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/17/cheney-trump-republicans-primary-results-giuliani-biden-latest-updates?page=with:block-62fced358f08595b289dfd87#block-62fced358f08595b289dfd87"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has appeared}}}\uc2  before a special grand jury in Atlanta that is investigating attempts to meddle with the state\u8217\'20\'19s election results in 2020. He has been told he is a target of the investigation.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The memoir of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s son-in-law and former White House adviser \uc2 Jared Kushner\uc2  was torn apart by \uc2 The New York Times\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/17/cheney-trump-republicans-primary-results-giuliani-biden-latest-updates?page=with:block-62fd0a358f080eafb89177b1#block-62fd0a358f080eafb89177b1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 book reviewer}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A court ruling allowed the Biden administration to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/17/cheney-trump-republicans-primary-results-giuliani-biden-latest-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62fcf56b8f083ef020e6f5a0#block-62fcf56b8f083ef020e6f5a0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 again pause}}}\uc2  new oil and gas drilling leases on federal land.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 While Alaska\u8217\'20\'19s elections were held yesterday, it may take till the end of the month to determine the winner of closely fought races, such as the special election for the state\u8217\'20\'19s vacant House of Representatives seat.\par \par \uc2 According to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.adn.com/politics/2022/08/16/alaska-special-us-house-election-results-show-a-close-race/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Anchorage Daily News}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CAs of 2 a.m. Wednesday, the Alaska Division of Elections had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.elections.alaska.gov/election-results/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 counted over 150,000 ballots}}}\uc2  in the race that will determine Alaska\u8217\'20\'19s next representative in Congress, in a special election to replace 49-year Rep. \uc2 Don Young\uc2 , who died unexpectedly in March. The Division will continue to accept ballots until Aug. 31, as long as they were postmarked on or before election day. Once the last ballots are counted \u8212\'20\'14 if no candidate crosses the 50% threshold needed to win under the state\u8217\'20\'19s new ranked choice voting system \u8212\'20\'14 the candidate in last place will be eliminated and the second-place votes of that candidate\u8217\'20\'19s supporters will be redistributed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Sarah Palin\uc2  may nearing a return to the national political stage, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/maanvi-singh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maanvi Singh}}}\uc2  reports, after Alaska voters gave her decent support in last night\u8217\'20\'19s special election:\par \par \uc2 Sarah Palin\uc2  looks set to be on the ballot in November\u8217\'20\'19s general election after the former governor of Alaska and ex vice-presidential candidate clinched one of four spots vying for a seat in the US House, according to the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 Palin, who rose to fame more than a decade ago as \uc2 John McCain\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s running mate, advanced to the general election along with her two challengers, Nick Begich III, a tech millionaire backed by the Alaska Republican party, and Mary Peltola, a former state legislator and Democrat. It was too early to call the fourth spot.\par \par \uc2 Palin, Peltola and Begich are competing for Alaska\u8217\'20\'19s only House seat, formerly occupied by \uc2 Don Young\uc2 , who died in March. The trio were also competing in a special election to serve the remainder of Young\u8217\'20\'19s term, which ends early next year.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/16/alaska-election-sarah-palin-career-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sarah Palin advances to November election for Alaska House seat}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis book is like a tour of a once majestic 18th-century wooden house, now burned to its foundations, that focuses solely on, and rejoices in, what\u8217\'20\'19s left amid the ashes: the two singed bathtubs, the gravel driveway and the mailbox.\u8221\'20\'1D That\u8217\'20\'19s a line in a New York Times review of a Trump administration official\u8217\'20\'19s newly published memoir. But whose?\par \par \uc2 The answer: \uc2 Jared Kushner\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/08/17/books/review-breaking-history-jared-kushner.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The literary savaging}}}\uc2  of \u8220\'20\'1CBreaking History\u8221\'20\'1D, the memoir of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s son-in-law who became one of his closest White House advisers, was carried out by Times literary critic Dwight Garner, who is clearly no fan of the former president\u8217\'20\'19s policies. \u8220\'20\'1CKushner almost entirely ignores the chaos, the alienation of allies, the breaking of laws and norms, the flirtations with dictators, the comprehensive loss of America\u8217\'20\'19s moral leadership, and so on, ad infinitum, to speak about his boyish tinkering (the \u8220\'20\'1Cmechanic\u8221\'20\'1D) with issues he was interested in,\u8221\'20\'1D Garner writes.\par \par \uc2 The reviewer however finds plenty of issues with the book\u8217\'20\'19s content and prose irrespective of its politics, concluding that it ultimately contains so little meaningful insights into the Trump administration as to be uninteresting to just about every party that would want to read it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou finish \u8216\'20\'18Breaking History\u8217\'20\'19 wondering: Who is this book for? There\u8217\'20\'19s not enough red meat for the MAGA crowd, and Kushner has never appealed to them anyway. Political wonks will be interested \u8212\'20\'14 maybe, to a limited degree \u8212\'20\'14 but this material is more thoroughly and reliably covered elsewhere. He\u8217\'20\'19s a pair of dimples without a demographic,\u8221\'20\'1D Garner says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the latest on \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s primary defeat and plans for political rebirth, from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/davidsmith"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 David Smith}}}\uc2  on the ground in Jackson, Wyoming along with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/richardluscombe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Richard Luscombe}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/joannawalters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joanna Walters}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Republican congresswoman \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  has announced she is considering her own run for the White House in an all-out effort to prevent \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  from winning another term as US president.\par \par \uc2 Cheney {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/16/wyoming-republican-primary-liz-cheney-donald-trump-harriet-hageman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decisively lost}}}\uc2  her Republican primary race on Tuesday night and will lose her seat in the \uc2 US Congress\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Trump-backed challenger Harriet Hageman beat Cheney by almost 40 points as Wyoming voters took revenge for her voting to impeach Trump and for focusing on her role on the January 6 House select committee.\par \par \uc2 The panel, of which Cheney is vice-chair and one of only two {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2 , is investigating Trump\u8217\'20\'19s role in fomenting the insurrection at the US Capitol by his supporters on 6 January 2021, in a vain attempt to stay in office following his defeat by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/17/liz-cheney-president-2024-trump-republican-primary-defeat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Liz Cheney considers run for president after Republican primary defeat}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  was praised on MSNBC this morning by, of all people, White House chief of staff \uc2 Ron Klain\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think there was anything we agree on,\u8221\'20\'1D said Klain, who was tasked by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  with getting his legislative proposals through Congress. \u8220\'20\'1CBut, I respect enormously her commitment to democracy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WHCOS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @WHCOS}}}\uc2 Ron Klain\uc2  commends Rep. \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  (R-WY) for upholding her oath to the Constitution, instead of swearing "fealty" to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 "I respect enormously [\uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 's] commitment to democracy... instead of her commitment to one man." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/wIKog8CyQQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/wIKog8CyQQ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1559915319438843904?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pence 'would consider' talking to January 6 committee - but with caveats\par \par \uc2 A closer look at former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s remarks about testifying before the January 6 committee indicates \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s one-time White House deputy would indeed entertain the request, but also has concerns about the constitutional implications.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a full video of his comments:\par \par \uc2 enltrFormer Vice President \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  when asked if he would cooperate if the January 6th committee called on him to testify:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf there was an invitation to participate, I would consider it.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/y9NFrHwYtf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/y9NFrHwYtf}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1559911020898000897?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Inflation Reduction Act signed yesterday was another major part of the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s climate plan, and includes a slew of new tax incentives to encourage green investments, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/oliver-milman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oliver Milman}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 The giant climate bill signed by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  on Tuesday is set to touch upon myriad aspects of Americans\u8217\'20\'19 lives, helping shape everything from the cars they drive to the stovetops in their kitchens.\par \par \uc2 Biden has lauded the $369bn of climate spending in the Inflation Reduction Act as the \u8220\'20\'1Clargest investment ever in combatting the existential crisis of climate change\u8221\'20\'1D and predicted it will save people hundreds of dollars each year in energy costs. This claim is based upon a series of investments aimed at shifting buying habits away from a polluting status quo towards cleaner, electrified vehicles and appliances.\par \par \uc2 A US household could save $1,800 on their energy costs each year, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rewiringamerica.org/policy/inflation-reduction-act"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a recent estimate}}}\uc2 , although this would require the installation of electric heat pumps for hot water and air conditioning, replacing a gasoline-powered car with an electric vehicle and installing solar panels on the roof.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/17/biden-climate-law-savings-rebate-electric-car-solar-panel-appliance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Electric cars to solar panels: tax breaks in Biden\u8217\'20\'19s climate law for Americans}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Court allows Biden administration to again pause oil and gas leases on federal land\par \par \uc2 A Louisiana judge has allowed the Biden administration to reinstate a pause on new oil and gas leases on federal land, in a win for the White House\u8217\'20\'19s climate policy, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 The order by a judge in the fifth circuit court of appeals overturns a previous lower court ruling that blocked the pause, which \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announced in the opening days of his administration. Earlier this year, the interior department began selling new onshore oil and natural gas drilling leases while the case made its way through court.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/16/public-lands-reopen-oil-gas-drilling-joe-biden-government"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Public lands to reopen for oil and gas drilling in a first under Biden}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mild tidbit of news from \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  during his appearance in New Hampshire, as reported by Politico:\par \par \uc2 enltrFormer VP \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  says if there was an invitation to testify before the Jan. 6 committee, "I would consider it." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/nhpolitics?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #nhpolitics}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lisa Kashinsky (@lisakashinsky) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lisakashinsky/status/1559887666316840960?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Pence isn\u8217\'20\'19t known to have talked to the committee. However, his name has been all over the public hearings, which have featured in-person and videotaped testimony from people close to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s vice-president about what he was doing in the days before the attack on the Capitol, and during the assault, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/16/mike-pence-40ft-from-mob-january-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 when he had to flee to a hidden area}}}\uc2 . Meanwhile, Pence\u8217\'20\'19s former chief of staff has spoken to a grand jury investigating the assault.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/25/mike-pence-ex-chief-of-staff-testifies-grand-jury-january-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mike Pence\u8217\'20\'19s ex-chief of staff testifies to grand jury investigating January 6}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lawyer \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  has arrived at an Atlanta court for his appearance before a special grand jury investigating the effort to overturn the state\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 election results.\par \par \uc2 He was greeted by something of a media circus:\par \par \uc2 enltrRudy Giuliani has arrived at the Fulton County Courthouse to testify in grand jury proceedings looking into interference in the 2020 election results. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cbs46?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @cbs46}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6mAC7AdcNQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/6mAC7AdcNQ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Madeline Montgomery (@MadelineTV) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MadelineTV/status/1559880772340928513?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrRudy Giuliani arrives at the Fulton County Courthouse, with a mob of cameras and reporters following his entrance, as he is set to testify behind closed doors in a special grand jury probe.\par \par \uc2 He is a target of the investigation. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/gapol?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #gapol}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/64BWdHcKVT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/64BWdHcKVT}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 stephen fowler (@stphnfwlr) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/stphnfwlr/status/1559882006355484674?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 17, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s appearance will not be public, but Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , who convened the special grand jury, has informed the one-time New York City mayor he is a target of the investigation. Giuliani made repeated efforts to convince state officials that Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 election results were fraudulent, but none of the allegations were ever found to have substance.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/15/rudy-giuliani-target-criminal-investigation-georgia-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rudy Giuliani informed he is target of criminal investigation in Georgia}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Many Republicans have stood against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Few have succeeded.\par \par \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  will now be the latest to try, looking to capitalize on her conservative voting record, her vice-chairmanship of the January 6 committee and of course her father\u8217\'20\'19s time as vice-president under Republican \uc2 George W. Bush\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump remains {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://morningconsult.com/2022/08/11/fbi-raid-increases-trumps-2024-primary-support/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the favorite}}}\uc2  among Republicans for the party\u8217\'20\'19s 2024 presidential nomination, and undoing that would require Cheney to convince the GOP to abandon the viewpoints and policies he brought into the mainstream when he won the White House in 2016. It\u8217\'20\'19s a tough ask, and no shortage of Republicans have failed in the past. Just ask the eight House Republicans who voted for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s impeachment but then were ousted by voters or opted to retire, or the various party fathers and moderates who begged the GOP not to back Trump, only to be bowled over by the will of the electorate.\par \par \uc2 Why is Cheney doing it? As {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsweek.com/read-liz-cheneys-concession-speech-congresswoman-ousted-wyoming-1734296"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 she said in her concession speech}}}\uc2  last night, \u8220\'20\'1CA few years ago, I won this primary with 73 percent of the vote. I could easily have done the same again. The path was clear, but it would have required that I go along with President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lie about the 2020 election\u8230\'20\'26 That was a path I could not and would not take.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/newsletters/playbook/2022/08/17/scoop-liz-cheneys-next-move-00052332?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=12069c7e-e346-405c-ad2c-71cb1a62e514&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico\u8217\'20\'19s Playbook has another theory}}}\uc2 . Cheney won\u8217\'20\'19t have much competition in the Trump-hating space, they write, with the GOP more or less in his grips and Democrats split over how big of a deal to make of him among their voters. \u8220\'20\'1CSo rather than a kamikaze mission, her primary loss may have been more like parachuting out of a plane that had outlived its usefulness. Her great task now is figuring out where to land,\u8221\'20\'1D Playbook says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 After primary loss, \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  aims for new job: Trump foe-in-chief\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. Last night, Republican voters rejected \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s bid to continue serving as their congresswoman, meaning she has only the remainder of the year left in the House of Representatives. She will continue in the highly public role of vice-chair of the January 6 committee, but this morning, Cheney said she is thinking about a run for presidency in 2024 \u8211\'20\'13 putting her in a position to compete directly against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , a fellow Republican whom she loathes.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re certain to hear more about that today, but here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In Alaska, ex-governor \uc2 Sarah Palin{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/16/alaska-election-sarah-palin-career-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  advanced in the special election}}}\uc2  to fill the state\u8217\'20\'19s open house seat, giving the one-time vice-presidential nominee a shot at returning to national politics. Voters will make their final decision in November.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 who also fell out with Trump \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=pence%20new%20hampshire&src=typed_query"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is in New Hampshire}}}\uc2 , another state where voters are known as early kingmakers for aspiring presidential candidates. Indeed, Pence has hinted he may run in 2024.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration will attempt a victory lap following the signing of the Inflation Reduction Act yesterday, the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 landmark spending plan to fight climate change and lower health care costs. However \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  himself is on vacation in Delaware.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220817ei8h001xr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
