\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Florida court rules teenager \u8216\'20\'18not mature enough\u8217\'20\'19 to have  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Erum Salam \par \uc2 380 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 August 2022\par 18:51 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The 16-year-old cited being a student and unemployed as reasons she is unprepared to have a baby\par \par \uc2 A pregnant teenager will be blocked from getting an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a Florida court ruled on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The 16-year-old initially petitioned to terminate her pregnancy, citing being a student and unemployed as reasons she is unprepared to have a baby.\par \par \uc2 A court ruled she was not mature enough to make the decision to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , blocking her from getting one.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe trial court found, based on the non adversarial presentation below, that Appellant had not established by clear and convincing evidence that she was sufficiently mature to decide whether to terminate her pregnancy,\u8221\'20\'1D the decision read.\par \par \uc2 Though the teen appealed the decision, the appellate court upheld the lower court\u8217\'20\'19s decision.\par \par \uc2 In order for a minor to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Florida, they must provide a physician with written consent from a parent or legal guardian, or request a waiver. The teenager explained her father is unable to assist her and that her \u8220\'20\'1Cguardian is fine with what [she] wants to do\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.documentcloud.org/documents/22136554/222476_dc05_08152022_170017_i.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 court documents}}}\uc2 , one judge, Scott Makar, acknowledged the trial judge viewed \u8220\'20\'1Cthis matter as a very close call\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe transcript demonstrates that the minor was knowledgeable about the relevant considerations in terminating her pregnancy along with four other statutory factors. She had done \uc2 Google\uc2  searches and reviewed a pamphlet (that she and a family member got from their visit to a medical clinic) to gain an understanding about her medical options and their consequences.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The teen\u8217\'20\'19s case is a result of the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  in June overturning Roe v Wade, the landmark 1973 case that gave Americans the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws are now left up to states. Since the supreme court decision, Florida banned abortions after 15 weeks of pregnancy, without exceptions for rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 Still, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/09/florida-abortion-ban-ron-desantis-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  laws}}}\uc2  are less restrictive than neighboring states, including South Carolina, Georgia, Mississippi, Alabama and Louisiana \u8211\'20\'13 which have either banned abortions after six weeks, or altogether.\par \par \uc2 For now, the teen is unable to access an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in her home state and must continue her pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220817ei8h002uw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
