\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden urged to clarify that  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  aid abroad unaffected by Roe v Wade ruling\b0\par\par\uc2 Noa Yachot \par \uc2 1,170 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 August 2022\par 10:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Senators also seek to correct misinterpretation by aid recipients of Helms amendment as a blanket ban on US funds for abortions\par \par \uc2 Supporters of reproductive rights in Congress are calling on the government to clarify to foreign aid recipients that the end of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the US does not affect US-funded family planning programs abroad, and to limit the damage of a half-century-old law that has functioned as a blanket ban that prevents US aid from supporting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care overseas.\par \par \uc2 Their efforts come as the Biden administration looks for ways to support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the wake of the supreme court decision overturning Roe v Wade \u8211\'20\'13 which scrapped \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights \u8211\'20\'13 and amid signs that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights could be a persuasive issue in midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 A group of senators on Thursday sent a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cardin.senate.gov/wp-content/uploads/2022/08/USAID-Letter-on-post-Dobbs-Guidance.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter}}}\uc2  to \uc2 Samantha Power\uc2 , head of the \uc2 US Agency for International Development\uc2 , asking her to address \u8220\'20\'1Cconfusion\u8221\'20\'1D and make clear to aid recipients that the changing landscape of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the United States does not affect \uc2 USAid\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s support for \u8220\'20\'1Cthe full range of family planning and reproductive health care services\u8221\'20\'1D permitted under the law.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe US is the largest donor of reproductive health and family planning services in the world,\u8221\'20\'1D the New Jersey senator \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2  told the Guardian. \u8220\'20\'1CIn order to mitigate the harms of the Dobbs decision globally, we must do all we can to increase access to reproductive health information and safe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care at home and abroad.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, more than 100 reproductive and gender rights groups signed on to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ipas.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/08/International-SRHR-post-Dobbs.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 separate letter}}}\uc2  sent to Power and the secretary of state, Anthony Blinken, asking them to clarify that the 1973 Helms amendment \u8211\'20\'13 which restricts overseas aid for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 does not affect abortions for those who suffered rape and incest or pregnancies that threaten the health of the mother.\par \par \uc2 Reproductive rights advocates say that the Helms amendment has led to many thousands of preventable maternal deaths since its passage, disproportionately affecting brown and Black women in poor countries and undermining healthcare systems that are reliant on US support.\par \par \uc2 The Helms amendment blocks US foreign aid from funding \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a method of family planning\u8221\'20\'1D. Elsewhere, US law is clear that the definition of \u8220\'20\'1Cfamily planning\u8221\'20\'1D excludes pregnancies as a result of rape and incest, along with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to save the life of the pregnant person.\par \par \uc2 But aid recipients overseas, fearing the loss of crucial US funds, have often misinterpreted the law as a total ban, the advocacy groups say.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[M]any organizations receiving US assistance lack proper guidance from \uc2 USAid\uc2  and the state department on the scope of the law and unduly limit the care they provide in fear of falling afoul of US funding restrictions,\u8221\'20\'1D the letter reads. \u8220\'20\'1CIn practice, this means that people are frequently denied often life-saving health information and that many victims of sexual assault and incest in medical emergencies are deprived of legal and necessary health care.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It really is unconscionable to imagine that a survivor of rape is being denied \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services because they happen to go to a clinic that receives US foreign assistance\par \par \uc2 Bethany Van Kampen Saravia\par \par \uc2 Booker, along with senators Tammy Duckworth, Mazie Hirono, Tina Smith and Richard Blumenthal, recently introduced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.booker.senate.gov/imo/media/doc/abortion_is_health_care_everywhere_act.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a bill}}}\uc2  to repeal the Helms amendment, a version of which was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2020/jul/29/democrats-introduce-bill-to-repeal-anti-abortion-rule-for-us-overseas-aid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first introduced}}}\uc2  in the House of Representatives in 2020 by congresswoman Jan Schakowsky of Illinois. With the 60-vote threshold required to advance legislation in the Senate, however, its prospects are dim.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CProcedural hurdles do not hinder my commitment to reproductive rights and the health of women across the globe,\u8221\'20\'1D Booker said. \u8220\'20\'1CAlthough the filibuster is a big obstacle, we can\u8217\'20\'19t be intimidated by Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 use of it to suppress and block effective legislation that the American people want, especially when the legislation would help people and save lives.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But supporters of the bill insist that the Biden administration does not need to turn to Congress to save lives \u8211\'20\'13 it can do so immediately by issuing guidance to US aid recipients laying out the exceptions to the law.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a reproductive rights research group, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2021/02/case-ending-global-gag-rule-and-helms-amendment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 estimated}}}\uc2  that 17,000 maternal deaths would be prevented every year if the Helms amendment were repealed, along with 19 million unsafe abortions.\par \par \uc2 Another congressional {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://schakowsky.house.gov/sites/schakowsky.house.gov/files/FINAL_08.02.22%20Helms%20Exceptions%20Letter%20to%20State%2C%20HHS%2C%20and%20USAID%20%281%29.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter}}}\uc2  sent earlier this month, signed by 76 members of Congress from both the House and Senate, highlighted the impact of the law, as it is currently interpreted, on Ukrainian victims of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs we write, there are mounting reports of Russian forces inflicting rape, sexual slavery and forced pregnancy on Ukrainians,\u8221\'20\'1D the letter read. \u8220\'20\'1CAs currently applied, Helms amendment restrictions on US foreign assistance funds mean that none of the more than $1.2bn in US humanitarian aid can be used to support victims who need access to safe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A domestic counterpart to Helms, the Hyde amendment was passed three years later and continues to bar federal Medicaid funds from supporting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the US. Critics say that both laws first and foremost penalize poor people and people of color, who are most likely to need \uc2 US government\uc2  support to access care.\par \par \uc2 The Helms amendment was named for Jesse Helms, the arch-conservative senator from North Carolina who was an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/magazine/2022/07/28/biden-repeal-helms-amendment-on-abortion-00048533"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 outspoken opponent}}}\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , civil rights, LGBTQ+ rights and government-funded Aids research. The law that bears his name was part of a conservative backlash to the Roe v Wade decision that established a federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before being overturned in June.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt really is unconscionable to imagine that a survivor of rape is being denied \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services because they happen to go to a clinic that receives US foreign assistance,\u8221\'20\'1D said Bethany Van Kampen Saravia, senior legal and policy adviser to Ipas, an international reproductive rights organizations that spearheaded Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s letter on behalf of advocacy groups. \u8220\'20\'1CThere is not a single law that says that they have to do that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She pointed as an example to the Democratic Republic of the Congo, where rape has been commonly used as a weapon of war. While \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws there were recently liberalized to allow the procedure in cases of rape, clinics continue to turn away pregnant victims out of fear of losing US funds.\par \par \uc2 With widespread public anger over the June supreme court decision overturning Roe, and proliferating state bans, the Biden administration has looked for ways to bolster \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Among other moves, the administration has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/08/joe-biden-to-sign-order-offering-protection-women-denied-right-to-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 created a taskforce to coordinate}}}\uc2  the federal effort to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/biden-executive-order-protect-abortion-access"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 directed the health and human services department}}}\uc2  to explore ways to support people in states with bans and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/02/idaho-abortion-ban-justice-department-sues"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sued in Idaho}}}\uc2  where the government argues the ban conflicts with federal law.\par \par \uc2 The government could immediately mitigate the harms of US \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy by clarifying the exceptions to the Helms amendment, Van Kampen Saravia says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s really a no-brainer.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220812ei8c001bd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
