\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 DoJ moves for Trump Mar-a-Lago search warrant to be unsealed \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein in Washington \par \uc2 5,429 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 August 2022\par 20:34 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 : DoJ has filed motion to make warrant publicSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  made the unusual step of appearing in Washington to take responsibility for the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s search of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago residence, and saying the department would ask a judge to unseal the warrant and property receipt from the search. Now, the ball is in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s court to object to the documents\u8217\'20\'19 release \u8211\'20\'13 should he so choose.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A gunman opened fire at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/11/trump-fbi-subpoenas-republicans-gas-prices-biden-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62f52abc8f083b8f443ff622#block-62f52abc8f083b8f443ff622"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FBI\u8217\'20\'19s office in Cincinnati}}}\uc2  as the agency faces increased threats following its search of Mar-a-Lago.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 More good economic data bolstered the case that inflation was set to meaningfully decline in the months to come, which the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/11/trump-fbi-subpoenas-republicans-gas-prices-biden-latest?page=with:block-62f5256f8f08181373da683f#block-62f5256f8f08181373da683f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 White House looked to capitalize on}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Top Senate Democrat \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  asked {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/11/trump-fbi-subpoenas-republicans-gas-prices-biden-latest?page=with:block-62f517d48f086d0d751efa53#block-62f517d48f086d0d751efa53"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voters to elect more Democrats}}}\uc2  and give them the chance to pass bills further improving social services.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A poll showed Liz Cheney{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/11/trump-fbi-subpoenas-republicans-gas-prices-biden-latest?page=with:block-62f5422e8f086d0d751efd16#block-62f5422e8f086d0d751efd16"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deep underwater with Wyoming Republicans}}}\uc2  in the upcoming primary, bolstering the case that she will be booted from Congress due to her opposition to Trump.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 , the Republican senator from South Carolina, weighed in on the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s announcement that it will move to release the warrant from the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s search of Mar-a-Lago.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe primary reason the attorney general and \uc2 FBI\uc2  are being pushed to disclose why the search was necessary is because of the deep mistrust of the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and DOJ when it comes to all things Trump\u8221\'20\'1D, Graham said, referring to other investigations involving the former president, such as \uc2 Robert Mueller\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s probe into his campaign\u8217\'20\'19s ties to Russia.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat I am looking for is the predicate for the search. Was the information provided to the judge sufficient and necessary to authorize a raid on the former president\u8217\'20\'19s home within ninety days of the midterm election? I am urging, actually insisting, the DOJ and the \uc2 FBI\uc2  lay their cards on the table as to why this course of action was necessary. Until that is done the suspicion will continue to mount,\u8221\'20\'1D the senator said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHalf the country believes that when it comes to President Trump there are no rules. They have lost faith in the system. The only way to address that problem is full disclosure of the facts and circumstances which led to this unprecedented action.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 The justice department\u8217\'20\'19s motion to unseal the warrant and property receipt from the Mar-a-Lago search have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.flsd.617854/gov.uscourts.flsd.617854.18.0_3.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posted publicly}}}\uc2 , and offers details of the legal reasoning behind the request.\par \par \uc2 The motion recounts that the search was carried out quietly with little public attention, until \u8220\'20\'1Clater that same day, former President Trump issued a public statement acknowledging the execution of the warrant. In the days since, the search warrant and related materials have been the subject of significant interest and attention from news media organizations and other entities.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe public\u8217\'20\'19s clear and powerful interest in understanding what occurred under these circumstances weighs heavily in favor of unsealing\u8221\'20\'1D, said the motion, which was signed by Juan Antonio Gonzalez, the US attorney for the southern district of Florida, and Jay I. Bratt, chief of the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s counterintelligence and export control section.\par \par \uc2 It asks for the documents to be released \u8220\'20\'1Cgiven the intense public interest presented by a search of a residence of a former president\u8230\'20\'26 absent objection from the former president.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  has finished his speech, and declined to take questions from the press.\par \par \uc2 The meat of his address was that the justice department will ask a judge to release the warrant allowing the \uc2 FBI\uc2  to search \u8220\'20\'1Ca premises located in Florida" as Garland put it, which we all know is Mar-a-Lago. It will also ask for the release of the property receipt from the search. Garland said copies of both were left with a lawyer for the ex-president after agents came to the house.\par \par \uc2 Garland noted that he personally approved the search and \u8220\'20\'1Cthe department does not take such a decision lightly\u8221\'20\'1D. He also condemned attacks on the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and federal law enforcement, saying \u8220\'20\'1CI will not stand by silently when their integrity is unfairly attacked\u8221\'20\'1D. Garland declined to comment further, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CMore information will be made available in the appropriate way and have the appropriate time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Justice department moves to release warrant for Mar-a-Lago search\par \par \uc2 Attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  said the justice department will ask a court to unseal the search warrant allowing it to search \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago residence earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe department filed the motion to make public the warrant and receipt in light of the former president\u8217\'20\'19s public confirmation of the search, the surrounding circumstances, and the substantial public interest in this matter,\u8221\'20\'1D Garland said in a press conference at justice department headquarters.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 In his speech, attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  will address the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s search of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago residence earlier this week, CNN confirms:\par \par \uc2 enltrThis will be about the Mar-a-Lago search, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/evanperez?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @evanperez}}}\uc2  reports.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kaitlan Collins (@kaitlancollins) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kaitlancollins/status/1557800933844721665?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The White House was given no advance notice of Garland\u8217\'20\'19s speech, NBC News reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrAs we await AG Merrick Garland and his statement, a senior WH official tells me the Biden WH was not informed this was happening:\par \par \uc2 "We have had no notice that he was giving remarks and no briefing on the content of them."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kelly O'Donnell (@KellyO) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KellyO/status/1557795865032626178?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  set to make public address\par \par \uc2 Attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  will soon make a public statement, days after the \uc2 FBI\uc2  searched former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago residence in Florida. According to reports, agents were acting on a tip that Trump had classified documents at the site.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/11/fbi-trump-classified-records-mar-a-lago"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FBI search of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago home followed tip classified records were there \u8211\'20\'13 report}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Speaking of foes of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , \uc2 John Bolton\uc2 , who served as his national security adviser before falling out with the then-president, said that his Secret Service detail was recalled after he left the White House.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s normal for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D, is how he described the situation to NBC News:\par \par \uc2 enltrFormer NSA \uc2 John Bolton\uc2  says Trump pulled his Secret Service detail \u8220\'20\'1Cwithin hours\u8221\'20\'1D of resigning. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mitchellreports?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @mitchellreports}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CIs that normal?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bolton: \u8220\'20\'1CNo, it\u8217\'20\'19s not normal. Well, it\u8217\'20\'19s normal for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 (Biden later renewed Bolton\u8217\'20\'19s protection due to Iran\u8217\'20\'19s assassination plot.) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/at17ESQnGY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/at17ESQnGY}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1557770364108914691?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Bolton\u8217\'20\'19s comments came after the justice department yesterday charged a member of Iran\u8217\'20\'19s Revolutionary Guards with plotting to kill him.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/10/john-bolton-murder-plot-iranian-man-charged"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US charges Iranian man over alleged plot to kill ex-Trump aide John Bolton}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s days in Congress are numbered.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s the conclusion reached by a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wysac.uwyo.edu/wysac/current-projects/uw-survey-finds-hageman-leading-cheney-in-wyoming-gop-primary/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 University of Wyoming survey}}}\uc2  that finds Cheney, the state\u8217\'20\'19s congresswoman who is vice-chairing the January 6 committee and has become an outspoken opponent of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , almost 30 percentage points behind her challenger Harriet Hageman in next week\u8217\'20\'19s primary.\par \par \uc2 Republicans dominate the rural state and thus the primary is almost certain to decide who will win Wyoming\u8217\'20\'19s lone seat in the House of Representatives. Cheney is politically conservative, but so is Hageman, who has embraced Trump\u8217\'20\'19s conspiracy theories surrounding the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/01/liz-cheney-harriet-hageman-wyoming-republican-primary-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Truth matters\u8217\'20\'19: Liz Cheney lambasts Trump-backed rival in Wyoming debate}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  to make statement at 2.30pm ET\par \par \uc2 News just in: attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  will make a statement at 2.30pm ET. No details on the subject matter yet. But certainly the \uc2 FBI\uc2  raid will be on journalists\u8217\'20\'19 minds.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 New details on Trump raid and documents\par \par \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  has an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/08/11/us/politics/trump-fbi-subpoena.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interesting read}}}\uc2 , revealing the existence of a subpoena for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , issued before the Mar-a-Lago raid by the \uc2 FBI\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Times {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/08/11/us/politics/trump-fbi-subpoena.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Former President \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2  received a subpoena this spring in search of documents that federal investigators believed he had failed to turn over earlier in the year, when he returned boxes of material he had improperly taken with him upon moving out of the White House, three people familiar with the matter said.\par \par \uc2 The existence of the subpoena helps to flesh out the sequence of events that led to the search of Mr. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Florida home on Monday by F.B.I. agents seeking classified material they believed might still be there, even after efforts by the National Archives and the Justice Department to ensure that it had been returned.\par \par \uc2 The subpoena suggests that the Justice Department tried methods short of a search warrant to account for the material before taking the politically explosive step of sending F.B.I. agents unannounced to Mar-a-Lago, Mr. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s home and members-only club.\par \par \uc2 But the most interesting snippet might be lower down the piece. It concerns the nature of the documents Trump possessed and why the \uc2 FBI\uc2  needed to take such firm action. The paper says:\par \par \uc2 Two people briefed on the classified documents that investigators believe remained at Mar-a-Lago indicated that they were so sensitive in nature, and related to national security, that the Justice Department had to act.\par \par \uc2 Interesting \u8211\'20\'13 more is surely yet to be revealed on this story.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Some Republicans hesitant over backing Trump vs \uc2 FBI\par \par \uc2 Since the \uc2 FBI\uc2  raided \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Florida home looking for missing, sensitive documents from his time in the White House, the cacophony of support and condemnation from Republicans has felt unanimous.\par \par \uc2 But not entirely.\par \par \uc2 In a sign that blindly pleasing and following Trump is not seen as an automatic vote-winner in some marginal races, a handful of Republicans have been more reticent in their reactions, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/08/11/how-the-trump-fbi-feud-puts-swing-state-republicans-in-a-bind-00051123"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to Politico}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The top of the piece lists a few.\par \par \uc2 While several Senate GOP nominees jumped to blast the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and federal justice officials, Republican candidates in the swing states of Pennsylvania and North Carolina held off. The next morning, as pressure mounted from vocal right-wing activists, celebrity doctor Mehmet Oz, who is running for the Senate in Pennsylvania, took to \uc2 Twitter\uc2  with a message that did not mention Trump by name but merely lamented the country\u8217\'20\'19s divisions and asserted that Americans had \u8220\'20\'1Cevery right\u8221\'20\'1D to demand answers about the search and seizure of documents.\par \par \uc2 Rep. \uc2 Ted Budd\uc2 , who is seeking a Senate seat in North Carolina, likewise eventually tweeted from his official Congress account after his office was bombarded with calls asking about his response. His statement said Americans deserved a \u8220\'20\'1Cfull explanation\u8221\'20\'1D of what happened.\par \par \uc2 Those calls for transparency from Oz and Budd differ markedly from the more fiery rebukes from other Republicans who painted America as a lawless banana republic \u8212\'20\'14 and reflect that some GOP candidates in battleground states are erring on the side of caution in discussing a Trump investigation that could influence critical independent and suburban voters.\par \par \uc2 Read the rest of the story {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://while/%20several%20Senate%20GOP%20nominees%20jumped%20to%20blast%20the%20FBI%20and%20federal%20justice%20officials,%20Republican%20candidates%20in%20the%20swing%20states%20of%20Pennsylvania%20and%20North%20Carolina%20held%20off.%20The%20next%20morning,%20as%20pressure%20mounted%20from%20vocal%20right-wing%20activists,%20celebrity%20doctor%20Mehmet%20Oz,%20who%20is%20running%20for%20the%20Senate%20in%20Pennsylvania,%20took%20to%20Twitter%20with%20a%20message%20that%20did%20not%20mention%20Trump%20by%20name%20but%20merely%20lamented%20the%20country’s%20divisions%20and%20asserted%20that%20Americans%20had%20“every%20right”%20to%20demand%20answers%20about%20the%20search%20and%20seizure%20of%20documents.%0A%0ARep.%20Ted%20Budd,%20who%20is%20seeking%20a%20Senate%20seat%20in%20North%20Carolina,%20likewise%20eventually%20tweeted%20from%20his%20official%20Congress%20account%20after%20his%20office%20was%20bombarded%20with%20calls%20asking%20about%20his%20response.%20His%20statement%20said%20Americans%20deserved%20a%20“full%20explanation”%20of%20what%20happened.%0A%0AThose%20calls%20for%20transparency%20from%20Oz%20and%20Budd%20differ%20markedly%20from%20the%20more%20fiery%20rebukes%20from%20other%20Republicans%20who%20painted%20America%20as%20a%20lawless%20banana%20republic%20—%20and%20reflect%20that%20some%20GOP%20candidates%20in%20battleground%20states%20are%20erring%20on%20the%20side%20of%20caution%20in%20discussing%20a%20Trump%20investigation%20that%20could%20influence%20critical%20independent%20and%20suburban%20voters."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here.}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Inflation Reduction Act doesn\u8217\'20\'19t just fight climate change and address health care costs. It also would give the \uc2 IRS\uc2  tax authority more resources, after years in which the agency complained of being so underfunded it could barely do its job.\par \par \uc2 Republicans have used the infusion of funds to warn voters that the bill\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic sponsors want to increase audits of the middle class. Treasury secretary \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  has responded to those attacks by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://home.treasury.gov/system/files/136/JLY-letter-to-Commissioner-Rettig-Signed.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sending a letter}}}\uc2  to commissioner \uc2 Charles P. Rettig\uc2  in which she says the agency should not use the money to increase audits for Americans making less than $400,000 a year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI direct that any additional resources \u8212\'20\'14 including any new personnel or auditors that are hired \u8212\'20\'14 shall not be used to increase the share of small business or households below the $400,000 threshold that are audited relative to historical levels,\u8221\'20\'1D Yellen wrote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis means that, contrary to the misinformation from opponents of this legislation, small business or households earning $400,000 per year or less will not see an increase in the chances that they are audited.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been a quiet one in Washington, but that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean the chess pieces aren\u8217\'20\'19t moving. Democrats are gearing up for the House of Representatives to meet tomorrow and pass a major plan to fight climate change and lower health care costs, while Republicans are looking ahead to November, when voters seem poised to return them to control of at least one chamber of Congress.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a rundown of what has happened in the day so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A gunman has attacked a \uc2 FBI\uc2  office in Ohio, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/11/trump-fbi-subpoenas-republicans-gas-prices-biden-latest?page=with:block-62f52abc8f083b8f443ff622#block-62f52abc8f083b8f443ff622"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly engaged}}}\uc2  in a shootout with police. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  will update this blog when more details of the incident become available.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The White House seized on yet another sign of inflation declining to make the case {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/11/trump-fbi-subpoenas-republicans-gas-prices-biden-latest?page=with:block-62f5256f8f08181373da683f#block-62f5256f8f08181373da683f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that better days are ahead for the economy}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A Republican lawmaker who will likely become the party\u8217\'20\'19s top investigator if it takes control of the House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/11/trump-fbi-subpoenas-republicans-gas-prices-biden-latest?page=with:block-62f51d148f083b8f443ff550#block-62f51d148f083b8f443ff550"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told Politico}}}\uc2  to expect investigations of Covid-19\u8217\'20\'19s origins and \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The top Senate Democrat Chuck Schumer{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/11/trump-fbi-subpoenas-republicans-gas-prices-biden-latest?page=with:block-62f517d48f086d0d751efa53#block-62f517d48f086d0d751efa53"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told voters}}}\uc2  that if they give him more senators, he\u8217\'20\'19ll pass more bills to lower costs for child and elder care, which the party failed to agree on in the current Congress.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Gunman opens fire at \uc2 FBI\uc2  office in Ohio amid threats over Trump search\par \par \uc2 An armed person who opened fire with a nail gun at a \uc2 FBI\uc2  office in Cincinnati has been chased into a field and is exchanging fire with police, according to federal investigators and media reports.\par \par \uc2 The agency has faced a number of threats since its search of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago residence earlier this week, prompting director \uc2 Christopher Wray\uc2  to declare, \u8220\'20\'1CViolence against law enforcement is not the answer, no matter who you\u8217\'20\'19re upset with,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/donald-trump-mar-a-lago-nebraska-omaha-christopher-wray-c4321830fd11e845851d8036b0e0a3fe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Associated Press}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FBI\uc2  confirms the attack began this morning at their office in the city in southern Ohio:\par \par \uc2 enltrAt approximately 9 AM this morning an armed subject attempted to breach the Visitor Screening Facility at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/FBI?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #FBI}}}\uc2  Cincinnati. After an alarm and a response by \uc2 FBI\uc2  special agents, the subject fled north onto Interstate 71. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vFZHnpbM9L"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/vFZHnpbM9L}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 FBI Cincinnati (@FBICincinnati) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FBICincinnati/status/1557756091785744385?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/FBI?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #FBI}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Ohio State Highway Patrol\uc2 , and local law enforcement partners are on scene near Wilmington, OH trying to resolve this critical incident.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/SWDZTkrnhL"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/SWDZTkrnhL}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 FBI Cincinnati (@FBICincinnati) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FBICincinnati/status/1557756293682692098?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 NBC News reports the assailant fired a nail gun at people in the office, and appeared to have an assault rifle:\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KenDilanianNBC?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @KenDilanianNBC}}}\uc2  : "Two law enforcement sources briefed on the matter tell NBC News a man entered an \uc2 FBI\uc2  field office today in Cincinnati, Ohio and fired a nail gun at law enforcement personnel. The male then held up an AR-15 style rifle before fleeing in a vehicle."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ryan J. Reilly (@ryanjreilly) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ryanjreilly/status/1557760860218613760?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 According to Fox News, police pursued the person to a field outside the city and engaged in a gun battle:\par \par \uc2 enltrAn armed gunman attacked an \uc2 FBI\uc2  office in Cincinnati this morning.\par \par \uc2 The suspect fled the scene and is reportedly engaged in a shootout with law enforcement in a corn field outside the city. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/SrjPaO7Vkw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/SrjPaO7Vkw}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1557759487095840768?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Another trend in the economy is unionization drives in industries and businesses not accustomed to it \u8211\'20\'13 such as \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 . As {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/michael-sainato"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michael Sainato}}}\uc2  reports, workers at the coffee chain have staged dozens of strikes as the company tries to frustrate their efforts to organize:\par \par \uc2 Workers at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/starbucks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Starbucks}}}\uc2  have held over 55 different strikes in at least 17 states in the US in recent months over the company\u8217\'20\'19s aggressive opposition to a wave of unionization.\par \par \uc2 According to an estimate by Starbucks Workers United, the strikes have cost \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  over $375,000 in lost revenue. The union {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bing.com/ck/a?!&&p=f16540133022ace0JmltdHM9MTY1OTc0NDAwMCZpZ3VpZD0wODQyZGNhZC01ODRjLTYyYTEtMzk2NC1jZDg5NTk2NTYzOTAmaW5zaWQ9NTE4MA&ptn=3&hsh=3&fclid=0842dcad-584c-62a1-3964-cd8959656390&u=a1aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuY25iYy5jb20vMjAyMi8wNi8wMi9zdGFyYnVja3MtdW5pb24tY3JlYXRlcy0xLW1pbGxpb24tZnVuZC10by1jb3Zlci1sb3N0LXBheS1mb3Itc3RyaWtpbmctYmFyaXN0YXMuaHRtbA&ntb=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 created}}}\uc2  a $1m strike fund in June 2022 to support \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers through their strikes and several {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://secure.actblue.com/donate/starbucksworkersfund"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 relief funds}}}\uc2  have been established for strikes and to support workers who have lost their jobs.\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  employees have alleged over 75 workers have been fired in retaliation for union organizing this year, and hundreds of allegations of misconduct by \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  related to the union campaign are currently under review at the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2 , including claims of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/jul/13/starbucks-close-16-us-stores-concern-employee-safety"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shutting down stores}}}\uc2  to bust unions, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/jul/09/us-starbucks-workers-fired-union-organizing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 firing workers}}}\uc2  and intimidating and threatening workers from unionizing. \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  has denied all allegations.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/11/starbucks-union-drive-strikes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Starbucks workers hold strikes in at least 17 states amid union drive}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House is trying to keep the good economic vibes going, a day after data showed inflation potentially beginning to decline across the United States.\par \par \uc2 The chair of the Council of Economic Advisers \uc2 Cecilia Rouse{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/08/11/statement-from-cea-chair-cecilia-rouse-on-encouraging-economic-news/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has released a statement}}}\uc2  on \u8220\'20\'1Cencouraging economic news\u8221\'20\'1D, pointing to the inflation numbers, the decline in gas prices and new data released today showing wholesale prices declining against expectations in July.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are continuing to see encouraging economic developments, including strong job growth and lower energy prices,\u8221\'20\'1D Rouse said. She called on Congress to pass the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s marquee spending plan to address climate change and lower health care costs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile the news from this week is encouraging, we have more work to do to bring inflation down, without giving up the substantial economic and labor market gains of the past year. Congress should pass the Inflation Reduction Act as soon as possible, which will help our economy address some of its most important near-term and long-term challenges.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Drew Findling is an attorney who has represented rap artists like Gucci Mane, Migos and Cardi B, and even has his own hashtag: #BillionDollarLawyer. He also has tweeted critically of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , calling him in 2018 \u8220\'20\'1Cthe racist architect of fraudulent Trump University.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 None of that stopped the former president from hiring Findling to represent him in Georgia, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/08/11/us/trump-hires-billion-dollar-lawyer.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The New York Times reports}}}\uc2 . A prosecutor in the state is investigating efforts to overturn the results of the 2020 election there, and Findling will presumably be providing Trump with advice concerning that.\par \par \uc2 From the Times\u8217\'20\'19 report:\par \par \uc2 The investigation into postelection meddling is being led by Fani T. Willis, the district attorney of Fulton County, which encompasses much of Atlanta. To date, at least 17 people have been designated as targets who could face criminal charges. Mr. Trump is not among them, but evidence and testimony are still being taken in by a special grand jury, and Ms. Willis has said she is weighing a number of potential criminal charges, including racketeering and conspiracy.\par \par \uc2 In a hearing on Tuesday, a state judge told lawyers for Mr. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s personal attorney, \uc2 Rudolph W. Giuliani\uc2 , that their client needed to travel to Atlanta to testify next week. And in a hearing in federal court here Wednesday, lawyers for Senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  of South Carolina faced a skeptical reception from a judge on their efforts to quash a subpoena from Ms. Willis\u8217\'20\'19s office seeking the senator\u8217\'20\'19s testimony.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.22pm BST\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/2022-election-forecast/house/?cid=rrpromo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Based on the way things are looking today}}}\uc2 , voters probably won\u8217\'20\'19t elect enough Democrats for the party to hold on to the House of Representatives, meaning Republicans will gain control of the chamber \u8211\'20\'13 and its ability to carry out investigations.\par \par \uc2 The GOP will undoubtedly use that power to focus on issues of particular contention with the Biden administration, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/08/11/james-comer-biden-investigations-00050927"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico today has published}}}\uc2  a profile of the man who will play a key role in that charge. James Comer is the Kentucky Republican who is poised to chair the House Oversight Committee, and according to the article, plans to investigate the origins of Covid-19 and the business dealings of the president\u8217\'20\'19s son, \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In public, he\u8217\'20\'19s used the usual Republican attack line against the Democratic administration, telling a crowd in Kentucky, \u8220\'20\'1CMy committee will be the main obstacle between the Biden socialist agenda and the U.S. Constitution.\u8221\'20\'1D In private, he was more conciliatory, saying he wanted his investigations to appear credible (a tough but common ask of lawmakers).\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not going to be chasing some of these right-wing blogs and some of their conspiracy theories,\u8221\'20\'1D Comer said in the article. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ll look into anything, but we\u8217\'20\'19re not going to declare a probe or an investigation unless we have proof.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Elect democrats, and you\u8217\'20\'19ll like what you get: that\u8217\'20\'19s the message Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  had today for voters who seem increasingly likely to hand at least the House of Representatives to the Republicans in the November midterms.\par \par \uc2 While Congress is poised to approve {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/07/inflation-reduction-act-senate-democrats-pass"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a marquee spending package to lower health care costs and fight climate change}}}\uc2 , Democrats promised voters much more when \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  took office last year. But many of their priorities were left on the cutting room floor due to Republican opposition and the tortuous negotiations among their own party\u8217\'20\'19s members, particularly senators Joe Manchin and \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5BoxWx94t1Y"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In an interview}}}\uc2  on SiriusXM\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CJoe Madison The Black Eagle\u8221\'20\'1D, Schumer said that if he had bigger numbers in the Senate, Democrats would pass voting rights and other legislation that they failed to over the past year-and-a-half:\par \par \uc2 If I got two or three more seats, the bill we did now, as good as it is, would be nothing. We would get childcare. We would get paid family leave. We would get help for the elderly, home care. We would get the kind of things that, you know, Joe Manchin was against. So we couldn\u8217\'20\'19t do them in this bill.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 A tip from an informant preceded the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s search of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago estate this week, according to The Wall Street Journal. Victoria Bekiempis reports:\par \par \uc2 Federal investigators searched {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  Mar-a-Lago home in Palm Beach after an informant told them he might be storing classified records at his private club, the Wall Street Journal has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/fbi-quest-for-trump-documents-started-with-breezy-chats-tour-of-a-crowded-closet-11660169349?mod=hp_lead_pos2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The search on Monday reportedly came two months after federal law enforcement officials came to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/mar-a-lago"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mar-a-Lago}}}\uc2  to talk about boxes of government documents that were being stored there.\par \par \uc2 Federal authorities searched Trump\u8217\'20\'19s sprawling south {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida}}}\uc2  residence having obtained a warrant to seek classified and White House records that the US justice department thought Trump had kept unlawfully, two sources previously told the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/11/fbi-trump-classified-records-mar-a-lago"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FBI search of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago home followed tip classified records were there \u8211\'20\'13 report}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 As a lightning storm that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/04/lightning-strike-white-house-four-injured"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would kill three people}}}\uc2  right in front of the White House thundered outside, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was holding a meeting last week with historians who delivered the president a warning: both in the United States and abroad, democracy is in jeopardy.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/08/10/biden-us-historians-democracy-threat/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to The Washington Post}}}\uc2 , the Biden administration has previously held several such sit-downs with outside experts on the challenges it faces, including Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion plans for Ukraine. While the Post didn\u8217\'20\'19t get too many details about the exchanges in this latest meeting, they report that if Biden runs again in 2024, he will play up the \u8220\'20\'1Cbattle for the soul of the nation\u8221\'20\'1D theme that he used successfully in his 2020 run.\par \par \uc2 The meeting wasn\u8217\'20\'19t confined to the situation in the United States, but the Post reports that many of the participants pointed to governance calamities like the January 6 attack on the US Capitol and former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s attempts to overturn the 2020 election as major warning signs for the country going forward:\par \par \uc2 One person familiar with the exchange said the conversation was mostly a way for Biden to hear and think about the larger context in which his tenure is unfolding. He did not make any major pronouncements or discuss his plans for the future.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of the conversation was about the larger context of the contest between democratic values and institutions and the trends toward autocracy globally,\u8221\'20\'1D the person said.\par \par \uc2 Most of the experts in attendance have been outspoken in recent months about the threat they see to the American democratic project, after the attack on the Capitol on Jan. 6, the continued denial by some Republicans of the 2020 election results and the efforts of election deniers to seek state office.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Republicans are having a surprising amount of trouble passing the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans they have long promised voters if Roe v. Wade is overturned, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/maya-yang"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maya Yang}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 In the leadup to the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturning {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  and thus scrapping federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protection, Republican lawmakers across the country maintained an uncompromising rallying cry against abortions, vowing to implement a sweeping wave of restrictions in their states.\par \par \uc2 However, since the highest court in the US overturned the ruling, many Republican leaders and officials have become more hesitant \u8211\'20\'13 or have even gone silent \u8211\'20\'13 over the exact type of bans they promised to enact.\par \par \uc2 As {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  move towards an election season rife with internal disagreements within their own party and mixed public opinions on exceptions in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans such as instances of rape and incest, many rightwing lawmakers are finding it increasingly difficult to implement cohesive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/11/republicans-anti-abortion-policies-roe-v-wade-kansas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 After the fall of Roe, Republican pursuit of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  bans appears to falter}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 With control of Congress at stake, the White House said the president, vice president and cabinet officials are preparing to fan out across the country to sell voters on their healthcare, climate change and tax bill.\par \par \uc2 The bill, which passed the Senate over the weekend and is poised to pass the House on Friday, achieves only a fraction of Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 long-sought policy ambitions, but nevertheless amounts to a significant and once-unimaginable legislative victory. Biden, who is on vacation in South Carolina, is expected to sign the bill into law with great fanfare after it arrives on his desk.\par \par \uc2 In a new memo, White House communications director \uc2 Kate Bedingfield\uc2  and senior advisor Anita Dunn previewed their pitch to voters, which includes touting their efforts on health care, gun control and climate while accusing Republicans of siding with special interests and pushing a nationwide ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe president and congressional Democrats beat the special interests and delivered what was best for the American people,\u8221\'20\'1D the memo says. \u8220\'20\'1CEvery step of the way, congressional Republicans sided with the special interests \u8212\'20\'14 pushing an extreme MAGA agenda that costs families.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 economic policy bill caps an unusually productive stretch for Congress, which is better known for inaction than action. Amid a flurry of legislative victories, Biden is also breathing a sigh of relief as new economic indicators suggest inflation has cooled in July and painfully-high gas prices are easing.\par \par \uc2 Republicans are still poised to do well in the midterms, thanks to historic trends in which the president\u8217\'20\'19s party tends to lose ground. And the GOP is already hammering Democrats over their plan, which they say amounts to reckless spending at a time when Americans face decades-high inflation \u8211\'20\'13 a top concern for voters.\par \par \uc2 But the picture has brightened somewhat for Democrats as they attempt to seize on this burst of momentum.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the choice before the American people,\u8221\'20\'1D the memo states. \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Biden and congressional Democrats taking on special interests for you and your family or Congressional Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 extreme, MAGA agenda that serves the wealthiest, corporations and themselves.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  sat for a deposition as part of the New York attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s investigation into his business dealings, but as Edward Helmore and Hugo Lowell report, he didn\u8217\'20\'19t have much to say:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  declined to answer questions under oath on Wednesday in New York state\u8217\'20\'19s civil investigation into his business dealings, pleading the fifth two days after the \uc2 FBI\uc2  raided his Florida home in a criminal case, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/10/fbi-searched-trumps-home-seeking-classified-presidential-records-sources"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seeking classified documents}}}\uc2  taken from the White House.\par \par \uc2 The former US president\u8217\'20\'19s decision to exercise his fifth-amendment constitutional right against self-incrimination was delivered during a closed-door deposition in Manhattan, where the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York}}}\uc2  state attorney general, Letitia James, is examining the Trump family real estate empire.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI declined to answer the questions under the rights and privileges afforded to every citizen under the United States constitution,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said in a statement released after the questioning began.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/10/donald-trump-deposition-new-york-business-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump declines to answer questions in New York business investigation}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 What does the \uc2 FBI\uc2  want from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pennlive.com/news/2022/08/fbi-delivers-subpoenas-to-several-pa-republican-lawmakers-sources-say.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pennsylvania lawmakers its agents visited}}}\uc2  and handed subpoenas to this week? That has not been publicly released yet, but their visit makes clear federal investigators\u8217\'20\'19 probe into attempts to tamper with the 2020 election continues to sprawl.\par \par \uc2 In June, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/23/jeff-clark-home-raid-election-overturn-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 they raided the home}}}\uc2  of Jeffrey Clark, a former justice department official who was seen as friendly to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s false claims the 2020 election was rigged. Earlier this week, they {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/09/scott-perry-says-phone-seized-fbi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seized the phone}}}\uc2  of Scott Perry, a Republican congressman from Pennsylvania who was another backer of the lie that the election was stolen.\par \par \uc2 According to the Patriot-News, Perry said he was informed that he wasn\u8217\'20\'19t a target of whatever the \uc2 FBI\uc2  was investigating, and that he would cooperate. However both Clark and Perry\u8217\'20\'19s names have come up in recent hearings of the January 6 committee, particularly Clark\u8217\'20\'19s, after Trump mounted a failed effort to install him as the head of the justice department to allegedly disrupt the certification of the election results. Perry has meanwhile been pointed to as the person who connected Trump\u8217\'20\'19s confidantes in the White House with Clark.\par \par \uc2 The takeaway from all this is that while the relationship between the January 6 committee\u8217\'20\'19s investigation and the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s is murky, it\u8217\'20\'19s clear that they are interested in the same people.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 FBI\uc2  hands subpoenas to Pennsylvania Republicans while Trump keeps mum on Mar-a-Lago\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. The Harrisburg, Pennsylvania Patriot-News is reporting that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pennlive.com/news/2022/08/fbi-delivers-subpoenas-to-several-pa-republican-lawmakers-sources-say.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FBI delivered subpoenas or visited the offices}}}\uc2  of several Republican state lawmakers over the past two days. While it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear what the investigators wanted, the interaction came around the time agents {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/09/scott-perry-says-phone-seized-fbi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seized the phone}}}\uc2  of a Republican congressman from the state whose name has come up repeatedly as being involved in efforts to stop \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  from taking office following the 2020 election. Meanwhile, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has yet to say much more about the \uc2 FBI\uc2  search of Mar-a-Lago earlier this week \u8211\'20\'13 besides complaining that it happened at all.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is going on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Gas prices have dipped under $4 a gallon on average, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gasprices.aaa.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to AAA}}}\uc2 , reversing the spike that happened in recent months and badly damaged Biden\u8217\'20\'19s approval rating.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Many members of Congress are expected to attend the funeral for \uc2 Jackie Walorski\uc2 , who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/jackie-walorski-dead-indiana-congress-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was killed in a car accident last week}}}\uc2 , along with two of her staffers.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden is on vacation in South Carolina, with nothing on his agenda, though he\u8217\'20\'19s certainly keeping abreast of lawmakers\u8217\'20\'19 moves to pass his top legislative priority, the Inflation Reduction Act, which the House of Representatives may do tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220811ei8b001xi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
