\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: Trump pleads the fifth in New York business investigation\b0\par\par\uc2 Nicola Slawson \par \uc2 1,395 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 August 2022\par 10:42 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Former president declines to answer questions two days after the \uc2 FBI\uc2  raided his Florida home seeking classified documents. Plus, how the culture wars came for drag queens\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 Donald {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/10/donald-trump-deposition-new-york-business-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump declined to answer questions under oath}}}\uc2  yesterday in New York state\u8217\'20\'19s civil investigation into his business dealings, pleading the fifth two days after the \uc2 FBI\uc2  raided his Florida home in a separate criminal case, seeking classified documents taken from the White House.\par \par \uc2 The former US president\u8217\'20\'19s decision to exercise his fifth amendment constitutional right against self-incrimination was delivered during a closed-door deposition in Manhattan, where the New York state attorney general, Letitia James, is examining the Trump family real estate empire.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI declined to answer the questions under the rights and privileges afforded to every citizen under the United States constitution,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said in a statement released after the questioning began.\par \par \uc2 The deposition, which took place in lower Manhattan, appears to have lasted roughly four hours. The former president departed 28 Liberty Street at 3.20pm in a black Secret Service SUV and peered out the rear window as his motorcade crawled out of an underground garage and past onlookers.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Did Trump say anything about the case?\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/live/2022/08/10/nyregion/trump-testimony-investigation-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to the New York Times}}}\uc2 , Trump accused the attorney general of having \u8220\'20\'1Copenly campaigned on a policy of destroying me\u8221\'20\'1D. Beyond that, from 9.30am to about 3pm, the former president had repeated the words \u8220\'20\'1Csame answer\u8221\'20\'1D to every question about \u8220\'20\'1Cvaluations and golf clubs and all that stuff\u8221\'20\'1D, his lawyer said.\par \par \uc2 After the fall of Roe, Republican pursuit of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans appears to falter\par \par \uc2 In the lead-up to the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturning Roe v Wade and thus scrapping federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protection, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/11/republicans-anti-abortion-policies-roe-v-wade-kansas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican lawmakers across the country maintained an uncompromising rallying cry against abortions}}}\uc2 , vowing to implement a sweeping wave of restrictions in their states.\par \par \uc2 However, since the highest court in the US overturned the ruling, many Republican leaders and officials have become more hesitant \u8211\'20\'13 or have even gone silent \u8211\'20\'13 over the exact type of bans they promised to enact.\par \par \uc2 As Republicans move towards an election season rife with internal disagreements within their own party and mixed public opinions on exceptions in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans such as instances of rape and incest, many rightwing lawmakers are finding it increasingly difficult to implement cohesive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies.\par \par \uc2 The phenomenon has been starkly illustrated by Kansas\u8217\'20\'19s referendum last week, where the usually reliably Republican state voted to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections in its state constitution, providing an unexpected boost from red state America to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights movement.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What do most Americans think about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights? According to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/fact-tank/2022/07/15/key-facts-about-the-abortion-debate-in-america/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 survey}}}\uc2  conducted between 27 June and 4 July by the \uc2 Pew Research\uc2  center, a majority of the public disapproves of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn Roe: 57% of adults disapprove of the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision.\par \par \uc2 China overtakes the US in scientific research output\par \par \uc2 China has overtaken the US as the world leader in scientific research output and \u8220\'20\'1Chigh impact\u8221\'20\'1D studies, according to a report published by Japan\u8217\'20\'19s science and technology ministry.\par \par \uc2 The report, published by Japan\u8217\'20\'19s National Institute of Science and Technology Policy (NISTP) on Tuesday, has found that China now publishes the highest number of scientific research papers yearly, followed by the US and Germany.\par \par \uc2 The figures were based on yearly averages between 2018 and 2020, and drawn from data compiled by the analytics firm \uc2 Clarivate\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Japanese NISTP report also found that Chinese research comprised 27.2% of the world\u8217\'20\'19s top 1% most frequently cited papers. The number of citations a research paper receives is a commonly used metric in academia. The more times a study is cited in subsequent papers by other researchers, the greater its \u8220\'20\'1Ccitation impact\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The US accounted for 24.9% of the top 1% most highly cited research studies, while UK research was third at 5.5%.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What is the US going to do to improve? The report was published on the day US president, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , signed the Chips and Science Act, legislation that would authorize $200bn in research funding over 10 years to make US scientific research more competitive with China\u8217\'20\'19s.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 North Korea has declared a \u8220\'20\'1Cshining victory\u8221\'20\'1D in its battle with Covid-19, amid suggestions from Kim Jong-un\u8217\'20\'19s sister that the country\u8217\'20\'19s leader had at one point been \u8220\'20\'1Cseriously ill\u8221\'20\'1D with the virus. His influential sister Kim Yo-jong said he had been among the tens of millions of North Koreans to have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/aug/11/kim-jong-un-fell-seriously-ill-during-north-korea-covid-crisis-his-sister-says"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 come down with a \u8220\'20\'1Cfever\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A 23-year-old man has been charged and remanded in custody after an American tourist was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/aug/10/man-charged-after-american-tourist-raped-in-paris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raped in a public toilet}}}\uc2  in the centre of Paris, in a case that has caused shock in the busy riverside area that was considered safe. The woman, 27, was found by her partner and immediately taken to a Paris hospital.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has said that the US knows \u8220\'20\'1Cwith certainty\u8221\'20\'1D that the Syrian government is holding Austin Tice \u8211\'20\'13 an American journalist who has been missing for a decade \u8211\'20\'13 and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/10/biden-syria-missing-journalist-austin-tice"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called on Damascus to release him}}}\uc2 . Biden said he is \u8220\'20\'1Ccalling on Syria to end this and help us bring him home\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kobe Bryant\u8217\'20\'19s widow is seeking compensation for snapshots taken of the \uc2 NBA\uc2  star\u8217\'20\'19s body after a crash that also killed her daughter. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/10/kobe-bryant-crash-photos-lawsuit-vanessa-bryant-los-angeles"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 law prompted by the crash}}}\uc2  makes it a crime for first responders to take unauthorized photos of deceased people at the scene of an accident or crime.\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: Record Death Valley flooding \u8216\'20\'18a once-in-1,000-year event\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Recent severe rains in California\u8217\'20\'19s Death Valley that flushed debris across roads, damaged infrastructure and carried away cars are being described by meteorologists and park officials as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/10/death-valley-floods-climate-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a once-in 1,000-year event}}}\uc2 . The arid area was pelted with roughly an inch and a half of rain on Friday, near the park\u8217\'20\'19s rainfall record for a single day. The storm poured a volume of water equal to roughly 75% of the average annual total in just three hours, according to experts at \uc2 Nasa\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Earth Observatory.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Getting harder and hotter\u8217\'20\'19: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/10/phoenix-fire-department-emergency-calls-heatwave"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Phoenix fire crews race to save lives in America\u8217\'20\'19s hottest city}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this:\par \par \uc2 how the culture wars hijacked Drag Queen Story Hour\par \par \uc2 Shows featuring drag queens reading to young children have proven increasingly popular in the UK \u8211\'20\'13 but, as in the US, they are also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2022/aug/11/im-just-trying-to-make-the-world-a-little-brighter-how-the-culture-wars-hijacked-drag-queen-story-hour"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attracting angry protests}}}\uc2 . How have we reached a place where these joyful events are seen as a threat to infants? Seb Samuel AKA Ada H Dee \u8211\'20\'13 the first drag queen in the UK to read stories to children in libraries \u8211\'20\'13 believes it is a knock-on effect of the normalisation of anti-LGBTQ+ attitudes in the wider world.\par \par \uc2 Climate check:\par \par \uc2 climate crisis fueling barrage, scientists say\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CClimate change is increasing the intensity and frequency of flooding and it will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/11/america-summer-floods-rainfall-climate-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 likely get worse with further warming}}}\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Andreas Prein, an expert in climate extremes at the National Center for Atmospheric Research, said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are also seeing these repeated storms hit the same area, like Kentucky, again and again in a short period of time, which isn\u8217\'20\'19t well understood. But we know the hot temperatures, like the eastern US has just had, has helped build the water in the atmosphere.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: Domino\u8217\'20\'19s retreats from Italy having failed to conquer the home of pizza\par \par \uc2 Domino\u8217\'20\'19s Pizza has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/aug/10/dominos-retreats-from-italy-having-failed-to-conquer-the-home-of-the-pizza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pulled out of the Italian market}}}\uc2  after failing in its mission to conquer the home of pizza. The company set out with ambitious plans of opening 880 outlets across the country by 2030, hopeful that it could win over Italian customers with pizza topped with pineapple. It got as far as opening 29 branches, all of which have now been closed. Domino\u8217\'20\'19s first foray into Italy was in Milan in 2015, before venturing to other cities. It did not, however, make it to Naples, the southern city where pizza margherita was created.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220811ei8b001jr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
