\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Nebraska teen and her mother charged for aborting and burying fetus\b0\par\par\uc2 Gloria Oladipo \par \uc2 660 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 August 2022\par 18:36 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The pair are facing several felony charges after the teen used \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to end the pregnancy at six months\par \par \uc2 A Nebraska mother and her daughter are facing felony charges after the mother allegedly helped her teenager abort her pregnancy, burn the fetus and then bury it.\par \par \uc2 Jessica Burgess, 41, is facing five criminal charges, including three felonies, after investigators accused her of helping her 17-year-old daughter obtain \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to end her pregnancy, as well as burning and interring the fetus.\par \par \uc2 Her daughter, who is being tried as an adult, is facing three charges, including one felony.\par \par \uc2 The alleged \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  happened before the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  in June overturned its ruling in Roe v Wade, which established federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights nearly 50 years earlier. Nonetheless, in addition to being charged with essentially failing to properly report a death, authorities are accusing Burgess of facilitating an illegal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Both women are awaiting trial in Madison county, Nebraska, district court while out on bond, and they have pleaded not guilty to all charges.\par \par \uc2 A 22-year-old man, accused of helping the two women bury the fetus, pleaded no contest to a misdemeanor charge and will be sentenced at a later date, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://journalstar.com/news/state-and-regional/nebraska/norfolk-mother-and-daughter-accused-of-illegal-abortion-burning-and-burying-body/article_ff99fd49-a710-5ec3-8d51-5aced3001c71.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  the Lincoln Journal Star}}}\uc2  reports.\par \par \uc2 According to a search warrant affidavit, the Norfolk, Nebraska, police department launched an investigation in April after receiving information that Burgess\u8217\'20\'19s daughter had miscarried and buried the fetus.\par \par \uc2 A detective in the department then obtained the daughter\u8217\'20\'19s health records, determining that she was nearly six months pregnant at the time of the miscarriage and expected to deliver in early July.\par \par \uc2 It is unclear how the detective obtained the teen\u8217\'20\'19s medical records or exactly how the tip was sent to police.\par \par \uc2 During an interview, Burgess and her daughter later told police that the teen had delivered a stillborn baby, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.siouxlandproud.com/news/local-news/2-adults-and-1-teen-concealed-death-of-baby-norfolk-police-says/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 confirmed by a 30 April autopsy}}}\uc2  done on the fetus, and that the two buried the fetus with the help of the 22-year-old man.\par \par \uc2 The two showed the detective where the fetus was buried on 29 April, with the 22-year-old man telling police that the two women tried to burn the fetus before it had been buried.\par \par \uc2 Police later exhumed the fetus and found signs of \u8220\'20\'1Cthermal wounds\u8221\'20\'1D, the Journal Star reported.\par \par \uc2 In June, Burgess and her daughter were both charged with removing, abandoning or concealing a dead human body \u8211\'20\'13 a felony \u8211\'20\'13 as well as concealing another person\u8217\'20\'19s death and false reporting, which are misdemeanor charges.\par \par \uc2 The pair were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.siouxlandproud.com/news/local-news/2-adults-and-1-teen-concealed-death-of-baby-norfolk-police-says/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 originally only given citations}}}\uc2  for concealing another person\u8217\'20\'19s death and false reporting.\par \par \uc2 But afterwards, investigators issued a search warrant to search Burgess and her daughter\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Facebook\uc2  accounts.\par \par \uc2 There, detectives found messages that suggested Burgess had bought \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills for her daughter and instructed her on how to take them.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[The daughter] talks about how she can\u8217\'20\'19t wait to get the \u8216\'20\'18thing\u8217\'20\'19 out of her body and reaffirms with [Jessica Burgess] that they will burn the evidence afterwards,\u8221\'20\'1D the detective wrote in court records, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://siouxlandnews.com/news/local/three-norfolk-residents-celeste-burgess-jessica-burgess-tanner-barnhill-charged-with-burning-burying-fetus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to Siouxland News}}}\uc2 , a local news affiliate.\par \par \uc2 Authorities in July charged Burgess with additional felonies for performing or attempting an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a pregnancy that is past 20 weeks and for performing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a non-licensed doctor.\par \par \uc2 Both women were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.siouxlandproud.com/news/local-news/2-adults-and-1-teen-concealed-death-of-baby-norfolk-police-says/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released from jail on bond}}}\uc2  as of Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The lawyer for Jessica Burgess declined to comment, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://journalstar.com/news/state-and-regional/nebraska/norfolk-mother-and-daughter-accused-of-illegal-abortion-burning-and-burying-body/article_ff99fd49-a710-5ec3-8d51-5aced3001c71.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Journal Star}}}\uc2  reported. An attorney representing her daughter could not be reached.\par \par \uc2 After June\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court ruling, abortions are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2022/jun/28/tracking-where-abortion-laws-stand-in-every-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banned in Nebraska after 22 weeks}}}\uc2 , although {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/25/abortion-ban-options-travel-pills-financial-legal-help"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  self-managed abortions}}}\uc2  are not prohibited.\par \par \uc2 Nebraska\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Pete Ricketts\uc2 , on Monday said that he would not call a special legislative session to further restrict access to abortions because Republican lawmakers in the state do not have enough votes to pass a 12-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/nebraska-republicans-lack-votes-pass-12-week-abortion-ban-2022-08-08/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Reuters}}}\uc2  reported.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220809ei89002s4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
