\par\par \uc2 Global development\par \b \uc2 UK government\uc2  honoured anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  figure before editing women\u8217\'20\'19s rights statement\b0\par\par\uc2 Lizzy Davies \par \uc2 1,347 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 August 2022\par 09:23 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Former US envoy given award at conference now engulfed in row over changes to reproductive rights pledges, while participant list revealed to have included members of group accused of hate speech\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 British government\uc2  presented a vehemently anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  former US envoy with an award for his services to freedom of religion just days before watering down {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/freedom-of-religion-or-belief-and-gender-equality-statement-at-the-international-ministerial-conference-2022/statement-on-freedom-of-religion-or-belief-and-gender-equality"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a statement}}}\uc2  on gender equality to remove commitments to reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 Sam Brownback\uc2 , a former governor of Kansas who targeted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights while in office and then became Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s ambassador-at-large for international religious freedom, was given the award during the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gov.uk/government/topical-events/international-ministerial-conference-on-freedom-of-religion-or-belief-london-2022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 international ministerial conference}}}\uc2  for freedom of religion or belief (FoRB) held in London last month.\par \par \uc2 Organised by the \uc2 Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office\uc2  (FCDO) and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gov.uk/government/speeches/foreign-secretarys-remarks-at-the-freedom-of-religion-or-belief-conference"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opened by}}}\uc2  the Tory leadership candidate Liz Truss, the gathering has since become engulfed in controversy after a statement signed by more than 20 countries was quietly removed from the FCDO website and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2022/jul/22/european-countries-pressurise-uk-over-removal-of-abortion-commitments-liz-truss"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 significantly edited}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It has now emerged that a number of participants to the conference, which \uc2 Fiona Bruce\uc2 , the prime minister\u8217\'20\'19s special envoy for religious freedom or belief, was involved in organising, are known for their strong anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  views.\par \par \uc2 Three, including one speaker, were from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://adfinternational.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ADF International}}}\uc2 , the global wing of a US legal advocacy organisation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.splcenter.org/fighting-hate/extremist-files/group/alliance-defending-freedom"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 considered a hate group}}}\uc2  by the \uc2 Southern Poverty Law Centre (SPLC)\uc2 , which monitors extremist groups in the US.\par \par \uc2 Founded by leaders of the Christian right, the \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2  (ADF) has long opposed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It writes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://adflegal.org/issues/sanctity-of-life/abortions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on its website}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CIn 2022, the pro-life movement achieved what was thought impossible by many: the overturning of Roe v Wade. But there\u8217\'20\'19s more work to be done.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Other participants were from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://religiousfreedominstitute.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Religious Freedom Institute}}}\uc2  (RFI), a rightwing thinktank based in Washington DC, which, alongside the ADF, is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://religiousfreedominstitute.org/medical-conscience-rights-initiative/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pushing for more laws}}}\uc2  protecting anti-choice medics from performing \u8220\'20\'1Cprocedures in violation of their conscience\u8221\'20\'1D, from \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to gender transition surgery.\par \par \uc2 J\u225\'00\'E1n Figel, a former EU special envoy for FoRB, was among the speakers. Figel\u8217\'20\'19s mandate was not renewed in 2020 after a group of pro-choice MEPs complained he had \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://lanuovabq.it/storage/docs/eu-special-envoy-on-forb-letter-to-vice-president_0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 undermined [the mandate\u8217\'20\'19s] credibility}}}\uc2  \u8230\'20\'26 by showing highly problematic acquaintances with organisations opposing women\u8217\'20\'19s sexual rights and LGBTI people\u8217\'20\'19s rights.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Figel said the MEPs\u8217\'20\'19 criticism had been rooted in \u8220\'20\'1Cfalse arguments... based on lies\u8221\'20\'1D, and added that he had nothing to do with the statement.\par \par \uc2 It is understood that Brownback, who received warm applause at the London conference, was given the award by the \uc2 UK government\uc2  in conjunction with the Dutch special envoy for FoRB, Jos Douma, in recognition of their work on FoRB around the world.\par \par \uc2 While in office, Brownback signed a number of pieces of anti-choice legislation. Last week, he bemoaned the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/kansas-abortion-vote-state-constitution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decisive victory}}}\uc2  of pro-choice campaigners in a Kansas referendum on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SamuelBrownback/status/1554820446293557252?s=20&t=M4c6FizSFFzVH4dGI095iw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 adding}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CWe fight on defending all life, mother and child, from beginning to end.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 According to one participant at the London conference, who requested anonymity: \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 UK government\uc2  says it advocates \u8216\'20\'18freedom of religion or belief for all\u8217\'20\'19. But some of those featured and celebrated at the ministerial don\u8217\'20\'19t support this. What they do instead is use their \u8216\'20\'18religious freedom\u8217\'20\'19 as an excuse to trample the rights and freedoms of others. People like \uc2 Sam Brownback\uc2  and the ADF, who seek to take away others\u8217\'20\'19 freedom of choice in this way, should be challenged, not celebrated.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The conference is an annual gathering that began in the US during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidency. This year it was held on 5-6 July.\par \par \uc2 Its agenda was centred on how to \u8220\'20\'1Cprotect and promote freedom of religion or belief internationally\u8221\'20\'1D, with topics ranging from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2021/jun/10/china-uyghur-xinjiang-dystopian-hellscape-says-amnesty-international-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 persecution of Uyghur Muslims}}}\uc2  in the Xinjiang region of China to the terrorist attacks of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2020/jul/09/mama-boko-haram-nigeria-maiduguri"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Boko Haram}}}\uc2  in Nigeria discussed by academics, analysts, politicians and faith leaders, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.archbishopofcanterbury.org/news/news-and-statements/archbishop-addresses-conference-freedom-religion-or-belief"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 including}}}\uc2  the archbishop of Canterbury, Justin Welby.\par \par \uc2 But its aftermath has been controversial, since it emerged that its statement on FoRB and gender equality had been edited to remove commitments to \u8220\'20\'1Csexual and reproductive health and rights\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cbodily autonomy\u8221\'20\'1D. The FCDO initially said it had made the changes to focus on key FoRB issues and to achieve a broader consensus of signatories.\par \par \uc2 Tariq Ahmad, a Foreign Office minister and former FoRB special envoy, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://questions-statements.parliament.uk/written-questions/detail/2022-07-21/hl1992"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  last week the statement had been edited to become \u8220\'20\'1Cmore inclusive of all perspectives and views\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cto allow for a constructive exchange of views on all issues\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 However, the watering-down of the statement, which had been painstakingly worked on and signed by more than 20 countries, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2022/jul/28/uk-in-diplomatic-standoff-over-deletion-of-abortion-rights-from-gender-statement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 provoked anger}}}\uc2  in a number of governments, many of which are refusing to sign the modified version. It currently has eight signatories, including Malta, where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/19/the-fight-for-abortion-in-malta"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  is illegal}}}\uc2 , and the UK.\par \par \uc2 It is understood that the pushback on the gender equality statement began the day after the conference, at a \u8220\'20\'1Cnext steps\u8221\'20\'1D meeting at Lancaster House, convened by Bruce. Among those present were Jim Shannon, of the Democratic Unionist party, and David Alton, a crossbench peer, who were also conference speakers.\par \par \uc2 After the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/jun/26/the-guardian-view-on-overturning-roe-v-wade-anti-abortionists-reign-supreme"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturning of Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , Lord Alton told the Universe Catholic Weekly he hoped the decision {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://universecatholicweekly.co.uk/roe-v-wade-overturned/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would lead to \u8220\'20\'1Cnew laws and resources\u8221\'20\'1D in the UK}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Rachael Clarke, chief of staff at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bpas.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 British Pregnancy Advisory Service}}}\uc2 , said the vast majority of British people saw through the \u8220\'20\'1Cfiction\u8221\'20\'1D that there was significant opposition in the UK to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. But words mattered, she added, which was why there was concern over the conference statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think what we\u8217\'20\'19ve really seen when it comes to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights is the power of words and the power of the direction that governments are moving [in] \u8230\'20\'26 I think what we really are concerned about seeing is any indication from this government or the next government that they are valuing women\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive rights as less than where they are currently,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Clarke added that, with Bruce {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gov.uk/government/people/fiona-bruce"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as special envoy}}}\uc2 , it would have been hard for the government to put out a statement on freedom of belief that was not inclusive of \u8220\'20\'1Cincredibly anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  views\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1C[Bruce] is the most anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  MP in the House of Commons.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for Brownback said he had no involvement in drafting the conference statement or in organising the event. Brownback was \u8220\'20\'1Cproud to be pro-life\u8221\'20\'1D, a stance that is \u8220\'20\'1Cimmaterial to his support for freedom of religion or belief\u8221\'20\'1D, he added.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmbassador Brownback has not tried to connect his support of unborn human life to the issue of religious freedom \u8230\'20\'26 Ambassador Brownback believes that anyone can support FoRB regardless of their position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . At a time when people are being killed and persecuted for what they choose to believe, Ambassador Brownback believes that the FoRB movement best moves forward by focusing on FoRB and not diverging into non-FoRB issues.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The ADF denies the accusation it espouses hate, accusing the SPLC of besmirching \u8220\'20\'1Chuge swaths of well-respected, mainstream, conservative America\u8221\'20\'1D in that categorisation of its beliefs.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson said: \u8220\'20\'1CAs the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest organisation committed to protecting religious freedom, ADF International were proud to take part in the ministerial. Our current projects include {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://adfinternational.org/maira/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defending}}}\uc2  girls in south-east Asia who have been abducted, forcibly married, and \u8216\'20\'18converted\u8217\'20\'19 from their faith; {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://adfinternational.org/bak/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 challenging}}}\uc2  the Russian authorities for prohibiting church communities from gathering to worship; and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://adfinternational.org/shagufta-and-shafqat-pakistan/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supporting}}}\uc2  those on death row for \u8216\'20\'18blasphemy\u8217\'20\'19 in Pakistan to escape to safety in Europe. We believe in the equality and dignity of all people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Nathan Berkeley, communications director of the RFI, said the thinktank worked to advance religious freedom throughout the globe and to defend those of all faiths who were persecuted.\par \par \uc2 An FCDO spokesperson said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe invited experts and representatives from a wide range of different fields and beliefs to the conference in the spirit of fostering positive discussion and collaboration on issues of freedom of religion or belief.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bruce, Alton and Shannon did not respond to requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220809ei89001e3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
