\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Peter Meijer, Republican who voted to impeach Trump, loses Michigan seat\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Gambino in Washington and Martin Pengelly in New York \par \uc2 1,010 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 August 2022\par 09:59 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Trump-backed challenger John Gibbs triumphs, while Democrats hopeful Kansas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  vote will energize voters in November\par \par \uc2 On one of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/02/primaries-abortion-trump-arizona-missouri-michigan-kansas-washington-races"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  most consequential nights}}}\uc2  of the US primary season, amplifiers of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s stolen-election myth {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/republican-candidates-2020-election-deniers-win-key-primaries"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won}}}\uc2  in Arizona and Michigan \u8211\'20\'13 in the latter state defeating a Republican who voted for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s impeachment \u8211\'20\'13 while voters in Kansas decisively rejected an attempt to remove \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections from the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 With fewer than 100 days left before the November midterm elections, the results confirmed Trump\u8217\'20\'19s grip on Republican voters and advanced his efforts to purge critics and elevate loyalist standard-bearers.\par \par \uc2 The verdicts rendered on Tuesday night are likely to have major implications for both parties.\par \par \uc2 Democrats face a difficult election cycle, hampered by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s low approval ratings and widespread dissatisfaction with leadership in Washington in the face of economic problems. Historically, the opposition party makes gains in the first midterms of any presidency, often by framing the election as a referendum on the president.\par \par \uc2 With narrow majorities in Congress, Democrats cannot afford to lose any seats in the Senate and only a handful in the House. But party leaders were hopeful on Tuesday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights verdict in Kansas might energize voters and boost Democrats in close contests to come.\par \par \uc2 Another midterm strategy employed by Democrats \u8211\'20\'13 boosting far-right candidates in Republican primaries in the hope of facing weaker opponents in November \u8211\'20\'13 met with success, despite bipartisan warnings that the approach could backfire, with dangerous consequences for US democracy.\par \par \uc2 In a congressional primary in Michigan, John Gibbs defeated Peter Meijer, the Republican incumbent who was one of 10 House Republicans to vote to impeach Trump over the Capitol attack, after Democrats ran ads highlighting Gibbs\u8217\'20\'19s pro-Trump credentials.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, \uc2 Meijer\uc2  said: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m proud to have remained true to my principles, even when doing so came at a significant political cost.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But he published angrier words on Monday, assailing Democrats who spent heavily in support of Gibbs.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.commonsense.news/p/why-the-democrats-are-funding-my"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  an online essay}}}\uc2 , Meijer wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CThe Democrats are justifying this political jiu-jitsu by making the argument that politics is a tough business. I don\u8217\'20\'19t disagree.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut that toughness is bound by certain moral limits: those who participated in the attack on the Capitol, for example, clearly fall outside those limits. But over the course of the midterms, Democrats seem to have forgotten just where those limits lie.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Meijer\uc2  was the second Republican who voted to impeach to lose a primary contest. Four have opted to retire rather than to seek re-election. Two others were on the ballot on Tuesday in Washington state. \uc2 Jaime Herrera Beutler\uc2  and \uc2 Dan Newhouse\uc2  were in close races against Trump-backed challengers which had yet to be called.\par \par \uc2 So far, only one Republican who voted to impeach Trump, David Valadao of California, has survived, with a narrow victory in California.\par \par \uc2 Michigan also saw a Trump-backed candidate win the Republican nomination for governor. Tudor Dixon, a conservative media personality, will face the Democratic governor, \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 , in November.\par \par \uc2 In an incumbent-on-incumbent Democratic primary for a newly redrawn Michigan House district, Haley Stevens, a moderate backed by the political arm of the \uc2 American Israel Public Affairs Committee\uc2 , defeated \uc2 Andy Levin\uc2 , a progressive from a prominent political family. Elsewhere, progressive members of \u8220\'20\'1Cthe Squad\u8221\'20\'1D, \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2  in Michigan and \uc2 Cori Bush\uc2  in Missouri, beat back moderate challengers.\par \par \uc2 In Arizona, a battleground state that became the epicenter of election denialism in the wake of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 victory, the Trump-endorsed \uc2 Blake Masters\uc2  won a crowded Republican primary to face Mark Kelly, the Democratic incumbent, in a contest that could determine control of the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the race for Arizona secretary of state, a post that oversees elections, Republicans nominated Mark Finchem, a self-identified member of the far-right Oath Keepers militia who has amplified false claims about the 2020 election and was backed by Trump.\par \par \uc2 The Republican primary for governor was too close to call but by Wednesday Kari Lake, a former TV anchor backed by Trump, was narrowly leading Karrin Taylor Robson, backed by the former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s quest for retribution against Republicans who crossed him gained a win when \uc2 Rusty Bowers\uc2 , Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s Republican House speaker, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/22/arizona-rusty-bowers-jan-6-trump-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rose to prominence}}}\uc2  when he testified to the House committee investigating the January 6 insurrection, lost his bid for a state Senate seat to David Farnsworth, who had Trump\u8217\'20\'19s support.\par \par \uc2 In Missouri, where Trump urged voters to choose \u8220\'20\'1CEric\u8221\'20\'1D without specifying which in a Senate primary contest with three Erics, Republican leaders were relieved it was \uc2 Eric Schmitt\uc2 , the attorney general, who emerged victorious.\par \par \uc2 Eric Greitens\uc2 , the scandal-plagued former governor who resigned in 2018 and was attempting a political comeback, finished third. Schmitt will now face Trudy Busch Valentine, a deep-pocketed beer heiress who Democrats nominated over the more populist Lucas Kunce.\par \par \uc2 Though Trump\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement record is mixed, his string of victories on Tuesday night underscored conservatives\u8217\'20\'19 enduring allegiance to the former president despite a stream of damaging revelations about his efforts to overturn the election and his conduct during the deadly assault on the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 Perhaps the most closely watched vote on Tuesday wasn\u8217\'20\'19t an election, but a referendum. In the first test of the potency of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as electoral issue in the post-Roe era, voters in Kansas {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/kansas-abortion-rights-referendum-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 resoundingly rejected }}}\uc2  an amendment that would have erased the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 The decisive vote in a state that voted overwhelmingly for Trump in 2020 is the first major electoral victory for supporters of reproductive rights since the the supreme court invalidated the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June.\par \par \uc2 It also serves as a warning to Republicans who have sought to downplay the significance of the issue in an election year otherwise dominated by inflation and economic woes.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220808ei88002yh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
