\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US jury finds in favor of pharmacist who denied woman morning-after pill\b0\par\par\uc2 Samira Asma-Sadeque \par \uc2 490 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 August 2022\par 13:08 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Rights groups express concern after Minnesota jury gives verdict that Andrea Anderson\u8217\'20\'19s rights were not violated by pharmacy\u8217\'20\'19s denial\par \par \uc2 A Minnesota jury found that a pharmacy did not discriminate against a woman when it refused to give her the morning-after pill.\par \par \uc2 The pharmacist gave \u8220\'20\'1Cbelief\u8221\'20\'1D as the reason for refusing to fill the prescription for emergency contraception. Although the jury decided that the woman\u8217\'20\'19s rights had not been violated, it did say that the emotional damage caused by the decision amounted to $25,000.\par \par \uc2 Gender Justice, a legal advocacy non-profit, filed the lawsuit on behalf of Andrea Anderson in 2019, though the case did not reach trial until Monday.\par \par \uc2 Anderson was denied morning-after contraceptive bills by numerous pharmacies, and said she would have to travel 100 miles total to get a pill.\par \par \uc2 In a statement released by Gender Justice, she expressed concern about the precedent the jury\u8217\'20\'19s decision sets and the message it gives to other women seeking emergency contraception.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat if they accept the pharmacist\u8217\'20\'19s decision and don\u8217\'20\'19t realize that this behavior is wrong? What if they have no other choice?\u8221\'20\'1D Anderson said. \u8220\'20\'1CNot everyone has the means or ability to drive hundreds of miles to get a prescription filled.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnfortunately, highly personal healthcare decisions such as whether to get pregnant and grow your family are heavily politicized,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jess Braverman, legal director at Gender Justice. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is illegal sex discrimination in the state of Minnesota for a pharmacist to refuse to dispense emergency contraception without, at the very least, ensuring a patient can get their prescription without extra delay and cost to them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The verdict comes on the heels of a June decision by the supreme court to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturn the constitutional right}}}\uc2  to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  initially protected in the case of Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 Minnesota still allows abortions legally after the overturning of Roe, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reproductiverights.org/maps/state/minnesota/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 permanently blocked}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cnumerous medically unnecessary restrictions\u8221\'20\'1D in July.\par \par \uc2 Friday\u8217\'20\'19s jury decision coincided with Indiana {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/aug/06/indiana-assembly-passes-anti-abortion-bill-sends-it-to-governor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 imposing a near-total ban on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , the first state to do so following the overturning of Roe.\par \par \uc2 Following the passing of that law, the pharmaceutical company \uc2 Eli Lilly{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/adamwren/status/1555894094244741120?ref_src=twsrc%5Egoogle%7Ctwcamp%5Eserp%7Ctwgr%5Etweet"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  it would be \u8220\'20\'1Cforced to plan for more employment growth outside our home state\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are concerned that this law will hinder Lilly\u8217\'20\'19s \u8211\'20\'13 and Indiana\u8217\'20\'19s \u8211\'20\'13 ability to attract diverse scientific, engineering and business talent from around the world,\u8221\'20\'1D it said.\par \par \uc2 Some traditionally conservative states such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-us-supreme-court-health-west-virginia-charleston-792346e76179351718fcd771b7d8e1ca"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 West Virginia}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.yahoo.com/south-carolina-republicans-pause-abortion-130029332.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 South Carolina}}}\uc2  continue to debate how to change their laws on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Last week, in the nation\u8217\'20\'19s first referendum on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the supreme court decision, voters in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/democrats-abortion-rights-victory-kansas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kansas rejected}}}\uc2  a change to their state constitution protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 The surprise victory was celebrated as a testament to the desire for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights nationwide, even in Republican-leaning states.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220806ei86001xh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
