\par\par \uc2 Culture\par \b \uc2 Seth Meyers on Kansas  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  vote: \u8216\'20\'18A promising sign of progress\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff \par \uc2 860 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 August 2022\par 15:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Late-night hosts discuss Kansas\u8217\'20\'19s overwhelming vote to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and Alex Jones\u8217\'20\'19s inept defamation trial lawyer\par \par \uc2 Seth Meyers\par \par \uc2 Seth Meyers celebrated a victory for reproductive rights in the US a month after the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade, as voters in Kansas {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/kansas-abortion-vote-state-constitution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overwhelmingly decided}}}\uc2  to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections in its state constitution. The defeat of a referendum to remove said rights from the constitution, 59% to 41%, was \u8220\'20\'1Cespecially encouraging\u8221\'20\'1D, said Meyers on Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s Late Night, \u8220\'20\'1Cgiven that anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists used every shady tactic they could think of and still lost\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The wording of the referendum was \u8220\'20\'1Cintentionally confusing\u8221\'20\'1D, Meyers explained, reading the vague paragraph out loud. \u8220\'20\'1CWow, I can\u8217\'20\'19t believe they hired the same guy who wrote the iTunes user agreement,\u8221\'20\'1D he joked. \u8220\'20\'1CI hope voters were given the options yes, no, and da fuck?\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat reads like the intro to a college paper you start writing at 3am the night before it\u8217\'20\'19s due.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Moreover, \u8220\'20\'1CKansas voters saw through the bullshit and overwhelmingly backed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights,\u8221\'20\'1D despite misleading text messages from a GOP group. The night before the election, the group sent voters a text that said: \u8220\'20\'1CWomen in KS are losing their choice on reproductive rights. Voting YES on the Amendment will give women a choice. Vote YES to protect women\u8217\'20\'19s health.\u8221\'20\'1D (Voting yes would do the opposite.)\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou know, as a general rule, if your best strategy is to try to trick people into accidentally voting for you, that\u8217\'20\'19s probably a sign that you\u8217\'20\'19re the bad guys,\u8221\'20\'1D Meyers said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s like, if in order to get people to watch this show online, we made the title of every \uc2 YouTube\uc2  video \u8216\'20\'18click here for free boner pills!\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLast night was both a promising sign of progress in the fight to safeguard \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights on the one hand, and a perfect case study of what the GOP has become on the other hand,\u8221\'20\'1D he concluded.\par \par \uc2 Stephen Colbert\par \par \uc2 Stephen Colbert also delved into the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/kansas-abortion-rights-referendum-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kansas referendum}}}\uc2  on the Late Show, calling the 59% to 41% decision \u8220\'20\'1Ckind of shocking, the scale of that victory. That\u8217\'20\'19s just not a win. That\u8217\'20\'19s a Kans-asskicking.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd may I remind you, Kansas is a state so bright red it looks like me after 30 seconds on the beach,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CKeep in mind, this blowout happened after a series of dirty tricks from Republicans in Kansas,\u8221\'20\'1D he continued. \u8220\'20\'1CFirst, they made the wording of the ballot measure extra confusing, then they sent voters text messages right before the election\u8221\'20\'1D that misleadingly equated a yes vote with personal choice.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey tried to trick them into voting the wrong way,\u8221\'20\'1D Colbert said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the most misleading political message since 1952\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18I Like Ike \u8230\'20\'26 too much to burden him with the presidency \u8211\'20\'13 vote Stevenson.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In other news, Colbert pointed to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/health/2022/08/02/processed-food-brain-function-study/10211114002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new study}}}\uc2  that found that eating processed food like ice-cream hurts brain function. \u8220\'20\'1CStop it, science,\u8221\'20\'1D Colbert pleaded. \u8220\'20\'1CJust stop studying things. This is why people turn against you and start eating horse paste. What\u8217\'20\'19s next? Puppy kisses cause herpes? Exposure to Chris Evans is depleting the ozone layer? Just let us have nice things!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trevor Noah\par \par \uc2 That moment when you're Alex Jones and your lawyer accidentally sends the prosecution evidence that you committed perjury {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/td4aHAhV9r"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/td4aHAhV9r}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 The Daily Show (@TheDailyShow) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TheDailyShow/status/1555006448555290625?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 4, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 And on the Daily Show, Trevor Noah looked into a jaw-dropping moment during the defamation trial of Alex Jones, a far-rightwing commentator and a \u8220\'20\'1Cguy who makes Donald Trump look like a reasonable human being\u8221\'20\'1D. During Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s hearing, Jones, on trial for defamation after he repeatedly and systematically called the 2012 Sandy Hook shooting a hoax, found out on the stand that his lawyer had mistakenly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/alex-jones-sandy-hook-shooting-defamation-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 emailed the prosecution evidence}}}\uc2  that proved he had committed perjury.\par \par \uc2 Noah cracked up at footage of a visibly reddened, flustered Jones confronted on the stand with his lies. \u8220\'20\'1CHe was so shocked, he started turning into every emoji,\u8221\'20\'1D Noah said. \u8220\'20\'1CAt one point he even tried to give himself Covid,\u8221\'20\'1D he added, pointing to a moment where Jones coughed on the stand. \u8220\'20\'1CDid you see that? \u8216\'20\'18Oh, I can\u8217\'20\'19t speak, you know the disease I said is fake? Yeah, I got it, I\u8217\'20\'19ve got it.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou know you\u8217\'20\'19re in trouble when the truth chokes you up like an episode of Hot Ones,\u8221\'20\'1D Noah continued.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut you realize, this moment is huge, because it shows that Alex Jones probably committed perjury. Which means Alex Jones lies about stuff,\u8221\'20\'1D he joked. \u8220\'20\'1CYeah, I know, that\u8217\'20\'19s shocking, because does that mean \u8230\'20\'26 chemtrails from planes aren\u8217\'20\'19t turning the frogs gay? Was that also a lie?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 2022-08-04T15:30:21Z 2022-08-04T15:37:43Z {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://media.guim.co.uk/60d936549fdff370f94636c5ca8173dd25ab475c/103_122_2591_1554/500.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://media.guim.co.uk/60d936549fdff370f94636c5ca8173dd25ab475c/103_122_2591_1554/500.jpg}}}\uc2  Seth Meyers on Kansas vote to preserve \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights: \u8216\'20\'18Especially encouraging, given that anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists used every shady tactic they could think of and still lost.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220804ei84002gz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex