\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden signs second executive order to protect US  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  access\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh \par \uc2 753 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 August 2022\par 15:21 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 25\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The directive equips the Heath and Human Services department to expand coverage for patients seeking out of state care\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  signed a second executive order on Wednesday that aims to protect access to reproductive healthcare after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  struck down the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Most significantly, the order directs the health and human services department to consider ways to expand coverage for patients traveling out of state for reproductive healthcare. Biden\u8217\'20\'19s order does not detail how this could be achieved; currently, government-subsidized Medicaid health insurance plans cover medically necessary abortions in only 16 states and do not reimburse patients who leave their state to seek an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A senior administration official told the Guardian that \uc2 HHS\uc2  will soon have more details on provisions to help women served by Medicaid health coverage cover certain costs of traveling for reproductive care.\par \par \uc2 Following the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s June decision overturning Roe v Wade, the landmark ruling that codified \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights for half a century, the procedure is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2022/jun/28/tracking-where-abortion-laws-stand-in-every-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 now banned}}}\uc2  in at least 10 states and partially banned in another four. Bans and restrictions are being legally challenged in several other states, with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in about half the country under threat.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/aug/01/kansas-abortion-vote-value-them-both-amendment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\uc2  were on the ballot in Kansas, where voters overwhelmingly rejected an amendment that would pave the way for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions.\par \par \uc2 Republicans \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t have a clue about the power of American women\u8221\'20\'1D, Biden said before signing his order. \u8220\'20\'1CLast night in Kansas they found out.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 People in states where abortions are restricted or clinics are scarce have been more frequently pushed across state lines to seek treatment. Many are unable to afford to do so \u8211\'20\'13 or are turning to non-profit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds to help defray the costs.\par \par \uc2 This latest order, which Biden signed at the kick-off meeting for an interagency taskforce on reproductive rights led by \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , will also direct \uc2 HHS\uc2  to help health workers navigate the confusing and shifting rules on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care following the supreme court decision, and track maternal and reproductive health outcomes to better assess the impacts of the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COK folks, we\u8217\'20\'19ve got a lot of work to do,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, after signing.\par \par \uc2 This order, like Biden\u8217\'20\'19s previous executive order on reproductive rights, is likely to face criticisms for failing to provide many details on how and when \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights will be protected. Although the White House is limited in what it could do to improve access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and reproductive rights without congressional action, advocates have urged federal agencies to make it easier to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills in states where they remain legal, and explicitly direct hospitals receiving federal funds for low-income healthcare programs to provide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs in life-threatening emergencies.\par \par \uc2 In July, Biden signed an executive order directing \uc2 HHS\uc2  to \u8220\'20\'1Ctake action\u8221\'20\'1D to protect access to medication for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and update guidance to ensure that emergency care is not affected by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions. It also directed the attorney general and the White House counsel to convene private lawyers and public interest organizations to encourage \u8220\'20\'1Crobust legal representation of patients, providers and third parties lawfully seeking or offering reproductive healthcare services throughout the country\u8221\'20\'1D. And it directed agencies to develop how-to guides for patients to protect their online data to shield themselves from state and local surveillance.\par \par \uc2 Pressure on the Biden administration to act has ramped up as women in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is banned or restricted increasingly find themselves in dangerous, life-threatening situations, while doctors find themselves in legal jeopardy for providing essential healthcare. Patients have also struggled to receive {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=29VPLXCadIg&t=251s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 routine care for miscarriages}}}\uc2  and ectopic pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 The Department of Justice announced this week it is suing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/idaho"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Idaho}}}\uc2  over the state\u8217\'20\'19s near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, set to take effect on 25 August. \u8220\'20\'1CThe justice department is going to use every tool we have to ensure reproductive freedom,\u8221\'20\'1D the attorney general, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/justice-department/justice-department-sues-idaho-abortion-ban-first-post-roe-litigation-rcna41174?cid=ed_npd_bn_tw_bn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Merrick Garland, told reporters}}}\uc2  on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 More than 60% of Americans believe in the legal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in all or most cases, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/fact-tank/2022/06/13/about-six-in-ten-americans-say-abortion-should-be-legal-in-all-or-most-cases-2/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pew Research Center}}}\uc2  poll from June.\par \par \uc2 But Republicans in the Senate \u8211\'20\'13 which is evenly divided along party lines \u8211\'20\'13 have already blocked a bill in May that would have invalidated \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions nationwide, and are poised to defeat a narrower, bipartisan measure introduced this week that would guarantee access to contraceptives and invalidate the toughest \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220803ei83001h3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
