\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Kansas\u8217\'20\'19s vote to protect  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights upends US midterm elections \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein \par \uc2 4,918 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 August 2022\par 20:11 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Kansas votes to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in state constitutionVote is a sign that overturning of Roe v? Wade will have unpredictable effects ahead of November electionsSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Washington spent today digesting the results of primary elections across the country, in which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/03/primary-elections-trump-kansas-abortion-biden-nato-pelosi?page=with:block-62ea76758f0892e28b4ab082#block-62ea76758f0892e28b4ab082"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kansas voted to protect \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights }}}\uc2  while Trump-aligned candidates {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/republican-candidates-2020-election-deniers-win-key-primaries"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 triumphed in Arizona and elsewhere}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap of what happened today:\par \par \uc2 * Indiana congresswoman Jackie Walorski{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/03/primary-elections-trump-kansas-abortion-biden-nato-pelosi?page=with:block-62ead0f98f0892e28b4ab4cf#block-62ead0f98f0892e28b4ab4cf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was among four people killed}}}\uc2  in a car accident in the state.\par \par \uc2 * The defamation trial of conspiracy theorist Alex Jones{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/03/primary-elections-trump-kansas-abortion-biden-nato-pelosi?page=with:block-62eaba558f0892e28b4ab449#block-62eaba558f0892e28b4ab449"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 took a dramatic turn}}}\uc2  when his cellphone data was accidentally shared with attorneys for the plaintiffs in the case, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/03/primary-elections-trump-kansas-abortion-biden-nato-pelosi?page=with:block-62eacaa98f0892e28b4ab4b3#block-62eacaa98f0892e28b4ab4b3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drawing the attention of the January 6 committee}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/03/primary-elections-trump-kansas-abortion-biden-nato-pelosi?page=with:block-62ea8ece8f0878ca99e20632#block-62ea8ece8f0878ca99e20632"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A poll from Monmouth University}}}\uc2  showed Democrats have taken a narrow lead when it comes to control of Congress, while Biden\u8217\'20\'19s approval rating plunge may have halted.\par \par \uc2 * Senate Republican leader Mitch McConnell{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/03/primary-elections-trump-kansas-abortion-biden-nato-pelosi?page=with:block-62eaabe08f0878ca99e207e4#block-62eaabe08f0878ca99e207e4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called for the chamber}}}\uc2  to approve Sweden and Finland\u8217\'20\'19s entry to \uc2 Nato\uc2 , which it is expected to do later today.\par \par \uc2 * House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  concluded her visit to Taiwan with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/03/primary-elections-trump-kansas-abortion-biden-nato-pelosi?page=with:block-62ea93f28f0892e28b4ab217#block-62ea93f28f0892e28b4ab217"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a reaffirmation that US leaders would stand up for the island}}}\uc2 , particularly against China.\par \par \uc2 * New York Democrat \uc2 Carolyn Maloney\uc2  had to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/03/primary-elections-trump-kansas-abortion-biden-nato-pelosi?page=with:block-62ea98308f08b58de97ebf62#block-62ea98308f08b58de97ebf62"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 walk back a comment }}}\uc2  suggesting Biden wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t stand for a second term.\par \par \uc2 * The president, meanwhile, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/03/primary-elections-trump-kansas-abortion-biden-nato-pelosi?page=with:block-62ea9c1d8f0892e28b4ab2a3#block-62ea9c1d8f0892e28b4ab2a3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 still has Covid-19}}}\uc2 , but he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/03/primary-elections-trump-kansas-abortion-biden-nato-pelosi?page=with:block-62ea8b5b8f08b58de97ebe8d#block-62ea8b5b8f08b58de97ebe8d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plans to sign a measure to boost semiconductor production}}}\uc2  next week in an outdoor ceremony.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Indiana congresswoman killed in car accident\par \par \uc2 Jackie Walorski\uc2 , a Republican House representative from Indiana, was among four people killed in a car accident while traveling in the state, WSBT reports:\par \par \uc2 enltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/BREAKING?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #BREAKING}}}\uc2  : U.S. Congresswoman \uc2 Jackie Walorski\uc2  (R-Indiana) has been killed in a crash that happened at 12:32 P.M. in Elkhart County on S.R. 19 south of S.R. 119. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/SbvhWlHgxL"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/SbvhWlHgxL}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Erica Finke WSBT (@EricaFinkeTV) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/EricaFinkeTV/status/1554915410880897024?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 3, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrA northbound passenger car traveled left of center and collided head on with a southbound vehicle.\par \par \uc2 Walorski, Zachary Potts with the St. Joseph County Republican Party, and Walorski's comm. director Emma Thompson all passed away.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Erica Finke WSBT (@EricaFinkeTV) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/EricaFinkeTV/status/1554916543078744066?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 3, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThe northbound vehicle driver, Edith Schmucker, died as well.\par \par \uc2 The investigation is continuing at this time. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/RIP?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #RIP}}}\uc2  to everyone involved in this horrifying crash.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Erica Finke WSBT (@EricaFinkeTV) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/EricaFinkeTV/status/1554916713921187840?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 3, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 A federal grand jury investigating the January 6 attack has subpoenaed former White House counsel \uc2 Pat Cipollone\uc2  and his deputy Patrick Philbin, according to media reports.\par \par \uc2 Both men were present in the White House during the time of the insurrection, and Cipollone has provided testimony to the House committee investigating the attack, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/21/jan-6-final-hearing-trump-capitol-latest-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62d9fc5a8f081aa0b1405ac4#block-62d9fc5a8f081aa0b1405ac4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was a major part of its most recent hearing}}}\uc2  and showed the lawyer trying to get \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to call off his supporters as they assaulted the Capitol.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/08/03/politics/philbin-subpoena/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN first reported Philbin}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s subpoena today, while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/US/white-house-counsel-subpoenaed-federal-grand-jury-investigating/story?id=87845397"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ABC News broke the story}}}\uc2  of Cipollone\u8217\'20\'19s subpoena yesterday.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 The January 6 committee plans to subpoena phone data from Alex Jones that was accidentally revealed in a defamation case against him, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rollingstone.com/politics/politics-news/alex-jones-cell-phone-jan6-committee-subpoeana-1392270/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rolling Stone reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Citing two sources, the magazine said investigators for the House committee investigating the attack were planning to take advantage of the the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/03/primary-elections-trump-kansas-abortion-biden-nato-pelosi?page=with:block-62eaba558f0892e28b4ab449#block-62eaba558f0892e28b4ab449"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 surprise development today}}}\uc2  in Jones\u8217\'20\'19 trial, where it was revealed his lawyer had accidentally shared a copy of Jones\u8217\'20\'19 phone data with attorneys for the parents of a child killed at Sandy Hook elementary school, who are suing Jones.\par \par \uc2 According to Rolling Stone, \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s unclear what, specifically, the committee will be looking for in Jones\u8217\'20\'19 communications but attorneys for the Sandy Hook plaintiffs have accused the InfoWars host of intentionally withholding relevant communications about the Sandy Hook shooting and lying about having conducted a search for them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Saying that Republicans \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t have a clue about the power of American women\u8221\'20\'1D, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  cheered Kansas voters\u8217\'20\'19 rejection of a ballot initiative that would have allowed lawmakers to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He made the comments while appearing virtually at a meeting where he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/08/03/fact-sheet-president-biden-issues-executive-order-at-the-first-meeting-of-the-task-force-on-reproductive-healthcare-access-2/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed an executive order}}}\uc2  that could allow Medicaid, the government health plan for poor and disabled Americans, to cover the travel costs of people who must cross state lines to seek an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1C[Republicans] don\u8217\'20\'19t have a clue about the power of American women. Last night in Kansas they found out.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden celebrates Kansas' defeat of a ballot initiative that would have repealed the state\u8217\'20\'19s right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/AsGe5t8FpR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/AsGe5t8FpR}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1554900800123670528?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 3, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 As the January 6 committee has explored the events surrounding the attack on the Capitol, one name has come up repeatedly: \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 . The former New York City mayor and lawyer for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been involved in that White House\u8217\'20\'19s many scandals, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/08/03/us/giuliani-charges-lobbying-inquiry-trump.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times reports}}}\uc2  today that one inquiry appears to be reaching a conclusion.\par \par \uc2 Federal investigators are unlikely to file charges against Giuliani after looking into whether he illegally lobbied for officials from Ukraine who had offered damaging information about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the Times\u8217\'20\'19 report:\par \par \uc2 While prosecutors had enough evidence last year to persuade a judge to order the seizure of Mr. Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s electronic devices, they did not uncover a smoking gun in the records, said the people, who spoke on the condition of anonymity to discuss a federal investigation.\par \par \uc2 The prosecutors have not closed the investigation, and if new evidence were to emerge, they could still pursue Mr. Giuliani. But in a telling sign that the inquiry is close to wrapping up without an indictment, investigators recently returned the electronic devices to Mr. Giuliani, the people said. Mr. Giuliani {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/04/12/politics/rudy-giuliani-phone-unlock/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also met with prosecutors}}}\uc2  and agents in February and answered their questions, a signal that his lawyers were confident he would not be charged.\par \par \uc2 This is unlikely to be the last time Giuliani hears from prosecutors, both at the federal or state level. In addition to the January 6 inquiry, he has been subpoenaed to appear before a special grand jury in Georgia that is investigating Trump\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn the 2020 election result in that state.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/20/giuliani-trump-georgia-election-meddling-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Giuliani ordered to go before grand jury in Trump election meddling case}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 There was an unusual and dramatic turn in the defamation trial of Alex Jones this afternoon, when it was revealed that his attorney accidentally sent a copy of the data from Jones\u8217\'20\'19 phone to a lawyer for the Sandy Hook parents who are suing him.\par \par \uc2 The revelations seem to open up the possibility that Jones could have perjured himself during his testimony. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the account of what happened from Ben Collins of NBC News:\par \par \uc2 enltrWow. Sandy Hook parents' lawyer is revealing that Alex Jones' lawyers sent him the contents of Jones' phone BY MISTAKE.\par \par \uc2 "12 days ago, your attorneys messed up and sent me a digital copy of every text" Jones has sent for years.\par \par \uc2 "You know what perjury is?" the lawyer asks.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Collins (@oneunderscore__) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/oneunderscore__/status/1554864067508060160?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 3, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrSandy Hook parents' lawyer is now asking Jones about the times he has emailed about Sandy Hook over the last several years, despite testifying under oath he couldn't find any emails about Sandy Hook. There are apparently a lot of them. One is on a screen right now.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Collins (@oneunderscore__) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/oneunderscore__/status/1554864549127503872?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 3, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrEven Jones is stunned by the fact Sandy Hook parents seem to have his emails. Jones just called it their lawyers' "Perry Mason moment." It's shocking.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Collins (@oneunderscore__) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/oneunderscore__/status/1554864860579696647?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 3, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrJudge instructing the jury on the entire contents of Alex Jones' phone, which was accidentally handed over from Jones' lawyers to the Sandy Hook parents' lawyers:\par \par \uc2 "What we do know is that it was not properly turned over when it should have been."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Collins (@oneunderscore__) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/oneunderscore__/status/1554866223460007936?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 3, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThese texts and emails are FINALLY revealing financials behind Infowars.\par \par \uc2 Some days in 2018, InfoWars was making $800,000 a day.\par \par \uc2 "Well after your deplatforming, your numbers keep getting better," Sandy Hook parents' lawyer says.\par \par \uc2 If they keep that up, that's ~$300 mill. a year.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Collins (@oneunderscore__) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/oneunderscore__/status/1554867649150156805?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 3, 2022}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/alex-jones-sandy-hook-shooting-defamation-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Per the Associated Press}}}\uc2 , closing arguments in the case are expected to begin today.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 The defamation trial of conspiracy theorist Alex Jones appears to be nearing a conclusion in Texas. The Associated Press reports Jones acknowledged in court that the Sandy Hook school shooting happened, after years in which he insisted it was a hoax:\par \par \uc2 The conspiracy theorist Alex Jones said on Wednesday he now understands it was irresponsible to declare {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2022/mar/13/sandy-hook-review-an-american-tragedy-elizabeth-williamson-facebook-youtube-alex-jones"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Sandy Hook school shooting}}}\uc2  a hoax, and now believes it was \u8220\'20\'1C100% real\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He was speaking in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/02/alex-jones-sandy-hook-shooting-hoax-claim-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his own defamation trial}}}\uc2 , a day after the parents of a six-year-old boy killed in the 2012 attack testified about suffering, death threats and harassment they have endured because of what Jones has trumpeted on his media platforms.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was \u8230\'20\'26 especially since I\u8217\'20\'19ve met the parents. It\u8217\'20\'19s 100% real,\u8221\'20\'1D Jones said, at the trial that will determine how much he owes for defaming the parents of Jesse Lewis, one of 20 children and six adults killed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2022/mar/13/sandy-hook-review-an-american-tragedy-elizabeth-williamson-facebook-youtube-alex-jones"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at the school in Newtown, Connecticut}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/alex-jones-sandy-hook-shooting-defamation-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s 100% real\u8217\'20\'19: Alex Jones admits in court Sandy Hook shooting not a hoax}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , the Republican Senate minority leader, has said Finland and Sweden\u8217\'20\'19s applications for membership of Nato \u8211\'20\'13 motivated by Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine \u8211\'20\'13 are \u8220\'20\'1Ca slam dunk for national security that deserves unanimous bipartisan support\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 McConnell made the remarks on the Senate floor today, before a vote scheduled later. The short version of what he said, provided by his office, is as follows:\par \par \uc2 Today, the Senate will approve ratification protocols to welcome Finland and Sweden as the two newest members of Nato \u8230\'20\'26 There is just no question that admitting these robust democratic countries with modern economies and capable, interoperable militaries will only strengthen the most successful military alliance in human history \u8230\'20\'26 This is a slam dunk for national security that deserves unanimous bipartisan support.\par \par \uc2 Approval is expected, though one prominent (and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/24/josh-hawley-republican-senator-ran-running-capitol-attack-kansas-city-star"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 notably sprightly}}}\uc2  ) Republican has said he will vote no.\par \par \uc2 In an op ed last month, \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2  of Missouri {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/policy/defense/3582757-hawley-vows-to-vote-no-on-adding-sweden-and-finland-to-nato/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CFinland and Sweden want to join the Atlantic Alliance to head off further Russian aggression in Europe. That is entirely understandable given their location and security needs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut America\u8217\'20\'19s greatest foreign adversary doesn\u8217\'20\'19t loom over Europe. It looms in Asia. I am talking of course about the People\u8217\'20\'19s Republic of China. And when it comes to Chinese imperialism, the American people should know the truth: the United States is not ready to resist it. Expanding American security commitments in Europe now would only make that problem worse \u8211\'20\'13 and America, less safe.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2 , the man in the middle of most things in Washington these days, spoke to the Senate rules committee this morning about reforming the Electoral Count Act, the creaky old mechanism which just about stood up to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attempt to overturn his defeat in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2 . Photograph: Shawn Thew/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 Reform to the act has emerged as a rare subject of bipartisan interest on Capitol Hill \u8211\'20\'13 and Manchin, being the only Democrat in statewide office in otherwise deep Republican red West Virginia, is generally a fan of bipartisan things.\par \par \uc2 He said: \u8220\'20\'1CAs we saw on 6 January 2021, a lot of the \u8216\'20\'18fixes\u8217\'20\'19 established by the original Electoral Count Act are not merely outdated but actually serve as the very mechanisms that bad actors have zeroed in on as a way to potentially invalidate presidential election results.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs I am sure you will hear from the panel of distinguished experts who will testify before you today \u8211\'20\'13 the time to reform the ECA is long overdue. The time for Congress to act is now.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo that end, I am proud of the bipartisan bill introduced by [the Republican] Senator [Susan] Collins [of Maine], myself, and my colleagues last month: The Electoral Count Reform and Presidential Transition Improvement Act.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Manchin said the new act would \u8220\'20\'1Cunambiguously clarifie that the vice-president is prohibited from interfering with the electoral votes; raise the objection [to electoral results] threshold from a single representative and a single senator to 20% of the members of both the House of Representatives and the Senate; and set a hard deadline for state governors to certify \u8230\'20\'26 electoral results \u8211\'20\'13 and if they fail to do so or submit a slate that does not match with the electoral results from the state, it creates an expedited judicial process to resolve\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Manchin and Sinema act out of ego, not principle\par \par \uc2 This week, the spotlight once again will be on Democratic senators \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  and \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  (dubbed \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2021/10/18/manchinema-become-k-street-darlings/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Manchinema}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D by the Washington press corps when the two blocked much of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s agenda).\par \par \uc2 Which is exactly where both of these politicians want it.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 last chance for a large package \u8211\'20\'13 Manchin agreed last week to $790bn \u8211\'20\'13 on the climate and healthcare, financed by a tax increase on the rich and big corporations. But will Sinema go along?\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been joked that the word \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitics\u8221\'20\'1D is derived from the Latin \u8220\'20\'1Cpoli\u8221\'20\'1D, meaning \u8220\'20\'1Cmany\u8221\'20\'1D, and \u8220\'20\'1Cticks\u8221\'20\'1D, meaning small blood-sucking insects. I don\u8217\'20\'19t hold such a cynical view. But I do know from 50 years\u8217\'20\'19 experience in and around Washington that most of the people who serve in our nation\u8217\'20\'19s capital have very, very large \u8211\'20\'13 shall we say? \u8211\'20\'13 egos.\par \par \uc2 Full column:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/aug/03/joe-manchin-kyrsten-sinema-attention-ego"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Manchin and Kyrsten Sinema act out of ego, not principle | Robert Reich}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Could things be looking up for Democrats? Between the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/03/primary-elections-trump-kansas-abortion-biden-nato-pelosi?page=with:block-62ea76758f0892e28b4ab082#block-62ea76758f0892e28b4ab082"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defeat of an anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ballot measure in Kansas}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/03/primary-elections-trump-kansas-abortion-biden-nato-pelosi?page=with:block-62ea8ece8f0878ca99e20632#block-62ea8ece8f0878ca99e20632"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 some positive polling data}}}\uc2 , president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s party has seen signs pulling out of the slump it fell into recently - but there\u8217\'20\'19s still months to go before the November midterms.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a look back at what has happened so far today:\par \par \uc2 * House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  concluded her visit to Taiwan with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/03/primary-elections-trump-kansas-abortion-biden-nato-pelosi?page=with:block-62ea93f28f0892e28b4ab217#block-62ea93f28f0892e28b4ab217"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a reaffirmation that US leaders would stand up for the island}}}\uc2 , particularly against China.\par \par \uc2 * New York Democrat \uc2 Carolyn Maloney\uc2  had to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/03/primary-elections-trump-kansas-abortion-biden-nato-pelosi?page=with:block-62ea98308f08b58de97ebf62#block-62ea98308f08b58de97ebf62"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 walk back a comment }}}\uc2  suggesting Biden wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t stand for a second term.\par \par \uc2 * The president, meanwhile, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/03/primary-elections-trump-kansas-abortion-biden-nato-pelosi?page=with:block-62ea9c1d8f0892e28b4ab2a3#block-62ea9c1d8f0892e28b4ab2a3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 still has Covid-19}}}\uc2 , but he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/aug/03/primary-elections-trump-kansas-abortion-biden-nato-pelosi?page=with:block-62ea8b5b8f08b58de97ebe8d#block-62ea8b5b8f08b58de97ebe8d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plans to sign a measure to boost semiconductor production}}}\uc2  next week in an outdoor ceremony.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has announced a new argument calendar for its cases in the fall, where the conservative majority could again move to upend laws across the United States.\par \par \uc2 enltrNew {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/SCOTUS?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #SCOTUS}}}\uc2  argument calendar. Affirmative action cases to be heard Oct. 31. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/hgyVlENvRj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/hgyVlENvRj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Adam Liptak (@adamliptak) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/adamliptak/status/1554857702333059072?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 3, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Of note is the 31 October argument of two cases against \uc2 Harvard University\uc2  and the \uc2 University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill\uc2 , in which the court could bar the usage of race as a factor in college admissions.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/02/supreme-court-affirmative-action-harvard"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme court could strike blow against affirmative action in Harvard case ruling}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden remains positive for Covid-19 but is otherwise feeling well, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2022/08/Update-8.3.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 White House doctor said}}}\uc2  in an update on the president\u8217\'20\'19s health.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe President continues to feel well,\u8221\'20\'1D Kevin O\u8217\'20\'19Connor wrote, noting Biden \u8220\'20\'1Cremains fever-free and in good spirits\u8221\'20\'1D and had completed \u8220\'20\'1Ca light workout\u8221\'20\'1D today.\par \par \uc2 Biden contracted the virus last month and appeared to have recovered, testing negative last week. But over the weekend, he tested positive again.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/30/biden-covid-positive-test"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden tests positive for Covid only days after testing negative}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 New York Democratic House representative \uc2 Carolyn Maloney\uc2  is doing a bit of clean-up this morning after suggesting in a debate last night that president Biden won\u8217\'20\'19t run for re-election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t believe he\u8217\'20\'19s running for reelection,\u8221\'20\'1D Maloney said during the debate, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/08/03/politics/carolyn-maloney-biden-reelection/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to CNN}}}\uc2 . The lawmaker appeared to be saying the quiet part out loud when it comes to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s viability as a candidate in 2024, given his age (he\u8217\'20\'19ll be 81 when the election is held) and dismal approval ratings.\par \par \uc2 In a series of tweets Wednesday, Maloney tried to clear the matter up:\par \par \uc2 enltrI will absolutely support President Biden, if he decides to run for re-election.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s leadership securing historic investments for healthcare, climate & economic justice prove once again why he is the strong and effective leader we need right now. ??\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Carolyn B. Maloney\uc2  (@CarolynBMaloney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CarolynBMaloney/status/1554847201041563649?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 3, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrI urge all Democrats to stay united & focused on working towards winning the midterms.\par \par \uc2 Right now, I am concentrating on the upcoming Democratic primary on August 23rd & the issues that matter to the voters of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/NY12?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #NY12}}}\uc2 . Request your absentee ballot by Monday, August 8th\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Carolyn B. Maloney\uc2  (@CarolynBMaloney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CarolynBMaloney/status/1554847202874474496?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 3, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Maloney represents a district that encompasses part of New York City, but after redistricting, she\u8217\'20\'19s vying to keep her seat against congressman \uc2 Jerry Nadler\uc2 , a fellow Democrat.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Congress' support for Taiwan 'remains ironclad', Pelosi says as she concludes trip\par \par \uc2 Following her visit to Taiwan and China\u8217\'20\'19s furious response, House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  has reiterated her commitment to standing up for the country and said it\u8217\'20\'19s shared by lawmakers across the \uc2 US Congress\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur Congressional delegation\u8217\'20\'19s visit should be seen as a strong statement that America stands with Taiwan. We came to Taiwan to listen to, learn from and show our support for the people of Taiwan, who have built a thriving Democracy that stands as one of the freest and most open in the world,\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi said in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.speaker.gov/newsroom/8322-2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a statement after the trip}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur partnership remains unwavering, and support in the Congress \u8211\'20\'13 House and Senate, Democrats and Republicans \u8211\'20\'13 remains ironclad.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Much of her statement recapped what she did during the visit to the island, which lasted about a day, and saw Pelosi discuss topics ranging from climate change to Taiwan\u8217\'20\'19s semiconductor industry to \u8220\'20\'1CCongress\u8217\'20\'19 ongoing commitment to helping Taiwan defend its freedom in the face of aggression\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Things could be looking up for Democrats: poll\par \par \uc2 Monmouth University\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.monmouth.edu/polling-institute/reports/monmouthpoll_US_080322/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this morning released a poll}}}\uc2  that contains some glimmers of hope for Democrats, who have been beaten down over the past year by high inflation and dissatisfaction with president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The data from the survey conducted from July 28 through August 1 shows 50 percent of respondents would prefer Democrats in control of Congress - putting the party ahead of Republicans on that question after the GOP took the lead earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 enltrNATIONAL POLL: Which party do Americans want in control of Congress?\par \par \uc2 38% DEM\par \par \uc2 12% not matter, but lean DEM\par \par \uc2 34% GOP\par \par \uc2 9% not matter, but lean GOP\par \par \uc2 5% not matter, no lean {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ITYL9gyPbd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/ITYL9gyPbd}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/GCmAnS7zq5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/GCmAnS7zq5}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 MonmouthPoll (@MonmouthPoll) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MonmouthPoll/status/1554844970426703874?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 3, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRecent events, such as the Jan. 6th committee hearings and Supreme Court decisions, seem to have generated a bit more energy for the Democrats\u8221\'20\'1D, said Patrick Murray, the director of the Monmouth University Polling Institute. However, \u8220\'20\'1CIt is not clear that this is actual momentum. It may simply be ongoing volatility in a public largely unhappy with the way things are going in Washington.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The poll also found some stabilization in views of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s job performance, which still remains dismal with 38 percent approving, and 56 percent disapproving. But, that approval ratings was up from 36 percent in June, while the disapproval rating was down from 58 percent the same month.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration just announced that the president will sign the CHIPS and Science Act on August 9 in the White House Rose Garden.\par \par \uc2 The $280 billion bill is meant to incentivize semiconductor producers to build more factories in the United States, and also funds scientific research. It was approved with bipartisan support in Congress, though did face opposition from some conservative Republicans and Bernie Sanders. While their objections did not completely align, they generally viewed the measure as \u8220\'20\'1Ccorporate welfare\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/31/bernie-sanders-conservative-thinktanks-semiconductor-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How Bernie Sanders and conservatives united against US semiconductor bill}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Later today, President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will sign a second executive order concerning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, this one intended to help people travel to access reproductive care, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/maanvi-singh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maanvi Singh}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is set to sign a second executive order on Wednesday that aims to protect access to reproductive healthcare after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  struck down the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Most significantly, the order directs the health and human services department to consider ways to expand coverage for patients traveling out of state for reproductive healthcare. Biden\u8217\'20\'19s order does not detail how this could be achieved; currently, government-subsidized Medicaid health insurance plans cover medically necessary abortions in only 16 states and do not reimburse patients who leave their state to seek an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A senior administration official told the Guardian that \uc2 HHS\uc2  will soon have more details on provisions to help women served by Medicaid health coverage cover certain costs of traveling for reproductive care.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/biden-executive-order-protect-abortion-access"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden set to sign second executive order to protect \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  has wrapped up her trip to Taiwan, one of the more dramatic foreign trips of a US politician in recent history due to China\u8217\'20\'19s threats of retaliation, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/helen-davidson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Helen Davidson}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 The US House speaker, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/nancy-pelosi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nancy Pelosi}}}\uc2 , has left Taiwan after a historic visit in which she promised the US\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Ccrucial\u8221\'20\'1D solidarity with the self-ruled democracy that faces major military threats from China\u8217\'20\'19s government.\par \par \uc2 Beijing has announced \u8220\'20\'1Cmilitary operations\u8221\'20\'1D including missile tests and live fire exercises in the waters around {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/taiwan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Taiwan}}}\uc2 , scheduled to begin on Wednesday night after Pelosi departs, but Taiwan\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Tsai Ing\uc2 -wen, has vowed to not back down.\par \par \uc2 At a press conference on Wednesday, Pelosi questioned the motivations of the Chinese president, \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2 , when asked about his strong response to her visit. Beijing has vowed \u8220\'20\'1Cconsequences\u8221\'20\'1D and said it would begin live fire drills close to Taiwan on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/aug/03/nancy-pelosi-taiwan-visit-speaker-pledges-us-solidarity-tsai-in-wen-china-military-drills"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nancy Pelosi leaves Taiwan as China orders live-fire drills off coast}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 While some races remain to be called, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/martin-pengelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Martin Pengelly}}}\uc2  reports that Peter Meijer, a Michigan Republican who voted to impeach \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  after the January 6 attack, lost his primary - thanks in part to Democratic meddling:\par \par \uc2 Peter Meijier of Michigan, one of 10 House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  who voted to impeach \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  over the Capitol attack, will not return to Congress next year.\par \par \uc2 Meijer\uc2  lost his primary on Tuesday to a Trump-backed election denier \u8211\'20\'13 while Trump supporters and election deniers won primaries across the country.\par \par \uc2 Meijer\uc2 , a first-term congressman, was beaten by John Gibbs. In a statement, \uc2 Meijer\uc2  said: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m proud to have remained true to my principles, even when doing so came at a significant political cost.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He published angrier words on Monday, lambasting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  who spent campaign dollars in support of Gibbs, seeing him as beatable in the midterms in November.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kansans weren\u8217\'20\'19t alone in going to the polls yesterday. Four other states held primary elections, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levine}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lauren-gambino"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauren Gambino}}}\uc2  have a rundown of what happened:\par \par \uc2 On one of the most consequential nights of this year\u8217\'20\'19s primary season, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s sway in a series of Republican races remained unclear but voters in red-state {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kansas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kansas}}}\uc2  resoundingly rejected an amendment aimed at restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday night\u8217\'20\'19s marquee races were in Arizona, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/01/arizona-republicans-kari-lake-mark-finchem"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 where Republicans are on the verge}}}\uc2  of tapping prominent election deniers to be their nominees in contests for governor, secretary of state and \uc2 US Senate\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the governor\u8217\'20\'19s race, Trump-backed Kari Lake, a former news anchor who has built her campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/10/16/politics/fact-check-kari-lake-arizona-governor-election-lies/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 around misinformation about the 2020 election}}}\uc2 , was trailing Karrin Taylor Robson, a wealthy real-estate developer who is endorsed by \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  and the current Arizona governor, \uc2 Doug Ducey\uc2 . The winner will take on \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2 , Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s current secretary of state, who was projected to win the Democratic gubernatorial nomination.\par \par \uc2 Down the ballot, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/feb/21/mark-finchem-trump-arizona-elections-secretary-of-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mark Finchem}}}\uc2 , a close ally of Trump who aggressively sought to overturn Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s election results, was on the verge of clinching the GOP nomination to be secretary of state in a four-way primary. Trump has endorsed Finchem in the contest, which typically gets little attention, boosting him to the front of the field.\par \par \uc2 If elected in November, Finchem would wield considerable power over elections in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/arizona"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona}}}\uc2 , including how ballots are counted and there is a loud alarm he could use that power to throw out an election result he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t like, especially given his efforts to overturn the results of the 2020 race.\par \par \uc2 Underscoring how deeply embedded Trump\u8217\'20\'19s election lies are among Republicans in Arizona, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/08/02/us/politics/arizona-trump-fake-electors.html?partner=slack&smid=sl-share"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times reported}}}\uc2  on Tuesday that two politicians involved in the efforts to overturn Biden\u8217\'20\'19s victory in the state worried the scheme could \u8220\'20\'1Cappear treasonous\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/poppy-noor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Poppy Noor}}}\uc2  is on the ground in Kansas, with full coverage of the state\u8217\'20\'19s vote to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights:\par \par \uc2 Kansans secured a huge win for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the US on Tuesday night when they voted to continue to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 The race was called by a host of US groups including NBC News, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  and Decision Desk HQ.\par \par \uc2 The move will be seen as huge a loss for the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement and a major win for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates across America, who will see the result as a bellwether for popular opinion.\par \par \uc2 Kansas \u8211\'20\'13 a deeply conservative and usually reliably Republican state \u8211\'20\'13 is the first US state to put \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to a vote since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  ruled to overturn constitutional protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in late June.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/kansas-abortion-vote-state-constitution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kansas votes to protect \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights in state constitution}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kansas is an unlikely place for a triumph of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Starting in the 1990s, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers in the state were repeated targets of violence, and in 2009, physician George Tiller {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/03/abortion-providers-violence-danger-roe-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was assassinated in Wichita}}}\uc2 . The state is a reliable GOP vote in presidential elections, and mostly sends Republicans to represent it in the Senate and House of Representatives - all of whom currently oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But as last night\u8217\'20\'19s vote to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections in the constitutions shows, its residents don\u8217\'20\'19t necessarily share their views. Around 59 percent of voters rejected a measure to change the constitution to allow the procedure to be cracked down on - about matching the 58 percent of Americans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/393275/steady-americans-not-roe-wade-overturned.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gallup found}}}\uc2  did not want Roe v. Wade overturned.\par \par \uc2 Whether red or blue, many states appear to share this dynamic. The Public Religion Research Institute says {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ava.prri.org/#reproh/2018/States/abortion_legality/3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 only in 10 states do majorities of voters}}}\uc2  want to make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  illegal in all or most cases. Nationally, only 40 percent of people would support doing that.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kansas' vote to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights upends midterms\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. Last night, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/kansas-abortion-vote-state-constitution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voters in Kansas backed a measure to protect \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\uc2  in the state constitution, and the contest wasn\u8217\'20\'19t even close. The state is a Republican stronghold but Kansans surged to the polls to resoundingly reject the measure, in one of the first signs that the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn Roe v Wade is having unpredictable political effects ahead of the November elections, where voters will decide who controls Congress.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s not all that happened last night:\par \par \uc2 * Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s Peter Meijer, a Republican congressman who voted to impeach \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , narrowly lost his primary, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/08/01/politics/rep-peter-meijer-michigan-gop-primary/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 after Democrats put money into supporting his challenger}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * The Republicans vying for the party\u8217\'20\'19s governorship nomination in Arizona were neck-and-neck, with Trump-backed Kari Lake up against Karrin Taylor Robson, who was endorsed by more mainstream Republicans like former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Blake Masters\uc2 , another Trump acolyte, won the GOP nomination for Senate in Arizona while Mark Finchem, a 2020 election denier, triumphed as the party\u8217\'20\'19s nominee for secretary of state.\par \par \uc2 * Back in Washington, the Senate will today vote on admitting Sweden and Finland to Nato, which it is expected to approve.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220803ei83002bh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
