\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18This is huge\u8217\'20\'19: Democrats hail  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights victory in Kansas\b0\par\par\uc2 Gloria Oladipo \par \uc2 443 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 August 2022\par 19:34 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Democrats celebrated the Kansas vote as a testament to the desire for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights nationwide, even in Republican-held states\par \par \uc2 Democrats including \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  hailed the outcome of an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/kansas-abortion-vote-state-constitution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights ballot question in Kansas}}}\uc2 , after a majority voted to protect the right in the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, the president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/08/02/statement-by-president-joe-biden-on-defeat-of-kansas-ballot-measure-threatening-womens-right-to-abortion/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CVoters in Kansas turned out in record numbers to reject extreme efforts to amend the state constitution to take away a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose and open the door for a statewide ban.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis vote makes clear what we know: the majority of Americans agree that women should have access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and should have the right to make their own healthcare decisions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Kansas vote was the first time \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights had been on the ballot since the conservative-dominated {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supreme court overturned Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , the 1973 ruling which guaranteed the right, in June.\par \par \uc2 A yes vote would have allowed the conservative Kansas legislature to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or ban it completely.\par \par \uc2 Other senior Democrats celebrated the Kansas vote as a testament to the desire for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights nationwide, even in Republican-held states.\par \par \uc2 The Massachusetts senator Elizabeth Warren {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ewarren/status/1554661481769205760"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThis is huge: \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights were on the ballot for the first time since Roe, and the people of Kansas voted to preserve access. I\u8217\'20\'19m grateful down to my toes for everyone who helped stop this dangerous ballot measure in its tracks.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The chairman of the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2 , \uc2 Jaime Harrison\uc2 , tweeted a congratulatory message \u8211\'20\'13 but did not mention the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  referendum.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile the GOP is pushing their ultra-MAGA agenda, Dems are nominating candidates who will work to cut costs and protect our freedoms,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/harrisonjaime/status/1554810567113801730"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he wrote}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 To many Democrats and analysts, the Kansas vote suggested that an emphasis on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights could pave the way to success in the November midterms.\par \par \uc2 The referendum question brought out a surge of new voters, with more than 800,000 people turning out, up on the 470,000 who participated in the 2018 gubernatorial primary, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businessinsider.com/republicans-should-be-terrified-over-abortion-referendum-turnout-in-kansas-2022-8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Insider}}}\uc2  reported.\par \par \uc2 Republicans who celebrated the supreme court ruling on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights have since rushed to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/jun/24/what-states-have-abortion-trigger-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pass state \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  bans}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But the Kansas vote presents an unexpected challenge for Republicans seeking to galvanize the issue for support in November. Even in more conservative states, voters largely support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CKansans bluntly rejected anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  politicians\u8217\'20\'19 attempts at creating a reproductive police state,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Kimberly Inez McGuire\uc2 , executive director of Unite for Reproductive & Gender Equity, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/2022-primary-elections-kansas-abortion-b6d62a852c2ce4617f2c03589fbb523e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Associated Press}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday\u8217\'20\'19s vote was a powerful rebuke and a promise of the mounting resistance.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220803ei83002pe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
