\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: Pelosi pledges solidarity with Taiwan amid alarm over China\u8217\'20\'19s reaction\b0\par\par\uc2 Nicola Slawson \par \uc2 1,470 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 August 2022\par 12:20 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Beijing reacts to House speaker\u8217\'20\'19s visit with outrage as Chinese military begin drills close to Taiwan. Plus, Batgirl gets cancelled\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 The US House speaker, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/nancy-pelosi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nancy Pelosi}}}\uc2 , has pledged America\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Ccrucial\u8221\'20\'1D solidarity with Taiwan, in a historic meeting with Taiwan\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Tsai Ing\uc2 -wen, who vowed not to back down in the face of military threats from China.\par \par \uc2 At a press conference on Wednesday, Pelosi questioned the motivations of Chinese president, \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2 , when asked about his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/aug/03/nancy-pelosi-in-taiwan-calls-for-calm-in-asia-as-us-china-tensions-rise-north-korea-south-korea"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strong response}}}\uc2  to her visit. China has vowed \u8220\'20\'1Cconsequences\u8221\'20\'1D and has said it will begin live fire drills close to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/taiwan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Taiwan}}}\uc2  on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIts really important for the message to be clear \u8230\'20\'26 [the US] is committed to the security of Taiwan \u8230\'20\'26 but it\u8217\'20\'19s about our shared values of democracy and freedom and how Taiwan has been an example to the world \u8230\'20\'26 Whether there are insecurities of the president of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/china"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 China}}}\uc2  relating to his own political situation I don\u8217\'20\'19t know.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Pelosi is in Taiwan for a controversial visit that has prompted a furious reaction from China, including planned missile tests and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/30/china-taiwan-military-exercises-nancy-pelosi-visit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 military \u8220\'20\'1Coperations\u8221\'20\'1D around the island,}}}\uc2  which Taiwan has said breach international law.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Why did she decide to visit? \u8220\'20\'1COur delegation came to Taiwan to make unequivocally clear we will not abandon Taiwan, and we are proud of our enduring friendship,\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What do Taiwanese Americans think of the media covering of her visit? To Taiwanese Americans, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/aug/02/taiwanese-americans-pelosi-visit-taiwan-china"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hyperbolic tenor of the debate}}}\uc2  over Pelosi\u8217\'20\'19s visit is indicative of how little most Americans know or care about the people of Taiwan, with one calling it \u8220\'20\'1Choopla and yellow journalism\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What is the Order of Propitious Clouds? Pelosi was given Taiwan\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/nancy-pelosis-taiwan-award-what-is-the-order-of-propitious-clouds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 highest civilian order}}}\uc2  during her visit to Taiwan, a \u8220\'20\'1Csymbol of America\u8217\'20\'19s strong and enduring friendship\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Biden\par \par \uc2 due to sign second executive order to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is expected to sign a second executive order on Wednesday that aims to protect access to reproductive healthcare after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  struck down the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Most significantly, the order directs the Health and Human Services (\uc2 HHS\uc2 ) agency to consider ways to expand coverage for patients traveling out of state for reproductive healthcare. Biden\u8217\'20\'19s order does not detail how this could be achieved; currently, government-subsidized Medicaid health insurance plans cover medically necessary abortions in only 16 states and do not reimburse patients who leave their state to seek an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A senior administration official told the Guardian that \uc2 HHS\uc2  would soon have more details on provisions to help women served by Medicaid health coverage cover certain costs of traveling for reproductive care.\par \par \uc2 Kansans secured a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/kansas-abortion-vote-state-constitution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 huge win for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights in the US}}}\uc2  last night when they voted to continue to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state constitution, while the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s Department of Justice is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/02/idaho-abortion-ban-justice-department-sues"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suing Idaho}}}\uc2  over the state\u8217\'20\'19s near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, due to take effect on 25 August.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Will the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access issue affect the mid\par \par \uc2 term elections? Possibly. The resounding win in Kansas came as a surprise in the deeply conservative state. The vote is viewed as a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/02/primaries-abortion-trump-arizona-missouri-michigan-kansas-washington-races"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 litmus test for the future of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access}}}\uc2  across the US.\par \par \uc2 How\par \par \uc2 Ayman al-Zawahiri\par \par \uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18pattern of life\u8217\'20\'19 allowed the US to kill al-Qaida leader\par \par \uc2 In the end it was one of the oldest mistakes in the fugitive\u8217\'20\'19s handbook that apparently did for Ayman al-Zawahiri, the top al-Qaida leader killed, according to US intelligence, by a drone strike on Sunday morning: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/aug/02/ayman-al-zawahiri-how-us-killed-al-qaida-leader"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he developed a habit}}}\uc2 , writes Ed Pilkington.\par \par \uc2 The co-planner of the 9/11 attacks on New York and Washington in 2001 had acquired a taste for sitting out on the balcony of his safe house in Sherpur, a well-to-do diplomatic enclave of Kabul. He grew especially fond of stepping out on to the balcony after morning prayers, so that he could watch the sun rise over the Afghan capital.\par \par \uc2 According to a US official who briefed reporters on Monday, it was such regular behavior that allowed intelligence agents, presumably CIA, to piece together what they called \u8220\'20\'1Ca pattern of life\u8221\'20\'1D of the target. That in turn allowed them to launch what the White House called a \u8220\'20\'1Ctailored airstrike\u8221\'20\'1D involving two Hellfire missiles fired from a Reaper drone that are claimed to have struck the balcony, with Zawahiri on it, at 6.18am on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 How have the families of\par \par \uc2 9/11 victims reacted? They have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/aug/02/ayman-al-zawahiri-reaction-9-11-families"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 celebrated Sunday\u8217\'20\'19s killing}}}\uc2  but they continued demanding accountability for the Saudi Arabian government\u8217\'20\'19s alleged role. The organization wrote that they have repeatedly requested meetings with the president about punishing the Saudi Arabia government for September 11, but Biden has refused to meet.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Russia has accused the White House of supplying target\par \par \uc2 ed information used by Kyiv to conduct long-range missile strikes. The country\u8217\'20\'19s defence ministry claimed Washington was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/aug/02/russia-claims-us-directly-involved-in-ukraine-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cdirectly involved\u8221\'20\'1D in the war}}}\uc2 , and had passed on intelligence that had led to the \u8220\'20\'1Cmass deaths of civilians\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Last year Cyber Ninjas, the firm overseeing the so-called audit into the 2020 election in Arizona, said it believed nearly 300 dead people may have voted. It turned out {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/02/investigation-finds-claim-300-dead-people-voted-arizona-2020-election-false"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not to be true}}}\uc2 . After investigating the allegations thoroughly, analysts found just one person who was actually dead at the time of the election.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tree enthusiasts who make the trek to the \u8220\'20\'1Cworld\u8217\'20\'19s tallest tree\u8221\'20\'1D, deep in a northern California forest, will face a fine and possible jail time after park officials declared the remote area off-limits\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/02/california-redwood-hyperion-worlds-tallest-tree"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 because of damage done}}}\uc2  by trampling visitors to the tree and surrounding forest, a park official said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In emotional testimony\par \par \uc2 on Tuesday, the father of a six-year-old victim of the Sandy Hook elementary school shooting said the rightwing conspiracy theorist {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/02/alex-jones-sandy-hook-shooting-hoax-claim-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alex Jones made his life a \u8220\'20\'1Cliving hell\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  by claiming the murders were a hoax involving actors and aimed at strengthening gun control.\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: \u8216\'20\'18Irredeemable\u8217\'20\'19 Batgirl movie among the most expensive cancelled cinematic projects ever\par \par \uc2 The previously announced Batgirl film starring Leslie Grace, Michael Keaton and Brendan Fraser {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2022/aug/03/irredeemable-batgirl-movie-unexpectedly-cancelled-despite-being-in-final-stages"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will not be released at all}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Warner Bros Discovery\uc2  has unexpectedly announced, despite the film being in post-production. The New York Post, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nypost.com/2022/08/02/batgirl-movie-gets-shelved-by-warner-bros-source/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 which broke the story on Tuesday}}}\uc2 , cited an unnamed source who said the budget had exceeded $100m and performed so poorly during early test screenings that \uc2 Warner Bros\uc2  decided to cut its losses. The decision means the film ranks among the most expensive cancelled cinematic projects ever.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: Why do men\u8217\'20\'19s paintings cost 10 times more than women\u8217\'20\'19s?\par \par \uc2 Are men 10 times better at painting than women? The market seems to think so. Helen Gorrill, the author of Women Can\u8217\'20\'19t Paint, has studied the prices of 5,000 paintings sold all over the world and found that for every \u163\'00\'A31 a male artist makes for his work, a woman makes a mere 10p. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/artanddesign/2022/aug/02/painting-gender-pay-gap-recalculating-art"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most shocking gender value gap}}}\uc2  that I\u8217\'20\'19ve come across in any industry at all,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. This is despite the fact that women have made up 70% of students in art college, selected on merit, and that the art world prides itself on its liberal, progressive values.\par \par \uc2 Climate check:\par \par \uc2 satellite images reveal shrinkage of Utah\u8217\'20\'19s Great Salt Lake\par \par \uc2 New satellite images from the \uc2 European Space Agency\uc2  have illustrated the extent of dwindling water levels in the Great Salt Lake in Utah, a month after it reached its lowest water level ever recorded. Highlighting falling water levels and the decreasing size of the lake, the report compares satellite images from 1985 and 2022. At its peak in the 1980s, it covered about 8,550 sq km (3,300 sq miles); in recent measurements, it has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/aug/02/satellite-images-reveal-shrinkage-of-utahs-great-salt-lake"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lost nearly half of its surface area}}}\uc2  from the historical average.\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: Bone App\u233\'00\'E9tit\par \par \uc2 \u8211\'20\'13 Jarlsberg cheese may help stave off osteoporosis\par \par \uc2 Eating Jarlsberg cheese may help to prevent bone thinning and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2022/aug/02/jarlsberg-cheese-may-help-stave-off-osteoporosis-small-study-suggests"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stave off osteoporosis}}}\uc2 , research suggests. Jarlsberg is a mild cheese made from cow\u8217\'20\'19s milk, with regular holes that mean it is classified as a Swiss-type cheese, although it originated in Norway. It is rich in vitamin K2, which has previously been found to improve bone health. The results of a study published in the journal BMJ Nutrition Prevention & Health suggest a daily portion could be beneficial to bone growth and regeneration.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220803ei83001xh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
