\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Kansas votes to protect  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights in state constitution\b0\par\par\uc2 Poppy Noor in Kansas City \par \uc2 850 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 August 2022\par 12:15 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Kansas is the first state to put \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to a vote since the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade\par \par \uc2 Kansans secured a huge win for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the US on Tuesday night when they voted to continue to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 The race was called by a host of US groups including NBC News, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  and Decision Desk HQ.\par \par \uc2 The move will be seen as huge a loss for the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement and a major win for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates across America, who will see the result as a bellwether for popular opinion.\par \par \uc2 Kansas \u8211\'20\'13 a deeply conservative and usually reliably Republican state \u8211\'20\'13 is the first US state to put \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to a vote since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  ruled to overturn constitutional protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in late June.\par \par \uc2 The state will remain a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2022/jun/28/tracking-where-abortion-laws-stand-in-every-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 safe haven for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  in the midwest}}}\uc2 , as one of the few states in the region where it remains legal to perform the procedure. Many other states have undertaken moves to make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  largely illegal since June.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  issued a statement welcoming the result. \u8220\'20\'1CThis vote makes clear what we know: the majority of Americans agree that women should have access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and should have the right to make their own healthcare decisions,\u8221\'20\'1D the US president said.\par \par \uc2 The Kansas state senator Dinah Sikes, a Democrat, cried as the vote came in, and turned to her friends and colleagues, showing them goosebumps on her arm.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s just amazing. It\u8217\'20\'19s breathtaking that women\u8217\'20\'19s voices were heard and we care about women\u8217\'20\'19s health,\u8221\'20\'1D she told the Guardian, after admitting she had thought the vote would be close. \u8220\'20\'1CBut we were close in a lot of rural areas and that really made the difference \u8211\'20\'13 I\u8217\'20\'19m just so grateful,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 The \u8220\'20\'1CNo\u8221\'20\'1D campaign \u8211\'20\'13 which was protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights \u8211\'20\'13 was strongly ahead in the referendum with 62% of the vote with the majority of ballots counted. That means millions of dollars lost for the Catholic church who contributed more than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://mediaassets.kshb.com/NWT/DAVID/valuethembothJuly2022.pdf?_ga=2.100872321.1653832198.1659365808-89616968.1659365808"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $3m}}}\uc2  trying to eradicate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in Kansas, according to campaign finance records.\par \par \uc2 Kansans turned out to vote in heavy numbers on Tuesday, in a referendum brought by the Kansas Republican legislature that was criticized for being misleading, fraught with misinformation and voter suppression tactics.\par \par \uc2 After failing to get a more directly named referendum, \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ballotpedia.org/Kansas_No_State_Constitutional_Right_to_Abortion_and_Legislative_Power_to_Regulate_Abortion_Amendment_(August_2022)"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kansas No State Constitutional Right to \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, on the ballot in 2020, Republicans switched tactics, naming this amendment \u8220\'20\'1CValue Them Both\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The vote was scheduled for August, when voter turnout is historically low, particularly among independents and Democrats, and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://sos.ks.gov/elections/22elec/2022-Primary-Election-Constitutional-Amendment-HCR-5003.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wording on the ballot paper }}}\uc2  was criticized for being unclear.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe ballot mentions a state constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funding in Kansas, but that funding has never really been on the table,\u8221\'20\'1D Mary Ziegler, a US \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law expert from the \uc2 University of California, Davis\uc2  told the Guardian on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/aug/01/kansas-abortion-vote-value-them-both-amendment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Monday}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Kansans for Life, one of the main backers for a yes vote, told church congregants on 27 July that removing protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Kansas would prevent late-term abortions, lack of parental consent and taxpayer funding for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , despite none of these being the law in Kansas. Abortions in Kansas are limited to 22 weeks in the cases of life threatening or severely compromised physical complications.\par \par \uc2 It was a tense and bitterly fought campaign that saw churches vandalized and yard signs stolen, in a state where the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doctor George Tiller was murdered by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists in 2009.\par \par \uc2 But on Tuesday night scenes of jubilation broke out at a watch party for the victorious No campaign in Kansas City. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re free!\u8221\'20\'1D shouted Mafutari Oneal, 56, who was working at the bar after the vote was called and a rush of drinks orders came in.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t want no government telling me what to do. I\u8217\'20\'19m so happy,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 In a speech just after victory was sealed, Rachel Sweet, the campaign manager for Kansans for Constitutional Freedom, said the win had come against all the odds.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe knew it was stacked against us from the moment we started but we did not despair \u8211\'20\'13 we did it, and these numbers speak for themselves,\u8221\'20\'1D Sweet said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe knocked tens of thousands of doors and had hundreds of thousands of phone calls \u8230\'20\'26 We countered millions of dollars in misinformation,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe will not tolerate extreme bans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in our state.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ashley All, the spokesperson for KCF, who led the no campaign alongside Planned Parenthood and the \uc2 ACLU\uc2 , told the Guardian that the key to driving voter turnout was not seeing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a partisan issue in Kansas.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe demonstrated Kansas\u8217\'20\'19 free state roots,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt will be interesting for other states to watch this and see this is not a partisan issue. Everyone from Republicans, to unaffiliated voters to hardcore libertarians came out to say: \u8216\'20\'18No, we don\u8217\'20\'19t want the government involved in what we do with our bodies\u8217\'20\'19.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220803ei83000gp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\pi