\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  access, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s sway and US democracy hang in balance in primaries\b0\par\par\uc2 Sam Levine in New York and Lauren Gambino in Washington \par \uc2 835 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 August 2022\par 11:37 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Kansas, Michigan, Missouri and Washington state vote with Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s ballot being the most closely watched\par \par \uc2 On one of the most consequential nights of this year\u8217\'20\'19s primary season, Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s sway in a series of Republican races remained unclear but voters in red-state Kansas resoundingly rejected an amendment aimed at restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday night\u8217\'20\'19s marquee races were in Arizona, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/01/arizona-republicans-kari-lake-mark-finchem"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 where Republicans are on the verge}}}\uc2  of tapping prominent election deniers to be their nominees in contests for governor, secretary of state and \uc2 US Senate\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the governor\u8217\'20\'19s race, Trump-backed Kari Lake, a former news anchor who has built her campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/10/16/politics/fact-check-kari-lake-arizona-governor-election-lies/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 around misinformation about the 2020 election}}}\uc2 , was trailing Karrin Taylor Robson, a wealthy real-estate developer who is endorsed by \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  and the current Arizona governor, \uc2 Doug Ducey\uc2 . The winner will take on \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2 , Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s current secretary of state, who was projected to win the Democratic gubernatorial nomination.\par \par \uc2 Down the ballot, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/feb/21/mark-finchem-trump-arizona-elections-secretary-of-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mark Finchem}}}\uc2 , a close ally of Trump who aggressively sought to overturn Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s election results, was on the verge of clinching the GOP nomination to be secretary of state in a four-way primary. Trump has endorsed Finchem in the contest, which typically gets little attention, boosting him to the front of the field.\par \par \uc2 If elected in November, Finchem would wield considerable power over elections in Arizona, including how ballots are counted and there is a loud alarm he could use that power to throw out an election result he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t like, especially given his efforts to overturn the results of the 2020 race.\par \par \uc2 Underscoring how deeply embedded Trump\u8217\'20\'19s election lies are among Republicans in Arizona, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/08/02/us/politics/arizona-trump-fake-electors.html?partner=slack&smid=sl-share"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times reported}}}\uc2  on Tuesday that two politicians involved in the efforts to overturn Biden\u8217\'20\'19s victory in the state worried the scheme could \u8220\'20\'1Cappear treasonous\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On the Democratic side, \uc2 Adrian Fontes\uc2 , the former top election official in Maricopa county, home to Phoenix, is vying for his party\u8217\'20\'19s nomination against Reginald Bolding, the minority leader in the Arizona house of representatives.\par \par \uc2 And in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  race, \uc2 Blake Masters\uc2 , who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/elections/2022/07/20/blake-masters-arizona-senate-trump/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has embraced}}}\uc2  extreme anti-immigrant positions and is backed by Trump and the tech billionaire \uc2 Peter Thiel\uc2 , is the frontrunner to win the GOP nomination. He will face Senator Mark Kelly this fall, who ran unopposed.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile in Kansas, a state that Trump won by nearly 15 points, voters defeated an amendment that would have paved the way for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions and delivered an energizing win for Democrats who face tough odds in the midterms.\par \par \uc2 The resounding win came as a surprise in a deeply conservative state. Republican lawmakers scheduled the vote during the partisan primaries thinking that low Democratic turnout would bolster their anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  cause, but the secretary of state, Scott Schwab, suggested that the massive voter turnout on Tuesday may match the turnout of the 2008 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 The vote is viewed as a litmus test for the future of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access across the US.\par \par \uc2 There is also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wmuk.org/wmuk-news/2022-07-29/michigans-3rd-district-gop-primary-meijer-vs-gibbs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a tight race}}}\uc2  in western Michigan, where the freshman congressman Peter Meijer is trying to fend off a challenge from John Gibbs, a former Trump administration official. \uc2 Meijer\uc2  was one of 10 House Republicans to back Trump\u8217\'20\'19s impeachment and Trump has backed Gibbs in an act of retribution. Whoever wins the district will be in a competitive race in November. Democrats have faced criticism in recent weeks for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/27/decmocrats-divided-michigan-effort-promote-election-denier-in-michigan-republican-primary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 trying to boost }}}\uc2  Gibbs, calculating that the more extreme candidate may be easier to beat in November.\par \par \uc2 Michigan Republicans nominated a conservative media commentator, Tudor Dixon, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/08/01/politics/trump-candidate-michigan-governor-primary/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who has falsely}}}\uc2  said Trump won the state in 2020 and earned a late endorsement from the former president. She will take on Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 , in November. Dixon emerged as the party\u8217\'20\'19s nominee after an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/07/26/gop-messiest-primary-michigan-00047790"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 extremely chaotic}}}\uc2  primary during which several candidates were disqualified and one was arrested for his involvement in the January 6 insurrection.\par \par \uc2 On the Democratic side, redistricting set two Democratic House incumbents against each other in Michigan. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/2022-primary-elections-house-representatives-a7d0e3032a2a4f6577a2dcddb375aab4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Andy Levin}}}\uc2 , a former president of his synagogue, was ultimately defeated by Haley Stevens, after a pro-Israel Super Pac funded ads attacking the former and amplifying the later. Levin has been critical of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s human rights record.\par \par \uc2 In Washington state, representatives \uc2 Jaime Herrera Beutler\uc2  and \uc2 Dan Newhouse\uc2 , both of whom voted to impeach Trump, are hoping to survive Trump-backed challengers.\par \par \uc2 In Missouri, \uc2 Eric Schmitt\uc2 , the state attorney general, prevailed in a competitive primary for an open \uc2 US Senate\uc2  seat. Schmitt trounced the state\u8217\'20\'19s scandal-plagued former governor, \uc2 Eric Greitens\uc2 , who was attempting a political comeback. Both vied for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement \u8211\'20\'13 and earned it \u8211\'20\'13 when the former president declined to choose between them. Instead Trump issued a statement on Monday announcing that he had endorsed \u8220\'20\'1CEric\u8221\'20\'1D but did not specify which one.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220802ei82003h3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichg