\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Justice department sues Idaho over state\u8217\'20\'19s near-total  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban\b0\par\par\uc2 Gloria Oladipo \par \uc2 298 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 August 2022\par 19:07 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Lawsuit is DoJ\u8217\'20\'19s first piece of litigation aimed at protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access since the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s Department of Justice is suing Idaho over the state\u8217\'20\'19s near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, set to take effect on 25 August.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit is the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s first piece of litigation aimed at protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  in June overturned the landmark Roe v Wade decision that established federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights nearly 50 years earlier.\par \par \uc2 During a press conference on Tuesday, the US attorney general, \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , announced the lawsuit alongside representatives from the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive rights taskforce.\par \par \uc2 Garland said Idaho\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban violates federal law which mandates that medical providers offer emergency care in the face of serious health consequences \u8211\'20\'13 not just in life-saving circumstances. The law makes no exceptions for abortions, regardless of what any state law says.\par \par \uc2 Under Idaho\u8217\'20\'19s law, abortions are only legal for victims of rape or incest as well as to save the life of a pregnant person. Doctors who do not provide sufficient evidence that an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was provided under those circumstances could face two to five years in prison and the forfeiture of their medical licenses.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe justice department is going to use every tool we have to ensure reproductive freedom,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/justice-department/justice-department-sues-idaho-abortion-ban-first-post-roe-litigation-rcna41174?cid=ed_npd_bn_tw_bn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Garland told reporters on Tuesday.}}}\par \par \uc2 More than half of US states have either banned or are expected to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision earlier this summer returned regulation of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the state level.\par \par \uc2 Bans like the one Idaho has imposed are forcing patients {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/25/us-abortion-bans-states-after-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seeking abortions to travel hundreds of miles from home}}}\uc2 , among other consequences.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220802ei820035z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
