\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Democracy runs through Arizona\u8217\'20\'19: candidate for attorney general says fate of the nation is at stake\b0\par\par\uc2 Nina Lakhani in Phoenix \par \uc2 1,480 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 August 2022\par 09:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Kris Mayes, a former Republican, says protecting democracy, the heating planet and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are urgent priorities\par \par \uc2 The future of American democracy could be determined by a handful of attorneys general, who will also play a crucial role in shielding women and doctors from draconian \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, according to the Democratic candidate for that office in Arizona.\par \par \uc2 Kris Mayes, 51, who switched parties in 2019 due to the expansion of Trumpism in the Republican party, is urging voters to take the attorney general and other down-ballot races like secretary of state seriously in the November midterms, or else risk losing US democracy altogether.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve never lived in a more dangerous time for our democracy. If we elect a couple of attorney generals who refuse to certify the 2024 elections, it essentially means our democracy is gone. It couldn\u8217\'20\'19t be more stark, so these elections really matter for the whole country,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mayes, in an interview with the Guardian at her Phoenix home.\par \par \uc2 In 2020, Trump pressured Republican officials to overturn Biden\u8217\'20\'19s victory in swing states including Arizona, where multiple investigations and lawsuits have ruled out fraud. Last week, House speaker \uc2 Rusty Bowers\uc2 , who testified in front of the January 6 congressional committee about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to force him and other local officials to overturn the results, was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.azfamily.com/2022/07/20/arizona-gop-censures-house-speaker-rusty-bowers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declared \u8220\'20\'1Cunfit to serve\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  by the state Republican party.\par \par \uc2 The sanction, which Mayes described as a \u8220\'20\'1Ctravesty\u8221\'20\'1D, reaffirmed her decision to leave the party.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was a lifelong Republican but the party left me and many moderates like me. We need a healthy two party system in this country, so it makes me really sad to see the party I once served has fallen this far and gotten this sick,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mayes, who grew up in a Republican family on a tree farm in Prescott about 90 miles north of Phoenix.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI appreciate those Republicans who have stayed to fight for democracy and our party, but ultimately I couldn\u8217\'20\'19t be a part of it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Arizona is among 33 states and US territories electing an attorney general in November \u8211\'20\'13 who as the top lawyer and top law enforcement officer plays a crucial role in the election process, including certification and preventing voter suppression.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/opa/pr/justice-department-files-lawsuit-against-state-arizona-over-restrictive-voter-registration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Department of Justice is suing Arizona }}}\uc2  over its latest voter restrictions, while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/2022-midterm-elections-arizona-presidential-government-and-politics-72711f64251e13693da72b8602339fca"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans recently tried (and failed) }}}\uc2  to ban mail voting for the midterms, even though the vast majority of Arizonans use vote-by-mail.\par \par \uc2 Mayes, who filed an amicus brief opposing the ban, said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have incredibly well-run, safe elections yet the Republican party continues to perpetuate the big lie. There\u8217\'20\'19s been a very clear trend to curtail voting rights and as attorney general I will use my bully pulpit and the courts to fight those efforts.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mayes\u8217\'20\'19 opponent will be decided in next week\u8217\'20\'19s primary, with the six Republican candidates vying for the nomination each having made border security and election integrity central to their platforms.\par \par \uc2 But it\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that has brought increased scrutiny to the attorney general race since the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade and handed back power to the states.\par \par \uc2 Shortly after, \uc2 Mark Brnovich\uc2 , the outgoing attorney general and senate candidate, tried {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://kjzz.org/content/1795171/brnovich-files-motion-allowing-charges-against-doctors-who-do-abortions-what-could"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to revive a statute from Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s territorial days}}}\uc2  that bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in almost all circumstances. The courts will decide whether this draconian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.azmirror.com/blog/ag-says-arizona-territorial-ban-on-abortion-now-law-of-the-land/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 1864 law is revived or}}}\uc2  new legislation banning terminations after 15 weeks comes into force in September. The law, which was signed in May, has no exceptions for rape or incest. In addition, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.azcentral.com/story/news/politics/arizona/2021/04/27/arizona-anti-abortion-bill-becomes-law/4855859001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2021 so-called personhood law}}}\uc2  that would provide rights to foetuses {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.azcentral.com/story/news/politics/arizona/2022/07/08/arizona-abortion-personhood-law-fetus-court-attorney-general-arguments/10014944002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 faces a court challenge}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As it stands, it\u8217\'20\'19s a legal mess.\par \par \uc2 Still, the Republican candidates have all indicated that they would enforce whichever restrictive law the courts decide takes precedence, whereas Mayes says she considers all three to be unconstitutional.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnlike the federal constitution under which Roe sat, the right to privacy in the Arizona state constitution is broad and explicit, which protects a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose and reproductive freedom. As attorney general I should not and will not enforce laws I believe are unconstitutional and therefore will not prosecute any woman, doctor, midwife, pharmacist under these laws.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think our founding fathers would be appalled by these laws,\u8221\'20\'1D added Mayes, who can use her supervisory authority over county attorneys to advise them that prosecutions would be unconstitutional.\par \par \uc2 Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s constitution is one of the most individually oriented in the country, but if Mayes wins, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will almost certainly end up in the state supreme court \u8211\'20\'13 which the outgoing governor \uc2 Doug Ducey\uc2  has packed with a conservative super majority.\par \par \uc2 Ultimately, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates will probably attempt to give Arizonans the final say through a ballot initiative, though recent changes by the Republican controlled legislature has made this harder. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://kjzz.org/content/1796549/abortion-ruling-puts-new-focus-arizonas-attorney-general-race"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Almost nine out of 10 Arizonans}}}\uc2  want \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to remain legal at least in some circumstances.\par \par \uc2 Mayes said: \u8220\'20\'1CRepublican leaders are in a race to bottom to satisfy a base which doesn\u8217\'20\'19t represent many moderate Republicans or independents who are repulsed by the criminalization of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has endorsed a bunch of big lie proponents in the state including attorney general hopeful Abe Hamadeh, 31, the son of Syrian immigrants and former Maricopa county prosecutor, who has indicated that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.azcentral.com/story/news/politics/elections/2022/07/10/arizona-attorney-general-candidates-share-their-stances-abortion/7706590001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he supports the pre-statehood \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  law}}}\uc2 , describes the humanitarian crisis at the border as an \u8220\'20\'1Cinvasion\u8221\'20\'1D and does not {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.azcentral.com/story/news/politics/elections/2022/07/06/abe-hamadeh-arizona-attorney-general-primary-2022-candidate/9747331002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 believe Biden won the 2020 election}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s office has been held by a Republican for the past decade, but Mayes says she doesn\u8217\'20\'19t fear any of the candidates. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re all the same \u8211\'20\'13 all six have said they would not have certified the 2020 election and to a person they seem almost giddy about prosecuting women and doctors after the fall of Roe. I know Arizonans are going to reject this brand of anti-democratic and anti-woman Republicanism.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mayes says she will use the state\u8217\'20\'19s $5bn surplus to target the huge explosion of fentanyl trafficking into the state, which mostly arrives from Mexico through legal points of entry, but is otherwise light on details about the southern border.\par \par \uc2 Unlike most of the Republican candidates, Mayes does not have experience in the criminal justice system, but argues that her background in environmental law and consumer protection makes her uniquely qualified to tackle the state\u8217\'20\'19s climate challenges.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are in the midst of an epic drought, escalating heat and dwindling water supplies. This is an all hands on deck moment if we are to survive as a state. There\u8217\'20\'19s a lot the attorney general could do and hasn\u8217\'20\'19t \u8230\'20\'26 we can\u8217\'20\'19t wait for the next generation to solve this,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mayes, who has worked as a senior sustainability scientist at \uc2 Arizona State University (ASU) \uc2 since 2010.\par \par \uc2 Before entering academia, Mayes served for seven years as a Republican on the \uc2 Arizona Corporation Commission\uc2  (ACC), a quasi-executive regulatory agency for utilities including energy and water which also oversees securities regulation and pipeline safety. Before that, she was a political reporter in Arizona.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHaving been a journalist made me a great corporation commissioner and will make me a great attorney general, because these jobs are all about asking tough questions of powerful entities and people, getting at the truth and following that wherever it leads you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mayes has been endorsed by a slew of local Democrats, the president of the Navajo nation, Planned Parenthood and the environmental group \uc2 the Sierra Club\uc2 . She\u8217\'20\'19s very much a moderate Democrat and hopes that her track record as a moderate and pragmatic Republican \u8211\'20\'13 and her reasons for leaving the party \u8211\'20\'13 will persuade the state\u8217\'20\'19s large number of independents and enough Republicans to vote for her.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.azmirror.com/2022/06/06/arizonas-independents-are-largely-powerless-in-primary-elections/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A third of the electorate }}}\uc2  is made up of independent or \u8220\'20\'1Cother\u8221\'20\'1D voters that aren\u8217\'20\'19t registered to a major political party. \u8220\'20\'1CI think that many Republicans identify with my journey \u8211\'20\'13 I\u8217\'20\'19m reaching out to them actively.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As a single mother to a nine-year-old daughter and an openly gay woman in an increasingly hostile political environment for LGBTQ communities, Mayes says her decision to re-enter politics was not an easy one. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think it\u8217\'20\'19s too much to say that American democracy runs through the state of Arizona in 2022, and whether or not we can preserve it may depend on what happens in down-ballot races like mine.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This article was amended on 29 July 2022. We misquoted Mayes referring to the certification of the \u8220\'20\'1C2022 election\u8221\'20\'1D; she was speaking about the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 This reporting was supported by the International Women\u8217\'20\'19s Media Foundation\u8217\'20\'19s Reproductive Health, Rights, and Justice in the Americas Initiative\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220802ei82002v7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
