\par\par \uc2 Law\par \b \uc2 Bloodied but unbowed: liberal justices wield dissents as weapon of resistance\b0\par\par\uc2 Ed Pilkington \par \uc2 1,650 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 August 2022\par 06:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The three justices may be in the minority, but their opinions are sounding an alarm that equal rights are under threat by the new rightwing supermajority of the supreme court\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 , with its new rightwing supermajority, is transforming America at breakneck speed. In a single judicial year, it overturned the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , unleashed legally carried guns on to city streets, stymied government action to combat the climate crisis and Covid pandemic, and took a hatchet to the time-honored separation of church and state.\par \par \uc2 Seasoned observers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/steve_vladeck/status/1542530788851437573"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 described the 2021-22 term}}}\uc2  that ended in June as perhaps the most momentous in the court\u8217\'20\'19s 233-year history. The six rightwing justices \u8211\'20\'13 three of them appointed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 demonstrated an iron grip over blockbuster cases.\par \par \uc2 The three liberal-leaning justices, by equal measure \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Stephen Breyer\uc2 , Elena Kagan and \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 were outnumbered and bloodied. When the court reconvenes in October, the retired Breyer will be replaced by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ketanji-brown-jackson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ketanji Brown Jackson}}}\uc2 , but the same punishing 6-to-3 dynamic will prevail.\par \par \uc2 Bloodied but unbowed. The three liberal justices may be in the minority, but they are fast emerging as a vital resistance to the Trump-instigated judicial revolution now under way.\par \par \uc2 That resistance is reflected in the dissenting opinions produced by the three. Not only were liberal dissents more in evidence in 2021-22 \u8211\'20\'13 Sotomayor alone {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.scotusblog.com/2022/07/as-unanimity-declines-conservative-majoritys-power-runs-deeper-than-the-blockbuster-cases/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote 13}}}\uc2 , more than she has in any previous term \u8211\'20\'13 but the language deployed in them was also direct and unrestrained.\par \par \uc2 The dissents went beyond polite disagreements over jurisprudence. They amounted to the sounding of an alarm, alerting the nation that equal rights, constitutional government, and even what it is to be an American, are all under threat.\par \par \uc2 Here are six of the most visceral warnings contained in the dissents of the three liberal-leaning justices.\par \par \uc2 1. Attacking equal rights and individual freedoms\par \par \uc2 Over 60 white-hot pages of dissent, Breyer, Sotomayor and Kagan tore into the majority ruling in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/21pdf/19-1392_6j37.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dobbs v Jackson}}}\uc2  that overturned the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Pointing out that such a right had been the law of the land for half a century, they decried the ruling as a full-on attack on an individual\u8217\'20\'19s freedom.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAfter today, young women will come of age with fewer rights than their mothers and grandmothers had,\u8221\'20\'1D the dissenting opinion said. From the moment of fertilization, \u8220\'20\'1Ca woman has no rights to speak of\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The decision struck at the core of American values, they said. Individual freedom and equal rights \u8220\'20\'1Chave gone far toward defining what it means to be an American. For in this nation, we do not believe that a government controlling all private choices is compatible with a free people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 2. Overriding the will of Congress and that of the American people\par \par \uc2 The ultimate source of power in the United States is \u8220\'20\'1Cwe the people\u8221\'20\'1D. Today there are 240 million citizens eligible to vote for their representatives in Congress and president.\par \par \uc2 And then there are the five men and one woman who control the supreme court and who are busily changing the face of America.\par \par \uc2 The liberal-leaning justices accuse their rightwing peers of supplanting their own will over that of \u8220\'20\'1Cwe the people\u8221\'20\'1D. Kagan wrote the dissent to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/21pdf/20-1530_n758.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 West Virginia v EPA}}}\uc2 , the majority ruling which hobbled the power of the \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency\uc2  (\uc2 EPA\uc2 ) to tackle the climate crisis by regulating fossil-fueled power plants.\par \par \uc2 Kagan charges the six rightwing justices of ignoring clear instructions given to the \uc2 EPA\uc2  by Congress to address the \u8220\'20\'1Cpotentially catastrophic harms\u8221\'20\'1D of global heating. The justices had in effect rewritten the Clean Air Act in favour of their own policymaking.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe court appoints itself \u8211\'20\'13 instead of Congress or the expert agency \u8211\'20\'13 the decisionmaker on climate policy. I cannot think of many things more frightening,\u8221\'20\'1D Kagan said.\par \par \uc2 In a separate 6-to-3 ruling, the supermajority {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jan/13/biden-military-covid-omicron-spike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s requirement}}}\uc2  that employees of large businesses vaccinate themselves against Covid or take weekly tests. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/21pdf/21a244_hgci.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dissenting opinion}}}\uc2  from all three liberal justices said that, here too, the majority had negated the will of the people as expressed in the 1970 law that commanded the \uc2 Occupational Safety and Health Administration (Osha) \uc2 to protect workers \u8220\'20\'1Cexposed to grave danger\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On the one hand, the dissent said, there is the Osha trying to protect employees from the \u8220\'20\'1Cgrave danger\u8221\'20\'1D of Covid. The agency is responsible to the president, who in turn \u8220\'20\'1Cis responsible to \u8211\'20\'13 and can be held to account by \u8211\'20\'13 the American public\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, there is the supreme court. \u8220\'20\'1CIts members,\u8221\'20\'1D the dissenters noted acerbically, \u8220\'20\'1Care elected by, and accountable to, no one\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 3. Undermining the integrity of the s\par \par \uc2 upreme c\par \par \uc2 ourt and the rule of law\par \par \uc2 The liberal-leaning justices accuse the supermajority of abandoning long-held legal principles in their rush towards radical change. Foremost of these is \u8220\'20\'1Cstare decisis\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Cto stand by things decided\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a respect for past precedents set by the court.\par \par \uc2 By throwing out the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  established in 1973 by Roe v Wade, the six rightwing justices had disregarded stare decisis, and shown that \u8220\'20\'1Ctoday, the proclivities of individuals rule. The court departs from its obligation to faithfully and impartially apply the law,\u8221\'20\'1D Breyer, Sotomayor and Kagan wrote.\par \par \uc2 The rightwing justices are very sensitive to the suggestion that they are acting according to political whim rather than legal principle. Last September, \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , arguably the de facto leader of the new supermajority, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.southbendtribune.com/story/news/2021/09/17/notre-dame-clarence-thomas-supreme-court-justice-lecture-south-bend-indiana/8370397002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 irritably denied}}}\uc2  the claim.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe media makes it sound as though you are just always going right to your personal preference,\u8221\'20\'1D he bemoaned.\par \par \uc2 He need not look to the media for such an accusation. Three of his fellow justices have expressed it forcefully.\par \par \uc2 In their dissenting opinion in Dobbs, the liberal justices noted that it took less than two years following the appointment of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s third pick, \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett\uc2 , for the court to overthrow Roe v Wade. Such a rapid shift, they argued, could not be explained by any change in the social landscape of the country.\par \par \uc2 The only thing that had changed was the composition of the court, and with it \u8220\'20\'1Cthe new views of new judges. The majority has overruled Roe for one and only one reason: because it has always despised them, and now has the votes to discard them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The consequences of the highest court being seen to be swayed by personal biases rather than legal principles are potentially cataclysmic. \u8220\'20\'1CIt undermines the court\u8217\'20\'19s legitimacy,\u8221\'20\'1D the dissenters warned.\par \par \uc2 4. One law for the rich, another for the poor\par \par \uc2 In their Dobbs dissent the three justices spell out the impact of ending of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights for women of contrasting means. Wealthy women will \u8220\'20\'1Cfind ways around a state\u8217\'20\'19s assertion of power\u8221\'20\'1D, travelling out of states that ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to those where it is legal.\par \par \uc2 Other women without the resources \u8220\'20\'1Cwill not be so fortunate\u8221\'20\'1D. They might resort to an illegal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and be harmed \u8220\'20\'1Cor even die\u8221\'20\'1D; they might give birth to the child at great cost to themselves and their families; \u8220\'20\'1Cat the least, they will incur the cost of losing control over their lives\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The dissenters warned that the consequences go beyond the devastating impact on individual women. A central pillar of the US constitution, of American values, has also been destroyed \u8211\'20\'13 equal protection under the laws.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe constitution will, today\u8217\'20\'19s majority holds, provide no shield, despite its guarantees of liberty and equality for all.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 5.\par \par \uc2 Turning the clock back to the 18th\par \par \uc2 century\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/21pdf/20-843_7j80.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York State Rifle & Pistol Association v Bruen}}}\uc2 , the supermajority threw out New York\u8217\'20\'19s restricted licensing regime for firearms, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/23/us-supreme-court-new-york-law-gun-control"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opening the door}}}\uc2  to concealed and loaded handguns being carried publicly in US cities.\par \par \uc2 Thomas, who wrote the ruling, rejected any argument relating to the dangers posed by guns in modern America, where gun violence far exceeds that in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/graphics/2022-us-gun-violence-world-comparison/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 comparable countries}}}\uc2 . Instead, he argued that licensing regimes had to be consistent with \u8220\'20\'1Cthis nation\u8217\'20\'19s historical tradition of firearm regulation\u8221\'20\'1D and specifically with the way the US ruled in 1791 when the second amendment right to bear arms was ratified.\par \par \uc2 In his dissent, Breyer said that this \u8220\'20\'1Chistory-only approach\u8221\'20\'1D not only ignored the \u8220\'20\'1Creal and present danger of guns in modern American society\u8221\'20\'1D, it set a framework that was so rigid it would be impossible to apply to modern situations \u8220\'20\'1Cbeyond the Framers\u8217\'20\'19 imaginations\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 How, for instance, could centuries-old laws \u8220\'20\'1Cdictate the legality of regulations targeting \u8216\'20\'18ghost guns\u8217\'20\'19 constructed with the aid of a three-dimensional printer?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 6. This is just the beginning\par \par \uc2 Perhaps the most chilling warning given by the liberal justices is that the hurricane of contentious rulings issued by the supermajority this term is not the end of the revolution \u8211\'20\'13 it is just the beginning.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo one should be confident that this majority is done with its work,\u8221\'20\'1D they write in their Dobbs dissent.\par \par \uc2 The supermajority could go on to ban all abortions nationwide, from the moment of conception and with no exemptions for rape or incest. They could also use exactly the same arguments deployed to overturn Roe to go after contraception, the right to same-sex intimacy and marriage, and even interracial marriage.\par \par \uc2 The logical conclusion of the supermajority\u8217\'20\'19s legal tactics is that \u8220\'20\'1Call rights that have no history stretching back to the mid-19th century are insecure \u8230\'20\'26 Additional constitutional rights are under threat.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sotomayor closed her dissent in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/21pdf/20-1088_dbfi.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Carson v Makin}}}\uc2  on a profoundly disturbing note. The 6-to-3 ruling bulldozed decades of precedent on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/jul/02/us-supreme-court-religion-church-state-separation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 separation of church and state}}}\uc2  by insisting that Maine had to extend its taxpayer-funded tuition assistance program to include students attending religious schools.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith growing concern for where this court will lead us next,\u8221\'20\'1D Sotomayor wrote, \u8220\'20\'1CI respectfully dissent.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220802ei82000ry\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
