\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Yes, Republicans really did try to make  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  punishable by death\b0\par\par\uc2 Arwa Mahdawi \par \uc2 1,242 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 August 2022\par 18:23 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 A bill introduced in the North Carolina legislature last year was largely performative but was part of the right\u8217\'20\'19s strategy to make the unthinkable mainstream\par \par \uc2 Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  zealots want to legalize murder\par \par \uc2 Is it legal to kill someone who is about to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ? I know that sounds like a ridiculous question, but some people on the far right would like it to be. Social media was recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://factcheck.afp.com/doc.afp.com.32EX3VW"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 awash with outrage}}}\uc2  over a bill introduced by North Carolina state legislators that would legalize violence against anyone undergoing or performing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://web.archive.org/web/20220710020606/https:/webservices.ncleg.gov/ViewBillDocument/2021/661/0/DRH40068-MLy-38A"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 North Carolina House Bill (HB) 158}}}\uc2 , sponsored by a Republican state representative, Larry Pittman, proposed that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  be considered first-degree murder and would have allowed civilians to use deadly force to prevent someone from ending a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 While this is clearly terrifying, it should be noted that a lot of discussion circulating about the bill online wasn\u8217\'20\'19t accurate: the outrage was sparked by a somewhat misleading post that made it look like the bill was actively being considered. In fact, however, HB 158 was introduced in February 2021 and didn\u8217\'20\'19t advance out of committee. An {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://factcheck.afp.com/doc.afp.com.32EX3VW"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AFP fact check}}}\uc2  also notes that it received little support from legislators.\par \par \uc2 Still, even though the bill was largely performative, that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean it shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be taken seriously. The far right constantly introduce extreme bills like this into state legislatures with the full knowledge that there is zero chance they will pass. It\u8217\'20\'19s part of a broader strategy to further their agenda that can be summed up as exhaust and inure. Exhaust : the more they overwhelm legislatures with extreme legislation, the harder it becomes for liberals to fight them. It becomes a game of \u8220\'20\'1CWhac-a-Mole\u8221\'20\'1D. Inure: proposing extreme ideas like this via legislation helps gradually desensitize people and shifts the Overton window to the right; step by step the unthinkable becomes mainstream.\par \par \uc2 All this isn\u8217\'20\'19t just my personal opinion, by the way: it\u8217\'20\'19s extracted from a playbook written by Christian nationalists. A few years ago a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://religiondispatches.org/project-blitz-seeks-to-do-for-christian-nationalism-what-alec-does-for-big-business/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 researcher called Frederick Clarkson}}}\uc2  uncovered an initiative from a coalition of far-right Christian groups called Project Blitz that gave their supporters detailed instructions on how to codify their views into law and gradually destroy the division between church and state. I highly recommend reading Clarkson\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://religiondispatches.org/project-blitz-seeks-to-do-for-christian-nationalism-what-alec-does-for-big-business/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writings}}}\uc2  on Project Blitz: they are essential for understanding the current moment. As Clarkson said when he first found the playbook: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s very rare that you come across a major primary source document that changes the way you view everything, and this is one of those times. This is a 116-page strategy manual hidden away on a website explaining at least what a section of the religious right are doing in the United States.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bills like the one in North Carolina, it can\u8217\'20\'19t be stressed enough, are not just frivolous one-offs by extremists. They\u8217\'20\'19re part of a coordinated \u8211\'20\'13 and highly effective \u8211\'20\'13 strategy to consolidate power by the right. Democrats should really be paying more attention to these tactics and learning from them. So many centrists are afraid that suggesting things like free healthcare will make them look like radicals hellbent on bringing communism to America. You think the right care about looking \u8220\'20\'1Cradical\u8221\'20\'1D? Of course not. They care about power. And they\u8217\'20\'19re very good at doing whatever it takes to get it.\par \par \uc2 South Carolina bill outlaws websites explaining how to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Want another example of that \u8220\'20\'1CWhac-a-Mole\u8221\'20\'1D strategy in action? South Carolina state senators {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/technology/2022/07/22/south-carolina-bill-abortion-websites/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently introduced legislation}}}\uc2  that would make it illegal to host a website or \u8220\'20\'1C[provide] an internet service\u8221\'20\'1D with information that is \u8220\'20\'1Creasonably likely to be used for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D. This is incredibly far-reaching language that means even news stories related to reproductive rights could be censored. This bill is unconstitutional and it\u8217\'20\'19s not clear that it will be law anytime soon. But, again, that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t make it any less worrying. As one expert told the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CThese are not going to be one-offs. These are going to be laws that spread like wildfire through states that have shown hostility to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A 99-year-old\u8217\'20\'19s dying wish was for a giant penis statue over her grave\par \par \uc2 I would describe this as a snippet of much-needed light news, but there is nothing light about the penis and testicles that now sit on top of Catarina Ordu\u241\'00\'F1a P\u233\'00\'E9rez\u8217\'20\'19s grave: they weigh nearly 600 pounds. The statue is also five-a-half-foot tall. \u8220\'20\'1CShe told me that [the statue] was her desire so that no one would forget her and that everything we loved about her would be remembered more easily,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vice.com/en/article/wxnnqw/mexico-dick-tombstone?"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 P\u233\'00\'E9rez\u8217\'20\'19s grandson told Vice}}}\uc2 . A legend.\par \par \uc2 Shireen Abu Akleh\u8217\'20\'19s family demand US action\par \par \uc2 It has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/may/17/shireen-abu-aqleh-was-a-lifeline-for-palestinians-and-her-killing-has-shaken-us-to-the-core"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 over two months}}}\uc2  now since the Palestinian American journalist was killed while covering a military raid in the occupied West Bank. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2022/06/24/israel-un-shireen-american-journalist/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UN rights body investigation}}}\uc2  found that the shot that killed Abu Akleh came from Israeli security forces, echoing eyewitness accounts of the shooting and analysis by other rights groups. Still, the US seems to have no desire to ensure there is accountability for her death; the journalist\u8217\'20\'19s family travelled to Washington to beg the secretary of state, \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 , to do something this week and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/07/28/shireen-abu-akleh-palestinian-journalist-killed-00048582"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he fobbed them off}}}\uc2 . If Abu Akleh had been murdered in Ukraine by Russian forces, I think the US response would be rather different. When journalists are killed by US allies (Jamal Khashoggi comes to mind), the US seems to rather relax its concerns about things like human rights and accountability.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I will never regret the time I spent with my children, but society is punishing me for it in my 60s\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPrecarity can happen so easily to anyone,\u8221\'20\'1D writes Louise Ihlein in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/jul/26/i-will-never-regret-the-time-i-spent-with-my-children-but-society-is-punishing-me-for-it-in-my-60s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 powerful piece in the Guardian}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1C[B]ut it happens a lot to women who have spent their lives caring for others.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Being a woman in Afghanistan has become \u8216\'20\'18death in slow motion\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 A chilling new report released by \uc2 Amnesty International\uc2  documents how the rights of women and girls in Afghanistan have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/sections/goatsandsoda/2022/07/27/1114033369/what-its-like-being-a-woman-in-afghanistan-today-death-in-slow-motion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cdecimated by the Taliban\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  in less than a year. Child marriage has surged and safeguards protecting women have collapsed.\par \par \uc2 Lebanese politician says used condoms were left in her office by male colleagues\par \par \uc2 Amnesty International\uc2  has condemned the sexist harassment of a newly elected female MP in Lebanon, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://english.alaraby.co.uk/news/amnesty-slams-lebanon-parliament-over-harassment-woman-mp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cynthia Zarazir}}}\uc2 . The legislator spoke out on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  about being catcalled and bullied, saying her colleagues gave her a filthy office full of pornographic magazines and condoms. \u8220\'20\'1CIf this is how they treat an elected fellow MP, how will they deal with those who are voiceless?\u8221\'20\'1D she tweeted.\par \par \uc2 The week in pawtriarchy\par \par \uc2 A group of roaming macaque monkeys have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/city-in-japan-under-siege-by-marauding-monkeys-180980493/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 terrorizing a southern Japanese city}}}\uc2  in recent weeks, attacking more than 50 individuals. Most of the victims have been children and women (who knew macaques could be so misogynistic?!) but it seems attacks on men are on the rise. \u8220\'20\'1CI have never seen anything like this my entire life,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/japan-monkey-attacks-97f8e316daa48d6f5a6fb43632d1353e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one city official said}}}\uc2 . Like many other things unfolding right now, the wild monkey attacks are unprecedented. What I would give to live in precedented times.\par \par \uc2 Arwa Mahdawi\u8217\'20\'19s new book, Strong Female Lead, is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://linktr.ee/ARWAMAHDAWI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 available for order}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220730ei7u001p6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
