\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I\u8217\'20\'19m not a radical\u8217\'20\'19: Kansas split ahead of critical post-Roe  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  vote\b0\par\par\uc2 Poppy Noor in Kansas City \par \uc2 1,338 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 August 2022\par 15:42 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s vote seeks to overturn state constitutional rights in a midwest \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  haven \u8211\'20\'13 which way will it go?\par \par \uc2 On 13 July, Sarah McGinnity, 39, sat down with her mother, 67, and six-year-old daughter and carefully wrote postcards to people she\u8217\'20\'19d never met.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDear voter, it will take all of us to protect reproductive rights in Kansas,\u8221\'20\'1D they read.\par \par \uc2 She sent the cards to voters in rural Kansas before a referendum on Tuesday, the first in the country to put \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights on the ballot since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the overturning}}}\uc2  in June of the landmark 1973 Roe v Wade ruling that secured federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI never in my life thought I\u8217\'20\'19d be doing that,\u8221\'20\'1D said McGinnity, a business owner from Overland Park, who was not always pro-choice.\par \par \uc2 McGinnity grew up in a Republican household and never discussed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  with her parents until recently.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut [for my Mom], to think of her granddaughter having fewer rights than she did \u8211\'20\'13 rights she thought had already been secured \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s pretty shocking,\u8221\'20\'1D McGinnity said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal in Kansas, but Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s vote, confusingly called the Value Them Both Amendment, seeks to overturn a 2019 Kansas supreme court decision, which ruled that the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution includes a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It represents the legislature\u8217\'20\'19s second shot at a referendum \u8211\'20\'13 in 2020, a more directly named amendment, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ballotpedia.org/Kansas_No_State_Constitutional_Right_to_Abortion_and_Legislative_Power_to_Regulate_Abortion_Amendment_(August_2022)"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kansas No State Constitutional Right to \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , failed to get on the ballot.\par \par \uc2 The vote could be a litmus test on public opinion, and will be watched by legislators looking to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in places like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.spotlightpa.org/news/2022/07/pa-abortion-restrictions-constitutional-amendment-voter-id/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pennsylvania}}}\uc2 , and to protect rights in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.freep.com/story/news/politics/2022/07/11/voters-abortion-michigan-ballot/10007016002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michigan}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://legislature.vermont.gov/Documents/2022/Docs/BILLS/PR0005/PR0005%20As%20adopted%20by%20the%20Senate%20Official.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vermont}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gov.ca.gov/2022/06/27/as-abortion-rights-constitutional-amendment-heads-to-ballot-governor-newsom-takes-additional-new-action-to-protect-women-and-providers-in-california/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 California}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Kansas has become a safe haven for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the midwest recently, as many surrounding states have banned the procedure since Roe was overturned. A yes vote to overturn state protections would be far-reaching.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CKansas has an opportunity to model what should happen for the rest of the nation,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jonathan McRoy, a 38-year-old military veteran from Wichita who supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m an outlier as a Black veteran and a progressive in the veteran community, but as someone who has pledged my life for the constitution, I\u8217\'20\'19m compelled to take action.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Millions of dollars have been donated on both sides, in a tense election that has seen yard signs stolen and churches vandalized. That hostility is not taken lightly in a state where an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doctor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global/2009/jul/29/george-tiller-abortion-doctor-shot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was murdered in 2009}}}\uc2  by an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activist.\par \par \uc2 At the Church of the Ascenscion in Overland Park, graffiti reading \u8220\'20\'1CMy body, my choice\u8221\'20\'1D has now been scrubbed clean. The church \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://account.kansascity.com/paywall/stop?resume=263336798"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 which donated thousands to the yes campaign}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 has several purple yes signs adorning its manicured lawns. Millions have poured into the \u8220\'20\'1Cyes\u8221\'20\'1D vote from the Catholic Archdiocese in Kansas, which raised more than $3m for the Value them Both coalition in 2022 according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://mediaassets.kshb.com/NWT/DAVID/valuethembothJuly2022.pdf?_ga=2.100872321.1653832198.1659365808-89616968.1659365808"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 campaign finance reports}}}\uc2 . Meanwhile, the \uc2 ACLU\uc2  and Planned Parenthood are the \u8220\'20\'1Cno\u8221\'20\'1D campaign\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://mediaassets.kshb.com/NWT/KansansFOrConstitutionalFreedomJuly2022.pdf?_ga=2.100872321.1653832198.1659365808-89616968.1659365808"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 biggest funders}}}\uc2 , contributing over $2m in 2022.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not a radical. I hate the ugly tactics on both sides,\u8221\'20\'1D said Christy McNally, 68, from Stillwell, who is voting yes to overturning the state constitutional protection. She believes abortions should be allowed in medical emergencies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut a medical emergency is not the same as using \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as birth control,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Marisel Walston, 56, a paralegal in Lenexa, stood proudly with her yes sign. She arrived from Cuba aged 14, fleeing communism.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe judges decided there was a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and I feel that\u8217\'20\'19s a pretty big stretch \u8230\'20\'26 It should be up to the people to decide,\u8221\'20\'1D said Walston.\par \par \uc2 Walston chairs the Johnson county Republican party. The party estimates the yes vote is ahead, but when campaigning on doorsteps \u8220\'20\'1Cit\u8217\'20\'19s fairly divided\u8221\'20\'1D, she said.\par \par \uc2 Quinn Patel, 19, also from Lenexa, will vote no, which means supporting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections, with his parents and sister on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 His mostly male social circle is following suit. \u8220\'20\'1CWe recognize this is something women should have a right to choose on,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Seth Simmons, a 37-year-old pharmaceutical worker, would support a total ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although he said that was not the aim of the amendment.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://kansasreflector.com/2022/07/15/kansas-abortion-ban-is-the-plan-officials-pushing-constitutional-amendment-tell-gop-crowd/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Regional directors at the Value them Both}}}\uc2  coalition have previously said it has pre-written legislation ready to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Kansas if they secure a yes vote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor me, it comes down to equal protection under the law for the unborn. They are humans, they have the same rights as the rest of us, and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is murder,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Republican lawmakers have been accused of setting out to confuse people and suppress votes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe ballot mentions a state constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funding in Kansas, but that funding has never really been on the table,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mary Ziegler, a US \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law expert from the \uc2 University of California, Davis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHistorically, in Kansas primaries, turnout is lower for Democrats and Independents \u8230\'20\'26 so the timing was probably designed to give the yes vote a boost,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Will the result accurately reflect Kansans\u8217\'20\'19 beliefs?\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn 2021, 60% of Kansas voters said they {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cjonline.com/story/news/politics/elections/2022/02/22/poll-shows-kansas-residents-skeptical-banning-abortion-all-cases/6878658001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 did not want an absolute ban on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 . So I would think that most Kansas voters, if they knew what this was, would not be in favor of it,\u8221\'20\'1D Ziegler said.\par \par \uc2 Misinformation abounds. On Wednesday, the Church of the Resurrection in Leawood hosted an informational event, inviting Great Plains Planned Parenthood, an obstetrician-gynecologist, and Kansans For Life to talk.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s one of the world\u8217\'20\'19s biggest methodist churches, and the founder, the Rev Adam Hamilton, discussed a questionnaire it had distributed, receiving over 4,000 responses. The state vote represents \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a binary issue, but survey respondents were mainly in the middle \u8211\'20\'13 not for a total ban nor for no limits, he said.\par \par \uc2 What followed was mixed messaging. In a pre-recorded message by Kansans for Life, communications director Danielle Underwood spoke about third trimester abortions, taxpayer funding for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , lack of regulation and no parental consent for youth abortions in Kansas \u8211\'20\'13 none of which are the law of the land in Kansas.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEither we have a limit to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  industry, or no limits. That\u8217\'20\'19s what the amendment says,\u8221\'20\'1D said Underwood.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI come at this analysis as a lawyer,\u8221\'20\'1D rebutted Emily Wales, chief executive of Great Plains Planned Parenthood.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe do have regulated \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . You don\u8217\'20\'19t see \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  accessible everywhere, [or] past 22 weeks, which is the state ban. And two-parent consent [for minors] is required,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Nearby, in a wealthy, conservative neighborhood with landscaped gardens, volunteer Nancy Mays, 60, was campaigning for Kansans for Constitutional Freedom on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m voting no on Tuesday, because I don\u8217\'20\'19t like government overreach,\u8221\'20\'1D she told the first couple who answer their door. The campaign knows that answer chimes well with Kansans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19ve got my vote!\u8221\'20\'1D said Ron Barnhart, 80, a retired doctor.\par \par \uc2 Around the corner, Tom Bruce, 72, said he was voting no. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t trust the Kansas legislature to do the right thing. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is already restricted enough here,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Driving from Johnson county to meet more canvassers in the working-class and more ethnically diverse area of Wyandotte county, the purple signage of the yes campaign gives way to the yellow and black sunflowers of no.\par \par \uc2 There, a 58-year-old pre-school teacher, who asked not to be named, said she was in a moral conundrum.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19d rather not do a yes or a no,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, wringing her hands. \u8220\'20\'1CI just keep saying it\u8217\'20\'19s a little human being \u8211\'20\'13 I\u8217\'20\'19m a Catholic.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut I also keep on thinking about what happened to that little girl, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/27/indiana-investigates-abortion-doctor-10-year-old-rape-victim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who was 10, and was forced to travel}}}\uc2  for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after being raped. It\u8217\'20\'19s just inhumane.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She doesn\u8217\'20\'19t know if she\u8217\'20\'19ll vote in Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s election.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220801ei810020c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
