\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Kansas referendum will test change in  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  landscape since Roe fell\b0\par\par\uc2 Jessica Glenza \par \uc2 984 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 July 2022\par 07:13 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The ballot measure is the first of many across the country that will decide where and how women can preserve reproductive rights\par \par \uc2 In the first of a wave of referendums across the country on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, Kansas voters will decide on Tuesday whether the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution protects the right to terminate a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Should Kansans pass the ballot measure , it would give state lawmakers leeway to ban the procedure, which they appear likely to do.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains legal in Kansas for now, with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers saying they have been overwhelmed by demand from patients in neighbouring Arkansas, Missouri, Oklahoma and Texas \u8211\'20\'13 all of which have banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and are now wrestling with the consequences.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere has been a great deal of shock at the local level from people who, I think, just didn\u8217\'20\'19t believe Roe would fall or that we could end up in this situation,\u8221\'20\'1D said Emily Wales, president and CEO of Planned Parenthood Great Plains, which operates in all four states.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CKansas is essential for the provision of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services here locally, and it is not hard for people to look across state lines\u8221\'20\'1D to see the consequences of bans, she said.\par \par \uc2 The ballot measure in this state will provide an early indication of how the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision in June to end a national right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has altered the American political landscape. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/27/california-abortion-rights-state-constitution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 California and Vermont}}}\uc2  are expected to vote on whether to affirm a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/28/abortion-rights-michigan-roe-wade-ballot-initiative"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 campaigners in Michigan}}}\uc2  are working to get a similar measure on the ballot. Kentucky and Montana will have anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ballot measures.\par \par \uc2 While supporters of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access said there has been a \u8220\'20\'1Cgroundswell\u8221\'20\'1D of support since the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision, winning the vote in Kansas will not be easy.\par \par \uc2 The new constitutional amendment, if approved, would override a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kscourts.org/Newsroom/News-Releases/News/2019-News-Releases/April-2019/Supreme-Court-announces-decision-in-Hodes-Nauser"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2019 Kansas supreme court ruling}}}\uc2  that people in the state have the right to terminate a pregnancy. But the measure appears on Kansas\u8217\'20\'19s primary ballot, typically reserved only for registered party voters, where they select the nominee for their party in the later November election.\par \par \uc2 Republican voters are far more likely to participate in August primaries in Kansas than Democrats are. Unaffiliated voters make up more than one-quarter of the state\u8217\'20\'19s electorate, but typically have no reason to come to the polls during primaries.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe only outcome that would shock me is if the no side [fighting to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legal] won easily or comfortably,\u8221\'20\'1D said Patrick Miller, an associate professor of political science at the \uc2 University of Kansas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI would not be surprised by a yes vote win because they\u8217\'20\'19ve been better organized.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Before the fall of Roe v Wade, abortions in Kansas represented {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/fact-sheet/state-facts-about-abortion-kansas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 less than 1%}}}\uc2  of all abortions performed in the country, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a reproductive rights research organization. About {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/reproductivehealth/data_stats/pdfs/kansas.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 560,000 women of reproductive age}}}\uc2  live in Kansas.\par \par \uc2 A ban in Kansas could ripple across the midwest. The region is now one of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2022/jun/28/tracking-where-abortion-laws-stand-in-every-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most hostile to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  in the US}}}\uc2 , and many states have already banned it or intend to.\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood Great Plains has been forced to tell patients that although clinics in Kansas might be nearest, they are unlikely to be able to accommodate them.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19ve got to get to Nebraska, Illinois if you can \u8211\'20\'13 New Mexico and Colorado,\u8221\'20\'1D Wales said she tells patients. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you\u8217\'20\'19re coming from Texas, we may be the closest geographically, but we just don\u8217\'20\'19t have enough appointments to meet the need.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Republican lawmakers in Kansas have refused to specify how they would restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but have signaled {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.kslegislature.org/li/b2021_22/measures/documents/hb2746_00_0000.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interest in outright \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  bans}}}\uc2 , and groups backing the amendment have told supporters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://kansasreflector.com/2022/07/15/kansas-abortion-ban-is-the-plan-officials-pushing-constitutional-amendment-tell-gop-crowd/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 their goal is an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/ValueThemBoth"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ads in favor}}}\uc2  of the amendments, however, tend to focus on \u8220\'20\'1Creasonable\u8221\'20\'1D limits on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 even though {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kansascity.com/news/politics-government/article263405598.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 many}}}\uc2  are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/fact-sheet/state-facts-about-abortion-kansas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 already in effect}}}\uc2 , such as a ban on taxpayer funding for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Neither Kansans for Life, a sponsor of the constitutional amendment, nor state representative Trevor Jacobs, a prominent proponent of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban legislation, responded to multiple requests for comment.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coefficient.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/KS-VTB-Amendment-7.18.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Public polling}}}\uc2  suggests the campaign will be close. As of July, 47% of voters said they supported the measure, 43% said they opposed it, and 10% were undecided. Polls from February show {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cjonline.com/story/news/politics/elections/2022/02/22/poll-shows-kansas-residents-skeptical-banning-abortion-all-cases/6878658001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 60% of Kansans}}}\uc2  oppose an outright ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But Kansas\u8217\'20\'19s legislature is \u8220\'20\'1Cmuch more conservative than the average Kansan on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D, said Miller.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a dynamic that has played out across many US states, as well as in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 . As the Republican party has grown closer to the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement, and lawmakers adopt more extreme positions, Republican-dominated legislatures have banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  even when public sentiment is mixed.\par \par \uc2 An estimated {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/1576/abortion.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 85% of Americans}}}\uc2  support legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in at least some circumstances, according to Gallup polling. Nevertheless, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/05/abortion-deserts-clinics-access-closed-map"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than half}}}\uc2  of US states are expected to try to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the procedure is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2022/jun/28/tracking-where-abortion-laws-stand-in-every-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 already banned}}}\uc2 , unavailable or legally contested in 17 states.\par \par \uc2 Kansas also has its own history with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , one that touches on the most violent extremes of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement. Thousands of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protesters descended on the state in 1991 for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kcur.org/podcast/my-fellow-kansans/2021-07-20/summer-of-mercy-rebroadcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSummer of Mercy\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 , blockading clinic entrances and harassing patients and doctors. Then, in 2009, a man assassinated {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global/2009/jul/29/george-tiller-abortion-doctor-shot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 George Tiller}}}\uc2 , a doctor who provided surgical abortions, outside his church in Wichita, Kansas.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have a chance, a good chance \u8211\'20\'13 again, complicated by being on the primary ballot,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ashley All, a spokesperson for Kansans for Constitutional Freedom, a coalition of groups that oppose the proposed constitutional amendment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut, if people are motivated and they understand this is something that takes away their constitutional rights, takes away their freedom to make decisions for themselves and their families \u8211\'20\'13 I think they\u8217\'20\'19ll show up and vote no.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220731ei7v000jh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
