\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18What about my life?\u8217\'20\'19 West Virginia girl, 12, speaks out against anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  bill\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang \par \uc2 571 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 July 2022\par 01:38 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 36\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Plea by Addison Gardner during public hearing against bill that would prohibit procedure in nearly all cases goes viral\par \par \uc2 An impassioned plea from a 12-year-old girl has gone viral after she spoke to West Virginia Republican lawmakers during a public hearing for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill that would prohibit the procedure in nearly all cases.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Addison Gardner of Buffalo middle school in Kenova, West Virginia, was among several people who spoke out against the bill.\par \par \uc2 Addressing the West Virginia house of delegates, Gardner, among about 90 other speakers, was given 45 seconds to plead her case.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy education is very important to me and I plan on doing great things in life. If a man decides that I\u8217\'20\'19m an object and does unspeakable and tragic things to me, am I, a child, supposed to carry and birth another child?\u8221\'20\'1D Gardner said.\par \par \uc2 She went on to add, \u8220\'20\'1CAm I to put my body through the physical trauma of pregnancy? Am I to suffer the mental implications, a child, who had no say in what was being done with my body? Some here say they are pro-life. What about my life? Does my life not matter to you?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As Gardner \u8211\'20\'13 a volleyball and track athlete at her middle school, spoke, she was looked on by Rita Ray, an 80-year-old woman who had an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 1959, 14 years before terminations were deemed a constitutional right.\par \par \uc2 In a photo captured by Kyle Vass, a journalist from the American Civil Liberties Union of West Virginia, Ray can be seen smiling in the background as Gardner issued her impassioned plea.\par \par \uc2 One user who tweeted the photo {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WilliamKyleVass/status/1552417018082623488?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1552417018082623488%7Ctwgr%5E%7Ctwcon%5Es1_c10&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.washingtonpost.com%2Fpolitics%2F2022%2F07%2F28%2Fabortion-west-virginia-girl-addison-gardner%2F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CRita Ray, 80, who risked her life pre-Roe by getting an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from someone who wasn\u8217\'20\'19t a healthcare provider, watches on as Addison Gardner, 12, contemplates her own future without access to legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in WV.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Despite speeches from Gardner and other \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights activists, the house passed the bill by an overwhelming vote of 69 to 23. Shortly after Gardner delivered her address, house members adopted an amendment that would allow abortions in cases of rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 However, the amendment, which passed narrowly with 46 to 43 votes, only allows for the procedure to be performed up to 14 weeks of pregnancy and only if the rape or incest is reported to the police.\par \par \uc2 The state senate\u8217\'20\'19s adoption of at least two of a dozen offered amendments on Friday means the bill must now go back to the house of delegates for consideration.\par \par \uc2 Unlike some other states which have \u8220\'20\'1Ctrigger bans\u8221\'20\'1D that would ban abortions within 30 days of Roe being overturned, West Virginia has a 150-year-old pre-Roe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that would come back into effect in the absence of Roe.\par \par \uc2 Last week, Kanawha county circuit judge Tera Salango blocked the enforcement of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and granted the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Center of West Virginia, the state\u8217\'20\'19s only \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic, the ability to continue performing the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Salango said its patients, \u8220\'20\'1Cespecially those who are impregnated as a result of a rape or incest, are suffering irreparable harm\u8221\'20\'1D, the Associated Press {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-health-west-virginia-charleston-government-and-politics-eccf3ac01cea7d51ea6dac5792520a48"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports.}}}\par \par \uc2 West Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general, Patrick Morrisey, described the ruling as \u8220\'20\'1Ca dark day for West Virginia\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press contributed reporting\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220729ei7t000s0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
