\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 DoJ reportedly preparing court fight to get Trump insiders to testify \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Richard Luscombe \par \uc2 4,989 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 July 2022\par 21:46 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Prosecutors expect former president to try to invoke executive privilege to prevent his ex-officials from speakingSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re closing the blog now at the end of a momentous week in US politics, with the landmark climate bill, the Inflation Reduction Act set to become a big win for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  ahead of the midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we followed:\par \par \uc2 * The US will not allow any further Russian annexation in Ukraine to go \u8220\'20\'1Cunchallenged or unpunished\u8221\'20\'1D, White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said, following secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s conversation with Russian foreign minister Sergei Lavrov earlier in which he pressed his Kremlin counterpart over negotiations to release jailed Americans Brittney Griner and Paul Whelan.\par \par \uc2 * Justice department prosecutors are readying for a likely court fight to get testimony from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s former White House officials over his illegitimate actions to overturn his 2020 election defeat. CNN reports they are preparing arguments if Trump invokes executive privilege to prevent those close to his Oval Office revealing what they know.\par \par \uc2 * Text messages of two of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s chief homeland security officials, \uc2 Chad Wolf\uc2  and Ken Cuccinelli, are missing for \u8220\'20\'1Ca key period\u8221\'20\'1D surrounding the January 6 insurrection, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2022/07/28/homeland-security-texts-jan6/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Joe Manchin and \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  had secret basement meetings in the Capitol building as they negotiated the Inflation Reduction Act, the AP said. The size and scope of the climate concessions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joe-manchin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Manchin}}}\uc2 , the rebel West Virginia Democrat, agreed to surprised the Senate majority leader.\par \par \uc2 * The treasury department has imposed sanctions on two Russian individuals and four entities that support the Kremlin\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cglobal malign influence and election interference operations\u8221\'20\'1D. They \u8220\'20\'1Cattempted to destabilize the US and its allies and partners, including Ukraine,\u8221\'20\'1D the department said.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  said it was \u8220\'20\'1Csick\u8221\'20\'1D that children are learning to use assault weapons, amid a surge of deadly gun violence and mass shootings in the US. The House speaker announced a vote in the chamber this afternoon on gun controls, including an assault weapons ban.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has nominated a lawyer who represented the Mississippi clinic at the heart of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights last month to become a federal appeals court judge, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Julie Rikelman\uc2 , an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights lawyer with the center for reproductive rights, was picked to serve on the Boston-based first circuit court of appeals, one of nine new judicial nominees announced by the president today.\par \par \uc2 Rikelman argued for the Jackson women\u8217\'20\'19s health organization - Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s only \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic - in challenging a Republican-backed law that banned the procedure after 15 weeks.\par \par \uc2 Republicans are likely to oppose her elevation in the equally divided Senate.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Report: Russia requested murderer's release for Griner and Whelan\par \par \uc2 Russian government officials asked that Vadim Krasikov, a spy and former army colonel {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2021/12/15/germany-russia-chechen-murder-berlin/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 convicted of murder in Germany last year}}}\uc2 , be added to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2022/jul/27/brittney-griner-prisoner-swap-biden-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposed prisoner swap}}}\uc2  for Brittney Griner and Paul Whelan, CNN reports.\par \par \uc2 Brittney Griner. Photograph: Kirill Kudryavtsev/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMultiple sources\u8221\'20\'1D familiar with the situation told the network that Russia communicated the request to the US earlier this month through an informal backchannel used by the spy agency, known as the FSB.\par \par \uc2 The request was problematic because Krasikov remains in German custody, the sources said, and because the request was not communicated formally the \uc2 US government\uc2  did not view it as a legitimate counter to its initial offer of arms dealer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/28/viktor-bout-brittney-griner-paul-whelan-prisoner-swap"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Viktor Bout.}}}\par \par \uc2 Secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  spoke with Russian foreign minister Sergei Lavrov earlier today and pressed for the release of Griner and Whelan, whom the US considers \u8220\'20\'1Cwrongfully detained\u8221\'20\'1D. It is not certain if Russia\u8217\'20\'19s reported request over Krasikov featured in the conversation.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 We promised you news of the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s changing position on Covid-19 boosters as the Omicron variant BA.5 continues to grip the nation. Here\u8217\'20\'19s my colleague Sam Levine \u8217\'20\'19s report:\par \par \uc2 Instead of expanding eligibility for a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2022/may/09/fourth-covid-jab-can-give-higher-immunity-than-initial-booster-study-finds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fourth Covid-19 booster shot}}}\uc2  now, the Biden administration will push this fall to get Americans to take another booster vaccination that is predicted to better protect against the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jul/21/why-are-there-so-many-omicron-subvariants-and-why-have-ba4-and-ba5-taken-hold"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Omicron BA.5 subvariant}}}\uc2  of the coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 Pharmaceutical companies \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  and \uc2 Moderna\uc2  are expected to start rolling out the reformulated boosters, which are expected to be authorized for anyone 12 and older, in September.\par \par \uc2 The decision comes amid {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/01/us-covid-surge-cases-rate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a surge in cases of the virus}}}\uc2  across the US \u8211\'20\'13 and Biden himself {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/27/biden-tests-negative-covid-ended-isolation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently recovered}}}\uc2  from an infection.\par \par \uc2 Some of the administration\u8217\'20\'19s top health experts, including presidential adviser \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2  and White House Covid coordinator Ashish Jha, had advocated for expanding eligibility for a second dose of the current booster because of the latest spread.\par \par \uc2 But public health officials worried that administering two different booster shots so close together could blunt their effectiveness.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou can\u8217\'20\'19t get a vaccine shot August 1 and get another vaccine shot September 15 and expect the second shot to do anything,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Shane Crotty\uc2 , a virologist at the La Jolla Institute for Immunology, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/07/28/us/politics/covid-booster-shots.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the New York Times}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19ve got so much antibody around, if you get another dose, it won\u8217\'20\'19t do anything.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The decision means that adults over 50 and those who are immunocompromised remain the only ones {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/coronavirus/2019-ncov/vaccines/booster-shot.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 authorized for a second booster}}}\uc2 , ie their fourth shot since the vaccine began being administered widely in 2021. Fewer than a third of people 50 and older who are eligible have gotten one, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://covid.cdc.gov/covid-data-tracker/#vaccinations_vacc-people-additional-dose-totalpop"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to data }}}\uc2  from the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  (CDC).\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/29/us-to-hold-push-for-covid-boosters-until-fall-in-order-to-better-protect-against-ba5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US to hold push for Covid boosters until fall in order to better protect against BA.5}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 A third candidate in a week has dropped out of the Wisconsin Democratic Senate primary, leaving Mandela Barnes, the state\u8217\'20\'19s lieutenant governor, a clear favorite to challenge Republican incumbent Ron Johnson in November.\par \par \uc2 Mandela Barnes. Photograph: Mike De Sisti/AP\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin treasurer Sarah Godlewski \u8217\'20\'19s withdrawal followed those of former state assemblyman Tom Nelson on Monday and Barnes\u8217\'20\'19 top rival, Alex Lasry, two days later.\par \par \uc2 Democrats are hopeful of seizing Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s seat in the fall in a state \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  won narrowly in the 2020 presidential election, reversing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s victory there in 2016.\par \par \uc2 Johsnon was quick to comment on Godlewski\u8217\'20\'19s announcement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShowing their lack of respect for voters and the democratic process, the power brokers of the Democrat party have now cleared the field for their most radical left candidate,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson tweeted.\par \par \uc2 Barnes, 35, would be the first Black senator from Wisconsin if elected.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House: Russian annexation in Ukraine 'won't go unpunished'\par \par \uc2 The US will not allow any further Russian annexation in Ukraine to go \u8220\'20\'1Cunchallenged or unpunished,\u8221\'20\'1D White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  has said at an afternoon briefing.\par \par \uc2 She is answering reporters\u8217\'20\'19 questions about secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s conversation with Russian foreign minister Sergei Lavrov earlier, in which he pressed his Kremlin counterpart over negotiations to release jailed Americans Brittney Griner and Paul Whelan.\par \par \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  addresses reporters at the White House on Friday. Photograph: Elizabeth Frantz/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Blinken \u8220\'20\'1Cthought it was it was important to make clear where we and our global partners stand on several key issues,\u8221\'20\'1D Jean-Pierre said:\par \par \uc2 He spoke about the importance of Russia allowing ships to depart Odessa and to adhere to their grain deals. He also emphasized how Russia\u8217\'20\'19s plan to annex parts of Ukraine by force, which we warned about from here at the podium, would be a gross violation of the \uc2 UN\uc2  charter and we would not allow it to go unchallenged or unpunished.\par \par \uc2 We are under no illusions that Moscow is prepared to engage meaningfully and constructively yet, so Secretary Blinken made clear that this was not about a return to business as usual.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has \u8220\'20\'1Cno plans\u8221\'20\'1D to call Russian president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  over that or any other issue, Jean-Pierre said.\par \par \uc2 As for Griner and Whelan, she added:\par \par \uc2 What the president is doing, the secretary and his national security team, is to make sure we keep our promise and [are] doing everything that we can in bringing home US nationals that are wrongfully detained.\par \par \uc2 This is top of [Biden\u8217\'20\'19s] mind, this is a priority. We are doing everything we can to bring Paul home, to bring Britney home.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Information House Jan 6 committee is getting from Republican witnesses "is good and sound" - Mulvaney\par \par \uc2 Mick Mulvaney\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s former acting chief of staff, testified on Thursday before the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jan-6-hearings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House select committee}}}\uc2  investigating the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/06/trump-capitol-american-carnage-washington"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 insurrection on January 6}}}\uc2 , 2021, and the-then US president\u8217\'20\'19s role in inciting it. And on Friday, Mulvaney spoke about it.\par \par \uc2 Mick Mulvaney\uc2  (left) and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at a working lunch in Washington in 2019. Photograph: Andrew Harnik/AP\par \par \uc2 He was asked questions by \u8220\'20\'1Cfour or five\u8221\'20\'1D lawyers for the committee, who interviewed him for about 2.5 hours behind closed doors, he told CNN on Friday morning.\par \par \uc2 He said they were courteous and there was \u8220\'20\'1Cno animosity\u8221\'20\'1D. he said the questions were \u8220\'20\'1Cdesigned to find out stuff that might make President Trump look bad\u8221\'20\'1D and pointed out there was no-one there asking \u8220\'20\'1Cthe other side of the questions\u8221\'20\'1D [note: it is a bipartisan committee co-chaired by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/20/january-6-hearings-key-players"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican Liz Cheney}}}\uc2  ] \u8220\'20\'1Cthat might have made President Trump look good\u8221\'20\'1D, but he added that that was \u8220\'20\'1Cfine\u8221\'20\'1D and it was not a fight, it was a free-flowing discussion.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI would have given the exact same answers, obviously, if there had been folks there from the other side of the political spectrum, so it just reaffirms in my mind that the committee is politically-biased, there is no question about that, the structure is politically biased.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut the information that you are getting is from Republicans, like myself, who are testifying - you are not under oath but you still can\u8217\'20\'19t lie to Congress anyway, that\u8217\'20\'19s still a crime, and I think the information they are getting is good and sound information.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mulvaney said the lawyers were at the meeting in person while some members of the committee, who are all members of Congress, attended remotely, and Cheney questioned him.\par \par \uc2 He also acknowledged that the separate Department of Justice investigation into events surrounding January 6 last year, when supporters of Trump stormed the US Capitol to try to stop the certification of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election victory over him, was now \u8220\'20\'1Cmoving closer and closer to the [Trump] White House\u8221\'20\'1D. CNN reported that federal prosecutors {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/29/trump-jan-6-manchin-biden-covid-boosters-us-politics-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62e3e6358f08c0014732708c#block-62e3e6358f08c0014732708c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 want to force}}}\uc2  Trump officials to testify.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey are starting to talk to people inside the Trump orbit as opposed to just the rioters themselves, the Proud Boys and the Oath Keepers,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s lunchtime, so time to take stock of where we\u8217\'20\'19re at today in US politics:\par \par \uc2 * Justice department prosecutors are readying for a likely court fight to get testimony from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s former White House officials over his illegitimate actions to overturn his 2020 election defeat. CNN reports they are preparing arguments if Trump invokes executive privilege to prevent those close to his Oval Office revealing what they know.\par \par \uc2 * Text messages of two of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s chief homeland security officials, \uc2 Chad Wolf\uc2  and Ken Cuccinelli, are missing for \u8220\'20\'1Ca key period\u8221\'20\'1D surrounding the January 6 insurrection, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2022/07/28/homeland-security-texts-jan6/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Joe Manchin and \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  had secret basement meetings in the Capitol building as they negotiated the Inflation Reduction Act, the AP said. The size and scope of the climate concessions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joe-manchin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Manchin}}}\uc2 , the rebel West Virginia Democrat, agreed to surprised the Senate majority leader.\par \par \uc2 * The treasury department has imposed sanctions on two Russian individuals and four entities that support the Kremlin\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cglobal malign influence and election interference operations\u8221\'20\'1D. They \u8220\'20\'1Cattempted to destabilize the US and its allies and partners, including Ukraine,\u8221\'20\'1D the department said.\par \par \uc2 * Secretary of State \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  said he pressed Russian foreign minister Sergei Lavrov to accept a US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2022/jul/27/brittney-griner-prisoner-swap-biden-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposal for the release}}}\uc2  of detained Americans Brittney Griner and Paul Whelan. Blinken said he had a \u8220\'20\'1Cfrank and direct\u8221\'20\'1D conversation with Lavrov earlier today.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  said it was \u8220\'20\'1Csick\u8221\'20\'1D that children are learning to use assault weapons, amid a surge of deadly gun violence and mass shootings in the US. The House speaker announced a vote in the chamber this afternoon on gun controls, including an assault weapons ban.\par \par \uc2 Please stick with us. There\u8217\'20\'19s more to come this afternoon, including White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s daily briefing.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Secretary of State \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  said on Friday he pressed Russian foreign minister Sergei Lavrov to accept a US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2022/jul/27/brittney-griner-prisoner-swap-biden-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposal for the release}}}\uc2  of detained Americans Brittney Griner and Paul Whelan.\par \par \uc2 Blinken said he had a \u8220\'20\'1Cfrank and direct\u8221\'20\'1D conversation with Lavrov earlier on Friday, and told his counterpart that Russia must fulfill commitments it made as part of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/22/ukraine-russia-sign-un-backed-deal-restart-grain-exports"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deal on the export of grain}}}\uc2  from Ukraine, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/29/ukraine-grain-ships-un-shipping-insurance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brokered by}}}\uc2  the United Nations and Turkey, and that the world would not accept Russian annexation of Ukrainian territory.\par \par \uc2 Blinken and Lavrov spoke on the phone a few hours after Lavrov indicated some interest in Blinken\u8217\'20\'19s offer.\par \par \uc2 Secretary of State \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  speaks during the U.S.-Japan Economic Policy Consultative Committee in Washington earlier today. Photograph: Tom Brenner/AP\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/brittney-griner"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Griner}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s trial resumes in Moscow on Monday.\par \par \uc2 This combination of pictures created on July 28, 2022 shows, L to R, Russian Viktor Bout, Russian arms dealer who could be swapped by the US for American \uc2 WNBA\uc2  basketball star Brittney Griner and Paul Whelan, a former US Marine accused of espionage and arrested in Russia. Photograph: Nicolas Asfouri/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House has issued a statement encouraging the House to pass an assault weapons ban later today.\par \par \uc2 The statement reminds the public that 40,000 Americans die from gunshot wounds every year and guns have \u8220\'20\'1Cbecome the top killer of children\u8221\'20\'1D in the US.\par \par \uc2 It notes that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  played a leading role when he was a US senator in the 1994 assault weapons ban, which stood for 10 years before the administration of \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  declined to extend it.\par \par \uc2 The White House further notes that \u8220\'20\'1Cwhen the ban expired, mass shootings tripled\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrWhite House issues statement in support of assault weapons bill to be voted on later today in the House. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/f7coJRwcXh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/f7coJRwcXh}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jamie Dupree (@jamiedupree) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jamiedupree/status/1553057780927447041?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 29, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, the US president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/11/majority-us-democrats-dont-want-biden-2024-house-january-6-capitol-attack-latest-updates?page=with:block-62cc4aae8f08038ec3b7f79a#block-62cc4aae8f08038ec3b7f79a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called once again}}}\uc2  for a ban on such rifles, saying the US was \u8220\'20\'1Cawash in weapons of war\u8221\'20\'1D and decrying how such weapons have become more and more powerful so that when hitting human flesh, people are ripped apart and parents have to supply DNA samples after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-school-shootings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 school shootings}}}\uc2 , such as in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas-school-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Uvalde, Texas}}}\uc2 , recently, because their children are so damaged from the bullets that they cannot otherwise be certainly identified.\par \par \uc2 Buffalo, in upstate New York, is still grieving mightily after a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/buffalo-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 racist mass shooting}}}\uc2  there, as well as the less-documented, everyday urban gun violence blighting life in many American neighborhoods, and the valiant attempts by some {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/03/these-community-organizers-have-helped-stop-daily-gun-violence-can-their-lessons-prevent-mass-shootings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 community leaders}}}\uc2  to tamp it.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, ICYMI, here\u8217\'20\'19s our Joanie Greve on what gun executives {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/27/ceos-gun-manufacturers-testify-before-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had to say}}}\uc2  at a congressional hearing earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/27/ceos-gun-manufacturers-testify-before-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gun executives tell Congress: don\u8217\'20\'19t blame us for deadly shootings}}}\par \par \uc2 And here\u8217\'20\'19s our Aben\u233\'00\'E9 Clayton\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/03/these-community-organizers-have-helped-stop-daily-gun-violence-can-their-lessons-prevent-mass-shootings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reporting}}}\uc2  as part of the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/series/guns-and-lies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Guns and Lies series}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/03/these-community-organizers-have-helped-stop-daily-gun-violence-can-their-lessons-prevent-mass-shootings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Can lessons of community violence interrupters prevent mass shootings?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pelosi: 'sick' that children learn to handle assault weapons\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  says it\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Csick\u8221\'20\'1D that children are learning to use assault weapons, amid a surge of deadly gun violence in the US that has claimed numerous lives in recent weeks in a series of mass shootings.\par \par \uc2 The House speaker was talking at a lunchtime press briefing at which she announced a vote in the chamber this afternoon on gun controls, including an assault weapons ban:\par \par \uc2 When I talk about it on the floor this afternoon I\u8217\'20\'19m going to show a presentation of what some totally irresponsible people are putting out there about little children, toddlers, learning how to use an assault weapon.\par \par \uc2 Smaller assault weapons, but a gun like mommy and daddy\u8217\'20\'19s, small assault weapons for getting their muscles ready to be able to use it. Is that sick?\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  addresses the media on Friday. Photograph: Jonathan Ernst/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Pelosi said there was an \u8220\'20\'1Coutcry\u8221\'20\'1D for an assault weapons ban:\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re hopeful [over the] vote for the assault weapons ban. I think the best, most important thing to do is to have background checks, that probably saves the most lives on the ongoing.\par \par \uc2 But with that it\u8217\'20\'19s very important is to reinstate [the assault weapons ban], we like to say reinstate because we did pass this before. And it did save lives.\par \par \uc2 Even if passed by the House, an assault weapons ban faces next to no chance of clearing the 50-50 divided Senate, where 60 votes would be needed for its passage.\par \par \uc2 Such a measure would be unlikely to attract any Republican support.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 New US sanctions for Russian citizens\par \par \uc2 The treasury department said Friday it had imposed sanctions on two Russian individuals and four entities that support the Kremlin\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cglobal malign influence and election interference operations \u8221\'20\'1D, according to Reuters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe individuals and entities designated today played various roles in Russia\u8217\'20\'19s attempts to manipulate and destabilize the United States and its allies and partners, including Ukraine,\u8221\'20\'1D the department said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://home.treasury.gov/news/press-releases/jy0899"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a statement}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Brian E Nelson, undersecretary of the treasury for terrorism and financial intelligence, said: \u8220\'20\'1CFree and fair elections form a pillar of American democracy that must be protected from outside influence.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Kremlin has repeatedly sought to threaten and undermine our democratic processes and institutions. The US will continue our extensive work to counter these efforts and safeguard our democracy from Russia\u8217\'20\'19s interference.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Russian citizens sanctioned are Aleksandr Viktorovich Ionov and Natalya Valeryevna Burlinova.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  has scheduled a press conference for noon, at which we\u8217\'20\'19re likely to learn of her plans for a House vote on the landmark Inflation Reduction Act announced yesterday, and whether she\u8217\'20\'19s heading to Taiwan as early as tonight {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/28/nancy-pelosi-invited-us-lawmakers-to-visit-taiwan-hears-committee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on a controversial trip}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you her comments when she speaks.\par \par \uc2 You can watch the speaker\u8217\'20\'19s press conference on her \uc2 YouTube\uc2  channel here:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 'Secret basement meetings' led to climate deal: report\par \par \uc2 Secret meetings in a dingy Capitol building basement, a \u8220\'20\'1Cvirtual handshake\u8221\'20\'1D across the miles to seal the deal... the Associated Press has published {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/inflation-biden-sports-congress-e499871130fa9881beb0618ebddfe88c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an extraordinary account}}}\uc2  of how the climate bill agreement between Joe Manchin and \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  that has set Washington abuzz this week came to be.\par \par \uc2 The size and scope of what {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joe-manchin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Manchin}}}\uc2 , the rebel West Virginia Democrat who had stalled almost the entirety of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s ambitious first term agenda, was willing to accept to form the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/28/joe-biden-climate-deal-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Inflation Reduction Act}}}\uc2  surprised Schumer, the Senate majority leader, the AP says.\par \par \uc2 Senator Joe Manchin (left) and Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  talk at the White House in March. Photograph: Patrick Semansky/AP\par \par \uc2 The news agency account suggests it was partly Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s fears about losing his gavel as chair of the Senate energy committee (he has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/jul/28/joe-manchin-climate-bill-fossil-fuels-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made millions from the coal industry}}}\uc2  ) that led to his reversal, and willingness to accept climate change provisions he had previously fiercely resisted.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe coal state conservative was being publicly singled out, shamed even, as the sole figure stopping help for a planet in peril,\u8221\'20\'1D the AP said, noting the barrage of criticism directed at Manchin from progressive Democrats and climate crisis activists after he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/video/2021/dec/19/joe-manchin-says-he-cannot-get-there-on-build-back-better-bill-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked Biden\u8217\'20\'19s flagship Build Back Better}}}\uc2  project.\par \par \uc2 According to the report, compiled with the help several people familiar with private conversations, and granted anonymity to discuss them, Manchin met Schumer secretly in a Capitol basement to get the conversation going.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat a beautiful office,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer reportedly said. \u8220\'20\'1CIs it mine?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Over several sessions, the two men and their staffs {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/jul/28/climate-bill-joe-manchin-whats-in-it"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 thrashed out the details}}}\uc2  of what would become the $739bn Inflation Reduction Act, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/28/joe-manchin-biden-democrats-climate-spending-bill-latest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hailed yesterday by Biden}}}\uc2  as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most significant legislation in history to tackle the climate crisis.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 They sealed the deal on Wednesday afternoon with a \u8220\'20\'1Cvirtual handshake\u8221\'20\'1D on a Zoom call, with Manchin isolating after testing positive for Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 Whether the bill becomes law remains to be seen. Democrats will need every one of their votes in the 50-50 divided Senate, while there will also be Republican opposition in the House. Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  says she\u8217\'20\'19ll bring members back from their summer break to vote on the bill next week.\par \par \uc2 Regardless of the outcome, just getting to this point was a remarkable achievement in itself, the AP says.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Fortune has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fortune.com/2022/07/28/summers-biden-manchin-inflation-reduction-act/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this intriguing account}}}\uc2  of the role of former treasury secretary and Biden critic \uc2 Larry Summers\uc2  in the saga, suggesting he may just have \u8220\'20\'1Csaved Biden\u8217\'20\'19s presidency\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/jul/28/climate-bill-joe-manchin-whats-in-it"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s in the climate bill that Joe Manchin supports \u8211\'20\'13 and what isn\u8217\'20\'19t }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 An impassioned plea from a 12-year-old girl has gone viral after she spoke to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/west-virginia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 West Virginia}}}\uc2  Republican lawmakers during a public hearing for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill that would prohibit the procedure in nearly all cases.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Addison Gardner of Buffalo middle school in Kenova, West Virginia, was among several people who spoke out against a bill that would not only ban abortions in most cases but also allow for physicians who perform abortions to be prosecuted.\par \par \uc2 Addressing the West Virginia house of delegates, Gardner, among about 90 other speakers, was given 45 seconds to plead her case.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy education is very important to me and I plan on doing great things in life. If a man decides that I\u8217\'20\'19m an object and does unspeakable and tragic things to me, am I, a child, supposed to carry and birth another child?\u8221\'20\'1D Gardner said.\par \par \uc2 Read more here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/28/west-virginia-girl-12-speaks-out-against-anti-abortion-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18What about my life?\u8217\'20\'19 West Virginia girl, 12, speaks out against anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  bill }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Homeland security officials' January 6 texts 'missing'\par \par \uc2 Text messages of two of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s chief homeland security officials, \uc2 Chad Wolf\uc2  and Ken Cuccinelli, are missing for \u8220\'20\'1Ca key period\u8221\'20\'1D surrounding the former president\u8217\'20\'19s January 6 insurrection, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2022/07/28/homeland-security-texts-jan6/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post reported}}}\uc2  Friday.\par \par \uc2 Chad Wolf\uc2 . Photograph: Sarah Silbiger/Reuters\par \par \uc2 It follows news that secret service texts from about the same time had been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/16/secret-service-deleted-text-messages-january-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mysteriously erased}}}\uc2 , hampering the House panel\u8217\'20\'19s inquiry into the deadly Capitol riot and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s illegitimate efforts to remain in office.\par \par \uc2 The previously unreported discovery of missing records for the most senior homeland security officials increases the volume of potential evidence that has vanished regarding the time around the Capitol attack, the Post says.\par \par \uc2 enltr??????BREAKING POGO INVESTIGATION: yet another story of missing text messages at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/DHS?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #DHS}}}\uc2 . This time, text messages to and from three top Trump-era officials at the dept. from early January 2021 are missing. Read the investigation now: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/AkWxoUu65Z"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/AkWxoUu65Z}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Project On Government Oversight\uc2  (@POGOwatchdog) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POGOwatchdog/status/1552842369065787392?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 29, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The homeland security department told the agency\u8217\'20\'19s inspector general in February that texts of Wolf and Cuccinelli were lost in a \u8220\'20\'1Creset\u8221\'20\'1D of their government phones when they left their jobs in January 2021 in preparation for the new Biden administration, the newspaper adds.\par \par \uc2 The Post says its source is an internal record obtained by the \uc2 Project on Government Oversight\uc2 , whose own report on the disappearance of the messages {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pogo.org/investigation/2022/07/missing-more-january-6-texts-sought-by-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 can be found here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Messages of a third senior department official, the undersecretary of management Randolph \u8220\'20\'1CTex\u8221\'20\'1D Alles, a former Secret Service director, are also no longer available because of the reset, according to the Post.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Manafort invokes Holocaust in memoir of life in prison\par \par \uc2 In his forthcoming memoir, the former Trump campaign manager \uc2 Paul Manafort\uc2  describes his travels through the US prison system after being convicted on tax charges \u8211\'20\'13 including a stay in a Manhattan facility alongside the financier and sex offender Jeffrey Epstein and the Mexican drug baron Joaqu\u237\'00\'EDn \u8220\'20\'1CEl Chapo\u8221\'20\'1D Guzm\u225\'00\'E1n.\par \par \uc2 Paul Manafort\uc2 . Photograph: Eduardo Mu\u241\'00\'F1oz/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Manafort also writes that during one transfer between facilities, at a private airfield \u8220\'20\'1Csomewhere in Ohio\u8221\'20\'1D, the sight of \u8220\'20\'1Cprisoners \u8230\'20\'26 being herded in long lines and then separated into other buses and on to \u8230\'20\'26 transport planes \u8230\'20\'26 reminded me of movies about the Holocaust\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 P olitical Prisoner: Persecuted, Prosecuted, but Not Silenced, will be published in the US next month. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  obtained a copy.\par \par \uc2 Manafort\u8217\'20\'19s book is not all quite so startling. But he does make the surprise admission that in 2020, he indirectly advised Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign while in home confinement as part of a seven-year sentence \u8211\'20\'13 advice he kept secret as he hoped for a presidential pardon.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI didn\u8217\'20\'19t want anything to get in the way of the president\u8217\'20\'19s re-election or, importantly, a potential pardon,\u8221\'20\'1D Manafort writes.\par \par \uc2 He got the pardon.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2022/jul/29/paul-manafort-indirectly-advising-trump-2020-secret-pardon-book-political-prisoner"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Paul Manafort admits indirectly advising Trump in 2020 but keeping it secret in wait for pardon }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Federal prosecutors ready for executive privilege fight\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors at the justice department are gearing up for a courtroom battle to force the testimony of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s former White House officials, as they pursue their criminal inquiry into his insurrection, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/07/28/politics/doj-court-trump-january-6-executive-privilege/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report published Friday by CNN}}}\uc2  says.\par \par \uc2 The former president is expected to try to invoke executive privilege to prevent his closest associates telling what they know about his conduct and actions following his 2020 election defeat, and efforts to prevent \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  taking office, according to the network.\par \par \uc2 But the department, which has taken a much more aggressive stance in recent weeks, is readying for that fight, CNN says, \u8220\'20\'1Cthe clearest sign yet\u8221\'20\'1D that the inquiry has become more narrowly focused on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s conversations and interactions.\par \par \uc2 Attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 . Photograph: Jacquelyn Martin/AP\par \par \uc2 This week attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  promised \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/26/garland-charge-trump-capitol-attack-jan-6-doj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 justice without fear or favor}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D for anyone caught up in insurrection efforts and would not rule out charging Trump criminally if that\u8217\'20\'19s where the evidence led.\par \par \uc2 He told NBC\u8217\'20\'19s Lester Holt :\par \par \uc2 We intend to hold everyone, anyone who was criminally responsible for events surrounding January 6, or any attempt to interfere with the lawful transfer of power from one administration to another, accountable.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s what we do. We don\u8217\'20\'19t pay any attention to other issues with respect to that.\par \par \uc2 CNN\u8217\'20\'19s story suggests that prosecutors are acutely aware that Trumpworld insiders who are initially reluctant to testify will be more inclined to do so with a judge\u8217\'20\'19s order compelling it.\par \par \uc2 The network also says Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attempt to maintain secrecy came up over recent federal grand jury testimony of two of former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s aides, Marc Short and Greg Jacob.\par \par \uc2 Questioning reportedly skirted around issues likely to be covered by executive privilege, with prosecutors having an expectation they could return to those subjects at a later date, CNN\u8217\'20\'19s sources said.\par \par \uc2 The development is set to add more legal pressure on Trump following the announcement of an evidence-sharing \u8220\'20\'1Cpartnership\u8221\'20\'1D between the justice department and the parallel House January 6 inquiry, in which transcripts of testimony from at least 20 witnesses are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/07/28/jan-6-witness-transcripts-doj-00048668"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passing to Garland\u8217\'20\'19s investigation.}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Good morning blog readers, we\u8217\'20\'19ve made it to the end of an extraordinary week in US politics, but we\u8217\'20\'19re not through quite yet. There\u8217\'20\'19s news today of more legal peril for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  over his efforts to illegitimately reverse his 2020 election defeat.\par \par \uc2 Justice department prosecutors, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/07/28/politics/doj-court-trump-january-6-executive-privilege/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to CNN}}}\uc2 , are preparing a court fight to force Trump insiders to testify over the former president\u8217\'20\'19s conversations and actions around January 6. They expect Trump to try to invoke executive privilege to prevent his former White House officials telling what they know.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll have more on that coming up, and will also be looking at the following:\par \par \uc2 * Washington is still abuzz with Senator Joe Manchin \u8217\'20\'19s stunning reversal, leading to the surprise announcement of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/28/joe-biden-climate-deal-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Inflation Reduction Act}}}\uc2  and the chance for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to achieve some of his signature climate policy goals.\par \par \uc2 * Text messages around the time of the January 6 Capitol riot \u8220\'20\'1Cvanished\u8221\'20\'1D from the the phones of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s senior homeland security officials \uc2 Chad Wolf\uc2  and Ken Cuccinelli, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2022/07/28/homeland-security-texts-jan6/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Washington Post reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * The Biden administration reportedly has a new plan for Covid-19 boosters, scrapping advice for a summer shot and concentrating instead on pushing next-generation vaccines in the fall.\par \par \uc2 * It could be a busy day in the House with possible votes on gun controls and police funding, before members head off for a six-week break. But the speaker, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , could call them back next week for a vote on the Inflation Reduction Act.\par \par \uc2 * The White House press secretary, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , has her daily briefing scheduled for 1.30pm. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has no public events listed.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220729ei7t0020d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
