\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: Texas Democrats push to blunt impact of state\u8217\'20\'19s  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban\b0\par\par\uc2 Nicola Slawson \par \uc2 1,305 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 July 2022\par 13:07 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Blue cities aim to pass bills to protect those who receive and provide abortions: \u8216\'20\'18The fight starts locally\u8217\'20\'19. Plus, the myth of Marilyn MonroeDon\u8217\'20\'19t already get First Thing in your inbox? Sign up here\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 Across Texas, Democratic-held cities are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/29/democratic-cities-texas-abortion-ban-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 galvanizing to mitigate the effects of the Republican-run state\u8217\'20\'19s near-total \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2  after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  voted in June to overturn Roe v Wade, the landmark case that gave Americans a constitutional right to terminate their pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 Texas\u8217\'20\'19s capital, Austin, voted last week to \u8220\'20\'1Cdecriminalize\u8221\'20\'1D \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the city by passing the Guarding the Right to \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Care for Everyone (Grace) Act. Although \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still illegal in the state, the passing of the Grace Act will redirect the city\u8217\'20\'19s budget to focus on going after more important crimes such as sexual assault, theft and burglary.\par \par \uc2 Local politicians in Waco, a city halfway between Austin and Dallas, followed suit and put forward their own version of the Grace Act for consideration.\par \par \uc2 Other cities such as San Antonio are also gearing up to protect those who receive and provide abortions. On Wednesday, the mayor, \uc2 Ron Nirenberg\uc2 , and the city council gathered on the steps of city hall to announce the consideration of a similar resolution in support of reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Will these cities succeed? Liberal cities face an uphill battle. City council member Teri Castillo, who drafted a resolution, anticipates the Republican party will identify ways to close potential loopholes or protections for those who wish or need to seek access to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What else is happening? The number of clinics offering \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care in 11 US states that have implemented total or six-week bans in the month since the supreme court overturned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights has dropped from 71 to 43, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/28/abortion-clincs-closing-states-roe-v-wade-guttmacher-study"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a study shows}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Could the US highways that split communities on racial lines finally fall?\par \par \uc2 When the US transportation department recently announced a $1bn five-year pilot program to aid communities racially segregated by \uc2 US government\uc2 -sponsored highway projects, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/29/could-the-us-highways-that-split-communities-on-racial-lines-finally-fall"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 local residents responded with a mix of optimism and tempered expectations}}}\uc2 . \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  singled out the Claiborne Expressway when the program, known as Reconnecting Communities, was first announced.\par \par \uc2 Experts and advocates question whether the initial investment is enough to reverse the devastation in Black neighborhoods in the name of connection. The amount unveiled by the transportation department is a far cry from the original $20bn proposed. But advocates agree that it\u8217\'20\'19s an unprecedented and welcome step in pursuit of highway reparations.\par \par \uc2 Under the department\u8217\'20\'19s program, announced in late June, cities, states, non-profits, tribal governments and city planning organizations can seek grants to conduct traffic studies, encourage public input on highway plans, and pursue other planning activities \u8220\'20\'1Cin advance of a project to remove, retrofit, or mitigate an existing eligible facility to restore community connectivity.\u8221\'20\'1D Communities can apply for $195m in grants in the first year, $50m for planning studies, and the remainder for capital construction.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What do those who live locally say? Amy Stelly, an urban designer and co-founder of the Claiborne Avenue Alliance, which is advocating for its removal, told the Guardian: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s the beginning, not the end, of the process.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18What about my life?\u8217\'20\'19 West Virginia girl, 12, speaks out against anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill\par \par \uc2 An impassioned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/28/west-virginia-girl-12-speaks-out-against-anti-abortion-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plea from a 12-year-old girl has gone viral}}}\uc2  after she spoke to West Virginia Republican lawmakers during a public hearing for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill that would prohibit the procedure in nearly all cases.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Addison Gardner of Buffalo middle school in Kenova, West Virginia, was among several people who spoke out against a bill that would not only ban abortions in most cases but also allow for physicians who perform abortions to be prosecuted.\par \par \uc2 Addressing the West Virginia house of delegates, Gardner, among about 90 other speakers, was given 45 seconds to plead her case.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy education is very important to me and I plan on doing great things in life. If a man decides that I\u8217\'20\'19m an object and does unspeakable and tragic things to me, am I, a child, supposed to carry and birth another child?\u8221\'20\'1D Gardner said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Why is \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  in the news? The US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/29/us-supreme-court-justice-mocks-prince-harry-and-boris-johnsons-criticism-of-roe-v-wade-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supreme court justice has mocked prominent figures around the world}}}\uc2  including British prime minister \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2 , French president \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2  and Prince Harry after they criticised last month\u8217\'20\'19s ruling that overturned Roe v Wade, the landmark 1973 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights decision.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Congressman\par \par \uc2 Andy Levin\par \par \uc2 , the scion of a distinguished Jewish political dynasty, a committed Zionist and the former president of his synagogue, has been stung by the largest pro-Israel lobby group\u8217\'20\'19s campaign to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/29/pro-israel-lobby-aipac-andy-levin-democratic-races"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 paint him as an enemy of the Jewish state}}}\uc2  because he has spoken up for the Palestinians.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Alabama has executed a man convicted of killing his ex-girlfriend nearly three decades ago, despite a request from the victim\u8217\'20\'19s family to spare his life. Joe Nathan James Jr received a lethal injection on Thursday night at a south Alabama prison after the US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/28/alabama-to-execute-convicted-killer-despite-opposition-from-victims-family"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supreme court denied his request for a stay}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Instagram\uc2  is reversing some changes to the app following a user backlash that saw influencer royalty\par \par \uc2 Kylie Jenner\par \par \uc2 and\par \par \uc2 Kim Kardashian\par \par \uc2 turning on the platform. The photo and video sharing app was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/jul/28/instagram-rolls-back-some-changes-to-app"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accused of mimicking TikTok}}}\uc2  at the expense of its most loyal users.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Novaya Gazeta\par \par \uc2 , one of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s last remaining independent news outlets, is under threat after the country\u8217\'20\'19s media watchdog demanded that its website and print edition be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/29/russian-news-outlet-novaya-gazeta-to-be-stripped-of-licence-under-court-order"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stripped of its licence}}}\uc2 . The announcement was made after the newspaper received two warnings over alleged violations.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: how Marilyn Monroe\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18sex bomb\u8217\'20\'19 image buries the truth\par \par \uc2 In life, Marilyn Monroe made herself noticed far beyond Hollywood and in ways very different from the corny \u8220\'20\'1Csex bomb\u8221\'20\'1D image that is the leitmotif of her modern iconography. Yet 60 years after she died, Monroe\u8217\'20\'19s vivid presence in the world\u8217\'20\'19s culture \u8211\'20\'13 only Diana, Princess of Wales rivals her hold over the public imagination \u8211\'20\'13 does not allow for nuance. The spectacle of Monroe\u8217\'20\'19s tumultuous life and death still holds us in its grip. With a major new biopic on the way, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2022/jul/29/the-myth-of-marilyn-monroe-how-her-sex-bomb-image-buries-the-truth"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 her biographer sorts fact from fiction}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Climate check:\par \par \uc2 what\u8217\'20\'19s in the climate bill that Joe Manchin supports \u8211\'20\'13 and what isn\u8217\'20\'19t\par \par \uc2 Joe Manchin, the centrist West Virginia senator and coal company owner who has repeatedly thwarted \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attempts to pass legislation to tackle the climate crisis, shocked Washington on Wednesday by saying he will support a bill aimed at cutting planet-heating emissions. The $369bn package has been touted by jubilant Democrats as the largest climate bill ever in the US, and even the world. So {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/jul/28/climate-bill-joe-manchin-whats-in-it"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 what\u8217\'20\'19s in the legislation?}}}\uc2  And what does Manchin support and not support in it?\par \par \uc2 Last Thing:\par \par \uc2 potential rival or running mate?\par \par \uc2 Kristi Noem\par \par \uc2 , the governor denying Trump a face on Mount Rushmore\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rough summer continues. Hammered by the January 6 committee, his influence ebbing and possible prosecution looming, now the former US president must face the death of a long-cherished dream. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/29/potential-rival-or-running-mate-kristi-noem-the-governor-denying-trump-a-face-on-mount-rushmore"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 No, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s face will not be carved into Mount Rushmore}}}\uc2 . \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2 , the Republican governor of South Dakota, home to the hallowed national memorial, has ruled out any additions to the 60-foot-tall (18-metre) faces of presidents George Washington, Thomas Jefferson, Abraham Lincoln and Theodore Roosevelt.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220729ei7t001gu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
