\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden hails \u8216\'20\'18most significant legislation to tackle climate crisis\u8217\'20\'19 after Manchin says yes \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Richard Luscombe \par \uc2 5,864 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 July 2022\par 20:04 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President lauds \u8216\'20\'18huge step forward\u8217\'20\'19 for his domestic agendaSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re closing the politics blog now on a rollercoaster Thursday for President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . The day began with depressing economic news that the US was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/jul/28/us-economy-gdp-second-quarter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 technically in a recession}}}\uc2 , but was brightened considerably by a bipartisan vote in the House that sends the $280bn Chips Act to his desk.\par \par \uc2 And then there was the unexpected development that Democratic West Virginia senator Joe Manchin, blamed for single handedly blocking the majority of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s first term agenda on the climate emergency and the economy, had reversed his position.\par \par \uc2 The Inflation Reduction Act Manchin negotiated with Democratic Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  is, Biden said, \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most significant legislation in history to tackle the climate crisis.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Thanks for joining us today. Before you go, please have a read of my colleague David Smith \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/28/joe-biden-climate-deal-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report on the reconciliation bill here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we followed today:\par \par \uc2 * Former treasury secretary \uc2 Steven Mnuchin\uc2  has spoken with the House panel investigating \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s January 6 insurrection, and the committee is negotiating to obtain testimony from other members of the former president\u8217\'20\'19s cabinet, the Associated Press reported.\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/07/28/doj-jan-6-panel-evidence-sharing-00048457"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reported}}}\uc2  that the House panel and the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s criminal inquiry had struck an testimony-sharing deal on witness transcripts and other evidence. The report came as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former chief of staff \uc2 Mick Mulvaney\uc2  spoke with the panel virtually.\par \par \uc2 * Biden and Chinese president \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2  spoke for more than two hours by phone, in what was reported to have been a sometimes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/28/xi-jinping-tells-joe-biden-not-to-play-with-fire-over-taiwan-in-two-hour-call"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 testy conversation}}}\uc2  including a discussion of \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s controversial upcoming trip to Taiwan.\par \par \uc2 * At least 43 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics in 11 states have closed since the supreme court eliminated federal protections for the procedure last month, and seven states no longer have any providers, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2022/07/one-month-post-roe-least-43-abortion-clinics-across-11-states-have-stopped-offering"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 study published Thursday}}}\uc2  by the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2  revealed. Prior to the ruling ending Roe v Wade protections, the 11 states had a total of 71 clinics providing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, the report says.\par \par \uc2 * The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.miamiherald.com/news/politics-government/state-politics/article263877522.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Miami Herald reported}}}\uc2  that a state operation touted last month by Republican governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  as a successful law enforcement action to \u8220\'20\'1Ckeep illegals out of Florida\u8221\'20\'1D ended up arresting mostly legal residents. Of 22 arrests in a three-day sweep from 7 to 9 June, the \u8220\'20\'1Cvast majority\u8221\'20\'1D were not related to immigration, the Herald said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 While chief of staff to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the retired general \uc2 John Kelly\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cshoved\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2  in a White House hallway, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jared-kushner"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jared Kushner}}}\uc2  writes in his forthcoming memoir.\par \par \uc2 The detail from Breaking History, which will be published in August, was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/07/27/kushner-kelly-shove-ivanka-trump/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  by the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Kushner, the Post said, writes that he and his wife saw Kelly as \u8220\'20\'1Cconsistently duplicitous\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne day he had just marched out of a contentious meeting in the Oval Office. Ivanka was walking down the main hallway in the West Wing when she passed him. Unaware of his heated state of mind, she said, \u8216\'20\'18Hello, chief.\u8217\'20\'19 Kelly shoved her out of the way and stormed by. She wasn\u8217\'20\'19t hurt, and didn\u8217\'20\'19t make a big deal about the altercation, but in his rage Kelly had shown his true character.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Jared Kushner\uc2  at her mother Ivana Trump\u8217\'20\'19s funeral on 20 July Photograph: Brendan McDermid/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Kushner writes that Kelly offered a \u8220\'20\'1Cmeek\u8221\'20\'1D apology about an hour later.\par \par \uc2 Kelly told the Post: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t recall anything like you describe. It is inconceivable that I would EVER shove a woman. Inconceivable. Never happen. Would never intentionally do something like that. Also, don\u8217\'20\'19t remember ever apologising to her for something I didn\u8217\'20\'19t do. I\u8217\'20\'19d remember that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ivanka-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ivanka Trump}}}\uc2  said her husband\u8217\'20\'19s description was accurate, the Post said.\par \par \uc2 The Post also said Kushner writes that Kelly gave his wife \u8220\'20\'1Ccompliments to her face that she knew were insincere.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThen the four-star general would call her staff to his office and berate and intimidate them over trivial procedural issues that his rigid system often created. He would frequently refer to her initiatives like paid family leave and the child tax credit as \u8216\'20\'18Ivanka\u8217\'20\'19s pet projects.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2022/jul/28/trump-chief-of-staff-john-kelly-ivanka-trump-shove-kushner-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump chief of staff \u8216\'20\'18shoved\u8217\'20\'19 Ivanka at White House, Kushner book says}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidential portrait will be unveiled at the White House in a September ceremony hosted by his former vice-president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Barack and \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2 . Photograph: Carolyn Kaster/AP\par \par \uc2 Portraits of the former president and first lady \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  will be presented in the East Room on 7 September, according to \uc2 Obama\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s office.\par \par \uc2 It will mark the first time the former first lady has returned to the White House since her husband left office in January 2017. \uc2 Barack Obama{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/video/2022/apr/05/obama-calls-biden-vice-president-on-return-to-the-white-house-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 went back in April}}}\uc2  to mark the 12th anniversary of his signature health care law.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 House passes Chips Act, places on Biden's desk\par \par \uc2 The House of Representative has delivered a big win for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , passing the $280bn {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.commerce.senate.gov/2022/7/view-the-chips-legislation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chips and Science Act}}}\uc2  that includes $52bn to boost the production of semiconductors.\par \par \uc2 The bill cleared the Senate 64-33 in a bipartisan vote yesterday, the president urging the House to get the bill to his desk as soon as possible to help ease a shortage in semiconductors he said is holding back US defense, healthcare and vehicle manufacturing industries.\par \par \uc2 Biden received the news of the bill\u8217\'20\'19s House passage, 243-187 in a strong bipartisan vote, during a virtual round table with business leaders at the White House this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe moment {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2  gets word that the CHIPS Act has enough votes to pass the House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2CqAnr8oVc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/2CqAnr8oVc}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Andrew Feinberg (@AndrewFeinberg) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewFeinberg/status/1552732347069566981?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 28, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Biden earlier highlighted the Chips Act as a central plank of his agenda to boost American industry, as he also hailed the newly announced $739bn Inflation Reduction Act.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/07/28/statement-from-president-biden-on-house-passage-of-chips-and-science-act-to-lower-costs-create-good-pay-jobs-and-strengthen-our-national-security/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In a statement}}}\uc2 , the president said the Chips Act \u8220\'20\'1Cwill make cars cheaper, appliances cheaper, and computers cheaper. It will lower the costs of every day goods. And, it will create high-paying manufacturing jobs across the country and strengthen US leadership in the industries of the future at the same time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Republicans had threatened to whip members against voting for the Chips Act after they were angered by last night\u8217\'20\'19s announcement of the reconciliation bill, brokered in a deal between Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  and previously reluctant West Virginia senator Joe Manchin.\par \par \uc2 Read my colleague David Smith \u8217\'20\'19s report on the proposed new legislation here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/28/joe-biden-climate-deal-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden hails Senate deal as \u8216\'20\'18most significant\u8217\'20\'19 US climate legislation ever}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden: 'Signs of economic progress in second quarter'\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a double helping of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  today, the president just delivering remarks on the economy at an afternoon White House roundtable of business leaders.\par \par \uc2 Once again, the president is downplaying the suggestion, bolstered by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/jul/28/us-economy-gdp-second-quarter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this morning\u8217\'20\'19s dismal GDP figures}}}\uc2 , that the US is in a recession:\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19ll be a lot of chatter today on Wall Street and among pundits about whether we are in a recession. But if you\u8217\'20\'19re looking at our job market, consumer spending business investment, we see signs of economic progress in the second quarter as well.\par \par \uc2 And yesterday, Fed chairman [Jerome] Powell made it clear that he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t think the US economy is currently in a recession. He said, quote, there are too many areas of economics where the economy is performing too well.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  with \uc2 Bank of America\uc2  chief executive \uc2 Brian Moynihan\uc2  at the virtual round table with business leaders. Photograph: Mandel Ngan/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 For the second time today, following his address earlier this afternoon on the Inflation Reduction Act, Biden listed positive factors, including job creation, low unemployment and foreign investment in US industry.\par \par \uc2 I applaud by the bipartisan effort to get the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/07/27/senate-chips-funding-bill-pass/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chips Act}}}\uc2  to my desk, which would advance our nation\u8217\'20\'19s competitiveness and technological edge by boosting our domestic semiconductor production and manufacturing.\par \par \uc2 Another thing Congress should do is to pass the Inflation Reduction Act to lower prescription drug costs, reduce the deficit, help ease inflationary pressures and ensure 13m Americans can continue to save an average of $800 per year on health care premiums.\par \par \uc2 Both of these bills are going to help the economy continue to grow, bring down inflation and make sure we aren\u8217\'20\'19t giving up on all the significant progress we made in the last year.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Mnuchin cooperating with January 6 inquiry\par \par \uc2 Former treasury secretary \uc2 Steven Mnuchin\uc2  has spoken with the House panel investigating \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s January 6 insurrection, and the committee is negotiating to obtain testimony from other members of the former president\u8217\'20\'19s cabinet, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Steven Mnuchin\uc2 . Photograph: Jim Lo Scalzo/AP\par \par \uc2 The panel is looking into the days following the deadly Capitol riot and discussions between senior officials over whether to try to remove the then-president from office.\par \par \uc2 The negotiations come as the committee was interviewing Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former chief of staff, \uc2 Mick Mulvaney\uc2 , on Thursday. The former South Carolina congressman was special envoy for Northern Ireland on January 6 2022, a post he resigned immediately after the riot.\par \par \uc2 The AP says Mnuchin\u8217\'20\'19s interview, and the negotiations with others, were confirmed by three people familiar with the committee\u8217\'20\'19s work, who spoke on condition of anonymity.\par \par \uc2 The agency says the committee asked Mnuchin about discussions among cabinet secretaries to possibly invoke the constitutional process in the 25th Amendment to remove Trump after the attack on the Capitol, according to one of the people, and is in talks to interview former secretary of state \uc2 Mike Pompeo\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The panel has already interviewed former acting attorney general Jeffrey Rosen, former labor secretary \uc2 Eugene Scalia\uc2  and former acting defense secretary \uc2 Christopher Miller\uc2  as it focuses on Trump and what he was doing in the days before, during and after the riot.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ve written plenty about the Inflation Reduction Act today, and heard that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  believes it\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most significant bill to tackle the climate crisis in history\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 So what\u8217\'20\'19s actually in it?\par \par \uc2 My colleague Oliver Milman has this handy explainer to what made it into the package. And what didn\u8217\'20\'19t:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/jul/28/climate-bill-joe-manchin-whats-in-it"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s in the climate bill that Joe Manchin supports \u8211\'20\'13 and what isn\u8217\'20\'19t }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 We now have the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/07/28/readout-of-president-bidens-call-with-president-xi-jinping-of-the-peoples-republic-of-china/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 White House readout }}}\uc2  of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s two hour conversation with China\u8217\'20\'19s President \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2  this morning:\par \par \uc2 The call was a part of the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to maintain and deepen lines of communication between the US and PRC [People\u8217\'20\'19s Republic of China] and responsibly manage our differences and work together where our interests align.\par \par \uc2 The two presidents discussed a range of issues important to the bilateral relationship and other regional and global issues, and tasked their teams to continue following up on today\u8217\'20\'19s conversation, in particular to address climate change and health security.\par \par \uc2 It seems they also touched on \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s controversial {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/28/nancy-pelosi-invited-us-lawmakers-to-visit-taiwan-hears-committee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 upcoming trip to Taiwan}}}\uc2 , which has angered Chinese leaders. The White House readout said:\par \par \uc2 On Taiwan, President Biden underscored that the United States policy has not changed and that the United States strongly opposes unilateral efforts to change the status quo or undermine peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait.\par \par \uc2 The Chinese take, according to the Associated Press, was equally defiant.\par \par \uc2 The news agency quoted an account of the call by China\u8217\'20\'19s ministry of foreign affairs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThose who play with fire will perish by it. It is hoped that the US will be clear-eyed about this,\u8221\'20\'1D it said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Xi underscored that to approach and define China-US relations in terms of strategic competition and view China as the primary rival and the most serious long-term challenge would be misperceiving China-US relations and misreading China\u8217\'20\'19s development, and would mislead the people of the two countries and the international community.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 At least 43 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics in 11 states have closed since the supreme court eliminated federal protections for the procedure last month, and seven states no longer have any providers, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2022/07/one-month-post-roe-least-43-abortion-clinics-across-11-states-have-stopped-offering"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 study published Thursday}}}\uc2  by the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2  has found.\par \par \uc2 Prior to the ruling ending Roe v Wade protections on 24 June, the 11 states had a total of 71 clinics providing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, the report says.\par \par \uc2 enltr?? As of July 24, these 7 US states ?? had banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  completely following the \uc2 SCOTUS\uc2  decision to overturn {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/RoeVWade?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #RoeVWade}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 ? Alabama\par \par \uc2 ? Arkansas\par \par \uc2 ? Mississippi\par \par \uc2 ? Missouri\par \par \uc2 ? Oklahoma\par \par \uc2 ? South Dakota\par \par \uc2 ? Texas {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/BansOffOurBodies?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #BansOffOurBodies}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6r9oaGNzqJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/6r9oaGNzqJ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2  (@Guttmacher) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Guttmacher/status/1552681553423106051?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 28, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 As of 24 July, there were only 28 clinics still offering abortions, all located in the four states with six-week bans. Across these 11 states, the number of clinics offering abortions dropped by 43 in just one month.\par \par \uc2 The seven states no longer offering any \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provision are Alabama (previously 5 clinics), Arkansas (2), Mississippi (1), Missouri (1), Oklahoma (5), South Dakota (1) and Texas (23 ).\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CObtaining an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was already difficult in many states even before the supreme court overturned Roe,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Rachel Jones\uc2 , Guttmacher\u8217\'20\'19s principal research scientist, said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese clinic closures resulting from state-level bans will further deepen inequities in access to care based on race, gender, income, age or immigration status since long travel distances to reach a clinic in another state will be a barrier for many people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  thanked Democratic senators Joe Manchin and \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the Senate majority leader, for their \u8220\'20\'1Cextraordinary effort\u8221\'20\'1D in negotiating the reconciliation bill.\par \par \uc2 It had looked like Manchin had killed hope of any of the president\u8217\'20\'19s signature policy goals on the climate emergency or the economy passing when he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/video/2021/dec/19/joe-manchin-says-he-cannot-get-there-on-build-back-better-bill-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 withdrew from talks}}}\uc2  on Build Back Better earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 The West Virginia senator, however, insisted earlier today he \u8220\'20\'1Cnever walked away\u8221\'20\'1D and was always open to renewed discussions, on parts of the package at least, which were finally concluded on Wednesday after weeks of secret meetings with Schumer and his staff.\par \par \uc2 Biden said:\par \par \uc2 I know can sometimes seem like nothing gets done in Washington. I know it never crossed any of your minds. But the work of the government can be slow and frustrating and sometimes even infuriating.\par \par \uc2 Then the hard work of hours and days and months from people who refuse to give up pays off.\par \par \uc2 History has been made. Lives have changed with this legislation. We\u8217\'20\'19re facing up to some of our biggest problems. And we\u8217\'20\'19re taking a giant step forward as a nation.\par \par \uc2 Biden closed his address with remarks on data that came out this morning showing the economy had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/jul/28/us-economy-gdp-second-quarter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shrunk for a second successive quarter}}}\uc2 , and that the US was technically in a recession.\par \par \uc2 He listed low unemployment, overseas investment in US manufacturing and yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s passing by the Senate of the Chips Act boosting semiconductor production among a number of reasons why he believes the US economy is strong.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat doesn\u8217\'20\'19t sound like a recession to me,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden: 'Most significant legislation in history to tackle climate crisis'\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  hailed the Inflation Reduction Act as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most significant legislation in history to tackle the climate crisis\u8221\'20\'1D in a White House address welcoming the wide-ranging legislative package.\par \par \uc2 The president outlined the benefits to Americans during his remarks, which followed the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/27/manchin-deal-democrats-schumer-reconciliation-bill-climate-health"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 surprise announcement of a deal last night}}}\uc2  between Democratic Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  and holdout West Virginia senator Joe Manchin.\par \par \uc2 This bill will be the most significant legislation in history to tackle the climate crisis and improve our energy security right away, and give us a tool to meet the climate goals... we\u8217\'20\'19ve agreed to by cutting emissions and accelerating clean energy. It\u8217\'20\'19s a huge step forward.\par \par \uc2 This bill will reduce inflationary pressures on the economy. It will cut your cost of living and reduce inflation, it lowers the deficit and strengthens our economy for the long run as well.\par \par \uc2 This bill has won the support of climate leaders like former vice-president \uc2 Al Gore\uc2 , who said the bill is, quote, long overdue and a necessary step to ensure the United States takes decisive action on the climate crisis that helps our economy and provides leadership for the world.\par \par \uc2 Climate activists have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/jul/28/joe-manchin-climate-bill-fossil-fuels-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 broadly welcomed the bill}}}\uc2  which, if passed by Congress, would give Biden a massive victory ahead of November\u8217\'20\'19s midterms. Inflation at 40-year highs and soaring prices in supermarkets and at gas pumps have contributed to the president\u8217\'20\'19s low approval ratings.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  speaks about the Inflation Reduction Act at the White House Thursday Photograph: Susan Walsh/AP\par \par \uc2 It also follows months of stalling on Biden\u8217\'20\'19s agenda, specifically by Manchin, who didn\u8217\'20\'19t like the cost of $1.8tn Build Back Better spending package featuring measures like extended child tax credit.\par \par \uc2 Biden acknowledged:\par \par \uc2 This bill is far from perfect. I know the bill doesn\u8217\'20\'19t include everything that I\u8217\'20\'19ve been pushing for since I got to office. For example, I\u8217\'20\'19m going to keep fighting to bring down the cost of things for working families and middle class families by providing for things like affordable childcare, affordable elder care, the cost of preschool, housing, helping students with the cost of college, closing the health care coverage gap...\par \par \uc2 My message to Congress is this. This is the strongest bill you can pass to lower inflation, cut the deficit, reduce health care costs, tackle the climate crisis and promote energy security, all the time while reducing the burdens facing working class and middle class families.\par \par \uc2 So pass it. Pass it for the American people. Pass it for America.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden speaks on Inflation Reduction Act\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is about to deliver a hastily arranged address about the Inflation Reduction Act, the White House says.\par \par \uc2 You can {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XMH_kuPjE5U"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 watch the president\u8217\'20\'19s remarks here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cwas not involved\u8221\'20\'1D in negotiations over the newly announced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/27/manchin-deal-democrats-schumer-reconciliation-bill-climate-health"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Inflation Reduction Act}}}\uc2 , Joe Manchin has said, claiming credit instead for himself and his own aides.\par \par \uc2 In a press call Thursday morning that shed a little more light, but not very much, on how the bill came to be, the Democratic West Virginia senator said:\par \par \uc2 It was me and my staff. And then we worked with [Senate majority leader Chuck] Schumer\u8217\'20\'19s staff. My staff was driving it. We wrote the bill. Schumer\u8217\'20\'19s staff would look at it and we would negotiate, and we worked that through them.\par \par \uc2 President Biden was not involved.\par \par \uc2 In comments to Punchbowl last night, Manchin said he and Schumer were old friends, and claimed he had pressed ahead with negotiations despite months of \u8220\'20\'1Cass kicking\u8221\'20\'1D from other Democrats angry he blocked Biden\u8217\'20\'19s flagship Build Back Better bill, a $1.8tn package incorporating tax reform, climate measures and social welfare spending.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Climate advocates reacted with surprise and delight to Joe Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/27/manchin-deal-democrats-schumer-reconciliation-bill-climate-health"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decision}}}\uc2  to back a sweeping bill to combat the climate crisis, with analysts predicting the legislation will bring the US close to its target of slashing planet-heating emissions.\par \par \uc2 The West Virginia senator, who has made millions from his ownership of a coal-trading company, had seemingly thwarted \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s hopes of passing meaningful climate legislation \u8211\'20\'13 only to reveal on Wednesday his support for a $369bn package to support renewable energy and electric vehicle rollout.\par \par \uc2 The move by the centrist Democrat shocked many of Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s colleagues, who despaired after more than 18 months of seemingly fruitless negotiations with the lawmaker, a crucial vote in an evenly divided Senate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHoly shit,\u8221\'20\'1D tweeted \uc2 Tina Smith\uc2 , a Democrat from Minnesota. \u8220\'20\'1CStunned, but in a good way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrHoly shit. Stunned, but in a good way. $370B for climate and energy and 40% emissions reduction by 2030.\par \par \uc2 BFD. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/0pNuIjh3hY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/0pNuIjh3hY}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senator \uc2 Tina Smith\uc2  (@SenTinaSmith) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenTinaSmith/status/1552414678214664193?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 27, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Should the bill pass both chambers of Congress and be signed by Biden, it will be the biggest and arguably first piece of climate legislation ever enacted by the US. The world\u8217\'20\'19s largest historical carbon polluter has repeatedly failed to act on the climate crisis due to missed opportunities, staunch Republican opposition and the machinations of the fossil fuel lobby.\par \par \uc2 The climate spending, part of a broader bill called the Inflation Reduction Act, \u8220\'20\'1Chas the potential to be a historic turning point\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Al Gore\uc2 , the former vice-president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt represents the single largest investment in climate solutions and environmental justice in US history. Decades of tireless work by climate advocates across the country led to this moment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The bulk of the bill includes hefty tax credits to unleash clean energy projects such as wind and solar as well as a rebate of up to $7,500 for Americans who want to buy new electric vehicles. There is $9bn to retrofit houses to make them more energy efficient, tax credits for heat pumps and rooftop solar and a $27bn \u8220\'20\'1Cclean energy technology accelerator\u8221\'20\'1D to help deploy new renewable technology.\par \par \uc2 A further $60bn would go towards environmental justice projects and there is a new program to reduce leaks of methane, a potent greenhouse gas, from oil and gas drilling.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/jul/28/joe-manchin-climate-bill-fossil-fuels-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Activists surprised and relieved at Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s decision to back climate bill}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Evidence-sharing 'partnership' spells new peril for Trump\par \par \uc2 There are developments today in the investigations into \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to stay in office following his 2020 election defeat, including news of a \u8220\'20\'1Cpartnership\u8221\'20\'1D between the House inquiry and justice department over witness testimony.\par \par \uc2 The sharing of witness transcripts and other evidence, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/07/28/doj-jan-6-panel-evidence-sharing-00048457"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported by Politico,}}}\uc2  is a \u8220\'20\'1Csignificant milestone\u8221\'20\'1D the media outlet says, and comes as justice department sources reveal its criminal inquiry has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2022/07/26/trump-justice-investigation-january-6/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 narrowed on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s own actions}}}\uc2  during the insurrection.\par \par \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2 . Photograph: J Scott Applewhite/AP\par \par \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2 , the Mississippi Democrat chairing the bipartisan House inquiry, told Politico: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve put a template together for sharing information, sharing it with Justice. My understanding is, there\u8217\'20\'19s general agreement on it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A number of Trumpworld insiders have testified to the panel in recent weeks, including the former president\u8217\'20\'19s ex-chief of staff, \uc2 Mick Mulvaney\uc2 , today.\par \par \uc2 Mulvaney {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/blogs/pundits-blog/healthcare/3540664-mulvaney-things-could-get-very-dark-for-trump-after-hutchinson-testimony/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told The Hill last month}}}\uc2  he believed \u8220\'20\'1Cthings could get very dark\u8221\'20\'1D for Trump after allegations in the House panel\u8217\'20\'19s recent public hearings that he attempted to intimidate witnesses from giving testimony.\par \par \uc2 Since then, others, including former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s ex-chief of staff Marc Short, have provided their own insight into Trump\u8217\'20\'19s scheming to prevent \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  from becoming president... potentially damaging testimony that is now, or soon could be, also in the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s hands.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with NBC News on Tuesday, attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  refused to rule out charging Trump, promising to \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/26/garland-charge-trump-capitol-attack-jan-6-doj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pursue justice without fear or favor}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D for anyone criminally responsible for the insurrection or preventing the peaceful transfer of power.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden: Economy 'on right path' despite unofficial recession\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is talking up the US economy in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/07/28/statement-by-president-biden-on-second-quarter-gdp-report/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement from the White House}}}\uc2 , even as depressing data released Thursday indicates a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/jul/28/us-economy-gdp-second-quarter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recession has technically begun}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CComing off of last year\u8217\'20\'19s historic economic growth - and regaining all the private sector jobs lost during the pandemic crisis - it\u8217\'20\'19s no surprise that the economy is slowing down as the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  acts to bring down inflation,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said, referring to Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s decision to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/jul/27/fed-increase-interest-rates-inflation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hike interest rates}}}\uc2  by 0.75%.\par \par \uc2 But even as we face historic global challenges, we are on the right path and we will come through this transition stronger and more secure. Our job market remains historically strong, with unemployment at 3.6% and more than 1m jobs created in the second quarter alone.\par \par \uc2 My economic plan is focused on bringing inflation down, without giving up all the economic gains we have made. Congress has an historic chance to do that by passing the Chips and Science Act and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/27/manchin-deal-democrats-schumer-reconciliation-bill-climate-health"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Inflation Reduction Act}}}\uc2  without delay.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll hear more from the president in public comments this lunchtime after he meets with chief executives of key industries.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Miami Herald is reporting that a state operation touted last month by Republican governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  as a successful law enforcement action to \u8220\'20\'1Ckeep illegals out of Florida\u8221\'20\'1D ended up arresting mostly legal residents.\par \par \uc2 According to the newspaper, of 22 arrests made by the Florida highway patrol and four county sheriffs offices in a three-day sweep from 7 to 9 June, the \u8220\'20\'1Cvast majority\u8221\'20\'1D were not related to immigration.\par \par \uc2 enltrGov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  highlighted a law enforcement operation designed to combat illegal immigration.\par \par \uc2 What he didn't mention is that vast majority of arrests were of legal residents, who committed drug-related crimes, a key focus of the operation. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/teu2riopsz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/teu2riopsz}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ana Ceballos (@anaceballos_) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/anaceballos_/status/1552643622620766209?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 28, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 At a press conference in Pensacola, DeSantis also implied that undocumented migrants had been arrested on drug-related crimes, when none were, the Herald said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey were able to recover these illegal aliens and enough fentanyl to kill off 2,000 people in the state of Florida,\u8221\'20\'1D DeSantis told reporters.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis, tipped as a likely contender for the Republican presidential nomination in 2024, frequently bashes \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  on immigration and has previously been criticized for spending taxpayer money on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tampabay.com/news/florida-politics/2021/11/30/desantis-law-enforcement-border-mission-racks-up-16-million-bill/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sending Florida law enforcement officers for security duty at the US southern border in Texas}}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.miamiherald.com/news/politics-government/state-politics/article263877522.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the Miami Herald\u8217\'20\'19s report here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 The comedian \uc2 Jon Stewart\uc2  ripped into Republican senators on Wednesday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/07/27/politics/senate-burn-pit-bill-fails/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 after they abruptly halted}}}\uc2  a bipartisan bill that would expand healthcare access for military veterans exposed to toxic burn pits.\par \par \uc2 The former host of the Daily Show, who now hosts The Problem with \uc2 Jon Stewart\uc2  on Apple TV+, has lobbied for the bill.\par \par \uc2 Jon Stewart\uc2 . Photograph: J Scott Applewhite/AP\par \par \uc2 He {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jonstewart/status/1552445098738450432"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  those who switched their votes \u8220\'20\'1Cstab-vets-in-the-back senators\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jonstewart/status/1552428722564775941"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 added}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CPS: fuck the Republican caucus and their empty promise to our veterans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The measure, called the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reed.senate.gov/news/releases/us-senate-passes-pact-act-to-support-veterans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Honoring our Pact Act}}}\uc2 , would make it easier for veterans to access military care related to exposure to Agent Orange in Vietnam and toxins from pits used to burn military waste in Iraq and Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 A version of the bill passed the Senate 84-14 earlier this year but was sent back to the House for some technical corrections. It easily passed there.\par \par \uc2 But on Wednesday, 25 Republican senators who previously supported the measure declined to move it forward.\par \par \uc2 John Cornyn\uc2 , a Texas Republican, told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/07/27/politics/senate-burn-pit-bill-fails/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN}}}\uc2  Republicans did not back the measure because \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the Senate majority leader, was blocking votes on amendments Republicans wanted.\par \par \uc2 Cornyn also said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  wanted to negotiate more, in order to cut out some of the mandatory spending contained in the bill.\par \par \uc2 Stewart called that justification {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jonstewart/status/1552429255430135810"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cbullshit\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Republicans blocked the veterans measure just after Schumer, from New York, and Joe Manchin, of West Virginia, announced they had reached a deal on a sweeping tax and climate measure.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/28/republicans-bill-healthcare-military-veterans-jon-stewart"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Anger as Republicans block bill to help military veterans exposed to toxins}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Schumer: Democrats must be disciplined on Manchin deal\par \par \uc2 Majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  told Senate Democrats at a private caucus meeting this morning they had an opportunity to achieve two \u8220\'20\'1Chugely important\u8221\'20\'1D priorities on health care and climate change, by approving the Inflation Reduction Act he brokered with Joe Manchin.\par \par \uc2 Schumer warned colleagues that final passage of the $739bn package will be hard in the 50-50 senate, according to the Associated Press, quoting an source granted anonymity to relay his private comments.\par \par \uc2 He said they would need to be disciplined in messaging and focus, but he believes they can get it done, the person added.\par \par \uc2 Two Democrats told the agency the Senate would vote on the wide-ranging measure next week, setting up \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Democrats for an unexpected victory in the run-up to November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections if the bill overcomes what will almost certainly be unanimous Republican opposition.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden and Xi in lengthy phone discussion\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is speaking with China\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2 , the fifth conversation of their presidencies, as the two leaders chart the future of their complicated relationship at a time of simmering economic and geopolitical tensions, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re waiting for the White House to reveal details of the call, which began at 8.33am, but the agency said Biden is seeking new ways to work with the rising global power as well as strategies to contain China\u8217\'20\'19s influence around the world.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s also tension over \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/28/nancy-pelosi-invited-us-lawmakers-to-visit-taiwan-hears-committee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposed upcoming trip to Taiwan}}}\uc2 , which has angered Chinese leadership.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you more information as we learn it.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Manchin: 'I've never walked away from anything'\par \par \uc2 Joe Manchin has been defending his unexpected U-turn on climate and tax policy that resulted in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/27/manchin-deal-democrats-schumer-reconciliation-bill-climate-health"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Inflation Reduction Act}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 West Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic senator, who is in isolation following a positive test for Covid-19, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://punchbowl.news/archive/7-28-22-punchbowl-news-am/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told Punchbowl}}}\uc2  that it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t a reversal at all.\par \par \uc2 Joe Manchin. Photograph: Elizabeth Frantz/Reuters\par \par \uc2 And he said that he had endured months of criticism from progressive Democrats and others for derailing much of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s ambitious first-term agenda - or \u8220\'20\'1Cone hell of an ass-kicking\u8221\'20\'1D as he eloquently described it.\par \par \uc2 Of his secretive negotiations with Democratic Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  that led to last night\u8217\'20\'19s announcement, Manchin said:\par \par \uc2 I never gave up.\par \par \uc2 The smart thing politically for me [to] do once Build Back Better was done and I walked away was to let a sleeping dog lie.\par \par \uc2 But when you get a moment in time, and if you know in your heart something needs to be done, it\u8217\'20\'19s the right thing.\par \par \uc2 Manchin also said the reconciliation bill was born of his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jan/08/joe-manchin-build-back-better-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 resistance to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s flagship $1.8tn Build Back Better}}}\uc2  spending package, which he scuppered because he didn\u8217\'20\'19t like the cost. He told Punchbowl:\par \par \uc2 Remember when I told you I didn\u8217\'20\'19t walk away? I never walked away. I\u8217\'20\'19ve never walked away from anything.\par \par \uc2 And I\u8217\'20\'19ve been trying to tell people that. The bottom line was inflation scared the bejesus out of me at 9.1%. I said, \u8216\'20\'18I\u8217\'20\'19m gonna go back and re-scrub that bill.\u8217\'20\'19 And then, you know, Chuck and I have a little bit of a relationship, if you will. Good, bad, indifferent at times, but it\u8217\'20\'19s always been respectful and he got mad...\par \par \uc2 So Monday, I said, \u8216\'20\'18Chuck, I\u8217\'20\'19m not walking away, never have, my people are still working. If you want to see if we can basically scrub everything and make sure it\u8217\'20\'19s not inflationary.\u8217\'20\'19 That\u8217\'20\'19s just how this went.\par \par \uc2 And he says, \u8216\'20\'18Yeah, we\u8217\'20\'19re willing to engage again.\u8217\'20\'19 And I said, \u8216\'20\'18OK, if you want to engage again.\u8217\'20\'19 I said, \u8216\'20\'18We haven\u8217\'20\'19t stopped, we\u8217\'20\'19re going through everything, taking out anything that we think could be inflammatory.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 And I gotta give him credit, they were OK. And we went through the whole thing.\par \par \uc2 Now the reconciliation bill is announced, and assuming it passes the scrutiny of the House and Senate parliamentarians, Democrats have to get it passed.\par \par \uc2 They will need all 50 of their votes in the Senate, and Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  is a notable tax-hike skeptic. A spokesperson told the Guardian she won\u8217\'20\'19t comment on the bill until she \u8220\'20\'1Creviews the text and what comes out of the parliamentarian process.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Another potential headache: Illinois Democrat Dick Durbin tested positive today for Covid-19 and is isolating, but is expected to be back for any Senate vote.\par \par \uc2 Over in the House, meanwhile, where Democrats hold a slim four-seat majority, there are questions over New Jersey representatives \uc2 Josh Gottheimer\uc2  and Mikie Sherill, and \uc2 Tom Suozzi\uc2  of New York, who say they won\u8217\'20\'19t support tax changes without certain concessions.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll hear more from Manchin at 10.45am in a hastily arranged press call.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Manchin reverses course on Biden reconciliation bill\par \par \uc2 Good morning politics blog readers and happy Thursday. If you didn\u8217\'20\'19t see it last night, you\u8217\'20\'19re waking to news of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/27/manchin-deal-democrats-schumer-reconciliation-bill-climate-health"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stunning reversal by senator Joe Manchin}}}\uc2  on tax and climate policy, and his agreement with Democratic Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  for a comprehensive new bill, following weeks of stealthy negotiations.\par \par \uc2 The concession by the rebel West Virginia Democrat, who almost single handedly has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/17/sanders-manchin-sabotages-biden-agenda"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 thwarted much of Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s ambitious first-term agenda}}}\uc2 , surprised and angered congressional Republicans, who in an immediate apparent act of revenge \u8211\'20\'13 and self-sabotage \u8211\'20\'13 then {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/28/republicans-bill-healthcare-military-veterans-jon-stewart"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked a bipartisan Senate bill}}}\uc2  expanding healthcare access for certain military veterans.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll have more analysis of Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s unexpected reversal, and the consequences of it, coming up.\par \par \uc2 Joe Manchin in February. Photograph: Tom Brenner/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re looking at today:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is scheduled to speak on the state of the economy at 2.15pm, following this morning\u8217\'20\'19s depressing data showing it has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/jul/28/us-economy-gdp-second-quarter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shrunk two quarters in a row}}}\uc2  and pushed the US closer to recession. The president is meeting chief executives of key sectors and industries this morning for updates.\par \par \uc2 * We\u8217\'20\'19ll have more news about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s actions surrounding the January 6 insurrection, which are the subject of inquiries by a House panel and the department of justice.\par \par \uc2 * Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  is hosting an event about reproductive health care at 11am.\par \par \uc2 * White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s daily briefing is listed for 3.15pm, but she has been running up to an hour late on other days this week.\par \par \uc2 * Republicans and Democrats can work out their grievances on the diamond in the annual congressional baseball game at 7pm.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220728ei7s001pf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
