\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Sharp rise in US  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  clinic closures after Roe v Wade overturned\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang in New York \par \uc2 492 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 July 2022\par 16:40 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Guttmacher\uc2  study shows reduction in clinics offering care in 11 states that have implemented bans since supreme court ruling\par \par \uc2 The number of clinics offering \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care in 11 US states that have implemented total or six-week bans in the month since the supreme court overturned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights has dropped from 71 to 43, a new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2022/07/one-month-post-roe-least-43-abortion-clinics-across-11-states-have-stopped-offering"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 study}}}\uc2  shows.\par \par \uc2 In the study released on Thursday, the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a nonprofit that studies sexual and reproductive health, said that among the the 11 states, as of 24 July seven no longer had a single clinic providing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care.\par \par \uc2 Those states were Alabama, Arkansas, Mississippi, Missouri, Oklahoma, South Dakota and Texas.\par \par \uc2 The majority of those states had between one and five \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics before the conservative-dominated court overturned Roe v Wade, the landmark 1973 decision that affirmed the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The seven states accounted for 80,500 abortions in 2020, an average of 6,700 a month.\par \par \uc2 As of 24 July, the Guttmacher report said, four states \u8211\'20\'13 Georgia, Ohio, South Carolina and Tennessee \u8211\'20\'13 had implemented an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban starting at six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 According to the study, Georgia and Tennessee now have fewer clinics providing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services than before the supreme court decision. Georgia, which previously had 14 clinics, now has 13. In Tennessee, the number of clinics dropped from seven to three.\par \par \uc2 One reason the institute cited as a probable cause for falling numbers of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics in such states is that many people are not able to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to the drastically shortened access window.\par \par \uc2 Before six weeks of pregnancy, many are unaware they are pregnant. Those who are aware are left with two weeks at most to decide whether to undergo an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , then schedule and obtain one, which usually includes logistical obstacles such as long and sometimes forced waiting periods.\par \par \uc2 Such restrictions can push people beyond the six-week limit, thus making an in-state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  very difficult to obtain.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, \uc2 Rachel Jones\uc2 , principal research scientist at the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , said: \u8220\'20\'1CWhile 11 states already had complete or six-week bans one month after the decision, even more will implement \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in the coming days, weeks and months.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CKentucky and Florida have begun rolling back access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  by implementing 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. Meanwhile, in Wisconsin, legal uncertainty over the status of the state\u8217\'20\'19s pre-Roe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban has caused providers to stop offering \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn total, as many as 26 states are certain or likely to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  now that Roe is no longer in place.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese clinic closures resulting from state-level bans will further deepen inequities in access to care based on race, gender, income, age or immigration status since long travel distances to reach a clinic in another state will be a barrier for many people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220728ei7s0025t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
