\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Judge blocks Georgia DA from investigating \u8216\'20\'18fake elector\u8217\'20\'19 in setback for Trump inquiry \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Richard Luscombe \par \uc2 5,618 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 July 2022\par 20:16 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Judge\u8217\'20\'19s decision considered a complication in inquiry widely seen as one of the best chances of holding Trump liable for his \u8216\'20\'18big lie\u8217\'20\'19Sign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re closing the US politics blog now. It\u8217\'20\'19s been a busy day, thanks for being with us, and please join us again tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what we\u8217\'20\'19ve been following today:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  appeared at a virtual White House roundtable on the semiconductor industry, sounding somewhat hoarse from his Covid-19 infection, coughing occasionally and sipping from a mug, but otherwise looking relatively healthy. White House physician Kevin O\u8217\'20\'19Connor said the president was \u8220\'20\'1Calmost completely\u8221\'20\'1D recovered after contracting the virus last week.\par \par \uc2 * Six staffers were arrested in Congress for staging a sit-in at Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s office to protest a lack of legislative action on the environment. One male staffer said they were demanding renewed negotiations on the climate reconciliation package.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Elaine Luria\uc2 , a member of the January 6 House panel looking into \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to reverse his 2020 election defeat, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1551571605121339392"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posted to Twitter}}}\uc2  a video featuring handwritten changes he made to a speech the day after the deadly Capitol riot. The original script showed deletions and changes including the removal by Trump of a line saying the rioters \u8220\'20\'1Cdo not represent me\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 * A Georgia judge has blocked Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  from investigating one of the 16 \u8220\'20\'1Cfake electors\u8221\'20\'1D who falsely certified \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as the winner of the 2020 election in the state. Superior court judge Robert McBurney said Willis\u8217\'20\'19s hosting of a fundraiser for a Democratic rival to Burt Jones, Republican candidate for Georgia lieutenant governor, precludes her from pursuing him.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  received rare praise from Republican former House speaker \uc2 Newt Gingrich\uc2  for her planned trip to Taiwan. Gingrich, the highest ranking American official ever to the island, said during a conservative conference in Washington DC that his Democratic successor should take a bipartisan delegation with her.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Covid-19 symptoms are \u8220\'20\'1Calmost completely\u8221\'20\'1D resolved, the president\u8217\'20\'19s physician Dr Kevin O\u8217\'20\'19Connor said in a letter. O\u8217\'20\'19Connor said Biden\u8217\'20\'19s blood pressure and breathing are normal, and he will continue to take the antiviral drug Paxlovid.\par \par \uc2 * Meanwhile, Joe Manchin, the Democratic senator for West Virginia, announced he had contracted the virus. Manchin said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  he is experiencing only mild symptoms and is working remotely.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  met with state lawmakers in Indiana to discuss a push for legislation to secure \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, one month after the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn Roe v Wade protections. Politico reports the vice-president is taking the lead in a push to promote action at state level, as Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 efforts to codify federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights falter.\par \par \uc2 * The White House is bracing for a slew of bad news in economic reports due this week, including the consumer confidence index and second quarter gross domestic product results, which could confirm the US is in recession. Biden administration officials have been talking up the strength of the economy, and low unemployment.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden 'feeling good', still has sore throat and cough from Covid\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was asked at the conclusion of the meeting how he was feeling, and says he hopes to be back at work in person \u8220\'20\'1Cby the end of this week\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Four days after testing positive for Covid-19, Biden said:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m feeling great. I\u8217\'20\'19ve had two full nights of sleep all the way through. My dog had to wake me up this morning, my wife\u8217\'20\'19s not here. She\u8217\'20\'19s takes him out in the morning while I\u8217\'20\'19m upstairs working out, so I felt this nuzzle of my dog\u8217\'20\'19s nose against my chest about five minutes to seven.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m feeling good. My voice is still raspy... I\u8217\'20\'19m feeling better every day. I still have this little bit of a sore throat and a little bit of a cough.\par \par \uc2 But it\u8217\'20\'19s changing significantly. It\u8217\'20\'19s now up in the upper part of my my throat, actually around my nose and everywhere else, and they tell me that\u8217\'20\'19s par for the course. And I think I\u8217\'20\'19m on my way to full recovery, God willing.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden's voice hoarse at virtual semiconductors summit\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is appearing virtually at a White House roundtable with leaders of the US semiconductor industry, sounding somewhat hoarse from his Covid-19 infection, but otherwise appearing relatively healthy.\par \par \uc2 White House physician Kevin O\u8217\'20\'19Connor gave an update on the president\u8217\'20\'19s condition earlier, saying he had \u8220\'20\'1Calmost completely\u8221\'20\'1D recovered from symptoms after contracting the virus last week.\par \par \uc2 He was seen occasionally coughing during the meeting, and regularly sipping from a mug on the desk beside him, but exhibited few other signs of his illness.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  covers his mouth while coughing during a virtual meeting with chief executives and labor leaders about the Chips act on Monday. Photograph: Brendan Smialowski/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s appearance at the summit, which also featured labor leaders, commerce secretary \uc2 Gina Raimondo\uc2 , and \uc2 Brian Deese\uc2 , the president\u8217\'20\'19s senior economic adviser, was announced at short notice, an apparent indication of the strength of his recovery.\par \par \uc2 Biden, wearing a blue suit and tie, and seated at his desk, gave brief opening remarks and listened attentively as the speakers laid out the importance of the US semiconductor industry to national security, healthcare and manufacturing.\par \par \uc2 The Chips act moving through Congress this week seeks billions of dollars in subsidies and tax credits for the industry. A semiconductor shortage has disrupted production in industries from automobiles to electronics and high-tech weapons.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are unable to get the components we need. Semiconductors are what makes everything happen in the industrial sector just as they do in the medical sector,\u8221\'20\'1D said Tom Linebarger, chief executive of Cummings Inc, a manufacturer of engines and power generation equipment.\par \par \uc2 Biden asked Linebarger about the effect any increased availability of semiconductors would have, particularly in the electric car industry.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe exponential curve will keep growing,\u8221\'20\'1D Linebarger replied. \u8220\'20\'1CWe solve the problems we need to solve in the US and use the same technology to export to the rest of the world.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have a big opportunity here but we need to invest now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Six staffers were reportedly arrested in Congress on Monday afternoon for staging a sit-in at Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s office and protesting about a lack of legislative action on the environment.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JulesJester/status/1551616214937620480"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweet posted by NBC News reporter Julia Jester}}}\uc2  features a short video purporting to show one of the staff members in handcuffs, explaining why the group jeopardized their careers to take the action.\par \par \uc2 enltrUSCP arrested six House staffers this afternoon for protesting inside {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenSchumer?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SenSchumer}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s office demanding the majority leader restart negotiations to pass climate legislation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s giving up, but some of us are going to live through the climate crisis,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/saaaauuull?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @saaaauuull}}}\uc2  told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NBCNews?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @NBCNews}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/YDHc0N1FFD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/YDHc0N1FFD}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Julia Jester (@JulesJester) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JulesJester/status/1551616214937620480?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The reporter asked the male staffer what they were demanding of the senior Democrat. He replied: \u8220\'20\'1Cto reopen negotiations on the climate reconciliation package... and pass climate legislation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to advance climate legislation have been thwarted largely because of the opposition of Democratic West Virginia senator Joe Manchin, who has been branded a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/15/joe-manchin-condemned-us-climate-action"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 modern day villain}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D for his ties to the fossil fuel industry and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/15/joe-manchin-climate-funding-tax-hikes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 killing off the president\u8217\'20\'19s environmental proposals}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The reporter asked why the group had chosen Schumer\u8217\'20\'19s office, and not that of Manchin. (Earlier today, Manchin announced he had tested positive for Covid-19 and was working remotely).\par \par \uc2 The staffer replied cryptically: \u8220\'20\'1CBecause there\u8217\'20\'19s always going to be a sheep that strays away from the herd.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Earlier today, a tweet from an activist named Saul, who identified himself as a staffer for Democratic Missouri congresswoman \uc2 Cori Bush\uc2 , said he was among the group.\par \par \uc2 enltrRight now, we Hill staffers are peacefully protesting Dem leaders INSIDE. To my knowledge, this has never been done.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ve also never seen climate catastrophe, so we\u8217\'20\'19re meeting the moment. Follow along as we fight with everything we have to jumpstart climate negotiations. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/PwuWVFQoED"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/PwuWVFQoED}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Saul (@saaaauuull) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/saaaauuull/status/1551587834666024960?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRight now, we Hill staffers are peacefully protesting Dem leaders INSIDE. To my knowledge, this has never been done,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve also never seen climate catastrophe, so we\u8217\'20\'19re meeting the moment. Follow along as we fight with everything we have to jumpstart climate negotiations\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 January 6 committee releases Trump's altered 'riot speech' notes\par \par \uc2 Elaine Luria\uc2 , a member of the January 6 House panel looking into \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to reverse his 2020 election defeat, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1551571605121339392"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posted to Twitter}}}\uc2  a video featuring handwritten changes he made to a speech the day after the deadly Capitol riot.\par \par \uc2 The committee showed last week during a public hearing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/video/2022/jul/21/trump-speech-outtake-election-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 outtakes of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s speech}}}\uc2  on 7 January 2021 in which he refused to speak certain phrases critical of his supporters who violently ransacked the Capitol building.\par \par \uc2 enltrIt took more than 24 hours for President Trump to address the nation again after his Rose Garden video on January 6th in which he affectionately told his followers to go home in peace.\par \par \uc2 There were more things he was unwilling to say. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/cJBIX5ROxs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/cJBIX5ROxs}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. \uc2 Elaine Luria\uc2  (@RepElaineLuria) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepElaineLuria/status/1551568001836670976?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The original script posted Monday by Luria, a Virginia Democrat, shows deletions and changes made by the outgoing president.\par \par \uc2 Lines included in the original stating that the justice department would \u8220\'20\'1Censure all lawbreakers are prosecuted to the fullest extent of the law\u8221\'20\'1D and that the rioters \u8220\'20\'1Cdo not represent me\u8221\'20\'1D were struck through in black ink, presumably by Trump.\par \par \uc2 The video also includes Trump\u8217\'20\'19s daughter, \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2 , confirming to the panel the document \u8220\'20\'1Clooks like a copy of a draft of the remarks for that day\u8221\'20\'1D and the writing \u8220\'20\'1Clooks like my father\u8217\'20\'19s handwriting\u8221\'20\'1D, the Associated Press reported.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepElaineLuria/status/1551568001836670976"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In her tweet Monday}}}\uc2 , Luria said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt took more than 24 hours for President Trump to address the nation again after his Rose Garden video on January 6th in which he affectionately told his followers to go home in peace. There were more things he was unwilling to say\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In other highlighted changes to the script, in the original line: \u8220\'20\'1CI am outraged and sickened by the violence, lawlessness and mayhem\u8221\'20\'1D, the word \u8220\'20\'1Csickened\u8221\'20\'1D is crossed out.\par \par \uc2 So, AP reports, are the later lines, \u8220\'20\'1CI want to be very clear you do not represent me. You do not represent our movement.\u8221\'20\'1D But Trump left in, \u8220\'20\'1CYou do not represent our country.\u8221\'20\'1D The line \u8220\'20\'1Cyou belong in jail\u8221\'20\'1D was replaced with \u8220\'20\'1Cyou will pay\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In its succession of public hearings, which has concluded for the time being, the panel was attempting to present to the American public substantial evidence of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s illegal efforts to reverse his election loss to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The justice department is pursuing its own inquiry.\par \par \uc2 Read more here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/23/january-6-hearings-us-democracy-roadmap-autocracy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18US democracy will not survive for long\u8217\'20\'19: how January 6 hearings plot a roadmap to autocracy}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand on a busy Monday in US politics:\par \par \uc2 * A Georgia judge has blocked Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  from investigating one of the 16 \u8220\'20\'1Cfake electors\u8221\'20\'1D who falsely certified \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as the winner of the 2020 election in the state. Superior court judge Robert McBurney said Willis\u8217\'20\'19s hosting of a fundraiser for a Democratic rival to Burt Jones, Republican candidate for Georgia lieutenant governor, precludes her from pursuing him.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  received rare praise from Republican former House speaker \uc2 Newt Gingrich\uc2  for her planned trip to Taiwan. Gingrich, the highest ranking American official ever to the island, said during a conservative conference in Washington DC that his Democratic successor should take a bipartisan delegation with her.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Covid-19 symptoms are \u8220\'20\'1Calmost completely\u8221\'20\'1D resolved, the president\u8217\'20\'19s physician Dr Kevin O\u8217\'20\'19Connor said in a letter. O\u8217\'20\'19Connor said Biden\u8217\'20\'19s blood pressure and breathing are normal, and he will continue to take the antiviral drug Paxlovid.\par \par \uc2 * Meanwhile, Joe Manchin, the Democratic senator for West Virginia, announced he had contracted the virus. Manchin said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  he is experiencing only mild symptoms and is working remotely.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  met with state lawmakers in Indiana to discuss a push for legislation to secure \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, one month after the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn Roe v Wade protections. Politico reports the vice-president is taking the lead in a push to promote action at state level, as Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 efforts to codify federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights falter.\par \par \uc2 * The White House is bracing for a slew of bad news in economic reports due this week, including the consumer confidence index and second quarter gross domestic product results, which could confirm the US is in recession. Biden administration officials have been talking up the strength of the economy, and low unemployment.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s plenty more politics to come this afternoon, including the release by the January 6 committee of additional evidence detailing Trump\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to reverse his election defeat. Please stick with us.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.49pm BST\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/dec/29/newt-gingrich-democrats-brainwash-next-generation-trump-us-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Newt Gingrich}}}\uc2 , the last speaker of the House of Representatives to visit Taiwan, has backed current speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s planned trip to the self-governing island.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI feel very strongly that Speaker Pelosi should go to Taiwan and she should take a bipartisan congressional delegation,\u8221\'20\'1D Gingrich told a conservative gathering in Washington on Monday. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I say this with some authority as the highest ranking American official ever to visit Taiwan.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Gingrich, a Republican, went to the island in 1997. Pelosi\u8217\'20\'19s planned visit has prompted China to threaten \u8220\'20\'1Cforceful measures\u8221\'20\'1D and even a possible military response, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ft.com/content/381ff6c9-ed6c-4f3c-bacc-f02a109d048c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Financial Times reported}}}\uc2 , causing a headache for the White House.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/21/nancy-pelosi-taiwan-trip-not-good-idea-right-now-joe-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden has said}}}\uc2  the US military assessed \u8220\'20\'1Cit is not a good idea right now\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But Gingrich, addressing the America First Policy Institute - a thinktank comprising many {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/17/trump-thinktank-america-first-policy-institute"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump administration alumni}}}\uc2  - accused the state department of \u8220\'20\'1Ctimidity covered by insecurity and an eagerness to appease\u8221\'20\'1D and claimed that the \u8220\'20\'1Cwoke\u8221\'20\'1D defence department\u8217\'20\'19s own timidity is \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerous\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrWould it surprise you to learn that \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  got a round of applause at a meeting of the Trump-backed America First Policy Institute? Because that\u8217\'20\'19s exactly what just happened, when Newt Gingrich declared support for her upcoming trip to Taiwan. \u8220\'20\'1CI commend Nancy,\u8221\'20\'1D said Newt {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/FJ1Xh8H0PK"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/FJ1Xh8H0PK}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Michael Tracey (@mtracey) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mtracey/status/1551613680336441349?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CIf the Department of Defense is not certain that it can protect the American speaker of the House in a public visit, why would they think they could protect Taiwan? If you\u8217\'20\'19re the Chinese communists and you watch us flinch after the total mess in Afghanistan and the total mess in Ukraine, you begin to think this is an administration that\u8217\'20\'19s just begging to be bullied.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Gingrich added that he has \u8220\'20\'1Cenormous disagreements\u8221\'20\'1D with Pelosi on many issues. \u8220\'20\'1CBut on this one, I think her instinct is right and I hope she sticks to her guns. The only thing I would suggest is she should make it a bipartisan congressional delegation to show both parties are committed to the independence of China.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Judge blocks Georgia DA from investigating Trump 'fake elector'\par \par \uc2 The criminal inquiry into \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn his election defeat by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in Georgia has hit a speed bump.\par \par \uc2 In what the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ajc.com/politics/judge-blocks-fulton-da-from-questioning-gop-senator-in-trump-probe/E5UE3RMBQBC5XJ4YSRVTLCALXY/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Atlanta Journal Constitution calls}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Ca surprise decision and a significant rebuke\u8221\'20\'1D of Fulton county district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , superior court judge Robert McBurney said Monday she cannot pursue her investigation of state senator Burt Jones.\par \par \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 . Photograph: John Bazemore/AP\par \par \uc2 Jones was one of the 16 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/07/trump-campaign-fake-georgia-electors-email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 secretive \u8220\'20\'1Cfake electors\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  who were lined up to fraudulently certify a Trump victory in the state he lost to Biden in 2020 by almost 12,000 votes.\par \par \uc2 McBurney granted a motion by Jones, a Republican running for Georgia lieutenant governor, to remove Willis and her team from looking into his role in the scandal, citing the fact Willis hosted a campaign fundraiser last month for Jones\u8217\'20\'19s now opponent, Democrat Charlie Bailey.\par \par \uc2 McBurney wrote:\par \par \uc2 An investigation of this significance, garnering the public attention it necessarily does and touching so many political nerves in our society, cannot be burdened by legitimate doubts about the district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s motives.\par \par \uc2 The district attorney does not have to be apolitical, but her investigations do.\par \par \uc2 As a consequence, an alternative prosecutor must now decide whether to continue treating Jones as \u8220\'20\'1Ca target\u8221\'20\'1D of the investigation, as Willis {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/georgia-prosecutors-target-16-fake-electors-2020-election/story?id=87120720"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 designated the 16 \u8220\'20\'1Cfake electors\u8221\'20\'1D last week}}}\uc2 , and whether to charge him with criminal misdeeds.\par \par \uc2 The Georgia inquiry is widely seen as one of the best chances of holding Trump liable for his \u8220\'20\'1Cbig lie\u8221\'20\'1D that the election was stolen from him, and efforts to alter the result, which included the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-capitol-breach"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deadly 6 January Capitol insurrection}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/05/georgia-grand-jury-subpoenas-trump-legal-advisers-2020-election-effort"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia prosecutors issued subpoenas}}}\uc2  for several members of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legal team, including South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s Republican senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  and former New York city mayor \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  to testify.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, CNN reported, Georgia governor \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2 , who has clashed frequently with Trump over the state\u8217\'20\'19s certification of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s victory, gave recorded testimony to a grand jury assisting the investigation.\par \par \uc2 The inquiry has focused in part on an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/04/trumps-phone-call-to-brad-raffensperger-five-key-points"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 infamous phone call Trump}}}\uc2  made to Georgia secretary of state \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2  after the 2020 election urging him to \u8220\'20\'1Cfind\u8221\'20\'1D the number of votes the outgoing president needed to win the state.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Dan Cox, an extremist pro-Trump Republican, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/07/19/us/politics/dan-cox-maryland-governors-race.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won}}}\uc2  his party\u8217\'20\'19s nomination for governor in Maryland last week thanks to \u8220\'20\'1Ccollusion between Trump and the national Democrats\u8221\'20\'1D, the current Republican governor said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think there\u8217\'20\'19s any chance that [Cox] can win,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2  added, speaking to CNN\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union.\par \par \uc2 Hogan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vice.com/en/article/epzxpa/maryland-gop-primary-dan-cox-michael-peroutka"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 previously}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MikenzieFrost/status/1463197778331549701?s=20&t=fEov8eHpac_Ml-Reu01Azg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  Cox \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thedailybeast.com/qanon-whack-job-dan-cox-wins-republican-nomination-for-maryland-governor-despite-larry-hogans-opposition"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a QAnon whack job}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2017/dec/14/collusion-how-russia-helped-trump-win-the-white-house-by-luke-harding-review"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Collusion}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D is a loaded word in US politics, in the long aftermath of the Russia investigation, in which the special counsel \uc2 Robert Mueller{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.americanbar.org/news/abanews/aba-news-archives/2019/03/mueller-concludes-investigation/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scrutinised}}}\uc2  election interference by Moscow and links between Trump aides and Russia.\par \par \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2 . presidential bid. (AP Photo/Brian Witte, File) Photograph: Brian Witte/AP\par \par \uc2 The battle to succeed Hogan as governor of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/maryland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maryland}}}\uc2  might seem small beer in comparison. But the race attracted national attention.\par \par \uc2 Cox, endorsed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , surged past Kelly Schulz, a member of Hogan\u8217\'20\'19s cabinet, to win the Republican nomination.\par \par \uc2 In the Democratic race, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uk.finance.yahoo.com/news/oprah-backing-wes-moore-triumphs-025925583.html?guccounter=1&guce_referrer=aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZ29vZ2xlLmNvbS8&guce_referrer_sig=AQAAAK5OpG4uiTmT_jck98rjWdy5LikTqNFSA3g6zUyEV1sT2DHLT8LgQ1fD1-cnQP_RaRHI18q_Hd5k-B1JNCq_beU58vZcdpVjvZ-Pn89HcNdmVtT6C6a1SXVRfptyKl20DYswev9Idwk5XS43kXKKHyjthwGPa3IaS7nj5mPapVQx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wes Moore}}}\uc2 , a bestselling author, beat candidates including \uc2 Tom Perez\uc2 , a former Democratic national committee chair and US labor secretary.\par \par \uc2 In a midterm election year, Democrats have sought {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/06/16/us/politics/democrats-midterms-trump-gop.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to boost pro-Trump Republicans}}}\uc2  in competitive states, placing the risky bet that as the January 6 committee remains in the headlines, extremists who support the former president\u8217\'20\'19s lie about electoral fraud in his 2020 defeat will prove unpalatable to voters.\par \par \uc2 Hogan said: \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s no question this was a big win for the \uc2 Democratic Governors Association\uc2  that I think spent over $3m trying to promote this guy [Cox]. And it was basically collusion between Trump and the national {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2 , who propped this guy up and got him elected.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut he really is not a serious candidate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read the full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/25/hogan-trump-maryland-democratic-collusion-dan-cox-qanon-wes-moore"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How a Trump-backed \u8216\'20\'18QAnon whack job\u8217\'20\'19 won with Democratic \u8216\'20\'18collusion\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/Update-7.25.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the letter}}}\uc2  from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s physician, Dr Kevin O\u8217\'20\'19Connor, giving the president an (almost) clean bill of health as he recovers from Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 Biden is apparently now feeling so robust he\u8217\'20\'19s willing to take on a virtual meeting later today with chief executives of \uc2 Lockheed Martin\uc2 , \uc2 Medtronic\uc2 , \uc2 Cummins Inc\uc2  and labor leaders to discuss the US semiconductor industry.\par \par \uc2 A bill moving through Congress this week seeks billions of dollars in subsidies and tax credits for the industry. A semiconductor shortage has disrupted production in industries from automobiles to electronics and high-tech weapons.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Progressive Democrat Tom Nelson has dropped out of the race to challenge incumbent Republican Ron Johnson for his Wisconsin Senate seat in November, he announced on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Nelson was trailing Lt Gov Mandela Barnes, businessman \uc2 Alex Lasry\uc2 , owner of basketball\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Milwaukee Bucks\uc2 , and state treasurer Sarah Godlewski, in support and donations for the 9 August primary.\par \par \uc2 Barnes and Lasry are in a close tussle for the nomination, with Nelson now opting to support Barnes.\par \par \uc2 Toppling Johnson and flipping the Wisconsin seat is one of the Democratic Party\u8217\'20\'19s top priorities in the midterms, with the most recent polling indicating {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/senate/wisconsin/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the race is a toss-up}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden's Covid symptoms 'almost completely' resolved\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Covid-19 symptoms are \u8220\'20\'1Calmost completely\u8221\'20\'1D resolved, his physician said in a memo on Monday, according to Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Biden tested positive for the virus last Thursday, and carried on working remotely. He is scheduled shortly to address remotely a gathering of black law enforcement executives.\par \par \uc2 In a White House memo released Monday morning, the president\u8217\'20\'19s physician, Dr Kevin O\u8217\'20\'19Connor, said: \u8220\'20\'1CWhen questioned, at this point he only notes some residual nasal congestion and minimal hoarseness\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Biden, the memo said, is experiencing no shortness of breath, his blood pressure is normal, and he is continuing to take the prescribed antiviral Paxlovid.\par \par \uc2 First lady Jill Biden, who remained in Delaware while her husband was in Washington, tested negative for Covid-19 this morning, her office said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 While we\u8217\'20\'19re (briefly) discussing Trump\u8217\'20\'19s apparently falling star, another b\u234\'00\'EAte noire, congressman \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2 , says the former president\u8217\'20\'19s waning popularity is extending even to his formerly \u8220\'20\'1Chard core\u8221\'20\'1D supporters.\par \par \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2 . Photograph: J Scott Applewhite/AP\par \par \uc2 The Illinois Republican and 6 January committee member made the comment on NBC\u8217\'20\'19s Meet the Press on Sunday, warning that \u8220\'20\'1CTrumpism isn\u8217\'20\'19t dying, even though Trump is becoming irrelevant\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Asked if he believed the 6 January panel\u8217\'20\'19s revelations about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn his 2020 election defeat to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was having any impact on colleagues, Kinzinger said:\par \par \uc2 Every day I ceased to be amazed at how much they\u8217\'20\'19re willing to accept and not say anything. In terms of Republicans in general, you have kind of the bulk of Republican voters, this doesn\u8217\'20\'19t appear to be having a ton of impact, maybe people are shifting more towards a potential for, I don\u8217\'20\'19t know, a \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m hearing a lot of anecdotal stuff around the edges of people who have been hard core with Trump that now just can\u8217\'20\'19t stand him... in like five years I still believe that it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be hard to find somebody that will admit they were ever a Trump supporter.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senator Joe Manchin has Covid-19\par \par \uc2 West Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic senator Joe Manchin has Covid-19, he announced this morning on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Manchin, who is vaccinated and boosted, said he was experiencing \u8220\'20\'1Cmild symptoms\u8221\'20\'1D of the infection and was continuing to work remotely.\par \par \uc2 enltrThis morning I tested positive for COVID-19. I am fully vaccinated and boosted and am experiencing mild symptoms. I will isolate and follow CDC guidelines as I continue to work remotely to serve West Virginians.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senator Joe Manchin (@Sen_JoeManchin) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Sen_JoeManchin/status/1551563772807917570?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The announcement comes as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , whose agenda Manchin has blocked in recent months, continues his own recovery after the president tested positive for Covid last week.\par \par \uc2 Biden is reportedly in much better condition this morning, and will address a gathering of black law enforcement executives at lunchtime remotely.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not been a good few days for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in media circles. Two prominent newspapers owned by one-time cheerleader \uc2 Rupert Murdoch\uc2  have turned against him, and one of the former president\u8217\'20\'19s favorite bugles, the far-right One America News (OAN), has lost its last major US television platform.\par \par \uc2 My colleague Ed Helmore {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2022/jul/25/new-york-post-trump-murdoch-wall-street-journal-fox-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has this report}}}\uc2  on the New York Post issuing an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/07/23/media/murdoch-trump-jan-6-new-york-post-wall-street-journal/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 excoriating editorial indictment}}}\uc2  of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s failure to stop the attack on the US Capitol on 6 January 2021.\par \par \uc2 The editorial, in a tabloid owned by Murdoch {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nypost.com/2021/03/11/happy-90th-birthday-to-rupert-murdoch-savior-of-the-post/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 since 1976}}}\uc2 , began: \u8220\'20\'1CAs his followers stormed the Capitol, calling for his vice-president to be hanged, President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  sat in his private dining room, watching TV, doing nothing. For three hours, seven minutes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s only focus, the Post said, was to block the peaceful transfer of power.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs a matter of principle, as a matter of character, Trump has proven himself unworthy to be this country\u8217\'20\'19s chief executive again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrNotable from the Murdoch-owned NY Post: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s up to the Justice Department to decide if this is a crime. But as a matter of principle, as a matter of character, Trump has proven himself unworthy to be this country\u8217\'20\'19s chief executive again.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/yiLjAVhDe6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/yiLjAVhDe6}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jim Sciutto (@jimsciutto) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jimsciutto/status/1550857037860417537?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 23, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal, another Murdoch paper, issued a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/the-president-who-stood-still-donald-trump-jan-6-committee-mike-pence-capitol-riot-11658528548"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 similar}}}\uc2  critique in which it said evidence before the House January 6 committee was a reminder that \u8220\'20\'1CTrump betrayed his supporters\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Sam Levine reports Verizon Fios will no longer carry OAN from the end of this month, dealing a major blow to the network that has become a hotbed of misinformation.\par \par \uc2 Verizon\uc2  was the largest pay-TV provider still carrying the OAN, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thedailybeast.com/far-right-channel-one-america-news-officially-dropped-by-verizon-fios"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Daily Beast}}}\uc2 , which first reported the network was getting dropped. \uc2 Verizon\uc2  and OAN {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.verizon.com/support/residential/content-agreement-information/content-info?cmp=afc_h_p_cj_na_ot_21_99_affiliate-8532386_11557999____vg__p_23040407__t_w__r_google.com__d_D&cid=e1658680209010200000&kpid=AdMarketplace_cmp-ADM_%20Native%20Search_adg-Verizon%20Native%20Search_kwd-verison_mt-Broad_id-1658680209010200000&AMPCLID=1658680209010200000&URL=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.verizon.com%2Fsupport%2Fresidential%2Fcontent-agreement-information%2Fcontent-info%3Fcmp%3DKNC-C-HQ-NON-R-AW-NONE-NONE-2K0VZ0-COE-ADM-7802%26cid%3De1658680209010200000%26kpid%3DAdMarketplace_cmp-ADM_%2520Native%2520Search_adg-Verizon%2520Native%2520Search_kwd-verison_mt-Broad_id-1658680209010200000%26AMPCLID%3D1658680209010200000&cjevent=50a149e20c0e11ed81d703a40a82b824&promotion_code=JUNCT/W04&AID=11557999&PID=8532386&SID=___vg__p_23040407__t_w__r_google.com__d_D&cjdata=MXxOfDB8WXww"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  were unable to reach an agreement}}}\uc2  to continue providing the network and customers will not be able to access the service after 30 July.\par \par \uc2 The development means that OAN in effect will not have a major television platform in the US. \uc2 DirecTV\uc2 , a major revenue provider, announced it was dropping the network in April.\par \par \uc2 OAN is facing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2022/jul/04/fox-oan-newsmax-lawsuits-election-fraud-claims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 billion-dollar lawsuits}}}\uc2  from voting equipment vendors {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2021/08/10/1026509404/dominion-sues-conservative-media-oan-newsmax-2020-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dominion}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/11/03/business/media/smartmatic-newsmax-oan.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Smartmatic}}}\uc2  over its false claims the 2020 election was stolen from Trump.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2022/jul/25/new-york-post-trump-murdoch-wall-street-journal-fox-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Is Murdoch tiring of Trump? Mogul\u8217\'20\'19s print titles dump the ex-president}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris takes lead on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights push\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is in Indianapolis this morning, talking to lawmakers in her new role as spearhead for the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s push to codify \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into law.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/07/25/harris-campaign-state-lawmakers-abortion-00047635?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=ef9757b7-1c82-4c99-8e9a-082111707afd&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to Politico}}}\uc2 , the vice-president is taking the lead on what looks to be an uphill fight following the Supreme Court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn Roe v Wade \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections one month ago.\par \par \uc2 She is planning an \u8220\'20\'1Caggressive bid to elevate Democratic state legislators and governors on the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights frontlines\u8221\'20\'1D, Politico says, claiming Harris recently told staff:\par \par \uc2 We need to make it a goal that we\u8217\'20\'19re out in America three days a week.\par \par \uc2 In a bleak assessment of the immediate aftermath of the Supreme Court decision, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Jessica Glenza reports today on the creation of a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/25/us-abortion-bans-states-after-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dystopian American reality}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D and consequences \u8220\'20\'1Cboth chaotic and predictable\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Alarmingly, activists are promising even more draconian restrictions to come.\par \par \uc2 Elizabeth Nash\uc2  of the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a reproductive rights research organization, told the Guardian:\par \par \uc2 Everything is super in flux right now. We\u8217\'20\'19re looking at probably about 15m women living in a state with an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 That number we expect to increase, because more states are looking to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and we could see as much as half of the country without \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access very soon.\par \par \uc2 Democrats lost their first attempt to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into federal law in May, West Virginia senator Joe Manchin crossing the aisle to join Republicans in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/11/senate-abortion-rights-bill-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voting down the measure}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A renewed effort {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/15/house-abortion-vote-approved"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed the House of Representatives}}}\uc2  earlier this month, but was largely symbolic because of ongoing Republican resistance in the evenly-divided Senate, where it would need 60 votes to pass.\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s upcoming tour is, Politico says, aimed more at securing action at state level. A poll taken in the aftermath of the Supreme Court decision showed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/politics/2022/07/06/majority-of-public-disapproves-of-supreme-courts-decision-to-overturn-roe-v-wade/#americans-views-of-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 62% of Americans said \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  should be legal}}}\uc2  in all or most cases.\par \par \uc2 Read more here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/25/us-abortion-bans-states-after-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The dystopian American reality one month after the Roe v Wade reversal}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 What some are calling \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/07/25/politics/biden-big-week-for-economy-inflation/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 moment of truth}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D on the economy comes this week, with a number of key data indicators likely to paint a bleak picture for the president as Congress heads for summer recess and the midterm elections loom ever larger.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s why treasury secretary \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  and other White House figures have been prominent, attempting to talk up the strengths and resilience of the US economy while inflation rages at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/jul/13/us-inflation-why-so-high-what-we-know"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 four-decade highs}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2 . Photograph: Manuel Balce Ceneta/AP\par \par \uc2 On Sunday, Yellen told NBC\u8217\'20\'19s Meet the Press that, despite what she conceded were \u8220\'20\'1Cthreats on the horizons\u8221\'20\'1D, the US was not in recession:\par \par \uc2 You don\u8217\'20\'19t see any of the signs now - a recession is a broad-based contraction that affects many sectors of the economy - we just don\u8217\'20\'19t have that.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a message \uc2 Brian Deese\uc2 , Biden\u8217\'20\'19s senior economic adviser and director of the national economic council, was keen to reinforce in an appearance on CNN on Monday:\par \par \uc2 We have seen extraordinary resilience in this economy due largely to the resilience of our businesses and our consumers, but we need to take more action right now to make things more affordable.\par \par \uc2 In a tweet, Deese insisted that \u8220\'20\'1Chiring, spending and production data look solid\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Their comments are widely seen as efforts to get ahead of bad news on the economy coming this week, starting with the consumer confidence index report coming tomorrow, an expected steep interest rate hike on Wednesday, then second quarter gross domestic product results the following day.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say the predicted interest rate rise by the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  could help slow inflation, but fuel the recession risk at the same time.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a gamble that Biden, whose popularity ratings are at term lows, is likely to support. In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/07/18/politics/cnn-poll-joe-biden-economy-us/index.html?utm_term=165870822817361cfb4c833b2&utm_source=cnn_Meanwhile+in+America+July+25&utm_medium=email&bt_ee=CbckiebeLfjzMvFd317JVPlJBFDXJrZM6mmtTE9scu0SXP99YeT5ZDtJH9rEkAM2&bt_ts=1658708228181"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN poll}}}\uc2  last week, only 18% of Americans described the nation\u8217\'20\'19s economy as in good shape, while 82% said economic conditions are poor.\par \par \uc2 Tellingly, 75% said inflation and the cost of living were the most important economic problems facing their family, up from 43% last summer.\par \par \uc2 enltrImpt context ahead of this wk's Q2 GDP release:\par \par \uc2 The data will capture Apr-Jun economic conditions, ie backward looking\par \par \uc2 Hiring, spending, and production data look solid\par \par \uc2 CEA outlines why economists look broadly at data to assess the economy\u8217\'20\'19s health {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vzl38Z2g5E"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/vzl38Z2g5E}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Brian Deese\uc2  (@BrianDeeseNEC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BrianDeeseNEC/status/1551291398355390471?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 24, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The conservative National Review on Monday accused Biden\u8217\'20\'19s economic team of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nationalreview.com/the-morning-jolt/biden-team-goes-into-recession-denial/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 being in \u8220\'20\'1Crecession denial\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 , and predicted that official confirmation the US was in recession could come as early as Thursday when the second quarter GDP figures are released.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Good morning, politics blog readers. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s allies are scrambling to get ahead of what\u8217\'20\'19s likely to be a troubling week of economic news for the White House, with Congress beginning to think about its August recess with little to no progress on the president\u8217\'20\'19s economic agenda, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/jul/13/us-inflation-why-so-high-what-we-know"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 inflation at 40-year highs}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Treasury secretary \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  has been talking up the resilience and \u8220\'20\'1Chistorical strengths\u8221\'20\'1D of the US economy, and low unemployment, while conceding \u8220\'20\'1Cthreats on the horizon\u8221\'20\'1D could nudge the country closer to recession, just as the midterm elections loom.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll get a snapshot of consumer confidence in a report tomorrow, while Wednesday is likely to bring a sharp hike in US interest rates that could help slow inflation, but fuel the recession risk.\par \par \uc2 Biden, whose popularity ratings are slumping, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/18/joe-biden-age-approval-rating-2024-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plenty else on his plate}}}\uc2 . Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re watching today.\par \par \uc2 * We\u8217\'20\'19ll get the chance to gauge the progress of the president\u8217\'20\'19s recovery from Covid-19 when he addresses the national organization of black law enforcement executives at 12.30pm.\par \par \uc2 * Covid-19 will feature heavily at the White House press briefing. Pandemic response coordinator Dr Ashish Jha will join WH press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  at the podium.\par \par \uc2 * It\u8217\'20\'19s the last full week in Congress before the August recess. Today, senators will discuss healthcare benefits for veterans episode to toxins, and vote to progress a bill providing grants to the computer chip industry.\par \par \uc2 * There\u8217\'20\'19s also a push to get the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/19/us-house-bill-protect-same-sex-interracial-marriage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 same-sex marriage bill}}}\uc2  through the Senate this week, after it passed the House with supports from dozens of Republicans last week.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you all the developments as they happen. Please stay with us...\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220725ei7p001uu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
