\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 The dystopian American reality one month after the Roe v Wade reversal\b0\par\par\uc2 Jessica Glenza \par \uc2 1,247 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 July 2022\par 14:04 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 In the month since the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision, states have embraced the ability to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with both chaotic and predictable consequences\par \par \uc2 Severe new restrictions upend reproductive care across whole regions of the US. Patients report delays for procedures that were once common and routine, as doctors fear vague new laws with criminal penalties. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/03/ohio-indiana-abortion-rape-victim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 10-year-old rape victim}}}\uc2  was forced to travel out of state to terminate a pregnancy. And activists promise more draconian restrictions to come.\par \par \uc2 In the month since the supreme court bombshell that ended the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , this picture is the new American reality, as states across the south and midwest embrace their new ability to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 at times without exception. The consequences have been both chaotic and predictable.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEverything is super in flux right now,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Elizabeth Nash\uc2  of the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a reproductive rights research organization.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re looking at probably about 15 million women living in a state with an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban right now. That number we expect to increase, because more states are looking to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and we could see as much as half of the country without \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access very soon.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At its most basic level, the upheaval caused by the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision in Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/13/texas-abortion-ban-maternal-health-risk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 endangered patients}}}\uc2 , doctors and lawyers said. Dobbs {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ended federal \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  protections}}}\uc2  nearly 50 years after the landmark decision Roe v Wade, and returned regulation of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to states.\par \par \uc2 Bans at six weeks gestation or earlier, before most women know they are pregnant, are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2022/jun/28/tracking-where-abortion-laws-stand-in-every-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in force in 12 states as of Thursday}}}\uc2 . The bans have forced patients seeking abortions, and who have the time and money, to travel hundreds of miles from home. At times, that travel has also placed friends, family and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights organizations in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/29/us-abortion-supreme-court-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 legal jeopardy}}}\uc2 , as states have criminalized helping people obtain abortions. Other patients have seen {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=29VPLXCadIg&t=251s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 routine care for miscarriages}}}\uc2  and ectopic pregnancies delayed, as doctors fear criminal sanctions should they accidentally violate bans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTruly frustrating and harrowing in my view, the state of Texas [being] intentionally ambiguous about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/14/texas-sues-guidance-emergency-abortions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 when hospitals can provide care}}}\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D said David Donatti, a staff attorney at the \uc2 American Civil Liberties Union (ACLU) \uc2 of Texas. Patients face \u8220\'20\'1Cprolonged pain and suffering for pregnancies that are not viable, because the chilling effect of what the state of Texas has done is so powerful\u8221\'20\'1D, he said.\par \par \uc2 More broadly, however, the court\u8217\'20\'19s late June decision has shifted what was once a fight over national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy to multiple fights in individual states, and even local governments. In Louisiana, the legality of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/27/louisiana-judge-abortion-ban-roe-v-wade-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 changed almost daily}}}\uc2 , as a court case about three new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans progresses. On the local level, some progressive cities such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/31/texas-austin-resolution-decriminalize-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Austin, Texas}}}\uc2 , intend to bar police from investigating \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related cases, even as the state bans the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/apr/27/us-tiny-towns-anti-abortion-ordinances"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 small towns}}}\uc2  and some conservative prosecutors have vowed enforcement. In Benton county, Arkansas, the local prosecutor warned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be investigated \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/jul/01/anti-abortion-movement-roe-reversal-what-next"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 like any other potential crime}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In those states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains legal, patients have suddenly found clinic appointments full. In Kansas, the nearest state to Arkansas, Missouri, Oklahoma and Texas (all of which have banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), clinics are at capacity.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe just don\u8217\'20\'19t have enough appointments to meet the need,\u8221\'20\'1D said Emily Wales, the president and CEO of Planned Parenthood Great Plains, which once operated clinics in Arkansas, Missouri and Oklahoma, as well as Kansas. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s something we\u8217\'20\'19re trying to make clear to Kansans as well.\u8221\'20\'1D The nearest clinics with appointments may now be in Illinois, Colorado, Nebraska and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/21/new-mexico-abortion-clinics-crisis-pregnancy-centers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New Mexico}}}\uc2 , she said.\par \par \uc2 A still untold number of patients will carry unwanted or dangerous pregnancies to term, a situation likely to worsen as more states bring bans online in the coming weeks.\par \par \uc2 North Dakota, Idaho and Wyoming are all expected to begin enforcing bans this summer. Indiana has called a special session to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A more severe criminal ban, providing punishments of 99 years in prison and $100,000 in fines, is also expected in Texas, where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is already banned.\par \par \uc2 The court\u8217\'20\'19s decision has also rippled into politics, as Americans absorb the shock of rescinding a nearly 50-year-old precedent.\par \par \uc2 Kansas is representative of one such political battle. On 2 August, voters there will cast ballots on the first \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related referendum in the country, in what is likely to be a tight and closely watched campaign. Its neighboring states have, one by one, banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 : when the supreme court allowed Texas to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at six weeks gestation in 2021, clinics in Oklahoma began to care for Texas patients; then Oklahoma passed a similar six-week ban, forcing patients to Missouri and Kansas; when the court ruled in Dobbs, Missouri banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , too. That has left Kansas as a legal haven for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It may not remain that way. Lawmakers have placed a statewide constitutional amendment vote on the primary ballot, which would give the Republican-dominated state legislature more latitude to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a state where lawmakers have already shown interest in banning it.\par \par \uc2 However, Kansas could also be a bellwether of how overturning Roe v Wade has changed the political landscape. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coefficient.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/KS-VTB-Amendment-7.18.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New polling suggests}}}\uc2  the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision may have galvanized supporters of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights \u8211\'20\'13 an issue that previously motivated its opponents more strongly than supporters. About 85% of Americans support legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  under at least some circumstances. Historically, however, they have been less well organized than anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups.\par \par \uc2 Now, there has been a \u8220\'20\'1Cdramatic increase in moderate Republicans, apolitical folks\u8221\'20\'1D who have found themselves interested in the Kansas referendum , said Ashley All from Kansas for Constitutional Freedom, a group that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. She said the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision \u8220\'20\'1Cwas a wake-up call for people who thought their constitutional rights were protected at the federal level \u8211\'20\'13 and that is not the case now\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Kansas won\u8217\'20\'19t be the only place where the new political reality is tested. A record number of states have ballot initiatives on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights this fall. Voters in Kentucky and Montana will be asked to vote on anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ballot measures, while voters in California and Vermont will be asked to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Campaigners {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/28/abortion-rights-michigan-roe-wade-ballot-initiative"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in Michigan}}}\uc2 , too, are working to secure a ballot initiative to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Notably, local campaigners said Kansas\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights vote has also energized the LGBTQ+ community. The rights to gay marriage, same-sex intimacy and contraception were all called into question in the Dobbs decision in a concurring opinion by Justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , who argued the court should {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/clarence-thomas-roe-gay-marriage-contraception-lgbtq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Creconsider\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  cases granting those rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re showing up and showing out,\u8221\'20\'1D Martha Pint, co-president of the \uc2 League of Women Voters\uc2  in Kansas. \u8220\'20\'1CThis right to reproductive choice \u8211\'20\'13 they honestly feel their rights will be next.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While there does appear to be bipartisan support in Congress for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/19/us-house-bill-protect-same-sex-interracial-marriage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 enshrining protections for gay marriage}}}\uc2  in statute \u8211\'20\'13 even as Senate Republicans are expected to block protections for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/14/joe-biden-middle-east-israel-inflation-polling-us-politics-latest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/07/21/us/politics/house-contraception.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 contraception}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 any hopes that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/20/republican-states-health-benefits-new-mothers-abortion-bans?utm_term=62b05a3cc6e313433467b29c23af0f9c&utm_campaign=GuardianTodayUS&utm_source=esp&utm_medium=Email&CMP=GTUS_email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increase support among Republicans for social safety net programs}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/05/roe-v-wade-abortion-republicans-social-safety-net"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have so far been dashed}}}\uc2 . Instead, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups have focused on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/07/14/anti-abotion-10-year-old-ohio-00045843"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 closing remaining legal routes to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen all is said and done, about half of the states [could ban] \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D said Nash. \u8220\'20\'1CMeaning {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/05/abortion-deserts-clinics-access-closed-map"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 34 million women}}}\uc2  of reproductive age would live without access.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220725ei7p000xh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
