\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 TikTok influencers fearmongering about birth control are playing into the hands of the right\b0\par\par\uc2 Arwa Mahdawi \par \uc2 1,144 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 July 2022\par 13:25 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Republicans aren\u8217\'20\'19t stopping at Roe v Wade. They\u8217\'20\'19re coming for all our rights. The last thing we need is \u8216\'20\'18hormone coaches\u8217\'20\'19 giving them a helping hand\par \par \uc2 TikTokers tout \u8216\'20\'18Vatican Roulette\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Q. What do you call people who exclusively use \u8220\'20\'1Cnatural\u8221\'20\'1D forms of birth control such as the rhythm method?\par \par \uc2 A. Parents.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s an old joke but it\u8217\'20\'19s still depressingly relevant: TikTok is exploding with self-proclaimed \u8220\'20\'1Cholistic healers\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Chormone coaches\u8221\'20\'1D who are urging women to ditch their intrauterine devices (IUDs) and hormonal birth control and start monitoring their fertility signals instead. As Vice reports, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vice.com/en/article/xgyd5a/natural-birth-control-tiktok"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 videos tagged #naturalbirthcontrol}}}\uc2  have been viewed nearly 30m times and there seems to be a growing movement of influencers who are pushing the idea that hormonal birth control is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tiktok.com/@gracegetsgreen/video/7083213224132267306?referer_url=https%3A%2F%2Fmelmagazine.com%2F&referer_video_id=7083213224132267306&refer=embed&referer_url=https://melmagazine.com/en-us/story/natural-birth-control-tiktok"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dangerous}}}\uc2  and unnecessary. One TikTok that has been viewed 1.1m times claims natural family planning methods are 98% effective at preventing pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 To be clear: these influencers aren\u8217\'20\'19t entirely wrong; monitoring your fertility signals is obviously a helpful way to understand when you\u8217\'20\'19re most likely to get pregnant. Britain\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/contraception/natural-family-planning/#:~:text=How%20effective%20is%20natural%20family,planning%20correctly%20will%20get%20pregnant."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 National Health Service\u8217\'20\'19s website}}}\uc2  notes: \u8220\'20\'1CIf natural family planning is followed consistently and correctly, it can be up to 99% effective.\u8221\'20\'1D But that\u8217\'20\'19s a very, very big \u8220\'20\'1Cif\u8221\'20\'1D. Measuring your fertility signals \u8211\'20\'13 which involves things like measuring your temperature daily, tracking your menstrual cycle and monitoring cervical secretions \u8211\'20\'13 is a lot of work and very easy to get wrong. It\u8217\'20\'19s hard to say what the actual effectiveness rate of natural family planning is, but the size of Catholic families might give you a clue.\par \par \uc2 Needless to say, this is not exactly the best time for TikTok influencers to be encouraging people in the US to play what is sometimes known as Vatican roulette. The supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn Roe v Wade has made it a very scary time to have an unintended pregnancy. The past few weeks have been full of horror stories of women being denied reproductive healthcare because doctors are afraid of the new laws that criminalize \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In Wisconsin, for example, a woman suffering an incomplete miscarriage was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.msnbc.com/rachel-maddow-show/maddowblog/roe-overturned-health-care-nightmares-become-real-rcna38922"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 left to bleed for 10 days}}}\uc2  after being denied treatment by hospital staff who were afraid of contravening state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws. With the fall of Roe v Wade, \u8220\'20\'1Cthe art of medicine is lost and actually has been replaced by fear\u8221\'20\'1D, one {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/us-news/abortion-laws-spark-profound-changes-medical-care-rcna38606"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 OB-GYN told NBC.}}}\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s important, I think, to acknowledge the many reasons why some of these online TikTok influencers are disillusioned with IUDs and hormonal birth control. Having an IUD inserted can be very {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://intrauterine%20devic/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 painful}}}\uc2  ; oral contraceptive pills can have numerous side effects. It\u8217\'20\'19s essential to discuss these issues. However, scaremongering about contraceptives and urging people to abandon them for natural methods is downright dangerous. As Dr Jennifer Lincoln, an Oregon-based OB-GYN told Vice: \u8220\'20\'1CGetting pregnant now has enormous consequences. I don\u8217\'20\'19t even know how these influencers sleep at night.\u8221\'20\'1D If I\u8217\'20\'19m guessing? Probably with lots of holistic herbal supplements.\par \par \uc2 TikTok influencers who are fearmongering about birth control are also playing into the hands of the right, who seem to be very keen on forcing everyone to start using natural family planning. Republicans have repeatedly said that fears they will come after contraception are unfounded; however (shock horror!), their actions don\u8217\'20\'19t seem to match up with their words.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rollingstone.com/politics/politics-news/republicans-vote-against-right-to-contraception-bill-1386356/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 195 Republicans voted against the Right to Contraception Act}}}\uc2 , a House bill codifying the right to contraceptives into federal law. Only eight Republicans voted in favour of the bill (two voted \u8220\'20\'1Cpresent\u8221\'20\'1D). If Republicans don\u8217\'20\'19t have plans to restrict access to contraceptives, how do they explain their hostility to the legislation? Well, according to Florida congresswoman Kat Cammack, the bill would \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rollingstone.com/politics/politics-news/republicans-vote-against-right-to-contraception-bill-1386356/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 allow more abortions}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D. Don\u8217\'20\'19t even try to figure out that logic, because there isn\u8217\'20\'19t any.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ll tell you what is easy to figure out: Republicans aren\u8217\'20\'19t stopping at Roe v Wade. They\u8217\'20\'19re coming for the right to access contraception. They\u8217\'20\'19re coming for the right to same-sex marriage. They\u8217\'20\'19re coming for all our rights. The last thing we need is \u8220\'20\'1Chormone coaches\u8221\'20\'1D on TikTok giving them a helping hand.\par \par \uc2 No condoms for you, I\u8217\'20\'19m religious!\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not just TikTokers who are intent on confiscating your contraceptives: \uc2 Walgreens{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/business/business-news/walgreens-employee-refused-sell-condoms-couple-faith-rcna39165"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently made headlines}}}\uc2  after an employee in a Wisconsin store refused to sell condoms to a couple on religious grounds. A \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  spokesperson said that was totally fine because its employees are allowed to refuse to complete transactions if they have a \u8220\'20\'1Cmoral or religious conviction\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 How US dollars put anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups at the heart of Romanian healthcare\par \par \uc2 In 1966, Romania\u8217\'20\'19s communist dictator, \uc2 Nicolae Ceausescu\uc2 , banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and contraception in an attempt to increase the birth rate. After his government was overthrown, in the early 1990s, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was legalized and reproductive rights improved. Now, however, things are going backwards again. Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  centers, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2022/jul/22/how-us-dollars-put-anti-abortion-groups-at-the-heart-of-romanian-healthcare"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 many of which are receiving funds from US charities}}}\uc2 , are popping up in the country; a recent investigation showed that in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.libertatea.ro/stiri/in-11-judete-din-romania-nu-s-a-facut-niciun-avort-la-cerere-in-2021-in-spitalele-publice-exista-femei-care-sunt-nevoite-sa-mearga-in-alt-judet-4195786?fbclid=IwAR1qoNP-xcD-pIJseUGp6Jc2caL7fiokRuH-97CZjibZLW3Kuqy7qpqbH1A"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  11 out of 42 counties in Romania}}}\uc2 , no public hospital performed abortions last year. Religious fanatics in the US aren\u8217\'20\'19t content with simply rolling back women\u8217\'20\'19s rights at home, they\u8217\'20\'19re trying to export their ideology abroad.\par \par \uc2 More than 160m women unable to get contraception they need\par \par \uc2 Another reminder not to take access to birth control for granted: according to a new study published in the Lancet, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2022/jul/21/more-than-160m-women-unable-to-get-contraception-they-need-study-finds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 many as one in 14 women worldwide}}}\uc2  who wanted contraception were not using it in 2019. Half the women unable to access contraception live in sub-Saharan Africa and south Asia.\par \par \uc2 Sexism in women\u8217\'20\'19s football still rife\par \par \uc2 Being a female footballer means being subject to a lot of misogynistic abuse online, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dw.com/en/euro-2022-sexism-in-womens-football-still-rife/a-62565688"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a new study}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Josh Hawley, expert on \u8216\'20\'18manliness\u8217\'20\'19, ran away from rioters like a terrified chicken\par \par \uc2 New footage has been made public of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/21/josh-hawley-running-away-rioters-january-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Missouri senator running away}}}\uc2  from January 6 rioters \u8211\'20\'13 after he\u8217\'20\'19d egged them on. Hawley, it should be said, likes to think of himself as something of an expert on manliness and has written a book on the subject called Manhood: The Masculine Virtues America Needs.\par \par \uc2 The week in pawtriarchy\par \par \uc2 Humans have been exhausting lately so it is no surprise that the hottest new release of the summer seems to be a video game called \u8220\'20\'1CStray\u8221\'20\'1D which lets {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/07/22/tech/stray-cat-video-game-hands-on/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 you pretend to be a cat}}}\uc2 . It\u8217\'20\'19s not just humans who are fans; pets seem to be obsessed and the internet is now full of a-mew-sing videos of cats who are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/07/21/entertainment/cats-stray-gaming-gamers/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 transfixed by the game.}}}\par \par \uc2 Arwa Mahdawi\u8217\'20\'19s new book, Strong Female Lead, is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://linktr.ee/ARWAMAHDAWI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 available for order}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220723ei7n0015p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
