\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 January 6 panel says Bannon conviction is a \u8216\'20\'18victory for the rule of law\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein \par \uc2 5,348 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 July 2022\par 22:13 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The former Trump adviser was charged with two counts of criminal contempt for refusing to appear before the House committeeSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 The jurors in \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s contempt of Congress trial {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/22/jan-6-hearing-trump-capitol-attack-biden-covid-us-politics-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-62daf1598f0856861af45896#block-62daf1598f0856861af45896"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 returned guilty verdicts}}}\uc2  today, meaning the former \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  adviser is likely to serve jail time. Bannon has vowed to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/22/jan-6-hearing-trump-capitol-attack-biden-covid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-62daf68b8f08d0ef4fa8d3f4#block-62daf68b8f08d0ef4fa8d3f4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeal the decision}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Covid-19 symptoms have \u8220\'20\'1Cimproved\u8221\'20\'1D, the White House doctor said, and the president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/22/jan-6-hearing-trump-capitol-attack-biden-covid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-62dafe258f08e7341cdd74dc#block-62dafe258f08e7341cdd74dc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeared later in the day}}}\uc2  at a virtual event to showcase declining US gas prices.\par \par \uc2 * Washington is still reeling from yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s January 6 committee hearing, where the panel laid out evidence that Trump resisted stopping the riot. One presidential historian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/22/jan-6-hearing-trump-capitol-attack-biden-covid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-62dace478f0856861af4572e#block-62dace478f0856861af4572e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2  Americans not to be complacent about what those behind the attack were trying to accomplish.\par \par \uc2 * Trump, if elected president again in 2024, would oust tens of thousands of civil servants across the \uc2 US government\uc2  and replace them with his supporters, sources {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/22/jan-6-hearing-trump-capitol-attack-biden-covid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-62dad2518f08e7341cdd732a#block-62dad2518f08e7341cdd732a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 close to the ex-leader told Axios}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * California\u8217\'20\'19s governor signed a law modeled on anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation in Texas that would allow citizen to sue {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/22/jan-6-hearing-trump-capitol-attack-biden-covid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-62db16ed8f08d0ef4fa8d4a4#block-62db16ed8f08d0ef4fa8d4a4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 distributors of illegal weapons or parts}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 California governor signs law allowing citizens to sue illegal assault weapon distributors\par \par \uc2 In its latest attempt to stop gun violence, California\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic leadership has taken inspiration from anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation first crafted in conservative Texas, the Associated Press reports:\par \par \uc2 California punched back Friday against two recent landmark \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  decisions as the state\u8217\'20\'19s governor signed a controversial, first-in-the-nation gun control law patterned after a Texas anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law.\par \par \uc2 The action by \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , a Democrat, comes one month after conservative justices overturned women\u8217\'20\'19s constitutional right to abortions and undermined gun control laws in states including California.\par \par \uc2 Newsom stitched the two hot-button topics together in approving a law allowing people to sue anyone who distributes illegal assault weapons, parts that can be used to build weapons, guns without serial numbers, or.50 caliber rifles. They would be awarded at least $10,000 in civil damages for each weapon, plus attorneys fees.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/22/new-california-gun-control-law-modeled-after-texas-anti-abortion-measure"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 California signs gun control law modeled after Texas anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  measure}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Expect to hear more from \uc2 Steven Bannon\uc2  about his contempt of Congress conviction, including in an interview with the conservative Fox News host \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  this evening, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Hugo Lowell reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrHearing that \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  will return to hosting War Room podcast tonight at 5p ET and then appear on \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s show on Fox News at 8p ET to discuss his conviction for contempt of Congress.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1550593504723832832?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  vowed to fight his contempt convictions. Photograph: Jim Lo Scalzo/\uc2 EPA\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters after his conviction, \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  declared, \u8220\'20\'1CWe may have lost a battle today, but we\u8217\'20\'19re not going to lose this war.\u8221\'20\'1D He added, \u8220\'20\'1CI stand with Trump, and the constitution.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He also attacked the House panel investigating the January 6 attack as \u8220\'20\'1Cgutless members of that show-trial committee\u8221\'20\'1D who \u8220\'20\'1Cdidn\u8217\'20\'19t have the guts to testify in open court\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 You can watch video of his remarks below:\par \par \uc2 enltrSteve Bannon, a longtime ally of former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , was convicted on Friday of contempt charges for defying a congressional subpoena from the House committee investigating the Jan. 6 insurrection at the U.S. Capitol. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ehJpCqr64t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/ehJpCqr64t}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/W1L4uFcu3r"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/W1L4uFcu3r}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Associated Press (@AP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AP/status/1550583653943726082?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 January 6 committee leaders call Bannon conviction 'victory for the rule of law'\par \par \uc2 Bennie Thomspon, the Democratic chair of the January 6 committee, and \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , the Republican vice chair, have released a statement applauding the conviction this afternoon of former Trump adviser \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  for defying the committee\u8217\'20\'19s subpoenas.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe conviction of \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  is a victory for the rule of law and an important affirmation of the Select Committee\u8217\'20\'19s work,\u8221\'20\'1D Thompson and Cheney said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs the prosecutor stated, \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  \u8216\'20\'18chose allegiance to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  over compliance with the law\u8217\'20\'19. Just as there must be accountability for all those responsible for the events of January 6th, anyone who obstructs our investigation into these matters should face consequences. No one is above the law.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/22/steve-bannon-trial-trump-contempt-congress-charges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Steve Bannon convicted of contempt of Congress for defying Capitol attack subpoena}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Secret Service has just {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.secretservice.gov/newsroom/releases/2022/07/statement-us-secret-service-director-james-murray-unwavering-cooperation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 put out a statement }}}\uc2  reaffirming its willingness to cooperate with the January 6 committee, amid an ongoing investigation over its deletion of text messages from around the time of the insurrection.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs an American and director of this incredible agency, I found the events at the Capitol on January 6th to be abhorrent. What happened on that day in January 2021 is anathema to democracy and the processes our constitution guarantees,\u8221\'20\'1D Secret Service director James Murray said. \u8220\'20\'1CSince day one, I have directed our personnel to cooperate fully and completely with the committee and we are currently finalizing dates and times for our personnel to make themselves available to the committee for follow up inquiries.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Separately, CNN reports that \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2 , a Republican lawmaker serving on the committee, said that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s former deputy chief of staff and the former head of his Secret Service detail have stopped cooperating with the inquiry.\par \par \uc2 enltrI asked {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepKinzinger?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RepKinzinger}}}\uc2  if he believes Trump\u8217\'20\'19s fmr Dep Chief of Staff Tony Ornato and fmr Secret Service lead agent Robert Engel are still cooperating with the Jan 6 Cmte. His answer was a hard \u8220\'20\'1CNo.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jim Sciutto (@jimsciutto) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jimsciutto/status/1550489496726257664?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/19/secret-service-investigation-erased-january-6-texts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Secret Service told to begin an inquiry into erased January 6 text messages}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre didn\u8217\'20\'19t have much to say about \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s conviction earlier this afternoon on contempt of Congress charges for defying subpoenas from the January 6 committee.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not going to comment specifically on that case, but obviously, everyone should cooperate with the January 6 committee,\u8221\'20\'1D she told reporters.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House has identified 17 close contacts of President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , who tested positive for Covid-19 yesterday.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at a briefing to reporters, press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said the group members have all been informed, but none has tested positive.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe White House medical unit has identified and informed 17 people determined to be close contacts of the president, including members of his senior staff. None of the staff members have tested positive to date, and all of them are wearing masks around other people,\u8221\'20\'1D Jean-Pierre said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has appeared at a White House event - virtually, due to his Covid-19 infection.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI feel much better than I sound,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, flashing a thumbs-up and smiling on-screen.\par \par \uc2 He didn\u8217\'20\'19t have much more to say about that, but the event is focusing on gas prices, which are declining nationally from their record high levels hit last month, according to GasBuddy\u8217\'20\'19s Patrick De Haan:\par \par \uc2 enltr37 days in a row: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/gasprices?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #gasprices}}}\uc2  keep falling, the national average ?? 2.2c to $4.419/gal. We\u8217\'20\'19re likely to fall to $4.399/gal by late today. 8 states under $4: TX, SC, GA, MS, LA, AL, TN, & AR. 35k stations <$4. Most common price in the US: $3.99.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Patrick De Haan ???? (@GasBuddyGuy) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GasBuddyGuy/status/1550433294520549376?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lawyer plans to challenge his conviction immediately after sentencing, \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Hugo Lowell reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrNew: \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lawyer David Schoen tells reporters outside the courthouse just now that they will appeal today\u8217\'20\'19s contempt of Congress conviction \u8212\'20\'14 they expect to file after sentencing on October 21 at 3p ET.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1550563729816883201?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 CNN reports attorney David Schoen is confident that the verdict against Bannon will be overturned:\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CBulletproof appeal,\u8221\'20\'1D David Schoen, Bannon lawyer, tells reporters. \u8220\'20\'1CYou will see this case reversed on appeal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1550561768056946690?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the latest from Guardian US reporters on the conviction of \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 , a noteworthy figure in the world of Trump advisers:\par \par \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  was on Friday convicted of contempt of Congress at trial in federal court in Washington DC, for defying a subpoena by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/21/january-6-hearing-donald-trump-us-capitol-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 committee investigating}}}\uc2  last year\u8217\'20\'19s attack on the Capitol by supporters of his former boss \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The case for criminal contempt went to the jury just a few hours prior on Friday, after prosecutors and defense lawyers made their final pitches about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former presidential adviser.\par \par \uc2 Bannon was charged with two counts of criminal contempt for refusing to appear before the House committee, each count carries a minimum of 30 days in jail and up to a year. He had denied the charges but was found guilty on both counts.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/22/steve-bannon-trial-trump-contempt-congress-charges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Steve Bannon convicted of contempt of Congress for defying Capitol attack subpoena}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Hugo Lowell reports that the judge presiding in the case hinted at a potential grounds for the appeal of any guilty verdict \u8211\'20\'13 which Bannon is likely to do:\par \par \uc2 enltrNew: \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  will almost certainly appeal after Judge Nichols, a Trump appointee, indicated pre-trial that he considered the controlling case law that forced him to exclude the main defence arguments bad law.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1550558013727145986?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Reuters has more details on the severity of the sentence Bannon could face:\par \par \uc2 enltrFor each of the two contempt of Congress counts, \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  could be sentenced from 30 days to one year behind bars and fined between $100 and $100,000\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Matt Spetalnick (@mattspetalnick) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mattspetalnick/status/1550555930663813120?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Bannon will wait a few months before being sentenced, according to NBC News:\par \par \uc2 enltrBannon will be sentenced on October 21, though an appeal is pretty certain.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ryan J. Reilly (@ryanjreilly) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ryanjreilly/status/1550555720386547712?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jury finds \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  guilty on two counts of contempt of Congress\par \par \uc2 A Washington jury has found \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  guilty on two counts of contempt of Congress after the former adviser to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  refused to cooperate with a subpoena from the January 6 committee.\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  GUILTY on both counts. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/apLhOX2dia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/apLhOX2dia}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ryan J. Reilly (@ryanjreilly) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ryanjreilly/status/1550553871877115905?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 A verdict has been reached in the trial of \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 , Politico reports.\par \par \uc2 enltrUPDATE: Court official says jury has verdicts in \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  contempt of Congress case. Earlier: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/aiUH35mw36"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/aiUH35mw36}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/K8K523jUc1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/K8K523jUc1}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Josh Gerstein (@joshgerstein) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/joshgerstein/status/1550548732583677953?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Bannon is a former adviser to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  who is facing contempt of Congress charges for defying a subpoena from the January 6 committee.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/18/steve-bannon-contempt-of-congress-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Steve Bannon appears in court as contempt-of-Congress trial begins}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 J oe Biden released a statement condemning the attack against \uc2 Lee Zeldin\uc2 , a congressman from New York who is the Republican candidate for governor in the state. During a speech yesterday, a man climbed onstage and pulled Zeldin to the ground. Zeldin was not injured as people started to rush the stage to assist him.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI condemn the attack on Congressman Zeldin in the strongest terms,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in his statement. \u8220\'20\'1CAs I\u8217\'20\'19ve said before, violence has absolutely no place in our society or our politics. I am especially grateful for the courage of those who immediately intervened, and that he is unharmed and was able to continue his speech.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden's statement on yesterday's attack on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/leezeldin?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @leezeldin}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/uVr7W08oa0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/uVr7W08oa0}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Erin McEwan (@erinmcewan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/erinmcewan/status/1550536600018468869?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Sports news website {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sbnation.com/2022/7/22/23274106/josh-hawley-january-6-capitol-run-40-time"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SB Nation}}}\uc2  managed to find a sports angle to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/21/josh-hawley-running-away-rioters-january-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 clip of Josh Hawley fleeing}}}\uc2  the Capitol during the insurrection after raising a fist to Trump supporters in solidarity.\par \par \uc2 Using some interesting mathematical calculations, SB Nation calculated that if the Republican senator was running a 40-yard-dash, he would have had a time of 7.2 seconds.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a pretty slow time, but \u8220\'20\'1CHawley is in dress shoes on a tile floor, not on astroturf in spikes\u8221\'20\'1D, noted James Dator, SB Nation writer. \u8220\'20\'1CFurthermore, it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear where in his stride he was when he crossed the hall. Maybe he was really winded before he got there?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tucked away in South Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s bill that outlaws \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a provision that would make it illegal to provide information of how to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the phone or internet.\par \par \uc2 Such a provision would take \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans to an extreme and is probably an indication of how radical anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws will be to come.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese are going to be laws that spread like wildfire through states that have shown hostility to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Michelle Goodwin, a professor at University of California at Irvine Law School, told the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/technology/2022/07/22/south-carolina-bill-abortion-websites/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post}}}\uc2 , which reported on the provision.\par \par \uc2 South Carolina currently has six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in place following the Supreme Court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn Roe v Wade. The state\u8217\'20\'19s House of Representatives has been considering even stricter legislation after the ruling. The House has convened a special session to pass \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow is a good time. We have children being aborted in our state, as well as the rest of the country, and we have the information,\u8221\'20\'1D South Carolina governor \uc2 Henry McMaster\uc2  told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thestate.com/news/politics-government/article263028453.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the State}}}\uc2 , a newspaper in South Carolina. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s time to get on with the discussion and make whatever decisions are necessary.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Covid-19 symptoms have \u8220\'20\'1Cimproved\u8221\'20\'1D, the White House doctor said Friday morning. While the president had a mild fever last night, his temperature has gone back to normal. Biden is currently taking anti-Covid drug Paxlovid. He is experiencing a runny nose and fatigue, with an occasional cough.\par \par \uc2 * Washington is still reeling from yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s January 6 committee hearing, where the committee laid out a case against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s inaction as the riot was taking place. One presidential historian has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/22/jan-6-hearing-trump-capitol-attack-biden-covid-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-62dace478f0856861af4572e#block-62dace478f0856861af4572e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2  Americans not to be complacent about what those behind the attack were trying to accomplish.\par \par \uc2 * A report from this morning revealed that Trump, if elected as president in 2024, would replace tens of thousands of civil servants across the \uc2 US government\uc2  with his supporters, according to sources close to the former president.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re still keeping an eye on the trial of \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 , which continues today, along with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s appearance at a rally later this afternoon. Stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jeffrey Clark was a key figure in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attempt to overturn the 2020 election. The president tried to appoint him to lead the justice department, which would have allowed Clark to send a letter to Georgia state lawmakers informing them that there were \u8220\'20\'1Csignificant concerns\u8221\'20\'1D about the results that showed \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  winning the state.\par \par \uc2 That effort was thwarted when Justice Department senior staff threatened to resign en masse if Clark, whom they viewed as unqualified, was appointed. Clark has since become the subject of a probe by the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s inspector general, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  raided his house last month, and today, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/legal/legalindustry/ex-trump-justice-official-clark-faces-legal-disciplinary-charges-2022-07-22/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Reuters reports}}}\uc2  that Washington DC\u8217\'20\'19s law license administrator is considering disciplinary action against him.\par \par \uc2 According to their report:\par \par \uc2 Clark, who is now also facing a federal investigation into his conduct, is accused of attempting to \u8220\'20\'1Cengage in conduct involving dishonesty\u8221\'20\'1D and attempting actions \u8220\'20\'1Cthat would seriously interfere with the administration of justice,\u8221\'20\'1D according to a petition filed by the D.C. Bar\u8217\'20\'19s Office of Disciplinary Counsel.\par \par \uc2 The ethics charges, dated June 29 and received by the Bar of the District of Columbia Court of Appeals on July 19, were made public on Friday, after Clark was served a copy of them in the morning, said Hamilton \u8220\'20\'1CPhil\u8221\'20\'1D Fox, the head of the D.C. Office of Disciplinary Counsel.\par \par \uc2 Rachel Semmel, a spokesperson from Center for Renewing America, Clark\u8217\'20\'19s new employer, called the charges \u8220\'20\'1Cthe latest attack on the legal qualifications of one of the only lawyers at the DOJ who had the interests of the American people at heart.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJeff Clark is an American hero and the media sure seems to enjoy being the press secretary for the J6 committee,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 As the report points out, similar charges have been filed against Trump lawyer \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 , who was involved in many of the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s schemes to overturn the result of the 2020 vote.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/23/jeff-clark-home-raid-election-overturn-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Raid of Jeffrey Clark\u8217\'20\'19s home escalation of inquiry into election overturn effort}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump plans civil service purge if returned to the White House: report\par \par \uc2 If voters were to elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to another term in the 2024 presidential election, he is considering using bureaucratic maneuvers to remove potentially tens of thousands of civil servants across the \uc2 US government\uc2  and replace them with people who adhere to his ideology, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2022/07/22/trump-2025-radical-plan-second-term"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a report from Axios}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That Trump expects his deputies to be unfailingly loyal to him is no secret, but during his time in the White House, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/13/jan-6-house-committee-second-hearing-conspiracy-theories"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 they didn\u8217\'20\'19t always do what he wanted}}}\uc2 . He intends to change that dramatically in a second term, according to the report, appointing staunch cabinet members and changing civil service regulations to allow him to dismiss up to 50,000 employees. He would replace these bureaucrats, who typically hold onto their jobs through presidential administrations, with people handpicked to support his \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica first\u8221\'20\'1D ideology.\par \par \uc2 Groups connected to him such as the Center for Renewing America and Jeffrey Clark, a former justice department official who Trump tried to install as attorney general but backed down after senior staff threatened a revolt, are already working to identify candidates, the report said.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from Axios on how the plan would work:\par \par \uc2 Trump signed an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://trumpwhitehouse.archives.gov/presidential-actions/executive-order-creating-schedule-f-excepted-service/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 executive order}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CCreating Schedule F in the Excepted Service,\u8221\'20\'1D in October 2020, which established a new employment category for federal employees. It received wide media coverage for a short period, then was largely forgotten in the mayhem and aftermath of Jan. 6 \u8212\'20\'14 and quickly was rescinded by President Biden.\par \par \uc2 Sources close to Trump say that if he were elected to a second term, he would immediately reimpose it.\par \par \uc2 Tens of thousands of civil servants who serve in roles deemed to have some influence over policy would be reassigned as \u8220\'20\'1CSchedule F\u8221\'20\'1D employees. Upon reassignment, they would lose their employment protections.\par \par \uc2 New presidents typically get to replace {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://presidentialtransition.org/faq/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 4,000}}}\uc2  so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitical\u8221\'20\'1D appointees to oversee the running of their administrations. But below this rotating layer of political appointees sits a mass of government workers who enjoy strong employment protections \u8212\'20\'14 and typically continue their service from one administration to the next, regardless of the president\u8217\'20\'19s party affiliation.\par \par \uc2 An initial estimate by the Trump official who came up with Schedule F found it could apply to as many as 50,000 federal workers \u8212\'20\'14 a fraction of a workforce of more than 2 million, but a segment with a profound role in shaping American life.\par \par \uc2 Trump, in theory, could fire tens of thousands of career government officials with no recourse for appeals. He could replace them with people he believes are more loyal to him and to his \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica First\u8221\'20\'1D agenda.\par \par \uc2 Even if Trump did not deploy Schedule F to this extent, the very fact that such power exists could create a significant chilling effect on government employees.\par \par \uc2 It would effectively upend the modern civil service, triggering a shock wave across the bureaucracy. The next president might then move to gut those pro-Trump ranks \u8212\'20\'14 and face the question of whether to replace them with her or his own loyalists, or revert to a traditional bureaucracy.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s plans to subvert power unconstitutionally were hiding in plain sight, Michael Beschloss said, as he continued his argument over the greater significance of January 6 in a series of tweets.\par \par \uc2 The views of Beschloss, who has written nine books about the American presidency, are worth reading in their entirety:\par \par \uc2 enltrAuthoritarians incite violence and then demand dictatorial power to enforce "law and order." (See modern Europe, history of.)\par \par \uc2 Looks increasingly as if this was Trump's game plan for January 6.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Michael Beschloss (@BeschlossDC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BeschlossDC/status/1550511149740765186?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrHow many times did we hear -- in public -- Trump boasting about all of the emergency powers a President had -- starting with martial law -- that he said he couldn't "talk about?"\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Michael Beschloss (@BeschlossDC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BeschlossDC/status/1550512198833029122?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrHow many times did Trump "joke" in public about remaining President beyond two terms?\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Michael Beschloss (@BeschlossDC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BeschlossDC/status/1550512757669109760?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThe January 6 attack and Trump's role in it was fully foreshadowed by the previous six years -- contempt for democracy, fascination with violence and how to exploit it, eagerness to grab authoritarian power.\par \par \uc2 He told us in public almost every day who he was and what he wanted.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Michael Beschloss (@BeschlossDC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BeschlossDC/status/1550514616005828609?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Michael Beschloss, a noted presidential historian, has warned in an interview on MSNBC about the corrosive effects of the January 6 insurrection and urged Americans not to get complacent about the attack\u8217\'20\'19s significance:\par \par \uc2 enltrOn Trump\u8217\'20\'19s action on Jan. 6, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BeschlossDC?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @BeschlossDC}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThis was a massive blueprint that didn't just happen by accident\u8230\'20\'26To treat this only as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  didn't do enough to stop something someone else started, I think the facts are suggesting something that's much larger.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/AMRstaff?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #AMRstaff}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Andrea Mitchell (@mitchellreports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mitchellreports/status/1550510147851657218?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrOn the significance of Jan. 6, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BeschlossDC?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @BeschlossDC}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CWhat I'm worried about is that we get so familiar with the story that we think this is the way that American history operates. We have never seen anything like this, you know, this is way off the track of democracy.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/AMRstaff?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #AMRstaff}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Andrea Mitchell (@mitchellreports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mitchellreports/status/1550510497937719299?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden's Covid-19 'symptoms have improved': White House doctor\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is on the mend from Covid-19, his doctor said in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/Letter-7.22.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an update on his health released by the White House this morning}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Csymptoms have improved,\u8221\'20\'1D Kevin C. O\u8217\'20\'19Connor wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CHe did mount a temperature yesterday evening to 99.4 degrees fahrenheit, which responded favorably to acetaminophen... His temperature has remained normal since then.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden is also taking anti-Covid drug Paxlovid. His symptoms currently include a running nose and fatigue, with the occasional cough.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe president is fully vaccinated and twice-boosted, so I anticipate that he will respond favorable, as most maximally protected patients do. There has been nothing in the course of his illness thus far which gives me cause to alter that initial expectation,\u8221\'20\'1D O\u8217\'20\'19Connor wrote.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 The January 6 committee in a nutshell: 'The mob was accomplishing president Trump\u8217\'20\'19s purpose' \u8220\'20\'1CWhat explains President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s behavior?\u8221\'20\'1D asked congressman \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2 , one of two Republicans on the January 6 committee. Photograph: Lamkey Rod/CNP/ABACA/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe mob was accomplishing president Trump\u8217\'20\'19s purpose. So of course he didn\u8217\'20\'19t intervene.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That was how \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2 , one of two Republicans on the January 6 committee, summed up what the panel uncovered last night. His statement near the start of the hearing was followed by testimony from two former White House officials present in the room and video clips from the lawmakers\u8217\'20\'19 interviews with former White House officials, including attorney \uc2 Pat Cipollone\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C What explains President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s behavior. Why did he not take immediate action in a time of crisis?\u8221\'20\'1D Kinzinger asked. \u8220\'20\'1CBecause president Trump\u8217\'20\'19s plan for January 6 was to halt or delay Congress\u8217\'20\'19s official proceeding to count the votes. The mob... attacking the Capitol quickly caused the evacuation of both the House and the Senate. The count ground to an absolute halt and was ultimately delayed for hours.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The committee won\u8217\'20\'19t host another hearing until sometime in September, and plans to use the coming weeks to continue their investigation. As the committee vice-chair, \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , put it last night: \u8220\'20\'1CDoors have opened, new subpoenas have been issued and the dam has begun to break.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 As the January 6 committee was airing evidence, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/andrew-lawrence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Andrew Lawrence}}}\uc2  entered an alternate universe, just by watching Fox News:\par \par \uc2 On Thursday night as the Congressional hearings into the January 6 Capitol riot drew to a close, \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  directed his outrage at a president he felt had lied and was not being held accountable for falsehoods that shook popular faith in the American democratic system. But he wasn\u8217\'20\'19t talking about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  inciting rioters to storm the Capitol. He was talking about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  getting Covid.\par \par \uc2 Whilemillions of people last night tuned into America\u8217\'20\'19s other TV news channels and heard testimony about what Trump did, or rather did not do, during the hours when the rioters stormed the Capitol, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/fox-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fox News}}}\uc2  viewers saw the network\u8217\'20\'19s primetime stars Carlson and \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2  chide the \u8220\'20\'1Ctwice jabbed, double-boosted\u8221\'20\'1D president for contracting the virus they say he alleged couldn\u8217\'20\'19t be caught with a vaccine.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/21/fox-news-january-6-hearing-biden-covid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 As the US watched the January 6 hearing, Fox News showed outrage \u8211\'20\'13 at Biden getting Covid}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  is one of the many Trump associates whose comments were shown by the January 6 committee last night, but he may be the only one currently embroiled in active criminal trial.\par \par \uc2 In fact, the charges he\u8217\'20\'19s facing center around his defiance of a subpoena from the committee, and both sides are today expected to finish making their cases before a jury. Politico reports that Bannon\u8217\'20\'19s legal team wants to question the jury about whether they watched last night\u8217\'20\'19s hearing.\par \par \uc2 enltrHAPPENING SOON: Bannon returns to court just hours after the Jan. 6 select committee featured him prominently at the close of their hearing. The case is expected to go to the jury today but I\u8217\'20\'19m anticipating some discussion about whether jurors may have watched.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1550456076360990721?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrAs expected, BANNON team raises his mention in last night's hearing as a potential problem for the jury. Here's a filing that just arrived: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/5WdvxXPzM1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/5WdvxXPzM1}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1550466845802651649?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrBANNON wants judge to question jury:\par \par \uc2 "The Defendant respectfully requests...that there should be some inquiry, while assuring the jurors of the importance of candor and that they will not suffer negative consequences if they acknowledge exposure to the broadcast or its subject."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1550467284866682883?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Closing arguments in the case are now underway:\par \par \uc2 enltrUPDATE: Closing arguments are now underway. Judge Nichols has already instructed the jurors, so they'll begin deliberating as soon as this is over. Expect they'll be deliberating by 11-11:30 a.m.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1550477918270148608?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 22, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/18/steve-bannon-contempt-of-congress-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Steve Bannon appears in court as contempt-of-Congress trial begins}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/davidsmith"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 David Smith}}}\uc2  was in the room last night as the January 6 committee conducted what some are calling its \u8220\'20\'1Cseason finale\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 They did it. They pulled it off. Anyone who feared that the January 6 committee\u8217\'20\'19s season finale would turn into an anti-climax \u8211\'20\'13 more Game of Thrones than M*A*S*H \u8211\'20\'13 need not have worried. There were shocks, horrors and even laughs.\par \par \uc2 The eight \u8220\'20\'1Cepisodes\u8221\'20\'1D have exceeded all expectations with their crisp narrative and sharp editing, a far cry from the usual dry proceedings on Capitol Hill. Each has recapped what came before, teased what is to come and compellingly joined the dots against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Much of the credit must go to James Goldston, the former president of ABC News, who was brought in to help produce the hearings like a true crime series. Give that man an Emmy (if only to infuriate Trump, a TV obsessive).\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/22/january-6-panel-gripping-finale-trump-us-capitol-riot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hearing delivers gripping \u8216\'20\'18finale\u8217\'20\'19 full of damning details about Trump}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today, the Republican party remains by and large the domain of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . He still {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/president-primary-r/2024/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leads in polls of potential candidates in the next election}}}\uc2 , and House Republican leadership routinely criticizes the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HouseGOP/status/1550310004900724738?s=20&t=DbVdBofv00Sdpzxt6Jjpmg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 6 committee}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Last night\u8217\'20\'19s hearing was however full of reminders that top Republicans appeared ready to break with Trump during and immediately after the insurrection - or at least were terrified by it. Case in point: the much-mocked video footage of rightwing senator \uc2 Josh Hawley{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/21/josh-hawley-running-away-rioters-january-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fleeing through the halls of the Capitol}}}\uc2  as the protesters he greeted as he walked in overwhelmed police.\par \par \uc2 Then there was Kevin McCarthy, the leader of the party in the House of Representatives who could be the chamber\u8217\'20\'19s next speaker, should Republicans gain seats in November\u8217\'20\'19s midterms. The committee last night showed that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/videos/politics/2022/07/22/kevin-mccarthy-trump-calls-january-6-hearing-vpx.cnn/video/playlists/the-january-6-hearings/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he pleaded with Trump}}}\uc2  as the insurrection was ongoing to call off the mob - which the president refused to do. Viewers also saw a repeat of his floor speech seven days after the attack, where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yw5TUmX6irY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he pinned the blame squarely on Trump}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Days later, McCarthy went to Florida, where he met with the former president and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/mccarthy-tries-to-mend-fences-with-trump-11611872037"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeared in a picture beside him}}}\uc2  that is now seen as having been key to reviving Trump\u8217\'20\'19s standing among the party.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 'He chose not to act': Washington grapples with evidence of Trump's willful inaction on January 6\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. Last night, the January 6 committee wrapped up its first weeks of hearings by airing evidence that showed \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/21/january-6-hearing-donald-trump-us-capitol-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 resisted efforts to forcefully condemn the rioters who broke into the Capitol that day}}}\uc2 , despite the pleas of top White House officials and his own family members to do so. As Congressman \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2  put it: \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump did not fail to act during the 187 minutes between leaving the Ellipse and telling the mob to go home. He chose not to act.\u8221\'20\'1D Expect the aftershocks from those revelations to wash through Washington today.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening today:\par \par \uc2 * Trump speaks at an Arizona rally for candidates in the state he has endorsed, which kicks off at 4 pm eastern time.\par \par \uc2 * The trial of \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 , a former top advisor to Trump who featured in last night\u8217\'20\'19s hearing, continues over contempt of Congress charges.\par \par \uc2 * Congress is still negotiating over a bunch of legislation, including measures to boost American competitiveness, codify same-sex marriage rights and lower prescription drug and health care costs.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220722ei7m001xh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
