\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez and House colleagues arrested during pro-choice protest\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Aratani in New York \par \uc2 717 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 July 2022\par 18:31 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 27\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The legislators were engaged in peaceful civil disobedience against the loss of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in front of the supreme court\par \par \uc2 Several prominent Democratic members of Congress were arrested on Wednesday during a protest in support of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in front of the supreme court, in the aftermath of the historic overturning of Roe v Wade last month.\par \par \uc2 The politicians gathered in front of the US Capitol before marching to the court building, chanting \u8220\'20\'1Cour bodies, our choice\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cwe won\u8217\'20\'19t go back\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The group, which included the prominent progressives Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez, \uc2 Ilhan Omar\uc2 , \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2  and Cori Bush, proceeded to stand along a crosswalk, or pedestrian crossing area, in front of the court, which is surrounded by a large black fence claimed to be unclimbable and erected to keep protesters away.\par \par \uc2 Happening rn: MOCs & EDs of orgs across the country are risking arrest at the Capitol. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/BansOffOurBodies?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #BansOffOurBodies}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CPDAction?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @CPDAction}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Cl9ldc9iBf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Cl9ldc9iBf}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 Maegan LLerena ?? (@maeganllerena) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/maeganllerena/status/1549444005783535618?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 19, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The group sat down in the middle of the street as an act of civil disobedience, as a group of police officers gathered around them, broadcasting a pre-recorded message announcing imminent arrest for blocking the street.\par \par \uc2 The officers then {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CapitolPolice/status/1549477982187700227"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arrested the lawmakers}}}\uc2 , escorting them to an area taped off away from the street.\par \par \uc2 Multiple members of Congress, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AOC?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @AOC}}}\uc2 , being arrested by \uc2 Capitol Police\uc2  for blocking traffic outside the Supreme Court in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights demonstration: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/fysQN1oBAw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/fysQN1oBAw}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 Andrew Solender (@AndrewSolender) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewSolender/status/1549445768683061249?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 19, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CPDAction/status/1549436741177602049?s=20&t=YdHlpBA_2zBe5Jbo9FSERw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 livestream}}}\uc2  of the protest was posted online by CPD Action, the protest-centered arm of the Center for Popular Democracy, a social justice organization, which coordinated the direct action.\par \par \uc2 CPD Action said 18 members of Congress were arrested. Seventeen were women. \uc2 Andy Levin\uc2  of Michigan was the sole congressman among them.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, \uc2 Carolyn Maloney\uc2 , a Democrat from New York who was also arrested, said: \u8220\'20\'1CI have the privilege of representing a state where reproductive rights are respected and protected \u8211\'20\'13 the least I can do is put my body on the line for the 33 million women at risk of losing their rights.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jackie Speier, a representative from California who was also arrested, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JackieSpeier"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CProud to march with my Democratic colleagues and get arrested for women\u8217\'20\'19s rights, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, the rights for people to control their own bodies and the future and our democracy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Reps. Jackie Speier and \uc2 Carolyn Maloney\uc2  getting arrested {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/c1AP7ILHDu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/c1AP7ILHDu}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 Nancy Vu (@NancyVu99) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NancyVu99/status/1549445667336110081?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 19, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 It has been less than a month since the supreme court overturned the landmark 1973 Roe v Wade ruling, which protected the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  under the constitution. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now banned or under threat of being banned in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2022/jun/28/tracking-where-abortion-laws-stand-in-every-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 60% of states}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Backlash against the supreme court, which is now dominated by six conservative justices, including three appointed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , intensified in May when a draft of the decision to overturn Roe was leaked. Soon after, the court installed the 7ft security fence.\par \par \uc2 Immediately after the release of the official decision, massive protests {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/24/us-cities-protest-roe-v-wade-abortion-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 swept}}}\uc2  the US from New York to Los Angeles, including in large cities of Republican-led states such as Missouri and Texas.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has announced and the House has since passed bills offering {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/15/house-abortion-vote-approved"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 federal protections}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 but these are largely symbolic as long as the Senate is all but certain to reject such legislation, and as the individual states now have the right to dictate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulation.\par \par \uc2 Analilia Mejia, co-executive director of the Center for Popular Democracy Action, said the protest \u8220\'20\'1Csent a powerful message to Republican lawmakers and [the supreme court]: we will not back down.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur rights, our freedoms, and our reproductive autonomy matters. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is healthcare and a human right \u8211\'20\'13 and you don\u8217\'20\'19t represent the vast majority of Americans who believe we, not the government, should dictate our own health decisions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Polling shows consistent majorities in favor of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  being legal.\par \par \uc2 Mejia said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe will not stop fighting for the world our communities deserve \u8211\'20\'13 one that honors our right to decide our futures.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This article was amended on 20 July 2022 to remove a reference to the lawmakers being handcuffed by police.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220719ei7j003ju\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
