\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden to make Wednesday climate address as dangerous heat grips US and world \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein in Washington \par \uc2 5,011 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 July 2022\par 20:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Manchin blunts Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 hopes of passing climate billSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  plans an address on climate change tomorrow, where he may announce new executive orders to curb US emissions after his attempts to achieve reductions via legislation stalled in Congress. However, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/19/biden-climate-emergency-congress-same-sex-marriage-bill-politics-latest?page=with:block-62d6e2358f08d02cb60eef0b#block-62d6e2358f08d02cb60eef0b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he won\u8217\'20\'19t declare a climate emergency}}}\uc2 , at least not yet.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else happened today:\par \par \uc2 * The January 6 committee will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/19/biden-climate-emergency-congress-same-sex-marriage-bill-politics-latest?page=with:block-62d6bc638f08d02cb60eec95#block-62d6bc638f08d02cb60eec95"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 continue with its hearing}}}\uc2  planned for the Thursday prime-time TV hour despite its chair \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2  testing positive for Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 * The second day of \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s trial {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/19/biden-climate-emergency-congress-same-sex-marriage-bill-politics-latest?page=with:block-62d6de9a8f08b3cb1ab4fe8d#block-62d6de9a8f08b3cb1ab4fe8d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 got underway}}}\uc2  in Washington.\par \par \uc2 * The Secret Service has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/19/biden-climate-emergency-congress-same-sex-marriage-bill-politics-latest?page=with:block-62d6ea1f8f08d02cb60eef44#block-62d6ea1f8f08d02cb60eef44"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lost for good text messages}}}\uc2  from 5 and 6 January 2021, when the US Capitol was attacked. The National Archives {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/19/biden-climate-emergency-congress-same-sex-marriage-bill-politics-latest?page=with:block-62d70b3a8f0883b6bb6b0538#block-62d70b3a8f0883b6bb6b0538"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is demanding}}}\uc2  an investigation.\par \par \uc2 * Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s first lady \uc2 Olena Zelenska\uc2  is in Washington {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/19/biden-climate-emergency-congress-same-sex-marriage-bill-politics-latest?page=with:block-62d702748f08d02cb60ef017#block-62d702748f08d02cb60ef017"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for meetings with the Biden administration and an address to Congress}}}\uc2  on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s reported trip to Taiwan has prompted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/19/biden-climate-emergency-congress-same-sex-marriage-bill-politics-latest?page=with:block-62d6b3ff8f08b3cb1ab4fbd0#block-62d6b3ff8f08b3cb1ab4fbd0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a warning from China}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * There are at least 120 Republicans election deniers running for office, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/19/biden-climate-emergency-congress-same-sex-marriage-bill-politics-latest?page=with:block-62d6c7268f0883b6bb6b0252#block-62d6c7268f0883b6bb6b0252"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an analysis by FiveThirtyEight}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * A small explosion and fire occurred at Hoover Dam, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/19/biden-climate-emergency-congress-same-sex-marriage-bill-politics-latest?page=with:block-62d6f8ee8f08b3cb1ab4ffb5#block-62d6f8ee8f08b3cb1ab4ffb5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was quickly contained}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 National Archives demands probe of Secret Service January 6 text message deletion\par \par \uc2 Following today\u8217\'20\'19s revelation that the Secret Service deleted text messages from the January 6 attack and the day before, \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  reports that National Archives is now demanding an investigation:\par \par \uc2 The US National Archives has asked the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/secret-service"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Secret Service}}}\uc2  to conduct an internal investigation over \u8220\'20\'1Cerased\u8221\'20\'1D text messages from the day before and the day of the Capitol attack, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.archives.gov/files/records-mgmt/resources/ud-2022-0054-dhs-usss-open.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a letter}}}\uc2  sent to the agency\u8217\'20\'19s records management officer on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The request marks the latest escalation of the matter after the watchdog for the Secret Service, the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  inspector general, notified Congress he had sought the texts {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/14/us-secret-service-agents-texts-erased-january-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 only to be told they no longer existed}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the letter sent to the Secret Service records officer, reviewed by the Guardian, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk/nationalarchives"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 National Archives}}}\uc2  requested the agency launch an internal review and report within 30 calendar days if it finds any texts were \u8220\'20\'1Cimproperly deleted\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/19/secret-service-investigation-erased-january-6-texts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Secret Service told to begin an inquiry into erased January 6 text messages}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s only \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic and the subject of the supreme court case that overturned Roe v. Wade last month, has given up its legal battle to continue operating.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/mississippi-abortion-clinic-drops-challenge-states-ban-after-sale-2022-07-19/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Reuters reports}}}\uc2  that the clinic was making a last-ditch legal effort before the state supreme court to get it to halt Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s almost total ban on abortions, but threw in the towel after the clinic\u8217\'20\'19s owner sold the building. Its fate seemed sealed earlier this month after a judge rejected the clinic\u8217\'20\'19s petition to halt the ban, which went into effect following last month\u8217\'20\'19s ruling by the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  in the case Dobbs v. Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/06/mississippi-abortion-clinic-closing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s only \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  clinic to close after judge leaves state law in force}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 U.S. first lady Jill Biden, first lady of Ukraine \uc2 Olena Zelenska\uc2  and U.S. president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  pose for photos as Zelenska arrives on the South Lawn of the White House July 19, 2022 in Washington, DC. Photograph: Drew Angerer/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s first lady \uc2 Olena Zelenska\uc2  is in Washington for meetings at the White House and an address to Congress. As you can see above, she\u8217\'20\'19s already met Joe and Jill Biden.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what Zelenska had to say about the visit after meeting with secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 enltrFeels strange \u8211\'20\'13 not to hear any sirens. At the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FLOTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @FLOTUS}}}\uc2  invitation, I arrived to the USA to discuss our needs in the fight against the aggressor. It is also the topic of the meeting with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SecBlinken?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SecBlinken}}}\uc2 . His position remains the same: independent ???? will exist much longer than Putin. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dTUA8QtFk9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/dTUA8QtFk9}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ????? ????????? (@ZelenskaUA) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ZelenskaUA/status/1549183170632994817?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 19, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Tomorrow, she will address senators and House representatives in the Capitol. In a letter to lawmakers, House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  said, \u8220\'20\'1CWe hope that all Members will take advantage of this important and timely opportunity to hear directly from First Lady Zelenska, to learn more about the terrible toll of the Russian invasion and to express our gratitude to the people of Ukraine for their fight for Democracy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile in Washington, a group of House Democrats was arrested in front of the supreme court after staging a demonstration in support of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 enltrMultiple members of Congress, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AOC?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @AOC}}}\uc2 , being arrested by \uc2 Capitol Police\uc2  for blocking traffic outside the Supreme Court in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights demonstration: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/fysQN1oBAw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/fysQN1oBAw}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Andrew Solender (@AndrewSolender) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewSolender/status/1549445768683061249?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 19, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrHere\u8217\'20\'19s where they\u8217\'20\'19re being corralled. The group also includes the assistant House speaker, Katherine Clark. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2jNIRB2WtU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/2jNIRB2WtU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Andrew Solender (@AndrewSolender) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewSolender/status/1549446663147757569?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 19, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrMembers arrested:\par \par \uc2 Dean, Velasquez, Lee, Speier, Clark, Jacobs, Ocasio-Cortez, Tlaib, \uc2 Andy Levin\uc2 , \uc2 Carolyn Maloney\uc2 , Adams, Watson Coleman, Escobar, Bush, Schakowsky, Omar & Pressley.\par \par \uc2 w/ {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/OrianaBeLike?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @OrianaBeLike}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/pR0b0sve5u"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/pR0b0sve5u}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Andrew Solender (@AndrewSolender) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewSolender/status/1549461645008715777?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 19, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Last week, the Democratic-led House approved legislation that protected \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access nationwide, after the supreme court overturned Roe v. Wade and allowed states to ban the procedure. However, there\u8217\'20\'19s no sign the legislation will be able to overcome a Republican filibuster in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/15/house-abortion-vote-approved"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House approves legislation to protect \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access across US }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 A small explosion and fire broke out but was quickly extinguished at Hoover Dam, which is at the center of the western United States\u8217\'20\'19s massive drought.\par \par \uc2 enltrtouring the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/hooverdam?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #hooverdam}}}\uc2  and heard an explosion {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/fire?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #fire}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/1tjWuNWBaZ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/1tjWuNWBaZ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kristy Hairston (@kristynashville) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kristynashville/status/1549441916000825344?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 19, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The embankment straddling the Nevada-Arizona border holds back Lake Mead, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/01/lake-mead-shrinking-second-world-war-boat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 which has dropped to its lowest level since it was full 20 years ago due to drought and climate change}}}\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/small-explosion-fire-hoover-dam-quickly-extinguished-2022-07-19/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Reuters reports}}}\uc2  that the blaze at Hoover Dam had been extinguished before the local fire department arrived.\par \par \uc2 It is unclear if the lake\u8217\'20\'19s low water level played a role in the explosion, but authorities warn that the reservoir could soon hit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/US/water-levels-lake-mead-dangerously-close-hitting-dead/story?id=85584196#:~:text=The%20minimum%20surface%20elevation%20needed,at%20895%20feet%20in%20elevation."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cdead pool\u8221\'20\'1D levels,}}}\uc2  when water will no longer be able to flow downstream.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former New York City mayor \uc2 Bill de Blasio\uc2  has ended his bid for the Democratic nomination in the state\u8217\'20\'19s 10th congressional district.\par \par \uc2 enltrIt\u8217\'20\'19s clear the people of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/NY10?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #NY10}}}\uc2  are looking for another option and I respect that. Time for me to leave electoral politics and focus on other ways to serve. I am really grateful for all the people I met, the stories I heard and the many good souls who helped out. Thank you all! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/gpt6V6WLUf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/gpt6V6WLUf}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Bill de Blasio\uc2  (@BilldeBlasio) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BilldeBlasio/status/1549443376189263873?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 19, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 De Blasio, who led America\u8217\'20\'19s largest city for eight years and left office with low approval ratings, was trailing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cityandstateny.com/politics/2022/07/rivera-niou-goldman-form-top-tier-new-10th-congressional-district-poll/374225/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://workingfamilies.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/220712_NY_10.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polls}}}\uc2  to represent the district that includes part of the city in the \uc2 U.S. House of Representatives\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Secret Service will tell Congress it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have any new texts to give to the House subcommittee investigating the January 6 insurrection, according to \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  reporter Carol Leonnig.\par \par \uc2 enltrMORE NEWWWS - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SecretService?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SecretService}}}\uc2  will tell Congress it doesn't have any new texts from its agents around Jan 6 attack to provide. Anything not already turned over has been purged. Its gone.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Carol Leonnig (@CarolLeonnig) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CarolLeonnig/status/1549428733307756545?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 19, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The House committee set a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/18/secret-service-deleted-texts-january-6-committee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deadline}}}\uc2  for today for the Secret Service to hand over deleted texts that were sent among agents, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  on the day before and the day of the riot. Last week, the inspector general for the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/14/us-secret-service-agents-texts-erased-january-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 notified}}}\uc2  the committee that texts from those days had been deleted. The explanation from the Secret Service for the deletions have shifted several times, from software upgrades to device replacements.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 From the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s senior reporter {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/nina-lakhani"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nina Lakhani}}}\uc2 , who reports on climate justice:\par \par \uc2 As attention focuses on the extreme temperatures scorching large swathes of Europe and the US, its worth drawing attention to other parts of the world where dangerous heat and drought have also been causing misery.\par \par \uc2 In Monterrey, Mexico\u8217\'20\'19s third largest city where temperatures above 100F are the norm throughout the summer, residents are enduring a second month of water rationing as three dams which supply households are almost dry. Authorities are turning on taps for only six hours per day, though some residents have gone without any running water for long spells, and are forced to spend hours every day lining up at communal taps. The national water authority has declared a state of emergency across the country because of drought.\par \par \uc2 According to the North American Drought Monitor, 56% of Mexico is experiencing some level of drought with northern states like Nuevo Leon (home to Monterrey), Sonora, Chihuahua, and Coahuila particularly badly due to a combination of La Ni\u241\'00\'F1a and global heating. Most of the country\u8217\'20\'19s wheat is farmed in this northern belt, which is among three crops (along with maize and rice) that make up almost half the world\u8217\'20\'19s calories. All three grains are vulnerable to extreme heat and drought, in large part because industrialised agriculture favors monocropping over crop diversity.\par \par \uc2 This was a little reported consequence of the punishing spring extreme heatwave in India and Pakistan, where more than a billion people faced temperatures from 100 to 122F from late March to the end of June, a period of almost 100 days. As a result, wheat yields dropped by about 15%, compounding the shortages caused by Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine. Livestock died across the subcontinent.\par \par \uc2 The number of deaths so far attributed directly to the extreme spring heat is surprisingly low, just 90, compared to more than 1100 so far in Spain and Portugal, though this is likely at least partly down to issues with counting and reporting heat deaths. (Recent floods in India and Bangladesh have led to high death tolls, but this could be because such deaths are easier to count.) It\u8217\'20\'19s the monsoon now in India, so temperatures have dropped significantly - it\u8217\'20\'19s only 90F in Delhi today - but the humidity is very high. Humid heat is far more dangerous than dry heat, so the death toll could rise across the Asian subcontinent without anyone paying much attention.\par \par \uc2 Read more about crop scientists in Mexico developing heat and climate resilient wheat varieties here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/jun/12/wheat-breeding-climate-crisis-drought-resistant"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The race against time to breed a wheat to survive the climate crisis}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is not going to declare a climate emergency when he delivers an address on climate change in Somerset, Massachusetts tomorrow, according to the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 A source told the AP that while Biden is planning to announce steps the White House is taking to address climate change, he will not declare a climate emergency.\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden is not going to issue an emergency climate declaration this week, according to an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AP?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @AP}}}\uc2  source. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/PWfms6Eq0R"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/PWfms6Eq0R}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chris Megerian (@ChrisMegerian) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChrisMegerian/status/1549428745836134404?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 19, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Earlier today, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/climate-environment/2022/07/18/biden-climate-emergency-manchin/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post}}}\uc2  reported that Biden was floating the idea of declaring an emergency after senator Joe Manchin effectively blocked a spending package that would have allocated billions toward addressing the climate emergency. Manchin told Democratic leaders last week that he does not support the package, ultimately striking down its chance of passage.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s day two of \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s federal trial in Washington DC as he faces charges of contempt for Congress, ignoring subpoenas from the House select committee investigating the January 6 insurrection.\par \par \uc2 A lawyer for Bannon has asked the judge to delay the trial by a month so the defense team can figure out what evidence they could offer. The judge, Carl J Nichols, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/dc-md-va/2022/07/18/steve-bannon-trial-jury/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 denied}}}\uc2  his lawyer\u8217\'20\'19s request, but said he may push back the start of opening arguments a day so both teams can organize themselves.\par \par \uc2 enltrJust in: Judge Carl Nichols denies \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8212\'20\'14 latest \u8212\'20\'14 request to delay trial, this time by a month\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1549408067799994368?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 19, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Bannon\u8217\'20\'19s trial began yesterday with jury selection. Attorneys have narrowed the pool down to 22 prospective, with a final 12 needed, along with two alternatives.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.ohio.gov/rod/docs/pdf/0/2022/2022-Ohio-2471.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has struck down}}}\uc2  the state\u8217\'20\'19s 15 congressional districts, saying they were so distorted in favor of Republicans that they violated the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 In a 4-3 ruling, the court gave the state legislature 30 days to come up with a new map. If the legislature fails to come up with a new plan, a GOP-controlled commission would then have another 30 days.\par \par \uc2 Any new map would be in effect for the 2024 elections. After striking down the initial map Republicans passed earlier this year, the Ohio supreme court declined to intervene again ahead of the state\u8217\'20\'19s primary and block a revised map. The map they struck down Tuesday was that revised plan.\par \par \uc2 The plan creates 10 Republican-leaning districts and five Democratic-leaning districts, the court noted. While all 10 GOP districts are solidly Republican, three of the five Democratic ones are highly competitive, meaning Republicans could win them in a strong year for the party. Projections show Democrats would most likely win four in the state\u8217\'20\'19s congressional delegation, despite winning around 47% of the statewide vote.\par \par \uc2 That split violates a provision in the state constitution that prohibits maps that \u8220\'20\'1Cunduly favors or disfavors a political party or its incumbents.\u8221\'20\'1D Ohio voters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ballotpedia.org/Ohio_Issue_1,_Congressional_Redistricting_Procedures_Amendment_(May_2018)"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overwhelmingly approved}}}\uc2  adding that language to the state constitution in 2018.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CComparative analyses and other metrics show that the March 2 plan allocates voters in ways that unnecessarily favor the Republican Party by packing Democratic voters into a few dense Democratic-leaning districts, thereby increasing the Republican vote share of the remaining districts,\u8221\'20\'1D the court\u8217\'20\'19s majority wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CAs a result, districts that would otherwise be strongly Democratic-leaning are now competitive or Republican-leaning districts.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The three judges who dissented argued that the majority opinion sought to use a system of proportional representation, which is not required under Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s constitution.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s ruling marks the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whio.com/news/local/ohio-supreme-court-rejects-gop-drawn-statehouse-maps-5th-time/G5O7V3AMGRGKHGRVO6UB67YMUE/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seventh time}}}\uc2  the Ohio supreme court has struck down congressional and state legislative maps this cycle. Despite all of those rulings, all of the maps struck down passed by lawmakers will be in place for at least the 2022 elections.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/12/ohio-republican-judge-blocking-party-from-distorting-electoral-districts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Republican judge blocking her party from rigging electoral districts}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  plans an address on climate change tomorrow, during which he could declare a national climate emergency after his attempts to get legislation lowering America\u8217\'20\'19s carbon emissions through Congress stalled.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened so far today:\par \par \uc2 * The January 6 committee will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/19/biden-climate-emergency-congress-same-sex-marriage-bill-politics-latest?page=with:block-62d6bc638f08d02cb60eec95#block-62d6bc638f08d02cb60eec95"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 continue with its hearing}}}\uc2  planned for the Thursday prime-time TV hour despite its chair \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2  testing positive for Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 * The Secret Service will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/19/biden-climate-emergency-congress-same-sex-marriage-bill-politics-latest?page=with:block-62d6af408f08d02cb60eebe1#block-62d6af408f08d02cb60eebe1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 turn over texts to the January 6 committee}}}\uc2  that were said to have been deleted.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s reported trip to Taiwan has prompted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/19/biden-climate-emergency-congress-same-sex-marriage-bill-politics-latest?page=with:block-62d6b3ff8f08b3cb1ab4fbd0#block-62d6b3ff8f08b3cb1ab4fbd0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a warning from China}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * There are about 120 Republicans election deniers running for office - at least, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/19/biden-climate-emergency-congress-same-sex-marriage-bill-politics-latest?page=with:block-62d6c7268f0883b6bb6b0252#block-62d6c7268f0883b6bb6b0252"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an analysis by FiveThirtyEight}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden plans Wednesday address on climate crisis\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will outline his next steps to tackle climate change in an address in Somerset, Massachusetts on Wednesday, the White House announced. \u8220\'20\'1CThe president will deliver remarks on tackling the climate crisis and seizing the opportunity of a clean energy future to create jobs and lower costs for families,\u8221\'20\'1D according to a statement.\par \par \uc2 The president may use the trip to declare the national climate emergency The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  reports his administration has been mulling. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/us-president-biden-deliver-remarks-climate-crisis-wednesday-2022-07-19/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Reuters quotes}}}\uc2  a White House official as saying, \u8220\'20\'1CWe are considering all options and no decision has been made.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 120. That\u8217\'20\'19s the number of Republican candidates who deny the results of the 2020 election and will be on the ballot this fall, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fivethirtyeight.com/features/at-least-120-republicans-who-deny-the-2020-election-results-will-be-on-the-ballot-in-november/?ex_cid=story-twitter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an analysis by FiveThirtyEight}}}\uc2 , which notes that may not be the full count.\par \par \uc2 Election denying is most common in House of Representatives and governorship races, and least in secretary of state and Senate contests, according to the analysis. It\u8217\'20\'19s also hard to pin down the degree to which Republican politicians refuse to accept the validity of the results of the last presidential race, since many haven\u8217\'20\'19t made their views known - which FiveThirtyEight concludes means some likely believe baseless theories about the outcome, but are keeping it to themselves.\par \par \uc2 Finally, the analysis finds that election denying is no surefire path to victory. Candidates who rejected the theory have in fact won 54 percent of races against an election denier, versus 36 percent for the deniers themselves. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what FiveThirtyEight has to say about that dynamic:\par \par \uc2 In other words, questioning the results of the 2020 election might not be a surefire path to the nomination, but it hasn\u8217\'20\'19t proven to be a dealbreaker for Republican voters, either. That speaks volumes as to the overall direction the Republican Party is moving in.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 The board of American journalism\u8217\'20\'19s highest honor, the Pulitzer Prizes, has put out a statement upholding its awarding of the 2018 prize in National Reporting to reporters from \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  and \uc2 The Washington Post\uc2  for their coverage of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s interference in the 2016 election and the Trump campaign\u8217\'20\'19s involvement.\par \par \uc2 The prize administrators had commissioned a review of the awards following \u8220\'20\'1Cinquiries\u8221\'20\'1D from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and others, but found no wrongdoing. Here\u8217\'20\'19s their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pulitzer.org/news/statement-pulitzer-prize-board-2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 full statement}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The Pulitzer Prize Board has an established, formal process by which complaints against winning entries are carefully reviewed. In the last three years, the Pulitzer Board has received inquiries, including from former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , about submissions from \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  and \uc2 The Washington Post\uc2  on Russian interference in the U.S. election and its connections to the Trump campaign--submissions that jointly won the 2018 National Reporting prize.\par \par \uc2 These inquiries prompted the Pulitzer Board to commission two independent reviews of the work submitted by those organizations to our National Reporting competition. Both reviews were conducted by individuals with no connection to the institutions whose work was under examination, nor any connection to each other. The separate reviews converged in their conclusions: that no passages or headlines, contentions or assertions in any of the winning submissions were discredited by facts that emerged subsequent to the conferral of the prizes.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pulitzer.org/winners/staffs-new-york-times-and-washington-post"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The 2018 Pulitzer Prizes in National Reporting}}}\uc2  stand.\par \par \uc2 Allegations that Trump colluded with Russia in the 2016 election sparked an investigation by special counsel \uc2 Robert Mueller\uc2 , which enraged the then-president but found no overarching conspiracy with Moscow, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/apr/18/mueller-report-william-barr-trump-russia-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 though it did turn up plenty of troubling conduct}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Maryland is holding its primary elections today, and \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/chrismcgreal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chris McGreal}}}\uc2  reports on the surprising involvement of pro-Israel lobbying groups in one of the races:\par \par \uc2 Pro-Israel lobby groups have poured millions of dollars into a Democratic primary for a Maryland congressional seat on Tuesday, in the latest attempt to block an establishment candidate who expressed support for the Palestinians.\par \par \uc2 A surge in political spending by organisations funded by hardline supporters of Israel, led by the \uc2 American Israel Public Affairs Committee\uc2  (\uc2 Aipac\uc2 ), has reshaped Democratic primaries over recent months even though debate about the country rarely figures as a major issue in the elections.\par \par \uc2 Critics accuse \uc2 Aipac\uc2  and its allies of distorting Democratic politics in part because much of the money used to influence primary races comes from billionaire Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/18/democratic-primaries-aipac-israel-hardline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pro-Israel hardliners spend millions to transform Democratic primaries}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 In other January 6 committee news, a lawmaker says the panel will be getting Secret Service text messages from the day of the insurrection and just before that the agency originally said had been deleted:\par \par \uc2 Deleted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/secret-service"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Secret Service}}}\uc2  texts sent on 6 January, the day of the insurrection at the US Capitol, and the day before will be released by Tuesday to the House committee investigating the failed attempt by supporters of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to overturn the 2020 presidential election result, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/policy/national-security/3563342-deleted-secret-service-texts-to-be-sent-to-jan-6-committee-by-tuesday-lofgren/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 panel member said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou can imagine how shocked we were to get the letter from the [\uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2 ] inspector general saying that he had been trying to get this information and that they had, in fact, been deleted after he\u8217\'20\'19d asked for them,\u8221\'20\'1D committee member and California Democratic congresswoman \uc2 Zoe Lofgren\uc2  told ABC\u8217\'20\'19s This Week.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need all the texts to get the full picture,\u8221\'20\'1D Lofgren added.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/18/secret-service-deleted-texts-january-6-committee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 6 committee to receive deleted Secret Service texts, Democrat says}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 January 6 committee will hold Thursday's hearing despite chair's Covid-19 test\par \par \uc2 The January 6 committee has just released a statement saying Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s hearing will proceed as scheduled, despite chair \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2  disclosing he had tested positive for Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile Chairman Thompson is disappointed with his COVID diagnosis, he has instructed the Select Committee to proceed with Thursday evening\u8217\'20\'19s hearing. Committee members and staff wish the Chairman a speedy recovery,\u8221\'20\'1D committee spokesperson Tim Mulvey said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 January 6 committee chair has Covid-19\par \par \uc2 Bennie Thomspon, the Democratic House representative leading the panel of lawmakers probing the January 6 insurrection, announced he has tested positive for Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 enltrI tested positive for COVID-19 yesterday, and I am experiencing mild symptoms. Gratefully, I am fully vaccinated and boosted.\par \par \uc2 I encourage each person in America to get vaccinated and continue to follow the guidelines to remain safe. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/brHXGlWmfq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/brHXGlWmfq}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Bennie G. Thompson\uc2  (@BennieGThompson) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BennieGThompson/status/1549394522215522304?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 19, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Thompson made no mention of how the diagnosis would impact the next hearing of the January 6 committee scheduled for Thursday, when two former top aides to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  are set to testify during the prime-time TV hour about what the president was doing as the Capitol was attacked.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  has the latest on the trial of former top Trump adviser \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 , which began yesterday, continues today and has thus far confirmed that Bannon still goes around wearing two shirts:\par \par \uc2 With jury selection nearly complete, opening arguments are expected to take place on Tuesday in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/18/steve-bannon-criminal-contempt-congress-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 federal trial against Steve Bannon}}}\uc2 , the top former Trump strategist charged with contempt of Congress after he failed to comply with a subpoena from the House January 6 committee.\par \par \uc2 Bannon appeared in federal court on Monday as his trial formally opened in Washington. The far-right provocateur \u8211\'20\'13 one of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/14/steve-bannon-audio-trump-declare-victory"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 principal architects}}}\uc2  of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attempts to overturn the 2020 election \u8211\'20\'13 is attempting to argue that he did not willfully fail to comply with the subpoena, which sought documents and testimony.\par \par \uc2 DC district court judge Carl Nichols is expected to proceed to opening arguments in the contempt trial once the final 12-person jury, with two alternates, is seated from a group of 22 prospective jurors, which was whittled down from an initial pool of 60 DC residents on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/18/steve-bannon-contempt-of-congress-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Steve Bannon appears in court as contempt-of-Congress trial begins}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 China warns US over Pelosi's reported trip to Taiwan\par \par \uc2 China has warned that its already-fraught relationship with the US will be further damaged if the House speaker, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , goes ahead with a reported trip to Taiwan next month.\par \par \uc2 Beijing said on Tuesday it would take \u8220\'20\'1Cforceful measures\u8221\'20\'1D if the visit took place. Pelosi had previously planned to travel with a congressional delegation to Taiwan in April. The trip was delayed because she tested positive for Covid.\par \par \uc2 Citing multiple sources, the \uc2 Financial Times\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 which first reported Pelosi\u8217\'20\'19s trip this week \u8211\'20\'13 said Pelosi and her delegation will also stop by Indonesia, Japan, Malaysia and Singapore, as well as Hawaii, where they will visit the headquarters of US Indo-Pacific command.\par \par \uc2 China regards Taiwan as a breakaway province and has vowed \u8211\'20\'13 repeatedly \u8211\'20\'13 to take it back, and by force if necessary. Beijing also calls the island\u8217\'20\'19s democratically-elected president, \uc2 Tsai Ing\uc2 -wen a \u8220\'20\'1Cseparatist\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Back in April, \uc2 China\u8217\'20\'19s foreign ministry\uc2  issued a similar warning, saying the trip would \u8220\'20\'1Cbring serious damage to the foundation of China-US relations, and would send the wrong messages to the Taiwan secessionists.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Tensions over the island of Taiwan has been on the rise. But China\u8217\'20\'19s Taiwan problem is not only with the United States. In the UK, the House of Commons Foreign Affairs Committee was also said to be planning on a trip to Taiwan in the autumn this year. But sources say the plan is rather uncertain now due to Conservative Party\u8217\'20\'19s leadership competition, which is under way.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 You may have seen {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CNN/status/1549184893397209090?s=20&t=lRdTiizAlxY_rTo-iWH1eQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the viral clip}}}\uc2  of a wave swamping a wedding in Hawaii. The Associated Press has the backstory to the rough seas, which were indeed caused, in part, by rising global temperatures:\par \par \uc2 Towering waves on Hawaii\u8217\'20\'19s south shores crashed into homes and businesses, spilled across highways and upended weddings over the weekend.\par \par \uc2 The large waves, some more than 20ft (6m) high, came from a combination of a strong south swell that peaked Saturday evening, particularly high tides and rising sea levels associated with climate change, the National Weather Service said Monday.\par \par \uc2 A wedding Saturday evening in Kailua-Kona was interrupted when a set of large waves swamped the event, sending tables and chairs crashing toward guests.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/18/hawaii-waves-swell-south-pacific"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Towering waves in Hawaii crash into homes, barrel through wedding venue}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Declaring a national climate emergency, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/climate-environment/2022/07/18/biden-climate-emergency-manchin/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Washington Post reports Biden is considering}}}\uc2  in response to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/15/joe-manchin-climate-funding-tax-hikes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 apparent demise of his efforts to get measures cutting America\u8217\'20\'19s climate emissions approved by Congress}}}\uc2 , would certainly generate headlines. But what exactly would it do?\par \par \uc2 The Post\u8217\'20\'19s report underline the ambiguities associated with the move:\par \par \uc2 It is unclear how, exactly, Biden plans to proceed if he opts to declare a climate emergency, which Senate Majority Leader \uc2 Charles E. Schumer\uc2  (D-N.Y.) urged him to do just days after the president took office last year.\par \par \uc2 Some climate activists have urged the White House in recent months to deploy an emergency declaration to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.biologicaldiversity.org/programs/energy-justice/pdfs/Climate-Emergency-Powers-Report.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 maximum effect}}}\uc2 , arguing that it would allow the president to halt crude oil exports, limit oil and gas drilling in federal waters, and direct agencies including the \uc2 Federal Emergency Management Agency\uc2  to boost renewable-energy sources.\par \par \uc2 The sad truth is that America is behind where it needs to be when it comes to keeping the planet from experiencing the worst effects of rising temperatures, and even if Biden had gotten his Build Back Better plan through Congress, it wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have been enough, as the below story from last October makes clear:\par \par \uc2 The Build Back Better plan will put America on track to meet its goals, but it must not be the only action congress takes to combat the climate crisis, said congresswoman \uc2 Kathy Castor\uc2 , a Florida Democrat and chair of the House select committee on the climate crisis. More federal action is needed to meet the scale of the emergency, she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEven if we pass the Build Back Better Act as it is, that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t get us to net-zero by 2050, which is the goal,\u8221\'20\'1D she said in an interview. Pointing to the latest climate research and a report by the \uc2 Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change\uc2  that declared a \u8220\'20\'1Ccode red\u8221\'20\'1D for humanity, she added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are going to have to do more.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Build Back Better is now dead, and it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear if the executive actions Biden says he will now resort to will be anywhere near as effective as his unrealized proposals to curb climate change.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2021/oct/18/joe-biden-climate-crisis-legislation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18This is our last chance\u8217\'20\'19: Biden urged to act as climate agenda hangs by a thread}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 With Congress paralyzed, Biden mulls declaring climate emergency\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. Is America in the midst of a national climate emergency? The White House may as soon as this week declare it is indeed, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/climate-environment/2022/07/18/biden-climate-emergency-manchin/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Washington Post reports}}}\uc2  today, after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s proposals to lower carbon emissions stalled in Congress, sending his administration looking for other ways to take action to curb the planet\u8217\'20\'19s warming. Meanwhile, much of the United States is dealing with a wave of high temperatures, while a heatwave in Europe is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/19/europe-heatwave-wildfires-death-toll-france-highest-temperatures"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 breaking records}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s not all that\u8217\'20\'19s happening:\par \par \uc2 * The January 6 committee\u8217\'20\'19s primetime hearing on Thursday will feature two former White House aides, who will testify as to what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was doing as the Capitol was attacked, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/capitol-siege-biden-donald-trump-government-and-politics-00896eaba6df614bf46fc6beebe63fce"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Maryland is holding its primary elections with a familiar dynamic: a Trump-backed candidate is standing against other mainstream Republicans for the governorship nomination.\par \par \uc2 * The trial of former top Trump adviser {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/18/steve-bannon-contempt-of-congress-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Steve Bannon}}}\uc2  resumes at 9am eastern time.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220719ei7j0020c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
