\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 West Virginia to resume abortions after judge blocks enforcement of ban \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris Stein in Washington \par \uc2 5,174 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 July 2022\par 20:06 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Decision clears way for the state\u8217\'20\'19s lone \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic to re-openSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Today has been a hot one across much of America, with parts of the country {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/18/us-faces-extreme-heat-biden-climate-crisis-plan-stalls-us-capitol-attack-latest-updates?page=with:block-62d56d388f082dc50bc2ad68#block-62d56d388f082dc50bc2ad68"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 enduring a wave of temperatures that hit dangerous levels in places}}}\uc2 , even as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/18/us-faces-extreme-heat-biden-climate-crisis-plan-stalls-us-capitol-attack-latest-updates?page=with:block-62d557ac8f083a0fe85d2e5f#block-62d557ac8f083a0fe85d2e5f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 major action against climate change has stalled indefinitely in Washington}}}\uc2 . Meanwhile, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates in West Virginia succeeded in getting the state\u8217\'20\'19s ban on the procedure {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/18/us-faces-extreme-heat-biden-climate-crisis-plan-stalls-us-capitol-attack-latest-updates?page=with:block-62d5a7dc8f083a0fe85d3296#block-62d5a7dc8f083a0fe85d3296"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocked}}}\uc2 , though the Republican-dominated statehouse {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/18/us-faces-extreme-heat-biden-climate-crisis-plan-stalls-us-capitol-attack-latest-updates?page=with:block-62d5b1178f08f134b15ffd23#block-62d5b1178f08f134b15ffd23"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appears to have been expecting such an outcome.}}}\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a rundown of the day\u8217\'20\'19s major events:\par \par \uc2 * A bipartisan group of lawmakers has introduced legislation to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/18/us-faces-extreme-heat-biden-climate-crisis-plan-stalls-us-capitol-attack-latest-updates?page=with:block-62d5a4458f08f134b15ffc80#block-62d5a4458f08f134b15ffc80"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 codify same-sex marriage rights into law}}}\uc2  after conservative supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  last month signaled the court could reconsider its ruling protecting the unions.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Jody Hice\uc2 , a Georgia congressman and 2020 election denier, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/18/us-faces-extreme-heat-biden-climate-crisis-plan-stalls-us-capitol-attack-latest-updates?page=with:block-62d57f978f08f134b15ffab2#block-62d57f978f08f134b15ffab2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has been subpoenaed}}}\uc2  by a grand jury looking into attempts to subvert the election results in the state.\par \par \uc2 * The trial of \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 , a former top adviser to Trump, got underway. He\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/18/us-faces-extreme-heat-biden-climate-crisis-plan-stalls-us-capitol-attack-latest-updates?page=with:block-62d577c18f083a0fe85d306d#block-62d577c18f083a0fe85d306d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 facing contempt charges}}}\uc2  for defying the January 6 committee.\par \par \uc2 * A prominent economist outlined his argument against the relentless pursuit of economic growth {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/18/us-faces-extreme-heat-biden-climate-crisis-plan-stalls-us-capitol-attack-latest-updates?page=with:block-62d571ea8f082dc50bc2adc0#block-62d571ea8f082dc50bc2adc0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in an interview with The New York Times Magazine}}}\uc2 , arguing it was unsustainable.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 The daily White House press briefing is happening now, with Council of Economic Advisers member Jared Bernstein at the podium. After the apparent defeat of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s legislative effort to fight climate change last week, \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s David Smith reports Bernstein is restating {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/15/joe-manchin-climate-funding-tax-hikes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the president\u8217\'20\'19s resolve to use executive actions to lower America\u8217\'20\'19s carbon emissions}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 enltrBernstein: "The president will aggressively fight to tackle climate change because he knows it's one of the reasons he's here."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1549117126652338176?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 18, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrBernstein on Biden: "He has taken unprecedented action already to tackle the climate crisis." He will continue to do so "even if the legislative path is closed to him".\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1549117538893811712?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 18, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrBernstein: "The president will always try to pursue the best legislative path to get the best deal for the people who sent him up here. But if that path closes, he will find another path."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1549118400512802818?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 18, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Bernstein is also mounting a defense of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s economic record, noting strength in retail sales and the recent drop in the budget deficit.\par \par \uc2 enltrAt White House press briefing. Economic adviser Jared Bernstein: \u8220\'20\'1CIf you look at retail sales from just last week, you\u8217\'20\'19ll see American consumers still helping to fuel really remarkable job gains\u8230\'20\'26. Where we are right now remains solidly within expansion.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/IxnURQxmnZ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/IxnURQxmnZ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1549112901771862019?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 18, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrBernstein: "The budget deficit has come down 77% in the first nine months of this fiscal year. That's the biggest decline on record."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Smith (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1549118913497153537?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 18, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Communities across parts of the greater Phoenix area are today dealing with fallen power lines, road closures and power outages after severe thunderstorms over the weekend triggered flash floods, dust storms and ping-pong ball sized hail.\par \par \uc2 The skies have been lit up by lightning across the region - from the White Mountains area to the Colorado River, with almost 25,000 flashes in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NWSPhoenix/status/1548713059669004289?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1548713059669004289%7Ctwgr%5E%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.azcentral.com%2Fstory%2Fnews%2Flocal%2Farizona-weather%2F2022%2F07%2F17%2Fburn-scars-boost-risk-flash-flooding-after-weekend-storm-events%2F10082261002%2F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 just 12 hours on Saturday, according to the National Weather Service.}}}\uc2  More thunderstorms are expected this afternoon and evening, which has made gardeners and farmers happy as last year\u8217\'20\'19s monsoon failed to deliver.\par \par \uc2 Much of Arizona is today enjoying a brief relief from above-average scorching temperatures thanks to a spate of monsoon storms over the past week, but it\u8217\'20\'19s expected to get hotter again tomorrow with temperatures in Phoenix, one of America\u8217\'20\'19s hottest cities, forecast to top 112F on four consecutive days from Tuesday to Friday. On a rare coolish day in Phoenix (top temperature 109F), the sweltering heat in the UK has caught the eye of meteorologists at the National Weather Service.\par \par \uc2 enltrWe in the Desert Southwest are not the only ones seeing very hot temperatures...much of the UK will be seeing record high temps today/tomorrow as well...forecast highs today/tomorrow for London are 36-38C (98-100F)! UK may see their 1st 40C (104F) ever! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/mm5MDGNyNf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/mm5MDGNyNf}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/cAn6AFdFgk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/cAn6AFdFgk}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 NWS Phoenix (@NWSPhoenix) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NWSPhoenix/status/1549056133523877888?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 18, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 West Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican leaders knew a court ruling could stop the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban from coming into effect.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe West Virginia Legislature is strongly advised to amend the laws in our state to provide for clear prohibitions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that are consistent with Dobbs\u8221\'20\'1D, attorney general Patrick Morrisey wrote in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ago.wv.gov/Documents/Final%20Dobbs%20Memorandum.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a June memorandum}}}\uc2  following the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision in Dobbs v. Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, which overturned the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However governor Jim Justice said lawmakers in the Republican-dominated Senate and House of Delegates \u8220\'20\'1Care not ready\u8221\'20\'1D right now to craft new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wvnews.com/statejournal/news/special-session-planned-for-west-virginia-gov-justices-income-tax-reform-proposal/article_845fdd64-fe1a-11ec-9684-f3d4618a79ee.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the State Journal reported}}}\uc2 . While the legislature will hold a special session later this month to debate a proposal to slash the state\u8217\'20\'19s income taxes, Justice predicted a special session on legislation to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have to be called later.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a little more on the West Virginia \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ruling. Circuit court judge Tera Salango sided with the state\u8217\'20\'19s last remaining \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic on Monday by overturning a 19th-century law that made performing or receiving the procedure a felony punishable by up to 10 years in prison.\par \par \uc2 The ruling allows the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Center of West Virginia to immediately resume providing abortions, which it stopped following the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/24/how-americans-lost-federal-abortion-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 24 June US Supreme Court decision}}}\uc2  overturning federal protections provided by Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 The state argued that an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban on the books dating back 150 years, which included an exception when the woman\u8217\'20\'19s life was in danger, was still enforceable.\par \par \uc2 But Salango agreed with the position of the ACLU of West Virginia, which argue for the clinic that the law was invalid, partly because it had not been enforced in more than 50 years, but also because it had been superseded by others, including a 2015 law allowing abortions until 20 weeks.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Judge approves resumption of West Virginia abortions\par \par \uc2 A West Virginia judge on Monday blocked officials from enforcing a 19th-century ban on abortions after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned the 1973 Roe v Wade decision that recognized the right of women nationally to terminate pregnancies, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 The decision by Kanawha county circuit judge Tera Salango clears the way for the state\u8217\'20\'19s lone \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic to resume services, which it suspended out of fear of prosecution following the high court\u8217\'20\'19s 24 June ruling.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll have more details soon...\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 A bipartisan group of congress members has introduced a bill called the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://judiciary.house.gov/news/documentsingle.aspx?DocumentID=4992"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Respect for Marriage Act}}}\uc2  in response to a warning from Justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  that the right wing Supreme Court majority could soon take aim at same-sex marriage.\par \par \uc2 Thomas, one of six conservatives on the panel, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/clarence-thomas-roe-gay-marriage-contraception-lgbtq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeared to signal in June}}}\uc2  that the court would likely follow up its overturning of Roe v Wade \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections by looking at other \u8220\'20\'1Csettled\u8221\'20\'1D issues, including the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/14pdf/14-556_3204.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2015 Obergefell ruling}}}\uc2  that legalized gay marriage.\par \par \uc2 House judiciary chair \uc2 Jerrold Nadler\uc2 , a New York Democrat, said Monday that the bipartisan group, which includes Republican Maine senator \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2 , was proposing the new act in an attempt to enshrine marriage equality into federal law.\par \par \uc2 Nadler said:\par \par \uc2 Three weeks ago, a conservative majority on the Supreme Court not only repealed Roe v Wade and walked back 50 years of precedent, it signaled that other rights, like the right to same-sex marriage, are next on the chopping block.\par \par \uc2 As this Court may take aim at other fundamental rights, we cannot sit idly by as the hard-earned gains of the Equality movement are systematically eroded.\par \par \uc2 If Justice Thomas\u8217\'20\'19s concurrence teaches anything it\u8217\'20\'19s that we cannot let your guard down or the rights and freedoms that we have come to cherish will vanish into a cloud of radical ideology and dubious legal reasoning.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s office has announced that \uc2 Olena Zelenska\uc2 , Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s first lady and wife of president \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , will address members of both chambers of Congress on Wednesday morning.\par \par \uc2 enltrOlena Zelenska, the First Lady of Ukraine, will speak to Congress on Wednesday. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/EHnZk5iVgZ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/EHnZk5iVgZ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Stewart (@KyleAlexStewart) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KyleAlexStewart/status/1549090692563173377?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 18, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The announcement said she will speak at 11am, but gave no details of the topic.\par \par \uc2 Zelenska, who has spent most of the war since Russia\u8217\'20\'19s 24 February invasion in an undisclosed location, has made only rare public appearances.\par \par \uc2 She spoke with the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Shaun Walker last month:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/18/olena-zelenska-ukraine-first-lady-rare-interview-family-under-threat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s first lady Olena Zelenska on being Russia\u8217\'20\'19s target No 2: \u8216\'20\'18When you see their crimes, maybe they really are capable of anything\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Betsy DeVos\uc2 , who served as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s education secretary throughout his single term of office, now believes the department she led should be abolished.\par \par \uc2 DeVos was speaking at a weekend conference in Florida hosted by Moms for Liberty, a conservative parents\u8217\'20\'19 activist group dedicated to electing rightwing candidates to school boards and opposing diversity and perceived \u8220\'20\'1Cwokeism\u8221\'20\'1D in classrooms.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI personally think the Department of Education should not exist,\u8221\'20\'1D DeVos told the three-day gathering in Tampa, to loud applause, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://floridaphoenix.com/blog/betsy-devos-calls-for-abolition-of-federal-education-department-she-once-led/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to Florida Phoenix}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Decisions about education, she said, should be made by state government and local school boards, which she asserted were best placed to serve their communities.\par \par \uc2 Betsy DeVos\uc2 . Photograph: Manuel Balce Ceneta/AP\par \par \uc2 Her comments almost exactly echoed the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://massie.house.gov/news/documentsingle.aspx?DocumentID=395319"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 language of a bill}}}\uc2  by Republican Kentucky congressman \uc2 Thomas Massie\uc2  last year that said: \u8220\'20\'1Cunelected bureaucrats in Washington DC should not be in charge of our children\u8217\'20\'19s intellectual and moral development.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 DeVos, who once advocated for guns to be allowed in schools to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2017/jan/18/betsy-devos-guns-schools-grizzly-bears"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 counter the threat from grizzly bears}}}\uc2 , was among several ultra-conservative speakers at the summit of a group set up during the Covid-19 pandemic to fight mask and vaccination mandates in schools.\par \par \uc2 They included Florida Republican senator \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2 , who was applauded by attendees for voting against the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/25/joe-biden-signs-gun-control-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bipartisan gun reform package}}}\uc2  signed into law by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  last month.\par \par \uc2 The conference also featured a breakout panel on school safety including Scott and Ryan Petty, a Florida board of education member whose daughter Alaina was among 17 murdered in a 2018 high school shooting in Parkland, Florida.\par \par \uc2 The panel, the Phoenix reported, discussed arming school personnel and tightening security on campuses, but not gun reforms advocates say might have prevented shootings such as in Parkland and in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas-school-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Uvalde, Texas}}}\uc2  in May, where a teenage gunman killed 19 students and two teachers.\par \par \uc2 The Moms for \uc2 Liberty\uc2  group has a high profile supporter in Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , whose raft of anti-LGBTQ+ legislation in recent months includes the so-called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/jul/02/dont-say-gay-florida-week-in-patriarchy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t say gay\u8221\'20\'1D bill}}}\uc2  banning discussion of sexual orientation and gender identity in classrooms.\par \par \uc2 DeSantis, a likely 2024 presidential candidate whose state education department {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/17/florida-rejects-math-textbooks-critical-race-theory"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banned dozens of math textbooks}}}\uc2  earlier this year for \u8220\'20\'1Cprohibited topics,\u8221\'20\'1D urged attendees to resist what he sees as left-wing wokeism.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow is not the time to be a shrinking violet. Now is not the time to let them grind you down. You\u8217\'20\'19ve got to stand up and you\u8217\'20\'19ve got to fight,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/07/15/moms-for-liberty-desantis-00046178"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to Politico}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 The president of Mexico, \uc2 Andres Manuel Lopez Obrador\uc2 , has defended {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/wikileaks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 WikiLeaks}}}\uc2  founder {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/julian-assange"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Julian Assange}}}\uc2 , and repeated his offer asylum to him. In June, the UK approved Assange\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2022/jun/17/julian-assange-extradition-to-us-approved-by-priti-patel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 extradition}}}\uc2  to the US to face prosecution for charges involving \uc2 WikiLeaks\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 disclosure of confidential diplomatic cables and military records.\par \par \uc2 At a routine press conference Monday, Reuters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/americas/mexican-president-renewed-asylum-offer-assange-letter-biden-2022-07-18/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Lopez Obrador\uc2  said: \u8220\'20\'1CI left a letter to the president about Assange, explaining that he did not commit any serious crime, did not cause anyone\u8217\'20\'19s death, did not violate any human rights and that he exercised his freedom, and that arresting him would mean a permanent affront to freedom of expression.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Lopez Obrador\uc2  has called Assange \u8220\'20\'1Cthe best journalist of our time.\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Lopez Obrador\uc2  claims to have penned a similar letter for former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  before he left office.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Legal fights over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access continue across the US. Today in West Virginia, the state\u8217\'20\'19s lone \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic is asking a judge to toss an 150-year-old state law so that the facility can immediately resume providing the procedure.\par \par \uc2 The Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Center of West Virginia suspended performing abortions on 24 June, when the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 . The 1800s West Virginia law states that obtaining or performing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a felony, which can result in up to 10 years imprisonment, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-health-west-virginia-charleston-government-and-politics-eccf3ac01cea7d51ea6dac5792520a48"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to The Associated Press}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The exception is for instances where a woman or other pregnant person\u8217\'20\'19s life is at risk. The American Civil Liberties Union of West Virginia has contended that the statute isn\u8217\'20\'19t valid because it hasn\u8217\'20\'19t been enforced in more than five decades, and has been superseded by more contemporary statutes on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which recognize the right to this procedure, AP says.\par \par \uc2 Advocates point to West Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s 2015 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, which permits the procedure up to 20 weeks. The state\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general, Patrick Morrisey, has contended that the old law remains enforceable.\par \par \uc2 Lawyers for the state contend that the law hasn\u8217\'20\'19t been enforced solely because Roe would have made illegal the prosecution of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  recipients and providers, per AP.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democratic Florida congresswoman Val Demings {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepValDemings/status/1549037686090272769?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Eembeddedtimeline%7Ctwterm%5Eprofile%3Arepvaldemings%7Ctwgr%%7Ctwcon%5Etimelinechrome&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fdemings.house.gov%2F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 revealed}}}\uc2  this morning that she has Covid-19. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve tested positive for Covid and am currently isolating with mild symptoms,\u8221\'20\'1D Demings {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepValDemings/status/1549037686090272769?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Eembeddedtimeline%7Ctwterm%5Eprofile%3Arepvaldemings%7Ctwgr%%7Ctwcon%5Etimelinechrome&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fdemings.house.gov%2F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThank you for the many well-wishes, and stay safe.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Demings, who is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/18/val-demings-florida-marco-rubio-senate-challenge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 campaigning against}}}\uc2  Republican senator {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/marco-rubio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Marco Rubio}}}\uc2  for the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 , reportedly attended Florida Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 Leadership Blue conference in the central Florida city of Tampa this weekend. At the conference, the congresswoman\u8217\'20\'19s husband, Orange ounty Mayor Jerry Demings, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/07/18/val-demings-covid-democrats-tampa-conference-00046335"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told Politico}}}\uc2  that her voice was hoarse from speaking at several events.\par \par \uc2 Politico notes that it\u8217\'20\'19s not known where Demings contracted Covid-19. Other prominent democrats \u8211\'20\'13 including Florida congressman \uc2 Charlie Crist\uc2  and Illinois governor JB Pritzker \u8211\'20\'13 attended the convention. Politico reports that no other top speakers have publicly disclosed whether they have tested positive for Covid.\par \par \uc2 Demings, who was once considered as a possible vice-president to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , attracted national attention when she worked as an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/jan/24/impeachment-day-four-takeaways-final-arguments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 impeachment manager}}}\uc2  during {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s first {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/jan/24/trump-impeachment-trial-suspense-day-four?ref=hvper.com&utm_source=hvper.com&utm_medium=website"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 impeachment trial}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a hot day across much of America, with parts of the country {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/18/us-faces-extreme-heat-biden-climate-crisis-plan-stalls-us-capitol-attack-latest-updates?page=with:block-62d56d388f082dc50bc2ad68#block-62d56d388f082dc50bc2ad68"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 enduring a wave of temperatures that will hit dangerous levels in places}}}\uc2 , however {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/18/us-faces-extreme-heat-biden-climate-crisis-plan-stalls-us-capitol-attack-latest-updates?page=with:block-62d557ac8f083a0fe85d2e5f#block-62d557ac8f083a0fe85d2e5f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 major action against climate change is still stalled indefinitely in Washington}}}\uc2 . Meanwhile, more allies of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  are feeling legal heat related to the 2020 election and the January 6 insurrection at the US Capitol.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Jody Hice\uc2 , a Georgia congressman and 2020 election denier, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/18/us-faces-extreme-heat-biden-climate-crisis-plan-stalls-us-capitol-attack-latest-updates?page=with:block-62d57f978f08f134b15ffab2#block-62d57f978f08f134b15ffab2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has been subpoenaed}}}\uc2  by a grand jury looking into attempts to subvert the election results in the state.\par \par \uc2 * The trial of \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 , a former top adviser to Trump, begins today. He\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/18/us-faces-extreme-heat-biden-climate-crisis-plan-stalls-us-capitol-attack-latest-updates?page=with:block-62d577c18f083a0fe85d306d#block-62d577c18f083a0fe85d306d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 facing contempt charges}}}\uc2  for defying the January 6 committee.\par \par \uc2 * A prominent economist outlined his argument against the relentless pursuit of economic growth {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jul/18/us-faces-extreme-heat-biden-climate-crisis-plan-stalls-us-capitol-attack-latest-updates?page=with:block-62d571ea8f082dc50bc2adc0#block-62d571ea8f082dc50bc2adc0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in an interview with The New York Times Magazine}}}\uc2 , arguing it was unsustainable.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  has published {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/climate-environment/2022/07/18/climate-change-manchin-math/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an excellent look}}}\uc2  at where US emissions are now, and what senator \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s death blow against Biden\u8217\'20\'19s climate agenda means for the fight to stop global temperatures from rising.\par \par \uc2 America\u8217\'20\'19s carbon emissions are already on the downward trajectory from their peak in 2005, the data says, and thus, Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s decision last week not to support provisions to hasten their decline means the US likely won\u8217\'20\'19t hit goals intended to keep global warming in check.\par \par \uc2 From the Post\u8217\'20\'19s report:\par \par \uc2 A major part of the goal can be achieved by riding the ongoing downward trend in emissions, which reflect government policies and actions taken by the private sector, particularly the energy industry, to become more sustainable. For instance, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://rhg.com/research/taking-stock-2022/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent analysis}}}\uc2  by the Rhodium Group, a research firm that closely tracks emissions policies, found that the United States is already on track to reduce emissions by somewhere between 24 and 35 percent below their 2005 level by 2030.\par \par \uc2 But that\u8217\'20\'19s nowhere near enough to meet the pledge.\par \par \uc2 The current blowup of negotiations with Manchin \u8220\'20\'1Cmakes it harder, and it makes any additional actions by the executive branch that much more critical. The stakes are now that much higher,\u8221\'20\'1D said John Larsen, a partner with Rhodium.\par \par \uc2 Several {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://rhg.com/research/build-back-better-congress-budget/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 analyses}}}\uc2  have suggested that policies like those contained in the Senate legislation could have accounted for about a billion additional tons of annual U.S. emissions reductions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe estimate the Senate budget deal likely would have cut emissions by roughly 800 million to 1 billion metric tons in 2030,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Princeton University\uc2  professor Jesse Jenkins, an energy policy expert and modeler.\par \par \uc2 In Jenkins\u8217\'20\'19s analysis, there would still be a gap, albeit a small one \u8211\'20\'13 of hundreds of millions of tons \u8211\'20\'13 to achieve the Biden administration pledge.\par \par \uc2 Somewhat separate from all of this is what it means for the Earth \u8211\'20\'13 after all, every major emitter has to act or else each one\u8217\'20\'19s progress, or lack thereof, will be moot.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/joan-greve"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joan E Greve}}}\uc2  has taken a look at a question swirling around \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  as he struggles with both his advanced age and record low approval ratings: could he decide not to run again in 2024?\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is having a rough summer. The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  has overturned Roe v Wade, ending federal protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. Although gas prices {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/business/energy/us-gasoline-prices-are-finally-falling-why-2022-07-14/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are now falling}}}\uc2 , they remain high and have driven inflation to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/jul/13/high-us-gas-food-prices-june-led-to-largest-annual-increase-inflation-40-years"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 its largest annual increase}}}\uc2  in more than 40 years. West Virginia senator \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  has finally ended any hopes that the president had of passing a climate bill in Congress. With an evenly divided Senate, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s options for addressing these problems \u8211\'20\'13 or enacting any of his other legislative priorities \u8211\'20\'13 are bleak.\par \par \uc2 The American people have taken note. Biden\u8217\'20\'19s approval rating has steadily fallen since April and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/biden-approval-rating/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 now sits in the high 30s}}}\uc2 . A recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.monmouth.edu/polling-institute/documents/monmouthpoll_us_070522.pdf/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Monmouth poll}}}\uc2  found that only 10% of Americans believe the country is heading in the right direction.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/18/joe-biden-age-approval-rating-2024-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Too old to run again? Biden faces questions about his age as crises mount}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jody Hice\uc2 , a Georgia congressman who believes the baseless theory that the 2020 election was stolen from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , has been subpoenaed by a grand jury investigating efforts to disrupt the results of the polls in the state, Politico reports:\par \par \uc2 enltrNEWS: Congressman \uc2 Jody HICE\uc2  says he's been subpoenaed by the grand jury in Fulton County, GA. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6Gob2KWF1f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/6Gob2KWF1f}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1549054243700559872?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 18, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrHICE is seeking to transfer his challenge to the subpoena to federal court. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6Gob2KF49H"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/6Gob2KF49H}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1549054437720838152?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 18, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrHice filed this action a day before the subpoena was supposed to compel his testimony. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6Gob2KWF1f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/6Gob2KWF1f}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/eDqsfxL6k2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/eDqsfxL6k2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1549054989154168832?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 18, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 In May, Hice lost his bid for the Republican nomination for Georgia secretary of state to \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , who famously rejected Trump\u8217\'20\'19s appeals to swing the state\u8217\'20\'19s election results in his direction.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/24/georgia-primary-elections-kemp-carr-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Resounding setback for Trump as Kemp wins Republican primary in Georgia}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump could soon announce a new bid for president, but a member of the House committee investigating the January 6 attack said this weekend that wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t affect their ongoing probe, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/ramon-antonio-vargas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ramon Antonio Vargas}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  won\u8217\'20\'19t blunt the investigation by the congressional committee investigating the deadly January 6th attack on the Capitol by announcing that he\u8217\'20\'19s running for the Oval Office again, a member of the panel said Sunday.\par \par \uc2 Elaine Luria\uc2 , a Virginia congresswoman and one of seven Democrats on the committee, told CNN\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Dana Bash\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CThe bottom line is that no one is above the law \u8211\'20\'13 whether he\u8217\'20\'19s a president, former president or a potential future presidential candidate, we are going to pursue the facts.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Luria\u8217\'20\'19s remarks were in response to an oft-asked question about whether Trump could simply announce he is running for president again in 2024 and shield himself from the threat of prosecution posed by the evidence presented during the January 6 committee\u8217\'20\'19s recent hearings.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/17/january-6-hearings-trump-capitol-attack-inquiry"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump won\u8217\'20\'19t blunt January 6 inquiry by entering 2024 race, panel member says}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 , a former top advisor to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , is going to trial today for defying a subpoena by the January 6 committee, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levine}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 A federal criminal trial is set to begin on Monday to determine whether {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/steve-bannon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Steve Bannon}}}\uc2 , the influential former adviser to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , broke the law by refusing to comply with a subpoena for documents and testimony by the panel investigating the January 6 attack on the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 Last fall, the congressional committee investigating the deadly Capitol riots {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.house.gov/meetings/IJ/IJ00/20211019/114156/HMTG-117-IJ00-20211019-SD001.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subpoenaed Bannon}}}\uc2  to sit for a deposition and to provide a wide range of documents related to the events of January 6. Bannon refused to comply. The committee cited him for contempt and referred him to the US justice department for prosecution {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/21/steve-bannon-house-vote-criminal-contempt-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  in October of last year}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The justice department pursued the referral, and a federal grand jury indicted Bannon on two counts of contempt of Congress, both misdemeanors, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/12/steve-bannon-indicted-capitol-attack-subpoena"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in November}}}\uc2 . It is extremely rare for the justice department to pursue such charges \u8211\'20\'13 before Bannon, the last contempt prosecution was in 1983. Bannon faces between 30 days and a year in prison if convicted on each charge.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/18/steve-bannon-criminal-contempt-congress-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Steve Bannon\u8217\'20\'19s criminal contempt of Congress trial set to begin}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Perhaps we are doing this whole development thing wrong. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2022/07/18/magazine/herman-daly-interview.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In an interview with The New York Times Magazine}}}\uc2 , Herman Daly, a lauded economist who was once a senior figure at the \uc2 World Bank\uc2  and is now a emeritus professor at the University of Maryland School of Public Policy, argues that modern economics\u8217\'20\'19 obsession with growth is misguided, due in part to the damage done to the planet.\par \par \uc2 Economic growth is considered a major barometer of a country\u8217\'20\'19s health, both for wealthy nations and the developing world. In the interview, Daly argues that we are viewing growth incorrectly, and that it\u8217\'20\'19s implausible all nations can continue expanding their GDP endlessly. From the interview, here\u8217\'20\'19s an encapsulation of his argument:\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a false assumption to say that growth is increasing the standard of living in the present world because we measure growth as growth in G.D.P. If it goes up, does that mean we\u8217\'20\'19re increasing standard of living? We\u8217\'20\'19ve said that it does, but we\u8217\'20\'19ve left out all the costs of increasing G.D.P. We really don\u8217\'20\'19t know that the standard is going up. If you subtract for the deaths and injuries caused by automobile accidents, chemical pollution, wildfires and many other costs induced by excessive growth, it\u8217\'20\'19s not clear at all. Now what I just said is most true for richer countries. Certainly for some other country that\u8217\'20\'19s struggling for subsistence then, by all means, G.D.P. growth increases welfare. They need economic growth. That means that the wealthy part of the world has to make ecological room for the poor to catch up to an acceptable standard of living. That means cutting back on per capita consumption, that we don\u8217\'20\'19t hog all the resources for trivial consumption.\par \par \uc2 The article only briefly gets into what Daly would propose to change the growth paradigm across the world, and indeed, his ideas would be a tough lift for many countries:\par \par \uc2 Daly\u8217\'20\'19s policy prescriptions for how this would happen include, among many ideas, establishing minimum and maximum income limits, setting caps for natural-resource use and, controversially, stabilizing the population by working to ensure that births plus immigration equals deaths plus emigration.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Many parts of the United States will today also face blistering heat, particularly in the south and southwest, and the Great Plains.\par \par \uc2 The New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2022/us/heat-wave-map-tracker.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has published a map}}}\uc2  looking at where temperatures will be highest. The good news is that the heat will cool later this week. The bad news is that for the next few days, much of the country will face heat levels that the \uc2 National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration\uc2  says warrant \u8220\'20\'1Cextreme caution\u8221\'20\'1D. And the worst affected areas will face temperatures at the \u8220\'20\'1Cdanger\u8221\'20\'1D level, when heat cramps or exhaustion are \u8220\'20\'1Clikely\u8221\'20\'1D and heat stroke is also a possibility.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Britain is weathering a record-breaking heat wave that just saw Wales endure its hottest day on record. Follow \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s live coverage for more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/live/2022/jul/18/uk-weather-heatwave-met-office-warning-forecast-temperature-london-schools-latest-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Extreme UK weather live: Wales provisionally records its hottest day with 35.3C in Gogerddan, near Aberystwyth}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 The unhoused are one group bearing the brunt of the climate crisis - particularly in California. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levin}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 In a remote stretch of southern {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/california"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 California}}}\uc2  desert, at least 200 unhoused people live outside, battling the extremes: blazing hot temperatures in the summer, snow in winter, rugged terrain inaccessible to many vehicles, a constant wind that blankets everything with silt, and no running water for miles.\par \par \uc2 For Candice Winfrey, the conditions almost proved deadly.\par \par \uc2 The 37-year-old lives in a camper in the Mojave desert, on the northern edge of Los Angeles county, miles from the nearest store. During a record-breaking heatwave in July 2020, she found herself running out of water. The jug of a gallon she had left had overheated, the water so hot it was barely drinkable. It was more than 110F (43C), and no one was around to help. She recalled laying in her tent, trying not to think about the heat exhaustion and dehydration overtaking her. \u8220\'20\'1CI thought I was gonna die. I was seeing the light. I was just waiting it out and praying to God that I\u8217\'20\'19d make it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/18/california-homelessness-crisis-mojave-desert"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 As police crack down on homelessness, unhoused end up in Mojave desert}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCollective suicide\u8221\'20\'1D: that\u8217\'20\'19s what the \uc2 UN\uc2  secretary general said humanity is facing due to rising temperatures, as \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/fiona-harvey"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fiona Harvey}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/17/forest-fires-rage-across-europe-as-heatwave-sends-temperatures-soaring"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wildfires and heatwaves}}}\uc2  wreaking havoc across swathes of the globe show humanity facing \u8220\'20\'1Ccollective suicide\u8221\'20\'1D, the \uc2 UN\uc2  secretary general has warned, as governments around the world scramble to protect people from the impacts of extreme heat.\par \par \uc2 Ant\u243\'00\'F3nio Guterres\uc2  told ministers from 40 countries meeting to discuss the climate crisis on Monday: \u8220\'20\'1CHalf of humanity is in the danger zone, from floods, droughts, extreme storms and wildfires. No nation is immune. Yet we continue to feed our fossil fuel addiction.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have a choice. Collective action or collective suicide. It is in our hands.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/jul/18/humanity-faces-collective-suicide-over-climate-crisis-warns-un-chief"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Humanity faces \u8216\'20\'18collective suicide\u8217\'20\'19 over climate crisis, warns UN chief}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 For the past year and a half, it seemed like \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  would get to sign a major piece of legislation addressing climate change.\par \par \uc2 The vehicle was at first his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/19/house-democrats-pass-biden-expansive-build-back-better-policy-plan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 marquee Build Back Better spending plan}}}\uc2 , which would have allocated more than a trillion dollars to addressing a host of Democratic priorities. Then that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/20/schumer-biden-build-back-better-manchin-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 died}}}\uc2 , and Democrats quietly began working on a follow-up bill that could pass both the Senate and the House of Representatives, which the party controlled with razor-thin margins.\par \par \uc2 Now, it seems like Congress won\u8217\'20\'19t act to curb America\u8217\'20\'19s carbon emissions at all. \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2 , the centrist Democrat whose vote is necessary to get any legislation that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t win Republican support through the Senate, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/16/joe-manchin-biden-climate-democrats-climate-plans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has said now is not the time to spend money fighting climate change}}}\uc2  due to the current high rate of inflation, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/15/us-weather-heat-warnings-alerts-record-temperatures"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 even as extreme weather continues to batter the United States and world}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The senator\u8217\'20\'19s declaration last week was a major loss for the White House, but Biden may still get to use his pen by signing to-be-announced executive orders intended to keep temperatures from rising.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 America's plan to fight climate crisis stalls as extreme heat batters US and the world\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. Today, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to take a closer look at the real-world consequences of American politics, specifically {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/15/joe-manchin-climate-funding-tax-hikes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the collapse last week of Democratic efforts to get Congress\u8217\'20\'19s approval of a plan to fight climate crisis}}}\uc2 . The United States and the world at large is today grappling with extreme heat and other calamities fueled by rising global temperatures, and experts warn if Washington and other top carbon emitters don\u8217\'20\'19t change something, it will only get worse.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more about what\u8217\'20\'19s happening today:\par \par \uc2 * Texas and much of the central US could {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/06/25/us/heat-wave-texas-oklahoma-plains.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 see their hottest temperatures of the summer this week}}}\uc2 , \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  reports. Meanwhile in Britain, temperatures may climb to an unheard-of 43C \u8211\'20\'13 or 109.4F. The Guardian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/live/2022/jul/18/uk-weather-heatwave-met-office-warning-forecast-temperature-london-schools-latest-updates#top-of-blog"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has a live blog covering the crisis}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Democrats may not be able to get a major climate change bill through Congress, but they are moving forward on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://punchbowl.news/archive/7-18-22-punchbowl-news-am/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 several other measures}}}\uc2  with an eye towards rescuing \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s presidency, Punchbowl News reports.\par \par \uc2 * The criminal contempt trial of \uc2 Steven Bannon\uc2 , a former top advisor to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/18/steve-bannon-criminal-contempt-congress-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 begins today, with jury selection}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220718ei7i001pa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
