\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  scraps plan to nominate anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  lawyer to Kentucky judgeship\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Aratani \par \uc2 588 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 July 2022\par 18:57 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Rand Paul\uc2  announced Friday he would not consent to Chad Meredith\u8217\'20\'19s nomination, vetoing the president\u8217\'20\'19s effort\par \par \uc2 After {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/06/biden-anti-abortion-lawyer-plan-emails"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 weeks of criticism}}}\uc2  from fellow Democrats and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocacy groups, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has deserted plans to nominate an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lawyer to be a federal judge in Kentucky.\par \par \uc2 The White House said on Friday that Republican Kentucky senator \uc2 Rand Paul\uc2  would not be consenting to the nomination of Chad Meredith, effectively vetoing Biden\u8217\'20\'19s move to put him on the bench.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn considering potential district court nominees, the White House learned that Senator \uc2 Rand Paul\uc2  will not return a blue slip on Chad Meredith,\u8221\'20\'1D said White House spokesperson Andrew Bates on Friday, referring to the \u8220\'20\'1Cblue slip\u8221\'20\'1D tradition that allows senators to veto judicial nominations from their home states. \u8220\'20\'1CTherefore, the White House will not nominate Mr Meredith.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Had Biden nominated Meredith, the attorney\u8217\'20\'19s promotion to the court would have been unusual in the lineup of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s judicial picks. The president has made it a point to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/mar/30/biden-federal-judicial-nominees-judges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nominate}}}\uc2  people from underrepresented backgrounds, public defenders and those with experience in civil rights law to the court instead of the usual slate of corporate lawyers and prosecutors.\par \par \uc2 Meredith served as chief deputy general counsel to former Republican Kentucky governor \uc2 Matt Bevin\uc2 , who was in office from 2015 to 2019. In this role, Meredith helped the state defend a 2017 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/dec/21/kentucky-governor-pardons-matt-bevin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 law}}}\uc2  that required doctors to perform ultrasounds and show images of the fetus to patients before performing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The law was ultimately upheld by a federal appeals court.\par \par \uc2 Working under Bevin, Meredith also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.courier-journal.com/story/news/politics/mitch-mcconnell/2022/07/05/who-chad-meredith-bidens-anti-abortion-pick-kentucky-judge/7790119001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 helped}}}\uc2  put together the former governor\u8217\'20\'19s slate of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/dec/21/kentucky-governor-pardons-matt-bevin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 controversial pardons}}}\uc2 , which included people convicted of murder and rape, according to the Louisville Courier-Journal.\par \par \uc2 After Bevin left office, Meredith began working for a private law firm in Cincinnati, Ohio.\par \par \uc2 News of his nomination was first reported by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.courier-journal.com/story/news/politics/mitch-mcconnell/2022/06/29/biden-backs-anti-abortion-judge-candidate-apparent-mcconnell-deal/7767539001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Courier-Journal}}}\uc2  on 29 June. Democrats started hounding the White House for an explanation behind its intention to nominate the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lawyer on the heels of the 24 June \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  decision overturning the nationwide right to terminate pregnancies embedded in Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 In a group statement, a coalition of national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocacy groups denounced news of the potential nomination.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are in this moment because anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  judges were intentionally nominated at every level to take away our fundamental right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and given his record, we know Chad Meredith would be no exception,\u8221\'20\'1D the statement read.\par \par \uc2 When White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  was questioned about the potential nomination, she said, \u8220\'20\'1CWe make it a point here to not comment on any vacancy, whether it is on the executive branch or the judicial branch, especially those where the nomination has not been made yet.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While the White House has been quiet behind its reasoning for considering Meredith, Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  said that Biden was close to taking up his judicial pick \u8220\'20\'1Cas a personal friendship gesture\u8221\'20\'1D, the Kentucky senator told the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/07/15/us/politics/biden-mcconnell-judge-abortion.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times}}}\uc2 . McConnell said that no specific deal between himself and Biden was made, and it simply represented the \u8220\'20\'1Ccollegiality\u8221\'20\'1D that exists between them.\par \par \uc2 Paul, who ultimately shut the nomination down, has not commented on his veto of Meredith\u8217\'20\'19s nomination. McConnell suggested to the Times that Paul may believe it is his turn to pick a judicial nominee, though he has not made such an agreement on judicial nominees with Paul.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220716ei7g00232\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
